INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('black_reach', '', '''black'':1A ''reach'':2A', '', '', '', '', '');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skooma', 'Skooma is a common narcotic in Tamriel, made from refined moon sugar. While illegal, it is widely available in Skyrim and known for its addictive properties.', '''addictiv'':26B ''and'':22B ''avail'':19B ''common'':5B ''for'':24B ''from'':10B ''illegal'':15B ''in'':7B,20B ''is'':3B,17B ''it'':16B ''its'':25B ''known'':23B ''mad'':9B ''moon'':12B ''narcotic'':6B ''properti'':27B ''refin'':11B ''skoom'':1A,2B ''skyrim'':21B ''sug'':13B ''tamriel'':8B ''whil'':14B ''widely'':18B', 'merchant, thief, khajit', 'You know it is a narcotic substance often associated with moon sugar but lack detailed knowledge.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bloodskal_barrow', 'Bloodskal Barrow is a small Nordic ruin located north of Raven Rock and south of Damphall Mine on Solstheim. Currently, the barrow is occupied by reavers .', '''and'':15B ''barrow'':2A,4B,24B ''bloodskal'':1A,3B ''by'':27B ''currently'':22B ''damphall'':18B ''is'':5B,25B ''locat'':10B ''min'':19B ''nordic'':8B ''north'':11B ''occupi'':26B ''of'':12B,17B ''on'':20B ''rav'':13B ''reavers'':28B ''rock'':14B ''ruin'':9B ''small'':7B ''solstheim'':21B ''south'':16B ''the'':23B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('companions', 'The Companions are a renowned group of warriors based in the city of Whiterun in Skyrim, with their headquarters located in the mead hall of Jorrvaskr. They trace their origins back to Ysgramor and his Five Hundred Companions, who accompanied him in his legendary return to Skyrim from Atmora, seeking vengeance against the elves during the Merethic Era. The modern Companions operate as mercenaries, accepting contracts from the public while maintaining a tradition of honor and neutrality, avoiding entanglement in political conflicts. The group is led by a Harbinger, an honorific title passed down from leader to leader, with Ysgramor himself regarded as the first Harbinger.

Within the Companions, the most elite members belong to the Circle, a governing body founded to uphold the ancient traditions of the group. However, the Circle harbored a dark secret: its members had accepted the curse of lycanthropy, turning them into werewolves under an ancient pact with the Glenmoril witches. While some, like Harbinger Kodlak Whitemane, sought to rid the Companions of this curse, others embraced it. The Companions have played a significant role in Skyrim’s history, holding a revered place as impartial warriors who value honor above all else.', '''abov'':196B ''accept'':141B ''accepting'':66B ''accompani'':41B ''against'':53B ''all'':197B ''an'':91B,151B ''ancient'':126B,152B ''and'':35B,77B ''are'':4B ''as'':64B,104B,190B ''atmor'':50B ''avoiding'':79B ''back'':32B ''bas'':10B ''belong'':115B ''body'':121B ''by'':88B ''circl'':118B,133B ''city'':13B ''companions'':1A,3B,39B,62B,110B,168B,176B ''conflicts'':83B ''contracts'':67B ''curs'':143B,171B ''dark'':136B ''down'':95B ''during'':56B ''elit'':113B ''else'':198B ''elves'':55B ''embrac'':173B ''entanglement'':80B ''first'':106B ''fiv'':37B ''found'':122B ''from'':49B,68B,96B ''glenmoril'':156B ''governing'':120B ''group'':7B,85B,130B ''had'':140B ''hall'':25B ''harbing'':90B,107B,161B ''harbor'':134B ''hav'':177B ''headquarters'':20B ''him'':42B ''himself'':102B ''his'':36B,44B ''history'':185B ''holding'':186B ''honor'':76B,195B ''honorific'':92B ''howev'':131B ''hundr'':38B ''impartial'':191B ''in'':11B,16B,22B,43B,81B,182B ''into'':148B ''is'':86B ''it'':174B ''its'':138B ''jorrvaskr'':27B ''kodlak'':162B ''lead'':97B,99B ''led'':87B ''legendary'':45B ''lik'':160B ''locat'':21B ''lycanthropy'':145B ''maintaining'':72B ''mead'':24B ''members'':114B,139B ''mercenari'':65B ''merethic'':58B ''modern'':61B ''most'':112B ''neutrality'':78B ''of'':8B,14B,26B,75B,128B,144B,169B ''operat'':63B ''origins'':31B ''others'':172B ''pact'':153B ''pass'':94B ''plac'':189B ''play'':178B ''political'':82B ''public'':70B ''regard'':103B ''renown'':6B ''return'':46B ''rever'':188B ''rid'':166B ''rol'':181B ''s'':184B ''secret'':137B ''seeking'':51B ''significant'':180B ''skyrim'':17B,48B,183B ''som'':159B ''sought'':164B ''the'':2B,12B,19B,23B,30B,54B,57B,60B,69B,84B,105B,109B,111B,117B,125B,129B,132B,142B,155B,167B,175B ''them'':147B ''they'':28B ''this'':170B ''titl'':93B ''to'':33B,47B,98B,116B,123B,165B ''trac'':29B ''tradition'':74B ''traditions'':127B ''turning'':146B ''under'':150B ''uphold'':124B ''valu'':194B ''vengeanc'':52B ''warriors'':9B,192B ''werewolv'':149B ''whil'':71B,158B ''whiteman'':163B ''whiterun'':15B ''who'':40B,193B ''witch'':157B ''with'':18B,100B,154B ''within'':108B ''ysgramor'':34B,101B', 'companions', '
The Companions are a legendary group of honorable warriors based in Whiterun, Skyrim, with their headquarters at Jorrvaskr. They trace their origins to Ysgramor and his Five Hundred Companions, who returned to Skyrim seeking vengeance against the elves. Today, they operate as neutral mercenaries, led by a Harbinger, and avoid political conflicts. The Companions hold a respected role in Skyrim''s history, valuing tradition and honor above all. There are rumors that they are secertly werewolves.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('thieves_guild', '
The Thieves Guild is a secretive organization in Skyrim dedicated to criminal activities, including burglary, pickpocketing, and smuggling. Despite its criminal nature, the guild often functions as a "crime regulator," maintaining order among thieves and ensuring a balance in illicit activities. Its headquarters, the Ragged Flagon, is hidden beneath the city of Riften within the network of tunnels known as the Ratway. The guild''s influence has spread across Skyrim, with members adhering to a code that discourages murder, unnecessary violence, and the targeting of the poor. Over the years, local authorities have tolerated the guild, benefiting from bribes and the guild''s role in regulating crime.

The guild offers many benefits to its members, such as specialized training, access to rare items, and opportunities to rise in rank. Those who advance within the guild may even become Nightingales, sworn to serve Nocturnal, the Daedric Prince of Night and Darkness. The guild''s reach extends into major cities like Solitude, Windhelm, Whiterun, and Markarth, where it restores its influence through special assignments.', '''access'':122B ''across'':71B ''activiti'':15B,43B ''adhering'':75B ''advanc'':134B ''among'':35B ''and'':19B,37B,84B,102B,126B,151B,165B ''as'':29B,62B,119B ''assignments'':174B ''authoriti'':94B ''balanc'':40B ''becom'':140B ''beneath'':51B ''benefiting'':99B ''benefits'':114B ''brib'':101B ''burglary'':17B ''citi'':160B ''city'':53B ''cod'':78B ''crim'':31B,109B ''criminal'':14B,23B ''daedric'':147B ''darkness'':152B ''dedicat'':12B ''despit'':21B ''discourag'':80B ''ensuring'':38B ''even'':139B ''extends'':157B ''flagon'':48B ''from'':100B ''functions'':28B ''guild'':2A,5B,26B,66B,98B,104B,111B,137B,154B ''hav'':95B ''headquarters'':45B ''hidd'':50B ''illicit'':42B ''in'':10B,41B,107B,130B ''including'':16B ''influenc'':68B,171B ''into'':158B ''is'':6B,49B ''it'':168B ''items'':125B ''its'':22B,44B,116B,170B ''known'':61B ''lik'':161B ''local'':93B ''maintaining'':33B ''major'':159B ''many'':113B ''markarth'':166B ''may'':138B ''members'':74B,117B ''murd'':81B ''natur'':24B ''network'':58B ''night'':150B ''nightingal'':141B ''nocturnal'':145B ''of'':54B,59B,87B,149B ''offers'':112B ''often'':27B ''opportuniti'':127B ''order'':34B ''organization'':9B ''over'':90B ''pickpocketing'':18B ''poor'':89B ''princ'':148B ''ragg'':47B ''rank'':131B ''rar'':124B ''ratway'':64B ''reach'':156B ''regulating'':108B ''regulator'':32B ''restor'':169B ''rift'':55B ''ris'':129B ''rol'':106B ''s'':67B,105B,155B ''secretiv'':8B ''serv'':144B ''skyrim'':11B,72B ''smuggling'':20B ''solitud'':162B ''special'':173B ''specializ'':120B ''spre'':70B ''such'':118B ''sworn'':142B ''targeting'':86B ''that'':79B ''the'':3B,25B,46B,52B,57B,63B,65B,85B,88B,91B,97B,103B,110B,136B,146B,153B ''thiev'':1A,4B,36B ''thos'':132B ''through'':172B ''to'':13B,76B,115B,123B,128B,143B ''tolerat'':96B ''training'':121B ''tunnels'':60B ''unnecessary'':82B ''violenc'':83B ''wher'':167B ''whiterun'':164B ''who'':133B ''windhelm'':163B ''with'':73B ''within'':56B,135B ''years'':92B', 'thievesguild', 'The Thieves Guild in Skyrim is a secretive organization focused on criminal activities like theft and smuggling while maintaining order among criminals. Based in Riften''s underground Ragged Flagon, the guild avoids targeting the poor and excessive violence, earning a degree of tolerance from authorities. The guild''s influence extends across Skyrim, restoring its power through key assignments in major cities.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dark_brotherhood', 'The Dark Brotherhood is a clandestine guild of assassins in Skyrim, renowned for carrying out murders for hire. Historically powerful, the guild has seen a significant decline in recent years. Unlike the more legally sanctioned Morag Tong in Morrowind, the Dark Brotherhood operates entirely outside the law, often feared and loathed by the general population. The organization was traditionally led by the Night Mother, but in Skyrim, Astrid has assumed control. The Brotherhood''s operations are based out of their Sanctuary, hidden deep within the wilderness, and they maintain a connection with the Thieves Guild in Riften.', '''and'':52B,89B ''are'':78B ''assassins'':11B ''assum'':72B ''astrid'':70B ''bas'':79B ''brotherhood'':2A,5B,44B,75B ''but'':67B ''by'':54B,63B ''carrying'':16B ''clandestin'':8B ''connection'':93B ''control'':73B ''dark'':1A,4B,43B ''declin'':29B ''deep'':85B ''entirely'':46B ''fear'':51B ''for'':15B,19B ''general'':56B ''guild'':9B,24B,97B ''hidd'':84B ''hir'':20B ''historically'':21B ''in'':12B,30B,40B,68B,98B ''is'':6B ''law'':49B ''led'':62B ''legally'':36B ''loath'':53B ''maintain'':91B ''mor'':35B ''morag'':38B ''morrowind'':41B ''moth'':66B ''murders'':18B ''night'':65B ''of'':10B,81B ''often'':50B ''operat'':45B ''operations'':77B ''organization'':59B ''out'':17B,80B ''outsid'':47B ''population'':57B ''powerful'':22B ''recent'':31B ''renown'':14B ''rift'':99B ''s'':76B ''sanction'':37B ''sanctuary'':83B ''seen'':26B ''significant'':28B ''skyrim'':13B,69B ''the'':3B,23B,34B,42B,48B,55B,58B,64B,74B,82B,87B,95B ''they'':90B ''thiev'':96B ''tong'':39B ''traditionally'':61B ''unlik'':33B ''was'':60B ''wilderness'':88B ''with'':94B ''within'':86B ''years'':32B', 'darkbrotherhood', 'The Dark Brotherhood is a secretive guild of assassins in Skyrim, specializing in murder-for-hire. Once powerful, it has declined in recent years and operates outside the law, feared by many. They are known to send notes with vague threats with a blackhand drawn on them. It is also rumored that you can summon the Dark Brotherhood to perform an assination using a secret dark ritual.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('imperial_legion', 'The Imperial Legion is the primary military force of the Empire of Tamriel, tasked with preserving peace, enforcing the rule of law, and protecting the Emperor and Imperial Province. Known for its discipline, vast numbers, and specialized troops, the Legion operates both as a garrison force during peacetime and an overwhelming invasion force during conflicts. Its recruits come from all races and regions, contributing to the Legion’s diverse but highly trained and loyal ranks. The Legion''s versatile structure includes archers, cavalry, battlemages, and healers, making it one of the most formidable armies in Tamriel’s history. In addition to military duties, the Legion acts as the Empire’s enforcer, providing guardsmen and maintaining order across the provinces.

The Legion''s history stretches back to the First Era, with its origins tied to the Alessian Empire. It played a key role in expanding and consolidating Imperial power under various rulers, including Tiber Septim during the creation of the Third Empire. Over the centuries, the Legion has fought in numerous wars and conflicts, from the Alessian conquest of Cyrodiil to the Great War against the Aldmeri Dominion. Despite facing challenges in later eras, such as the Great War and the Skyrim Civil War, the Imperial Legion remains a symbol of the Empire''s military strength and resilience.', '''across'':119B ''acts'':108B ''addition'':102B ''against'':186B ''aldmeri'':188B ''alessi'':138B,178B ''all'':62B ''an'':52B ''and'':25B,29B,38B,51B,64B,75B,87B,116B,147B,174B,201B,218B ''archers'':84B ''armi'':96B ''as'':45B,109B,197B ''back'':127B ''battlemag'':86B ''both'':44B ''but'':72B ''cavalry'':85B ''centuri'':166B ''challeng'':192B ''civil'':204B ''com'':60B ''conflicts'':57B,175B ''conquest'':179B ''consolidating'':148B ''contributing'':66B ''creation'':159B ''cyrodiil'':181B ''despit'':190B ''disciplin'':35B ''div'':71B ''dominion'':189B ''during'':49B,56B,157B ''duti'':105B ''emperor'':28B ''empir'':13B,111B,139B,163B,214B ''enforc'':113B ''enforcing'':20B ''expanding'':146B ''facing'':191B ''first'':130B ''for'':33B ''forc'':10B,48B,55B ''formid'':95B ''fought'':170B ''from'':61B,176B ''garrison'':47B ''great'':184B,199B ''guardsm'':115B ''healers'':88B ''highly'':73B ''history'':100B,125B ''imperial'':1A,4B,30B,149B,207B ''in'':97B,101B,145B,171B,193B ''includ'':83B ''including'':154B ''invasion'':54B ''is'':6B ''it'':90B,140B ''its'':34B,58B,133B ''key'':143B ''known'':32B ''lat'':194B ''law'':24B ''legion'':2A,5B,42B,69B,79B,107B,123B,168B,208B ''loyal'':76B ''maintaining'':117B ''making'':89B ''military'':9B,104B,216B ''most'':94B ''numbers'':37B ''numerous'':172B ''of'':11B,14B,23B,92B,160B,180B,212B ''one'':91B ''operat'':43B ''order'':118B ''origins'':134B ''over'':164B ''overwhelming'':53B ''peac'':19B ''peacetim'':50B ''play'':141B ''pow'':150B ''preserving'':18B ''primary'':8B ''protecting'':26B ''providing'':114B ''provinc'':31B,121B ''rac'':63B ''ranks'':77B ''recruits'':59B ''regions'':65B ''remains'':209B ''resilienc'':219B ''rol'':144B ''rul'':22B ''rulers'':153B ''s'':70B,80B,99B,112B,124B,215B ''septim'':156B ''skyrim'':203B ''specializ'':39B ''strength'':217B ''stretch'':126B ''structur'':82B ''such'':196B ''symbol'':211B ''tamriel'':15B,98B ''task'':16B ''the'':3B,7B,12B,21B,27B,41B,68B,78B,93B,106B,110B,120B,122B,129B,137B,158B,161B,165B,167B,177B,183B,187B,198B,202B,206B,213B ''third'':162B ''tib'':155B ''tied'':135B ''to'':67B,103B,128B,136B,182B ''train'':74B ''troops'':40B ''under'':151B ''various'':152B ''vast'':36B ''versatil'':81B ''war'':185B,200B,205B ''wars'':173B ''with'':17B,132B', 'legion, imperial, noble', '
The Imperial Legion is the Empire of Tamriel''s primary military force, tasked with maintaining peace, enforcing laws, and protecting the Empire. Known for its discipline and diverse, highly trained troops, it includes specialized units like archers, cavalry, and battlemages. Established in the First Era, the Legion has expanded Imperial power and played a key role in major conflicts, including the Great War and the Skyrim Civil War. Despite challenges, it remains a symbol of the Empire''s strength and unity.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('forsaken_cave', 'Forsaken Cave is a medium-sized cave located west of Windhelm, inhabited by ice wraiths and draugr. ', '''and'':19B ''by'':16B ''cav'':2A,4B,10B ''draugr'':20B ''forsak'':1A,3B ''ice'':17B ''inhabit'':15B ''is'':5B ''locat'':11B ''medium'':8B ''medium-siz'':7B ''of'':13B ''siz'':9B ''west'':12B ''windhelm'':14B ''wraiths'':18B', 'pale', 'Forsaken Cave is a medium-sized cave located west of Windhelm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('volkihar', 'The Volkihar Vampire Clan is an ancient and powerful group of vampires led by Lord Harkon, located in Skyrim. Known as one of the most formidable vampire courts in the region, the Volkihar reside in Volkihar Keep, a remote castle situated on an island off the coast of Haafingar. This clan is distinguished by its ancient lineage and pure-blooded members, making it a feared presence in the realm.
', '''an'':7B,44B ''ancient'':8B,57B ''and'':9B,59B ''as'':22B ''blood'':62B ''by'':15B,55B ''castl'':41B ''clan'':5B,52B ''coast'':48B ''courts'':29B ''distinguish'':54B ''fear'':67B ''formid'':27B ''group'':11B ''haafing'':50B ''harkon'':17B ''in'':19B,30B,36B,69B ''is'':6B,53B ''island'':45B ''it'':65B ''its'':56B ''keep'':38B ''known'':21B ''led'':14B ''lineag'':58B ''locat'':18B ''lord'':16B ''making'':64B ''members'':63B ''most'':26B ''of'':12B,24B,49B ''off'':46B ''on'':43B ''one'':23B ''powerful'':10B ''presenc'':68B ''pur'':61B ''pure-blood'':60B ''realm'':71B ''region'':32B ''remot'':40B ''resid'':35B ''situat'':42B ''skyrim'':20B ''the'':2B,25B,31B,33B,47B,70B ''this'':51B ''vampir'':4B,13B,28B ''volkih'':1A,3B,34B,37B', 'vampire, dawnguard', 'The Volkihar Vampire Clan, led by Lord Harkon, is an ancient and powerful vampire group in Skyrim. Based in Volkihar Keep, a castle on an island off Haafingar''s coast, the clan is known for its pure-blooded members and fearsome reputation as one of the region''s most formidable vampire courts.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('synod', 'The Synod is one of two prominent magical organizations that arose following the dissolution of the Mages Guild at the start of the Fourth Era, the other being the College of Whispers. The Synod is known for its more restrictive approach to magical knowledge and its rivalry with the College of Whispers. Unlike its rival, the Synod has continued the Mages Guild’s ban on necromancy and has imposed restrictions on certain forms of conjuration. The organization places significant emphasis on controlling access to knowledge, with members needing to pay dues and work within the organization for years to gain access to advanced spells.', '''access'':84B,102B ''advanc'':104B ''and'':46B,68B,93B ''approach'':42B ''aros'':12B ''at'':20B ''ban'':65B ''being'':29B ''certain'':73B ''colleg'':31B,51B ''conjuration'':76B ''continu'':60B ''controlling'':83B ''dissolution'':15B ''dues'':92B ''emphasis'':81B ''following'':13B ''for'':38B,98B ''forms'':74B ''fourth'':25B ''gain'':101B ''guild'':19B,63B ''impos'':70B ''is'':4B,36B ''its'':39B,47B,55B ''knowledg'':45B,86B ''known'':37B ''mag'':18B,62B ''magical'':9B,44B ''members'':88B ''mor'':40B ''necromancy'':67B ''needing'':89B ''of'':6B,16B,23B,32B,52B,75B ''on'':66B,72B,82B ''one'':5B ''organization'':78B,97B ''organizations'':10B ''other'':28B ''pay'':91B ''plac'':79B ''prominent'':8B ''restrictions'':71B ''restrictiv'':41B ''rival'':56B ''rivalry'':48B ''s'':64B ''significant'':80B ''spells'':105B ''start'':22B ''synod'':1A,3B,35B,58B ''that'':11B ''the'':2B,14B,17B,21B,24B,27B,30B,34B,50B,57B,61B,77B,96B ''to'':43B,85B,90B,100B,103B ''two'':7B ''unlik'':54B ''whispers'':33B,53B ''with'':49B,87B ''within'':95B ''work'':94B ''years'':99B', 'collegeofwinterhold, imperial, legion', 'The Synod is a magical organization formed after the dissolution of the Mages Guild, rivaling the College of Whispers. Known for its restrictive approach, the Synod bans necromancy and limits some forms of conjuration. It emphasizes control over magical knowledge, requiring members to pay dues and work for years to access advanced spells.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nord_hero_arrow', 'Nord Hero Arrow is an arrow that deals great damage. 
Its visual design is clean and refined, with a pale wooden shaft, a sharp, steel-like arrowhead, and smooth, symmetrical fletching. It can not be crafted but found on powerful Draugr.', '''an'':8B ''and'':19B,32B ''arrow'':3A,6B,9B ''arrowh'':31B ''be'':39B ''but'':41B ''can'':37B ''cle'':18B ''craft'':40B ''damag'':13B ''deals'':11B ''design'':16B ''draugr'':45B ''fletching'':35B ''found'':42B ''great'':12B ''her'':2A,5B ''is'':7B,17B ''it'':36B ''its'':14B ''lik'':30B ''nord'':1A,4B ''not'':38B ''on'':43B ''pal'':23B ''powerful'':44B ''refin'':20B ''shaft'':25B ''sharp'':27B ''smooth'':33B ''steel'':29B ''steel-lik'':28B ''symmetrical'':34B ''that'':10B ''visual'':15B ''with'':21B ''wood'':24B', 'blacksmith', 'Nord Hero Arrow is an arrow that deals great damage. 
Its visual design is clean and refined, with a pale wooden shaft, a sharp, steel-like arrowhead, and smooth, symmetrical fletching. It can not be crafted but found on powerful Draugr.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stormcloaks', 'The Stormcloaks are a rebel faction in Skyrim, led by Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak of Windhelm. They seek to overthrow the Imperial Legion''s control over Skyrim and establish it as an independent kingdom, free from the influence of the Empire. Their rebellion was sparked by the Empire''s enforcement of the White-Gold Concordat, particularly the ban on Talos worship, which the Nords view as an affront to their traditions and sovereignty. The Stormcloaks aim to restore Skyrim’s ancient customs and resist what they see as Imperial and Thalmor oppression.

Most of the eastern regions of Skyrim are under Stormcloak control, including their stronghold in Windhelm. The central hold of Whiterun remains a strategic focus for both sides, though it starts as neutral but friendly to Imperial interests. The conflict between the Stormcloaks and the Imperial Legion divides Skyrim, with towns, cities, and holds aligning with one side or the other as the civil war progresses. The faction''s ultimate goal is to install Ulfric as High King of an independent Skyrim.', '''affront'':69B ''aim'':77B ''aligning'':148B ''an'':32B,68B,173B ''ancient'':82B ''and'':28B,73B,84B,91B,137B,146B ''are'':4B,101B ''as'':31B,67B,89B,125B,155B,169B ''ban'':59B ''betw'':134B ''both'':120B ''but'':127B ''by'':11B,46B ''central'':111B ''citi'':145B ''civil'':157B ''concordat'':56B ''conflict'':133B ''control'':25B,104B ''customs'':83B ''divid'':141B ''eastern'':97B ''empir'':41B,48B ''enforcement'':50B ''establish'':29B ''faction'':7B,161B ''focus'':118B ''for'':119B ''fre'':35B ''friendly'':128B ''from'':36B ''goal'':164B ''gold'':55B ''high'':170B ''hold'':112B ''holds'':147B ''imperial'':22B,90B,130B,139B ''in'':8B,108B ''including'':105B ''independent'':33B,174B ''influenc'':38B ''install'':167B ''interests'':131B ''is'':165B ''it'':30B,123B ''jarl'':12B ''king'':171B ''kingdom'':34B ''led'':10B ''legion'':23B,140B ''most'':94B ''neutral'':126B ''nords'':65B ''of'':15B,39B,51B,95B,99B,113B,172B ''on'':60B ''one'':150B ''oppression'':93B ''or'':152B ''other'':154B ''over'':26B ''overthrow'':20B ''particularly'':57B ''progress'':159B ''rebel'':6B ''rebellion'':43B ''regions'':98B ''remains'':115B ''resist'':85B ''restor'':79B ''s'':24B,49B,81B,162B ''see'':88B ''seek'':18B ''sid'':121B,151B ''skyrim'':9B,27B,80B,100B,142B,175B ''sovereignty'':74B ''spark'':45B ''starts'':124B ''stormcloak'':14B,103B ''stormcloaks'':1A,3B,76B,136B ''strategic'':117B ''stronghold'':107B ''tal'':61B ''thalmor'':92B ''the'':2B,21B,37B,40B,42B,47B,52B,58B,64B,71B,75B,96B,106B,110B,132B,135B,138B,153B,156B,160B ''they'':17B,87B ''though'':122B ''to'':19B,70B,78B,129B,166B ''towns'':144B ''traditions'':72B ''ulfric'':13B,168B ''ultimat'':163B ''under'':102B ''view'':66B ''war'':158B ''was'':44B ''what'':86B ''which'':63B ''whit'':54B ''white-gold'':53B ''whiterun'':114B ''windhelm'':16B,109B ''with'':143B,149B ''worship'':62B', 'stormcloak, nord, noble', '
The Stormcloaks, led by Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak of Windhelm, are a rebel faction in Skyrim fighting for independence from the Empire. Their rebellion arose from opposition to the White-Gold Concordat, particularly the ban on Talos worship, which they see as an attack on Nordic traditions. Controlling much of eastern Skyrim, the Stormcloaks aim to install Ulfric as High King and establish Skyrim as a sovereign kingdom free from Imperial and Thalmor influence. The civil war divides Skyrim, with holds and cities choosing sides in the conflict.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bards_college', '
The Bards College is a prestigious institution located in Solitude, dedicated to the arts of music, poetry, and storytelling. Aspiring bards from across Skyrim come to the college to train in the skills of song and tale-telling. It is situated near Proudspire Manor and the Blue Palace within the city. Its influence extends throughout Skyrim, with many of the province’s bards having trained there.', '''across'':25B ''and'':20B,38B,48B ''arts'':16B ''aspiring'':22B ''bards'':1A,4B,23B,66B ''blu'':50B ''city'':54B ''colleg'':2A,5B,30B ''com'':27B ''dedicat'':13B ''extends'':57B ''from'':24B ''having'':67B ''in'':11B,33B ''influenc'':56B ''institution'':9B ''is'':6B,43B ''it'':42B ''its'':55B ''locat'':10B ''manor'':47B ''many'':61B ''music'':18B ''near'':45B ''of'':17B,36B,62B ''palac'':51B ''poetry'':19B ''prestigious'':8B ''proudspir'':46B ''provinc'':64B ''s'':65B ''situat'':44B ''skills'':35B ''skyrim'':26B,59B ''solitud'':12B ''song'':37B ''storytelling'':21B ''tal'':40B ''tale-telling'':39B ''telling'':41B ''the'':3B,15B,29B,34B,49B,53B,63B ''ther'':69B ''throughout'':58B ''to'':14B,28B,31B ''train'':32B,68B ''with'':60B ''within'':52B', 'bard, noble', 'The Bards College, located in Solitude near Proudspire Manor and the Blue Palace, is a renowned institution dedicated to music, poetry, and storytelling. Aspiring bards from across Skyrim come to train in the art of song and tale-telling, making the college a key influence on Skyrim''s cultural traditions.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tribunal_temple', 'The Tribunal Temple was the dominant religion of the Dunmer in Morrowind, centered around the worship of three god-like figures: Almalexia, Sotha Sil, and Vivec, collectively known as the Tribunal or Almsivi. The Temple played a key role in the defense of Morrowind, particularly through the creation of the Ghostfence, a magical barrier designed to contain the Blight spreading from Red Mountain. Strong ties existed between the Temple and the Dunmer Great Houses, especially House Indoril and House Redoran, who actively supported the Tribunal and its religious order, including its military arm, the Ordinators.

Following the collapse of the Tribunal and the events of the Red Year, the Temple reformed into what became known as the New Temple, abandoning the worship of the Tribunal and returning to the veneration of the Dunmer''s ancestral faith, focusing on the "Three Good Daedra": Azura, Mephala, and Boethiah. However, some heretical groups continued to secretly worship the Tribunal, even building hidden temples such as Ashfall''s Tear on Solstheim. These underground cults were considered illegal by the New Temple and faced persecution for their beliefs.', '''abandoning'':123B ''actively'':85B ''almalexi'':25B ''almsivi'':36B ''ancestral'':138B ''and'':28B,73B,81B,89B,105B,129B,148B,181B ''arm'':96B ''around'':16B ''as'':32B,119B,165B ''ashfall'':166B ''azur'':146B ''barri'':57B ''becam'':117B ''beliefs'':186B ''betw'':70B ''blight'':62B ''boethiah'':149B ''building'':161B ''by'':177B ''center'':15B ''collaps'':101B ''collectively'':30B ''consider'':175B ''contain'':60B ''continu'':154B ''creation'':51B ''cults'':173B ''daedr'':145B ''defens'':45B ''design'':58B ''dominant'':8B ''dunm'':12B,75B,136B ''especially'':78B ''even'':160B ''events'':107B ''exist'':69B ''fac'':182B ''faith'':139B ''figur'':24B ''focusing'':140B ''following'':99B ''for'':184B ''from'':64B ''ghostfenc'':54B ''god'':22B ''god-lik'':21B ''good'':144B ''great'':76B ''groups'':153B ''heretical'':152B ''hidd'':162B ''hous'':77B,79B,82B ''howev'':150B ''illegal'':176B ''in'':13B,43B ''including'':93B ''indoril'':80B ''into'':115B ''its'':90B,94B ''key'':41B ''known'':31B,118B ''lik'':23B ''magical'':56B ''mephal'':147B ''military'':95B ''morrowind'':14B,47B ''mountain'':66B ''new'':121B,179B ''of'':10B,19B,46B,52B,102B,108B,126B,134B ''on'':141B,169B ''or'':35B ''order'':92B ''ordinators'':98B ''particularly'':48B ''persecution'':183B ''play'':39B ''red'':65B,110B ''redor'':83B ''reform'':114B ''religion'':9B ''religious'':91B ''returning'':130B ''rol'':42B ''s'':137B,167B ''secretly'':156B ''sil'':27B ''solstheim'':170B ''som'':151B ''soth'':26B ''spreading'':63B ''strong'':67B ''such'':164B ''support'':86B ''tear'':168B ''templ'':2A,5B,38B,72B,113B,122B,163B,180B ''the'':3B,7B,11B,17B,33B,37B,44B,50B,53B,61B,71B,74B,87B,97B,100B,103B,106B,109B,112B,120B,124B,127B,132B,135B,142B,158B,178B,185B ''thes'':171B ''thre'':20B,143B ''through'':49B ''ties'':68B ''to'':59B,131B,155B ''tribunal'':1A,4B,34B,88B,104B,128B,159B ''underground'':172B ''veneration'':133B ''vivec'':29B ''was'':6B ''wer'':174B ''what'':116B ''who'':84B ''worship'':18B,125B,157B ''year'':111B', 'darkelf', 'The Tribunal Temple was the primary religion of the Dunmer in Morrowind, worshiping the god-like Tribunal: Almalexia, Sotha Sil, and Vivec. It was central to Dunmer society, defending Morrowind through efforts like the Ghostfence and maintaining ties with Great Houses like Indoril and Redoran. After the Tribunal''s fall and the Red Year, it reformed into the New Temple, returning to the ancestral worship of Azura, Mephala, and Boethiah. Despite this shift, underground groups continued to secretly venerate the Tribunal, facing persecution from the New Temple.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('blades', 'The Blades are an elite organization originally formed from the Akaviri Dragonguard, tasked with protecting and serving the Dragonborn emperors of Tamriel. Their origins trace back to the Reman Dynasty, where they began as the personal bodyguard of Emperor Reman I. Over time, the Blades expanded into an Imperial intelligence network, operating in secret as spies, diplomats, and military leaders. They played key roles in shaping major events across Tamriel, such as the reassembly of Numidium and the defeat of Dagoth Ur. The Blades are best known for their loyalty to the Dragonborn emperors, including their service to Tiber Septim and Uriel Septim VII.

With the rise of the Aldmeri Dominion and the outbreak of the Great War, the Blades were disbanded and targeted for elimination by the Thalmor. Many Blades were hunted down and killed, and the organization went into hiding. Their headquarters, such as the famous Cloud Ruler Temple, became sacred sites, and their members continued to operate in secret, awaiting the arrival of a new Dragonborn to serve.', '''across'':70B ''akaviri'':12B ''aldmeri'':111B ''an'':5B,49B ''and'':17B,59B,78B,102B,113B,124B,136B,138B,156B ''are'':4B,86B ''arrival'':166B ''as'':35B,56B,73B,147B ''awaiting'':164B ''back'':27B ''becam'':153B ''beg'':34B ''best'':87B ''blad'':1A,3B,46B,85B,121B,132B ''bodyguard'':38B ''by'':128B ''cloud'':150B ''continu'':159B ''dagoth'':82B ''defeat'':80B ''diplomats'':58B ''disband'':123B ''dominion'':112B ''down'':135B ''dragonborn'':20B,94B,170B ''dragonguard'':13B ''dynasty'':31B ''elimination'':127B ''elit'':6B ''emperor'':40B ''emperors'':21B,95B ''events'':69B ''expand'':47B ''famous'':149B ''for'':89B,126B ''form'':9B ''from'':10B ''great'':118B ''headquarters'':145B ''hiding'':143B ''hunt'':134B ''i'':42B ''imperial'':50B ''in'':54B,66B,162B ''including'':96B ''intelligenc'':51B ''into'':48B,142B ''key'':64B ''kill'':137B ''known'':88B ''leaders'':61B ''loyalty'':91B ''major'':68B ''many'':131B ''members'':158B ''military'':60B ''network'':52B ''new'':169B ''numidium'':77B ''of'':22B,39B,76B,81B,109B,116B,167B ''operat'':161B ''operating'':53B ''organization'':7B,140B ''originally'':8B ''origins'':25B ''outbreak'':115B ''over'':43B ''personal'':37B ''play'':63B ''protecting'':16B ''reassembly'':75B ''rem'':30B,41B ''ris'':108B ''rol'':65B ''rul'':151B ''sacr'':154B ''secret'':55B,163B ''septim'':101B,104B ''serv'':172B ''servic'':98B ''serving'':18B ''shaping'':67B ''sit'':155B ''spi'':57B ''such'':72B,146B ''tamriel'':23B,71B ''target'':125B ''task'':14B ''templ'':152B ''thalmor'':130B ''the'':2B,11B,19B,24B,29B,36B,45B,74B,79B,84B,90B,93B,97B,107B,110B,114B,117B,120B,129B,139B,144B,148B,157B,165B ''they'':33B,62B ''tib'':100B ''tim'':44B ''to'':28B,92B,99B,160B,171B ''trac'':26B ''ur'':83B ''uriel'':103B ''vii'':105B ''war'':119B ''went'':141B ''wer'':122B,133B ''wher'':32B ''with'':15B,106B', 'imperial, legion, esbern, delphine', 'The Blades, originally formed from the Akaviri Dragonguard, were an elite group dedicated to serving and protecting the Dragonborn emperors of Tamriel. Initially bodyguards to Emperor Reman I, they evolved into a secretive intelligence network, playing crucial roles in Tamriel''s history. Known for their loyalty to the Dragonborn, they served figures like Tiber Septim and Uriel Septim VII. Disbanded after the Great War and persecuted by the Thalmor, the Blades went into hiding and have not been seen since.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('blood_horkers', 'The Blood Horkers are a notorious group of pirates operating in the Sea of Ghosts under the command of a battlemage named Haldyn. Known for their ruthless raids along the northern coastline of Tamriel, they have exploited the chaos of the Civil War in Skyrim to intensify their attacks without fear of reprisal from the major factions. The group has a secret stronghold, Japhet''s Folly, where Haldyn employs powerful magic to shroud the island in fog, ensuring its location remains hidden.', '''along'':31B ''are'':6B ''attacks'':51B ''battlemag'':23B ''blood'':1A,4B ''cha'':41B ''civil'':44B ''coastlin'':34B ''command'':20B ''employs'':71B ''ensuring'':80B ''exploit'':39B ''factions'':59B ''fear'':53B ''fog'':79B ''folly'':68B ''for'':27B ''from'':56B ''ghosts'':17B ''group'':9B,61B ''haldyn'':25B,70B ''hav'':38B ''hidd'':84B ''horkers'':2A,5B ''in'':13B,46B,78B ''intensify'':49B ''island'':77B ''its'':81B ''japhet'':66B ''known'':26B ''location'':82B ''magic'':73B ''major'':58B ''nam'':24B ''northern'':33B ''notorious'':8B ''of'':10B,16B,21B,35B,42B,54B ''operating'':12B ''pirat'':11B ''powerful'':72B ''raids'':30B ''remains'':83B ''reprisal'':55B ''ruthless'':29B ''s'':67B ''secret'':64B ''shroud'':75B ''skyrim'':47B ''stronghold'':65B ''tamriel'':36B ''the'':3B,14B,19B,28B,32B,40B,43B,50B,57B,60B,76B ''they'':37B ''to'':48B,74B ''under'':18B ''war'':45B ''wher'':69B ''without'':52B', 'eastmarch, sailor, thief', 'The Blood Horkers are a ruthless pirate group led by the battlemage Haldyn, operating in the Sea of Ghosts. Exploiting Skyrim''s Civil War, they conduct raids along Tamriel''s northern coast. ', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chitin_armor', 'Chitin Armor is a basic chitin chest piece with good protection quality. Its visual design is organic and jagged, with dark, shell-like plates and a rough, natural texture. To craft it: 2 leather, 1 iron ingot and 5 chitin at a blacksmith forge.  An Adept smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using chitin at a workbench.', '''1'':38B ''2'':36B ''5'':42B ''adept'':49B ''an'':48B ''and'':20B,28B,41B ''armor'':2A,4B ''at'':44B,61B ''basic'':7B ''be'':56B ''blacksmith'':46B ''by'':58B ''can'':51B,55B ''chest'':9B ''chitin'':1A,3B,8B,43B,60B ''craft'':34B,52B ''dark'':23B ''design'':17B ''forg'':47B ''good'':12B ''ingot'':40B ''iron'':39B ''is'':5B,18B ''it'':35B,53B,54B ''its'':15B ''jagg'':21B ''leath'':37B ''lik'':26B ''natural'':31B ''organic'':19B ''piec'':10B ''plat'':27B ''protection'':13B ''quality'':14B ''rough'':30B ''shell'':25B ''shell-lik'':24B ''smith'':50B ''tempered/improved'':57B ''textur'':32B ''to'':33B ''using'':59B ''visual'':16B ''with'':11B,22B ''workbench'':63B', 'blacksmith', 'Chitin Armor is a basic chitin chest piece with good protection quality. Its visual design is organic and jagged, with dark, shell-like plates and a rough, natural texture. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('forsworn', '
The Forsworn, also known as the Madmen of the Reach, are a faction of insurgent Reachmen who claim to be the rightful rulers of the Reach in western Skyrim. Their rebellion began after the Markarth Incident in 4E 176, when the Empire, distracted by the Great War, left the region vulnerable. The Reachmen briefly took control of Markarth but were ousted by a Nord militia led by Ulfric Stormcloak. Following this, the surviving Reachmen fled into the wilderness, forming the Forsworn, a guerrilla faction committed to driving out the Nords and restoring their independence.

The Forsworn are known for their primitive, tribal appearance and society, with their warriors clad in fur, feathers, and bones. They follow hagravens, matriarchal witches who perform dark rituals, including the creation of Briarhearts—Forsworn warriors who undergo a ritual where their hearts are replaced by Briar Hearts, giving them unnatural strength. The Forsworn reject all attempts at peace, instead waging a relentless campaign of violence against Nords and the Empire, seeking vengeance for their lost land.', '''176'':40B ''4e'':39B ''after'':34B ''against'':162B ''all'':151B ''also'':4B ''and'':92B,105B,114B,164B ''appearanc'':104B ''are'':12B,98B,139B ''as'':6B ''at'':153B ''attempts'':152B ''be'':21B ''beg'':33B ''bon'':115B ''bri'':142B ''briarhearts'':129B ''briefly'':55B ''but'':60B ''by'':45B,63B,68B,141B ''campaign'':159B ''clad'':110B ''claim'':19B ''committ'':86B ''control'':57B ''creation'':127B ''dark'':123B ''distract'':44B ''driving'':88B ''empir'':43B,166B ''faction'':14B,85B ''feathers'':113B ''fled'':76B ''follow'':117B ''following'':71B ''for'':100B,169B ''forming'':80B ''forsworn'':1A,3B,82B,97B,130B,149B ''fur'':112B ''giving'':144B ''great'':47B ''guerrill'':84B ''hagravens'':118B ''hearts'':138B,143B ''in'':28B,38B,111B ''incident'':37B ''including'':125B ''independenc'':95B ''inste'':155B ''insurgent'':16B ''into'':77B ''known'':5B,99B ''land'':172B ''led'':67B ''left'':49B ''lost'':171B ''madm'':8B ''markarth'':36B,59B ''matriarchal'':119B ''militi'':66B ''nord'':65B ''nords'':91B,163B ''of'':9B,15B,25B,58B,128B,160B ''oust'':62B ''out'':89B ''peac'':154B ''perform'':122B ''primitiv'':102B ''reach'':11B,27B ''reachm'':17B,54B,75B ''rebellion'':32B ''region'':51B ''reject'':150B ''relentless'':158B ''replac'':140B ''restoring'':93B ''rightful'':23B ''ritual'':135B ''rituals'':124B ''rulers'':24B ''seeking'':167B ''skyrim'':30B ''society'':106B ''stormcloak'':70B ''strength'':147B ''surviving'':74B ''the'':2B,7B,10B,22B,26B,31B,35B,42B,46B,50B,53B,73B,78B,81B,90B,94B,96B,101B,108B,126B,137B,148B,165B,170B ''them'':145B ''they'':116B ''this'':72B ''to'':20B,87B ''took'':56B ''tribal'':103B ''ulfric'':69B ''underg'':133B ''unnatural'':146B ''vengeanc'':168B ''violenc'':161B ''vulner'':52B ''waging'':156B ''war'':48B ''warriors'':109B,131B ''wer'':61B ''western'':29B ''when'':41B ''wher'':136B ''who'':18B,121B,132B ''wilderness'':79B ''witch'':120B ''with'':107B', 'forsworn, witch', '
The Forsworn, also called the Madmen of the Reach, are a faction of Reachmen fighting to reclaim the Reach in western Skyrim. Their rebellion began after the Markarth Incident in 4E 176, when they were ousted by Ulfric Stormcloak''s militia. Living in the wilderness, they formed a guerrilla faction, known for their tribal society and allegiance to hagravens, who conduct dark rituals like creating Briarhearts. Rejecting peace, the Forsworn wage a violent campaign against Nords and the Empire to restore their independence.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('greybeards', 'The Greybeards are a reclusive and ancient order of monks who reside at High Hrothgar, a monastery on the slopes of the Throat of the World, the highest mountain in Skyrim. They are masters of the Voice, or Thu''um, a form of powerful speech that can be used as a weapon. Founded by Jurgen Windcaller after the Battle of Red Mountain, the Greybeards follow the Way of the Voice, a philosophy that advocates peaceful meditation and the belief that the power of the Thu''um should only be used in times of "True Need." They dedicate their lives to spiritual study and silence, with the only exception being their reverence for the gods, which they express through their shouts.', '''advocat'':75B ''after'':58B ''ancient'':8B ''and'':7B,78B,104B ''are'':4B,34B ''as'':51B ''at'':14B ''battl'':60B ''be'':49B,90B ''being'':110B ''belief'':80B ''by'':55B ''can'':48B ''dedicat'':98B ''exception'':109B ''express'':118B ''follow'':66B ''for'':113B ''form'':43B ''found'':54B ''gods'':115B ''greybeards'':1A,3B,65B ''high'':15B ''highest'':29B ''hrothg'':16B ''in'':31B,92B ''jurg'':56B ''liv'':100B ''masters'':35B ''meditation'':77B ''monastery'':18B ''monks'':11B ''mountain'':30B,63B ''need'':96B ''of'':10B,22B,25B,36B,44B,61B,69B,84B,94B ''on'':19B ''only'':89B,108B ''or'':39B ''order'':9B ''peaceful'':76B ''philosophy'':73B ''pow'':83B ''powerful'':45B ''reclusiv'':6B ''red'':62B ''resid'':13B ''reverenc'':112B ''should'':88B ''shouts'':121B ''silenc'':105B ''skyrim'':32B ''slop'':21B ''speech'':46B ''spiritual'':102B ''study'':103B ''that'':47B,74B,81B ''the'':2B,20B,23B,26B,28B,37B,59B,64B,67B,70B,79B,82B,85B,99B,107B,111B,114B,120B ''they'':33B,97B,117B ''throat'':24B ''through'':119B ''thu'':40B,86B ''tim'':93B ''to'':101B ''tru'':95B ''um'':41B,87B ''used'':50B,91B ''voic'':38B,71B ''way'':68B ''weapon'':53B ''which'':116B ''who'':12B ''windcall'':57B ''with'':106B ''world'':27B', 'nord, dragon, noble', 'The Greybeards are an ancient order of monks living at High Hrothgar on Skyrim''s Throat of the World. Masters of the Thu''um, or Voice, they follow the Way of the Voice, a philosophy of peaceful meditation advocating the Thu''um''s use only in times of "True Need." Founded by Jurgen Windcaller, they lead lives of spiritual study and silence, breaking it only to express reverence for the gods through their shouts.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('brook_bass', 'Brook Bass are small slender grey fish commonly found in temperate lakes and rivers. They can be eaten and have a terrible taste.', '''and'':15B,21B ''are'':5B ''bass'':2A,4B ''be'':19B ''brook'':1A,3B ''can'':18B ''commonly'':10B ''eat'':20B ''fish'':9B ''found'':11B ''grey'':8B ''hav'':22B ''in'':12B ''lak'':14B ''rivers'':16B ''slend'':7B ''small'':6B ''tast'':25B ''temperat'':13B ''terribl'':24B ''they'':17B', 'fisher', 'Brook Bass are small slender grey fish. They can be eaten and have a terrible taste. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('penitus_oculatus', 'The Penitus Oculatus is an elite Imperial organization responsible for the security of the Emperor and conducting espionage and counter-intelligence operations on behalf of the Empire. Following the disbandment of the Blades, the Penitus Oculatus took over as the primary protective force for the Emperor, carrying out covert operations and, when necessary, assassinations to ensure the Empire''s stability and security. Their influence and authority extend across Imperial territories, though their main focus remains in Cyrodiil.

In Skyrim, their presence is limited, with a small outpost located in Dragon Bridge. This outpost operates primarily to safeguard Imperial interests in the province during the ongoing civil war. While they are relatively discreet, the Penitus Oculatus is a formidable force known for its loyalty to the Emperor and the Empire.', '''across'':71B ''an'':7B ''and'':18B,21B,54B,64B,68B,130B ''are'':113B ''as'':42B ''assassinations'':57B ''authority'':69B ''behalf'':27B ''blad'':36B ''bridg'':94B ''carrying'':50B ''civil'':109B ''conducting'':19B ''count'':23B ''counter-intelligenc'':22B ''covert'':52B ''cyrodiil'':80B ''disbandment'':33B ''discreet'':115B ''dragon'':93B ''during'':106B ''elit'':8B ''emperor'':17B,49B,129B ''empir'':30B,61B,132B ''ensur'':59B ''espionag'':20B ''extend'':70B ''focus'':77B ''following'':31B ''for'':12B,47B,124B ''forc'':46B,122B ''formid'':121B ''imperial'':9B,72B,101B ''in'':79B,81B,92B,103B ''influenc'':67B ''intelligenc'':24B ''interests'':102B ''is'':6B,85B,119B ''its'':125B ''known'':123B ''limit'':86B ''locat'':91B ''loyalty'':126B ''main'':76B ''necessary'':56B ''oculatus'':2A,5B,39B,118B ''of'':15B,28B,34B ''on'':26B ''ongoing'':108B ''operat'':97B ''operations'':25B,53B ''organization'':10B ''out'':51B ''outpost'':90B,96B ''over'':41B ''penitus'':1A,4B,38B,117B ''presenc'':84B ''primarily'':98B ''primary'':44B ''protectiv'':45B ''provinc'':105B ''relatively'':114B ''remains'':78B ''respons'':11B ''s'':62B ''safeguard'':100B ''security'':14B,65B ''skyrim'':82B ''small'':89B ''stability'':63B ''territori'':73B ''the'':3B,13B,16B,29B,32B,35B,37B,43B,48B,60B,66B,75B,83B,104B,107B,116B,128B,131B ''they'':112B ''this'':95B ''though'':74B ''to'':58B,99B,127B ''took'':40B ''war'':110B ''when'':55B ''whil'':111B ''with'':87B', 'imperial, legion', '
The Penitus Oculatus is an elite Imperial organization tasked with protecting the Emperor and conducting espionage to ensure the Empire''s stability. Replacing the Blades, they carry out covert operations, including assassinations, across Imperial territories. In Skyrim, they maintain a small outpost in Dragon Bridge to safeguard Imperial interests during the civil war, operating discreetly but with unwavering loyalty to the Emperor.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('psijic_order', 'The Psijic Order is the oldest monastic group in Tamriel, devoted to the study and practice of Mysticism, which they refer to as the "Old Ways." Founded on the Isle of Artaeum in the Summerset archipelago, the Psijics are highly reclusive and known for their deep understanding of magic, spirituality, and the natural forces that govern change in the world. Their members, primarily Altmer, but also select individuals from other races, are chosen for their magical abilities through a complex ritual. The Order believes in guiding the world through periods of change, considering it the most sacred force, and their counsel has often been sought by rulers, though they avoid direct involvement in politics.', '''abiliti'':79B ''also'':68B ''altmer'':66B ''and'':17B,44B,53B,101B ''archipelag'':38B ''are'':41B,74B ''artaeum'':34B ''as'':25B ''avo'':112B ''been'':106B ''believ'':86B ''but'':67B ''by'':108B ''chang'':59B,94B ''chos'':75B ''complex'':82B ''considering'':95B ''counsel'':103B ''deep'':48B ''devot'':13B ''direct'':113B ''for'':46B,76B ''forc'':56B,100B ''found'':29B ''from'':71B ''govern'':58B ''group'':10B ''guiding'':88B ''highly'':42B ''in'':11B,35B,60B,87B,115B ''individuals'':70B ''involvement'':114B ''is'':6B ''isle'':32B ''it'':96B ''known'':45B ''magic'':51B ''magical'':78B ''members'':64B ''monastic'':9B ''most'':98B ''mysticism'':20B ''natural'':55B ''of'':19B,33B,50B,93B ''often'':105B ''old'':27B ''oldest'':8B ''on'':30B ''order'':2A,5B,85B ''other'':72B ''periods'':92B ''politics'':116B ''practic'':18B ''primarily'':65B ''psijic'':1A,4B ''psijics'':40B ''rac'':73B ''reclusiv'':43B ''ref'':23B ''ritual'':83B ''rulers'':109B ''sacr'':99B ''select'':69B ''sought'':107B ''spirituality'':52B ''study'':16B ''summerset'':37B ''tamriel'':12B ''that'':57B ''the'':3B,7B,15B,26B,31B,36B,39B,47B,54B,61B,63B,77B,84B,89B,97B,102B ''they'':22B,111B ''though'':110B ''through'':80B,91B ''to'':14B,24B ''understanding'':49B ''ways'':28B ''which'':21B ''world'':62B,90B', 'psijic, highelf, scholar', 'The Psijic Order is the oldest monastic group in Tamriel, dedicated to the study of Mysticism, or the "Old Ways." Based on the Isle of Artaeum in the Summerset archipelago, the reclusive Order is renowned for its mastery of magic and spirituality. Comprised mainly of Altmer, with select members from other races, the Psijics guide the world through periods of change, a force they consider sacred, while avoiding direct political involvement.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('silver_hand', '
The Silver Hand is an organized group of criminals, originally formed as werewolf hunters. Over time, however, their purpose became corrupted, and they now engage in indiscriminate violence, targeting anyone they perceive as enemies. Their actions are often brutal, with a history of capturing, torturing, and killing civilians.', '''actions'':38B ''an'':7B ''and'':24B,48B ''anyon'':32B ''are'':39B ''as'':14B,35B ''becam'':22B ''brutal'':41B ''capturing'':46B ''civilians'':50B ''corrupt'':23B ''criminals'':11B ''enemi'':36B ''engag'':27B ''form'':13B ''group'':9B ''hand'':2A,5B ''history'':44B ''howev'':19B ''hunters'':16B ''in'':28B ''indiscriminat'':29B ''is'':6B ''killing'':49B ''now'':26B ''of'':10B,45B ''often'':40B ''organiz'':8B ''originally'':12B ''over'':17B ''perceiv'':34B ''purpos'':21B ''silv'':1A,4B ''targeting'':31B ''the'':3B,20B,37B ''they'':25B,33B ''tim'':18B ''torturing'':47B ''violenc'':30B ''werewolf'':15B ''with'':42B', 'companions, werewolf', 'The Silver Hand is a criminal group that originated as werewolf hunters but became corrupted over time. They now engage in indiscriminate violence, often using brutal tactics such as capturing, torturing, and killing civilians, targeting anyone they consider an enemy.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skaal', 'The Skaal are a distinct tribe of Nords residing in northeastern Solstheim, known for their strong connection to the land and their self-sufficient way of life. Their village, located along the Felsaad Coast near Lake Fjalding, is home to a hospitable people who welcome strangers without suspicion. The Skaal believe that Solstheim was once part of Skyrim and became an island following a great conflict between Dragon Cult loyalists, from whom they claim descent, and rebels. Their isolation allowed them to form a unique culture over time, one rooted in oral traditions and a deep spiritual bond with the natural world.

The Skaal''s way of life revolves around their environment, as they rely solely on the land for their needs and rarely engage in trade with outsiders. Their history includes a splinter group, led by Hrothmund the Red, that founded Thirsk Mead Hall to return to the old ways of unrestrained hunting and combat. In the Fourth Era, the Skaal faced challenges as the aftermath of the Red Year led to ashfall from Red Mountain, which poisoned the land and drove desperate wildlife into their territory. Despite these hardships, the Skaal maintain their traditions and strong sense of community.', '''aftermath'':169B ''allow'':82B ''along'':33B ''an'':63B ''and'':22B,61B,78B,96B,125B,157B,184B,199B ''are'':4B ''around'':112B ''as'':115B,167B ''ashfall'':176B ''becam'':62B ''believ'':53B ''betw'':69B ''bond'':100B ''by'':139B ''challeng'':166B ''claim'':76B ''coast'':36B ''combat'':158B ''community'':203B ''conflict'':68B ''connection'':18B ''cult'':71B ''cultur'':88B ''deep'':98B ''descent'':77B ''desperat'':186B ''despit'':191B ''distinct'':6B ''dragon'':70B ''drov'':185B ''engag'':127B ''environment'':114B ''fac'':165B ''fels'':35B ''fjalding'':39B ''following'':65B ''for'':15B,122B ''form'':85B ''found'':144B ''fourth'':161B ''from'':73B,177B ''great'':67B ''group'':137B ''hall'':147B ''hardships'':193B ''history'':133B ''hom'':41B ''hospit'':44B ''hrothmund'':140B ''hunting'':156B ''in'':11B,93B,128B,159B ''includ'':134B ''into'':188B ''is'':40B ''island'':64B ''isolation'':81B ''known'':14B ''lak'':38B ''land'':21B,121B,183B ''led'':138B,174B ''lif'':29B,110B ''locat'':32B ''loyalists'':72B ''maintain'':196B ''mead'':146B ''mountain'':179B ''natural'':103B ''near'':37B ''needs'':124B ''nords'':9B ''northeastern'':12B ''of'':8B,28B,59B,109B,154B,170B,202B ''old'':152B ''on'':119B ''once'':57B ''one'':91B ''oral'':94B ''outsiders'':131B ''over'':89B ''part'':58B ''peopl'':45B ''poison'':181B ''rarely'':126B ''rebels'':79B ''red'':142B,172B,178B ''rely'':117B ''residing'':10B ''return'':149B ''revolv'':111B ''root'':92B ''s'':107B ''self'':25B ''self-sufficient'':24B ''sens'':201B ''skaal'':1A,3B,52B,106B,164B,195B ''skyrim'':60B ''solely'':118B ''solstheim'':13B,55B ''spiritual'':99B ''splint'':136B ''strangers'':48B ''strong'':17B,200B ''sufficient'':26B ''suspicion'':50B ''territory'':190B ''that'':54B,143B ''the'':2B,16B,20B,23B,30B,34B,51B,80B,102B,105B,113B,120B,123B,132B,141B,151B,160B,163B,168B,171B,182B,189B,194B,197B ''them'':83B ''thes'':192B ''they'':75B,116B ''thirsk'':145B ''tim'':90B ''to'':19B,42B,84B,148B,150B,175B ''trad'':129B ''traditions'':95B,198B ''trib'':7B ''uniqu'':87B ''unrestrain'':155B ''villag'':31B ''was'':56B ''way'':27B,108B ''ways'':153B ''welcom'':47B ''which'':180B ''who'':46B ''whom'':74B ''wildlif'':187B ''with'':101B,130B ''without'':49B ''world'':104B ''year'':173B', 'solstheim, scholar', '
The Skaal are a tribe of Nords living in northeastern Solstheim, near Lake Fjalding, known for their deep spiritual bond with the land and self-sufficient lifestyle. Believing Solstheim was once part of Skyrim, their culture, rooted in oral traditions, formed through centuries of isolation. They rely solely on the land, rarely trading with outsiders, and uphold strong community ties. ', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('earth_stone', 'The Earth Stone is one of the All-Maker Stones located on Solstheim, situated southwest of Raven Rock. This sacred site is deeply tied to the Skaal''s spiritual beliefs and their worship of the All-Maker.', '''all'':11B,40B ''all-mak'':10B,39B ''and'':34B ''beliefs'':33B ''deeply'':26B ''earth'':1A,4B ''is'':6B,25B ''locat'':14B ''mak'':12B,41B ''of'':8B,19B,37B ''on'':15B ''one'':7B ''rav'':20B ''rock'':21B ''s'':31B ''sacr'':23B ''sit'':24B ''situat'':17B ''skaal'':30B ''solstheim'':16B ''southwest'':18B ''spiritual'':32B ''ston'':2A,5B,13B ''the'':3B,9B,29B,35B,38B ''this'':22B ''tied'':27B ''to'':28B ''worship'':36B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('high_elf', 'The Altmer, commonly known as High Elves, are a tall, golden-skinned race originating from the Summerset Isles. Renowned for their mastery of the arcane arts, they are considered the most gifted in magic among all races of Tamriel. The Altmer possess long lifespans, living two to three times longer than humans, which allows them to dedicate many years to the study of magic and scholarly pursuits. Known for their intelligence and cultured way of life, the Altmer have contributed greatly to Tamriel''s language, laws, arts, and sciences, with much of the Empire’s customs derived from their traditions.

Despite their contributions, the Altmer are often viewed with suspicion and resentment by other races, who see them as proud, elitist, and aloof. This perception is reinforced by the Altmer''s own belief in their cultural superiority, which has caused friction between them and the other inhabitants of Tamriel. Nevertheless, the Altmer''s influence, particularly in magic and intellectual endeavors, remains a defining aspect of their legacy in the continent.', '''all'':39B ''allows'':57B ''aloof'':126B ''altmer'':4B,44B,81B,108B,133B,155B ''among'':38B ''and'':68B,75B,91B,114B,125B,147B,161B ''arcan'':28B ''are'':10B,31B,109B ''arts'':29B,90B ''as'':7B,122B ''aspect'':167B ''belief'':136B ''betw'':145B ''by'':116B,131B ''caus'':143B ''commonly'':5B ''consider'':32B ''continent'':173B ''contribut'':83B ''contributions'':106B ''cultur'':76B ''cultural'':139B ''customs'':99B ''dedicat'':60B ''defining'':166B ''deriv'':100B ''despit'':104B ''elf'':2A ''elitist'':124B ''elves'':9B ''empir'':97B ''endeavors'':163B ''for'':23B,72B ''friction'':144B ''from'':18B,101B ''gift'':35B ''gold'':14B ''golden-skinn'':13B ''greatly'':84B ''hav'':82B ''high'':1A,8B ''humans'':55B ''in'':36B,137B,159B,171B ''influenc'':157B ''inhabitants'':150B ''intellectual'':162B ''intelligenc'':74B ''is'':129B ''isles'':21B ''known'':6B,71B ''languag'':88B ''laws'':89B ''legacy'':170B ''lif'':79B ''lifespans'':47B ''living'':48B ''long'':46B,53B ''magic'':37B,67B,160B ''many'':61B ''mastery'':25B ''most'':34B ''much'':94B ''nevertheless'':153B ''of'':26B,41B,66B,78B,95B,151B,168B ''often'':110B ''originating'':17B ''other'':117B,149B ''own'':135B ''particularly'':158B ''perception'':128B ''possess'':45B ''proud'':123B ''pursuits'':70B ''rac'':16B,40B,118B ''reinforc'':130B ''remains'':164B ''renown'':22B ''resentment'':115B ''s'':87B,98B,134B,156B ''scholarly'':69B ''scienc'':92B ''see'':120B ''skinn'':15B ''study'':65B ''summerset'':20B ''superiority'':140B ''suspicion'':113B ''tall'':12B ''tamriel'':42B,86B,152B ''than'':54B ''the'':3B,19B,24B,27B,33B,43B,64B,73B,80B,96B,102B,105B,107B,132B,138B,148B,154B,169B,172B ''them'':58B,121B,146B ''they'':30B ''this'':127B ''thre'':51B ''tim'':52B ''to'':50B,59B,63B,85B ''traditions'':103B ''two'':49B ''view'':111B ''way'':77B ''which'':56B,141B ''who'':119B ''with'':93B,112B ''years'':62B', 'highelf, scholar', 'The Altmer, or High Elves, are a tall, golden-skinned race from the Summerset Isles, renowned for their unparalleled mastery of magic and intellectual pursuits. Their long lifespans enable them to excel in the arcane arts, scholarship, and culture, with much of Tamriel''s language, laws, and traditions influenced by their contributions. While admired for their achievements, they are often seen as aloof and elitist due to their belief in their cultural superiority, causing tension with other races. Despite this, their impact on magic and civilization is undeniable.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('thalmor', 'The Thalmor are the ruling government of the Third Aldmeri Dominion, a political and military alliance between the Altmer (High Elves) and Bosmer (Wood Elves). They promote a supremacist ideology, seeking to establish Mer (Elves) as racially superior to Men and to extend their control across Tamriel. By 4E 201, the Thalmor have a significant presence in Skyrim, where they enforce the White-Gold Concordat, a peace treaty signed after the Great War between the Empire and the Aldmeri Dominion. One of the treaty''s key provisions is the banning of Talos worship, a point of great contention between the Thalmor and many Nords.

In Skyrim, the Thalmor operate from their embassy in Haafingar, north of Solitude, and use Northwatch Keep as a detention center for political prisoners. Thalmor Justiciars, who act as enforcers of their policies, can often be seen traveling Skyrim''s roads, sometimes escorting prisoners. While they may not initially show hostility, questioning them about Talos or other sensitive topics can provoke aggressive responses. The Thalmor''s activities and their enforcement of the ban on Talos worship have fueled resentment among Skyrim''s populace, particularly among Stormcloak rebels who oppose both the Empire and the Dominion.', '''201'':51B ''4e'':50B ''about'':160B ''across'':47B ''act'':134B ''activiti'':173B ''after'':72B ''aggressiv'':168B ''aldmeri'':11B,81B ''allianc'':17B ''altmer'':20B ''among'':186B,191B ''and'':15B,23B,42B,79B,104B,120B,174B,199B ''are'':4B ''as'':37B,124B,135B ''ban'':179B ''banning'':92B ''be'':142B ''betw'':18B,76B,101B ''bosm'':24B ''both'':196B ''by'':49B ''can'':140B,166B ''cent'':127B ''concordat'':67B ''contention'':100B ''control'':46B ''detention'':126B ''dominion'':12B,82B,201B ''elves'':22B,26B,36B ''embassy'':114B ''empir'':78B,198B ''enforc'':62B ''enforcement'':176B ''enforcers'':136B ''escorting'':149B ''establish'':34B ''extend'':44B ''for'':128B ''from'':112B ''fuel'':184B ''gold'':66B ''government'':7B ''great'':74B,99B ''haafing'':116B ''hav'':54B,183B ''high'':21B ''hostility'':157B ''ideology'':31B ''in'':58B,107B,115B ''initially'':155B ''is'':90B ''justiciars'':132B ''keep'':123B ''key'':88B ''many'':105B ''may'':153B ''men'':41B ''mer'':35B ''military'':16B ''nords'':106B ''north'':117B ''northwatch'':122B ''not'':154B ''of'':8B,84B,93B,98B,118B,137B,177B ''often'':141B ''on'':180B ''one'':83B ''operat'':111B ''oppos'':195B ''or'':162B ''other'':163B ''particularly'':190B ''peac'':69B ''point'':97B ''polici'':139B ''political'':14B,129B ''populac'':189B ''presenc'':57B ''prisoners'':130B,150B ''promot'':28B ''provisions'':89B ''provok'':167B ''questioning'':158B ''racially'':38B ''rebels'':193B ''resentment'':185B ''respons'':169B ''roads'':147B ''ruling'':6B ''s'':87B,146B,172B,188B ''seeking'':32B ''seen'':143B ''sensitiv'':164B ''show'':156B ''sign'':71B ''significant'':56B ''skyrim'':59B,108B,145B,187B ''solitud'':119B ''sometim'':148B ''stormcloak'':192B ''superior'':39B ''supremacist'':30B ''tal'':94B,161B,181B ''tamriel'':48B ''thalmor'':1A,3B,53B,103B,110B,131B,171B ''the'':2B,5B,9B,19B,45B,52B,63B,73B,77B,80B,85B,91B,102B,109B,113B,138B,170B,175B,178B,197B,200B ''them'':159B ''they'':27B,61B,152B ''third'':10B ''to'':33B,40B,43B ''topics'':165B ''traveling'':144B ''treaty'':70B,86B ''use'':121B ''war'':75B ''wher'':60B ''whil'':151B ''whit'':65B ''white-gold'':64B ''who'':133B,194B ''wood'':25B ''worship'':95B,182B', 'thalmor, highelf, woodelf, redguard, noble', '
The Thalmor are the ruling government of the Third Aldmeri Dominion, an alliance of Altmer and Bosmer promoting elven supremacy and seeking dominance over Tamriel. By 4E 201, they enforce the White-Gold Concordat in Skyrim, including the controversial ban on Talos worship, sparking resentment among Nords, especially Stormcloak rebels. Operating from their embassy near Solitude and using Northwatch Keep as a detention center, Thalmor Justiciars patrol Skyrim''s roads, enforcing their policies and suppressing dissent.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vigil_of_stendarr', 'The Vigil of Stendarr is a devout order of holy warriors dedicated to the eradication of Daedra, vampires, werewolves, witches, and other so-called "abominations" in the name of the god Stendarr, the Divine of Mercy. Vigilants of Stendarr are often found patrolling the roads of Skyrim in their quest to rid the land of these creatures. They offer healing services, including curing diseases, to those they encounter on their travels. The order''s main base in Skyrim is the Hall of the Vigilant, located south of Dawnstar, though they also maintain a presence at Stendarr''s Beacon in The Rift.', '''abominations'':29B ''also'':95B ''and'':24B ''are'':44B ''at'':99B ''bas'':80B ''beacon'':102B ''call'':28B ''creatur'':61B ''curing'':67B ''daedr'':20B ''dawnst'':92B ''dedicat'':15B ''devout'':10B ''dis'':68B ''divin'':38B ''encount'':72B ''eradication'':18B ''found'':46B ''god'':35B ''hall'':85B ''healing'':64B ''holy'':13B ''in'':30B,52B,81B,103B ''including'':66B ''is'':8B,83B ''land'':58B ''locat'':89B ''main'':79B ''maintain'':96B ''mercy'':40B ''nam'':32B ''of'':2A,6B,12B,19B,33B,39B,42B,50B,59B,86B,91B ''offer'':63B ''often'':45B ''on'':73B ''order'':11B,77B ''other'':25B ''patrolling'':47B ''presenc'':98B ''quest'':54B ''rid'':56B ''rift'':105B ''roads'':49B ''s'':78B,101B ''servic'':65B ''skyrim'':51B,82B ''so'':27B ''so-call'':26B ''south'':90B ''stendarr'':3A,7B,36B,43B,100B ''the'':4B,17B,31B,34B,37B,48B,53B,57B,74B,76B,84B,87B,104B ''thes'':60B ''they'':62B,71B,94B ''thos'':70B ''though'':93B ''to'':16B,55B,69B ''travels'':75B ''vampir'':21B ''vigil'':1A,5B ''vigilant'':88B ''vigilants'':41B ''warriors'':14B ''werewolv'':22B ''witch'':23B', 'dawnguard, priest, daedric, daedra, noble', '
The Vigil of Stendarr is a holy order dedicated to eradicating Daedra, vampires, werewolves, witches, and other "abominations" in the name of Stendarr, the Divine of Mercy. Vigilants patrol Skyrim''s roads, offering healing services and curing diseases. Their main base, the Hall of the Vigilant, is south of Dawnstar, with an additional presence at Stendarr''s Beacon in The Rift.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('argonian', 'Argonians, known to themselves as Saxhleel or "People of the Root," are the reptilian natives of Black Marsh, a vast swampy province in southeastern Tamriel. Their unique physiology grants them a natural resistance to poison and disease, making them well-suited to their treacherous homeland. They are agile swimmers, able to breathe underwater, and are known for their skills in stealth and guerrilla warfare, which they have employed for centuries to defend their borders from invaders. Their connection to the Hist, a race of sentient trees, is central to their culture and way of life, and their alien nature often makes them seem mysterious to outsiders.

Argonians are often misunderstood and referred to derogatorily by other races as "lizards" or "beasts." They are known for their reserved and expressionless demeanor, making it difficult for other races to relate to them. Some Argonians who have left Black Marsh for other regions, such as Cyrodiil, adopt Imperial customs and names to better integrate into foreign societies. Despite their reputation for being difficult to know, those who take the time to understand Argonian culture often gain a deep respect for this resilient and noble people.', '''able'':52B ''adopt'':156B ''agil'':50B ''ali'':100B ''and'':37B,56B,64B,94B,98B,113B,130B,159B,192B ''are'':13B,49B,57B,110B,125B ''argoni'':1A,182B ''argonians'':2B,109B,144B ''as'':6B,120B,154B ''beasts'':123B ''being'':171B ''bett'':162B ''black'':18B,148B ''borders'':76B ''breath'':54B ''by'':117B ''central'':90B ''centuri'':72B ''connection'':80B ''cultur'':93B,183B ''customs'':158B ''cyrodiil'':155B ''deep'':187B ''defend'':74B ''demeanor'':132B ''derogatorily'':116B ''despit'':167B ''difficult'':135B,172B ''dis'':38B ''employ'':70B ''expressionless'':131B ''for'':59B,71B,127B,136B,150B,170B,189B ''foreign'':165B ''from'':77B ''gain'':185B ''grants'':30B ''guerrill'':65B ''hav'':69B,146B ''hist'':83B ''homeland'':47B ''imperial'':157B ''in'':24B,62B ''integrat'':163B ''into'':164B ''invaders'':78B ''is'':89B ''it'':134B ''know'':174B ''known'':3B,58B,126B ''left'':147B ''lif'':97B ''lizards'':121B ''mak'':103B ''making'':39B,133B ''marsh'':19B,149B ''misunderstood'':112B ''mysterious'':106B ''nam'':160B ''nativ'':16B ''natur'':101B ''natural'':33B ''nobl'':193B ''of'':10B,17B,86B,96B ''often'':102B,111B,184B ''or'':8B,122B ''other'':118B,137B,151B ''outsiders'':108B ''peopl'':9B,194B ''physiology'':29B ''poison'':36B ''provinc'':23B ''rac'':85B,119B,138B ''referr'':114B ''regions'':152B ''relat'':140B ''reptili'':15B ''reputation'':169B ''reserv'':129B ''resilient'':191B ''resistanc'':34B ''respect'':188B ''root'':12B ''saxhleel'':7B ''seem'':105B ''sentient'':87B ''skills'':61B ''societi'':166B ''som'':143B ''southeastern'':25B ''stealth'':63B ''such'':153B ''suit'':43B ''swampy'':22B ''swimmers'':51B ''tak'':177B ''tamriel'':26B ''the'':11B,14B,27B,45B,60B,75B,79B,82B,92B,99B,128B,168B,178B ''them'':31B,40B,104B,142B ''themselv'':5B ''they'':48B,68B,124B ''this'':190B ''thos'':175B ''tim'':179B ''to'':4B,35B,44B,53B,73B,81B,91B,107B,115B,139B,141B,161B,173B,180B ''tre'':88B ''treacherous'':46B ''understand'':181B ''underwat'':55B ''uniqu'':28B ''vast'':21B ''warfar'':66B ''way'':95B ''well'':42B ''well-suit'':41B ''which'':67B ''who'':145B,176B', 'argonian, scholar', '
Argonians, or Saxhleel, are the reptilian natives of Black Marsh, known for their natural resistance to poison and disease, their ability to breathe underwater, and their skills in stealth and guerrilla warfare. Deeply connected to the Hist, sentient trees central to their culture, Argonians are often seen as mysterious by outsiders due to their reserved demeanor. While some integrate into other societies by adopting foreign customs, those who take the time to understand them find a resilient and noble people.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('warp_in_the_west', 'The Warp in the West, also known as the Miracle of Peace or the Second Numidian Effect, was a significant event that transpired between the 9th and 11th of Frostfall in 3E 417. It was triggered by the death of King Lysandus of Daggerfall, leading to an upheaval in the regions of Hammerfell and High Rock. This phenomenon is often likened to a Dragon Break, reminiscent of the Middle Dawn from the First Era, although its effects were localized to the Iliac Bay.

Central to the Warp was the Totem of Tiber Septim, an ancient artifact that allowed its wielder to control the colossal war machine known as Numidium. An unknown hero, believed to be an agent of the Blades, acquired the Totem, igniting a fierce competition among various factions, including Sentinel, Wayrest, Daggerfall, and Orsinium, all vying for its power. Following a series of mysterious cataclysms, the political landscape of the Iliac Bay dramatically shifted from forty-four city-states to just four, all of which pledged loyalty to the Emperor. The Warp also had far-reaching consequences, with figures like Mannimarco utilizing the Totem for personal ascendance, while the Underking reclaimed his lost heart from Numidium, creating an expansive anti-magic zone around the area. Rumors persist that the Blades agent was ultimately killed in the effort to activate Numidium.', '''11th'':32B ''3e'':36B ''417'':37B ''9th'':30B ''acquir'':125B ''activat'':229B ''agent'':121B,221B ''all'':141B,171B ''allow'':102B ''also'':10B,181B ''although'':79B ''among'':132B ''an'':51B,98B,114B,120B,207B ''ancient'':99B ''and'':31B,58B,139B ''anti'':210B ''anti-magic'':209B ''are'':215B ''around'':213B ''artifact'':100B ''as'':12B,112B ''ascendanc'':196B ''bay'':87B,158B ''be'':119B ''believ'':117B ''betw'':28B ''blad'':124B,220B ''break'':69B ''by'':41B ''cataclysms'':151B ''central'':88B ''city'':166B ''city-stat'':165B ''colossal'':108B ''competition'':131B ''consequenc'':186B ''control'':106B ''creating'':206B ''daggerfall'':48B,138B ''dawn'':74B ''death'':43B ''dragon'':68B ''dramatically'':159B ''effect'':21B ''effects'':81B ''effort'':227B ''emperor'':178B ''event'':25B ''expansiv'':208B ''factions'':134B ''far'':184B ''far-reaching'':183B ''fierc'':130B ''figur'':188B ''first'':77B ''following'':146B ''for'':143B,194B ''forty'':163B ''forty-four'':162B ''four'':164B,170B ''from'':75B,161B,204B ''frostfall'':34B ''had'':182B ''hammerfell'':57B ''heart'':203B ''her'':116B ''high'':59B ''his'':201B ''igniting'':128B ''iliac'':86B,157B ''in'':2A,7B,35B,53B,225B ''including'':135B ''is'':63B ''it'':38B ''its'':80B,103B,144B ''just'':169B ''kill'':224B ''king'':45B ''known'':11B,111B ''landscap'':154B ''leading'':49B ''lik'':189B ''liken'':65B ''localiz'':83B ''lost'':202B ''loyalty'':175B ''lysandus'':46B ''machin'':110B ''magic'':211B ''mannimarc'':190B ''middl'':73B ''miracl'':14B ''mysterious'':150B ''numidi'':20B ''numidium'':113B,205B,230B ''of'':15B,33B,44B,47B,56B,71B,95B,122B,149B,155B,172B ''often'':64B ''or'':17B ''orsinium'':140B ''peac'':16B ''persist'':217B ''personal'':195B ''phenomenon'':62B ''pledg'':174B ''political'':153B ''pow'':145B ''reaching'':185B ''reclaim'':200B ''regions'':55B ''reminiscent'':70B ''rock'':60B ''rumors'':216B ''second'':19B ''sentinel'':136B ''septim'':97B ''seri'':148B ''shift'':160B ''significant'':24B ''stat'':167B ''that'':26B,101B,218B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,13B,18B,29B,42B,54B,72B,76B,85B,90B,93B,107B,123B,126B,152B,156B,177B,179B,192B,198B,214B,219B,226B ''this'':61B ''tib'':96B ''to'':50B,66B,84B,89B,105B,118B,168B,176B,228B ''totem'':94B,127B,193B ''transpir'':27B ''trigger'':40B ''ultimately'':223B ''underking'':199B ''unknown'':115B ''upheaval'':52B ''utilizing'':191B ''various'':133B ''vying'':142B ''war'':109B ''warp'':1A,6B,91B,180B ''was'':22B,39B,92B,222B ''wayrest'':137B ''wer'':82B ''west'':4A,9B ''which'':173B ''whil'':197B ''wield'':104B ''with'':187B ''zon'':212B', 'scholar, breton', '
The Warp in the West, or the Miracle of Peace, occurred between 9th and 11th Frostfall in 3E 417, reshaping the Iliac Bay region. Triggered by the death of King Lysandus and centered around the Totem of Tiber Septim, which controlled the Numidium, the event caused a Dragon Break-like phenomenon. Competing factions, including Daggerfall, Wayrest, Sentinel, and Orsinium, vied for the Totem''s power. The chaos ended with the consolidation of forty-four city-states into four loyal to the Empire. The Warp''s aftermath saw figures like Mannimarco ascending and the Underking reclaiming his heart, creating an anti-magic zone. The Blades agent instrumental in activating Numidium is rumored to have perished during the event.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ruins_edge', 'Ruin''s Edge is a unique dark bow featuring an animated eyeball above the grip. Its enchantment triggers a random effect upon use.', '''abov'':15B ''an'':12B ''animat'':13B ''bow'':10B ''dark'':9B ''edge'':2A,5B ''effect'':23B ''enchantment'':19B ''eyeball'':14B ''featuring'':11B ''grip'':17B ''is'':6B ''its'':18B ''random'':22B ''ruin'':3B ''ruins'':1A ''s'':4B ''the'':16B ''triggers'':20B ''uniqu'':8B ''upon'':24B ''use'':25B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
Ruin''s Edge is a dark bow with an animated eyeball, known for its enchantment that triggers random effects with each use.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('breton', 'Bretons are a race of both human and elven ancestry, primarily inhabiting the province of High Rock and the Systres Archipelago. Their origins stem from centuries of interbreeding between the Nedic peoples and Aldmer settlers, particularly Clan Direnni. This mixed heritage has given Bretons a natural affinity for magic, with many excelling in spellcraft, enchantment, and alchemy. Despite their human lifespans, which limit their study time compared to their elven peers, Bretons are known for their intelligence and magical resistance, making them formidable in both intellectual and combative pursuits.

Culturally, Bretons are shaped by a feudal society, with a deep-rooted obsession with nobility, status, and lineage. They have a strong tradition of knighthood and chivalry, which forms a key part of their identity. Their lands are politically fragmented, with frequent internal conflicts, but Bretons share common traditions of bardic storytelling and heroic tales. They are also known for their unique druidic roots, with some Bretons seeking to reconnect with the natural world through these ancient traditions. Overall, Bretons balance their human and elven heritage, blending aspects of both into a distinct culture that values magic, honor, and adventure.', '''adventur'':191B ''affinity'':48B ''alchemy'':58B ''aldmer'':35B ''also'':149B ''ancestry'':11B ''ancient'':168B ''and'':9B,19B,34B,57B,79B,88B,108B,117B,144B,175B,190B ''archipelag'':22B ''are'':3B,74B,93B,129B,148B ''aspects'':179B ''balanc'':172B ''bardic'':142B ''betw'':30B ''blending'':178B ''both'':7B,86B,181B ''breton'':1A ''bretons'':2B,45B,73B,92B,137B,158B,171B ''but'':136B ''by'':95B ''centuri'':27B ''chivalry'':118B ''clan'':38B ''combativ'':89B ''common'':139B ''compar'':68B ''conflicts'':135B ''cultur'':185B ''culturally'':91B ''deep'':102B ''deep-root'':101B ''despit'':59B ''direnni'':39B ''distinct'':184B ''druidic'':154B ''elven'':10B,71B,176B ''enchantment'':56B ''excelling'':53B ''feudal'':97B ''for'':49B,76B,151B ''formid'':84B ''forms'':120B ''fragment'':131B ''frequent'':133B ''from'':26B ''giv'':44B ''hav'':111B ''heritag'':42B,177B ''heroic'':145B ''high'':17B ''honor'':189B ''hum'':8B,61B,174B ''identity'':126B ''in'':54B,85B ''inhabiting'':13B ''intellectual'':87B ''intelligenc'':78B ''interbreeding'':29B ''internal'':134B ''into'':182B ''key'':122B ''knighthood'':116B ''known'':75B,150B ''lands'':128B ''lifespans'':62B ''limit'':64B ''lineag'':109B ''magic'':50B,188B ''magical'':80B ''making'':82B ''many'':52B ''mix'':41B ''natural'':47B,164B ''nedic'':32B ''nobility'':106B ''obsession'':104B ''of'':6B,16B,28B,115B,124B,141B,180B ''origins'':24B ''overall'':170B ''part'':123B ''particularly'':37B ''peers'':72B ''peopl'':33B ''politically'':130B ''primarily'':12B ''provinc'':15B ''pursuits'':90B ''rac'':5B ''reconnect'':161B ''resistanc'':81B ''rock'':18B ''root'':103B ''roots'':155B ''seeking'':159B ''settlers'':36B ''shap'':94B ''shar'':138B ''society'':98B ''som'':157B ''spellcraft'':55B ''status'':107B ''stem'':25B ''storytelling'':143B ''strong'':113B ''study'':66B ''systres'':21B ''tal'':146B ''that'':186B ''the'':14B,20B,23B,31B,60B,65B,70B,77B,125B,127B,152B,163B,173B ''them'':83B ''thes'':167B ''they'':110B,147B ''this'':40B ''through'':166B ''tim'':67B ''to'':69B,160B ''tradition'':114B ''traditions'':140B,169B ''uniqu'':153B ''valu'':187B ''which'':63B,119B ''with'':51B,99B,105B,132B,156B,162B ''world'':165B', 'breton, scholar, forsworn', '
Bretons, a race of mixed human and elven ancestry, primarily inhabit High Rock and the Systres Archipelago. Known for their natural affinity for magic and resistance to spells, they excel in spellcraft, alchemy, and enchantment. Bretons are shaped by a feudal society, emphasizing nobility, knighthood, and chivalry, with a shared tradition of bardic storytelling and heroism. Despite their politically fragmented lands, they balance their human and elven heritage, blending magic, honor, and adventure into a unique culture.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dark_elf', 'The Dunmer, also known as Dark Elves, are the grey-skinned, red-eyed elven people of Morrowind. While "Dark Elf" is the common term used by outsiders, the Dunmer and their Aldmeri kin prefer the term "Dunmer," with "dark" symbolizing their somber, shadowed history and often unfortunate fate. Known for their powerful intellects and agile physiques, Dunmer make excellent warriors and sorcerers, seamlessly blending swordplay, archery, and destructive magic in combat. Their long lifespans, often extending beyond two centuries, enable them to hone their abilities, with some of the oldest Dunmer mages living for over five hundred years or more through mystical rituals.

Dunmer society is typically seen as grim, aloof, and harsh by outsiders, who often perceive them as clannish and ruthless. Loyalty to family and clan is of utmost importance in their culture, and they have a reputation for quick tempers and a deep-seated distrust of other races. Despite these negative perceptions, Dunmer value honor, and their vengeful nature stems from a long history of betrayal and conflict. Those raised in Morrowind tend to be less approachable compared to Dunmer who have integrated into Imperial culture. Their homeland''s harsh conditions also make them more vulnerable to skin diseases, commonly referred to as "corprus," though this differs from the infamous Divine Disease of the same name.', '''abiliti'':89B ''agil'':59B ''aldmeri'':36B ''aloof'':115B ''also'':5B,200B ''and'':34B,49B,58B,65B,71B,116B,126B,131B,140B,148B,164B,175B ''approach'':185B ''archery'':70B ''are'':10B ''as'':7B,113B,124B,211B ''be'':183B ''betrayal'':174B ''beyond'':81B ''blending'':68B ''by'':30B,118B ''centuri'':83B ''clan'':132B ''clannish'':125B ''combat'':75B ''common'':27B ''commonly'':208B ''compar'':186B ''conditions'':199B ''conflict'':176B ''corprus'':212B ''cultur'':139B,194B ''dark'':1A,8B,23B,43B ''deep'':151B ''deep-seat'':150B ''despit'':157B ''destructiv'':72B ''differs'':215B ''dis'':207B,220B ''distrust'':153B ''divin'':219B ''dunm'':4B,33B,41B,61B,95B,108B,161B,188B ''elf'':2A,24B ''elven'':18B ''elves'':9B ''enabl'':84B ''excellent'':63B ''extending'':80B ''eyed'':17B ''family'':130B ''fat'':52B ''fiv'':100B ''for'':54B,98B,145B ''from'':169B,216B ''grey'':13B ''grey-skinn'':12B ''grim'':114B ''harsh'':117B,198B ''hav'':142B,190B ''history'':48B,172B ''homeland'':196B ''hon'':87B ''honor'':163B ''hundr'':101B ''imperial'':193B ''importanc'':136B ''in'':74B,137B,179B ''infamous'':218B ''integrat'':191B ''intellects'':57B ''into'':192B ''is'':25B,110B,133B ''kin'':37B ''known'':6B,53B ''less'':184B ''lifespans'':78B ''living'':97B ''long'':77B,171B ''lo