B', 'darkelf, scholar', '
The Morag Tong, an ancient assassin guild in Morrowind, operates under the patronage of Mephala, settling Great House disputes through sanctioned Honorable Writs of Execution, granting legal immunity to its assassins. Founded in the First Era, the guild is known for its precision, subtlety, and use of shortblades and chitinous-themed weaponry, reflecting Mephala''s influence. Though their power declined after events like the Red Year, they remain active in Solstheim and Morrowind, often clashing with the Dark Brotherhood, a splinter group linked to their Sithis-worshipping origins. The Morag Tong continues to embody Morrowind''s dark yet lawful traditions.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orc', 'Orcs, also known as Orsimer (meaning "Pariah Folk" in Aldmeris), are a race of elves primarily from the mountainous regions of Wrothgar, Dragontail, and Skyrim, as well as their stronghold city of Orsinium. Though they share elven ancestry, Orcs are often considered distinct from other Mer and are sometimes grouped with goblin-kin or even classified as beastfolk. Historically, Orcs were feared and regarded as savage barbarians by other races of Tamriel, but over time they have won respect, particularly for their martial prowess and skilled craftsmanship. Their armorers are among the best in Tamriel, and their warriors, known for their berserker rage, are highly valued in Imperial Legions.

Orc society is structured around strongholds and clans, each led by a chief. They follow a strict martial tradition and place great value on honor, strength, and endurance. Orcs worship Malacath, the Daedric Prince of Outcasts, whom they believe was once the elven god Trinimac before being transformed. Malacath is viewed as the protector of the Orcs, and his teachings form the foundation of their cultural and moral code. Despite their rough reputation, Orcs are a disciplined and honorable people who value fairness and justice within their communities.', '''aldmeris'':11B ''also'':3B ''among'':93B ''ancestry'':39B ''and'':25B,48B,65B,87B,98B,118B,131B,138B,169B,178B,189B,195B ''are'':12B,41B,49B,92B,106B,186B ''armorers'':91B ''around'':116B ''as'':5B,27B,29B,59B,67B,163B ''barbarians'':69B ''beastfolk'':60B ''befor'':157B ''being'':158B ''believ'':150B ''berserk'':104B ''best'':95B ''but'':75B ''by'':70B,122B ''chief'':124B ''city'':32B ''clans'':119B ''classifi'':58B ''cod'':180B ''communiti'':199B ''consider'':43B ''craftsmanship'':89B ''cultural'':177B ''daedric'':144B ''despit'':181B ''disciplin'':188B ''distinct'':44B ''dragontail'':24B ''each'':120B ''elven'':38B,154B ''elves'':16B ''enduranc'':139B ''even'':57B ''fairness'':194B ''fear'':64B ''folk'':9B ''follow'':126B ''for'':83B,102B ''form'':172B ''foundation'':174B ''from'':18B,45B ''goblin'':54B ''goblin-kin'':53B ''god'':155B ''great'':133B ''group'':51B ''hav'':79B ''highly'':107B ''his'':170B ''historically'':61B ''honor'':136B,190B ''imperial'':110B ''in'':10B,96B,109B ''is'':114B,161B ''justic'':196B ''kin'':55B ''known'':4B,101B ''led'':121B ''legions'':111B ''malacath'':142B,160B ''martial'':85B,129B ''meaning'':7B ''mer'':47B ''moral'':179B ''mountainous'':20B ''of'':15B,22B,33B,73B,146B,166B,175B ''often'':42B ''on'':135B ''once'':152B ''or'':56B ''orc'':1A,112B ''orcs'':2B,40B,62B,140B,168B,185B ''orsim'':6B ''orsinium'':34B ''other'':46B,71B ''outcasts'':147B ''over'':76B ''pariah'':8B ''particularly'':82B ''peopl'':191B ''plac'':132B ''primarily'':17B ''princ'':145B ''protector'':165B ''prowess'':86B ''rac'':14B,72B ''rag'':105B ''regard'':66B ''regions'':21B ''reputation'':184B ''respect'':81B ''rough'':183B ''savag'':68B ''shar'':37B ''skill'':88B ''skyrim'':26B ''society'':113B ''sometim'':50B ''strength'':137B ''strict'':128B ''stronghold'':31B ''strongholds'':117B ''structur'':115B ''tamriel'':74B,97B ''teachings'':171B ''the'':19B,30B,84B,90B,94B,99B,103B,143B,153B,164B,167B,173B,176B,182B,198B ''they'':36B,78B,125B,149B ''though'':35B ''tim'':77B ''tradition'':130B ''transform'':159B ''trinimac'':156B ''valu'':108B,134B,193B ''view'':162B ''warriors'':100B ''was'':151B ''well'':28B ''wer'':63B ''who'':192B ''whom'':148B ''with'':52B ''within'':197B ''won'':80B ''worship'':141B ''wrothg'':23B', 'orc, scholar', 'Orcs, or Orsimer ("Pariah Folk"), are an elven race from mountainous regions like Wrothgar and Skyrim, known for their martial skill and exceptional craftsmanship. Historically feared as barbarians, they are now respected for their honor, strength, and berserker warriors, often serving in the Imperial Legion. Orc society is clan-based, centered around strongholds led by chiefs, and they worship Malacath, the Daedric Prince of Outcasts, whose teachings shape their cultural and moral code. Despite their rugged reputation, Orcs are disciplined and value fairness and justice within their communities.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('redguard', 'Redguards are a human race native to Hammerfell, with ancestral ties to the lost continent of Yokuda. They are renowned across Tamriel for their martial prowess, tactical brilliance, and adaptability in combat. Their homeland, once called the Deathlands due to its harsh, arid climate and dangerous creatures, has shaped Redguard culture into one that values strength, endurance, and survival. Hammerfell’s desert terrain is reflected in the Redguards’ resilience, including their natural resistance to poison and their impressive agility and strength. Many Redguards can be found traveling as adventurers, sailors, and mercenaries throughout Tamriel.

Physically, Redguards are distinguished by their tall, muscular builds, and skin tones that range from light brown to nearly black, often with a red tint. They typically have curly or wavy hair and are known for their love of tattoos and body piercings. Redguard society is deeply rooted in their martial traditions, particularly the legendary Sword-Singers, warriors capable of creating magical blades with their mastery of swordsmanship. This warrior culture, combined with a love for exploration and the sea, defines much of the Redguard identity.', '''across'':22B ''adaptability'':31B ''adventurers'':90B ''agility'':80B ''ancestral'':11B ''and'':30B,46B,59B,77B,81B,92B,105B,128B,136B,174B ''are'':3B,20B,98B,129B ''arid'':44B ''as'':89B ''be'':86B ''black'':115B ''blad'':159B ''body'':137B ''brillianc'':29B ''brown'':112B ''builds'':104B ''by'':100B ''call'':37B ''can'':85B ''capabl'':155B ''climat'':45B ''combat'':33B ''combin'':168B ''continent'':16B ''creating'':157B ''creatur'':48B ''cultur'':52B,167B ''curly'':124B ''dangerous'':47B ''deathlands'':39B ''deeply'':142B ''defin'':177B ''desert'':63B ''distinguish'':99B ''due'':40B ''enduranc'':58B ''exploration'':173B ''for'':24B,131B,172B ''found'':87B ''from'':110B ''hair'':127B ''hammerfell'':9B,61B ''harsh'':43B ''hav'':123B ''homeland'':35B ''hum'':5B ''identity'':182B ''impressiv'':79B ''in'':32B,67B,144B ''including'':71B ''into'':53B ''is'':65B,141B ''its'':42B ''known'':130B ''legendary'':150B ''light'':111B ''lost'':15B ''lov'':133B,171B ''magical'':158B ''many'':83B ''martial'':26B,146B ''mastery'':162B ''mercenari'':93B ''much'':178B ''muscul'':103B ''nativ'':7B ''natural'':73B ''nearly'':114B ''of'':17B,134B,156B,163B,179B ''often'':116B ''once'':36B ''one'':54B ''or'':125B ''particularly'':148B ''physically'':96B ''piercings'':138B ''poison'':76B ''prowess'':27B ''rac'':6B ''rang'':109B ''red'':119B ''redguard'':1A,51B,139B,181B ''redguards'':2B,69B,84B,97B ''reflect'':66B ''renown'':21B ''resilienc'':70B ''resistanc'':74B ''root'':143B ''s'':62B ''sailors'':91B ''shap'':50B ''singers'':153B ''skin'':106B ''society'':140B ''strength'':57B,82B ''survival'':60B ''sword'':152B ''sword-singers'':151B ''swordsmanship'':164B ''tactical'':28B ''tall'':102B ''tamriel'':23B,95B ''tatto'':135B ''terrain'':64B ''that'':55B,108B ''the'':14B,25B,34B,38B,68B,72B,78B,101B,132B,145B,149B,161B,175B,180B ''they'':19B,121B ''this'':165B ''throughout'':94B ''ties'':12B ''tint'':120B ''to'':8B,13B,41B,75B,113B ''ton'':107B ''traditions'':147B ''traveling'':88B ''typically'':122B ''valu'':56B ''warrior'':166B ''warriors'':154B ''wavy'':126B ''with'':10B,117B,160B,169B ''yokud'':18B', 'redguard, scholar', '
Redguards, a human race from Hammerfell with ancestral ties to Yokuda, are renowned for their martial skill, tactical brilliance, and adaptability in combat. Shaped by their arid, harsh homeland, they possess natural resilience, including resistance to poison, and are known for their agility and strength. Physically, they are tall and muscular, with skin tones ranging from light brown to nearly black, often with tattoos and piercings. Rooted in a warrior culture, they revere the legendary Sword-Singers and are widely recognized as adventurers, sailors, and mercenaries across Tamriel.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wood_elf', 'The Bosmer, commonly known as Wood Elves, are the native Elven people of Valenwood, a forested region in southwestern Tamriel. Unlike their Altmeri cousins, the Bosmer embrace a simpler, more natural lifestyle, living in harmony with their forested environment. Agile and nimble, they are renowned for their skill as archers and scouts, often regarded as the best bowmen in Tamriel. Many Bosmer are also adept at stealth and possess the unique ability to command animals or blend seamlessly into the forest. Despite their wild and free-spirited nature, they are also known for their quick wit and often succeed in scholarly or mercantile pursuits.

Bosmer society is shaped by the Green Pact, a unique belief system that prohibits harming Valenwood’s plant life, leading many Bosmer to live as strict carnivores, even practicing ritual cannibalism in accordance with their religious customs. Though less politically influential than other Elven races, the Bosmer are prolific and have spread across Tamriel, living two to three times as long as humans. Despite being perceived by some as unruly or naive, their deep connection to the wilderness and survival skills make them a formidable people.', '''ability'':74B ''accordanc'':140B ''across'':160B ''adept'':67B ''agil'':42B ''also'':66B,94B ''altmeri'':25B ''and'':43B,53B,70B,87B,100B,157B,186B ''animals'':77B ''archers'':52B ''are'':10B,46B,65B,93B,155B ''as'':7B,51B,57B,132B,167B,169B,176B ''at'':68B ''being'':172B ''belief'':118B ''best'':59B ''blend'':79B ''bosm'':4B,28B,64B,108B,129B,154B ''bowm'':60B ''by'':112B,174B ''cannibalism'':138B ''carnivor'':134B ''command'':76B ''commonly'':5B ''connection'':182B ''cousins'':26B ''customs'':144B ''deep'':181B ''despit'':84B,171B ''elf'':2A ''elven'':13B,151B ''elves'':9B ''embrac'':29B ''environment'':41B ''even'':135B ''for'':48B,96B ''forest'':18B,40B,83B ''formid'':192B ''fre'':89B ''free-spirit'':88B ''gre'':114B ''harming'':122B ''harmony'':37B ''hav'':158B ''humans'':170B ''in'':20B,36B,61B,103B,139B ''influential'':148B ''into'':81B ''is'':110B ''known'':6B,95B ''leading'':127B ''less'':146B ''lif'':126B ''lifestyl'':34B ''liv'':131B ''living'':35B,162B ''long'':168B ''mak'':189B ''many'':63B,128B ''mercantil'':106B ''mor'':32B ''naiv'':179B ''nativ'':12B ''natur'':91B ''natural'':33B ''nimbl'':44B ''of'':15B ''often'':55B,101B ''or'':78B,105B,178B ''other'':150B ''pact'':115B ''peopl'':14B,193B ''perceiv'':173B ''plant'':125B ''politically'':147B ''possess'':71B ''practicing'':136B ''prohibits'':121B ''prolific'':156B ''pursuits'':107B ''quick'':98B ''rac'':152B ''regard'':56B ''region'':19B ''religious'':143B ''