INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('a_game_at_dinner', 'A Game at Dinner, written by an anonymous spy, recounts the harrowing experience of a spy embedded in the court of Prince Helseth, the cunning and paranoid heir to the throne of Morrowind. Framed as a letter to a shadowy superior, the story revolves around a tense dinner where the Prince uses a macabre test of loyalty to identify disloyal advisors and spies. Guests discover that their cutlery, not the food, is poisoned, leaving them uncertain of their fate as they navigate the Prince''s mind games. Themes of betrayal, paranoia, and the ruthlessness of political ambition permeate the narrative, painting Helseth as a figure who thrives on manipulation and fear.

The book stands alone as a vivid exploration of the deadly politics within Morrowind’s royal court. Through the spy''s perspective, the reader experiences the psychological torment of Helseth''s machinations, culminating in a gruesome and public display of power. The story underscores the precariousness of loyalty and the personal toll of espionage, leaving the spy pleading for release from their role. With its blend of suspense and moral ambiguity, the book highlights the dangerous interplay of trust and deception in the pursuit of power.', '''advisors'':65B ''alon'':119B ''ambiguity'':186B ''ambition'':101B ''an'':11B ''and'':30B,66B,96B,114B,152B,164B,184B,195B ''anonymous'':12B ''around'':49B ''as'':39B,84B,107B,120B ''at'':3A,7B ''betrayal'':94B ''blend'':181B ''book'':117B,188B ''by'':10B ''court'':24B,132B ''culminating'':148B ''cunning'':29B ''cutlery'':72B ''dangerous'':191B ''deadly'':126B ''deception'':196B ''dinn'':4A,8B,52B ''discov'':69B ''disloyal'':64B ''display'':154B ''embedd'':21B ''espionag'':169B ''experienc'':17B,140B ''exploration'':123B ''fat'':83B ''fear'':115B ''figur'':109B ''food'':75B ''for'':174B ''fram'':38B ''from'':176B ''gam'':2A,6B,91B ''gruesom'':151B ''guests'':68B ''harrowing'':16B ''heir'':32B ''helseth'':27B,106B,145B ''highlights'':189B ''identify'':63B ''in'':22B,149B,197B ''interplay'':192B ''is'':76B ''its'':180B ''leaving'':78B,170B ''lett'':41B ''loyalty'':61B,163B ''macabr'':58B ''machinations'':147B ''manipulation'':113B ''mind'':90B ''moral'':185B ''morrowind'':37B,129B ''narrativ'':104B ''navigat'':86B ''not'':73B ''of'':18B,25B,36B,60B,81B,93B,99B,124B,144B,155B,162B,168B,182B,193B,200B ''on'':112B ''painting'':105B ''paran'':31B ''paranoi'':95B ''permeat'':102B ''personal'':166B ''perspectiv'':137B ''pleading'':173B ''poison'':77B ''political'':100B ''politics'':127B ''pow'':156B,201B ''precariousness'':161B ''princ'':26B,55B,88B ''psychological'':142B ''public'':153B ''pursuit'':199B ''read'':139B ''recounts'':14B