INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stros_m-kai_rum', 'Stros M''Kai Rum is a rare beverage tied to seafaring traditions. Known for its strong and smooth taste, it is cherished by sailors and adventurers.', '''adventurers'':31B ''and'':22B,30B ''beverag'':13B ''by'':28B ''cherish'':27B ''for'':19B ''is'':10B,26B ''it'':25B ''its'':20B ''kai'':4A,8B ''known'':18B ''m'':3A,7B ''m-kai'':2A ''rar'':12B ''rum'':5A,9B ''sailors'':29B ''seafaring'':16B ''smooth'':23B ''strong'':21B ''stros'':1A,6B ''tast'':24B ''tied'':14B ''to'':15B ''traditions'':17B', 'sorex_vinius, falk_firebeard, sailor, merchant', 'You know nothing about this rum or its origins.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('a_hypothetical_treachery', 'A Hypothetical Treachery, written by Anthil Morvir, is a one-act play depicting the darkly humorous and treacherous dynamics between a group of adventurers seeking to escape Eldengrove with the prized Ebony Mail. The main characters—a High Elf battlemage (Malvasian), a Dark Elf battlemage (Inzoliah), a Cyrodiil healer (Dolcettus), and an Argonian barbarian (Schiavas)—succumb to paranoia and betrayal as they navigate the perilous forest. The play masterfully blends tension, irony, and wit, showcasing the characters’ moral ambiguities and self-serving motivations. The narrative crescendos with a double-cross where scheming battlemages eliminate one another in pursuit of power, ending with Inzoliah’s ruthless triumph.

Thematically, the play explores trust, ambition, and the seductive allure of power, highlighting how alliances crumble under greed and suspicion. It cleverly critiques human (and mer) nature through its satirical portrayal of manipulative and self-serving characters, ultimately leading to their downfall. The epilogue reinforces the futility of treachery, as even the victor’s success is marred by unforeseen consequences. This stand-alone work captivates with its layered dialogue, moral complexity, and biting humor, making it a quintessential commentary on betrayal in the guise of an adventurous tale.', '''act'':15B ''adventurers'':28B ''adventurous'':201B ''allianc'':127B ''allur'':122B ''alon'':177B ''ambiguiti'':83B ''ambition'':118B ''an'':56B,200B ''and'':21B,55B,63B,77B,84B,119B,131B,137B,146B,186B ''anoth'':102B ''anthil'':9B ''argoni'':57B ''as'':65B,163B ''barbari'':58B ''battlemag'':44B,49B,99B ''betrayal'':64B,195B ''betw'':24B ''biting'':187B ''blends'':74B ''by'':8B,171B ''captivat'':179B ''characters'':40B,81B,150B ''cleverly'':134B ''commentary'':193B ''complexity'':185B ''consequenc'':173B ''crescend'':91B ''critiqu'':135B ''cross'':96B ''crumbl'':128B ''cyrodiil'':52B ''dark'':47B ''darkly'':19B ''depicting'':17B ''dialog'':183B ''dolcettus'':54B ''doubl'':95B ''double-cross'':94B ''downfall'':155B ''dynamics'':23B ''ebony'':36B ''eldengrov'':32B ''elf'':43B,48B ''eliminat'':100B ''ending'':107B ''epilog'':157B ''escap'':31B ''even'':164B ''explor'':116B ''forest'':70B ''futility'':160B ''gre'':130B ''group'':26B ''guis'':198B ''heal'':53B ''high'':42B ''highlighting'':125B ''how'':126B ''hum'':136B ''humor'':188B ''humorous'':20B ''hypothetical'':2A,5B ''in'':103B,196B ''inzoliah'':50B,109B ''irony'':76B ''is'':11B,169B ''it'':133B,190B ''its'':141B,181B ''layer'':182B ''leading'':152B ''mail'':37B ''main'':39B ''making'':189B ''malvasi'':45B ''manipulativ'':145B ''marr'':170B ''masterfully'':73B ''mer'':138B ''moral'':82B,184B ''morv'':10B ''motivat