INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('a_tragedy_in_black', 'A Tragedy in Black, written by an anonymous author, recounts a grim folk tale from the time of the Oblivion Crisis, illustrating the dangers of naivety and hubris in dealing with Daedric forces. The story follows a young, overconfident aspiring mage who summons a Dremora to create a magical gift for his mother. Despite his bravado and belief in his knowledge, the boy falls victim to the Dremora''s cunning, resulting in his soul being trapped in a black soul gem—a cruel reminder of the perilous consequences of meddling with forces beyond his understanding.

Thematically, the tale explores hubris, innocence, and the inherent dangers of ambition unchecked by wisdom. It underscores the manipulative nature of Daedra and the harsh lessons of overconfidence. This standalone work serves as both a cautionary tale and a chilling narrative, warning against the recklessness of summoning Daedric entities without understanding their true nature.', '''against'':142B ''ambition'':111B ''an'':11B ''and'':31B,61B,106B,122B,137B ''anonymous'':12B ''as'':132B ''aspiring'':44B ''author'':13B ''being'':79B ''belief'':62B ''beyond'':97B ''black'':4A,8B,83B ''both'':133B ''boy'':67B ''brav'':60B ''by'':10B,113B ''cautionary'':135B ''chilling'':139B ''consequenc'':92B ''creat'':51B ''crisis'':25B ''cruel'':87B ''cunning'':74B ''daedr'':121B ''daedric'':36B,147B ''dangers'':28B,109B ''dealing'':34B ''despit'':58B ''dremor'':49B,72B ''entiti'':148B ''explor'':103B ''falls'':68B ''folk'':17B ''follows'':40B ''for'':55B ''forc'':37B,96B ''from'':19B ''gem'':85B ''gift'':54B ''grim'':16B ''harsh'':124B ''his'':56B,59B,64B,77B,98B ''hubris'':32B,104B ''illustrating'':26B ''in'':3A,7B,33B,63B,76B,81B ''inherent'':108B ''innocenc'':105B ''it'':115B ''knowledg'':65B ''lessons'':125B ''mag'':45B ''magical'':53B ''manipulativ'':118B ''meddling'':94B ''moth'':57B ''naivety'':30B ''narrativ'':140B ''natur'':119B,153B ''oblivion'':24B ''of'':22B,29B,89B,93B,110B,120B,126B,145B ''overconfidenc'':127B ''overconfident'':43B ''perilous'':91B ''recklessness'':144B ''recounts'':14B ''remind'':88B ''resulting'':75B ''s'':73B ''serv'':131B ''soul'':78B,84B ''standalon'':129B ''story'':39B ''summoning'':146B ''summons'':47B ''tal'':18B,102B,136B ''the'':20B,23B,27B,38B,66B,71B,90B,101B,107B,117B,123B,143B,151B ''thematically'':100B ''this'':128B ''tim'':21B ''to'':50B,70B ''tragedy'':2A,6B ''trapp'':80B ''tru'':152B ''uncheck'':112B ''underscor'':116B ''understanding'':99B,150B ''victim'':69B ''warning'':141B ''who'':46B ''wisdom'':114B ''with'':35B,95B ''without''