INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('aedra_and_daedra', '
Aedra and Daedra, written by an anonymous author, provides an accessible explanation of the fundamental differences between Aedra, Daedra, and their associations with gods and demons. The book clarifies that the terms "Aedra" and "Daedra" are precise in Elvish, with Aedra meaning "ancestor" and Daedra translating to "not our ancestors." This distinction is particularly important to the Dunmer, reflecting their ideological and mythical divide. Aedra are tied to stasis, creation, and the mortal world, bound to the Earth Bones and vulnerable to death, as illustrated by the fate of Lorkhan. In contrast, Daedra embody change and transformation, lacking the ability to create but possessing the power to influence and alter reality, and they can only be banished, not killed.

Thematically, the book explores concepts of permanence versus adaptability, creation versus influence, and the nature of divine authority in Tamriel. It also touches on cultural perspectives, such as the Dunmer''s unique interpretation of these entities. This single-volume work is an essential primer for understanding the cosmology of The Elder Scrolls universe and the roles of these powerful beings.', '''ability'':103B ''access'':14B ''adaptability'':131B ''aedr'':1A,4B,21B,36B,44B,68B ''also'':144B ''alter'':113B ''an'':9B,13B,165B ''ancestor'':46B ''ancestors'':53B ''and'':2A,5B,23B,28B,37B,47B,65B,74B,83B,99B,112B,115B,135B,177B ''anonymous'':10B ''are'':39B,69B ''as'':87B,150B ''associations'':25B ''author'':11B ''authority'':140B ''banish'':120B ''be'':119B ''beings'':183B ''betw'':20B ''bon'':82B ''book'':31B,125B ''bound'':78B ''but'':106B ''by'':8B,89B ''can'':117B ''chang'':98B ''clarifi'':32B ''concepts'':127B ''contrast'':95B ''cosmology'':171B ''creat'':105B ''creation'':73B,132B ''cultural'':147B ''daedr'':3A,6B,22B,38B,48B,96B ''death'':86B ''demons'':29B ''differenc'':19B ''distinction'':55B ''divid'':67B ''divin'':139B ''dunm'':61B,152B ''earth'':81B ''elder'':174B ''elvish'':42B ''embody'':97B ''entiti'':158B ''essential'':166B ''explanation'':15B ''explor'':126B ''fat'':91B ''for'':168B ''fundamental'':18B ''gods'':27B ''ideological'':64B ''illustrat'':88B ''important'':58B ''in'':41B,94B,141B ''influenc'':111B,134B ''interpretation'':155B ''is'':56B,164B ''it'':143B ''kill'':122B ''lacking'':101B ''lorkh'':93B ''meaning'':45B ''mortal'':76B ''mythical'':66B ''natur'':137B ''not'':51B,121B ''of'':16B,92B,128B,138B,156B,172B,180B ''on'':146B ''only'':118B ''our'':52B ''particularly'':57B ''permanenc'':129B ''perspectiv'':148B ''possessing'':107B ''pow'':109B ''powerful'':182B ''precis'':40B ''prim'':167B ''provid'':12B ''reality'':114B ''reflecting'':62B ''rol'':179B ''s'':153B ''scrolls'':175B ''singl'':161B ''single-volum'':160B ''stasis'':72B ''