INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ancestors_and_the_dunmer', '
Ancestors and the Dunmer, written by an anonymous scholar, is a guide for outsiders seeking to understand the ancestor veneration and spirit magic practiced by the Dunmer of Morrowind. The text explores the sacred bond between the Dunmer and their ancestors, maintained through rituals at family shrines called Waiting Doors and fortified by ghost fences constructed from ancestral remains. These practices emphasize the importance of familial duty and the spiritual protection ancestors provide to their descendants. However, spirits bound against their will may become "mad ghosts," used as guardians or manipulated for rituals. The book highlights how the Dunmer view Oblivion as interconnected with the mortal world, unlike the dualistic perspective of humans, and how foreign views often misinterpret ancestor worship as necromancy.

Thematically, the book delves into reverence, familial loyalty, and the clash of cultural perceptions, particularly regarding necromancy, which the Dunmer abhor outside their sacred traditions. The text also touches on the Empire’s policy of tolerance and the adaptation of ancestral practices in the wake of changes like the construction of the Great Ghostfence. This singular work offers insight into the spiritual foundations of Dunmer society and their intricate relationship with death and memory.', '''abhor'':148B ''adaptation'':166B ''against'':84B ''also'':155B ''an'':11B ''ancestor'':23B,124B ''ancestors'':1A,5B,45B,76B ''ancestral'':62B,168B ''and'':2A,6B,25B,43B,55B,72B,118B,136B,164B,194B,200B ''anonymous'':12B ''as'':92B,106B,126B ''at'':49B ''becom'':88B ''betw'':40B ''bond'':39B ''book'':99B,130B ''bound'':83B ''by'':10B,29B,57B ''call'':52B ''chang'':174B ''clash'':138B ''construct'':60B ''construction'':177B ''cultural'':140B ''death'':199B ''delv'':131B ''descendants'':80B ''doors'':54B ''dualistic'':114B ''dunm'':4A,8B,31B,42B,103B,147B,192B ''duty'':71B ''emphasiz'':66B ''empir'':159B ''explor'':36B ''familial'':70B,134B ''family'':50B ''fenc'':59B ''for'':17B,96B ''foreign'':120B ''fortifi'':56B ''foundations'':190B ''from'':61B ''ghost'':58B ''ghostfenc'':181B ''ghosts'':90B ''great'':180B ''guardians'':93B ''guid'':16B ''highlights'':100B ''how'':101B,119B ''howev'':81B ''humans'':117B ''importanc'':68B ''in'':170B ''insight'':186B ''interconnect'':107B ''into'':132B,187B ''intricat'':196B ''is'':14B ''lik'':175B ''loyalty'':135B ''mad'':89B ''magic'':27B ''maintain'':46B ''manipulat'':95B ''may'':87B ''memory'':201B ''misinterpret'':123B ''morrowind'':33B ''mortal'':110B ''necromancy'':127B,144B ''oblivion'':105B ''of'':32B,69B,116B,139B,162B,167B,173B,178B,191B ''offers'':185B ''often'':122B ''on'':157B ''or'':94B ''outsid'':149B ''outsiders'':18B ''particularly'':142B ''perceptions'':141B ''perspectiv'':115B ''policy'':161B ''practic'':28B,65B,1