Mephala, the Webspinner, is a Daedric Prince of murder, lies, deception, secrets, and intrigue. Often depicted as androgynous and referred to as the Spinner or Spider, she weaves intricate plots that manipulate mortals and lead to conflict and betrayal. Revered as one of the "Good Daedra" in Morrowind, Mephala is credited with shaping the Great Houses and founding the assassin group Morag Tong, with some legends linking her to the Dark Brotherhood. Her artifacts, like the Ebony Blade, empower their wielders through betrayal and violence. A master of hidden knowledge, Mephala’s influence thrives wherever secrets and strife take hold.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_art_of_war_magic', '
The Art of War Magic, written by Zurin Arctus with commentary by other learned masters, explores the philosophy and strategy behind mastering warfare through a blend of arcane and mundane tactics. The book emphasizes the importance of preparation, balance, and psychological insight. Arctus advises that the most skilled battlemages ensure victory before battle through superior planning, understanding the enemy''s vulnerabilities, and employing strategies that combine magic with practical considerations. It warns against relying solely on brute force or flashy tactics, highlighting that true mastery lies in achieving victory with minimal confrontation and preserving resources.

Thematically, the book delves into foresight, discipline, and the integration of intellect with power, asserting that the greatest victories come from unseen but decisive preparation. Through historical anecdotes and strategic principles, it teaches that the art of war magic is not about overwhelming destruction but achieving subtle and inevitable triumphs. This single-volume work combines wisdom, history, and commentary to guide aspiring battlemages in the higher art of conflict.', '''about'':142B ''achieving'':93B,146B ''advis'':49B ''against'':78B ''and'':24B,34B,45B,67B,98B,108B,129B,148B,159B ''anecdot'':128B ''arcan'':33B ''arctus'':14B,48B ''art'':2A,7B,136B,168B ''aspiring'':163B ''asserting'':115B ''balanc'':44B ''battl'':58B ''battlemag'':54B,164B ''befor'':57B ''behind'':26B ''blend'':31B ''book'':38B,103B ''brut'':82B ''but'':123B,145B ''by'':12B,17B ''com'':120B ''combin'':71B,156B ''commentary'':16B,160B ''conflict'':170B ''confrontation'':97B ''considerations'':75B ''decisiv'':124B ''delv'':104B ''destruction'':144B ''disciplin'':107B ''emphasiz'':39B ''employing'':68B ''enemy'':64B ''ensur'':55B ''explor'':21B ''flashy'':85B ''forc'':83B ''foresight'':106B ''from'':121B ''greatest'':118B ''guid'':162B ''high'':167B ''highlighting'':87B ''historical'':127B ''history'':158B ''importanc'':41B ''in'':92B,165B ''inevit'':149B ''insight'':47B ''integration'':110B ''intellect'':112B ''into'':105B ''is'':140B ''it'':76B,132B ''learn'':19B ''lies'':91B ''magic'':5A,10B,72B,139B ''mastering'':27B ''masters'':20B ''mastery'':90B ''minimal'':96B ''most'':52B ''mundan'':35B ''not'':141B ''of'':3A,8B,32B,42B,111B,137B,169B ''on'':81B ''or'':84B ''other'':18B ''overwhelming'':143B ''philosophy'':23B ''planning'':61B ''pow'':114B ''practical'':74B ''preparation'':43B,125B ''preserving'':99B ''principl'':131B ''psychological'':46B ''relying'':79B ''resourc'':100B ''s'':65B ''singl'':153B ''single-volum'':152B ''skill'':53B ''solely'':80B ''strategi'':69B ''strategic'