INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('flame_cloak', 'Flame Cloak is a Destruction spell that surrounds the caster with a fiery aura, dealing fire damage to nearby enemies. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':26B ''an'':25B ''aur'':16B ''cast'':12B,30B ''cloak'':2A,4B ''damag'':19B ''dealing'':17B ''destruction'':7B ''enemi'':22B ''fiery'':15B ''fir'':18B ''flam'':1A,3B ''is'':5B ''it'':23B ''level'':28B ''nearby'':21B ''requir'':24B ''skill'':27B ''spell'':8B ''surrounds'':10B ''that'':9B ''the'':11B ''to'':20B,29B ''with'':13B', 'mage', 'Flame Cloak is a spell that surrounds the caster with a fiery aura, dealing fire damage to any nearby enemies. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('azura_and_the_box', '
Ancient Tales of the Dwemer, Part XI: Azura and the Box, written by Marobar Sul, recounts a fable exploring Dwemer skepticism and divine power. The story follows Nchylbar, a wise Dwemer sage determined to test the limits of the gods'' omniscience. Assisted by a reluctant Chimer priest named Athynic, Nchylbar summons the Daedric Prince Azura and presents her with a sealed wooden box, challenging her to identify its contents. Azura declares the box holds a red-petaled flower, but when it is opened, it is empty. Though Azura vanishes in fury, a single red petal later falls from Nchylbar’s robe. The sage, content with his newfound understanding, dies peacefully that night, leaving an enigmatic truth behind.

The tale''s themes include the pursuit of knowledge, skepticism, and the complex relationship between mortals and divine beings. It reflects the Dwemer''s characteristic irreverence for the gods, which may have contributed to their mysterious disappearance from Tamriel. The story also contrasts various cultural interpretations, with Dunmer and Aldmeri versions presenting different outcomes, from Azura’s wrath to an intricate magical illusion. This single book is part of a larger series that encapsulates the values and mysteries of the Dwemer civilization.', '''aldmeri'':172B ''also'':164B ''an'':119B,182B ''ancient'':5B ''and'':2A,13B,26B,60B,133B,139B,171B,199B ''assist'':46B ''athynic'':53B ''azur'':1A,12B,59B,74B,93B,178B ''behind'':122B ''beings'':141B ''betw'':137B ''book'':188B ''box'':4A,15B,67B,77B ''but'':84B ''by'':17B,47B ''challenging'':68B ''characteristic'':147B ''chim'':50B ''civilization'':204B ''complex'':135B ''content'':109B ''contents'':73B ''contrasts'':165B ''contribut'':155B ''cultural'':167B ''daedric'':57B ''declar'':75B ''determin'':37B ''dies'':114B ''different'':175B ''disappearanc'':159B ''divin'':27B,140B ''dunm'':170B ''dwem'':9B,24B,35B,145B,203B ''empty'':91B ''encapsulat'':196B ''enigmatic'':120B ''exploring'':23B ''fabl'':22B ''falls'':102B ''flow'':83B ''follows'':31B ''for'':149B ''from'':103B,160B,177B ''fury'':96B ''gods'':44B,151B ''hav'':154B ''her'':62B,69B ''his'':111B ''holds'':78B ''identify'':71B ''illusion'':185B ''in'':95B ''includ'':127B ''interpretations'':168B ''intricat'':183B ''irreverenc'':148B ''is'':87B,90B,189B ''it'':86B,89B,142B ''its'':72B ''knowledg'':131B ''larg'':193B ''lat'':101B ''leaving'':118B ''limits'':41B ''magical'':184B ''marob'':18B ''may'':153B ''mortals'':138B ''mysteri'':200B ''mysterious'':158B ''nam'':52B ''nchylbar'':32B,54B,104B ''newfound'':112B ''night'':117B ''of'':7B,42B,130B,191B,201B ''omniscienc'':45B ''open'':88B ''outcom'':176B ''part'':10B,190B ''peacefully'':115B ''petal'':82B