INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('biography_of_the_wolf_queen', '
Biography of the Wolf Queen, written by Katar Eriphanes, chronicles the infamous life of Queen Potema, known as the Wolf Queen of Solitude. Born in 3E 67 to the Imperial family, Potema rose to power through her marriage to King Mantiarco of Solitude, leveraging her influence and intelligence to pursue an unrelenting ambition for dominance. The text details her manipulation of political alliances, involvement in civil war, and eventual rebellion against the Empire, culminating in the War of the Red Diamond. Potema''s relentless pursuit of power saw her employing necromancy, summoning daedra, and creating a kingdom of death and madness until her final defeat at the siege of Solitude in 3E 137.

The themes of Biography of the Wolf Queen include unchecked ambition, political manipulation, and the consequences of hubris. Potema''s story serves as a cautionary tale of how power, when sought without restraint or morality, can lead to ruin and infamy. Her legacy persists as a figure of terror and malevolence, with some rumors even suggesting her spirit continues to inspire chaos and treachery. This single-volume account paints a vivid picture of Potema''s life, her downfall, and the enduring stain of her deeds on Tamriel''s history.', '''137'':118B ''3e'':31B,117B ''67'':32B ''account'':187B ''against'':76B ''allianc'':68B ''ambition'':58B,129B ''an'':56B ''and'':52B,73B,99B,105B,132B,158B,168B,181B,198B ''as'':23B,141B,163B ''at'':111B ''biography'':1A,6B,122B ''born'':29B ''by'':12B ''can'':154B ''cautionary'':143B ''cha'':180B ''chronicl'':15B ''civil'':71B ''consequenc'':134B ''continu'':177B ''creating'':100B ''culminating'':79B ''daedr'':98B ''death'':104B ''deeds'':204B ''defeat'':110B ''details'':63B ''diamond'':86B ''dominanc'':60B ''downfall'':197B ''empir'':78B ''employing'':95B ''enduring'':200B ''eriphan'':14B ''even'':173B ''eventual'':74B ''family'':36B ''figur'':165B ''final'':109B ''for'':59B ''her'':42B,50B,64B,94B,108B,160B,175B,196B,203B ''history'':208B ''how'':146B ''hubris'':136B ''imperial'':35B ''in'':30B,70B,80B,116B ''includ'':127B ''infamous'':17B ''infamy'':159B ''influenc'':51B ''inspir'':179B ''intelligenc'':53B ''involvement'':69B ''kat'':13B ''king'':45B ''kingdom'':102B ''known'':22B ''lead'':155B ''legacy'':161B ''leveraging'':49B ''lif'':18B,195B ''madness'':106B ''malevolenc'':169B ''manipulation'':65B,131B ''mantiarc'':46B ''marriag'':43B ''morality'':153B ''necromancy'':96B ''of'':2A,7B,19B,27B,47B,66B,83B,91B,103B,114B,121B,123B,135B,145B,166B,192B,202B ''on'':205B ''or'':152B ''paints'':188B ''persists'':162B ''pictur'':191B ''political'':67B,130B ''potem'':21B,37B,87B,137B,193B ''pow'':40B,92B,147B ''pursu'':55B ''pursui