INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_black_arrow', 'The Black Arrow, written by Gorgic Guine, tells a tale of revenge and mastery in archery, revolving around the tragic events surrounding the Duchess of Woda''s estate and the enigmatic archer Missun Akin. Narrated by a former servant of the Duchess, the story unfolds in Valenwood, where the Duchess harbors resentment toward the nearby village of Moliva and its renowned archery school run by Hiomaste. When a mysterious fire devastates the village, killing the students and the narrator''s friend Prolyssa, suspicions of the Duchess''s involvement arise. What follows is a series of eerie and skillful acts of vengeance, culminating in Missun Akin''s use of unparalleled archery to deliver poetic justice to the oppressive Duchess.

The story explores themes of revenge, justice, and the artistry of skill. It contrasts the oppressive arrogance of nobility with the resilience and ingenuity of the oppressed. Through the lens of a servant''s perspective, the narrative highlights the quiet power of those dismissed by society and the extraordinary feats possible through precision and perseverance. This single-volume work resonates as both a thrilling tale of retribution and a celebration of the craftsmanship of archery.', '''acts'':102B ''akin'':37B,108B ''and'':16B,32B,62B,80B,100B,129B,144B,168B,175B,190B ''archer'':35B ''archery'':19B,65B,113B,197B ''aris'':92B ''around'':21B ''arroganc'':138B ''arrow'':3A,6B ''artistry'':131B ''as'':183B ''black'':2A,5B ''both'':184B ''by'':8B,39B,68B,166B ''celebration'':192B ''contrasts'':135B ''craftsmanship'':195B ''culminating'':105B ''deliv'':115B ''devastat'':74B ''dismiss'':165B ''duchess'':27B,45B,53B,89B,121B ''eeri'':99B ''enigmatic'':34B ''estat'':31B ''events'':24B ''explor'':124B ''extraordinary'':170B ''feats'':171B ''fir'':73B ''follows'':94B ''form'':41B ''friend'':84B ''gorgic'':9B ''guin'':10B ''harbors'':54B ''highlights'':159B ''hiom'':69B ''in'':18B,49B,106B ''ingenuity'':145B ''involvement'':91B ''is'':95B ''it'':134B ''its'':63B ''justic'':117B,128B ''killing'':77B ''lens'':151B ''mastery'':17B ''missun'':36B,107B ''moliv'':61B ''mysterious'':72B ''narrat'':38B ''narrativ'':158B ''narrator'':82B ''nearby'':58B ''nobility'':140B ''of'':14B,28B,43B,60B,87B,98B,103B,111B,126B,132B,139B,146B,152B,163B,188B,193B,196B ''oppress'':148B ''oppressiv'':120B,137B ''perseveranc'':176B ''perspectiv'':156B ''poetic'':116B ''possibl'':172B ''pow'':162B ''precision'':174B ''prolyss'':85B ''quiet'':161B ''renown'':64B ''resentment'':55B ''resilienc'':143B ''resonat'':182B ''retribution'':189B ''reveng'':15B,127B ''revolving'':20B ''run'':67B ''s'':30B,83B,90B,109B,155B ''school'':66B ''seri'':97B ''servant'':42B,154B ''singl'':179B ''single-volum'':178B ''