INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_black_arts_on_trial', 'The Black Arts On Trial, written by Hannibal Traven, Archmagister of the Mages Guild, chronicles the debate that led to the Mages Guild’s resolution on the practice of Necromancy. The book explores the arguments for and against officially sanctioning the study of the Black Arts within the Guild. Master Voth Karlyss argues that Necromancy is inherently dangerous and morally corrupting, advocating for its prohibition to maintain the Guild’s ethical integrity and public trust. In contrast, Master Ulliceta gra-Kogg defends the study as essential for understanding and combating its practitioners, emphasizing that censoring knowledge undermines the Guild''s intellectual mission. Ultimately, Traven concludes that Necromancy’s risks outweigh its benefits, allowing limited and supervised study only for combating its misuse.

The themes of the book revolve around the ethical boundaries of scholarly inquiry, the balance between knowledge and responsibility, and the corruption of power. The text underscores the danger of delving too deeply into forbidden practices while acknowledging the need for vigilance against their misuse. This single-volume work provides an insightful look into the internal conflicts and moral dilemmas faced by the Mages Guild.', '''acknowledging'':166B ''advocating'':67B ''against'':43B,171B ''allowing'':119B ''an'':180B ''and'':42B,64B,78B,95B,121B,146B,148B,187B ''archmagist'':15B ''arg'':58B ''arguments'':40B ''around'':135B ''arts'':3A,8B,51B ''as'':91B ''balanc'':143B ''benefits'':118B ''betw'':144B ''black'':2A,7B,50B ''book'':37B,133B ''boundari'':138B ''by'':12B,191B ''censoring'':101B ''chronicl'':20B ''combating'':96B,126B ''conclud'':111B ''conflicts'':186B ''contrast'':82B ''corrupting'':66B ''corruption'':150B ''dang'':157B ''dangerous'':63B ''debat'':22B ''deeply'':161B ''defends'':88B ''delving'':159B ''dilemm'':189B ''emphasizing'':99B ''essential'':92B ''ethical'':76B,137B ''explor'':38B ''fac'':190B ''for'':41B,68B,93B,125B,169B ''forbidd'':163B ''gra'':86B ''gra-kogg'':85B ''guild'':19B,28B,54B,74B,105B,194B ''hannibal'':13B ''in'':81B ''inherently'':62B ''inquiry'':141B ''insightful'':181B ''integrity'':77B ''intellectual'':107B ''internal'':185B ''into'':162B,183B ''is'':61B ''its'':69B,97B,117B,127B ''karlyss'':57B ''knowledg'':102B,145B ''kogg'':87B ''led'':24B ''limit'':120B ''look'':182B ''mag'':18B,27B,193B ''maintain'':72B ''mast'':55B,83B ''mission'':108B ''misus'':128B,173B ''moral'':188B ''morally'':65B ''necromancy'':35B,60B,113B ''need'':168B ''of'':16B,34B,48B,131B,139B,151B,158B ''officially'':44B ''on'':4A,9B,31B ''only'':124B ''outweigh'':116B ''pow'':152B ''practic'':33B,164B ''practitioners'':98B ''prohibition'':70B ''provid'':179B ''public'':79B ''resolution'':30B ''responsibility'':147B ''revolv'':134B ''risks'':115B ''s'':29B