INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_book_of_the_dragonborn', '
The Book of the Dragonborn, written by Prior Emelene Madrine, explores the significance, history, and mysteries surrounding the Dragonborn, individuals blessed by Akatosh with "dragon blood." The book traces the origins of the Dragonborn to the Covenant of Akatosh, when St. Alessia was granted divine power to light the Dragonfires and protect Tamriel from Oblivion. It examines how the title has historically been associated with the rulers of the Empire, from Alessia''s line to Tiber Septim and his heirs. However, it emphasizes that the Dragonborn is not purely hereditary, but a divine mystery that transcends bloodlines. The text delves into the Akaviri''s role in identifying and supporting Dragonborn, particularly Reman Cyrodiil, and raises questions about the nature of their powers and the possibility of multiple Dragonborn existing simultaneously.

Themes include divine intervention, legitimacy of rule, and the mystical connection between mortals and dragons. The book also highlights the prophecy of the Last Dragonborn, linking it to cataclysmic events such as the fall of towers and the awakening of the World-Eater, Alduin. This singular volume serves as both a historical treatise and a speculative exploration of the prophecy, leaving readers with a sense of the unresolved nature of Akatosh''s gift to mortals and its ultimate significance for Tamriel.', '''about'':122B ''akatosh'':28B,44B,207B ''akaviri'':108B ''alduin'':180B ''alessi'':47B,77B ''also'':153B ''and'':20B,56B,83B,113B,119B,128B,143B,149B,172B,190B,212B ''as'':167B,185B ''associat'':69B ''awakening'':174B ''been'':68B ''betw'':147B ''bless'':26B ''blood'':31B ''bloodlin'':102B ''book'':2A,7B,33B,152B ''both'':186B ''but'':96B ''by'':12B,27B ''cataclysmic'':164B ''connection'':146B ''covenant'':42B ''cyrodiil'':118B ''delv'':105B ''divin'':50B,98B,138B ''dragon'':30B ''dragonborn'':5A,10B,24B,39B,91B,115B,133B,160B ''dragonfir'':55B ''dragons'':150B ''eat'':179B ''emelen'':14B ''emphasiz'':88B ''empir'':75B ''events'':165B ''examin'':62B ''existing'':134B ''explor'':16B ''exploration'':193B ''fall'':169B ''for'':216B ''from'':59B,76B ''gift'':209B ''grant'':49B ''heirs'':85B ''hereditary'':95B ''highlights'':154B ''his'':84B ''historical'':188B ''historically'':67B ''history'':19B ''how'':63B ''howev'':86B ''identifying'':112B ''in'':111B ''includ'':137B ''individuals'':25B ''intervention'':139B ''into'':106B ''is'':92B ''it'':61B,87B,162B ''its'':213B ''last'':159B ''leaving'':197B ''legitimacy'':140B ''light'':53B ''lin'':79B ''linking'':161B ''madrin'':15B ''mortals'':148B,211B ''multipl'':132B ''mysteri'':21B ''mystery'':99B ''mystical'':145B ''natur'':124B,205B ''not'':93B ''oblivion'':60B ''of'':3A,8B,37B,43B,73B,125B,131B,141B,157B,170B,175B,194B,202B,206B ''origins'':36B ''particularly'':116B ''possibility'':130B ''pow'':51B ''powers'':127