INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('leather_bracers', 'Leather Bracers are a pair of leather bracers with basic protection quality. Its visual design is simple and flexible, with dark, weathered leather panels stitched together for mobility and basic protection. To craft it: 1 leather and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge.  A Novice smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''1'':37B ''2'':40B ''and'':20B,31B,39B ''are'':5B ''at'':43B,60B ''basic'':12B,32B ''be'':55B ''blacksmith'':45B ''bracers'':2A,4B,10B ''by'':57B ''can'':50B,54B ''craft'':35B,51B ''dark'':23B ''design'':17B ''flexibl'':21B ''for'':29B ''forg'':46B ''is'':18B ''it'':36B,52B,53B ''its'':15B ''leath'':1A,3B,9B,25B,38B,41B,59B ''mobility'':30B ''novic'':48B ''of'':8B ''pair'':7B ''panels'':26B ''protection'':13B,33B ''quality'':14B ''simpl'':19B ''smith'':49B ''stitch'':27B ''strips'':42B ''tempered/improved'':56B ''to'':34B ''togeth'':28B ''using'':58B ''visual'':16B ''weather'':24B ''with'':11B,22B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Leather Bracers are a pair of leather bracers with basic protection quality. Its visual design is simple and flexible, with dark, weathered leather panels stitched together for mobility and basic protection. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('brothers_of_darkness', 'The Brothers of Darkness, written by Pellarne Assi, explores the enigmatic origins and evolution of the Dark Brotherhood, Tamriel''s infamous guild of assassins. The text traces their roots to the Morag Tong, a Second Era religious cult devoted to the Daedric Prince Mephala. The Morag Tong''s shift to the Dark Brotherhood marked a significant transformation, as they transitioned from ritualistic murder to a profit-driven organization serving rulers and wealthy patrons. This shift solidified their role as both a feared cult and a necessary, albeit unlawful, institution across Tamriel.

The book highlights key historical moments, such as the assassination of Potentate Versidue-Shaie in 2E 324 and the infamous massacre of Emperor-Potentate Savirien-Chorak and his heirs in 2E 430. Themes of secrecy, power, and moral ambiguity run throughout, emphasizing the Brotherhood''s dual identity as both a cult and a business. Though officially condemned, their services remain widely tolerated, securing their position as a shadowy yet indispensable force in Tamriel''s political landscape.', '''2e'':112B,129B ''324'':113B ''430'':130B ''across'':94B ''albeit'':91B ''ambiguity'':137B ''and'':16B,75B,88B,114B,125B,135B,150B ''as'':61B,83B,103B,146B,164B ''assassination'':105B ''assassins'':27B ''assi'':11B ''book'':97B ''both'':84B,147B ''brotherhood'':21B,56B,142B ''brothers'':1A,5B ''business'':152B ''by'':9B ''chorak'':124B ''condemn'':155B ''cult'':41B,87B,149B ''daedric'':45B ''dark'':20B,55B ''darkness'':3A,7B ''devot'':42B ''driv'':71B ''dual'':144B ''emperor'':120B ''emperor-potentat'':119B ''emphasizing'':140B ''enigmatic'':14B ''evolution'':17B ''explor'':12B ''fear'':86B ''forc'':169B ''from'':64B ''guild'':25B ''heirs'':127B ''highlights'':98B ''his'':126B ''historical'':100B ''identity'':145B ''in'':111B,128B,170B ''indispens'':168B ''infamous'':24B,116B ''institution'':93B ''key'':99B ''landscap'':174B ''mark'':57B ''massacr'':117B ''mephal'':47B ''moments'':101B ''morag'':35B,49B ''moral'':136B ''murd'':66B ''necessary'':90B ''of'':2A,6B,18B,26B,106B,118B,132B ''officially'':154B ''organization'':72B ''origins'':15B ''patrons'':77B ''pellarn'':10B ''political'':173B ''position'':163B ''potentat'':107B,121B ''pow'':134B ''princ'':46B ''profit'':70B ''profit-driv'':69B ''religious'':40B ''remain'':158B ''ritualistic'':65B ''rol'':82B ''roots'':32B ''rulers'':74B ''run'':138B ''s'':23B,51B,143B,172B ''saviri'':123B ''savirien-chorak'':122B ''second'':38B ''secrecy'':133B ''securing'':161B ''servic'':157B ''serving'':73B ''shadowy'':166B ''shai'':110B '