Meridia, the Lady of Infinite Energies, is a Daedric Prince associated with life, light, and the energies of living things. Known for her hatred of the undead and necromancy, she rewards those who combat decay and false-life. Though not malevolent, she is sometimes viewed as obsessively orderly and called the Lady of Greed. Meridia''s realm, the Colored Rooms, is inhabited by her Auroran servants. Believed to have been one of the Magne-Ge before her fall, she often allies with mortals against rivals like Molag Bal. Her notable artifacts include Dawnbreaker, a sword imbued with holy light, and the Ring of Khajiiti, bestowed upon her champions.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('catalogue_of_armor_enchantments', 'Complete Catalogue of Enchantments for Armor, written by Yvonne Bienne, provides an overview of known armor enchantments crafted by modern mages. While not exhaustive, the catalogue covers enchantments that enhance attributes like health, magicka, and stamina, as well as resistances to elements, poisons, and magic. These enchantments are practical for warriors, wizards, and adventurers, offering benefits tailored to their needs, such as increased resilience, spellcasting efficiency, or physical endurance.

The book also delves into rarer enchantments, such as waterbreathing, muffle, and those that accelerate recovery rates for health, magicka, or stamina. These enhancements reflect both the creativity and pragmatism of enchanters, catering to niche challenges like stealth, underwater exploration, or prolonged combat. Themes of adaptability, innovation, and the utility of magic underscore the text, making it a useful resource for those seeking to understand the practical applications of enchantments.', '''accelerat'':88B ''adaptability'':119B ''adventurers'':58B ''also'':76B ''an'':16B ''and'':39B,48B,57B,85B,102B,121B ''applications'':141B ''are'':52B ''armor'':3A,10B,20B ''as'':41B,43B,66B,82B ''attribut'':35B ''benefits'':60B ''bienn'':14B ''book'':75B ''both'':99B ''by'':12B,23B ''catalog'':1A,6B,30B ''catering'':106B ''challeng'':109B ''combat'':116B ''complet'':5B ''covers'':31B ''craft'':22B ''creativity'':101B ''delv'':77B ''efficiency'':70B ''elements'':46B ''enchanters'':105B ''enchantments'':4A,8B,21B,32B,51B,80B,143B ''enduranc'':73B ''enhanc'':34B ''enhancements'':97B ''exhaustiv'':28B ''exploration'':113B ''for'':9B,54B,91B,134B ''health'':37B,92B ''increas'':67B ''innovation'':120B ''into'':78B ''it'':130B ''known'':19B ''lik'':36B,110B ''mag'':25B ''magic'':49B,125B ''magick'':38B,93B ''making'':129B ''modern'':24B ''muffl'':84B ''needs'':64B ''nich'':108B ''not'':27B ''of'':2A,7B,18B,104B,118B,124B,142B ''offering'':59B ''or'':71B,94B,114B ''overview'':17B ''physical'':72B ''poisons'':47B ''practical'':53B,140B ''pragmatism'':103B ''prolong'':115B ''provid'':15B ''rar'':79B ''rat'':90B ''recovery'':89B ''reflect'':98B ''resilienc'':68B ''resistanc'':44B ''resourc'':133B ''seeking'':136B ''spellcasting'':69B ''stamin'':40B,95B ''stealth'':111B ''such'':65B,81B ''tailor'':61B ''text'':128B ''that'':33B,87B ''the'':29B,63B,74B,100B,122B,127B,139B ''them'':117B ''thes'':50B,96B ''thos'':86B,135B ''to'':45B,62B,107B,137B ''underscor'':126B ''understand'':13