INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('children_of_the_sky', 'Children of the Sky, written by Yvonne Bienne, explores the culture and mystical powers of the Nords, focusing particularly on their connection to the Thu''um, or Shout. The Nords view themselves as the "children of the sky," believing that their land, Skyrim, was formed when the sky exhaled upon it. This powerful, spiritual connection to the sky is reflected in their unique ability to use their breath as a weapon and form of expression, most notably through the Thu''um. The strongest Nords, called "Tongues," can harness this power to perform extraordinary feats, such as knocking down doors with a single shout or striking enemies with forceful roars. The book delves into the significance of speech in their culture, with the greatest warriors being those who can wield their voices to instill fear, command, or even travel vast distances.

The themes of power, identity, and elemental force permeate the text, illustrating the Nords’ deep connection to the elements of Skyrim, particularly wind, which is central to their nature. As the book progresses, it emphasizes the physical and mental toll of mastering the Thu''um, suggesting that the most powerful Nords must suppress their voices to avoid destruction. The narrative also touches on the Nords’ sense of alienation, as they view themselves as eternal outsiders, even when they conquer and rule others. The book reflects the harsh, elemental nature of Skyrim and its people, providing insight into the profound impact that the Thu''um has on their lives and culture.', '''ability'':68B ''alienation'':212B ''also'':205B ''and'':16B,76B,150B,182B,224B,236B,253B ''as'':37B,73B,100B,174B,213B,217B ''avo'':201B ''being'':129B ''believing'':43B ''bienn'':12B ''book'':115B,176B,228B ''breath'':72B ''by'':10B ''call'':89B ''can'':91B,132B ''central'':170B ''childr'':1A,5B,39B ''command'':139B ''connection'':26B,59B,160B ''conqu'':223B ''cultur'':15B,124B,254B ''deep'':159B ''delv'':116B ''destruction'':202B ''distanc'':144B ''doors'':103B ''down'':102B ''elemental'':151B,232B ''elements'':163B ''emphasiz'':179B ''enemi'':110B ''eternal'':218B ''even'':141B,220B ''exhal'':53B ''explor'':13B ''expression'':79B ''extraordinary'':97B ''fear'':138B ''feats'':98B ''focusing'':22B ''forc'':152B ''forceful'':112B ''form'':49B,77B ''greatest'':127B ''harness'':92B ''harsh'':231B ''identity'':149B ''illustrating'':156B ''impact'':244B ''in'':65B,122B ''insight'':240B ''instill'':137B ''into'':117B,241B ''is'':63B,169B ''it'':55B,178B ''its'':237B ''knocking'':101B ''land'':46B ''liv'':252B ''mastering'':186B ''mental'':183B ''most'':80B,193B ''must'':196B ''mystical'':17B ''narrativ'':204B ''natur'':173B,233B ''nords'':21B,34B,88B,158B,195B,209B ''notably'':81B ''of'':2A,6B,19B,40B,78B,120B,147B,164B,185B,211B,234B ''on'':24B,207B,250B ''or'':31B,108B,140B ''others'':226B ''o