INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_dragon_break_reexamined', '
The Dragon Break Reexamined, written by Fal Droon, explores the historical error that led to the myth of the "Dragon Break" and its lasting impact on Tamrielic history. The concept of the Dragon Break, widely accepted as an event during Tiber Septim''s rise to power, was based on a timeline error in the Encyclopedia Tamrielica due to misinterpretations of Alessian records. The book argues that this error, compounded by obsession with religious and eschatological themes, became entrenched in historical accounts, despite the absence of solid evidence for such an event. Droon''s work reveals that the actual historical period of the Alessians was much shorter than traditionally believed, and the Dragon Break was a product of scholarly misunderstanding and the repetition of faulty traditions.

The themes of the book center around the fallibility of historical records, the dangers of relying on outdated or erroneous traditions, and the way myths can be perpetuated through scholarly inertia. Droon''s examination highlights the importance of critically reexamining historical events and the influence of cultural and religious beliefs on the interpretation of history. This work is a single, standalone volume that challenges long-held beliefs in Tamrielic history, encouraging readers to question the foundations of widely accepted myths.', '''absenc'':88B ''accept'':40B,209B ''accounts'':85B ''actual'':102B ''alessi'':65B ''alessians'':107B ''an'':42B,94B ''and'':26B,78B,114B,124B,151B,172B,177B ''arg'':69B ''around'':136B ''as'':41B ''bas'':52B ''be'':156B ''becam'':81B ''beliefs'':179B,197B ''believ'':113B ''book'':68B,134B ''break'':3A,7B,25B,38B,117B ''by'':10B,74B ''can'':155B ''cent'':135B ''challeng'':193B ''compound'':73B ''concept'':34B ''critically'':168B ''cultural'':176B ''dangers'':143B ''despit'':86B ''dragon'':2A,6B,24B,37B,116B ''droon'':12B,96B,161B ''due'':61B ''during'':44B ''encouraging'':201B ''encyclopedi'':59B ''entrench'':82B ''erroneous'':149B ''error'':16B,56B,72B ''eschatological'':79B ''event'':43B,95B ''events'':171B ''evidenc'':91B ''examination'':163B ''explor'':13B ''fal'':11B ''fallibility'':138B ''faulty'':128B ''for'':92B ''foundations'':206B ''held'':196B ''highlights'':164B ''historical'':15B,84B,103B,140B,170B ''history'':32B,184B,200B ''impact'':29B ''importanc'':166B ''in'':57B,83B,198B ''inerti'':160B ''influenc'':174B ''interpretation'':182B ''is'':187B ''its'':27B ''lasting'':28B ''led'':18B ''long'':195B ''long-held'':194B ''misinterpretations'':63B ''misunderstanding'':123B ''much'':109B ''myth'':21B ''myths'':154B,210B ''obsession'':75B ''of'':22B,35B,64B,89B,105B,121B,127B,132B,139B,144B,167B,175B,183B,207B ''on'':30B,53B,146B,180B ''or'':148B ''outdat'':147B ''period'':104B ''perpetuat'':157B ''pow'':50B ''product'