The Doors of Oblivion, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, follows the journey of Morian Zenas, a mage consumed by the pursuit of forbidden knowledge across various Daedric realms. Themes of obsession, the dangers of seeking knowledge beyond mortal understanding, and the descent into madness are central, emphasizing the cost of uncovering hidden truths in the world of Oblivion.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('zahkriisos', 'Zahkriios is one of the high-ranking dragon priests in Solstheim. He was an aloof Dragon priest who did nothing of note during the Dragon war It is also rumored he was a secret worshipper of Hermaeus Mora''.', '''aloof'':17B ''also'':31B ''an'':16B ''did'':21B ''dragon'':10B,18B,27B ''during'':25B ''hermaeus'':39B ''high'':8B ''high-ranking'':7B ''in'':12B ''is'':3B,30B ''it'':29B ''mor'':40B ''not'':24B ''nothing'':22B ''of'':5B,23B,38B ''one'':4B ''priest'':19B ''priests'':11B ''ranking'':9B ''rumor'':32B ''secret'':36B ''solstheim'':13B ''the'':6B,26B ''war'':28B ''was'':15B,34B ''who'':20B ''worshipp'':37B ''zahkrii'':2B ''zahkriis'':1A', 'scholar, dragon, miraakcult', 'Zahkriios must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Solstheim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('a_dream_of_sovngarde', 'A Dream of Sovngarde, written by Skardan Free-Winter, recounts the vision experienced by a Nord soldier before the Battle of the Red Ring, offering him guidance and courage in the face of certain death. As he prepares for a desperate battle against the Aldmeri, Skardan prays to Talos and dreams of walking through mists towards Sovngarde, the hall of the honored dead. There, he meets the warrior Tsun, who grants him passage to the great hall, where Ysgramor, the father of Skyrim, shares wisdom about death and valor. Ysgramor tells him that a Nord is judged not by how they live, but by how they die, imparting a sense of pride and bravery in the face of imminent peril.

The themes of the story focus on bravery, honor, and the Nordic perspective on life and death, particularly the importance of dying with courage and strength. Skardan’s dream offers a reflection on what it means to be a true Nord, reinforcing the values of their culture—courage in battle, respect for ancestors, and a focus on how one faces death. The story is a single volume, conveying a poignant and personal message to those who may follow in Skardan’s footsteps, instilling them with the courage needed to face their own trials.', '''about'':91B ''against'':48B ''aldmeri'':50B ''ancestors'':178B ''and'':33B,55B,93B,118B,135B,141B,150B,179B,196B ''as'':41B ''battl'':25B,47B,175B ''be'':163B ''befor'':23B ''bravery'':119B,133B ''but'':108B ''by'':10B,19B,104B,109B ''certain'':39B ''conveying'':193B ''courag'':34B,149B,173B,212B ''cultur'':172B ''dead'':68B ''death'':40B,92B,142B,186B ''desperat'':46B ''die'':112B ''dream'':2A,6B,154B ''dreams'':56B ''dying'':147B ''experienc'':18B ''fac'':37B,122B,185B,215B ''fath'':86B ''focus'':131B,181B ''follow'':203B ''footsteps'':207B ''for'':44B,177B ''fre'':13B ''free-wint'':12B ''grants'':76B ''great'':81B ''guidanc'':32B ''hall'':64B,82B ''him'':31B,77B,97B ''honor'':67B,134B ''how'':105B,110B,183B ''imminent'':124B ''imparting'':113B ''importanc'':145B ''in'':35B,120B,174B,204B ''instilling'':208B ''is'':101B,189B ''it'':160B ''judg'':102B ''lif'':140B ''liv'':107B ''may'':202B ''means'':161B ''meets'':71B ''messag'':198B ''mists'':60B ''need'':213B ''nord'':21B,100B,166B ''nordic'':137B ''not'':103B ''of'':3A,7B,26B,38B,57B,65B,87B,116B,123B,128B,146B,170B ''offering'':30B ''offers'':155B ''on'':132B,139B,158B,182B ''one'':184B ''own'':217B ''particularly'':143B ''passag'':78B ''peril'':125B ''personal'':197B ''perspectiv'':138B ''poignant'':195B ''prays'':52B ''prepar'':43B ''prid'':117B ''recounts'':15B ''red'':28B ''reflection'':157B ''reinforcing'':167B ''respect'':176B ''ring'':29B ''s'':153B,206B ''sens'':115B ''shar