INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('feyfolken', 'Feyfolken, written by Waughin Jarth, tells the story of Thaurbad Hulzik, a scribe suffering from the Crimson Plague and his encounters with a cursed quill enchanted by a Daedric spirit called Feyfolken. Set during the Second Era, Thaurbad lives a solitary life, communicating only through written words after losing his voice. His discovery of the magical Feyfolken quill leads him to great artistic and professional success, as it brings his mundane writings to life with divine beauty. However, the quill''s magic takes a sinister turn, gradually driving Thaurbad to madness and ultimately leading to his tragic death. The story delves into themes of creativity, the destructive nature of power, and the fine line between genius and madness.

The narrative explores the complexities of magical influence and the moral consequences of using enchanted tools, particularly in the context of Thaurbad’s transformation from a humble scribe to a cursed artist. His story is a tragic commentary on the dangers of seeking perfection through unnatural means and the corrupting force of magical power. This tale spans multiple volumes, offering a detailed examination of the interaction between Thaurbad and the Feyfolken quill, and the gradual unraveling of his life due to its influence.', '''after'':49B ''and'':20B,65B,93B,112B,118B,128B,167B,188B,192B ''artist'':151B ''artistic'':64B ''as'':68B ''beauty'':78B ''betw'':116B,186B ''brings'':70B ''by'':4B,28B ''call'':32B ''commentary'':157B ''communicating'':44B ''complexiti'':124B ''consequenc'':131B ''context'':139B ''corrupting'':169B ''creativity'':106B ''crimson'':18B ''curs'':25B,150B ''daedric'':30B ''dangers'':160B ''death'':99B ''delv'':102B ''destructiv'':108B ''detail'':181B ''discovery'':54B ''divin'':77B ''driving'':89B ''due'':199B ''during'':35B ''enchant'':27B,134B ''encounters'':22B ''examination'':182B ''explor'':122B ''feyfolk'':1A,2B,33B,58B,190B ''fin'':114B ''forc'':170B ''from'':16B,144B ''genius'':117B ''gradual'':194B ''gradually'':88B ''great'':63B ''him'':61B ''his'':21B,51B,53B,71B,97B,152B,197B ''howev'':79B ''hulzik'':12B ''humbl'':146B ''in'':137B ''influenc'':127B,202B ''interaction'':185B ''into'':103B ''is'':154B ''it'':69B ''its'':201B ''jarth'':6B ''leading'':95B ''leads'':60B ''lif'':43B,75B,198B ''lin'':115B ''liv'':40B ''losing'':50B ''madness'':92B,119B ''magic'':83B ''magical'':57B,126B,172B ''means'':166B ''moral'':130B ''multipl'':177B ''mundan'':72B ''narrativ'':121B ''natur'':109B ''of'':10B,55B,105B,110B,125B,132B,140B,161B,171B,183B,196B ''offering'':179B ''on'':158B ''only'':45B ''particularly'':136B ''perfection'':163B ''plag'':19B ''pow'':111B,173B ''professional'':66B ''quill'':26B,59B,81B,191B ''s'':82B,142B ''scrib'':14B