INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shield_of_ysgramor', '
The Shield of Ysgramor is a legendary artifact buried with the famed Nord hero Ysgramor in his tomb during the Late Merethic Era. While it is unclear if Ysgramor used the shield in battle, it grants its wielder enhanced durability and resistance to magic, making it a prized relic of Nordic heritage.', '''and'':44B ''artifact'':11B ''battl'':37B ''buri'':12B ''durability'':43B ''during'':22B ''enhanc'':42B ''fam'':15B ''grants'':39B ''her'':17B ''heritag'':55B ''his'':20B ''if'':31B ''in'':19B,36B ''is'':8B,29B ''it'':28B,38B,49B ''its'':40B ''lat'':24B ''legendary'':10B ''magic'':47B ''making'':48B ''merethic'':25B ''nord'':16B ''nordic'':54B ''of'':2A,6B,53B ''priz'':51B ''relic'':52B ''resistanc'':45B ''shield'':1A,5B,35B ''the'':4B,14B,23B,34B ''to'':46B ''tomb'':21B ''uncle'':30B ''used'':33B ''whil'':27B ''wield'':41B ''with'':13B ''ysgramor'':3A,7B,18B,32B', 'scholar', 'The Shield of Ysgramor is a legendary artifact from the Late Merethic Era, granting enhanced durability and resistance to magic. Buried with the Nord hero Ysgramor, it is a treasured relic of Nordic heritage.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('invocation_of_azura', 'Invocation of Azura, written by Sigillah Parate, is a work that emphasizes the author''s personal journey of devotion to Azura, the Daedric Princess of Moonshadow. The book recounts the author''s experiences as a priestess of Azura after having previously served under other Daedric Princes, including Molag Bal, Boethiah, and Nocturnal. It outlines the differences between these deities, highlighting Azura''s unique qualities—her compassion for her followers, the depth of her emotional engagement, and her focus on the genuine love and devotion of those who worship her. In contrast to the more impersonal and demanding nature of the other Daedric Princes, Azura’s attention to the emotional connection and self-reflection of her followers sets her apart.

The central theme of the book is the superiority of Azura over other Daedric Princes, as the author argues that Azura is not only a source of power but also a nurturing figure who cares deeply for her followers'' inner emotional states. This devotion to Azura, with its emphasis on authentic love and self-acceptance, is presented as both a personal and philosophical commitment. The work is part of a single volume, offering a reflective exploration of Daedric worship and the unique place of Azura in the pantheon of Tamriel’s divine figures.', '''acceptanc'':179B ''after'':42B ''also'':153B ''and'':54B,79B,86B,99B,114B,176B,186B,204B ''apart'':123B ''arg'':142B ''as'':37B,139B,182B ''attention'':109B ''authentic'':174B ''author'':17B,34B,141B ''azur'':3A,6B,24B,41B,64B,107B,134B,144B,169B,209B ''bal'':52B ''betw'':60B ''boethiah'':53B ''book'':31B,129B ''both'':183B ''but'':152B ''by'':8B ''car'':158B ''central'':125B ''commitment'':188B ''compassion'':69B ''connection'':113B ''contrast'':94B ''daedric'':26B,48B,105B,137B,202B ''deeply'':159B ''deiti'':62B ''demanding'':100B ''depth'':74B ''devotion'':22B,87B,167B ''differenc'':59B ''divin'':216B ''emotional'':77B,112B,164B ''emphasis'':172B ''emphasiz'':15B ''engagement'':78B ''experienc'':36B ''exploration'':200B ''figur'':156B,217B ''focus'':81B ''followers'':72B,120B,162B ''for'':70B,160B ''genuin'':84B ''having'':43B ''her'':68B,71B,76B,80B,92B,119B,122B,161B ''highlighting'':63B ''impersonal'':98B ''in'':93B,210B ''including'':50B ''inner'':163B ''invocation'':1A,4B ''is'':11B,130B,145B,180B,191B ''it'':56B ''its'':171B ''journey'':20B ''lov'':85B,175B ''molag'':51B ''moonshadow'':29B ''mor'':97B ''natur'':101B ''nocturnal'':55B ''not'':146B ''nurturing'':155B ''of'':2A,5B,21B,28B,40B,75B,88B,102B,118B,127B,133B,150B,193B,201B,208B,213B ''offering'':197B ''on'':82B,173B ''only'':147B ''other'':47B,104B,136B ''outlin'':57B ''over'':135B ''pantheon'':212B ''parat'':10B ''part'':192B ''personal'':19B,185B ''philosop