INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_legend_of_red_eagle', 'The Legend of Red Eagle, written by Tredayn Dren, Archivist of Winterhold, is an ancient tale about the invasion of the Reach by the First Empire. The story follows the rise and fall of Faolan, a child born in the Sundered Hills who becomes the legendary Red Eagle, a warrior destined to unite the Reach. As he grows in strength, he leads his people in rebellion against the invading Empress Hestra, but despite his fierce resistance, the Reach falls under Imperial control. Faolan makes a pact with an ancient Hagraven, gaining power at the cost of his humanity, and continues his fight for freedom. The tale ends with his death, but not before he swears his sword will be returned to his people when the Reach is finally free.

The story explores themes of destiny, sacrifice, and the consequences of power, particularly the cost of alliances made with dark forces. The narrative also emphasizes the unyielding spirit of the Reach and the eternal struggle for freedom against oppressive invaders. The legend, though rooted in the distant past, remains relevant in the context of the Reach''s long history of resistance and rebellion. This tale is one of many oral traditions about Red Eagle, suggesting it may have evolved over time, with varying elements added to the myth as it was passed down.', '''about'':22B,206B ''added'':219B ''against'':72B,172B ''allianc'':151B ''also'':158B ''an'':19B,93B ''ancient'':20B,94B ''and'':37B,104B,142B,166B,196B ''archivist'':15B ''as'':61B,223B ''at'':98B ''be'':124B ''becom'':49B ''befor'':118B ''born'':43B ''but'':77B,116B ''by'':12B,28B ''child'':42B ''consequenc'':144B ''context'':187B ''continu'':105B ''control'':87B ''cost'':100B,149B ''dark'':154B ''death'':115B ''despit'':78B ''destin'':56B ''destiny'':140B ''distant'':181B ''down'':227B ''dren'':14B ''eagl'':5A,10B,53B,208B ''elements'':218B ''emphasiz'':159B ''empir'':31B ''empress'':75B ''ends'':112B ''eternal'':168B ''evolv'':213B ''explor'':137B ''fall'':38B ''falls'':84B ''faol'':40B,88B ''fierc'':80B ''fight'':107B ''finally'':133B ''first'':30B ''follows'':34B ''for'':108B,170B ''forc'':155B ''fre'':134B ''freedom'':109B,171B ''gaining'':96B ''grows'':63B ''hagrav'':95B ''hav'':212B ''hestr'':76B ''hills'':47B ''his'':68B,79B,102B,106B,114B,121B,127B ''history'':193B ''humanity'':103B ''imperial'':86B ''in'':44B,64B,70B,179B,185B ''invaders'':174B ''invading'':74B ''invasion'':24B ''is'':18B,132B,200B ''it'':210B,224B ''leads'':67B ''legend'':2A,7B,176B ''legendary'':51B ''long'':192B ''mad'':152B ''mak'':89B ''many'':203B ''may'':211B ''myth'':222B ''narrativ'':157B ''not'':117B ''of'':3A,8B,16B,25B,39B,101B,139B,145B,150B,163B,188B,194B,202B ''one'':201B ''oppressiv'':173B ''oral'':204B ''over'