INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('myths_of_sheogorath', 'Myths of Sheogorath, written by Mymophonus, is a collection of magical and whimsical myths surrounding the Daedric Prince of Madness, Sheogorath. The myths are playful, bizarre, and illustrate Sheogorath’s chaotic nature. In one tale, Sheogorath invents music by transforming a woman into instruments, creating the first melodies for mortals. In another, he teaches King Lyandir a lesson in creativity and madness by ensuring every child born in the city is born mad, eventually leading to the king''s death at the hands of his deranged son. The final myth involves a wizard named Ravate, who seeks a favor from Sheogorath but is instead put through a test of sanity, eventually breaking his mind.

The themes of Myths of Sheogorath focus on the unpredictable and capricious nature of Sheogorath, illustrating his love for chaos and the absurdity of his actions. The myths explore the consequences of resisting creativity, the madness that often accompanies power, and the fine line between genius and insanity. Each story reflects Sheogorath’s influence on mortals, driving them toward madness, destruction, and eventual surrender to his will. The book is composed of multiple parts, each presenting a different myth that highlights various aspects of Sheogorath’s influence on the world.', '''absurdity'':140B ''accompani'':156B ''actions'':143B ''and'':15B,30B,64B,128B,138B,158B,164B,179B ''anoth'':55B ''are'':27B ''aspects'':200B ''at'':84B ''betw'':162B ''bizarr'':29B ''book'':186B ''born'':70B,75B ''breaking'':115B ''but'':105B ''by'':8B,42B,66B ''capricious'':129B ''cha'':137B ''chaotic'':34B ''child'':69B ''city'':73B ''collection'':12B ''comp'':188B ''consequenc'':148B ''creating'':48B ''creativity'':63B,151B ''daedric'':20B ''death'':83B ''derang'':89B ''destruction'':178B ''different'':195B ''driving'':174B ''each'':166B,192B ''ensuring'':67B ''eventual'':180B ''eventually'':77B,114B ''every'':68B ''explor'':146B ''favor'':102B ''fin'':160B ''final'':92B ''first'':50B ''focus'':124B ''for'':52B,136B ''from'':103B ''genius'':163B ''hands'':86B ''highlights'':198B ''his'':88B,116B,134B,142B,183B ''illustrat'':31B ''illustrating'':133B ''in'':36B,54B,62B,71B ''influenc'':171B,204B ''insanity'':165B ''inste'':107B ''instruments'':47B ''into'':46B ''invents'':40B ''involv'':94B ''is'':10B,74B,106B,187B ''king'':58B,81B ''leading'':78B ''lesson'':61B ''lin'':161B ''lov'':135B ''lyand'':59B ''mad'':76B ''madness'':23B,65B,153B,177B ''magical'':14B ''melodi'':51B ''mind'':117B ''mortals'':53B,173B ''multipl'':190B ''music'':41B ''mymophonus'':9B ''myth'':93B,196B ''myths'':1A,4B,17B,26B,121B,145B ''nam'':97B ''natur'':35B,130B ''of'':2A,5B,13B,22B,87B,112B,120B,122B,131