INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nords_arise', 'Nords Arise!, written by an anonymous author, is a passionate recruitment essay calling for rebellion against the Empire, urging the Nords of Skyrim to reject Imperial oppression. The essay appeals to the pride and heritage of the Nords, emphasizing their right to worship Talos, the god who rose from their homeland and who represents the honor and might of Skyrim. It criticizes the Empire for betraying the Nord people by forbidding the worship of Talos and accuses King Torygg of treason for agreeing to a pact with the Thalmor. Drawing parallels to historical events, such as Ysgramor’s war against the elves, the essay champions Ulfric Stormcloak as a hero who stands up against the Empire and the Thalmor.

The themes of resistance, national pride, and religious freedom are central to the essay. It emphasizes the historical struggles of the Nords against external threats and positions the Stormcloak rebellion as a righteous cause to reclaim their freedom and honor. This work calls for unity among the Nords, urging them to stand together against the Empire''s division and control. The essay is a rallying cry for rebellion, rooted in the mythic past and the belief in Talos’ divine power.', '''accus'':79B ''against'':18B,102B,116B,144B,175B ''agreeing'':85B ''among'':167B ''an'':7B ''and'':36B,54B,59B,78B,119B,128B,147B,160B,180B,195B ''anonymous'':8B ''appeals'':32B ''are'':131B ''aris'':2A,4B ''as'':98B,110B,152B ''author'':9B ''belief'':197B ''betraying'':68B ''by'':6B,72B ''calling'':15B ''calls'':164B ''caus'':155B ''central'':132B ''champions'':107B ''control'':181B ''criticiz'':64B ''cry'':187B ''divin'':200B ''division'':179B ''drawing'':92B ''elves'':104B ''emphasiz'':137B ''emphasizing'':41B ''empir'':20B,66B,118B,177B ''essay'':14B,31B,106B,135B,183B ''events'':96B ''external'':145B ''for'':16B,67B,84B,165B,188B ''forbidding'':73B ''freedom'':130B,159B ''from'':51B ''god'':48B ''her'':112B ''heritag'':37B ''historical'':95B,139B ''homeland'':53B ''honor'':58B,161B ''imperial'':28B ''in'':191B,198B ''is'':10B,184B ''it'':63B,136B ''king'':80B ''might'':60B ''mythic'':193B ''national'':126B ''nord'':70B ''nords'':1A,3B,23B,40B,143B,169B ''of'':24B,38B,61B,76B,82B,124B,141B ''oppression'':29B ''pact'':88B ''parallels'':93B ''passionat'':12B ''past'':194B ''peopl'':71B ''positions'':148B ''pow'':201B ''prid'':35B,127B ''rallying'':186B ''rebellion'':17B,151B,189B ''reclaim'':157B ''recruitment'':13B ''reject'':27B ''religious'':129B ''represents'':56B ''resistanc'':125B ''right'':43B ''righteous'':154B ''root'':190B ''ros'':50B ''s'':100B,178B ''skyrim'':25B,62B ''stand'':173B ''stands'':114B ''stormcloak'':109B,150B ''struggl'':140B ''such'':97B ''tal'':46B,77B,19