INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('olaf_and_the_dragon', 'Olaf and the Dragon, written by Adonato Leotelli, explores the legendary tale of Olaf One-Eye, a hero who defeated the dragon Numinex in an epic battle for Skyrim''s future. The dragon, a terrifying force that had ravaged Skyrim, was eventually confronted by Olaf, a warrior who would later become the High King of Skyrim. The legend tells of Olaf''s battle against Numinex atop Mount Athor, where the two engage in a brutal shouting contest that shatters the land. Ultimately, Olaf triumphs, capturing the dragon and bringing him to Whiterun, where the beast is imprisoned in a place that would become known as Dragonsreach. Olaf''s victory solidifies his leadership, ending a bitter war of succession among Skyrim''s holds.

Themes of heroism, power, and the distortion of history are prevalent throughout the work. Leotelli presents Olaf''s victory as a symbol of Nordic strength and unity, though he acknowledges doubts surrounding the legend''s authenticity. Alternative versions of the story suggest that Numinex was already weak due to age, and that Olaf and his men may have fabricated the tale for personal gain. The account also references a rebellious bard, Svaknir, who challenged Olaf''s version, adding an intriguing layer of historical ambiguity. The book raises important questions about how history is remembered and the ways in which legends are shaped by those in power.', '''about'':217B ''account'':193B ''acknowledg'':157B ''adding'':205B ''adonat'':11B ''against'':69B ''age'':177B ''already'':173B ''also'':194B ''alternativ'':164B ''ambiguity'':211B ''among'':124B ''an'':30B,206B ''and'':2A,6B,93B,132B,153B,178B,181B,222B ''are'':137B,228B ''as'':110B,147B ''athor'':73B ''atop'':71B ''authenticity'':163B ''bard'':198B ''battl'':32B,68B ''beast'':100B ''becom'':56B,108B ''bitt'':120B ''book'':213B ''bringing'':94B ''brutal'':80B ''by'':10B,49B,230B ''capturing'':90B ''challeng'':201B ''confront'':48B ''contest'':82B ''defeat'':25B ''distortion'':134B ''doubts'':158B ''dragon'':4A,8B,27B,38B,92B ''dragonsreach'':111B ''due'':175B ''ending'':118B ''engag'':77B ''epic'':31B ''eventually'':47B ''explor'':13B ''eye'':21B ''fabricat'':186B ''for'':33B,189B ''forc'':41B ''futur'':36B ''gain'':191B ''had'':43B ''hav'':185B ''her'':23B ''heroism'':130B ''high'':58B ''him'':95B ''his'':116B,182B ''historical'':210B ''history'':136B,219B ''holds'':127B ''how'':218B ''important'':215B ''imprison'':102B ''in'':29B,78B,103B,225B,232B ''intriguing'':207B ''is'':101B,220B ''king'':59B ''known'':109B ''land'':86B ''lat'':55B ''lay'':208B ''leadership'':117B ''legend'':63B,161B ''legendary'':15B ''legends'':227B ''leotelli'':12B,142B ''may'':184B ''men'':183B ''mount'':72B ''nordic'':151B ''numinex