INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('staff_of_magnus', 'Staff of Magnus is an ancient and powerful artifact in Tamriel, originally created by Arch-Mage Magnus, the God of Magic. It is often referred to as the Golden Staff and is believed to have served as a metaphysical battery during its creator''s time in Mundus. After Magnus fled, the staff remained behind and has since been associated with various legends; some consider it a gift, others a theft, and some even view it as a test for mortals.', '''after'':52B ''an'':8B ''ancient'':9B ''and'':10B,35B,59B,75B ''arch'':19B ''arch-mag'':18B ''artifact'':12B ''as'':31B,41B,80B ''associat'':63B ''battery'':44B ''been'':62B ''behind'':58B ''believ'':37B ''by'':17B ''consid'':68B ''creat'':16B ''creator'':47B ''during'':45B ''even'':77B ''fled'':54B ''for'':83B ''gift'':71B ''god'':23B ''gold'':33B ''hav'':39B ''in'':13B,50B ''is'':7B,27B,36B ''it'':26B,69B,79B ''its'':46B ''legends'':66B ''mag'':20B ''magic'':25B ''magnus'':3A,6B,21B,53B ''metaphysical'':43B ''mortals'':84B ''mundus'':51B ''of'':2A,5B,24B ''often'':28B ''originally'':15B ''others'':72B ''powerful'':11B ''referr'':29B ''remain'':57B ''s'':48B ''serv'':40B ''sinc'':61B ''som'':67B,76B ''staff'':1A,4B,34B,56B ''tamriel'':14B ''test'':82B ''the'':22B,32B,55B ''theft'':74B ''tim'':49B ''to'':30B,38B ''various'':65B ''view'':78B ''with'':64B', 'collegeofwinterhold, scholar, mage, priest', 'The Staff of Magnus is an ancient artifact created by the God of Magic, Magnus, known for its immense power and connection to Tamriel''s magical energy. It is surrounded by legends, seen as a gift, a theft, or a test for mortals.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('short_history_of_morrowind', '
A Short History of Morrowind, written by Jeanette Sitte, provides a comprehensive overview of the history of Morrowind, from the earliest Dunmer migrations to the region, to its integration into the Empire and the challenges it faces in the Fourth Era. The book highlights the rise of the Dunmer as a powerful people under the leadership of the Tribunal Temple and the eventual consolidation of their tribes into the Great House system. It also discusses the political dynamics of Morrowind under Imperial rule, including the complexities of governance, religion, and internal strife. The introduction delves into the relationship between the Dunmer and the Empire, particularly how Morrowind was one of the last provinces to peacefully join the Empire.

The section on Vvardenfell focuses on the dramatic changes to the island after its reorganization into an Imperial Provincial District in 3E 414. It describes the competition for control of the land between the Great Houses, the Temple, and the Empire, as well as the external threats posed by Ashlanders, House rivalries, and the growing danger of the Red Mountain blight. The book explores themes of colonization, power struggles, and environmental hazards, particularly the threat of Dagoth Ur and his forces. The narrative underscores the political instability and challenges faced by both the Imperial and Dunmer leadership, offering insight into the precarious situation on Vvardenfell.', '''3e'':144B ''414'':145B ''after'':135B ''also'':78B ''an'':139B ''and'':37B,65B,94B,106B,161B,175B,192B,201B,210B,217B ''as'':54B,164B,166B ''ashlanders'':172B ''betw'':103B,155B ''blight'':183B ''book'':47B,185B ''both'':214B ''by'':11B,171B,213B ''challeng'':39B,211B ''chang'':131B ''colonization'':189B ''competition'':149B ''complexiti'':90B ''comprehensiv'':16B ''consolidation'':68B ''control'':151B ''dagoth'':199B ''dang'':178B ''delv'':99B ''describ'':147B ''discuss'':79B ''district'':142B ''dramatic'':130B ''dunm'':26B,53B,105B,218B ''dynamics'':82B ''earliest'':25B ''empir'':36B,108B,122B,163B ''environmental'':193B ''eventual'':67B ''explor'':186B ''external'':168B ''fac'':41B,212B ''focus'':127B ''for'':150B ''forc'':203B ''fourth'':44B ''from'':23B ''governanc'':92B ''great'':74B,157B ''growing'':177B ''hazards'':194B ''highlights'':48B ''his'':202B ''history'':2A,7B,20B ''hous'':75B,158B,173B ''how'':110B ''imperial'':86B,140B,216B ''in'':42B,143B ''including'':88B ''insight'':221B ''instability'':209B ''integration'':33B ''internal'':95B ''into'':34B,72B,100B,138B,222B ''introduction'':98B ''island'':134B ''it'':40B,77B,146B ''its'':32B,136B ''jeanett'':12B ''join'':120B ''land'':154B ''last'':116B ''leadership'':60B,219B ''migrations'':27B ''morrowind'':4A,9B,22B,84B,1