INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('palla', 'Palla, written by Vojne Mierstyyd, is a tragic tale of a conjurer''s obsession with a woman he believes to be the epitome of beauty and strength. The narrator, an initiate at the Mages Guild in Mir Corrup, becomes infatuated with a statue of a woman named Palla, depicted in a heroic struggle with a monstrous figure. As he becomes more obsessed, he learns that Palla was a fierce warrior who died in battle, leaving behind a daughter, Betaniqi. Despite knowing Palla is deceased, the narrator seeks to resurrect her through necromantic means, using an artifact he finds. His obsession grows as he immerses himself in the study of enchantment, convinced that his love will be strong enough to bring her back.

The story explores themes of obsession, love, and the dangerous consequences of seeking to defy death. The narrator’s fixation on Palla blinds him to reality, and in the end, he learns too late that he had misunderstood the nature of the woman he loved. The narrative is both a commentary on the destructive power of unrequited love and a reflection on the perilous boundaries between life, death, and magic. Palla is presented in two volumes, each deepening the tragic nature of the conjurer''s infatuation and his ultimate downfall.', '''an'':31B,96B ''and'':27B,131B,150B,182B,192B,210B ''artifact'':97B ''as'':59B,103B ''at'':33B ''back'':123B ''battl'':75B ''be'':22B,117B ''beauty'':26B ''becom'':40B,61B ''behind'':77B ''believ'':20B ''betaniqi'':80B ''betw'':189B ''blinds'':146B ''both'':172B ''boundari'':188B ''bring'':121B ''by'':4B ''commentary'':174B ''conjur'':13B,207B ''consequenc'':134B ''convinc'':112B ''corrup'':39B ''dangerous'':133B ''daught'':79B ''death'':139B,191B ''deceas'':85B ''deepening'':201B ''defy'':138B ''depict'':50B ''despit'':81B ''destructiv'':177B ''died'':73B ''downfall'':213B ''each'':200B ''enchantment'':111B ''end'':153B ''enough'':119B ''epitom'':24B ''explor'':126B ''fierc'':70B ''figur'':58B ''finds'':99B ''fixation'':143B ''grows'':102B ''guild'':36B ''had'':160B ''her'':91B,122B ''heroic'':53B ''him'':147B ''himself'':106B ''his'':100B,114B,211B ''immers'':105B ''in'':37B,51B,74B,107B,151B,197B ''infatuat'':41B ''infatuation'':209B ''initiat'':32B ''is'':7B,84B,171B,195B ''knowing'':82B ''lat'':157B ''learns'':65B,155B ''leaving'':76B ''lif'':190B ''lov'':115B,130B,168B,181B ''mag'':35B ''magic'':193B ''means'':94B ''mierstyyd'':6B ''mir'':38B ''misunderstood'':161B ''monstrous'':57B ''mor'':62B ''nam'':48B ''narrativ'':170B ''narrator'':30B,87B,141B ''natur'':163B,204B ''necromantic'':93B ''obsess'':63B ''obsession'':15B,101B,129B ''of'':11B,25B,45B,110B,128B,135B,164B,179B,205B ''on'':144B,175B,185B ''pall'':1A,2B,49B,67B,83B,145B