INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('where_were_you_when_the_dragon_broke', '
Where Were You When the Dragon Broke?, written by Various authors, is a collection of accounts and perspectives on the mysterious and enigmatic event known as the Dragon Break. The text explores the concept of the "Middle Dawn," a period marked by strange, chaotic shifts in time, reality, and space. Various characters from different cultures in Tamriel—such as Corax from Cyrodiil, Mehra Nabisi of the Dunmer, and R''leyt-harhr of the Khajiit—offer their interpretations of the Dragon Break, with each presenting a different understanding of its causes, effects, and significance. Some describe it as a cosmic disturbance, others as a breakdown in the flow of time itself, and still others see it as a divine manipulation or even a manifestation of Lorkhan’s will.

The themes of this text revolve around the fluidity of time, the instability of reality, and the conflicting accounts of history and prophecy across cultures. The book reflects on the nature of divine influence, fate, and how different peoples of Tamriel interpret cosmic events through their own religious and cultural lenses. The Dragon Break, a moment when time seemingly fractured and events occurred in multiple realities simultaneously, is central to the narrative, with characters wrestling with the consequences of such a paradoxical occurrence. The work emphasizes the concept of multiple truths existing simultaneously, depending on one’s perspective, and the impossibility of fully understanding the mysteries of the universe. This book presents an intriguing look at one of Tamriel''s most profound and enigmatic events.', '''accounts'':23B,154B ''across'':159B ''an'':248B ''and'':24B,29B,56B,75B,100B,119B,151B,157B,171B,184B,196B,234B,258B ''around'':142B ''as'':33B,66B,105B,110B,124B ''at'':251B ''authors'':18B ''book'':162B,246B ''break'':36B,89B,189B ''breakdown'':112B ''brok'':7A,14B ''by'':16B,49B ''caus'':98B ''central'':204B ''chaotic'':51B ''characters'':59B,209B ''collection'':21B ''concept'':41B,223B ''conflicting'':153B ''consequenc'':213B ''corax'':67B ''cosmic'':107B,178B ''cultur'':62B,160B ''cultural'':185B ''cyrodiil'':69B ''dawn'':45B ''depending'':229B ''describ'':103B ''different'':61B,94B,173B ''disturbanc'':108B ''divin'':126B,168B ''dragon'':6A,13B,35B,88B,188B ''dunm'':74B ''each'':91B ''effects'':99B ''emphasiz'':221B ''enigmatic'':30B,259B ''even'':129B ''event'':31B ''events'':179B,197B,260B ''existing'':227B ''explor'':39B ''fat'':170B ''flow'':115B ''fluidity'':144B ''fractur'':195B ''from'':60B,68B ''fully'':238B ''harhr'':79B ''history'':156B ''how'':172B ''impossibility'':236B ''in'':53B,63B,113B,199B ''influenc'':169B ''instability'':148B ''interpret'':177B ''interpretations'':85B ''intriguing'':249B ''is'':19B,203B ''it'':104B,123B 