INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_wild_elves', 'The Wild Elves, written by Kier-Jo Chorvak, provides an overview of the Ayleids, often called the Wild Elves, who have remained secluded from the mainstream cultures of Tamriel. While the other Elven races—the Altmer, Bosmer, and Dunmer—have integrated into society, the Ayleids continue to follow their ancient customs, living far from civilization. They speak a variation of Old Cyrodilic and maintain a dark and reserved demeanor that contrasts with the more familiar Elven cultures. Although outsiders view them with suspicion, scholars like Tjurhane Fyrre offer a different perspective, suggesting that the Ayleids have a vibrant and multifaceted culture.

The book explores themes of cultural isolation, fear of the unknown, and the complexity of ancient traditions. The Ayleids'' refusal to assimilate into Tamrielic society has led to their enigmatic status, with little documented history to illuminate their ways. Their mysterious nature, combined with their elusive presence in history, has kept them one of the most enigmatic peoples of Tamriel. Chorvak''s work underscores how the Ayleids'' reluctance to engage with the outside world has preserved their culture, but also left them shrouded in myth and legend. The book is a single volume and serves as a brief yet intriguing introduction to a largely forgotten race of elves.', '''also'':185B ''although'':82B ''altmer'':40B ''an'':14B ''ancient'':54B,121B ''and'':42B,67B,71B,103B,117B,191B,199B ''as'':201B ''assimilat'':127B ''ayleids'':18B,49B,99B,124B,172B ''book'':107B,194B ''bosm'':41B ''brief'':203B ''but'':184B ''by'':8B ''call'':20B ''chorvak'':12B,166B ''civilization'':59B ''combin'':148B ''complexity'':119B ''continu'':50B ''contrasts'':75B ''cultur'':31B,81B,105B,183B ''cultural'':111B ''customs'':55B ''cyrodilic'':66B ''dark'':70B ''demeanor'':73B ''different'':94B ''document'':139B ''dunm'':43B ''elusiv'':151B ''elven'':37B,80B ''elves'':3A,6B,23B,213B ''engag'':175B ''enigmatic'':135B,162B ''explor'':108B ''famili'':79B ''far'':57B ''fear'':113B ''follow'':52B ''forgott'':210B ''from'':28B,58B ''fyrre'':91B ''hav'':25B,44B,100B ''history'':140B,154B ''how'':170B ''illuminat'':142B ''in'':153B,189B ''integrat'':45B ''into'':46B,128B ''intriguing'':205B ''introduction'':206B ''is'':195B ''isolation'':112B ''jo'':11B ''kept'':156B ''kier'':10B ''kier-j'':9B ''largely'':209B ''led'':132B ''left'':186B ''legend'':192B ''lik'':89B ''littl'':138B ''living'':56B ''mainstream'':30B ''maintain'':68B ''mor'':78B ''most'':161B ''multifacet'':104B ''mysterious'':146B ''myth'':190B ''natur'':147B ''of'':16B,32B,64B,110B,114B,120B,159B,164B,212B ''offer'':92B ''often'':19B 