For the darkness has passed, and the legend yet grows.
You''ll know, You''ll know the Dragonborn''s come.', '''all'':51B ''an'':45B ''ancient'':35B ''and'':65B ''art'':37B ''believ'':38B,39B ''bewar'':55B,56B ''claims'':14B ''com'':3A,8B,27B,42B,59B,79B ''darkness'':62B ''dragonborn'':2A,7B,26B,41B,58B,77B ''end'':46B ''evil'':49B ''foes'':54B ''for'':5B,60B ''grows'':69B ''heart'':18B ''her'':11B,13B ''i'':19B,22B ''it'':43B ''know'':72B,75B ''legend'':67B ''ll'':71B,74B ''nord'':36B ''of'':33B,50B ''our'':10B,12B ''pass'':64B ''pow'':32B ''s'':17B,44B,53B,78B ''skyrim'':52B ''song'':9B ''tell'':20B,23B ''the'':1A,6B,25B,34B,40B,48B,57B,61B,66B,76B ''to'':47B ''vers'':4B ''voic'':30B ''warrior'':16B ''wielding'':31B ''with'':28B ''yet'':68B ''you'':21B,24B,70B,73B', 'bard, scholar', 'The Dragonborn Comes song speaks of the arrival of the Dragonborn, a legendary hero with the power of the ancient Nord Voice, destined to vanquish evil and bring an end to Skyrim''s foes, with their legend growing as they fulfill their destiny. You don''t know the lyrics by heart.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('unknown_potion', 'This is a mysterious potion that appears when mixing ingredients with unknown effects. Its purpose is experimental, and it cannot be obtained normally.', '''and'':20B ''appears'':9B ''be'':23B ''cannot'':22B ''effects'':15B ''experimental'':19B ''ingredients'':12B ''is'':4B,18B ''it'':21B ''its'':16B ''mixing'':11B ''mysterious'':6B ''normally'':25B ''obtain'':24B ''potion'':2A,7B ''purpos'':17B ''that'':8B ''this'':3B ''unknown'':1A,14B ''when'':10B ''with'':13B', 'blocked', 'You have no knowledge of this potion or its effects. You guess that''s why it''s called ''unknown''.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_age_of_oppression', 'Verses for The Age of Oppression song:
We drink to our youth, and to days come and gone. For the age of oppression is now nearly done.
We''ll drive out the Empire from this land that we own. With our blood and our steel we will take back our home.
All hail to Ulfric! You are the High King! In your great honor we drink and we sing.
We''re the children of Skyrim, and we fight all our lives. And when Sovngarde beckons, every one of us dies!
But this land is ours and we''ll see it wiped clean. Of the scourge that has sullied our hopes and our dreams.', '''age'':2A,8B,25B ''all'':56B,83B ''and'':17B,21B,47B,71B,80B,86B,100B,115B ''are'':61B ''back'':53B ''beckons'':89B ''blood'':46B ''but'':95B ''childr'':77B ''cle'':106B ''com'':20B ''days'':19B ''dies'':94B ''don'':31B ''dreams'':117B ''drink'':13B,70B ''driv'':34B ''empir'':37B ''every'':90B ''fight'':82B ''for'':6B,23B ''from'':38B ''gon'':22B ''great'':67B ''hail'':57B ''high'':63B ''hom'':55B ''honor'':68B ''hop'':114B ''in'':65B ''is'':28B,98B ''it'':104B ''king'':64B ''land'':40B,97B ''liv'':85B ''ll'':33B,102B ''nearly'':30B ''now'':29B ''of'':3A,9B,26B,78B,92B,107B ''one'':91B ''oppression'':4A,10B,27B ''our'':15B,45B,48B,54B,84B,113B,116B ''ours'':99B ''out'':35B ''own'':43B ''re'':75B ''scourg'':109B ''see'':103B ''sing'':73B ''skyrim'':79B ''song'':11B ''sovngard'':88B ''steel'':49B ''sulli'':112B ''tak'':52B ''that'':41B,110B ''the'':1A,7B,24B,36B,62B,76B,108B ''this'':39B,96B ''to'':14B,18B,58B ''ulfric'':59B ''us'':93B ''vers'':5B ''we'':12B,32B,42B,50B,69B,72B,74B,81B,101B ''when'':87B ''will'':51B ''wip'':105B ''with'':44B ''you'':60B ''your'':66B ''youth'':16B', 'bard, scholar', 'The Age of Oppression song celebrates the defiance of the Nords against the Empire, with a call to reclaim their homeland through blood and steel, honoring their leader Ulfric and vowing to fight until their last breath to preserve Skyrim and its legacy. You don''t know the lyrics by heart.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bloodworm_helm', '
The Bloodworm Helm is a necromantic artifact crafted by the lich Mannimarco from trollbone, known for its unsettling beauty and dark powers. The helm enhances Conjuration skills, allows the wearer to turn undead, drain enemy essence, and summon a skeletal minion. For undead wearers, it also strengthens their attacks. Mannimarco left the helm behind upon ascending to godhood during the Warp in the West.', '''allows'':30B ''also'':48B ''and'':22B,39B ''artifact'':9B ''ascending'':58B ''attacks'':51B ''beauty'':21B ''behind'':56B ''bloodworm'':1A,4B ''by'':11B ''conjuration'':28B ''craft'':10B ''dark'':23B ''drain'':36B ''during'':61B ''enemy'':37B ''enhanc'':27B ''essenc'':38B ''for'':18B,44B ''from'':15B ''godhood'':60B ''helm'':2A,5B,26B,55B ''in'':64B ''is'':6B ''it'':47B ''its'':19B ''known'':17B ''left'':53B ''lich'':13B ''mannimarc'':14B,52B ''minion'':43B ''necromantic'':8B ''powers'':24B ''skeletal'':42B ''skills'':29B ''strengthens'':49B ''summon'':40B ''the'':3B,12B,25B,31B,50B,54B,62B,65B ''to'':33B,59B ''trollbon'':16B ''turn'':34B ''unde'':35B,45B ''unsettling'':20B ''upon'':57B ''warp'':63B ''wear'':32B ''wearers'':46B ''west'':66B', 'scholar', '
The Bloodworm Helm is a necromantic artifact created by Mannimarco, enhancing Conjuration, turning undead, and summoning minions. Left behind during Mannimarco''s ascent to godhood, it also boosts attacks for undead wearers.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('akatosh', 'Akatosh, also known by different names such as Auri-El to the elves and Alkosh to the Khajiit, is the chief deity of the Nine Divines in Tamrielic religion. He is revered as the Dragon God of Time, the patron of endurance, invincibility, and legitimacy, and is often depicted as a golden dragon. As one of the first Aedric spirits to form at the beginning of time, Akatosh holds a central place in many cultures, symbolizing both the orderly progression of time and the eternal stability of the Empire. His worship extends across Tamriel, where he is seen as the father of all dragons, and Alduin, a god of destruction in Nordic myth, is considered a controversial aspect of Akatosh.

Akatosh is also closely associated with the founding of the Cyrodilic Empire. His blood was mystically joined with that of the first human Empress, Alessia, creating a divine covenant that protected the Empire from Daedric influence, symbolized by the Amulet of Kings. His role in maintaining the cosmic order is further emphasized during significant historical events like the Oblivion Crisis, where the Septim Emperor Martin transformed into Akatosh''s fiery avatar to defeat the Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon. Akatosh is revered as the guardian of time and the embodiment of divine order, with his influence felt in the very fabric of the world.', '''across'':95B ''aedric'':61B ''akatosh'':1A,2B,70B,122B,123B,190B,201B ''alduin'':108B ''alessi'':147B ''alkosh'':17B ''all'':105B ''also'':3B,125B ''amulet'':162B ''and'':16B,46B,48B,85B,107B,209B ''as'':9B,35B,52B,56B,101B,204B ''aspect'':120B ''associat'':127B ''at'':65B ''auri'':11B ''auri-el'':10B ''avat'':193B ''beginning'':67B ''blood'':136B ''both'':79B ''by'':5B,160B ''central'':73B ''chief'':23B ''closely'':126B ''consider'':117B ''controversial'':119B ''cosmic'':170B ''covenant'':151B ''creating'':148B ''crisis'':182B ''cultur'':77B ''cyrodilic'':133B ''daedric'':157B,197B ''dagon'':200B ''defeat'':195B ''deity'':24B ''depict'':51B ''destruction'':112B ''different'':6B ''divin'':28B,150B,213B ''dragon'':37B,55B ''dragons'':106B ''during'':175B ''elves'':15B ''embodiment'':211B ''emperor'':186B ''emphasiz'':174B ''empir'':91B,134B,155B ''empress'':146B ''enduranc'':44B ''eternal'':87B ''events'':178B ''extends'':94B ''fabric'':222B ''fath'':103B ''felt'':218B ''fiery'':192B ''first'':60B,144B ''form'':64B ''founding'':130B ''from'':156B ''furth'':173B ''god'':38B,110B ''gold'':54B ''guardi'':206B ''his'':92B,135B,165B,216B ''historical'':177B ''holds'':71B ''hum'':145B ''in'':29B,75B,113B,167B,219B ''influenc'':158B,217B ''into'':189B ''invincibility'':45B ''is'':21B,33B,49B,99B,116B,124B,172B,202B ''join'':139B ''khajiit'':20B ''kings'':164B ''known'':4B ''legitimacy'':47B ''lik'':179B ''maintaining'':168B ''many'':76B ''martin'':187B ''mehrun'':199B ''mystically'':138B ''myth'':115B ''nam'':7B ''nin'':27B ''nordic'':114B ''oblivion'':181B ''of'':25B,39B,43B,58B,68B,83B,89B,104B,111B,121B,131B,142B,163B,207B,212B,223B ''often'':50B ''one'':57B ''order'':171B,214B ''orderly'':81B ''patron'':42B ''plac'':74B ''princ'':198B ''progression'':82B ''protect'':153B ''religion'':31B ''rever'':34B,203B ''rol'':166B ''s'':191B ''seen'':100B ''septim'':185B ''significant'':176B ''spirits'':62B ''stability'':88B ''such'':8B ''symboliz'':159B ''symbolizing'':78B ''tamriel'':96B ''tamrielic'':30B ''that'':141B,152B ''the'':14B,19B,22B,26B,36B,41B,59B,66B,80B,86B,90B,102B,129B,132B,143B,154B,161B,169B,180B,184B,196B,205B,210B,220B,224B ''tim'':40B,69B,84B,208B ''to'':13B,18B,63B,194B ''transform'':188B ''very'':221B ''was'':137B ''wher'':97B,183B ''with'':128B,140B,215B ''world'':225B ''worship'':93B', 'priest, snowelf, scholar, dragon', 'Akatosh, the Dragon God of Time, is a powerful and honored deity in Tamriel, often seen as a golden dragon. He represents endurance, order, and the steady flow of time. Worshiped across the land, Akatosh is said to be the father of all dragons and played a key role in protecting the Empire through a divine bond with its first ruler, Alessia. His influence is felt in great events like the Oblivion Crisis, where his avatar defeated a Daedric prince to save the world. To many, he symbolizes stability, time’s guardianship, and the Empire’s divine right to rule.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('calvicus_vile', 'Clavicus Vile is a Daedric Prince associated with trickery, bargains, and the granting of wishes. Known as the Prince of Trickery and Bargains, Clavicus enjoys making pacts with mortals, often granting them their desires in ways that benefit him or lead to unintended consequences. He is often depicted alongside his loyal companion, Barbas, a shapeshifting Daedra who frequently takes the form of a dog. Barbas holds a portion of Clavicus Vile''s power, leading to speculation that the two may be halves of the same being. Vile''s realm, the Fields of Regret, is a tranquil and idyllic landscape that reflects his playful but deceptive nature.

Clavicus Vile is known for his sophisticated and calculating approach, making deals that often ensnare those who seek his help. Despite his love for manipulation, he is not always malevolent and has, on occasion, acted in ways that benefit the greater good, though always with his interests in mind. His notable artifacts include the Masque of Clavicus Vile, which grants charm to its wearer, and the Umbra Sword, a soul-trapping blade tied to sentient power. Clavicus Vile is regarded as one of the more neutral Daedric Princes, though his bargains often come with hidden costs.', '''acted'':143B ''alongsid'':51B ''always'':137B,152B ''and'':13B,24B,99B,116B,139B,173B ''approach'':118B ''artifacts'':160B ''as'':19B,190B ''associat'':9B ''barb'':55B,67B ''bargains'':12B,25B,200B ''be'':83B ''being'':88B ''benefit'':40B,147B ''blad'':181B ''but'':106B ''calculating'':117B ''calvicus'':1A ''charm'':169B ''clavicus'':3B,26B,72B,109B,165B,186B ''com'':202B ''companion'':54B ''consequenc'':46B ''costs'':205B ''daedr'':58B ''daedric'':7B,196B ''deals'':120B ''deceptiv'':107B ''depict'':50B ''desir'':36B ''despit'':129B ''dog'':66B ''enjoys'':27B ''ensnar'':123B ''fields'':93B ''for'':113B,132B ''form'':63B ''frequently'':60B ''good'':150B ''granting'':15B,33B ''grants'':168B ''great'':149B ''halv'':84B ''help'':128B ''hidd'':204B ''him'':41B ''his'':52B,104B,114B,127B,130B,154B,158B,199B ''holds'':68B ''idyllic'':100B ''in'':37B,144B,156B ''includ'':161B ''interests'':155B ''is'':5B,48B,96B,111B,135B,188B ''its'':171B ''known'':18B,112B ''landscap'':101B ''lead'':43B ''leading'':76B ''lov'':131B ''loyal'':53B ''making'':28B,119B ''malevolent'':138B ''manipulation'':133B ''masqu'':163B ''may'':82B ''mind'':157B ''mor'':194B ''mortals'':31B ''natur'':108B ''neutral'':195B ''not'':136B ''notabl'':159B ''occasion'':142B ''of'':16B,22B,64B,71B,85B,94B,164B,192B ''often'':32B,49B,122B,201B ''on'':141B ''one'':191B ''or'':42B ''pacts'':29B ''playful'':105B ''portion'':70B ''pow'':75B,185B ''princ'':8B,21B,197B ''realm'':91B ''reflects'':103B ''regard'':189B ''regret'':95B ''s'':74B,90B ''sam'':87B ''seek'':126B ''sentient'':184B ''shapeshifting'':57B ''sophisticat'':115B ''soul'':179B ''soul-trapping'':178B ''speculation'':78B ''sword'':176B ''tak'':61B ''that'':39B,79B,102B,121B,146B ''the'':14B,20B,35B,62B,80B,86B,92B,148B,162B,174B,193B ''them'':34B ''thos'':124B ''though'':151B,198B ''tied'':182B ''to'':44B,77B,170B,183B ''tranquil'':98B ''trapping'':180B ''trickery'':11B,23B ''two'':81B ''umbra'':175B ''unintend'':45B ''vil'':2A,4B,73B,89B,110B,166B,187B ''ways'':38B,145B ''wear'':172B ''which'':167B ''who'':59B,125B ''wish'':17B ''with'':10B,30B,153B,203B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Clavicus Vile, the Daedric Prince of Trickery and Bargains, is known for making pacts with mortals, granting their desires in ways that often lead to unintended consequences. Accompanied by Barbas, a shapeshifting Daedra who may be an extension of himself, Clavicus resides in the Fields of Regret, a deceptive yet tranquil realm. His deals are sophisticated and calculating, sometimes benefiting mortals but always serving his own interests. Notable artifacts tied to him include the Masque of Clavicus Vile, which enhances charm, and the Umbra Sword, a soul-trapping blade with sentient power. Clavicus Vile is seen as a neutral figure among the Daedric Princes, offering rewards that often come with hidden costs.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dibella', 'Dibella is the Goddess of Beauty, Love, and Art, often referred to as the Lady of Love or the Passion Dancer. As one of the Divines, Dibella embodies the ideals of beauty, affection, and artistic expression. She teaches mortals to seek truth through beauty, encouraging the cultivation of love, friendship, and artistic inspiration. Dibella''s followers, through devotion to her teachings, are believed to gain charm, grace, and harmony in their lives. She also emphasizes the importance of quality in love, rather than quantity, and discourages relationships with those of impure spirits, such as the undead.

Worship of Dibella is widespread across Tamriel, with different regions venerating various aspects of her divinity. In Cyrodiil, Hammerfell, High Rock, and Skyrim, numerous cults and temples are dedicated to her, some focusing on women, art, or erotic instruction. Dibella’s influence is deeply personal, with her worshipers often engaging in intimate, direct relationships with their goddess. Her sacred places include the Temple of Dibella in Markarth, where the Sybil, a spiritual leader chosen through a secretive ceremony, serves as her earthly representative. Dibella is also associated with the Brush of Truepaint, an artifact said to have the power to bring artistic creations to life.', '''across'':103B ''affection'':34B ''also'':75B,183B ''an'':190B ''and'':9B,35B,52B,69B,86B,119B,123B ''are'':63B,125B ''art'':10B,133B ''artifact'':191B ''artistic'':36B,53B,199B ''as'':14B,23B,95B,177B ''aspects'':110B ''associat'':184B ''beauty'':7B,33B,45B ''believ'':64B ''bring'':198B ''brush'':187B ''ceremony'':175B ''charm'':67B ''chos'':171B ''creations'':200B ''cultivation'':48B ''cults'':122B ''cyrodiil'':115B ''danc'':22B ''dedicat'':126B ''deeply'':141B ''devotion'':59B ''dibell'':1A,2B,28B,55B,100B,137B,162B,181B ''different'':106B ''direct'':150B ''discourag'':87B ''divin'':27B ''divinity'':113B ''earthly'':179B ''embodi'':29B ''emphasiz'':76B ''encouraging'':46B ''engaging'':147B ''erotic'':135B ''expression'':37B ''focusing'':130B ''followers'':57B ''friendship'':51B ''gain'':66B ''goddess'':5B,154B ''grac'':68B ''hammerfell'':116B ''harmony'':70B ''hav'':194B ''her'':61B,112B,128B,144B,155B,178B ''high'':117B ''ideals'':31B ''importanc'':78B ''impur'':92B ''in'':71B,81B,114B,148B,163B ''includ'':158B ''influenc'':139B ''inspiration'':54B ''instruction'':136B ''intimat'':149B ''is'':3B,101B,140B,182B ''lady'':16B ''lead'':170B ''lif'':202B ''liv'':73B ''lov'':8B,18B,50B,82B ''markarth'':164B ''mortals'':40B ''numerous'':121B ''of'':6B,17B,25B,32B,49B,79B,91B,99B,111B,161B,188B ''often'':11B,146B ''on'':131B ''one'':24B ''or'':19B,134B ''passion'':21B ''personal'':142B ''plac'':157B ''pow'':196B ''quality'':80B ''quantity'':85B ''rath'':83B ''referr'':12B ''regions'':107B ''relationships'':88B,151B ''representativ'':180B ''rock'':118B ''s'':56B,138B ''sacr'':156B ''said'':192B ''secretiv'':174B ''seek'':42B ''serv'':176B ''she'':38B,74B ''skyrim'':120B ''som'':129B ''spirits'':93B ''spiritual'':169B ''such'':94B ''sybil'':167B ''tamriel'':104B ''teach'':39B ''teachings'':62B ''templ'':124B,160B ''than'':84B ''the'':4B,15B,20B,26B,30B,47B,72B,77B,96B,153B,159B,166B,186B,195B ''thos'':90B ''through'':44B,58B,172B ''to'':13B,41B,60B,65B,127B,193B,197B,201B ''truepaint'':189B ''truth'':43B ''unde'':97B ''various'':109B ''venerating'':108B ''wher'':165B ''widespr'':102B ''with'':89B,105B,143B,152B,185B ''wom'':132B ''worship'':98B ''worshipers'':145B', 'priest, scholar', 'Dibella, the Lady of Love, is the Goddess of Beauty, Love, and Art, inspiring mortals to find truth through beauty and cultivate love, friendship, and creativity. Her followers believe devotion to her brings charm and harmony, while she teaches the value of deep, pure relationships over fleeting ones. Worship of Dibella is common across Tamriel. Dibella is also tied to art and creation, with legends of artifacts like the Brush of Truepaint that bring artworks to life.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mara', 'Mara, known as the Mother-Goddess, is the Divine of Love, Fertility, and Compassion. Worshiped across Tamriel, she embodies the nurturing aspects of life, offering her blessings in the realms of agriculture, family, and marriage. Originally venerated as a fertility goddess, Mara''s influence expanded to include love and the protection of home and family. She is often invoked at weddings, where her priests bless unions and sanctify the vows between partners. Mara is also considered the patron of motherhood and is seen as a figure of mercy and benevolence, guiding mortals toward peaceful and harmonious lives. Her teachings emphasize the importance of love, both in relationships and within the broader community, promoting unity and tolerance.

Mara is revered by nearly all races in Tamriel, except for the Dunmer and Argonians, though even in those regions, she is recognized by smaller groups. Her presence in the pantheons varies, with the Nords viewing her as the concubine of Shor, while the Bretons and Altmer see her as the wife of Akatosh or Auriel. Mara is closely linked to fertility deities in other cultures, such as the Redguard goddess Morwha. Her worship often focuses on the nurturing aspects of life, and her temples and shrines, such as the one in Riften, are centers for marriage ceremonies and blessings. Artifacts associated with Mara, like the Amulet of Mara, symbolize love and union, further reinforcing her role as a protector of human bonds.', '''across'':18B ''agricultur'':34B ''akatosh'':172B ''all'':124B ''also'':77B ''altmer'':165B ''amulet'':225B ''and'':15B,36B,51B,56B,69B,83B,91B,97B,110B,117B,132B,164B,201B,204B,217B,230B ''are'':212B ''argonians'':133B ''artifacts'':219B ''as'':4B,40B,86B,156B,168B,186B,207B,236B ''aspects'':24B,198B ''associat'':220B ''at'':62B ''auriel'':174B ''benevolenc'':92B ''betw'':73B ''bless'':67B ''blessings'':29B,218B ''bonds'':241B ''both'':107B ''bretons'':163B ''broad'':113B ''by'':122B,142B ''centers'':213B ''ceremoni'':216B ''closely'':177B ''community'':114B ''compassion'':16B ''concubin'':158B ''consider'':78B ''cultur'':184B ''deiti'':181B ''divin'':11B ''dunm'':131B ''embodi'':21B ''emphasiz'':102B ''even'':135B ''except'':128B ''expand'':47B ''family'':35B,57B ''fertility'':14B,42B,180B ''figur'':88B ''focus'':194B ''for'':129B,214B ''furth'':232B ''goddess'':8B,43B,189B ''groups'':144B ''guiding'':93B ''harmonious'':98B ''her'':28B,65B,100B,145B,155B,167B,191B,202B,234B ''hom'':55B ''hum'':240B ''importanc'':104B ''in'':30B,108B,126B,136B,147B,182B,210B ''includ'':49B ''influenc'':46B ''invok'':61B ''is'':9B,59B,76B,84B,120B,140B,176B ''known'':3B ''lif'':26B,200B ''lik'':223B ''link'':178B ''liv'':99B ''lov'':13B,50B,106B,229B ''mar'':1A,2B,44B,75B,119B,175B,222B,227B ''marriag'':37B,215B ''mercy'':90B ''mortals'':94B ''morwh'':190B ''moth'':7B ''mother-goddess'':6B ''motherhood'':82B ''nearly'':123B ''nords'':153B ''nurturing'':23B,197B ''of'':12B,25B,33B,54B,81B,89B,105B,159B,171B,199B,226B,239B ''offering'':27B ''often'':60B,193B ''on'':195B ''one'':209B ''or'':173B ''originally'':38B ''other'':183B ''pantheons'':149B ''partners'':74B ''patron'':80B ''peaceful'':96B ''presenc'':146B ''priests'':66B ''promoting'':115B ''protection'':53B ''protector'':238B ''rac'':125B ''realms'':32B ''recogniz'':141B ''redguard'':188B ''regions'':138B ''reinforcing'':233B ''relationships'':109B ''rever'':121B ''rift'':211B ''rol'':235B ''s'':45B ''sanctify'':70B ''see'':166B ''seen'':85B ''she'':20B,58B,139B ''shor'':160B ''shrin'':205B ''small'':143B ''such'':185B,206B ''symboliz'':228B ''tamriel'':19B,127B ''teachings'':101B ''templ'':203B ''the'':5B,10B,22B,31B,52B,71B,79B,103B,112B,130B,148B,152B,157B,162B,169B,187B,196B,208B,224B ''thos'':137B ''though'':134B ''to'':48B,179B ''toleranc'':118B ''toward'':95B ''union'':231B ''unions'':68B ''unity'':116B ''vari'':150B ''venerat'':39B ''viewing'':154B ''vows'':72B ''weddings'':63B ''wher'':64B ''whil'':161B ''wif'':170B ''with'':151B,221B ''within'':111B ''worship'':17B,192B', 'priest, scholar', 'Mara, the Mother-Goddess, is the Divine of Love, Fertility, and Compassion, celebrated as a protector of family, marriage, and harmony. She blesses agriculture, nurtures families, and is often called upon during weddings to sanctify unions. Her teachings promote love, unity, and peace within communities. Her shrines, like the one in Riften, serve as places for blessings and marriage ceremonies, with her symbol, the Amulet of Mara, representing love and human connection.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('idgrod', 'Idgrod Ravencrone is the elderly Nord Jarl of Hjaalmarch, residing in Highmoon Hall in Morthal. As a mystic, she is known for her visions, which she claims are granted to her by the Eight Divines. These visions often influence her decisions more than the opinions of her subjects, leading to some skepticism among the townsfolk regarding her judgments.

Idgrod governs alongside her husband, Aslfur, who acts as her steward, and is accompanied by her housecarl, Gorm. She is also the mother of Idgrod the Younger and Joric. Despite her reliance on visions, she maintains an essential position within the community, demonstrating a connection to both the spiritual and political realms of her hold. Idgrod is generally seen as unaggressive and holds a moral stance that does not involve crime, reflecting her role as a leader guided by her mystical insights.', '''accompani'':73B ''acts'':67B ''alongsid'':62B ''also'':80B ''among'':54B ''an'':96B ''and'':71B,87B,109B,121B ''are'':29B ''as'':17B,68B,119B,134B ''aslfur'':65B ''both'':106B ''by'':33B,74B,138B ''claims'':28B ''community'':101B ''connection'':104B ''crim'':130B ''decisions'':42B ''demonstrating'':102B ''despit'':89B ''divin'':36B ''does'':127B ''eight'':35B ''elderly'':6B ''essential'':97B ''for'':23B ''generally'':117B ''gorm'':77B ''governs'':61B ''grant'':30B ''guid'':137B ''hall'':14B ''her'':24B,32B,41B,48B,58B,63B,69B,75B,90B,113B,132B,139B ''highmoon'':13B ''hjaalmarch'':10B ''hold'':114B ''holds'':122B ''housecarl'':76B ''husband'':64B ''idgrod'':1A,2B,60B,84B,115B ''in'':12B,15B ''influenc'':40B ''insights'':141B ''involv'':129B ''is'':4B,21B,72B,79B,116B ''jarl'':8B ''joric'':88B ''judgments'':59B ''known'':22B ''lead'':136B ''leading'':50B ''maintains'':95B ''mor'':43B ''moral'':124B ''morthal'':16B ''moth'':82B ''mystic'':19B ''mystical'':140B ''nord'':7B ''not'':128B ''of'':9B,47B,83B,112B ''often'':39B ''on'':92B ''opinions'':46B ''political'':110B ''position'':98B ''ravencron'':3B ''realms'':111B ''reflecting'':131B ''regarding'':57B ''relianc'':91B ''residing'':11B ''rol'':133B ''seen'':118B ''she'':20B,27B,78B,94B ''skepticism'':53B ''som'':52B ''spiritual'':108B ''stanc'':125B ''steward'':70B ''subjects'':49B ''than'':44B ''that'':126B ''the'':5B,34B,45B,55B,81B,85B,100B,107B ''thes'':37B ''to'':31B,51B,105B ''townsfolk'':56B ''unaggressiv'':120B ''visions'':25B,38B,93B ''which'':26B ''who'':66B ''within'':99B ''young'':86B', 'scholar, noble', 'Idgrod Ravencrone is the elderly Jarl of Hjaalmarch, known for her mystical visions, which she believes are granted by the Eight Divines and influence her decisions. She rules alongside her husband, Aslfur, and her housecarl, Gorm. The mother of Idgrod the Younger and Joric, she is seen as a moral leader who avoids crime. While some townsfolk are skeptical of her reliance on visions, she maintains an essential position in both the spiritual and political life of Morthal.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stendarr', 'Stendarr, also known as Stendarr the Steadfast, is the Divine of Mercy, Charity, Justice, and Righteous Might. He is a compassionate god who offers protection and healing to the weak and the suffering. His teachings encourage kindness, generosity, and the defense of the vulnerable, making him the patron of magistrates, rulers, knights, and the Imperial Legion. Stendarr''s worship is widespread across Tamriel, and he is considered part of the pantheons of the Imperials, Bretons, Altmer, Bosmer, and Khajiit, where he is known as S''rendarr. His followers are called to offer help to those in need, and his mercy extends to all mortals, regardless of their faith.

Stendarr''s priests, templars, and organizations like the Vigil of Stendarr uphold his values by combating Abominations—unnatural creatures such as daedra, vampires, lycanthropes, and the undead, who are viewed as enemies of mankind. Stendarr also bestows upon mortals the gift of magic, particularly in healing and protection, which his followers use in his name. Artifacts associated with Stendarr, such as the Gauntlets of the Crusader and Stendarr’s Hammer, symbolize his strength and righteous power. Temples dedicated to him provide healing and training, and his followers live by precepts of mercy, justice, and service to those in need.', '''abominations'':126B ''across'':63B ''all'':104B ''also'':3B,145B ''altmer'':77B ''and'':16B,27B,32B,40B,54B,65B,79B,99B,114B,134B,156B,176B,183B,192B,194B,203B ''are'':90B,138B ''artifacts'':165B ''as'':5B,85B,130B,140B,170B ''associat'':166B ''bestows'':146B ''bosm'':78B ''bretons'':76B ''by'':124B,198B ''call'':91B ''charity'':14B ''combating'':125B ''compassionat'':22B ''consider'':68B ''creatur'':128B ''crusad'':175B ''daedr'':131B ''dedicat'':187B ''defens'':42B ''divin'':11B ''encourag'':37B ''enemi'':141B ''extends'':102B ''faith'':109B ''followers'':89B,160B,196B ''gauntlets'':172B ''generosity'':39B ''gift'':150B ''god'':23B ''hamm'':179B ''healing'':28B,155B,191B ''help'':94B ''him'':47B,189B ''his'':35B,88B,100B,122B,159B,163B,181B,195B ''imperial'':56B ''imperials'':75B ''in'':97B,154B,162B,207B ''is'':9B,20B,61B,67B,83B ''justic'':15B,202B ''khajiit'':80B ''kindness'':38B ''knights'':53B ''known'':4B,84B ''legion'':57B ''lik'':116B ''liv'':197B ''lycanthrop'':133B ''magic'':152B ''magistrat'':51B ''making'':46B ''mankind'':143B ''mercy'':13B,101B,201B ''might'':18B ''mortals'':105B,148B ''nam'':164B ''need'':98B,208B ''of'':12B,43B,50B,70B,73B,107B,119B,142B,151B,173B,200B ''offer'':93B ''offers'':25B ''organizations'':115B ''pantheons'':72B ''part'':69B ''particularly'':153B ''patron'':49B ''pow'':185B ''precepts'':199B ''priests'':112B ''protection'':26B,157B ''provid'':190B ''regardless'':106B ''rendarr'':87B ''righteous'':17B,184B ''rulers'':52B ''s'':59B,86B,111B,178B ''servic'':204B ''steadfast'':8B ''stendarr'':1A,2B,6B,58B,110B,120B,144B,168B,177B ''strength'':182B ''such'':129B,169B ''suffering'':34B ''symboliz'':180B ''tamriel'':64B ''teachings'':36B ''templ'':186B ''templars'':113B ''the'':7B,10B,30B,33B,41B,44B,48B,55B,71B,74B,108B,117B,135B,149B,171B,174B ''thos'':96B,206B ''to'':29B,92B,95B,103B,188B,205B ''training'':193B ''unde'':136B ''unnatural'':127B ''uphold'':121B ''upon'':147B ''use'':161B ''valu'':123B ''vampir'':132B ''view'':139B ''vigil'':118B ''vulner'':45B ''weak'':31B ''wher'':81B ''which'':158B ''who'':24B,137B ''widespr'':62B ''with'':167B ''worship'':60B', 'priest, scholar', '
Stendarr, the Divine of Mercy and Justice, is a compassionate god who protects the weak and punishes the wicked. He teaches kindness, charity, and the defense of the vulnerable, making him a patron of knights, rulers, and healers. Worshiped widely across Tamriel, his followers, like the Vigil of Stendarr, fight against abominations like daedra and vampires. Stendarr’s blessings include healing and protective magic, and his temples provide aid to those in need.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('arkay', 'Arkay, also known as the Lord of the Wheel of Life, is the Divine associated with the cycle of birth and death, and the god of funerals, burial rites, and seasons. As a member of the Divines, Arkay ensures the natural order of life and death is maintained, and his priests play a critical role in preventing necromancy by bestowing Arkay''s Law on the deceased. This divine protection ensures that the dead cannot be raised as undead. Necromancers see Arkay as their greatest foe, as his followers are dedicated to stopping the profane manipulation of mortal souls.

Arkay’s worship is widespread across Tamriel, from the Bretons, who believe he was once a mortal granted godhood by Mara, to the Nords, where he has replaced the older figure of Orkey. Redguards see him as a guide of souls through life and death, while Bosmer invoke him in matters concerning the Green Pact. Temples dedicated to Arkay, such as the Great Chapel of Arkay in Cyrodiil, perform sacred rites and house relics such as the Sword of the Crusader, a holy artifact. His followers, known as Arkayns, uphold his teachings by maintaining the balance of life and death, fiercely opposing necromancy and ensuring the proper passage of souls into the afterlife.', '''across'':105B ''afterlif'':212B ''also'':3B ''and'':22B,24B,31B,46B,50B,143B,171B,198B,203B ''are'':90B ''arkay'':1A,2B,39B,62B,82B,100B,158B,165B ''arkayns'':188B ''artifact'':183B ''as'':5B,33B,78B,83B,87B,136B,160B,175B,187B ''associat'':16B ''balanc'':195B ''be'':76B ''believ'':111B ''bestowing'':61B ''birth'':21B ''bosm'':146B ''bretons'':109B ''burial'':29B ''by'':60B,119B,192B ''cannot'':75B ''chapel'':163B ''concerning'':151B ''critical'':55B ''crusad'':180B ''cycle'':19B ''cyrodiil'':167B ''dead'':74B ''death'':23B,47B,144B,199B ''deceas'':67B ''dedicat'':91B,156B ''divin'':15B,38B,69B ''ensur'':40B,71B ''ensuring'':204B ''fiercely'':200B ''figur'':130B ''foe'':86B ''followers'':89B,185B ''from'':107B ''funerals'':28B ''god'':26B ''godhood'':118B ''grant'':117B ''gre'':153B ''great'':162B ''greatest'':85B ''guid'':138B ''him'':135B,148B ''his'':51B,88B,184B,190B ''holy'':182B ''hous'':172B ''in'':57B,149B,166B ''into'':210B ''invok'':147B ''is'':13B,48B,103B ''known'':4B,186B ''law'':64B ''lif'':12B,45B,142B,197B ''lord'':7B ''maintain'':49B ''maintaining'':193B ''manipulation'':96B ''mar'':120B ''matters'':150B ''memb'':35B ''mortal'':98B,116B ''natural'':42B ''necromancers'':80B ''necromancy'':59B,202B ''nords'':123B ''of'':8B,11B,20B,27B,36B,44B,97B,131B,139B,164B,178B,196B,208B ''older'':129B ''on'':65B ''once'':114B ''opposing'':201B ''order'':43B ''orkey'':132B ''pact'':154B ''passag'':207B ''perform'':168B ''play'':53B ''preventing'':58B ''priests'':52B ''profan'':95B ''prop'':206B ''protection'':70B ''rais'':77B ''redguards'':133B ''relics'':173B ''replac'':127B ''rit'':30B,170B ''rol'':56B ''s'':63B,101B ''sacr'':169B ''seasons'':32B ''see'':81B,134B ''souls'':99B,140B,209B ''stopping'':93B ''such'':159B,174B ''sword'':177B ''tamriel'':106B ''teachings'':191B ''templ'':155B ''that'':72B ''the'':6B,9B,14B,18B,25B,37B,41B,66B,73B,84B,94B,108B,122B,128B,152B,161B,176B,179B,194B,205B,211B ''this'':68B ''through'':141B ''to'':92B,121B,157B ''unde'':79B ''uphold'':189B ''was'':113B ''wheel'':10B ''wher'':124B ''whil'':145B ''who'':110B ''widespr'':104B ''with'':17B ''worship'':102B', 'priest, scholar', '
Arkay, the Divine of birth, death, and the seasons, governs the natural cycle of life and death. Known as the Lord of the Wheel of Life, he is revered for his role in funerals, burial rites, and preventing necromancy through Arkay''s Law, which protects the dead from being raised as undead. Worship of Arkay is widespread, with cultures like the Bretons believing he was once mortal, the Nords replacing Orkey with him, and the Redguards viewing him as a soul guide. Temples dedicated to Arkay, such as the Great Chapel in Cyrodiil, uphold his teachings, perform sacred rites, and house relics like the Sword of the Crusader, while his followers fiercely oppose necromancy and safeguard the passage of souls.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('argonian_ale', 'Argonian Ale is a rare and potent drink, said to invigorate the body at the cost of slowing its recovery. It is sought after by certain individuals and is a point of pride among Argonians.', '''after'':26B ''ale'':2A,4B ''among'':36B ''and'':8B,30B ''argoni'':1A,3B ''argonians'':37B ''at'':16B ''body'':15B ''by'':27B ''certain'':28B ''cost'':18B ''drink'':10B ''individuals'':29B ''invigorat'':13B ''is'':5B,24B,31B ''it'':23B ''its'':21B ''of'':19B,34B ''point'':33B ''potent'':9B ''prid'':35B ''rar'':7B ''recovery'':22B ''said'':11B ''slowing'':20B ''sought'':25B ''the'':14B,17B ''to'':12B', 'argonian, brenuin', 'You have only heard vague references to Argonian Ale but know nothing specific about it.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('julianos', 'Julianos, the God of Wisdom and Logic, is one of the Divines in the Cyrodilic pantheon, revered for his governance over knowledge, law, history, and intellectual pursuits. He is often associated with magic and is particularly venerated by scholars, wizards, and legal minds. His teachings emphasize the importance of learning, logic, and the pursuit of truth. His domains include sorcery, alchemy, and enchantment, making him a popular deity among those who value scholarship and wisdom. His symbol, a triangle, reflects the structured nature of his teachings, and his followers are known to seek wisdom from books and scholars. Monastic orders dedicated to Julianos, such as those founded by Tiber Septim, are also responsible for the preservation of the Elder Scrolls.

Worship of Julianos is prevalent in the Imperial City, where a Chantry is dedicated to him, as well as in the Iliac Bay region, where his temples are called Schools of Julianos, functioning as centers of education. The ancient Nords once worshipped him as Jhunal, the father of language and mathematics, before he became part of the Divines under the name Julianos. He is the patron of several regions, including Lainlyn and Satakalaam, and remains a respected figure for those seeking justice and knowledge. Julianos is said to have created the Shield of the Crusader to aid Pelinal Whitestrake in his battle against Umaril the Unfeathered, further cementing his role as a protector of justice. His planet, JHUNAL, represents his place in the celestial order, marking the eye of the Mage constellation in the skies of Mundus.', '''against'':224B ''aid'':218B ''alchemy'':62B ''also'':113B ''among'':70B ''ancient'':160B ''and'':7B,26B,35B,42B,53B,63B,75B,88B,98B,171B,193B,195B,204B ''are'':91B,112B,149B ''as'':106B,138B,140B,155B,165B,232B ''associat'':32B ''battl'':223B ''bay'':144B ''becam'':175B ''befor'':173B ''books'':97B ''by'':39B,109B ''call'':150B ''celestial'':245B ''cementing'':229B ''centers'':156B ''chantry'':133B ''city'':130B ''constellation'':253B ''creat'':211B ''crusad'':216B ''cyrodilic'':16B ''dedicat'':102B,135B ''deity'':69B ''divin'':13B,179B ''domains'':59B ''education'':158B ''elder'':120B ''emphasiz'':47B ''enchantment'':64B ''eye'':249B ''fath'':168B ''figur'':199B ''followers'':90B ''for'':19B,115B,200B ''found'':108B ''from'':96B ''functioning'':154B ''furth'':228B ''god'':4B ''governanc'':21B ''hav'':210B ''him'':66B,137B,164B ''his'':20B,45B,58B,77B,86B,89B,147B,222B,230B,237B,241B ''history'':25B ''iliac'':143B ''imperial'':129B ''importanc'':49B ''in'':14B,127B,141B,221B,243B,254B ''includ'':60B ''including'':191B ''intellectual'':27B ''is'':9B,30B,36B,125B,134B,185B,207B ''jhunal'':166B,239B ''julian'':1A,2B,104B,124B,153B,183B,206B ''justic'':2