INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('uriel_septim_seventh', 'Uriel Septim VII was the twenty-first or twenty-fourth Emperor of the Third Empire and the Septim Dynasty. He ascended to the throne in 3E 368 following the death of his father, Pelagius Septim IV, and ruled for 55 of the 65 years until his assassination in 3E 433. Uriel VII''s reign was marked by significant challenges and upheaval, culminating in the crisis that followed his death.

During his time as emperor, Uriel VII married Princess Caula Voria, with whom he had four legitimate heirs: Ariella, Geldall, Enman, and Ebel. Additionally, he fathered at least two sons outside of marriage—Calaxes, who was publicly acknowledged, and Martin, who remained secreted away and unacknowledged. Martin would later play a pivotal role in the events of the Oblivion Crisis, ultimately becoming the last of the Septim bloodline.', '''368'':32B ''3e'':31B,54B ''433'':55B ''55'':45B ''65'':48B ''acknowledg'':112B ''additionally'':98B ''and'':21B,42B,65B,96B,113B,119B ''ariell'':93B ''as'':78B ''ascend'':26B ''assassination'':52B ''at'':101B ''away'':118B ''becoming'':136B ''bloodlin'':142B ''by'':62B ''calax'':108B ''caul'':84B ''challeng'':64B ''crisis'':70B,134B ''culminating'':67B ''death'':35B,74B ''during'':75B ''dynasty'':24B ''ebel'':97B ''emperor'':16B,79B ''empir'':20B ''enman'':95B ''events'':130B ''fath'':38B ''father'':100B ''first'':11B ''follow'':72B ''following'':33B ''for'':44B ''four'':90B ''fourth'':15B ''geldall'':94B ''had'':89B ''heirs'':92B ''his'':37B,51B,73B,76B ''in'':30B,53B,68B,128B ''iv'':41B ''last'':138B ''lat'':123B ''least'':102B ''legitimat'':91B ''mark'':61B ''marri'':82B ''marriag'':107B ''martin'':114B,121B ''oblivion'':133B ''of'':17B,36B,46B,106B,131B,139B ''or'':12B ''outsid'':105B ''pelagius'':39B ''pivotal'':126B ''play'':124B ''princess'':83B ''publicly'':111B ''reign'':59B ''remain'':116B ''rol'':127B ''rul'':43B ''s'':58B ''secret'':117B ''septim'':2A,5B,23B,40B,141B ''seventh'':3A ''significant'':63B ''sons'':104B ''that'':71B ''the'':8B,18B,22B,28B,34B,47B,69B,129B,132B,137B,140B ''third'':19B ''thron'':29B ''tim'':77B ''to'':27B ''twenty'':10B,14B ''twenty-first'':9B ''twenty-fourth'':13B ''two'':103B ''ultimately'':135B ''unacknowledg'':120B ''until'':50B ''upheaval'':66B ''uriel'':1A,4B,56B,80B ''vii'':6B,57B,81B ''vori'':85B ''was'':7B,60B,110B ''who'':109B,115B ''whom'':87B ''with'':86B ''would'':122B ''years'':49B', 'imperial, scholar, noble', 'Uriel Septim VII was the Emperor of the Third Empire and the Septim Dynasty, ruling from 3E 368 until his assassination in 3E 433. He married Princess Caula Voria and had four legitimate heirs: Ariella, Geldall, Enman, and Ebel. Uriel also fathered two sons outside marriage—Calaxes, who was publicly acknowledged, and Martin, who was kept secret. Martin later became the last of the Septim bloodline, playing a key role in the Oblivion Crisis.', '', '', 'figures');
