INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vivec', 'Vivec, also known as Vehk, is the Warrior-Poet deity of the Dunmer and a central figure in the pantheon of Morrowind. As the Guardian God-King of Vvardenfell, he serves as the protector against the dark forces associated with Red Mountain. His dual heritage, being both Dunmer and Chimer, symbolizes the complexity of the Dunmeri spirit. Vivec is renowned for his artistic prowess, producing numerous writings, including the enigmatic "36 Lessons," which serve as guidance for the prophesied Nerevarine.

Throughout his extensive reign, Vivec became a pivotal figure for the Dunmer, residing in his namesake city where pilgrims sought his wisdom. He wielded various artifacts, such as his legendary spear Muatra, and was known for his dualistic nature, embodying both martial prowess and poetic expression. However, as the Third Era drew to a close, he sacrificed his divinity, leading to his disappearance and the subsequent collapse of the Tribunal Temple. In the New Temple''s teachings, Vivec is reinterpreted as Saint Vivec, distanced from his former divine status, illustrating the complex legacy of a god who was both revered and contested.', '''36'':74B ''against'':38B ''also'':3B ''and'':16B,52B,116B,127B,147B,184B ''artifacts'':109B ''artistic'':66B ''as'':5B,25B,35B,78B,111B,131B,164B ''associat'':42B ''becam'':89B ''being'':49B ''both'':50B,124B,182B ''central'':18B ''chim'':53B ''city'':100B ''clos'':138B ''collaps'':150B ''complex'':175B ''complexity'':56B ''contest'':185B ''dark'':40B ''deity'':12B ''disappearanc'':146B ''distanc'':167B ''divin'':171B ''divinity'':142B ''drew'':135B ''dual'':47B ''dualistic'':121B ''dunm'':15B,51B,95B ''dunmeri'':59B ''embodying'':123B ''enigmatic'':73B ''expression'':129B ''extensiv'':86B ''figur'':19B,92B ''for'':64B,80B,93B,119B ''forc'':41B ''form'':170B ''from'':168B ''god'':29B,179B ''god-king'':28B ''guardi'':27B ''guidanc'':79B ''heritag'':48B ''his'':46B,65B,85B,98B,104B,112B,120B,141B,145B,169B ''howev'':130B ''illustrating'':173B ''in'':20B,97B,155B ''including'':71B ''is'':7B,62B,162B ''king'':30B ''known'':4B,118B ''leading'':143B ''legacy'':176B ''legendary'':113B ''lessons'':75B ''martial'':125B ''morrowind'':24B ''mountain'':45B ''muatr'':115B ''namesak'':99B ''natur'':122B ''nerevarin'':83B ''new'':157B ''numerous'':69B ''of'':13B,23B,31B,57B,151B,177B ''pantheon'':22B ''pilgrims'':102B ''pivotal'':91B ''poet'':11B ''poetic'':128B ''producing'':68B ''prophesi'':82B ''protector'':37B ''prowess'':67B,126B ''red'':44B ''reign'':87B ''reinterpret'':163B ''renown'':63B ''residing'':96B ''rever'':183B ''s'':159B ''sacrific'':140B ''saint'':165B ''serv'':34B,77B ''sought'':103B ''spe'':114B ''spirit'':60B ''status'':172B ''subsequent'':149B ''such'':110B ''symboliz'':54B ''teachings'':160B ''templ'':154B,158B ''the'':8B,14B,21B,26B,36B,39B,55B,58B,72B,81B,94B,132B,148B,152B,156B,174B ''third'':133B ''throughout'':84B ''to'':136B,144B ''tribunal'':153B ''various'':108B ''vehk'':6B ''vivec'':1A,2B,61B,88B,161B,166B ''vvardenfell'':32B ''warrior'':10B ''warrior-poet'':9B ''was'':117B,181B ''wher'':101B ''which'':76B ''who'':180B ''wield'':107B ''wisdom'':105B ''with'':43B ''writings'':70B', 'darkelf, daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Vivec, also known as Vehk, is the Warrior-Poet deity of the Dunmer and a central figure in the pantheon of Morrowind. As the Guardian God-King of Vvardenfell, he protected against the dark forces of Red Mountain. With a dual heritage as both Dunmer and Chimer, he symbolizes the complexity of the Dunmeri spirit. Vivec was known for his artistic prowess, producing the "36 Lessons" for the prophesied Nerevarine. Throughout his reign, he wielded artifacts like his spear Muatra, balancing martial skill and poetry. At the end of the Third Era, he sacrificed his divinity, leading to his disappearance and the collapse of the Tribunal Temple. In the New Temple, he is reinterpreted as Saint Vivec, far from his former divine status.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pelinal_whitestrake', 'Pelinal Whitestrake is a legendary figure revered as a demigod and champion of Queen Alessia during the early First Era''s Alessian Slave Rebellion. Known for his fierce combat prowess, Pelinal fought against the Ayleid oppressors, wielding the Crusader''s Relics bestowed upon him by the Eight Divines. His name, derived from Pelin-El, meaning "Star-Made Knight," reflects his celestial connection and glory in battle. Throughout his conquests across Tamriel, Pelinal is said to have embodied both heroism and chaos, often succumbing to bouts of madness that drove him to indiscriminately slay enemies and alter the very landscape.

Pelinal is remembered by many titles, including Pelinal the Bloody, the Divine Crusader, and Pelinal Insurgent, with some legends suggesting he had incarnated multiple times. His connection to Queen Alessia was profound, with their names occasionally combined to signify their unity in the fight for freedom. Khajiiti tales recount him as the White Snake, further highlighting his mythic status. Despite his feats, Pelinal''s legacy is complex, as he is equally known for the destruction he wrought, embodying both the hope of liberation and the peril of unchecked power.', '''across'':74B ''against'':35B ''alessi'':17B,24B,133B ''alter'':100B ''and'':13B,67B,84B,99B,117B,187B ''as'':10B,154B,171B ''ayle'':37B ''battl'':70B ''bestow'':44B ''bloody'':113B ''both'':82B,182B ''bouts'':89B ''by'':47B,107B ''celestial'':65B ''cha'':85B ''champion'':14B ''combat'':31B ''combin'':140B ''complex'':170B ''connection'':66B,130B ''conquests'':73B ''crusad'':41B,116B ''demigod'':12B ''deriv'':53B ''despit'':163B ''destruction'':178B ''divin'':50B,115B ''drov'':93B ''during'':18B ''early'':20B ''eight'':49B ''embodi'':81B ''embodying'':181B ''enemi'':98B ''equally'':174B ''feats'':165B ''fierc'':30B ''fight'':147B ''figur'':8B ''first'':21B ''for'':28B,148B,176B ''fought'':34B ''freedom'':149B ''from'':54B ''furth'':158B ''glory'':68B ''had'':125B ''hav'':80B ''heroism'':83B ''highlighting'':159B ''him'':46B,94B,153B ''his'':29B,51B,64B,72B,129B,160B,164B ''hop'':184B ''in'':69B,145B ''incarnat'':126B ''including'':110B ''indiscriminately'':96B ''insurgent'':119B ''is'':5B,77B,105B,169B,173B ''khajiiti'':150B ''knight'':62B ''known'':27B,175B ''landscap'':103B ''legacy'':168B ''legendary'':7B ''legends'':122B ''liberation'':186B ''mad'':61B ''madness'':91B ''many'':108B ''meaning'':58B ''multipl'':127B ''mythic'':161B ''nam'':52B,138B ''occasionally'':139B ''of'':15B,90B,185B,190B ''often'':86B ''oppressors'':38B ''pelin'':56B ''pelin-el'':55B ''pelinal'':1A,3B,33B,76B,104B,111B,118B,166B ''peril'':189B ''pow'':192B ''profound'':135B ''prowess'':32B ''que'':16B,132B ''rebellion'':26B ''recount'':152B ''reflects'':63B ''relics'':43B ''remember'':106B ''rever'':9B ''s'':23B,42B,167B ''said'':78B ''signify'':142B ''slav'':25B ''slay'':97B ''snak'':157B ''som'':121B ''star'':60B ''star-mad'':59B ''status'':162B ''succumbing'':87B ''suggesting'':123B ''tal'':151B ''tamriel'':75B ''that'':92B ''the'':19B,36B,40B,48B,101B,112B,114B,137B,143B,146B,155B,177B,183B,188B ''throughout'':71B ''tim'':128B ''titl'':109B ''to'':79B,88B,95B,131B,141B ''uncheck'':191B ''unity'':144B ''upon'':45B ''very'':102B ''was'':134B ''whit'':156B ''whitestrak'':2A,4B ''wielding'':39B ''with'':120B,136B ''wrought'':180B', ' highelf, scholar, imperial, priest', 'Pelinal Whitestrake is a legendary figure, revered as a demigod and champion of Queen Alessia during the Alessian Slave Rebellion. Known for his combat prowess, he fought against the Ayleid oppressors using the Crusader''s Relics bestowed by the Eight Divines. His name, Pelin-El, meaning "Star-Made Knight," reflects his celestial nature. Pelinal is remembered by titles such as Pelinal the Bloody and the Divine Crusader. He had a deep connection to Queen Alessia, and some Khajiiti tales call him the White Snake. Though a hero, Pelinal’s legacy is marked by both the hope of liberation and the destruction he caused.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('jagar_tharn', 'Jagar Tharn was the Imperial Battlemage of Tamriel who ascended to the throne as Emperor following a nefarious scheme. He secretly imprisoned Emperor Uriel Septim VII in Oblivion and utilized Illusion magic to impersonate him for a decade, ruling from 3E 389 to 3E 399 during a tumultuous period known as the Imperial Simulacrum. While Tharn held the reins of power over the war-torn Empire, the specifics of his ambitions and achievements during this time remain largely unclear. His actions significantly impacted the political landscape of Tamriel, but the true extent of his goals and motivations has been lost to history.', '''389'':44B ''399'':47B ''3e'':43B,46B ''achievements'':76B ''actions'':84B ''ambitions'':74B ''and'':31B,75B,99B ''as'':16B,53B ''ascend'':12B ''battlemag'':8B ''been'':102B ''but'':92B ''decad'':40B ''during'':48B,77B ''emperor'':17B,25B ''empir'':69B ''extent'':95B ''following'':18B ''for'':38B ''from'':42B ''goals'':98B ''held'':59B ''him'':37B ''his'':73B,83B,97B ''history'':105B ''illusion'':33B ''impact'':86B ''imperial'':7B,55B ''impersonat'':36B ''imprison'':24B ''in'':29B ''jag'':1A,3B ''known'':52B ''landscap'':89B ''largely'':81B ''lost'':103B ''magic'':34B ''motivations'':100B ''nefarious'':20B ''oblivion'':30B ''of'':9B,62B,72B,90B,96B ''over'':64B ''period'':51B ''political'':88B ''pow'':63B ''reins'':61B ''remain'':80B ''ruling'':41B ''schem'':21B ''secretly'':23B ''septim'':27B ''significantly'':85B ''simulacrum'':56B ''specifics'':71B ''tamriel'':10B,91B ''tharn'':2A,4B,58B ''the'':6B,14B,54B,60B,65B,70B,87B,93B ''this'':78B ''thron'':15B ''tim'':79B ''to'':13B,35B,45B,104B ''torn'':68B ''tru'':94B ''tumultuous'':50B ''uncle'':82B ''uriel'':26B ''utiliz'':32B ''vii'':28B ''war'':67B ''war-torn'':66B ''was'':5B ''whil'':57B ''who'':11B', 'imperial, scholar', 'Jagar Tharn was the Imperial Battlemage who ascended to the throne through deception, secretly imprisoning Emperor Uriel Septim VII in Oblivion and using Illusion magic to impersonate him. He ruled as Emperor from 3E 389 to 3E 399 during the Imperial Simulacrum, a period of political turmoil. Although Tharn held power, the details of his ambitions and achievements remain largely unclear, and his actions significantly influenced the political landscape of Tamriel. The full extent of his goals and motivations has been lost to history.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('alduin', 'Alduin, often referred to as the World-Eater, is a powerful black dragon revered in Nord mythology as the harbinger of the end times. Known by various titles, including the First Dragon and the Time-Eater, Alduin is believed to periodically destroy the world, making way for a new cycle of existence. He is considered the self-proclaimed First-Born of Akatosh, embodying a malevolent aspect of the deity associated with time and dragons.

The name "Alduin" can be translated in the Dragon Language to mean "Destroyer Devour Master," reflecting his fearsome nature and role as a force of annihilation. Alduin commands a legion of dragons, dragon priests, and draugr, and his return is seen as a sign of impending doom, signaling the end of the current world and the dawn of a new one. His lore intertwines with the beliefs and traditions of the Nords, who view him both as a deity and a harbinger of destruction.', '''akatosh'':67B ''alduin'':1A,2B,40B,82B,106B ''and'':35B,78B,99B,114B,116B,134B,147B,159B ''annihilation'':105B ''as'':6B,20B,101B,121B,156B ''aspect'':71B ''associat'':75B ''be'':84B ''beliefs'':146B ''believ'':42B ''black'':14B ''born'':65B ''both'':155B ''by'':28B ''can'':83B ''commands'':107B ''consider'':58B ''current'':132B ''cycle'':53B ''dawn'':136B ''deity'':74B,158B ''destroy'':45B,92B ''destruction'':163B ''devour'':93B ''doom'':126B ''dragon'':15B,34B,88B,112B ''dragons'':79B,111B ''draugr'':115B ''eat'':10B,39B ''embodying'':68B ''end'':25B,129B ''existenc'':55B ''fearsom'':97B ''first'':33B,64B ''first-born'':63B ''for'':50B ''forc'':103B ''harbing'':22B,161B ''him'':154B ''his'':96B,117B,141B ''impending'':125B ''in'':17B,86B ''including'':31B ''intertwin'':143B ''is'':11B,41B,57B,119B ''known'':27B ''languag'':89B ''legion'':109B ''lor'':142B ''making'':48B ''malevolent'':70B ''mast'':94B ''mean'':91B ''mythology'':19B ''nam'':81B ''natur'':98B ''new'':52B,139B ''nord'':18B ''nords'':151B ''of'':23B,54B,66B,72B,104B,110B,124B,130B,137B,149B,162B ''often'':3B ''one'':140B ''periodically'':44B ''powerful'':13B ''priests'':113B ''proclaim'':62B ''referr'':4B ''reflecting'':95B ''return'':118B ''rever'':16B ''rol'':100B ''seen'':120B ''self'':61B ''self-proclaim'':60B ''sign'':123B ''signaling'':127B ''the'':7B,21B,24B,32B,36B,46B,59B,73B,80B,87B,128B,131B,135B,145B,150B ''tim'':26B,38B,77B ''time-eat'':37B ''titl'':30B ''to'':5B,43B,90B ''traditions'':148B ''translat'':85B ''various'':29B ''view'':153B ''way'':49B ''who'':152B ''with'':76B,144B ''world'':9B,47B,133B ''world-eat'':8B', 'scholar, dragon, priest, miraakcult', 'Alduin, the World-Eater, is a powerful black dragon in Nord mythology, known as the harbinger of the end times. Believed to destroy the world periodically, Alduin is considered the First-Born of Akatosh and represents a malevolent aspect of the deity tied to time and dragons. His name, "Alduin," translates to "Destroyer Devour Master" in the Dragon Language, highlighting his destructive nature. He commands dragons, dragon priests, and draugr, with his return signaling the end of the world and the start of a new cycle. Nords view him both as a deity and a force of annihilation.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('alessia', 'Alessia, also known as Queen Alessia, Saint Alessia, Lady of Heaven, and the Mother of the Empire, was a pivotal figure in Tamriel''s history as the first Empress of Cyrodiil and the founder of the Alessian Empire. Born in the early First Era, she led the Alessian Slave Rebellion against the Ayleids, liberating the Nedes of Cyrodiil from enslavement and establishing a new order in the region.

Her reign lasted from 1E 243 until her death in 1E 266, during which she created a new religion that fused elements of the Nordic and Aldmeri pantheons, known as the Eight Divines. On her deathbed, Alessia was canonized by Akatosh, with her soul encased in the central stone of the Amulet of Kings, forming a divine covenant to protect Tamriel from the forces of Oblivion.', '''1e'':74B,80B ''243'':75B ''266'':81B ''against'':52B ''akatosh'':110B ''aldmeri'':96B ''alessi'':1A,2B,7B,9B,38B,49B,106B ''also'':3B ''amulet'':121B ''and'':13B,33B,62B,95B ''as'':5B,27B,99B ''ayleids'':54B ''born'':40B ''by'':109B ''canoniz'':108B ''central'':117B ''covenant'':127B ''creat'':85B ''cyrodiil'':32B,59B ''death'':78B ''deathb'':105B ''divin'':102B,126B ''during'':82B ''early'':43B ''eight'':101B ''elements'':91B ''empir'':18B,39B ''empress'':30B ''encas'':114B ''enslavement'':61B ''establishing'':63B ''figur'':22B ''first'':29B,44B ''forc'':133B ''forming'':124B ''found'':35B ''from'':60B,73B,131B ''fus'':90B ''heav'':12B ''her'':70B,77B,104B,112B ''history'':26B ''in'':23B,41B,67B,79B,115B ''kings'':123B ''known'':4B,98B ''lady'':10B ''last'':72B ''led'':47B ''liberating'':55B ''moth'':15B ''ned'':57B ''new'':65B,87B ''nordic'':94B ''oblivion'':135B ''of'':11B,16B,31B,36B,58B,92B,119B,122B,134B ''on'':103B ''order'':66B ''pantheons'':97B ''pivotal'':21B ''protect'':129B ''que'':6B ''rebellion'':51B ''region'':69B ''reign'':71B ''religion'':88B ''s'':25B ''saint'':8B ''she'':46B,84B ''slav'':50B ''soul'':113B ''ston'':118B ''tamriel'':24B,130B ''that'':89B ''the'':14B,17B,28B,34B,37B,42B,48B,53B,56B,68B,93B,100B,116B,120B,132B ''to'':128B ''until'':76B ''was'':19B,107B ''which'':83B ''with'':111B', 'imperial, highelf, scholar, priest', 'Alessia, also known as Queen Alessia, Saint Alessia, and Lady of Heaven, was the first Empress of Cyrodiil and the founder of the Alessian Empire. She led the Alessian Slave Rebellion in the early First Era, liberating the Nedes from Ayleid enslavement. Her reign from 1E 243 to 1E 266 saw the creation of the Eight Divines, a new religion blending Nordic and Aldmeri pantheons. On her deathbed, Alessia was canonized by Akatosh, and her soul was placed in the Amulet of Kings, creating a divine covenant to protect Tamriel from Oblivion.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('creep_cluster', 'Creep Cluster is a mass of orange-brown roots found growing over rocks in the sulfur-rich region of Eastmarch. Alchemy effects: Restore Magicka, Damage Stamina Regen, Fortify Carry Weight, and Weakness to Magic.', '''alchemy'':25B ''and'':35B ''brown'':11B ''carry'':33B ''clust'':2A,4B ''creep'':1A,3B ''damag'':29B ''eastmarch'':24B ''effects'':26B ''fortify'':32B ''found'':13B ''growing'':14B ''in'':17B ''is'':5B ''magic'':38B ''magick'':28B ''mass'':7B ''of'':8B,23B ''orang'':10B ''orange-brown'':9B ''over'':15B ''reg'':31B ''region'':22B ''restor'':27B ''rich'':21B ''rocks'':16B ''roots'':12B ''stamin'':30B ''sulfur'':20B ''sulfur-rich'':19B ''the'':18B ''to'':37B ''weakness'':36B ''weight'':34B', 'alchemist', 'Creep Cluster is a mass of orange-brown roots found growing over rocks in the sulfur-rich region of Eastmarch. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('morihaus', 'Morihaus, also known as Morihaus-Breath-of-Kyne and the Winged Bull, is a revered demigod associated with the winds and considered a significant figure in both Cyrodiil and Skyrim. He is the son of the divine Kyne (Kynareth) and the consort of Saint Alessia, playing a vital role in the establishment of the Alessian Empire. Morihaus is celebrated for his exceptional archery skills and is often depicted as a winged bull, possessing golden wings, horns, and a nose-ring.

In addition to his physical prowess, Morihaus is connected to the powerful artifact known as the Lord''s Mail, which was created by his mother to aid those who would bear the burdens of the land. His arrogance led to Kyne reclaiming the armor at one point, but he is still recognized for his strength and his alignment with the constellation known as The Lord. Morihaus is often portrayed engaging in heroic deeds, including hunting and slaying beasts alongside the Demiprince Fa-Nuit-Hen, further solidifying his status as a protector and symbol of strength in Tamriel.', '''addition'':85B ''aid'':110B ''alessi'':47B,57B ''alignment'':141B ''alongsid'':162B ''also'':3B ''and'':11B,23B,31B,42B,67B,79B,139B,159B,176B ''archery'':65B ''armor'':127B ''arroganc'':121B ''artifact'':96B ''as'':5B,71B,98B,146B,173B ''associat'':19B ''at'':128B ''bear'':114B ''beasts'':161B ''both'':29B ''breath'':8B ''bull'':14B,74B ''burdens'':116B ''but'':131B ''by'':106B ''celebrat'':61B ''connect'':92B ''consider'':24B ''consort'':44B ''constellation'':144B ''creat'':105B ''cyrodiil'':30B ''deeds'':156B ''demigod'':18B ''demiprinc'':164B ''depict'':70B ''divin'':39B ''empir'':58B ''engaging'':153B ''establishment'':54B ''exceptional'':64B ''fa'':166B ''fa-nuit-h'':165B ''figur'':27B ''for'':62B,136B ''furth'':169B ''gold'':76B ''hen'':168B ''heroic'':155B ''his'':63B,87B,107B,120B,137B,140B,171B ''horns'':78B ''hunting'':158B ''in'':28B,52B,84B,154B,180B ''including'':157B ''is'':15B,34B,60B,68B,91B,133B,150B ''known'':4B,97B,145B ''kynareth'':41B ''kyne'':10B,40B,124B ''land'':119B ''led'':122B ''lord'':100B,148B ''mail'':102B ''morihaus'':1A,2B,7B,59B,90B,149B ''morihaus-breath-of-kyn'':6B ''moth'':108B ''nos'':82B ''nose-ring'':81B ''nuit'':167B ''of'':9B,37B,45B,55B,117B,178B ''often'':69B,151B ''one'':129B ''physical'':88B ''playing'':48B ''point'':130B ''portray'':152B ''possessing'':75B ''powerful'':95B ''protector'':175B ''prowess'':89B ''reclaiming'':125B ''recogniz'':135B ''rever'':17B ''ring'':83B ''rol'':51B ''s'':101B ''saint'':46B ''significant'':26B ''skills'':66B ''skyrim'':32B ''slaying'':160B ''solidifying'':170B ''status'':172B ''still'':134B ''strength'':138B,179B ''symbol'':177B ''tamriel'':181B ''the'':12B,21B,35B,38B,43B,53B,56B,94B,99B,115B,118B,126B,143B,147B,163B ''thos'':111B ''to'':86B,93B,109B,123B ''vital'':50B ''was'':104B ''which'':103B ''who'':112B ''winds'':22B ''wing'':13B,73B ''wings'':77B ''with'':20B,142B ''would'':113B', 'imperial, scholar, priest', 'Morihaus, also known as Morihaus-Breath-of-Kyne and the Winged Bull, is a revered demigod in Cyrodiil and Skyrim. The son of the divine Kyne (Kynareth) and consort of Saint Alessia, he played a key role in the establishment of the Alessian Empire. Known for his exceptional archery skills, Morihaus is often depicted as a winged bull with golden wings and horns. He is connected to the Lord''s Mail, an artifact created by Kyne. Though his arrogance led to the armor being reclaimed by his mother, he is still celebrated for his strength and connection to the constellation The Lord. He is also known for his heroic deeds, including hunting beasts with Fa-Nuit-Hen.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tiber_septim', 'Tiber Septim, also known as Talos Stormcrown, Hjalti Early-Beard, and Tiberius Imperator, was a pivotal military leader and one of the most renowned figures in Tamrielic history. He served under the Cyrodilic king Cuhlecain as General Talos before embarking on a campaign to unify Cyrodiil and eventually all of Tamriel. His efforts culminated in 2E 896 with the establishment of the Third Empire and the onset of the Third Era.

Reigning as Emperor Tiber Septim from 2E 854 to 3E 38, he ruled for 81 years and is often celebrated as the greatest emperor in history. His legacy continues through the lineage of Cyrodilic Emperors known as the Septims. Following his death, Tiber Septim was venerated as a god and saint, worshipped as one of the Nine Divines under the name of Talos, which means "Stormcrown" in the ancient Ehlnofey language.', '''2e'':59B,81B ''38'':85B ''3e'':84B ''81'':89B ''854'':82B ''896'':60B ''all'':52B ''also'':5B ''ancient'':143B ''and'':14B,22B,50B,68B,91B,124B ''as'':7B,39B,76B,95B,111B,121B,127B ''beard'':13B ''befor'':42B ''campaign'':46B ''celebrat'':94B ''continu'':103B ''cuhlecain'':38B ''culminat'':57B ''cyrodiil'':49B ''cyrodilic'':36B,108B ''death'':116B ''divin'':132B ''early'':12B ''early-beard'':11B ''efforts'':56B ''ehlnofey'':144B ''embarking'':43B ''emperor'':77B,98B ''emperors'':109B ''empir'':67B ''establishment'':63B ''eventually'':51B ''figur'':28B ''following'':114B ''for'':88B ''from'':80B ''general'':40B ''god'':123B ''greatest'':97B ''his'':55B,101B,115B ''history'':31B,100B ''hjalti'':10B ''imperator'':16B ''in'':29B,58B,99B,141B ''is'':92B ''king'':37B ''known'':6B,110B ''languag'':145B ''lead'':21B ''legacy'':102B ''lineag'':106B ''means'':139B ''military'':20B ''most'':26B ''nam'':135B ''nin'':131B ''of'':24B,53B,64B,71B,107B,129B,136B ''often'':93B ''on'':44B ''one'':23B,128B ''onset'':70B ''pivotal'':19B ''reigning'':75B ''renown'':27B ''rul'':87B ''saint'':125B ''septim'':2A,4B,79B,118B ''septims'':113B ''serv'':33B ''stormcrown'':9B,140B ''tal'':8B,41B,137B ''tamriel'':54B ''tamrielic'':30B ''the'':25B,35B,62B,65B,69B,72B,96B,105B,112B,130B,134B,142B ''third'':66B,73B ''through'':104B ''tib'':1A,3B,78B,117B ''tiberius'':15B ''to'':47B,83B ''under'':34B,133B ''unify'':48B ''venerat'':120B ''was'':17B,119B ''which'':138B ''with'':61B ''worshipp'':126B ''years'':90B', 'imperial, nord, scholar, priest', 'Tiber Septim, also known as Talos Stormcrown, Hjalti Early-Beard, and Tiberius Imperator, was a crucial military leader who unified Cyrodiil and later all of Tamriel. He served as General Talos under King Cuhlecain and established the Third Empire in 2E 896. Tiber Septim ruled as Emperor from 2E 854 to 3E 38, leading for 81 years and becoming one of the greatest emperors in history. After his death, he was venerated as a god, worshipped as Talos, one of the Nine Divines, with his name meaning "Stormcrown" in the ancient Ehlnofey language.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bunglers_bane', 'Bungler''s Bane is an ingredient originating from Vvardenfell, available for purchase from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Slow, Ravage Stamina, Damage Stamina Regen, and Resist Magic.', '''alchemy'':18B ''an'':7B ''and'':26B ''avail'':12B ''ban'':2A,5B ''bungl'':3B ''bunglers'':1A ''caravans'':17B ''damag'':23B ''effects'':19B ''for'':13B ''from'':10B,15B ''ingredient'':8B ''is'':6B ''khajiit'':16B ''magic'':28B ''originating'':9B ''purch'':14B ''ravag'':21B ''reg'':25B ''resist'':27B ''s'':4B ''slow'':20B ''stamin'':22B,24B ''vvardenfell'':11B', 'alchemist', 'Bungler''s Bane is an ingredient originating from Vvardenfell, available for purchase from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('eternal_champion', 'The Eternal Champion, reputedly known as Talin, emerged as a pivotal hero in Tamriel''s history during the late Third Era. Born in 3E 370, he is best remembered for his critical role in ending the Imperial Simulacrum in 3E 399. The Eternal Champion successfully gathered the fragments of the Staff of Chaos, a powerful artifact, which enabled him to confront and defeat the impostor emperor, Jagar Tharn. His quest culminated in the rescue of the true emperor, Uriel Septim VII, alongside General Talin Warhaft, who had been imprisoned in a realm of Tharn''s choosing for a decade. This heroic act not only restored the rightful leadership of the Empire but also ended Tharn''s deceptive reign.', '''370'':27B ''399'':43B ''3e'':26B,42B ''act'':104B ''alongsid'':84B ''also'':115B ''and'':64B ''artifact'':58B ''as'':8B,11B ''been'':90B ''best'':30B ''born'':24B ''but'':114B ''cha'':55B ''champion'':2A,5B,46B ''choosing'':98B ''confront'':63B ''critical'':34B ''culminat'':73B ''decad'':101B ''deceptiv'':119B ''defeat'':65B ''during'':19B ''emerg'':10B ''emperor'':68B,80B ''empir'':113B ''enabl'':60B ''ended'':116B ''ending'':37B ''eternal'':1A,4B,45B ''for'':32B,99B ''fragments'':50B ''gather'':48B ''general'':85B ''had'':89B ''her'':14B ''heroic'':103B ''him'':61B ''his'':33B,71B ''history'':18B ''imperial'':39B ''impostor'':67B ''imprison'':91B ''in'':15B,25B,36B,41B,74B,92B ''is'':29B ''jag'':69B ''known'':7B ''lat'':21B ''leadership'':110B ''not'':105B ''of'':51B,54B,77B,95B,111B ''only'':106B ''pivotal'':13B ''powerful'':57B ''quest'':72B ''realm'':94B ''reign'':120B ''remember'':31B ''reputedly'':6B ''rescu'':76B ''restor'':107B ''rightful'':109B ''rol'':35B ''s'':17B,97B,118B ''septim'':82B ''simulacrum'':40B ''staff'':53B ''successfully'':47B ''talin'':9B,86B ''tamriel'':16B ''tharn'':70B,96B,117B ''the'':3B,20B,38B,44B,49B,52B,66B,75B,78B,108B,112B ''third'':22B ''this'':102B ''to'':62B ''tru'':79B ''uriel'':81B ''vii'':83B ''warhaft'':87B ''which'':59B ''who'':88B', 'scholar', 'The Eternal Champion, reputedly known as Talin, played a pivotal role in ending the Imperial Simulacrum in 3E 399. Born in 3E 370, he is remembered for gathering the fragments of the Staff of Chaos, allowing him to defeat the impostor emperor, Jagar Tharn. His quest led to the rescue of the true emperor, Uriel Septim VII, and General Talin Warhaft, who had been imprisoned for a decade. This act restored the rightful leadership of the Empire and ended Tharn''s reign.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('saint_jiub', 'Saint Jiub, also known as Jiub the Magnificent and Eradicator of the Winged Menace, is a revered figure in the Tribunal Temple and the New Temple. Originally a Dunmer assassin with a troubled past marked by addiction and crime, Jiub sought redemption after being imprisoned for his deeds. He famously dedicated himself to eradicating the cliff racers that plagued Vvardenfell, achieving this feat after years of effort. His actions earned him sainthood from Vivec, who admired his virtue, and he became celebrated as a hero throughout Morrowind.

In 3E 433, during the onset of the Oblivion Crisis, Jiub was in Kvatch working on an extensive autobiography when the city was attacked. He was trapped in the Soul Cairn by a Dremora, leading to a long existence in that realm. His spirit remained unaware of his death until he encountered the Last Dragonborn in 4E 201, who assisted him in compiling his memoirs. Jiub''s story serves as a testament to his transformation from a fallen assassin to a saint, embodying themes of redemption and legacy in Tamriel.', '''201'':147B ''3e'':91B ''433'':92B ''4e'':146B ''achieving'':63B ''actions'':71B ''addiction'':39B ''admir'':78B ''after'':45B,66B ''also'':5B ''an'':106B ''and'':11B,25B,40B,81B,176B ''as'':7B,85B,159B ''assassin'':32B,168B ''assist'':149B ''attack'':113B ''autobiography'':108B ''becam'':83B ''being'':46B ''by'':38B,121B ''cairn'':120B ''celebrat'':84B ''city'':111B ''cliff'':58B ''compiling'':152B ''crim'':41B ''crisis'':99B ''death'':138B ''dedicat'':53B ''deeds'':50B ''dragonborn'':144B ''dremor'':123B ''dunm'':31B ''during'':93B ''earn'':72B ''effort'':69B ''embodying'':172B ''encounter'':141B ''eradicating'':56B ''eradicator'':12B ''existenc'':128B ''extensiv'':107B ''fall'':167B ''famously'':52B ''feat'':65B ''figur'':20B ''for'':48B ''from'':75B,165B ''her'':87B ''him'':73B,150B ''himself'':54B ''his'':49B,70B,79B,132B,137B,153B,163B ''imprison'':47B ''in'':21B,90B,102B,117B,129B,145B,151B,178B ''is'':17B ''jiub'':2A,4B,8B,42B,100B,155B ''known'':6B ''kvatch'':103B ''last'':143B ''leading'':124B ''legacy'':177B ''long'':127B ''magnificent'':10B ''mark'':37B ''memoirs'':154B ''menac'':16B ''morrowind'':89B ''new'':27B ''oblivion'':98B ''of'':13B,68B,96B,136B,174B ''on'':105B ''onset'':95B ''originally'':29B ''past'':36B ''plagu'':61B ''racers'':59B ''realm'':131B ''redemption'':44B,175B ''remain'':134B ''rever'':19B ''s'':156B ''saint'':1A,3B,171B ''sainthood'':74B ''serv'':158B ''sought'':43B ''soul'':119B ''spirit'':133B ''story'':157B ''tamriel'':179B ''templ'':24B,28B ''testament'':161B ''that'':60B,130B ''the'':9B,14B,22B,26B,57B,94B,97B,110B,118B,142B ''them'':173B ''this'':64B ''throughout'':88B ''to'':55B,125B,162B,169B ''transformation'':164B ''trapp'':116B ''tribunal'':23B ''troubl'':35B ''unawar'':135B ''until'':139B ''virtu'':80B ''vivec'':76B ''vvardenfell'':62B ''was'':101B,112B,115B ''when'':109B ''who'':77B,148B ''wing'':15B ''with'':33B ''working'':104B ''years'':67B', 'darkelf, daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Saint Jiub, also known as Jiub the Magnificent and Eradicator of the Winged Menace, is a revered figure in both the Tribunal Temple and the New Temple. Once a Dunmer assassin with a troubled past, he sought redemption by eradicating the cliff racers of Vvardenfell, a feat that earned him sainthood from Vivec. In 3E 433, during the Oblivion Crisis, Jiub was trapped in the Soul Cairn, unaware of his death, until he encountered the Last Dragonborn in 4E 201. Jiub’s transformation from a fallen assassin to a saint embodies themes of redemption and legacy.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hide_shield', 'Hide Shield is a basic hide shield with little protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides bound together with crude stitching. To craft it: 4 leather and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Novice smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''2'':38B ''4'':35B ''and'':19B,37B ''animal'':25B ''at'':41B,58B ''basic'':7B ''be'':53B ''blacksmith'':43B ''bound'':27B ''by'':55B ''can'':48B,52B ''craft'':33B,49B ''crud'':30B ''design'':16B ''forg'':44B ''hid'':1A,3B,8B,26B ''is'':5B,17B ''it'':34B,50B,51B ''its'':14B ''leath'':36B,39B,57B ''light'':23B ''littl'':11B ''mad'':21B ''novic'':46B ''of'':22B ''primitiv'':20B ''protection'':12B ''quality'':13B ''rough'':18B ''shield'':2A,4B,9B ''smith'':47B ''stitching'':31B ''strips'':40B ''tann'':24B ''tempered/improved'':54B ''to'':32B ''togeth'':28B ''using'':56B ''visual'':15B ''with'':10B,29B ''workbench'':60B', 'blacksmith', 'Hide Shield is a basic hide shield with little protection quality. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hero_of_daggerfall', 'The Agent, often referred to as the Hero of Daggerfall, was a covert operative of the Blades, dispatched by Emperor Uriel Septim VII in 3E 375. Tasked with exorcising the spirit of King Lysandus and recovering a sensitive letter sent to Queen Mynisera, the Agent became embroiled in the tumultuous political landscape of the Iliac Bay. This period was marked by intense power struggles involving the Empire, various regional kingdoms—including the Orcs of Nova Orsinium—Mannimarco, the King of Worms, and the mythical Underking, all vying for control of the legendary Numidium.

The Agent''s actions ultimately led to the activation of the Numidium in 3E 417, resulting in the Warp in the West, a significant event that dramatically altered the political and physical geography of the region. Following the Warp, the Agent mysteriously vanished, and the Blades could not establish contact despite their efforts. It is widely believed that the Agent perished during the activation of the Numidium, becoming a part of the enigmatic and chaotic legacy of that pivotal moment in history.', '''375'':29B ''3e'':28B,110B ''417'':111B ''actions'':100B ''activation'':105B,160B ''agent'':5B,48B,98B,137B,156B ''all'':89B ''alter'':124B ''and'':38B,85B,127B,140B,170B ''as'':9B ''bay'':59B ''becam'':49B ''becoming'':164B ''believ'':153B ''blad'':20B,142B ''by'':22B,64B ''chaotic'':171B ''contact'':146B ''control'':92B ''could'':143B ''covert'':16B ''daggerfall'':3A,13B ''despit'':147B ''dispatch'':21B ''dramatically'':123B ''during'':158B ''efforts'':149B ''embroil'':50B ''emperor'':23B ''empir'':70B ''enigmatic'':169B ''establish'':145B ''event'':121B ''exorcising'':32B ''following'':133B ''for'':91B ''geography'':129B ''her'':1A,11B ''history'':178B ''iliac'':58B ''in'':27B,51B,109B,113B,116B,177B ''including'':74B ''intens'':65B ''involving'':68B ''is'':151B ''it'':150B ''king'':36B,82B ''kingdoms'':73B ''landscap'':55B ''led'':102B ''legacy'':172B ''legendary'':95B ''lett'':42B ''lysandus'':37B ''mannimarc'':80B ''mark'':63B ''moment'':176B ''myniser'':46B ''mysteriously'':138B ''mythical'':87B ''not'':144B ''nov'':78B ''numidium'':96B,108B,163B ''of'':2A,12B,18B,35B,56B,77B,83B,93B,106B,130B,161B,167B,173B ''often'':6B ''operativ'':17B ''orcs'':76B ''orsinium'':79B ''part'':166B ''period'':61B ''perish'':157B ''physical'':128B ''pivotal'':175B ''political'':54B,126B ''pow'':66B ''que'':45B ''recovering'':39B ''referr'':7B ''region'':132B ''regional'':72B ''resulting'':112B ''s'':99B ''sensitiv'':41B ''sent'':43B ''septim'':25B ''significant'':120B ''spirit'':34B ''struggl'':67B ''task'':30B ''that'':122B,154B,174B ''the'':4B,10B,19B,33B,47B,52B,57B,69B,75B,81B,86B,94B,97B,104B,107B,114B,117B,125B,131B,134B,136B,141B,148B,155B,159B,162B,168B ''this'':60B ''to'':8B,44B,103B ''tumultuous'':53B ''ultimately'':101B ''underking'':88B ''uriel'':24B ''vanish'':139B ''various'':71B ''vii'':26B ''vying'':90B ''warp'':115B,135B ''was'':14B,62B ''west'':118B ''widely'':152B ''with'':31B ''worms'':84B', 'scholar, breton', 'The Agent, known as the Hero of Daggerfall, was a covert operative of the Blades sent by Emperor Uriel Septim VII in 3E 375. Tasked with exorcising King Lysandus'' spirit and recovering a letter for Queen Mynisera, the Agent became involved in political struggles in the Iliac Bay. Their actions led to the activation of the Numidium in 3E 417, causing the Warp in the West, which drastically changed the region. Afterward, the Agent mysteriously vanished, and it is believed they perished during the Warp, becoming part of the chaotic legacy of that moment.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fur_gauntlets', 'Fur Gauntlets have basic protection quality. Their visual design is rugged and stitched, made from scraps of fur and leather. They can not be crafted. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''adept'':29B ''an'':28B ''and'':14B,21B ''at'':40B ''basic'':6B ''be'':26B,35B ''by'':37B ''can'':24B,31B,34B ''craft'':27B,32B ''design'':11B ''from'':17B ''fur'':1A,3B,20B ''gauntlets'':2A,4B ''hav'':5B ''is'':12B ''it.it'':33B ''leath'':22B,39B ''mad'':16B ''not'':25B ''of'':19B ''protection'':7B ''quality'':8B ''rugg'':13B ''scraps'':18B ''smith'':30B ''stitch'':15B ''tempered/improved'':36B ''the'':9B ''they'':23B ''using'':38B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':42B', 'blacksmith', 'Fur Gauntlets have basic protection quality. Their visual design is rugged and stitched, made from scraps of fur and leather. They can not be crafted. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('leather_helmet', 'Leather Helmet is a basic leather helmet with basic protection quality. Its visual design is simple and flexible, with dark, weathered leather panels stitched together for mobility and basic protection. To craft it: 2 leather and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge.  A Novice smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''1'':39B ''2'':36B ''and'':19B,30B,38B ''at'':42B,59B ''basic'':7B,11B,31B ''be'':54B ''blacksmith'':44B ''by'':56B ''can'':49B,53B ''craft'':34B,50B ''dark'':22B ''design'':16B ''flexibl'':20B ''for'':28B ''forg'':45B ''helmet'':2A,4B,9B ''is'':5B,17B ''it'':35B,51B,52B ''its'':14B ''leath'':1A,3B,8B,24B,37B,40B,58B ''mobility'':29B ''novic'':47B ''panels'':25B ''protection'':12B,32B ''quality'':13B ''simpl'':18B ''smith'':48B ''stitch'':26B ''strip'':41B ''tempered/improved'':55B ''to'':33B ''togeth'':27B ''using'':57B ''visual'':15B ''weather'':23B ''with'':10B,21B ''workbench'':61B', 'blacksmith', 'Leather Helmet is a basic leather helmet with basic protection quality. Its visual design is simple and flexible, with dark, weathered leather panels stitched together for mobility and basic protection. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hero_of_kvatch', 'The Hero of Kvatch, also referred to as the Champion, is a significant figure in the history of Tamriel, known for their pivotal role during the Oblivion Crisis in the Third Era. He help Martin Septim defeat Mehrunes Dagon and save tamriel from an invasion from Oblivion. Their identity remains shrouded in mystery, with their race and gender unknown to most. ', '''also'':8B ''an'':47B ''and'':43B,60B ''as'':11B ''champion'':13B ''crisis'':31B ''dagon'':42B ''defeat'':40B ''during'':28B ''figur'':17B ''for'':24B ''from'':46B,49B ''gend'':61B ''help'':37B ''her'':1A,5B ''history'':20B ''identity'':52B ''in'':18B,32B,55B ''invasion'':48B ''is'':14B ''known'':23B ''kvatch'':3A,7B ''martin'':38B ''mehrun'':41B ''most'':64B ''mystery'':56B ''oblivion'':30B,50B ''of'':2A,6B,21B ''pivotal'':26B ''rac'':59B ''referr'':9B ''remains'':53B ''rol'':27B ''sav'':44B ''septim'':39B ''shroud'':54B ''significant'':16B ''tamriel'':22B,45B ''the'':4B,12B,19B,25B,29B,33B,51B,58B ''third'':34B ''to'':10B,63B ''unknown'':62B ''with'':57B', 'imperial, scholar', 'The Hero of Kvatch, also referred to as the Champion, is a significant figure in the history of Tamriel, known for their pivotal role during the Oblivion Crisis in the Third Era. Their identity remains shrouded in mystery, with their race and gender unknown to most. ', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('martin_septim', 'Martin Septim, the illegitimate son of Uriel Septim VII, was a key figure during the tumultuous events of the Oblivion Crisis. As an infant, he was rescued by Jauffre, the Grandmaster of the Blades, who ensured his safety away from the imperial court. Growing up unaware of his royal lineage, Martin became a devoted Priest of Akatosh in the city of Kvatch.

His life took a dramatic turn when the Mythic Dawn assassinated his father and half-brothers, leaving him as the unexpected heir to the Ruby Throne. Blades agents located Martin and protected him during the crisis, culminating in his reluctant rise to power. In a final act of sacrifice, Martin embraced his destiny and gave his life to thwart the Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon, thus securing the safety of Tamriel. His legacy is marked by his bravery, humility, and the heavy burden of his royal heritage.', '''act'':112B ''agents'':93B ''akatosh'':59B ''an'':25B ''and'':78B,96B,119B,144B ''as'':24B,84B ''assassinat'':75B ''away'':41B ''becam'':54B ''blad'':36B,92B ''bravery'':142B ''brothers'':81B ''burd'':147B ''by'':30B,140B ''city'':62B ''court'':45B ''crisis'':23B,101B ''culminating'':102B ''daedric'':126B ''dagon'':129B ''dawn'':74B ''destiny'':118B ''devot'':56B ''dramatic'':69B ''during'':16B,99B ''embrac'':116B ''ensur'':38B ''events'':19B ''fath'':77B ''figur'':15B ''final'':111B ''from'':42B ''gav'':120B ''grandmast'':33B ''growing'':46B ''half'':80B ''half-brothers'':79B ''heavy'':146B ''heir'':87B ''heritag'':151B ''him'':83B,98B ''his'':39B,50B,65B,76B,104B,117B,121B,136B,141B,149B ''humility'':143B ''illegitimat'':6B ''imperial'':44B ''in'':60B,103B,109B ''infant'':26B ''is'':138B ''jauffr'':31B ''key'':14B ''kvatch'':64B ''leaving'':82B ''legacy'':137B ''lif'':66B,122B ''lineag'':52B ''locat'':94B ''mark'':139B ''martin'':1A,3B,53B,95B,115B ''mehrun'':128B ''mythic'':73B ''oblivion'':22B ''of'':8B,20B,34B,49B,58B,63B,113B,134B,148B ''pow'':108B ''priest'':57B ''princ'':127B ''protect'':97B ''reluctant'':105B ''rescu'':29B ''ris'':106B ''royal'':51B,150B ''ruby'':90B ''sacrific'':114B ''safety'':40B,133B ''securing'':131B ''septim'':2A,4B,10B ''tamriel'':135B ''the'':5B,17B,21B,32B,35B,43B,61B,72B,85B,89B,100B,125B,132B,145B ''thron'':91B ''thus'':130B ''thwart'':124B ''to'':88B,107B,123B ''took'':67B ''tumultuous'':18B ''turn'':70B ''unawar'':48B ''unexpect'':86B ''up'':47B ''uriel'':9B ''vii'':11B ''was'':12B,28B ''when'':71B ''who'':37B', 'imperial, scholar', 'Martin Septim, the illegitimate son of Uriel Septim VII, played a crucial role during the Oblivion Crisis. Raised as a Priest of Akatosh in Kvatch and unaware of his royal lineage, his life changed when the Mythic Dawn assassinated his father and half-brothers, making him the heir to the Ruby Throne. Protected by Blades agents, Martin reluctantly rose to power. In his final act, he sacrificed himself to defeat the Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon and save Tamriel. His legacy is defined by his bravery, humility, and the weight of his royal heritage.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('high_king_torygg', 'High King Torygg was the ruler of Skyrim and the Jarl of Solitude until his death in 4E 201. The son of Istlod, who had reigned for nearly twenty-five years, Torygg was formally named his successor by the Moot, despite the growing calls for Skyrim''s independence from the influential Ulfric Stormcloak. Torygg respected Ulfric''s passionate stance and sought to engage him in dialogue about his views, unaware that Ulfric had come with the intention of challenging him for the throne.

The encounter between Torygg and Ulfric culminated in tragedy, as Ulfric used his thu''um to overpower the young king and subsequently killed him. While Ulfric viewed the act as a rightful challenge for leadership, many—including the Empire and several Jarls—considered it regicide, noting Torygg''s limited martial training compared to Ulfric''s experience as a war veteran. Following Torygg''s death, his widow, Elisif the Fair, ascended to the position of Jarl of Solitude and aimed to claim the title of High Queen with the support of the Empire. ', '''201'':22B ''4e'':21B ''about'':71B ''act'':116B ''aim'':166B ''and'':12B,64B,92B,108B,127B,165B ''as'':97B,117B,144B ''ascend'':157B ''betw'':90B ''by'':42B ''calls'':48B ''challeng'':120B ''challenging'':83B ''claim'':168B ''com'':78B ''compar'':139B ''consider'':130B ''culminat'':94B ''death'':19B,151B ''despit'':45B ''dialog'':70B ''elisif'':154B ''empir'':126B,179B ''encount'':89B ''engag'':67B ''experienc'':143B ''fair'':156B ''fiv'':34B ''following'':148B ''for'':30B,49B,85B,121B ''formally'':38B ''from'':53B ''growing'':47B ''had'':28B,77B ''high'':1A,4B,172B ''him'':68B,84B,111B ''his'':18B,40B,72B,100B,152B ''in'':20B,69B,95B ''including'':124B ''independenc'':52B ''influential'':55B ''intention'':81B ''istlod'':26B ''it'':131B ''jarl'':14B,162B ''jarls'':129B ''kill'':110B ''king'':2A,5B,107B ''leadership'':122B ''limit'':136B ''many'':123B ''martial'':137B ''moot'':44B ''nam'':39B ''nearly'':31B ''noting'':133B ''of'':10B,15B,25B,82B,161B,163B,171B,177B ''overpow'':104B ''passionat'':62B ''position'':160B ''que'':173B ''regicid'':132B ''reign'':29B ''respect'':59B ''rightful'':119B ''rul'':9B ''s'':51B,61B,135B,142B,150B ''several'':128B ''skyrim'':11B,50B ''solitud'':16B,164B ''sought'':65B ''stanc'':63B ''stormcloak'':57B ''subsequently'':109B ''successor'':41B ''support'':176B ''that'':75B ''the'':8B,13B,23B,43B,46B,54B,80B,86B,88B,105B,115B,125B,155B,159B,169B,175B,178B ''thron'':87B ''thu'':101B ''titl'':170B ''to'':66B,103B,140B,158B,167B ''torygg'':3A,6B,36B,58B,91B,134B,149B ''tragedy'':96B ''training'':138B ''twenty'':33B ''twenty-fiv'':32B ''ulfric'':56B,60B,76B,93B,98B,113B,141B ''um'':102B ''unawar'':74B ''until'':17B ''used'':99B ''veter'':147B ''view'':114B ''views'':73B ''war'':146B ''was'':7B,37B ''whil'':112B ''who'':27B ''widow'':153B ''with'':79B,174B ''years'':35B ''young'':106B', 'nord, scholar', 'High King Torygg was the ruler of Skyrim and the Jarl of Solitude until his death in 4E 201. The son of Istlod, he was named his successor by the Moot, despite Ulfric Stormcloak''s growing calls for Skyrim''s independence. Torygg respected Ulfric’s views and sought dialogue, unaware that Ulfric came to challenge him for the throne. The confrontation ended when Ulfric used his thu''um to kill Torygg, an act many, including the Empire, considered regicide. After his death, his widow, Elisif the Fair, became Jarl of Solitude and sought to claim the title of High Queen with the Empire’s support.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('general_tullius', 'General Tullius is a prominent Imperial military leader tasked with suppressing the Stormcloak Rebellion in Skyrim. Originally hailing from Cyrodiil, he was appointed as the Military Governor of the region and viewed Ulfric Stormcloak as a dangerous usurper whose actions posed a significant threat to the Empire. Tullius earned a reputation among Imperial supporters as their best hope for victory against the rebellion. Initially dismissive of Nordic culture, he eventually came to respect it, recognizing its importance in the context of the conflict.

In 4E 201, Tullius nearly executed both Ulfric Stormcloak and the Last Dragonborn during a critical moment before the dragon Alduin''s attack on Helgen. Surviving this encounter, he returned to Solitude to continue his campaign against the Stormcloaks, undeterred by the resurgence of dragons. As Ulfric''s forces grew more aggressive, Tullius focused on securing the allegiance of Balgruuf the Greater, the neutral Jarl of Whiterun. His efforts were ultimately rewarded when Balgruuf pledged loyalty to the Empire in exchange for reinforcements to defend against an impending Stormcloak siege, highlighting Tullius''s strategic acumen amidst the chaos of war.', '''201'':88B ''4e'':87B ''actions'':42B ''acum'':180B ''against'':63B,122B,171B ''aggressiv'':137B ''alduin'':106B ''allegianc'':143B ''amidst'':181B ''among'':54B ''an'':172B ''and'':33B,95B ''appoint'':25B ''as'':26B,37B,57B,131B ''attack'':108B ''balgruuf'':145B,159B ''befor'':103B ''best'':59B ''both'':92B ''by'':126B ''cam'':73B ''campaign'':121B ''cha'':183B ''conflict'':85B ''context'':82B ''continu'':119B ''critical'':101B ''cultur'':70B ''cyrodiil'':22B ''dangerous'':39B ''defend'':170B ''dismissiv'':67B ''dragon'':105B ''dragonborn'':98B ''dragons'':130B ''during'':99B ''earn'':51B ''efforts'':154B ''empir'':49B,164B ''encount'':113B ''eventually'':72B ''exchang'':166B ''execut'':91B ''focus'':139B ''for'':61B,167B ''forc'':134B ''from'':21B ''general'':1A,3B ''governor'':29B ''great'':147B ''grew'':135B ''hailing'':20B ''helg'':110B ''highlighting'':176B ''his'':120B,153B ''hop'':60B ''impending'':173B ''imperial'':8B,55B ''importanc'':79B ''in'':17B,80B,86B,165B ''initially'':66B ''is'':5B ''it'':76B ''its'':78B ''jarl'':150B ''last'':97B ''lead'':10B ''loyalty'':161B ''military'':9B,28B ''moment'':102B ''mor'':136B ''nearly'':90B ''neutral'':149B ''nordic'':69B ''of'':30B,68B,83B,129B,144B,151B,184B ''on'':109B,140B ''originally'':19B ''pledg'':160B ''pos'':43B ''prominent'':7B ''rebellion'':16B,65B ''recognizing'':77B ''region'':32B ''reinforcements'':168B ''reputation'':53B ''respect'':75B ''resurgenc'':128B ''return'':115B ''reward'':157B ''s'':107B,133B,178B ''securing'':141B ''sieg'':175B ''significant'':45B ''skyrim'':18B ''solitud'':117B ''stormcloak'':15B,36B,94B,174B ''stormcloaks'':124B ''strategic'':179B ''supporters'':56B ''suppressing'':13B ''surviving'':111B ''task'':11B ''the'':14B,27B,31B,48B,58B,64B,81B,84B,96B,104B,123B,127B,142B,146B,148B,163B,182B ''this'':112B ''threat'':46B ''to'':47B,74B,116B,118B,162B,169B ''tullius'':2A,4B,50B,89B,138B,177B ''ulfric'':35B,93B,132B ''ultimately'':156B ''undeterr'':125B ''usurp'':40B ''victory'':62B ''view'':34B ''war'':185B ''was'':24B ''wer'':155B ''when'':158B ''whiterun'':152B ''whos'':41B ''with'':12B', 'imperial, scholar', 'General Tullius is an Imperial military leader assigned to suppress the Stormcloak Rebellion in Skyrim. He was appointed as Military Governor and saw Ulfric Stormcloak as a major threat to the Empire. Although initially dismissive of Nordic culture, Tullius eventually came to respect it. In 4E 201, he nearly executed both Ulfric and the Last Dragonborn before Alduin''s attack on Helgen. Tullius continued his campaign, securing Balgruuf the Greater''s loyalty in exchange for reinforcements to defend against a Stormcloak siege.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chitin_boots', 'Chitin Boots are a pair of chitin boots with good protection quality. Its visual design is organic and jagged, with dark, shell-like plates and a rough, natural texture. To craft it: 1 leather, 1 iron ingot and 3 chitin at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using chitin at a workbench.', '''1'':36B,38B ''3'':42B ''adept'':49B ''an'':48B ''and'':20B,28B,41B ''are'':5B ''at'':44B,61B ''be'':56B ''blacksmith'':46B ''boots'':2A,4B,10B ''by'':58B ''can'':51B,55B ''chitin'':1A,3B,9B,43B,60B ''craft'':34B,52B ''dark'':23B ''design'':17B ''forg'':47B ''good'':12B ''ingot'':40B ''iron'':39B ''is'':18B ''it'':35B,53B,54B ''its'':15B ''jagg'':21B ''leath'':37B ''lik'':26B ''natural'':31B ''of'':8B ''organic'':19B ''pair'':7B ''plat'':27B ''protection'':13B ''quality'':14B ''rough'':30B ''shell'':25B ''shell-lik'':24B ''smith'':50B ''tempered/improved'':57B ''textur'':32B ''to'':33B ''using'':59B ''visual'':16B ''with'':11B,22B ''workbench'':63B', 'blacksmith', 'Chitin Boots are a pair of chitin boots with good protection quality. Its visual design is organic and jagged, with dark, shell-like plates and a rough, natural texture. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('jyggalag', 'Jyggalag, the Prince of Order, is a Daedric Prince whose sphere encompasses logical order, deduction, and the unyielding structure of the cosmos. Known as the "Gray Prince of Order," Jyggalag once ruled a realm of perfect symmetry and foresight, boasting a Great Library that held predictions of every event in Mundus and Oblivion. His expansion across the seas of Oblivion struck fear and envy into the hearts of other Daedric Princes, leading them to curse him into becoming Sheogorath, the Madgod—his antithesis. This curse created a paradox: Jyggalag, the embodiment of order, became the incarnation of chaos and madness. However, every era culminated in the Greymarch, a cycle where Jyggalag would briefly reclaim his form, only to be reverted back to Sheogorath after his conquest of the Shivering Isles.

The cycle of the Greymarch was ultimately broken during the events of the Third Era when the Hero of Kvatch, chosen by Sheogorath, confronted Jyggalag during his return. Armed with the Staff of Sheogorath and the mantle of the Madgod, the Hero defeated the Prince of Order, ending the Greymarch and separating Jyggalag from Sheogorath forever. Jyggalag acknowledged the Hero''s victory, departing the Shivering Isles to roam Oblivion once more, perhaps to exact vengeance on those who cursed him or to pursue grander, unknown ambitions. His legacy endures through his artifact, the Sword of Jyggalag, a crystalline claymore imbued with the power to reveal the flow of time. Though his presence has waned, the balance of power within Oblivion remains uncertain, as Jyggalag''s return could herald a new era of unyielding order across the realms.', '''acknowledg'':189B ''across'':57B,266B ''after'':125B ''ambitions'':217B ''and'':17B,39B,53B,64B,100B,166B,182B ''antithesis'':84B ''armed'':160B ''artifact'':223B ''as'':25B,254B ''back'':122B ''balanc'':247B ''be'':120B ''becam'':95B ''becoming'':79B ''boasting'':41B ''briefly'':114B ''brok'':139B ''by'':153B ''cha'':99B ''chos'':152B ''claymor'':230B ''confront'':155B ''conquest'':127B ''cosm'':23B ''could'':258B ''creat'':87B ''crystallin'':229B ''culminat'':105B ''curs'':76B,86B,210B ''cycle'':110B,133B ''daedric'':9B,71B ''deduction'':16B ''defeat'':174B ''departing'':194B ''during'':140B,157B ''embodiment'':92B ''encompass'':13B ''ending'':179B ''endur'':220B ''envy'':65B ''event'':50B ''events'':142B ''every'':49B,103B ''exact'':205B ''expansion'':56B ''fear'':63B ''flow'':238B ''foresight'':40B ''forev'':187B ''form'':117B ''from'':185B ''grand'':215B ''gray'':27B ''great'':43B ''greymarch'':108B,136B,181B ''hearts'':68B ''held'':46B ''her'':149B,173B,191B ''herald'':259B ''him'':77B,211B ''his'':55B,83B,116B,126B,158B,218B,222B,242B ''howev'':102B ''imbu'':231B ''in'':51B,106B ''incarnation'':97B ''into'':66B,78B ''is'':7B ''isles'':131B,197B ''jyggalag'':1A,2B,31B,90B,112B,156B,184B,188B,227B,255B ''known'':24B ''kvatch'':151B ''leading'':73B ''legacy'':219B ''library'':44B ''logical'':14B ''madgod'':82B,171B ''madness'':101B ''mantl'':168B ''mor'':202B ''mundus'':52B ''new'':261B ''oblivion'':54B,61B,200B,251B ''of'':5B,21B,29B,36B,48B,60B,69B,93B,98B,128B,134B,143B,150B,164B,169B,177B,226B,239B,248B,263B ''on'':207B ''once'':32B,201B ''only'':118B ''or'':212B ''order'':6B,15B,30B,94B,178B,265B ''other'':70B ''paradox'':89B ''perfect'':37B ''perhaps'':203B ''pow'':234B,249B ''predictions'':47B ''presenc'':243B ''princ'':4B,10B,28B,72B,176B ''pursu'':214B ''realm'':35B ''realms'':268B ''reclaim'':115B ''remains'':252B ''return'':159B,257B ''reveal'':236B ''revert'':121B ''roam'':199B ''rul'':33B ''s'':192B,256B ''separating'':183B ''sheogorath'':80B,124B,154B,165B,186B ''shivering'':130B,196B ''spher'':12B ''staff'':163B ''struck'':62B ''structur'':20B ''sword'':225B ''symmetry'':38B ''that'':45B ''the'':3B,18B,22B,26B,58B,67B,81B,91B,96B,107B,129B,132B,135B,141B,144B,148B,162B,167B,170B,172B,175B,180B,190B,195B,224B,233B,237B,246B,267B ''them'':74B ''third'':145B ''this'':85B ''thos'':208B ''though'':241B ''through'':221B ''tim'':240B ''to'':75B,119B,123B,198B,204B,213B,235B ''ultimately'':138B ''uncertain'':253B ''unknown'':216B ''unyielding'':19B,264B ''vengeanc'':206B ''victory'':193B ''wan'':245B ''was'':137B ''when'':147B ''wher'':111B ''who'':209B ''whos'':11B ''with'':161B,232B ''within'':250B ''would'':113B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Jyggalag, the Daedric Prince of Order, governs logical order, deduction, and the cosmos''s structure. Once ruling a realm of perfect symmetry, his Great Library predicted every event. Fearing his power, other Daedric Princes cursed him into becoming Sheogorath, the Madgod, creating a paradox. Each era saw Jyggalag briefly reclaim his form during the Greymarch before returning to Sheogorath. This cycle ended when the Hero of Kvatch defeated Jyggalag, breaking the curse. His legacy persists through the Sword of Jyggalag, a claymore that reveals the flow of time. His return could signal a new era of order across Oblivion.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('magnus', 'Magnus, the God of Magic and the Great Architect, is a revered figure among many cultures in Tamriel, known as the creator of the schematics for Mundus. During the Dawn Era, he collaborated with other et''Ada to forge the mortal plane, but upon realizing the great sacrifice required, he abandoned the project. His departure from Mundus tore a hole into Aetherius, forming the sun, which is also referred to as Magnus. The stars, believed to be fragments of his being or tears in the sky made by his followers, the Magna Ge, illuminate the night as remnants of his retreat. Magnus’s legacy is steeped in mysticism, as he is credited with creating powerful artifacts like the Staff of Magnus and the Eye of Magnus, each holding immense arcane power capable of influencing the balance of the magical world.

Worship of Magnus varies across Tamriel. The Altmer and Bretons revere him as the God of Sight and Insight, while the Khajiit call him Magrus, the Cat''s Eye, integrating his mythos into their lunar cycles. The Ayleids dedicated temples to his name, celebrating his association with light and divine order. Legends suggest Magnus influences powerful mages, lending them his energy, though his contributions to Mundus are viewed with skepticism by the Imperials, who question the dual nature of his gift. Despite his detachment from Nirn, Magnus remains a symbol of the enigmatic power of magic, with his artifacts and celestial presence serving as constant reminders of the god who shaped the mystical fabric of the world.', '''abandon'':52B ''across'':146B ''ada'':38B ''aetherius'':63B ''also'':69B ''altmer'':149B ''among'':15B ''and'':7B,123B,150B,159B,190B,241B ''arcan'':131B ''architect'':10B ''are'':208B ''artifacts'':117B,240B ''as'':21B,72B,98B,110B,154B,245B ''association'':187B ''ayleids'':179B ''balanc'':137B ''be'':78B ''being'':82B ''believ'':76B ''bretons'':151B ''but'':44B ''by'':89B,212B ''call'':164B ''capabl'':133B ''cat'':168B ''celebrating'':185B ''celestial'':242B ''collaborat'':34B ''constant'':246B ''contributions'':205B ''creating'':115B ''creator'':23B ''credit'':113B ''cultur'':17B ''cycles'':177B ''dawn'':31B ''dedicat'':180B ''departur'':56B ''despit'':223B ''detachment'':225B ''divin'':191B ''dual'':218B ''during'':29B ''each'':128B ''energy'':202B ''enigmatic'':234B ''et'':37B ''eye'':125B,170B ''fabric'':255B ''figur'':14B ''followers'':91B ''for'':27B ''forg'':40B ''forming'':64B ''fragments'':79B ''from'':57B,226B ''ge'':94B ''gift'':222B ''god'':4B,156B,250B ''great'':9B,48B ''him'':153B,165B ''his'':55B,81B,90B,101B,172B,183B,186B,201B,204B,221B,224B,239B ''hol'':61B ''holding'':129B ''illuminat'':95B ''immens'':130B ''imperials'':214B ''in'':18B,85B,108B ''influenc'':196B ''influencing'':135B ''insight'':160B ''integrating'':171B ''into'':62B,174B ''is'':11B,68B,106B,112B ''khajiit'':163B ''known'':20B ''legacy'':105B ''legends'':193B ''lending'':199B ''light'':189B ''lik'':118B ''lun'':176B ''mad'':88B ''mag'':198B ''magic'':6B,237B ''magical'':140B ''magn'':93B ''magnus'':1A,2B,73B,103B,122B,127B,144B,195B,228B ''magrus'':166B ''many'':16B ''mortal'':42B ''mundus'':28B,58B,207B ''mystical'':254B ''mysticism'':109B ''mythos'':173B ''nam'':184B ''natur'':219B ''night'':97B ''nirn'':227B ''of'':5B,24B,80B,100B,121B,126B,134B,138B,143B,157B,220B,232B,236B,248B,256B ''or'':83B ''order'':192B ''other'':36B ''plan'':43B ''pow'':132B,235B ''powerful'':116B,197B ''presenc'':243B ''project'':54B ''question'':216B ''realizing'':46B ''referr'':70B ''remains'':229B ''reminders'':247B ''remnants'':99B ''requir'':50B ''retreat'':102B ''rever'':13B,152B ''s'':104B,169B ''sacrific'':49B ''schematics'':26B ''serving'':244B ''shap'':252B ''sight'':158B ''skepticism'':211B ''sky'':87B ''staff'':120B ''stars'':75B ''steep'':107B ''suggest'':194B ''sun'':66B ''symbol'':231B ''tamriel'':19B,147B ''tears'':84B ''templ'':181B ''the'':3B,8B,22B,25B,30B,41B,47B,53B,65B,74B,86B,92B,96B,119B,124B,136B,139B,148B,155B,162B,167B,175B,178B,213B,217B,233B,249B,253B,257B ''them'':200B ''though'':203B ''to'':39B,71B,77B,182B,206B ''tor'':59B ''upon'':45B ''vari'':145B ''view'':209B ''which'':67B ''whil'':161B ''who'':215B,251B ''with'':35B,114B,188B,210B,238B ''world'':141B,258B ''worship'':142B', 'scholar, priest, mage, collegeofwinterhold', 'Magnus, the God of Magic and the Great Architect, is credited with creating the schematics for Mundus during the Dawn Era. He collaborated with other et''Ada but abandoned the project when he realized the sacrifice required, creating the sun and stars in the process. Magnus''s followers, the Magna Ge, are believed to have left remnants of his being in the stars. He is known for powerful artifacts like the Staff of Magnus and the Eye of Magnus. Worshiped by the Altmer, Bretons, and Khajiit, Magnus is viewed as a symbol of magical power and mysticism.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mannimarco', 'Mannimarco, known as the God of Worms and founder of the Order of the Black Worm, is one of the most infamous figures in Tamrielic history. Originally an Altmer (or Aldmer by his own claim) and a member of the Psijic Order on Artaeum, Mannimarco''s dark fascination with necromancy led to his expulsion after his practices horrified his peers, including his former friend Vanus Galerion, who later founded the Mages Guild. This exile marked the beginning of Mannimarco''s ascent into infamy as he gathered followers and became the world''s first lich, earning the title "King of Worms." His mastery of necromancy allowed him to tap into forbidden arts, consorting with Daedra like Molag Bal and creating vile artifacts such as the Necromancer''s Amulet and the Staff of Worms. Mannimarco''s influence spread across Tamriel through his cult, the Worm Cult, which orchestrated political schemes and dark rituals, including the catastrophic Soulburst during the Planemeld.

Mannimarco''s pursuit of power culminated during the Warp in the West, a mysterious event in which he achieved apotheosis, transforming into a divine being embodied by the Necromancer''s Moon, also known as the Revenant. Despite this ascension, Mannimarco maintained a tangible presence in Tamriel, clashing with the Mages Guild and other enemies, such as the Hero of Kvatch, who destroyed his mortal form in 3E 433. His divine legacy, however, persisted, as the Necromancer''s Moon continued to empower his followers, allowing them to corrupt soul gems and perpetuate his dark influence. Through his artifacts, rituals, and the enduring shadow of his cult, Mannimarco remains an enduring figure of dread in Tamriel, a symbol of the dangerous allure of necromancy and the pursuit of immortality at any cost.', '''3e'':226B ''433'':227B ''achiev'':178B ''across'':138B ''after'':56B ''aldmer'':32B ''allow'':106B ''allowing'':243B ''allur'':279B ''also'':191B ''altmer'':30B ''amulet'':128B ''an'':29B,267B ''and'':9B,37B,89B,119B,129B,150B,211B,249B,258B,282B ''any'':288B ''apotheosis'':179B ''artaeum'':45B ''artifacts'':122B,256B ''arts'':112B ''as'':4B,85B,124B,193B,215B,233B ''ascension'':198B ''ascent'':82B ''at'':287B ''bal'':118B ''becam'':90B ''beginning'':78B ''being'':184B ''black'':16B ''by'':33B,186B ''catastrophic'':155B ''claim'':36B ''clashing'':206B ''consorting'':113B ''continu'':238B ''corrupt'':246B ''cost'':289B ''creating'':120B ''culminat'':165B ''cult'':142B,145B,264B ''daedr'':115B ''dangerous'':278B ''dark'':48B,151B,252B ''despit'':196B ''destroy'':221B ''divin'':183B,229B ''dre'':271B ''during'':157B,166B ''earning'':96B ''embodi'':185B ''empow'':240B ''enduring'':260B,268B ''enemi'':213B ''event'':174B ''exil'':75B ''expulsion'':55B ''fascination'':49B ''figur'':24B,269B ''first'':94B ''followers'':88B,242B ''forbidd'':111B ''form'':64B,224B ''found'':10B,70B ''friend'':65B ''galerion'':67B ''gather'':87B ''gems'':248B ''god'':6B ''guild'':73B,210B ''her'