INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hevnoraak', '
Hevnoraak was a tyrannical Dragon Priest who ruled Valthume with fear, manipulating and torturing his followers without consequence. As his death approached, he became obsessed with ensuring his resurrection, filling vessels with his own blood to transfer his power after death. After Hevnoraak''s demise, a warrior named Valdar vowed to guard his tomb and prevent his return, keeping watch for generations.', '''after'':41B,43B ''and'':14B,56B ''approach'':23B ''as'':20B ''becam'':25B ''blood'':36B ''consequenc'':19B ''death'':22B,42B ''demis'':46B ''dragon'':6B ''ensuring'':28B ''fear'':12B ''filling'':31B ''followers'':17B ''for'':62B ''generations'':63B ''guard'':53B ''hevnoraak'':1A,2B,44B ''his'':16B,21B,29B,34B,39B,54B,58B ''keeping'':60B ''manipulating'':13B ''nam'':49B ''obsess'':26B ''own'':35B ''pow'':40B ''prevent'':57B ''priest'':7B ''resurrection'':30B ''return'':59B ''rul'':9B ''s'':45B ''to'':37B,52B ''tomb'':55B ''torturing'':15B ''transf'':38B ''tyrannical'':5B ''vald'':50B ''valthum'':10B ''vessels'':32B ''vow'':51B ''warrior'':48B ''was'':3B ''watch'':61B ''who'':8B ''with'':11B,27B,33B ''without'':18B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Hevnoraak must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Skyrim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('krosis', '
Krosis was a high-ranking Dragon Priest in the Merethic Era, serving the Dragon Cult with great power and mastery over both magic and the Thu''um. After the Dragon War, he was entombed at Shearpoint, where he remained until his reawakening in the Fourth Era. Known for his magical abilities and enhanced powers from his iron mask, Krosis became a lich, sustained by his draugr servants'' worship. He was ultimately defeated and sealed away.', '''abiliti'':53B ''after'':30B ''and'':21B,26B,54B,75B ''at'':37B ''away'':77B ''becam'':62B ''both'':24B ''by'':66B ''cult'':17B ''defeat'':74B ''dragon'':8B,16B,32B ''draugr'':68B ''enhanc'':55B ''entomb'':36B ''for'':50B ''fourth'':47B ''from'':57B ''great'':19B ''high'':6B ''high-ranking'':5B ''his'':43B,51B,58B,67B ''in'':10B,45B ''iron'':59B ''known'':49B ''krosis'':1A,2B,61B ''lich'':64B ''magic'':25B ''magical'':52B ''mask'':60B ''mastery'':22B ''merethic'':12B ''over'':23B ''pow'':20B ''powers'':56B ''priest'':9B ''ranking'':7B ''reawakening'':44B ''remain'':41B ''seal'':76B ''servants'':69B ''serving'':14B ''shearpoint'':38B ''sustain'':65B ''the'':11B,15B,27B,31B,46B ''thu'':28B ''ultimately'':73B ''um'':29B ''until'':42B ''war'':33B ''was'':3B,35B,72B ''wher'':39B ''with'':18B ''worship'':70B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Krosis must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Skyrim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('morokei', '
Morokei, also known as the Deathless, was a powerful Dragon Priest in the Merethic Era who achieved lichdom through the worship of his draugr servants. Gifted a magical moonstone mask by his dragon overlord, he was immune to death except by the Thu''um of a dragon. After the Dragon War, he was sealed in the ruins of Bromjunaar, later known as Labyrinthian, by sacred fires to prevent him from seeking vengeance. Morokei was ultimately destroyed around 4E 201.', '''201'':80B ''4e'':79B ''achiev'':18B ''after'':49B ''also'':3B ''around'':78B ''as'':5B,63B ''bromjun'':60B ''by'':32B,42B,65B ''death'':40B ''deathless'':7B ''destroy'':77B ''dragon'':11B,34B,48B,51B ''draugr'':25B ''except'':41B ''fir'':67B ''from'':71B ''gift'':27B ''him'':70B ''his'':24B,33B ''immun'':38B ''in'':13B,56B ''known'':4B,62B ''labyrinthi'':64B ''lat'':61B ''lichdom'':19B ''magical'':29B ''mask'':31B ''merethic'':15B ''moonston'':30B ''morokei'':1A,2B,74B ''of'':23B,46B,59B ''overlord'':35B ''powerful'':10B ''prevent'':69B ''priest'':12B ''ruins'':58B ''sacr'':66B ''seal'':55B ''seeking'':72B ''servants'':26B ''the'':6B,14B,21B,43B,50B,57B ''through'':20B ''thu'':44B ''to'':39B,68B ''ultimately'':76B ''um'':45B ''vengeanc'':73B ''war'':52B ''was'':8B,37B,54B,75B ''who'':17B ''worship'':22B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Morokei, must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Skyrim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
