INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vittoria_vici', 'Vittoria Vici is an influential Imperial from Solitude, cousin to Emperor Titus Mede II, and oversees the East Empire Company''s holdings in the city. Engaged to Stormcloak Asgeir Snow-Shod, their upcoming wedding is seen as a symbolic end to the civil war. However, the event attracts the attention of the Dark Brotherhood, who plan to use it to restore their reputation.', '''an'':6B ''and'':17B ''as'':40B ''asge'':31B ''attention'':53B ''attracts'':51B ''brotherhood'':57B ''city'':27B ''civil'':46B ''company'':22B ''cousin'':11B ''dark'':56B ''east'':20B ''emperor'':13B ''empir'':21B ''end'':43B ''engag'':28B ''event'':50B ''from'':9B ''holdings'':24B ''howev'':48B ''ii'':16B ''imperial'':8B ''in'':25B ''influential'':7B ''is'':5B,38B ''it'':62B ''med'':15B ''of'':54B ''overs'':18B ''plan'':59B ''reputation'':66B ''restor'':64B ''s'':23B ''seen'':39B ''shod'':34B ''snow'':33B ''snow-shod'':32B ''solitud'':10B ''stormcloak'':30B ''symbolic'':42B ''the'':19B,26B,35B,45B,49B,52B,55B,65B ''titus'':14B ''to'':12B,29B,44B,60B,63B ''upcoming'':36B ''use'':61B ''vici'':2A,4B ''vittori'':1A,3B ''war'':47B ''wedding'':37B ''who'':58B', 'noble, darkbrotherhood', 'Vittoria Vici is an influential Imperial from Solitude, cousin to Emperor Titus Mede II, and oversees the East Empire Company''s holdings in the city. She is having a wedding in Solitude at somepoint.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('otar_the_mad', 'Otar the Mad was a high-ranking Dragon Priest in the Merethic Era, once a just ruler who descended into madness, causing the downfall of Ragnvald. He wielded powerful magic and the Thu''um, and was known for his oppressive rule. After being defeated by heroes Saerek and Torsten, he was sealed in Ragnvald''s tomb, with his fate tied to two keys held by his captors. Otar was reawakened in the Fourth Era, still bound by his tomb and his past malevolent power.', '''after'':46B ''and'':35B,39B,52B,84B ''being'':47B ''bound'':80B ''by'':49B,69B,81B ''captors'':71B ''causing'':26B ''defeat'':48B ''descend'':23B ''downfall'':28B ''dragon'':12B ''fat'':63B ''for'':42B ''fourth'':77B ''held'':68B ''her'':50B ''high'':10B ''high-ranking'':9B ''his'':43B,62B,70B,82B,85B ''in'':14B,57B,75B ''into'':24B ''just'':20B ''keys'':67B ''known'':41B ''mad'':3A,6B ''madness'':25B ''magic'':34B ''malevolent'':87B ''merethic'':16B ''of'':29B ''once'':18B ''oppressiv'':44B ''otar'':1A,4B,72B ''past'':86B ''pow'':88B ''powerful'':33B ''priest'':13B ''ragnvald'':30B,58B ''ranking'':11B ''reawaken'':74B ''rul'':21B,45B ''s'':59B ''saerek'':51B ''seal'':56B ''still'':79B ''the'':2A,5B,15B,27B,36B,76B ''thu'':37B ''tied'':64B ''to'':65B ''tomb'':60B,83B ''torst'':53B ''two'':66B ''um'':38B ''was'':7B,40B,55B,73B ''who'':22B ''wield'':32B ''with'':61B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Otar the Mad must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Skyrim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rahgot', '
Rahgot, an ancient Dragon Priest of Skyrim, led the last remnants of the Dragon Cult from the monastery of Forelhost until 1E 140. After the defeat of Alduin, Rahgot and his followers went into hiding, believing Alduin would eventually return. When King Harald''s soldiers discovered his stronghold, Rahgot orchestrated a mass suicide among his cultists to deter the soldiers from uncovering his survival. Rahgot was later encased in a sarcophagus within the monastery, with his followers'' sacrifice keeping the magic barrier intact.', '''140'':24B ''1e'':23B ''after'':25B ''alduin'':29B,38B ''among'':55B ''an'':3B ''ancient'':4B ''and'':31B ''barri'':83B ''believing'':37B ''cult'':16B ''cultists'':57B ''defeat'':27B ''det'':59B ''discover'':47B ''dragon'':5B,15B ''encas'':69B ''eventually'':40B ''followers'':33B,78B ''forelhost'':21B ''from'':17B,62B ''harald'':44B ''hiding'':36B ''his'':32B,48B,56B,64B,77B ''in'':70B ''intact'':84B ''into'':35B ''keeping'':80B ''king'':43B ''last'':11B ''lat'':68B ''led'':9B ''magic'':82B ''mass'':53B ''monastery'':19B,75B ''of'':7B,13B,20B,28B ''orchestrat'':51B ''priest'':6B ''rahgot'':1A,2B,30B,50B,66B ''remnants'':12B ''return'':41B ''s'':45B ''sacrific'':79B ''sarcophagus'':72B ''skyrim'':8B ''soldiers'':46B,61B ''stronghold'':49B ''suicid'':54B ''survival'':65B ''the'':10B,14B,18B,26B,60B,74B,81B ''to'':58B ''uncovering'':63B ''until'':22B ''was'':67B ''went'':34B ''when'':42B ''with'':76B ''within'':73B ''would'':39B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Rahgot must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Skyrim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
