INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vahlok_the_jailor', '
Vahlok the Jailor was a Dragon Priest who once ruled Solstheim and was tasked with guarding the traitor Miraak. After uncovering Miraak''s plot against their masters, Vahlok defeated him in a legendary battle and was later entombed in Vahlok''s Tomb in Solstheim.', '''after'':23B ''against'':28B ''and'':15B,38B ''battl'':37B ''defeat'':32B ''dragon'':9B ''entomb'':41B ''guarding'':19B ''him'':33B ''in'':34B,42B,46B ''jailor'':3A,6B ''lat'':40B ''legendary'':36B ''masters'':30B ''miraak'':22B,25B ''once'':12B ''plot'':27B ''priest'':10B ''rul'':13B ''s'':26B,44B ''solstheim'':14B,47B ''task'':17B ''the'':2A,5B,20B,29B ''tomb'':45B ''traitor'':21B ''uncovering'':24B ''vahlok'':1A,4B,31B,43B ''was'':7B,16B,39B ''who'':11B ''with'':18B', 'scholar, dragon, miraakcult', 'Vahlok the Jailor must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Solstheim. You really don''t know much more apart from that. You have a hunch he must of been being a jailor for someone important, but don''t know what.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ahzidal', 'Ahzidal, known as "the Embittered Destroyer," was a powerful Dragon Priest and the first great Nord enchanter. He was born in Saarthal and, after his home was destroyed by Elves, sought vengeance by mastering various magical disciplines, including Elven and Dwemer enchantments. He later became a high-ranking Dragon Priest, gaining power through dragon magic and Daedric knowledge. His obsession with power led to his eventual exile and servitude under Miraak. After Miraak''s defeat, Ahzidal was sealed in Kolbjorn Barrow with his powerful relics.', '''after'':25B,74B ''ahzidal'':1A,2B,78B ''and'':13B,24B,41B,58B,70B ''as'':4B ''barrow'':83B ''becam'':46B ''born'':21B ''by'':30B,34B ''daedric'':59B ''defeat'':77B ''destroy'':7B,29B ''disciplin'':38B ''dragon'':11B,51B,56B ''dwem'':42B ''elven'':40B ''elves'':31B ''embitter'':6B ''enchant'':18B ''enchantments'':43B ''eventual'':68B ''exil'':69B ''first'':15B ''gaining'':53B ''great'':16B ''high'':49B ''high-ranking'':48B ''his'':26B,61B,67B,85B ''hom'':27B ''in'':22B,81B ''including'':39B ''knowledg'':60B ''known'':3B ''kolbjorn'':82B ''lat'':45B ''led'':65B ''magic'':57B ''magical'':37B ''mastering'':35B ''miraak'':73B,75B ''nord'':17B ''obsession'':62B ''pow'':54B,64B ''powerful'':10B,86B ''priest'':12B,52B ''ranking'':50B ''relics'':87B ''s'':76B ''saarthal'':23B ''seal'':80B ''servitud'':71B ''sought'':32B ''the'':5B,14B ''through'':55B ''to'':66B ''under'':72B ''various'':36B ''vengeanc'':33B ''was'':8B,20B,28B,79B ''with'':63B,84B', 'scholar, dragon, miraakcult', 'Ahzidal must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Solstheim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dukaan', 'Dukaan is one of the high-ranking dragon priests in Solstheim. He was an aloof Dragon priest who did nothing of note during the Dragon war.', '''aloof'':17B ''an'':16B ''did'':21B ''dragon'':10B,18B,27B ''duk'':1A,2B ''during'':25B ''high'':8B ''high-ranking'':7B ''in'':12B ''is'':3B ''not'':24B ''nothing'':22B ''of'':5B,23B ''one'':4B ''priest'':19B ''priests'':11B ''ranking'':9B ''solstheim'':13B ''the'':6B,26B ''war'':28B ''was'':15B ''who'':20B', 'scholar, dragon, miraakcult', 'Dukaan must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Solstheim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('yffre', 'Y''ffre, also known as the Singer, the Storyteller, and the God of Song and Forest, is the central deity of the Bosmer pantheon, revered also by the Altmer, Bretons, and Snow Elves. Y''ffre played a critical role in the creation of the physical world during the Dawn Era, and is considered the first of the Ehlnofey to transform into an Earth Bone, establishing the laws of nature and life on Nirn. These laws are embodied in stories that Bosmer tribes strive to interpret, with Y''ffre''s teachings guiding the natural world and the cycle of life. Y''ffre''s influence extends to the natural world, where he sometimes intervenes to select key figures, such as the Silvenar, or sends wisps to herald the changing of seasons.

Y''ffre is deeply associated with stories and songs, shaping the world and its creatures through his music. His priests, known as Spinners, view life as an ongoing story and use narrative magic to influence others, altering their memories or even their physical forms. Y''ffre''s act of creation is considered a series of beautiful songs that caused the stars to dance and established the world''s laws, and his influence continues through his priests'' teachings. Spinners also weave new identities for individuals, using their magical abilities to alter someone''s appearance, such as giving them antlers as a mark of worthiness.', '''abiliti'':218B ''act'':178B ''also'':4B,27B,209B ''alter'':220B ''altering'':167B ''altmer'':30B ''an'':63B,157B ''and'':11B,16B,32B,52B,71B,96B,138B,143B,160B,194B,200B ''antlers'':228B ''appearanc'':223B ''are'':77B ''as'':6B,119B,152B,156B,225B,229B ''associat'':135B ''beautiful'':186B ''bon'':65B ''bosm'':24B,82B ''bretons'':31B ''by'':28B ''caus'':189B ''central'':20B ''changing'':128B ''consider'':54B,182B ''continu'':203B ''creation'':43B,180B ''creatur'':145B ''critical'':39B ''cycle'':98B ''danc'':193B ''dawn'':50B ''deeply'':134B ''deity'':21B ''during'':48B ''earth'':64B ''ehlnofey'':59B ''elves'':34B ''embodi'':78B ''establish'':195B ''establishing'':66B ''even'':171B ''extends'':105B ''ffre'':3B,36B,89B,102B,132B,176B ''figur'':117B ''first'':56B ''for'':213B ''forest'':17B ''forms'':174B ''giving'':226B ''god'':13B ''guiding'':92B ''herald'':126B ''his'':147B,149B,201B,205B ''identiti'':212B ''in'':41B,79B ''individuals'':214B ''influenc'':104B,165B,202B ''interpret'':86B ''interven'':113B ''into'':62B ''is'':18B,53B,133B,181B ''its'':144B ''key'':116B ''known'':5B,151B ''laws'':68B,76B,199B ''lif'':72B,100B,155B ''magic'':163B ''magical'':217B ''mark'':231B ''memori'':169B ''music'':148B ''narrativ'':162B ''natur'':70B ''natural'':94B,108B ''new'':211B ''nirn'':74B ''of'':14B,22B,44B,57B,69B,99B,129B,179B,185B,232B ''on'':73B ''ongoing'':158B ''or'':122B,170B ''others'':166B ''pantheon'':25B ''physical'':46B,173B ''play'':37B ''priests'':150B,206B ''rever'':26B ''rol'':40B ''s'':90B,103B,177B,198B,222B ''seasons'':130B ''select'':115B ''sends'':123B ''seri'':184B ''shaping'':140B ''silven'':121B ''sing'':8B ''snow'':33B ''someon'':221B ''sometim'':112B ''song'':15B ''songs'':139B,187B ''spinners'':153B,208B ''stars'':191B ''stori'':80B,137B ''story'':159B ''storytell'':10B ''striv'':84B ''such'':118B,224B ''teachings'':91B,207B ''that'':81B,188B ''the'':7B,9B,12B,19B,23B,29B,42B,45B,49B,55B,58B,67B,93B,97B,107B,120B,127B,141B,168B,172B,190B,196B,216B ''them'':227B ''thes'':75B ''through'':146B,204B ''to'':60B,85B,106B,114B,125B,164B,192B,219B ''transform'':61B ''trib'':83B ''use'':161B ''using'':215B ''view'':154B ''weav'':210B ''wher'':110B ''wisps'':124B ''with'':87B,136B ''world'':47B,95B,109B,142B,197B ''worthiness'':233B ''yffre'':1A', 'woodelf, scholar', '
Y''ffre, the God of Song and Forest, is the central deity of the Bosmer pantheon and played a crucial role in the creation of the world, establishing the laws of nature through stories and songs. His influence extends through his priests, the Spinners, who use narrative magic to shape life and the physical world. Y''ffre''s teachings guide the natural world, and his power is felt in the changing seasons and in his selection of key figures like the Silvenar. Spinners also have the ability to alter identities, symbolizing Y''ffre’s continued influence over the Bosmer and beyond.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('zen', '
Z''en, also known as Xen in Altmeri folklore, is a God of Toil, vengeance, agriculture, and payment, worshipped by the Bosmer. His influence extends beyond crops and cattle, as he is believed to embody a higher cosmic order, guiding balance and the resolution of conflicts. Z''en’s worship is closely tied to vengeance and toil, and some Bosmer wear a special cap to signify devotion to these aspects, even renouncing love while wearing it. Z''en’s origins are believed to trace back to both Akaviri and Argonian cultures, with the Kothringi initially venerating him as their chief deity. His mythology is intertwined with that of Zenithar, the Imperial god of commerce, who shares many aspects with Z''en.

Historically, Z''en’s shrines were widespread across Valenwood until the Knahaten Flu decimated his followers, a disaster attributed to the influence of Argonian Shadowscales. By 2E 582, the last of his dedicated followers, a Bosmer clan in the Bloodtoil Valley, were embroiled in a conflict with the Drublog Clan of Wood Orcs. Z''en sent his emissary to intervene when the Bosmer threatened to unleash a curse upon their enemies, though the outcome remains uncertain. ', '''2e'':149B ''582'':150B ''across'':130B ''agricultur'':17B ''akaviri'':89B ''also'':4B ''altmeri'':9B ''and'':18B,29B,43B,57B,59B,90B ''are'':82B ''argoni'':91B,146B ''as'':6B,31B,99B ''aspects'':71B,119B ''attribut'':141B ''back'':86B ''balanc'':42B ''believ'':34B,83B ''beyond'':27B ''bloodtoil'':162B ''bosm'':23B,61B,158B,185B ''both'':88B ''by'':21B,148B ''cap'':65B ''cattl'':30B ''chief'':101B ''clan'':159B,172B ''closely'':53B ''commerc'':115B ''conflict'':168B ''conflicts'':47B ''cosmic'':39B ''crops'':28B ''cultur'':92B ''curs'':190B ''decimat'':136B ''dedicat'':155B ''deity'':102B ''devotion'':68B ''disast'':140B ''drublog'':171B ''embody'':36B ''embroil'':165B ''emissary'':180B ''enemi'':193B ''even'':72B ''extends'':26B ''flu'':135B ''folklor'':10B ''followers'':138B,156B ''god'':13B,113B ''guiding'':41B ''high'':38B ''him'':98B ''his'':24B,103B,137B,154B,179B ''historically'':123B ''imperial'':112B ''in'':8B,160B,166B ''influenc'':25B,144B ''initially'':96B ''intertwin'':106B ''interven'':182B ''is'':11B,33B,52B,105B ''it'':77B ''knahat'':134B ''known'':5B ''kothringi'':95B ''last'':152B ''lov'':74B ''many'':118B ''mythology'':104B ''of'':14B,46B,109B,114B,145B,153B,173B ''orcs'':175B ''order'':40B ''origins'':81B ''outcom'':196B ''payment'':19B ''remains'':197B ''renouncing'':73B ''resolution'':45B ''s'':50B,80B,126B ''sent'':178B ''shadowscal'':147B ''shar'':117B ''shrin'':127B ''signify'':67B ''som'':60B ''special'':64B ''that'':108B ''the'':22B,44B,94B,100B,111B,133B,143B,151B,161B,170B,184B,192B,195B ''thes'':70B ''though'':194B ''threaten'':186B ''tied'':54B ''to'':35B,55B,66B,69B,84B,87B,142B,181B,187B ''toil'':15B,58B ''trac'':85B ''uncertain'':198B ''unleash'':188B ''until'':132B ''upon'':191B ''valenwood'':131B ''valley'':163B ''venerating'':97B ''vengeanc'':16B,56B ''wear'':62B ''wearing'':76B ''wer'':128B,164B ''when'':183B ''whil'':75B ''who'':116B ''widespr'':129B ''with'':93B,107B,120B,169B ''wood'':174B ''worship'':51B ''worshipp'':20B ''xen'':7B ''z'':2B,48B,78B,121B,124B,176B ''zen'':1A ''zenith'':110B', 'woodelf, scholar', '
Z''en is a god worshipped by the Bosmer, associated with toil, vengeance, agriculture, and cosmic balance. His influence extends beyond crops, guiding the resolution of conflicts, and his worship includes symbols like a cap worn by devotees to signify renunciation of love and devotion to vengeance. ', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('baan_dar', 'Baan Dar, known as the Bandit God, the Pariah, or the Man of a Thousand Faces, is a trickster spirit worshipped primarily by the Khajiit of Elsweyr, but also influential in places like Valenwood. He embodies the cleverness and desperate genius of the Khajiit, helping them outplay their oppressors and outwit others. His domain, the Five Fingers Dance, symbolizes his ability to shape lives and lands for the better, often through unconventional means. His name is widely used, particularly by thieves and criminals who take on the persona of Baan Dar to mask their identity or seek inspiration. To the Khajiit, Baan Dar represents defiance against oppression, while to other races, such as the Bretons, he is associated with sneaky thieves and living legends.

Baan Dar’s influence extends beyond his Khajiiti followers. In Valenwood, he is viewed as a god of archery, while to the Bretons, he is known as the Bandit and revered by the Thieves Guild in the Iliac Bay. His name is even used by the Baandari Pedlars, a traveling merchant tribe. In addition, Baan Dar is commemorated by the Khajiit and Bosmer at the ruins of Thormar, where they participate in the "Boast," a festival of pranks between the two races. Despite the varying interpretations of his nature across cultures, Baan Dar remains a symbol of defiance, resourcefulness, and the clever trickster spirit that shapes the world around him.', '''ability'':63B ''across'':216B ''addition'':180B ''against'':108B ''also'':31B ''and'':41B,52B,67B,84B,124B,156B,188B,226B ''archery'':145B ''around'':235B ''as'':6B,115B,141B,153B ''associat'':120B ''at'':190B ''baan'':1A,3B,92B,104B,127B,181B,218B ''baandari'':173B ''bandit'':8B,155B ''bay'':165B ''bett'':71B ''betw'':205B ''beyond'':132B ''boast'':200B ''bosm'':189B ''bretons'':117B,149B ''but'':30B ''by'':25B,82B,158B,171B,185B ''clev'':228B ''cleverness'':40B ''commemorat'':184B ''criminals'':85B ''cultur'':217B ''danc'':60B ''dar'':2A,4B,93B,105B,128B,182B,219B ''defianc'':107B,224B ''desperat'':42B ''despit'':209B ''domain'':56B ''elsweyr'':29B ''embodi'':38B ''even'':169B ''extends'':131B ''fac'':18B ''festival'':202B ''fingers'':59B ''fiv'':58B ''followers'':135B ''for'':69B ''genius'':43B ''god'':9B,143B ''guild'':161B ''helping'':47B ''him'':236B ''his'':55B,62B,76B,133B,166B,214B ''identity'':97B ''iliac'':164B ''in'':33B,136B,162B,179B,198B ''influenc'':130B ''influential'':32B ''inspiration'':100B ''interpretations'':212B ''is'':19B,78B,119B,139B,151B,168B,183B ''khajiit'':27B,46B,103B,187B ''khajiiti'':134B ''known'':5B,152B ''lands'':68B ''legends'':126B ''lik'':35B ''liv'':66B ''living'':125B ''man'':14B ''mask'':95B ''means'':75B ''merchant'':177B ''nam'':77B,167B ''natur'':215B ''of'':15B,28B,44B,91B,144B,193B,203B,213B,223B ''often'':72B ''on'':88B ''oppression'':109B ''oppressors'':51B ''or'':12B,98B ''other'':112B ''others'':54B ''outplay'':49B ''outwit'':53B ''pariah'':11B ''participat'':197B ''particularly'':81B ''pedlars'':174B ''person'':90B ''plac'':34B ''pranks'':204B ''primarily'':24B ''rac'':113B,208B ''remains'':220B ''represents'':106B ''resourcefulness'':225B ''rever'':157B ''ruins'':192B ''s'':129B ''seek'':99B ''shap'':65B,232B ''sneaky'':122B ''spirit'':22B,230B ''such'':114B ''symbol'':222B ''symboliz'':61B ''tak'':87B ''that'':231B ''the'':7B,10B,13B,26B,39B,45B,50B,57B,70B,89B,96B,102B,116B,148B,154B,159B,163B,172B,186B,191B,199B,206B,210B,227B,233B ''them'':48B ''they'':196B ''thiev'':83B,123B,160B ''thorm'':194B ''thousand'':17B ''through'':73B ''to'':64B,94B,101B,111B,147B ''traveling'':176B ''trib'':178B ''trickst'':21B,229B ''two'':207B ''unconventional'':74B ''used'':80B,170B ''valenwood'':36B,137B ''varying'':211B ''view'':140B ''wher'':195B ''whil'':110B,146B ''who'':86B ''widely'':79B ''with'':121B ''world'':234B ''worshipp'':23B', 'woodelf, khajiit, scholar', '
Baan Dar, the Bandit God or Man of a Thousand Faces, is a trickster spirit worshipped by the Khajiit of Elsweyr and influential in Valenwood. He embodies cleverness and defiance, helping the Khajiit outwit their oppressors. His domain, the Five Fingers Dance, symbolizes his power to shape lives and lands through unconventional means. ', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sithis', '
Sithis, also known as the Dread Father, is a primordial representation of chaos and change, often linked with the Dark Brotherhood and associated with serpent-like imagery. Although not classified as Aedric or Daedric, he is viewed as the personification of the Void and the primordial force of destruction and creation. Sithis plays a critical role in various Tamrielic mythologies, including the creation of the world, the intersection of Anuiel and Padomay, and the origin of Lorkhan. To the Dark Brotherhood, Sithis is a central figure, with followers believing that the souls of those killed in his name are sent to the Void after death. Sithis’ influence is depicted in multiple ways, from his presence in the creation of Aurbis to his embodiment of the ongoing forces of stasis and change.

The worship of Sithis is often secretive and tied to assassin guilds, notably the Dark Brotherhood and Morag Tong. These organizations act as intermediaries for Sithis, with the Dark Brotherhood following rituals, such as the Rite of Penance, and the Morag Tong committing sanctioned political assassinations. The Dark Brotherhood’s worship is macabre and ritualistic, involving effigies and gruesome symbols, with members believing that traitors are claimed by the Wrath of Sithis and dragged to the Void. In contrast, the Morag Tong views assassination as a ceremonial reenactment of the original murder of Nir, focusing less on bloodshed and more on the celebration of life. Despite the differences in practices, both guilds revere Sithis as the source of ultimate power and divine vengeance.', '''act'':155B ''aedric'':34B ''after'':106B ''also'':3B ''although'':30B ''and'':15B,23B,46B,52B,73B,75B,132B,141B,150B,172B,187B,191B,206B,232B,254B ''anuiel'':72B ''are'':101B,199B ''as'':5B,33B,40B,156B,167B,218B,248B ''assassin'':144B ''assassination'':217B ''assassinations'':179B ''associat'':24B ''aurbis'':122B ''believing'':91B,196B ''bloodsh'':231B ''both'':244B ''brotherhood'':22B,83B,149B,163B,182B ''by'':201B ''celebration'':236B ''central'':87B ''ceremonial'':220B ''cha'':14B ''chang'':16B,133B ''claim'':200B ''classifi'':32B ''committing'':176B ''contrast'':212B ''creation'':53B,65B,120B ''critical'':57B ''daedric'':36B ''dark'':21B,82B,148B,162B,181B ''death'':107B ''depict'':111B ''despit'':239B ''destruction'':51B ''differenc'':241B ''divin'':255B ''dragg'':207B ''dre'':7B ''effigi'':190B ''embodiment'':125B ''fath'':8B ''figur'':88B ''focusing'':228B ''followers'':90B ''following'':164B ''for'':158B ''forc'':49B,129B ''from'':115B ''gruesom'':192B ''guilds'':145B,245B ''his'':99B,116B,124B ''imagery'':29B ''in'':59B,98B,112B,118B,211B,242B ''including'':63B ''influenc'':109B ''intermediari'':157B ''intersection'':70B ''involving'':189B ''is'':9B,38B,85B,110B,138B,185B ''kill'':97B ''known'':4B ''less'':229B ''lif'':238B ''lik'':28B ''link'':18B ''lorkh'':79B ''macabr'':186B ''members'':195B ''mor'':233B ''morag'':151B,174B,214B ''multipl'':113B ''murd'':225B ''mythologi'':62B ''nam'':100B ''nir'':227B ''not'':31B ''notably'':146B ''of'':13B,43B,50B,66B,71B,78B,95B,121B,126B,130B,136B,170B,204B,222B,226B,237B,251B ''often'':17B,139B ''on'':230B,234B ''ongoing'':128B ''or'':35B ''organizations'':154B ''origin'':77B ''original'':224B ''padomay'':74B ''penanc'':171B ''personification'':42B ''plays'':55B ''political'':178B ''pow'':253B ''practic'':243B ''presenc'':117B ''primordial'':11B,48B ''reenactment'':221B ''representation'':12B ''rever'':246B ''rit'':169B ''ritualistic'':188B ''rituals'':165B ''rol'':58B ''s'':183B ''sanction'':177B ''secretiv'':140B ''sent'':102B ''serpent'':27B ''serpent-lik'':26B ''sithis'':1A,2B,54B,84B,108B,137B,159B,205B,247B ''souls'':94B ''sourc'':250B ''stasis'':131B ''such'':166B ''symbols'':193B ''tamrielic'':61B ''that'':92B,197B ''the'':6B,20B,41B,44B,47B,64B,67B,69B,76B,81B,93B,104B,119B,127B,134B,147B,161B,168B,173B,180B,202B,209B,213B,223B,235B,240B,249B ''thes'':153B ''thos'':96B ''tied'':142B ''to'':80B,103B,123B,143B,208B ''tong'':152B,175B,215B ''traitors'':198B ''ultimat'':252B ''various'':60B ''vengeanc'':256B ''view'':39B ''views'':216B ''void'':45B,105B,210B ''ways'':114B ''with'':19B,25B,89B,160B,194B ''world'':68B ''worship'':135B,184B ''wrath'':203B', 'darkbrotherhood, daedra, scholar', '
Sithis is a primordial force of chaos and change, worshiped mainly by the Dark Brotherhood, who believe that the souls of those killed in his name are sent to the Void. He is the personification of the Void and plays a key role in creation myths, including the birth of the world and Lorkhan. ', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fur_helmet', 'Fur Helmet has basic protection quality. Its visual design is crude and practical, crafted from animal pelts with fur-lined edges. It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''and'':14B ''animal'':18B ''at'':32B ''basic'':6B ''be'':27B ''by'':29B ''can'':26B ''craft'':16B ''crud'':13B ''design'':11B ''edges'':24B ''from'':17B ''fur'':1A,3B,22B ''fur-lin'':21B ''helmet'':2A,4B ''is'':12B ''it'':25B ''its'':9B ''leath'':31B ''lin'':23B ''pelts'':19B ''practical'':15B ''protection'':7B ''quality'':8B ''tempered/improved'':28B ''using'':30B ''visual'':10B ''with'':20B ''workbench'':34B', 'blacksmith', 'Fur Helmet has basic protection quality. Its visual design is crude and practical, crafted from animal pelts with fur-lined edges. It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('all-maker', 'The All-Maker, also known as the All-Father, is an ancient and mysterious deity revered by the Skaal of Solstheim, representing the wellspring of creation. It is believed that the All-Maker resides in the spirit world, where the souls of the dead return to be shaped into new life. This eternal cycle is seen as a flow of life from and back to the All-Maker, with death marking the next phase in the journey. The Skaal view life as a sacred gift from the All-Maker, with harmony and respect for nature being central to their practices. They believe the All-Maker blesses them with power when they live in balance with their surroundings, and the six All-Maker Stones are seen as conduits through which the All-Maker’s power flows into the world.

The Skaal believe that their harmony with the land is crucial to pleasing the All-Maker, and they practice rituals like the Ristaag and the Ritual of the Gifts to demonstrate their gratitude. The All-Maker is also opposed by the Adversary, a force that seeks to corrupt the All-Maker’s dominion. In some traditions, the All-Maker is speculated to have connections with other deities, such as Alduin or Sithis, though these relationships remain mysterious. The All-Maker''s teachings emphasize the sanctity of life, the importance of preserving balance, and the rejection of greed, while also warning of the consequences of disrupting the natural order.', '''adversary'':193B ''alduin'':223B ''all'':2A,6B,13B,38B,74B,96B,113B,131B,142B,165B,186B,202B,211B,233B ''all-fath'':12B ''all-mak'':1A,5B,37B,73B,95B,112B,130B,141B,164B,185B,201B,210B,232B ''also'':8B,189B,253B ''an'':16B ''ancient'':17B ''and'':18B,69B,100B,127B,167B,174B,247B ''are'':134B ''as'':10B,63B,89B,136B,222B ''back'':70B ''balanc'':123B,246B ''be'':53B ''being'':104B ''believ'':34B,110B,152B ''bless'':115B ''by'':22B,191B ''central'':105B ''conduits'':137B ''connections'':217B ''consequenc'':257B ''corrupt'':199B ''creation'':31B ''crucial'':160B ''cycle'':60B ''dead'':50B ''death'':77B ''deiti'':220B ''deity'':20B ''demonstrat'':181B ''disrupting'':259B ''dominion'':205B ''emphasiz'':237B ''eternal'':59B ''fath'':14B ''flow'':65B ''flows'':146B ''for'':102B ''forc'':195B ''from'':68B,93B ''gift'':92B ''gifts'':179B ''gratitud'':183B ''gre'':251B ''harmony'':99B,155B ''hav'':216B ''importanc'':243B ''in'':41B,82B,122B,206B ''into'':55B,147B ''is'':15B,33B,61B,159B,188B,213B ''it'':32B ''journey'':84B ''known'':9B ''land'':158B ''lif'':57B,67B,88B,241B ''lik'':171B ''liv'':121B ''mak'':3A,7B,39B,75B,97B,114B,132B,143B,166B,187B,203B,212B,234B ''marking'':78B ''mysterious'':19B,230B ''natur'':103B ''natural'':261B ''new'':56B ''next'':80B ''of'':25B,30B,48B,66B,177B,240B,244B,250B,255B,258B ''oppos'':190B ''or'