INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('azura_star', 'Azura''s Star is a legendary Daedric artifact linked to the Daedric Prince Azura. It functions as a reusable grand soul gem, capable of storing souls without being consumed like ordinary soul gems. This makes it an invaluable tool for enchanters and adventurers alike, as it can be used repeatedly to recharge weapons or enchant items. ', '''adventurers'':45B ''alik'':46B ''an'':39B ''and'':44B ''artifact'':10B ''as'':19B,47B ''azur'':1A,3B,16B ''be'':50B ''being'':30B ''can'':49B ''capabl'':25B ''consum'':31B ''daedric'':9B,14B ''enchant'':57B ''enchanters'':43B ''for'':42B ''functions'':18B ''gem'':24B ''gems'':35B ''grand'':22B ''invalu'':40B ''is'':6B ''it'':17B,38B,48B ''items'':58B ''legendary'':8B ''lik'':32B ''link'':11B ''mak'':37B ''of'':26B ''or'':56B ''ordinary'':33B ''princ'':15B ''recharg'':54B ''repeatedly'':52B ''reusabl'':21B ''s'':4B ''soul'':23B,34B ''souls'':28B ''star'':2A,5B ''storing'':27B ''the'':13B ''this'':36B ''to'':12B,53B ''tool'':41B ''used'':51B ''weapons'':55B ''without'':29B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', '
Azura''s Star is a powerful Daedric artifact that is thought to act like a soul gem.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ebony_mail', 'The Ebony Mail is a legendary Daedric artifact created by Boethiah, the Daedric Prince of deceit, treachery, and conspiracy. This enchanted ebony armor, typically a cuirass, grants its wearer resistance to fire, magical attacks, and physical blows while enabling stealthy movements and the ability to poison enemies upon close contact. Forged from the blood of Lorkhan after his heart was cast into the sea, the Ebony Mail embodies Boethiah’s cunning and deadly nature. Only individuals chosen by Boethiah can wield the artifact, as the Prince determines both its owner and duration of ownership.', '''ability'':46B ''after'':59B ''and'':20B,37B,44B,74B,93B ''armor'':25B ''artifact'':10B,85B ''as'':86B ''attacks'':36B ''blood'':56B ''blows'':39B ''boethiah'':13B,71B,81B ''both'':90B ''by'':12B,80B ''can'':82B ''cast'':63B ''chos'':79B ''clos'':51B ''conspiracy'':21B ''contact'':52B ''creat'':11B ''cuirass'':28B ''cunning'':73B ''daedric'':9B,15B ''deadly'':75B ''deceit'':18B ''determin'':89B ''duration'':94B ''ebony'':1A,4B,24B,68B ''embodi'':70B ''enabling'':41B ''enchant'':23B ''enemi'':49B ''fir'':34B ''forg'':53B ''from'':54B ''grants'':29B ''heart'':61B ''his'':60B ''individuals'':78B ''into'':64B ''is'':6B ''its'':30B,91B ''legendary'':8B ''lorkh'':58B ''magical'':35B ''mail'':2A,5B,69B ''movements'':43B ''natur'':76B ''of'':17B,57B,95B ''only'':77B ''owner'':92B ''ownership'':96B ''physical'':38B ''poison'':48B ''princ'':16B,88B ''resistanc'':32B ''s'':72B ''stealthy'':42B ''the'':3B,14B,45B,55B,65B,67B,84B,87B ''this'':22B ''to'':33B,47B ''treachery'':19B ''typically'':26B ''upon'':50B ''was'':62B ''wear'':31B ''whil'':40B ''wield'':83B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', '
The Ebony Mail is a powerful Daedric artifact created by Boethiah thought to  grant its wearer extra powers.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rueful_axe', 'The Rueful Axe is a Daedric artifact forged by Clavicus Vile, the Prince of bargains and twisted desires, as the result of a grim pact. This massive iron-like battleaxe, adorned with engravings of werewolves but crafted from ebony, carries a powerful enchantment that saps the strength of those it strikes and is particularly effective against beasts. The axe is a testament to Clavicus Vile''s propensity for granting wishes in ways that bring misery, as its creation embodies the consequences of dark bargains.', '''adorn'':34B ''against'':59B ''and'':18B,55B ''artifact'':9B ''as'':21B,79B ''axe'':2A,5B,62B ''bargains'':17B,87B ''battleax'':33B ''beasts'':60B ''bring'':77B ''but'':39B ''by'':11B ''carri'':43B ''clavicus'':12B,67B ''consequenc'':84B ''craft'':40B ''creation'':81B ''daedric'':8B ''dark'':86B ''desir'':20B ''ebony'':42B ''effectiv'':58B ''embodi'':82B ''enchantment'':46B ''engravings'':36B ''for'':71B ''forg'':10B ''from'':41B ''granting'':72B ''grim'':26B ''in'':74B ''iron'':31B ''iron-lik'':30B ''is'':6B,56B,63B ''it'':53B ''its'':80B ''lik'':32B ''massiv'':29B ''misery'':78B ''of'':16B,24B,37B,51B,85B ''pact'':27B ''particularly'':57B ''powerful'':45B ''princ'':15B ''propensity'':70B ''result'':23B ''rueful'':1A,4B ''s'':69B ''saps'':48B ''strength'':50B ''strik'':54B ''testament'':65B ''that'':47B,76B ''the'':3B,14B,22B,49B,61B,83B ''this'':28B ''thos'':52B ''to'':66B ''twist'':19B ''vil'':13B,68B ''ways'':75B ''werewolv'':38B ''wish'':73B ''with'':35B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', '
The Rueful Axe is a Daedric artifact created by Clavicus Vile,thought ot be enchanted .', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('masque_of_clavicus_vile', 'The Masque of Clavicus Vile is a Daedric artifact associated with Clavicus Vile, the Daedric Prince of wishes and bargains. This helm enhances the wearer''s charm and popularity, making them seem more trustworthy and likable to those around them. However, like many Daedric artifacts, the Masque remains under Clavicus Vile''s control and can be recalled by him at any time.

One of the most famous stories surrounding the Masque involves a noblewoman named Avalea. After being disfigured by a servant, Avalea made a pact with Clavicus Vile, receiving the Masque in exchange. Though her appearance remained unchanged, the Masque granted her admiration and respect. She eventually married a powerful baron, but a year and a day later, Clavicus Vile reclaimed the Masque. Pregnant with the baron''s child, Avalea was banished, and years later, her daughter exacted vengeance by killing the baron. This tale highlights the unpredictable and often cruel nature of bargains with Clavicus Vile.', '''admiration'':108B ''after'':81B ''and'':23B,32B,39B,58B,109B,120B,138B,154B ''any'':65B ''appearanc'':101B ''around'':43B ''artifact'':13B ''artifacts'':49B ''associat'':14B ''at'':64B ''avale'':80B,87B,135B ''banish'':137B ''bargains'':24B,159B ''baron'':116B,132B,148B ''be'':60B ''being'':82B ''but'':117B ''by'':62B,84B,145B ''can'':59B ''charm'':31B ''child'':134B ''clavicus'':3A,8B,16B,54B,92B,124B,161B ''control'':57B ''cruel'':156B ''daedric'':12B,19B,48B ''daught'':142B ''day'':122B ''disfigur'':83B ''enhanc'':27B ''eventually'':112B ''exact'':143B ''exchang'':98B ''famous'':71B ''grant'':106B ''helm'':26B ''her'':100B,107B,141B ''highlights'':151B ''him'':63B ''howev'':45B ''in'':97B ''involv'':76B ''is'':10B ''killing'':146B ''lat'':123B,140B ''lik'':46B ''likabl'':40B ''mad'':88B ''making'':34B ''many'':47B ''marri'':113B ''masqu'':1A,6B,51B,75B,96B,105B,128B ''mor'':37B ''most'':70B ''nam'':79B ''natur'':157B ''noblewom'':78B ''of'':2A,7B,21B,68B,158B ''often'':155B ''one'':67B ''pact'':90B ''popularity'':33B ''powerful'':115B ''pregnant'':129B ''princ'':20B ''recall'':61B ''receiving'':94B ''reclaim'':126B ''remain'':102B ''remains'':52B ''respect'':110B ''s'':30B,56B,133B ''seem'':36B ''servant'':86B ''she'':111B ''stori'':72B ''surrounding'':73B ''tal'':150B ''the'':5B,18B,28B,50B,69B,74B,95B,104B,127B,131B,147B,152B ''them'':35B,44B ''this'':25B,149B ''thos'':42B ''though'':99B ''tim'':66B ''to'':41B ''trustworthy'':38B ''unchang'':103B ''under'':53B ''unpredict'':153B ''vengeanc'':144B ''vil'':4A,9B,17B,55B,93B,125B,162B ''was'':136B ''wear'':29B ''wish'':22B ''with'':15B,91B,130B,160B ''year'':119B ''years'':139B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', 'The Masque of Clavicus Vile is a Daedric artifact that is thought to make the wearer irresistable.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fur_bracers', 'Fur Bracers have basic protection quality. Their visual design is minimal, with strips of fur and leather bound for light coverage. They can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''and'':18B ''at'':36B ''basic'':6B ''be'':27B,31B ''bound'':20B ''bracers'':2A,4B ''by'':33B ''can'':25B,30B ''coverag'':23B ''craft'':28B ''design'':11B ''for'':21B ''fur'':1A,3B,17B ''hav'':5B ''is'':12B ''it'':29B ''leath'':19B,35B ''light'':22B ''minimal'':13B ''not'':26B ''of'':16B ''protection'':7B ''quality'':8B ''strips'':15B ''tempered/improved'':32B ''the'':9B ''they'':24B ''using'':34B ''visual'':10B ''with'':14B ''workbench'':38B', 'blacksmith', 'Fur Bracers have basic protection quality. Their visual design is minimal, with strips of fur and leather bound for light coverage. They can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('oghma_infinium', 'The Oghma Infinium is an ancient and powerful artifact, also known as the Tome of Power or the Book that Knows. Written by Xarxes, the scribe of the god Auri-El, the knowledge within was granted to him by the Daedric Prince Hermaeus Mora. The tome’s name derives from Oghma, a figure Xarxes created from his most cherished moments in history. This artifact contains vast, arcane knowledge that can bestow near-demi-god powers upon its reader.', '''also'':12B ''an'':7B ''ancient'':8B ''and'':9B ''arcan'':70B ''artifact'':11B,67B ''as'':14B ''auri'':33B ''auri-el'':32B ''bestow'':74B ''book'':21B ''by'':25B,42B ''can'':73B ''cherish'':62B ''contains'':68B ''creat'':58B ''daedric'':44B ''demi'':77B ''deriv'':52B ''figur'':56B ''from'':53B,59B ''god'':31B,78B ''grant'':39B ''hermaeus'':46B ''him'':41B ''his'':60B ''history'':65B ''in'':64B ''infinium'':2A,5B ''is'':6B ''its'':81B ''knowledg'':36B,71B ''known'':13B ''knows'':23B ''moments'':63B ''mor'':47B ''most'':61B ''nam'':51B ''near'':76B ''near-demi-god'':75B ''of'':17B,29B ''oghma'':1A,4B,54B ''or'':19B ''pow'':18B ''powerful'':10B ''powers'':79B ''princ'':45B ''read'':82B ''s'':50B ''scrib'':28B ''that'':22B,72B ''the'':3B,15B,20B,27B,30B,35B,43B,48B ''this'':66B ''to'':40B ''tom'':16B,49B ''upon'':80B ''vast'':69B ''was'':38B ''within'':37B ''writt'':24B ''xarx'':26B,57B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', 'The Oghma Infinium, also called the Tome of Power, is an ancient artifact . It is thought to bestow near-demi-god powers on its reader.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('saviors_hide', 'Savior''s Hide, also known as Hircine''s Hide or the Scourge of the Oathbreaker, is a Daedric artifact associated primarily with the Daedric Prince Hircine. It was originally part of a full set of armor, but over time, the term has come to refer only to the cuirass, as the rest of the set has not been seen since the Third Era. The cuirass is known for granting the wearer resistance to magic, making it a prized item for those facing powerful sorcerers or hostile enchantments.

There are multiple origins for the Hide. One popular version claims Hircine himself gifted the Hide to the first mortal to escape his Hunting Grounds, who then fashioned it into armor. Another tale suggests that Hircine sewed the armor from the hide of a werewolf. A lesser-known tradition credits Malacath, though this version mistakenly claims the Hide made its wearer vulnerable to magic. Despite these differences, all stories agree that the Hide offers protection against the blows of oathbreakers and the Spear of Bitter Mercy.', '''against'':166B ''agre'':160B ''all'':158B ''also'':6B ''and'':171B ''anoth'':121B ''are'':91B ''armor'':38B,120B,128B ''artifact'':21B ''as'':8B,52B ''associat'':22B ''been'':60B ''bitt'':175B ''blows'':168B ''but'':39B ''claims'':100B,146B ''com'':45B ''credits'':140B ''cuirass'':51B,67B ''daedric'':20B,26B ''despit'':155B ''differenc'':157B ''enchantments'':89B ''escap'':111B ''facing'':84B ''fashion'':117B ''first'':108B ''for'':70B,82B,94B ''from'':129B ''full'':35B ''gift'':103B ''granting'':71B ''grounds'':114B ''hid'':2A,5B,11B,96B,105B,131B,148B,163B ''himself'':102B ''hircin'':9B,28B,101B,125B ''his'':112B ''hostil'':88B ''hunting'':113B ''into'':119B ''is'':18B,68B ''it'':29B,78B,118B ''item'':81B ''its'':150B ''known'':7B,69B,138B ''less'':137B ''lesser-known'':136B ''mad'':149B ''magic'':76B,154B ''making'':77B ''malacath'':141B ''mercy'':176B ''mistakenly'':145B ''mortal'':109B ''multipl'':92B ''not'':59B ''oathbreak'':17B ''oathbreakers'':170B ''of'':15B,33B,37B,55B,132B,169B,174B ''offers'':164B ''one'':97B ''only'':48B ''or'':12B,87B ''originally'':31B ''origins'':93B ''over'':40B ''part'':32B ''popul'':98B ''powerful'':85B ''primarily'':23B ''princ'':27B ''priz'':80B ''protection'':165B ''ref'':47B ''resistanc'':74B ''rest'':54B ''s'':4B,10B ''savior'':3B ''saviors'':1A ''scourg'':14B ''seen'':61B ''set'':36B,57B ''sew'':126B ''sinc'':62B ''sorcerers'':86B ''spe'':173B ''stori'':159B ''suggests'':123B ''tal'':122B ''term'':43B ''that'':124B,161B ''the'':13B,16B,25B,42B,50B,53B,56B,63B,66B,72B,95B,104B,107B,127B,130B,147B,162B,167B,172B ''then'':116B ''ther'':90B ''thes'':156B ''third'':64B ''this'':143B ''thos'':83B ''though'':142B ''tim'':41B ''to'':46B,49B,75B,106B,110B,153B ''tradition'':139B ''version'':99B,144B ''vulner'':152B ''was'':30B ''wear'':73B,151B ''werewolf'':134B ''who'':115B ''with'':24B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar, werewolf, hunter', 'Savior''s Hide, is a Daedric artifact linked to Hircine. It is a cuirass that is thought to protect against powerful sorcerers and enchantments. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ring_of_hircine', 'The Ring of Hircine is a powerful Daedric artifact created by Hircine, the Daedric Prince of the Hunt. Typically depicted as an engraved ring adorned with the image of a wolf''s head, the ring grants control over the wearer''s lycanthropy, allowing them to transform into a werewolf at will, bypassing the usual restrictions of the moon and bloodlust. For non-lycanthropes, the ring''s effects are usually dormant, though it has been known to extend life or induce werewolf transformations. However, Hircine can curse the ring, causing unpredictable transformations for those who have not earned it.', '''adorn'':28B ''allowing'':46B ''an'':25B ''and'':62B ''are'':72B ''artifact'':12B ''as'':24B ''at'':53B ''been'':78B ''bloodlust'':63B ''by'':14B ''bypassing'':55B ''can'':89B ''causing'':93B ''control'':40B ''creat'':13B ''curs'':90B ''daedric'':11B,17B ''depict'':23B ''dormant'':74B ''earn'':101B ''effects'':71B ''engrav'':26B ''extend'':81B ''for'':64B,96B ''grants'':39B ''hav'':99B ''head'':36B ''hircin'':3A,7B,15B,88B ''howev'':87B ''hunt'':21B ''imag'':31B ''induc'':84B ''into'':50B ''is'':8B ''it'':76B,102B ''known'':79B ''lif'':82B ''lycanthrop'':67B ''lycanthropy'':45B ''moon'':61B ''non'':66B ''non-lycanthrop'':65B ''not'':100B ''of'':2A,6B,19B,32B,59B ''or'':83B ''over'':41B ''powerful'':10B ''princ'':18B ''restrictions'':58B ''ring'':1A,5B,27B,38B,69B,92B ''s'':35B,44B,70B ''the'':4B,16B,20B,30B,37B,42B,56B,60B,68B,91B ''them'':47B ''thos'':97B ''though'':75B ''to'':48B,80B ''transform'':49B ''transformations'':86B,95B ''typically'':22B ''unpredict'':94B ''usual'':57B ''usually'':73B ''wear'':43B ''werewolf'':52B,85B ''who'':98B ''will'':54B ''with'':29B ''wolf'':34B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar, werewolf, hunter', 'The Ring of Hircine is a Daedric artifact created by Hircine, the Daedric Prince of the Hunt. Itis rumoured to allow the wearer to transform into a werewolf.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('voldenrung', 'Volendrung, also known as the Hammer of Might, is a legendary artifact originally crafted by the Rourken clan of the Dwemer. This massive warhammer, made of Dwarven metal, was not only a formidable weapon but also a symbol of the clan''s honor. When the Rourken refused to join the First Council with other Dwemer clans, their chieftain hurled Volendrung across Tamriel, declaring that the clan would settle wherever the hammer landed. It came to rest in what is now known as Hammerfell, a name derived from the Rourken’s journey and the hammer itself.

Despite its Dwemer origins, Volendrung eventually became associated with the Daedric Prince Malacath, one of the Dwemer''s greatest enemies. How it transitioned into a Daedric artifact is unclear, though some speculate that Malacath claimed it as a way to mock Dwemer craftsmanship or to wield one of their prized creations against them. Volendrung is known for its immense destructive power, able to demolish walls with ease and sap the strength of those it strikes, transferring that power to its wielder. Over time, the hammer has disappeared and resurfaced at various points in history, much like the Dwemer themselves.', '''able'':158B ''across'':62B ''against'':148B ''also'':3B,37B ''and'':93B,164B,184B ''artifact'':13B,123B ''as'':5B,83B,133B ''associat'':104B ''at'':186B ''becam'':103B ''but'':36B ''by'':16B ''cam'':75B ''chieftain'':59B ''claim'':131B ''clan'':19B,42B,67B ''clans'':57B ''council'':53B ''craft'':15B ''craftsmanship'':139B ''creations'':147B ''daedric'':107B,122B ''declaring'':64B ''demolish'':160B ''deriv'':87B ''despit'':97B ''destructiv'':156B ''disappear'':183B ''dwarv'':28B ''dwem'':22B,56B,99B,113B,138B,194B ''eas'':163B ''enemi'':116B ''eventually'':102B ''first'':52B ''for'':153B ''formid'':34B ''from'':88B ''greatest'':115B ''hamm'':7B,72B,95B,181B ''hammerfell'':84B ''history'':190B ''honor'':44B ''how'':117B ''hurl'':60B ''immens'':155B ''in'':78B,189B ''into'':120B ''is'':10B,80B,124B,151B ''it'':74B,118B,132B,170B ''its'':98B,154B,176B ''itself'':96B ''join'':50B ''journey'':92B ''known'':4B,82B,152B ''land'':73B ''legendary'':12B ''lik'':192B ''mad'':26B ''malacath'':109B,130B ''massiv'':24B ''metal'':29B ''might'':9B ''mock'':137B ''much'':191B ''nam'':86B ''not'':31B ''now'':81B ''of'':8B,20B,27B,40B,111B,144B,168B ''one'':110B,143B ''only'':32B ''or'':140B ''originally'':14B ''origins'':100B ''other'':55B ''over'':178B ''points'':188B ''pow'':157B,174B ''princ'':108B ''priz'':146B ''refus'':48B ''rest'':77B ''resurfac'':185B ''rourk'':18B,47B,90B ''s'':43B,91B,114B ''sap'':165B ''settl'':69B ''som'':127B ''speculat'':128B ''strength'':167B ''strik'':171B ''symbol'':39B ''tamriel'':63B ''that'':65B,129B,173B ''the'':6B,17B,21B,41B,46B,51B,58B,66B,71B,89B,94B,106B,112B,145B,166B,180B,193B ''them'':149B ''themselv'':195B ''this'':23B ''thos'':169B ''though'':126B ''tim'':179B ''to'':49B,76B,136B,141B,159B,175B ''transferring'':172B ''transition'':119B ''uncle'':125B ''various'':187B ''voldenrung'':1A ''volendrung'':2B,61B,101B,150B ''walls'':161B ''warhamm'':25B ''was'':30B ''way'':135B ''weapon'':35B ''what'':79B ''when'':45B ''wherev'':70B ''wield'':142B,177B ''with'':54B,105B,162B ''would'':68B', 'daedric, daedra, orc, scholar', 'Volendrung, known as the Hammer of Might, is a powerful warhammer originally crafted by the Dwemer''s Rourken clan. The hammer symbolizes their honor and was thrown across Tamriel by their chieftain when they refused to join the First Council, coming to rest in Hammerfell. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('merhrunes_razor', 'Mehrunes'' Razor, also known as the Dagger of the Final Wounds, the Bane of the Righteous, and the Kingslayer, is a deadly Daedric artifact created by Mehrunes Dagon, the Daedric Prince of Destruction. The Razor is famed for its ability to slay enemies instantly, as there is a small chance that Dagon will claim the soul of anyone struck by it. Forged from ebony and inscribed with Daedric script, the dagger has an ominous appearance and seems to absorb the very light that touches it.', '''ability'':42B ''absorb'':81B ''also'':5B ''an'':75B ''and'':19B,67B,78B ''anyon'':60B ''appearanc'':77B ''artifact'':26B ''as'':7B,47B ''ban'':15B ''by'':28B,62B ''chanc'':52B ''claim'':56B ''creat'':27B ''daedric'':25B,32B,70B ''dagg'':9B,73B ''dagon'':30B,54B ''deadly'':24B ''destruction'':35B ''ebony'':66B ''enemi'':45B ''fam'':39B ''final'':12B ''for'':40B ''forg'':64B ''from'':65B ''inscrib'':68B ''instantly'':46B ''is'':22B,38B,49B ''it'':63B,87B ''its'':41B ''kingslay'':21B ''known'':6B ''light'':84B ''mehrun'':3B,29B ''merhrun'':1A ''of'':10B,16B,34B,59B ''ominous'':76B ''princ'':33B ''razor'':2A,4B,37B ''righteous'':18B ''script'':71B ''seems'':79B ''slay'':44B ''small'':51B ''soul'':58B ''struck'':61B ''that'':53B,85B ''the'':8B,11B,14B,17B,20B,31B,36B,57B,72B,82B ''ther'':48B ''to'':43B,80B ''touch'':86B ''very'':83B ''will'':55B ''with'':69B ''wounds'':13B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', 'Mehrunes'' Razor, known as the Dagger of the Final Wounds, the Bane of the Righteous, and the Kingslayer, is a Daedric artifact created by Mehrunes Dagon. It is infamous for its ability to instantly slay enemies.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ebony_blade', 'The Ebony Blade, also known as the Vampire or the Leech, is a malevolent Daedric artifact created by the Daedric Prince Mephala. This ebony katana is infamous for its ability to absorb the life force of those it strikes, transferring their health and stamina to the wielder. It is a weapon associated with deceit, corruption, and betrayal, and has the power to silence its victims, preventing them from casting spells. In Khajiiti legends, it is referred to as "the killing word of the Spider" and "the black edge of shadow," underscoring its sinister reputation.

Throughout history, the Ebony Blade has driven its wielders to madness, corrupting their souls and leading them to commit acts of great evil. Those who use it are said to consign their souls to Oblivion, cursed by the blade''s dark influence. In an attempt to prevent further destruction, a charm was cast on the blade in the Second Era, ensuring it could not remain with any one person for too long. Despite this, the Ebony Blade''s bloody legacy continues, known for perverting the ambitions of those who fall under its spell.', '''ability'':32B ''absorb'':34B ''acts'':116B ''also'':6B ''ambitions'':182B ''an'':140B ''and'':45B,58B,60B,87B,111B ''any'':163B ''are'':124B ''artifact'':18B ''as'':8B,80B ''associat'':54B ''attempt'':141B ''betrayal'':59B ''black'':89B ''blad'':2A,5B,101B,135B,152B,173B ''bloody'':175B ''by'':20B,133B ''cast'':149B ''casting'':71B ''charm'':147B ''commit'':115B ''consign'':127B ''continu'':177B ''corrupting'':108B ''corruption'':57B ''could'':159B ''creat'':19B ''curs'':132B ''daedric'':17B,22B ''dark'':137B ''deceit'':56B ''despit'':169B ''destruction'':145B ''driv'':103B ''ebony'':1A,4B,26B,100B,172B ''edge'':90B ''ensuring'':157B ''evil'':119B ''fall'':186B ''for'':30B,166B,179B ''forc'':37B ''from'':70B ''furth'':144B ''great'':118B ''health'':44B ''history'':98B ''in'':73B,139B,153B ''infamous'':29B ''influenc'':138B ''is'':14B,28B,51B,77B ''it'':40B,50B,76B,123B,158B ''its'':31B,66B,94B,104B,188B ''katan'':27B ''khajiiti'':74B ''killing'':82B ''known'':7B,178B ''leading'':112B ''leech'':13B ''legacy'':176B ''legends'':75B ''lif'':36B ''long'':168B ''madness'':107B ''malevolent'':16B ''mephal'':24B ''not'':160B ''oblivion'':131B ''of'':38B,84B,91B,117B,183B ''on'':150B ''one'':164B ''or'':11B ''person'':165B ''perverting'':180B ''pow'':63B ''prevent'':143B ''preventing'':68B ''princ'':23B ''referr'':78B ''remain'':161B ''reputation'':96B ''s'':136B,174B ''said'':125B ''second'':155B ''shadow'':92B ''silenc'':65B ''sinist'':95B ''souls'':110B,129B ''spell'':189B ''spells'':72B ''spid'':86B ''stamin'':46B ''strik'':41B ''the'':3B,9B,12B,21B,35B,43B,48B,62B,81B,85B,88B,99B,109B,128B,134B,151B,154B,171B,181B ''them'':69B,113B ''this'':25B,170B ''thos'':39B,120B,184B ''throughout'':97B ''to'':33B,47B,64B,79B,106B,114B,126B,130B,142B ''too'':167B ''transferring'':42B ''under'':187B ''underscoring'':93B ''use'':122B ''vampir'':10B ''victims'':67B ''was'':148B ''weapon'':53B ''who'':121B,185B ''wield'':49B ''wielders'':105B ''with'':55B,162B ''word'':83B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', '
The Ebony Blade is a malevolent Daedric artifact created by Mephala, known for absorbing life force and silencing victims. Associated with deceit and corruption, it corrupts its wielders, driving them to madness and evil.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dawnbreaker', 'Dawnbreaker is a sacred Daedric artifact created by the Daedric Prince Meridia, known for its radiant power and effectiveness against the undead and other corrupt beings. This longsword features a unique crystal, the Dawnstar Gem, embedded in its cross-guard, emitting holy light. Forged to "burn away corruption and false life," Dawnbreaker is especially potent against Meridia''s enemies, such as undead, Daedra, and werewolves. When wielded, it deals magical or fire damage and has a chance to create a fiery explosion upon killing an undead enemy, which can harm other nearby undead and cause them to flee.', '''against'':21B,58B ''an'':87B ''and'':19B,24B,51B,66B,76B,96B ''artifact'':7B ''as'':63B ''away'':49B ''beings'':27B ''burn'':48B ''by'':9B ''can'':91B ''caus'':97B ''chanc'':79B ''corrupt'':26B ''corruption'':50B ''creat'':8B,81B ''cross'':41B ''cross-guard'':40B ''crystal'':33B ''daedr'':65B ''daedric'':6B,11B ''damag'':75B ''dawnbreak'':1A,2B,54B ''dawnst'':35B ''deals'':71B ''effectiveness'':20B ''embedd'':37B ''emitting'':43B ''enemi'':61B ''enemy'':89B ''especially'':56B ''explosion'':84B ''fals'':52B ''featur'':30B ''fiery'':83B ''fir'':74B ''fle'':100B ''for'':15B ''forg'':46B ''gem'':36B ''guard'':42B ''harm'':92B ''holy'':44B ''in'':38B ''is'':3B,55B ''it'':70B ''its'':16B,39B ''killing'':86B ''known'':14B ''lif'':53B ''light'':45B ''longsword'':29B ''magical'':72B ''meridi'':13B,59B ''nearby'':94B ''or'':73B ''other'':25B,93B ''potent'':57B ''pow'':18B ''princ'':12B ''radiant'':17B ''s'':60B ''sacr'':5B ''such'':62B ''the'':10B,22B,34B ''them'':98B ''this'':28B ''to'':47B,80B,99B ''unde'':23B,64B,88B,95B ''uniqu'':32B ''upon'':85B ''werewolv'':67B ''when'':68B ''which'':90B ''wield'':69B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', 'Dawnbreaker is a sacred Daedric artifact created by the Daedric Prince Meridia, known for its radiant power and effectiveness against the undead and other corrupt beings.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mace_of_molag_bal', 'The Mace of Molag Bal, also known as the Vampire''s Mace, is a Daedric artifact associated with Molag Bal, the Daedric Prince of Domination and Enslavement. This powerful weapon is enchanted to drain the stamina and magicka of its victims, transferring their energy to its wielder. It is also capable of sapping an enemy''s strength and even trapping their soul, making it a fearsome weapon against wizards and other formidable foes. The mace is often described as a symbol of Molag Bal''s power and cruelty, embodying his desire to dominate and enslave.

The origins of the Mace can be traced back to when Molag Bal tricked an Orcish blacksmith into forging it while enslaving him in Coldharbour, the Daedric Prince''s plane of Oblivion. The mace is frequently granted to mortals deemed worthy by Molag Bal, who relishes the trail of death and destruction it leaves in its wake. Worshippers of Molag Bal refer to the weapon as the Master''s Mace and often invoke it in their prayers and oaths.', '''against'':72B ''also'':10B,54B ''an'':58B,114B ''and'':30B,41B,62B,74B,91B,98B,150B,170B,177B ''artifact'':20B ''as'':12B,83B,165B ''associat'':21B ''back'':108B ''bal'':4A,9B,24B,88B,112B,143B,160B ''be'':106B ''blacksmith'':116B ''by'':141B ''can'':105B ''capabl'':55B ''coldharbour'':124B ''cruelty'':92B ''daedric'':19B,26B,126B ''death'':149B ''deem'':139B ''describ'':82B ''desir'':95B ''destruction'':151B ''dominat'':97B ''domination'':29B ''drain'':38B ''embodying'':93B ''enchant'':36B ''enemy'':59B ''energy'':48B ''enslav'':99B ''enslavement'':31B ''enslaving'':121B ''even'':63B ''fearsom'':70B ''foes'':77B ''forging'':118B ''formid'':76B ''frequently'':135B ''grant'':136B ''him'':122B ''his'':94B ''in'':123B,154B,174B ''into'':117B ''invok'':172B ''is'':17B,35B,53B,80B,134B ''it'':52B,68B,119B,152B,173B ''its'':44B,50B,155B ''known'':11B ''leav'':153B ''mac'':1A,6B,16B,79B,104B,133B,169B ''magick'':42B ''making'':67B ''mast'':167B ''molag'':3A,8B,23B,87B,111B,142B,159B ''mortals'':138B ''oaths'':178B ''oblivion'':131B ''of'':2A,7B,28B,43B,56B,86B,102B,130B,148B,158B ''often'':81B,171B ''orcish'':115B ''origins'':101B ''other'':75B ''plan'':129B ''pow'':90B ''powerful'':33B ''prayers'':176B ''princ'':27B,127B ''ref'':161B ''relish'':145B ''s'':15B,60B,89B,128B,168B ''sapping'':57B ''soul'':66B ''stamin'':40B ''strength'':61B ''symbol'':85B ''the'':5B,13B,25B,39B,47B,65B,78B,100B,103B,125B,132B,146B,163B,166B,175B ''this'':32B ''to'':37B,49B,96B,109B,137B,162B ''trac'':107B ''trail'':147B ''transferring'':46B ''trapping'':64B ''trick'':113B ''vampir'':14B ''victims'':45B ''wak'':156B ''weapon'':34B,71B,164B ''when'':110B ''whil'':120B ''who'':144B ''wield'':51B ''with'':22B ''wizards'':73B ''worshippers'':157B ''worthy'':140B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', '
The Mace of Molag Bal is a Daedric artifact that drains stamina and magicka, traps souls, and embodies Molag Bal''s power and cruelty. Forged through deceit, it is a symbol of domination and destruction.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ring_of_namira', 'The Ring of Namira is a Daedric artifact associated with Namira, the Daedric Prince of darkness, decay, and repulsion. It is granted to those who perform tasks in her name and embodies her macabre themes. The ring is known for its versatile powers, including reflecting damage onto attackers or enhancing the wearer’s stamina and health when they engage in cannibalism.

Throughout history, the ring has been bestowed upon notable figures who pleased Namira.', '''and'':21B,34B,58B ''artifact'':11B ''associat'':12B ''attackers'':51B ''been'':70B ''bestow'':71B ''cannibalism'':64B ''daedric'':10B,16B ''damag'':49B ''darkness'':19B ''decay'':20B ''embodi'':35B ''engag'':62B ''enhancing'':53B ''figur'':74B ''for'':43B ''grant'':25B ''health'':59B ''her'':32B,36B ''history'':66B ''in'':31B,63B ''including'':47B ''is'':8B,24B,41B ''it'':23B ''its'':44B ''known'':42B ''macabr'':37B ''nam'':33B ''namir'':3A,7B,14B,77B ''notabl'':73B ''of'':2A,6B,18B ''onto'':50B ''or'':52B ''perform'':29B ''pleas'':76B ''powers'':46B ''princ'':17B ''reflecting'':48B ''repulsion'':22B ''ring'':1A,5B,40B,68B ''s'':56B ''stamin'':57B ''tasks'':30B ''the'':4B,15B,39B,54B,67B ''them'':38B ''they'':61B ''thos'':27B ''throughout'':65B ''to'':26B ''upon'':72B ''versatil'':45B ''wear'':55B ''when'':60B ''who'':28B,75B ''with'':13B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', 'The Ring of Namira is a Daedric artifact associated with Namira, the Daedric Prince of darkness, decay, and repulsion. It is believed to be given to those who perform tasks for her', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skeleton_key', 'The Skeleton Key is a powerful Daedric artifact linked to Nocturnal, the Daedric Prince of Night and Shadows. Though typically appearing as a key or lockpick, its form can vary. The Skeleton Key is renowned for its ability to unlock any lock, making it a coveted tool for thieves and adventurers alike. When it manifests as a lockpick, it is nearly indestructible, bypassing even the toughest barriers. However, some wizards, seeking to limit its power, placed restrictions on the Key, such as limiting its use to once per day and ensuring it never stays in the possession of one thief for long, eventually disappearing.', '''ability'':40B ''adventurers'':53B ''alik'':54B ''and'':19B,52B,92B ''any'':43B ''appearing'':23B ''artifact'':10B ''as'':24B,58B,84B ''barriers'':69B ''bypassing'':65B ''can'':31B ''covet'':48B ''daedric'':9B,15B ''day'':91B ''disappearing'':106B ''ensuring'':93B ''even'':66B ''eventually'':105B ''for'':38B,50B,103B ''form'':30B ''howev'':70B ''in'':97B ''indestruct'':64B ''is'':6B,36B,62B ''it'':46B,56B,61B,94B ''its'':29B,39B,76B,86B ''key'':2A,5B,26B,35B,82B ''limit'':75B ''limiting'':85B ''link'':11B ''lock'':44B ''lockpick'':28B,60B ''long'':104B ''making'':45B ''manifests'':57B ''nearly'':63B ''nev'':95B ''night'':18B ''nocturnal'':13B ''of'':17B,100B ''on'':80B ''once'':89B ''one'':101B ''or'':27B ''per'':90B ''plac'':78B ''possession'':99B ''pow'':77B ''powerful'':8B ''princ'':16B ''renown'':37B ''restrictions'':79B ''seeking'':73B ''shadows'':20B ''skeleton'':1A,4B,34B ''som'':71B ''stays'':96B ''such'':83B ''the'':3B,14B,33B,67B,81B,98B ''thief'':102B ''thiev'':51B ''though'':21B ''to'':12B,41B,74B,88B ''tool'':49B ''toughest'':68B ''typically'':22B ''unlock'':42B ''use'':87B ''vary'':32B ''when'':55B ''wizards'':72B', 'daedric, daedra, thievesguild, scholar', 'The Skeleton Key is a Daedric artifact of Nocturnal, known for its ability to unlock any lock. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('umbra', 'Umbra, also known as the Umbra Sword, is a Daedric artifact created for the purpose of trapping souls. Crafted sometime before 2E 582 by the ancient witch Naenra Waerr at the behest of the Daedric Prince Clavicus Vile, the sword was intended to be a mischievous tool that would capture the souls of mortals. However, the sword''s initial design was unstable, necessitating Clavicus Vile to lend a fragment of his power to stabilize it. This act, however, backfired as the piece of power became sentient and took on the name Umbra.', '''2e'':23B ''582'':24B ''act'':78B ''also'':3B ''ancient'':27B ''and'':88B ''artifact'':12B ''as'':5B,81B ''at'':31B ''backfir'':80B ''be'':45B ''becam'':86B ''befor'':22B ''behest'':33B ''by'':25B ''captur'':51B ''clavicus'':38B,65B ''craft'':20B ''creat'':13B ''daedric'':11B,36B ''design'':61B ''for'':14B ''fragment'':70B ''his'':72B ''howev'':56B,79B ''initial'':60B ''intend'':43B ''is'':9B ''it'':76B ''known'':4B ''lend'':68B ''mischievous'':47B ''mortals'':55B ''naenr'':29B ''nam'':92B ''necessitating'':64B ''of'':17B,34B,54B,71B,84B ''on'':90B ''piec'':83B ''pow'':73B,85B ''princ'':37B ''purpos'':16B ''s'':59B ''sentient'':87B ''sometim'':21B ''souls'':19B,53B ''stabiliz'':75B ''sword'':8B,41B,58B ''that'':49B ''the'':6B,15B,26B,32B,35B,40B,52B,57B,82B,91B ''this'':77B ''to'':44B,67B,74B ''took'':89B ''tool'':48B ''trapping'':18B ''umbra'':1A,2B,7B,93B ''unstabl'':63B ''vil'':39B,66B ''waerr'':30B ''was'':42B,62B ''witch'':28B ''would'':50B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', 'Umbra is a Daedric artifact created by Naenra Waerr for Clavicus Vile, designed to trap souls. The sword became sentient after absorbing a fragment of Vile''s power, gaining its own identity as Umbra.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stendarrs_hammer', 'Stendarr''s Hammer is a legendary artifact believed to have been wielded by Stendarr, the God of Justice and Righteous Might. This formidable weapon is constructed from ebony and adorned with sapphire, which can enhance its tempering. It is noted for its significant weight, making it difficult for most individuals to wield effectively; it reportedly required the strength of four men to lift it onto its display podium in a museum.', '''adorn'':32B ''and'':21B,31B ''artifact'':9B ''been'':13B ''believ'':10B ''by'':15B ''can'':36B ''construct'':28B ''difficult'':49B ''display'':69B ''ebony'':30B ''effectively'':55B ''enhanc'':37B ''for'':43B,50B ''formid'':25B ''four'':62B ''from'':29B ''god'':18B ''hamm'':2A,5B ''hav'':12B ''in'':71B ''individuals'':52B ''is'':6B,27B,41B ''it'':40B,48B,56B,66B ''its'':38B,44B,68B ''justic'':20B ''legendary'':8B ''lift'':65B ''making'':47B ''men'':63B ''might'':23B ''most'':51B ''museum'':73B ''not'':42B ''of'':19B,61B ''onto'':67B ''podium'':70B ''reportedly'':57B ''requir'':58B ''righteous'':22B ''s'':4B ''sapphir'':34B ''significant'':45B ''stendarr'':3B,16B ''stendarrs'':1A ''strength'':60B ''tempering'':39B ''the'':17B,59B ''this'':24B ''to'':11B,53B,64B ''weapon'':26B ''weight'':46B ''which'':35B ''wield'':14B,54B ''with'':33B', 'priest, scholar', '
Stendarr''s Hammer is a legendary ebony weapon adorned with sapphire, associated with Stendarr, the God of Justice. Known for its immense weight, it requires extraordinary strength to wield effectively.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lords_mail', 'Lord''s Mail, also referred to as the Armor of Morihaus or the Gift of Kynareth, is a revered artifact bestowed upon mortals by Kynareth, one of the Eight Divines. This ancient cuirass, crafted from either adamantium or mithril, is regarded as some of the finest heavy armor available, offering exceptional quality and protection.', '''adamantium'':39B ''also'':6B ''ancient'':34B ''and'':55B ''armor'':11B,50B ''artifact'':22B ''as'':9B,44B ''avail'':51B ''bestow'':23B ''by'':26B ''craft'':36B ''cuirass'':35B ''divin'':32B ''eight'':31B ''eith'':38B ''exceptional'':53B ''finest'':48B ''from'':37B ''gift'':16B ''heavy'':49B ''is'':19B,42B ''kynareth'':18B,27B ''lord'':3B ''lords'':1A ''mail'':2A,5B ''mithril'':41B ''morihaus'':13B ''mortals'':25B ''of'':12B,17B,29B,46B ''offering'':52B ''one'':28B ''or'':14B,40B ''protection'':56B ''quality'':54B ''referr'':7B ''regard'':43B ''rever'':21B ''s'':4B ''som'':45B ''the'':10B,15B,30B,47B ''this'':33B ''to'':8B ''upon'':24B', 'priest, imperial, scholar', '
Lord''s Mail is a legendary cuirass gifted by Kynareth, known for its exceptional protection and craftsmanship, made from adamantium or mithril. It is revered as one of the finest pieces of heavy armor.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wraithguard', 'Wraithguard is a legendary gauntlet crafted by the Dwemer Tonal Architect Lord Kagrenac. It was specifically designed to safely wield two other powerful artifacts, Keening and Sunder, which together serve as the necessary tools for interacting with the Heart of Lorkhan.', '''and'':27B ''architect'':12B ''artifacts'':25B ''as'':32B ''by'':8B ''craft'':7B ''design'':18B ''dwem'':10B ''for'':36B ''gauntlet'':6B ''heart'':40B ''interacting'':37B ''is'':3B ''it'':15B ''kagrenac'':14B ''keening'':26B ''legendary'':5B ''lord'':13B ''lorkh'':42B ''necessary'':34B ''of'':41B ''other'':23B ''powerful'':24B ''safely'':20B ''serv'':31B ''specifically'':17B ''sund'':28B ''the'':9B,33B,39B ''to'':19B ''togeth'':30B ''tonal'':11B ''tools'':35B ''two'':22B ''was'':16B ''which'':29B ''wield'':21B ''with'':38B ''wraithguard'':1A,2B', 'dwemer', '
Wraithguard is a legendary Dwemer gauntlet created by Lord Kagrenac, designed to safely wield the powerful artifacts Keening and Sunder in conjunction with the Heart of Lorkhan.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('crown_of_barenziah', 'The Crown of Barenziah is a legendary coronation artifact crafted for Queen Barenziah during her ascension to the throne of Mournhold in the early Third Era, under the reign of Emperor Tiber Septim. This golden crown features a striking winged motif adorned with twenty-four ornate jewels, known as the Stones of Barenziah, set across its wings and a central gem on its temple. However, the crown’s grandeur was short-lived as it was stolen shortly after the coronation. The thief pried the stones from the crown, scattering them across Skyrim. The crown itself remained in Morrowind for much of its history, while the Thieves Guild of Skyrim sought to recover its scattered stones for centuries.', '''across'':59B,96B ''adorn'':45B ''after'':83B ''and'':62B ''artifact'':12B ''as'':53B,78B ''ascension'':19B ''barenziah'':3A,7B,16B,57B ''central'':64B ''centuri'':122B ''coronation'':11B,85B ''craft'':13B ''crown'':1A,5B,39B,71B,93B,99B ''during'':17B ''early'':27B ''emperor'':34B ''featur'':40B ''for'':14B,104B,121B ''four'':49B ''from'':91B ''gem'':65B ''gold'':38B ''grandeur'':73B ''guild'':112B ''her'':18B ''history'':108B ''howev'':69B ''in'':25B,102B ''is'':8B ''it'':79B ''its'':60B,67B,107B,118B ''itself'':100B ''jewels'':51B ''known'':52B ''legendary'':10B ''liv'':77B ''morrowind'':103B ''motif'':44B ''mournhold'':24B ''much'':105B ''of'':2A,6B,23B,33B,56B,106B,113B ''on'':66B ''ornat'':50B ''pri'':88B ''que'':15B ''recov'':117B ''reign'':32B ''remain'':101B ''s'':72B ''scatter'':119B ''scattering'':94B ''septim'':36B ''set'':58B ''short'':76B ''short-liv'':75B ''shortly'':82B ''skyrim'':97B,114B ''sought'':115B ''stol'':81B ''ston'':55B,90B,120B ''striking'':42B ''templ'':68B ''the'':4B,21B,26B,31B,54B,70B,84B,86B,89B,92B,98B,110B ''them'':95B ''thief'':87B ''thiev'':111B ''third'':28B ''this'':37B ''thron'':22B ''tib'':35B ''to'':20B,116B ''twenty'':48B ''twenty-four'':47B ''under'':30B ''was'':74B,80B ''whil'':109B ''wing'':43B ''wings'':61B ''with'':46B', 'scholar', 'The Crown of Barenziah is a legendary artifact created for Queen Barenziah''s coronation in the early Third Era. The golden crown, adorned with twenty-four jewels known as the Stones of Barenziah, was stolen after the coronation, and its jewels were scattered across Skyrim. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mace_of_the_crusader', '
The Mace of the Crusader, also known as the Mace of Zenithar, is a holy artifact crafted by Zenithar, imbued with the power to burn foes with holy flames and turn the undead. According to legend, after Pelinal Whitestrake''s death, the mace was brought to Leyawiin, where it inspired the creation of the Great Chapel of Zenithar by Saint Kaladas.', '''according'':38B ''after'':41B ''also'':10B ''and'':34B ''artifact'':20B ''as'':12B ''brought'':49B ''burn'':29B ''by'':22B,63B ''chapel'':60B ''craft'':21B ''creation'':56B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''death'':45B ''flam'':33B ''foes'':30B ''great'':59B ''holy'':19B,32B ''imbu'':24B ''inspir'':54B ''is'':17B ''it'':53B ''kal'':65B ''known'':11B ''legend'':40B ''leyawiin'':51B ''mac'':1A,6B,14B,47B ''of'':2A,7B,15B,57B,61B ''pelinal'':42B ''pow'':27B ''s'':44B ''saint'':64B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,13B,26B,36B,46B,55B,58B ''to'':28B,39B,50B ''turn'':35B ''unde'':37B ''was'':48B ''wher'':52B ''whitestrak'':43B ''with'':25B,31B ''zenith'':16B,23B,62B', 'scholar, imperial', 'The Mace of the Crusader, or Mace of Zenithar, is a holy artifact crafted by Zenithar that burns foes with holy flames and turns the undead. It inspired the creation of Leyawiin''s Great Chapel of Zenithar after being brought there following Pelinal Whitestrake''s death.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('necromancer_amulet', 'Necromancer''s Amulet is a legendary artifact created by Mannimarco, known as the King of Worms. This exquisite amulet is often adorned with a jade skull, sometimes intricately carved to resemble a tiny skull with glowing eyes. The amulet provides its wearer with magical protection akin to plate armor and grants enhanced regenerative abilities, resistance to mundane weapons, and the power to absorb both magicka and life force. Additionally, it significantly boosts the wearer''s wisdom and proficiency in the School of Conjuration.', '''abiliti'':56B ''absorb'':65B ''additionally'':71B ''adorn'':24B ''akin'':48B ''amulet'':2A,5B,21B,41B ''and'':52B,61B,68B,79B ''armor'':51B ''artifact'':9B ''as'':14B ''boosts'':74B ''both'':66B ''by'':11B ''carv'':31B ''conjuration'':85B ''creat'':10B ''enhanc'':54B ''exquisit'':20B ''eyes'':39B ''forc'':70B ''glowing'':38B ''grants'':53B ''in'':81B ''intricately'':30B ''is'':6B,22B ''it'':72B ''its'':43B ''jad'':27B ''king'':16B ''known'':13B ''legendary'':8B ''lif'':69B ''magical'':46B ''magick'':67B ''mannimarc'':12B ''mundan'':59B ''necromanc'':1A,3B ''of'':17B,84B ''often'':23B ''plat'':50B ''pow'':63B ''proficiency'':80B ''protection'':47B ''provid'':42B ''regenerativ'':55B ''resembl'':33B ''resistanc'':57B ''s'':4B,77B ''school'':83B ''significantly'':73B ''skull'':28B,36B ''sometim'':29B ''the'':15B,40B,62B,75B,82B ''this'':19B ''tiny'':35B ''to'':32B,49B,58B,64B ''weapons'':60B ''wear'':44B,76B ''wisdom'':78B ''with'':25B,37B,45B ''worms'':18B', 'mage, scholar', 'The Necromancer''s Amulet is a powerful artifact created by Mannimarco, enhancing conjuration, granting magical protection, and providing resistance, regeneration, and the ability to absorb magicka and life force.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ring_of_khajiit', 'Ring of Khajiiti is a Daedric artifact associated with the Daedric Princes Meridia and Mephala, both of whom have been known to offer the Ring in exchange for service. This legendary ring bestows its wearer with the powers of invisibility, silence, and enhanced agility.', '''agility'':47B ''and'':17B,45B ''artifact'':10B ''associat'':11B ''been'':23B ''bestows'':36B ''both'':19B ''daedric'':9B,14B ''enhanc'':46B ''exchang'':30B ''for'':31B ''hav'':22B ''in'':29B ''invisibility'':43B ''is'':7B ''its'':37B ''khajiit'':3A ''khajiiti'':6B ''known'':24B ''legendary'':34B ''mephal'':18B ''meridi'':16B ''of'':2A,5B,20B,42B ''offer'':26B ''powers'':41B ''princ'':15B ''ring'':1A,4B,28B,35B ''servic'':32B ''silenc'':44B ''the'':13B,27B,40B ''this'':33B ''to'':25B ''wear'':38B ''whom'':21B ''with'':12B,39B', 'khajiit, daedric, daedra, scholar', 'The Ring of Khajiiti is a Daedric artifact linked to Meridia and Mephala, granting its wearer invisibility, silence, and enhanced agility.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('amulet_of_kings', 'The Amulet of Kings, often referred to as the Amulet of the Kings of Glory, is a prestigious pendant traditionally worn by the ruling emperor of Cyrodiil. At its center lies the Chim-el Adabal, known as the Red Diamond, a significant soul gem of Ayleid origin, which is surrounded by eight smaller gems representing the Eight Divines of the original Cyrodilic pantheon established by Queen Alessia. The amulet symbolizes the divine right of Cyrodilic emperors and plays a crucial role in the coronation ceremony, serving as a powerful artifact for divination.

The soul of each reigning emperor is believed to be enshrined within the central stone during the coronation ritual involving the Dragonfires, forming a collective ''oversoul'' that provides counsel to their successors. Only those with the ''Dragon Blood'' in their veins can wear the amulet, though the precise criteria for this have been debated. While the Amulet of Kings is a sacred symbol of the Empire, many regard the Red Dragon Crown as the primary emblem of imperial power, and the Red Diamond has become closely associated with the Imperials.', '''adabal'':39B ''alessi'':71B ''amulet'':1A,5B,13B,73B,141B,153B ''and'':81B,176B ''artifact'':94B ''as'':11B,41B,91B,169B ''associat'':183B ''at'':31B ''ayle'':50B ''be'':106B ''becom'':181B ''been'':149B ''believ'':104B ''blood'':134B ''by'':25B,55B,69B ''can'':138B ''cent'':33B ''central'':110B ''ceremony'':89B ''chim'':37B ''chim-el'':36B ''closely'':182B ''collectiv'':121B ''coronation'':88B,114B ''counsel'':125B ''criteri'':145B ''crown'':168B ''crucial'':84B ''cyrodiil'':30B ''cyrodilic'':66B,79B ''debat'':150B ''diamond'':44B,179B ''divin'':62B,76B ''divination'':96B ''dragon'':133B,167B ''dragonfir'':118B ''during'':112B ''each'':100B ''eight'':56B,61B ''emblem'':172B ''emperor'':28B,102B ''emperors'':80B ''empir'':162B ''enshrin'':107B ''establish'':68B ''for'':95B,146B ''forming'':119B ''gem'':48B ''gems'':58B ''glory'':18B ''hav'':148B ''imperial'':174B ''imperials'':186B ''in'':86B,135B ''involving'':116B ''is'':19B,53B,103B,156B ''its'':32B ''kings'':3A,7B,16B,155B ''known'':40B ''lies'':34B ''many'':163B ''of'':2A,6B,14B,17B,29B,49B,63B,78B,99B,154B,160B,173B ''often'':8B ''only'':129B ''origin'':51B ''original'':65B ''oversoul'':122B ''pantheon'':67B ''pendant'':22B ''plays'':82B ''pow'':175B ''powerful'':93B ''precis'':144B ''prestigious'':21B ''primary'':171B ''provid'':124B ''que'':70B ''red'':43B,166B,178B ''referr'':9B ''regard'':164B ''reigning'':101B ''representing'':59B ''right'':77B ''ritual'':115B ''rol'':85B ''ruling'':27B ''sacr'':158B ''serving'':90B ''significant'':46B ''small'':57B ''soul'':47B,98B ''ston'':111B ''successors'':128B ''surround'':54B ''symbol'':159B ''symboliz'':74B ''that'':123B ''the'':4B,12B,15B,26B,35B,42B,60B,64B,72B,75B,87B,97B,109B,113B,117B,127B,132B,136B,140B,143B,152B,161B,165B,170B,177B,185B ''this'':147B ''thos'':130B ''though'':142B ''to'':10B,105B,126B ''traditionally'':23B ''veins'':137B ''wear'':139B ''which'':52B ''whil'':151B ''with'':131B,184B ''within'':108B ''worn'':24B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
The Amulet of Kings is a sacred pendant symbolizing the divine right of Cyrodilic emperors, featuring the Ayleid Red Diamond and gems representing the Eight Divines. It is tied to the Dragon Blood lineage and plays a key role in coronation rituals and the Empire''s legacy.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('black_books', 'Black Books are Daedric artifacts created by Hermaeus Mora, the Daedric Prince of Fate and Knowledge. These ancient tomes, bound in black covers and emitting an eerie mist, contain forbidden secrets from the past, present, or future. Each book serves as a gateway to Apocrypha, Mora''s realm in Oblivion, and holds dangerous yet tantalizing knowledge for those the Prince favors. Crafted with extraordinary materials, such as Seeker ink and Lurker leather, the books are perilous to read, often driving mortals insane. However, those who can navigate Apocrypha’s trials are rewarded with powerful insights or abilities. The true number of Black Books is known only to Hermaeus Mora, and they are often found hidden in ancient, treacherous dungeons across Tamriel.

In 4E 201, several Black Books were discovered on Solstheim, drawing mortals into Mora''s realm to test their resolve. When read, tentacles from the book envelop the reader, transporting their consciousness to Apocrypha while leaving a tethered apparition behind in Mundus. Within the realm, readers must face Mora’s gauntlets to claim the book’s secrets. While death in Apocrypha typically results in banishment back to Tamriel, the knowledge gained can be revisited by rereading the book. Revered for their otherworldly power, Black Books stand as a testament to the vast, unfathomable reach of Hermaeus Mora''s influence over time, space, and mortal curiosity.', '''201'':126B ''4e'':125B ''abiliti'':99B ''across'':122B ''an'':28B ''ancient'':20B,119B ''and'':17B,26B,53B,72B,112B,226B ''apocryph'':47B,90B,157B,184B ''apparition'':162B ''are'':5B,77B,93B,114B ''artifacts'':7B ''as'':43B,69B,210B ''back'':189B ''banishment'':188B ''be'':196B ''behind'':163B ''black'':1A,3B,24B,104B,128B,207B ''book'':41B,149B,178B,201B ''books'':2A,4B,76B,105B,129B,208B ''bound'':22B ''by'':9B,198B ''can'':88B,195B ''claim'':176B ''consciousness'':155B ''contain'':31B ''covers'':25B ''craft'':64B ''creat'':8B ''curiosity'':228B ''daedric'':6B,13B ''dangerous'':55B ''death'':182B ''discover'':131B ''drawing'':134B ''driving'':82B ''dungeons'':121B ''each'':40B ''eeri'':29B ''emitting'':27B ''envelop'':150B ''extraordinary'':66B ''fac'':171B ''fat'':16B ''favors'':63B ''for'':59B,203B ''forbidd'':32B ''found'':116B ''from'':34B,147B ''futur'':39B ''gain'':194B ''gateway'':45B ''gauntlets'':174B ''hermaeus'':10B,110B,219B ''hidd'':117B ''holds'':54B ''howev'':85B ''in'':23B,51B,118B,124B,164B,183B,187B ''influenc'':222B ''ink'':71B ''insan'':84B ''insights'':97B ''into'':136B ''is'':106B ''knowledg'':18B,58B,193B ''known'':107B ''leath'':74B ''leaving'':159B ''lurk'':73B ''materials'':67B ''mist'':30B ''mor'':11B,48B,111B,137B,172B,220B ''mortal'':227B ''mortals'':83B,135B ''mundus'':165B ''must'':170B ''navigat'':89B ''numb'':102B ''oblivion'':52B ''of'':15B,103B,218B ''often'':81B,115B ''on'':132B ''only'':108B ''or'':38B,98B ''otherworldly'':205B ''over'':223B ''past'':36B ''perilous'':78B ''pow'':206B ''powerful'':96B ''present'':37B ''princ'':14B,62B ''reach'':217B ''read'':80B,145B,152B ''readers'':169B ''realm'':50B,139B,168B ''rereading'':199B ''resolv'':143B ''results'':186B ''rever'':202B ''revisit'':197B ''reward'':94B ''s'':49B,91B,138B,173B,179B,221B ''secrets'':33B,180B ''seek'':70B ''serv'':42B ''several'':127B ''solstheim'':133B ''spac'':225B ''stand'':209B ''such'':68B ''tamriel'':123B,191B ''tantalizing'':57B ''tentacl'':146B ''test'':141B ''testament'':212B ''tether'':161B ''the'':12B,35B,61B,75B,100B,142B,148B,151B,154B,167B,177B,192B,200B,204B,214B ''thes'':19B ''they'':113B ''thos'':60B,86B ''tim'':224B ''to'':46B,79B,109B,140B,156B,175B,190B,213B ''tom'':21B ''transporting'':153B ''treacherous'':120B ''trials'':92B ''tru'':101B ''typically'':185B ''unfathom'':216B ''vast'':215B ''wer'':130B ''when'':144B ''whil'':158B,181B ''who'':87B ''with'':65B,95B ''within'':166B ''yet'':56B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Black Books are Daedric artifacts created by Hermaeus Mora, the Daedric Prince of Fate and Knowledge. These ancient tomes, bound in black and emitting mist, contain forbidden secrets and serve as gateways to Apocrypha, Mora''s realm. They are dangerous to read, often driving mortals insane, but those who survive the trials of Apocrypha gain powerful knowledge or abilities. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('studded_armor', 'Studded Armor is a basic studded hide chest piece with little protection quality. Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides and iron studs bound together with crude stitching. To craft it: 1 Iron Ingot, 4 leather and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge.  A Novice smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '''1'':40B ''3'':46B ''4'':43B ''and'':21B,29B,45B ''animal'':27B ''armor'':2A,4B ''at'':49B,66B ''basic'':7B ''be'':61B ''blacksmith'':51B ''bound'':32B ''by'':63B ''can'':56B,60B ''chest'':10B ''craft'':38B,57B ''crud'':35B ''design'':18B ''forg'':52B ''hid'':9B,28B ''ingot'':42B ''iron'':30B,41B,65B ''is'':5B,19B ''it'':39B,58B,59B ''its'':16B ''leath'':44B,47B ''light'':25B ''littl'':13B ''mad'':23B ''novic'':54B ''of'':24B ''piec'':11B ''primitiv'':22B ''protection'':14B ''quality'':15B ''rough'':20B ''smith'':55B ''stitching'':36B ''strips'':48B ''studd'':1A,3B,8B ''studs'':31B ''tann'':26B ''tempered/improved'':62B ''to'':37B ''togeth'':33B ''using'':64B ''visual'':17B ''with'':12B,34B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Studded Armor is a basic studded hide chest piece with little protection quality. Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides and iron studs bound together with crude stitching. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bloodthirst', 'Bloodthirst is a legendary Akaviri longsword, crafted in the style of Dawnfang and Duskfang, with a design that evokes unease through its beast-like blade and blood-infused jewel. Renowned for its unquenchable thirst for blood, the sword enhances its wielder''s strength and speed. After a convoluted history involving betrayal, necromancy, and failed plots.', '''after'':49B ''akaviri'':6B ''and'':14B,28B,47B,56B ''beast'':25B ''beast-lik'':24B ''betrayal'':54B ''blad'':27B ''blood'':30B,39B ''blood-infus'':29B ''bloodthirst'':1A,2B ''convolut'':51B ''craft'':8B ''dawnfang'':13B ''design'':18B ''duskfang'':15B ''enhanc'':42B ''evok'':20B ''fail'':57B ''for'':34B,38B ''history'':52B ''in'':9B ''infus'':31B ''involving'':53B ''is'':3B ''its'':23B,35B,43B ''jewel'':32B ''legendary'':5B ''lik'':26B ''longsword'':7B ''necromancy'':55B ''of'':12B ''plots'':58B ''renown'':33B ''s'':45B ''spe'':48B ''strength'':46B ''style'':11B ''sword'':41B ''that'':19B ''the'':10B,40B ''thirst'':37B ''through'':22B ''une'':21B ''unquench'':36B ''wield'':44B ''with'':16B', 'scholar', 'Bloodthirst is a legendary Akaviri longsword with a beast-like design and blood-infused jewel, known for enhancing the wielder''s strength and speed. Its history is marked by betrayal, necromancy, and failed schemes.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chillrend', '
Chillrend is a unique glass shortsword of unknown origin, distinguished by its blue hue instead of the typical green of malachite. Crafted with rare metals and moonstone, it is enchanted to inflict frost damage and may also weaken opponents to frost or cause temporary paralysis. Notably, Chillrend can repair itself when its wielder takes frost damage, making it a formidable and enduring weapon.', '''also'':38B ''and'':27B,36B,62B ''blu'':14B ''by'':12B ''can'':49B ''caus'':44B ''chillrend'':1A,2B,48B ''craft'':23B ''damag'':35B,57B ''distinguish'':11B ''enchant'':31B ''enduring'':63B ''formid'':61B ''frost'':34B,42B,56B ''glass'':6B ''gre'':20B ''hue'':15B ''inflict'':33B ''inste'':16B ''is'':3B,30B ''it'':29B,59B ''its'':13B,53B ''itself'':51B ''making'':58B ''malachit'':22B ''may'':37B ''metals'':26B ''moonston'':28B ''notably'':47B ''of'':8B,17B,21B ''opponents'':40B ''or'':43B ''origin'':10B ''paralysis'':46B ''rar'':25B ''rep'':50B ''shortsword'':7B ''tak'':55B ''temporary'':45B ''the'':18B ''to'':32B,41B ''typical'':19B ''uniqu'':5B ''unknown'':9B ''weak'':39B ''weapon'':64B ''when'':52B ''wield'':54B ''with'':24B', 'scholar, thievesguild', 'Chillrend is a unique blue glass shortsword crafted with rare materials, enchanted to inflict frost damage, weaken enemies, and cause paralysis. It can repair itself when its wielder takes frost damage, making it both powerful and enduring.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dawnfang', 'Dawnfang and Duskfang are a sentient Tsaesci longsword with four transformative forms: Dawnfang, Duskfang, and their superior variants. Known for their serpent-like design, pronged blade resembling a beast''s maw, and jeweled embellishments, the sword changes form at dawn and dusk, shifting between fiery and icy enchantments. The superior forms, Dawnfang Superior and Duskfang Superior, are achieved by satisfying the sword''s craving for lifeforce, with each transformation enhancing its powers to absorb health or magicka. The weapon repairs and recharges itself with each transformation, symbolizing its sinister purpose of dependency and corruption.', '''absorb'':76B ''achiev'':60B ''and'':3B,16B,34B,43B,48B,56B,83B,95B ''are'':5B,59B ''at'':41B ''beast'':31B ''betw'':46B ''blad'':28B ''by'':61B ''chang'':39B ''corruption'':96B ''craving'':66B ''dawn'':42B ''dawnfang'':1A,2B,14B,54B ''dependency'':94B ''design'':26B ''dusk'':44B ''duskfang'':4B,15B,57B ''each'':70B,87B ''embellishments'':36B ''enchantments'':50B ''enhancing'':72B ''fiery'':47B ''for'':21B,67B ''form'':40B ''forms'':13B,53B ''four'':11B ''health'':77B ''icy'':49B ''its'':73B,90B ''itself'':85B ''jewel'':35B ''known'':20B ''lifeforc'':68B ''lik'':25B ''longsword'':9B ''magick'':79B ''maw'':33B ''of'':93B ''or'':78B ''powers'':74B ''prong'':27B ''purpos'':92B ''recharg'':84B ''repairs'':82B ''resembling'':29B ''s'':32B,65B ''satisfying'':62B ''sentient'':7B ''serpent'':24B ''serpent-lik'':23B ''shifting'':45B ''sinist'':91B ''superior'':18B,52B,55B,58B ''sword'':38B,64B ''symbolizing'':89B ''the'':17B,22B,37B,51B,63B,80B ''to'':75B ''transformation'':71B,88B ''transformativ'':12B ''tsaesci'':8B ''variants'':19B ''weapon'':81B ''with'':10B,69B,86B', 'scholar', '
Dawnfang and Duskfang are sentient Tsaesci longswords that transform at dawn and dusk, shifting between fiery and icy enchantments. Their superior forms are achieved by feeding on lifeforce, enhancing their ability to absorb health or magicka, and they repair themselves with each transformation.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('duskfang', 'Dawnfang and Duskfang are a sentient Tsaesci longsword with four transformative forms: Dawnfang, Duskfang, and their superior variants. Known for their serpent-like design, pronged blade resembling a beast''s maw, and jeweled embellishments, the sword changes form at dawn and dusk, shifting between fiery and icy enchantments. The superior forms, Dawnfang Superior and Duskfang Superior, are achieved by satisfying the sword''s craving for lifeforce, with each transformation enhancing its powers to absorb health or magicka. The weapon repairs and recharges itself with each transformation, symbolizing its sinister purpose of dependency and corruption.', '''absorb'':76B ''achiev'':60B ''and'':3B,16B,34B,43B,48B,56B,83B,95B ''are'':5B,59B ''at'':41B ''beast'':31B ''betw'':46B ''blad'':28B ''by'':61B ''chang'':39B ''corruption'':96B ''craving'':66B ''dawn'':42B ''dawnfang'':2B,14B,54B ''dependency'':94B ''design'':26B ''dusk'':44B ''duskfang'':1A,4B,15B,57B ''each'':70B,87B ''embellishments'':36B ''enchantments'':50B ''enhancing'':72B ''fiery'':47B ''for'':21B,67B ''form'':40B ''forms'':13B,53B ''four'':11B ''health'':77B ''icy'':49B ''its'':73B,90B ''itself'':85B ''jewel'':35B ''known'':20B ''lifeforc'':68B ''lik'':25B ''longsword'':9B ''magick'':79B ''maw'':33B ''of'':93B ''or'':78B ''powers'':74B ''prong'':27B ''purpos'':92B ''recharg'':84B ''repairs'':82B ''resembling'':29B ''s'':32B,65B ''satisfying'':62B ''sentient'':7B ''serpent'':24B ''serpent-lik'':23B ''shifting'':45B ''sinist'':91B ''superior'':18B,52B,55B,58B ''sword'':38B,64B ''symbolizing'':89B ''the'':17B,22B,37B,51B,63B,80B ''to'':75B ''transformation'':71B,88B ''transformativ'':12B ''tsaesci'':8B ''variants'':19B ''weapon'':81B ''with'':10B,69B,86B', 'scholar', '
Dawnfang and Duskfang are sentient Tsaesci longswords that transform between fiery and icy enchantments at dawn and dusk. Their superior forms enhance their ability to absorb health or magicka, with each transformation recharging the weapon and deepening its sinister nature.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sword_of_the_crusader', '
The Sword of the Crusader, created by Arkay, burns foes with holy flames and drains their magicka. Cursed in undeath by its original wielder, Sir Berich Vlindrel, the sword stunted the magicka of the righteous. A pilgrim recovered the weapon from Vlindrel''s wraith in Underpall Cave and reconsecrated it at the Great Chapel of Arkay in Cheydinhal, lifting the curse.', '''and'':18B,52B ''arkay'':12B,60B ''at'':55B ''berich'':30B ''burns'':13B ''by'':11B,25B ''cav'':51B ''chapel'':58B ''cheydinhal'':62B ''creat'':10B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''curs'':22B,65B ''drains'':19B ''flam'':17B ''foes'':14B ''from'':45B ''great'':57B ''holy'':16B ''in'':23B,49B,61B ''it'':54B ''its'':26B ''lifting'':63B ''magick'':21B,36B ''of'':2A,7B,37B,59B ''original'':27B ''pilgrim'':41B ''reconsecrat'':53B ''recover'':42B ''righteous'':39B ''s'':47B ''sir'':29B ''stunt'':34B ''sword'':1A,6B,33B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,20B,32B,35B,38B,43B,56B,64B ''undeath'':24B ''underpall'':50B ''vlindrel'':31B,46B ''weapon'':44B ''wield'':28B ''with'':15B ''wraith'':48B', 'imperial, scholar', '
Dawnfang and Duskfang are sentient Tsaesci longswords that transform between fiery and icy enchantments at dawn and dusk. Their superior forms enhance their ability to absorb health or magicka, with each transformation recharging the weapon and deepening its sinister nature.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nerveshatter', '
Nerveshatter is a warhammer made from madness ore and amber, enchanted to deal shock damage. Associated with Lady Syl, Duchess of Dementia, it was wielded by her in Xirethard until her death during the Greymarch, after which it was claimed by the Hero of Kvatch.', '''after'':37B ''amber'':11B ''and'':10B ''associat'':17B ''by'':27B,42B ''claim'':41B ''damag'':16B ''deal'':14B ''death'':33B ''dementi'':23B ''duchess'':21B ''during'':34B ''enchant'':12B ''from'':7B ''greymarch'':36B ''her'':28B,32B,44B ''in'':29B ''is'':3B ''it'':24B,39B ''kvatch'':46B ''lady'':19B ''mad'':6B ''madness'':8B ''nerveshatt'':1A,2B ''of'':22B,45B ''ore'':9B ''shock'':15B ''syl'':20B ''the'':35B,43B ''to'':13B ''until'':31B ''warhamm'':5B ''was'':25B,40B ''which'':38B ''wield'':26B ''with'':18B ''xirethard'':30B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Nerveshatter is a warhammer crafted from madness ore and amber, enchanted to deal shock damage. Once wielded by Lady Syl, Duchess of Dementia, it was claimed by the Hero of Kvatch after her death during the Greymarch.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shadowrend', '
Shadowrend is a Daedric artifact taking the form of a shadowy two-handed weapon, appearing as either a claymore or battleaxe. Found in the Grove of Reflection in the Shivering Isles, it can be claimed by defeating a shadowy doppelganger summoned by the grove''s ancient magic.', '''ancient'':48B ''appearing'':17B ''artifact'':6B ''as'':18B ''battleax'':23B ''be'':36B ''by'':38B,44B ''can'':35B ''claim'':37B ''claymor'':21B ''daedric'':5B ''defeating'':39B ''doppelgang'':42B ''eith'':19B ''form'':9B ''found'':24B ''grov'':27B,46B ''hand'':15B ''in'':25B,30B ''is'':3B ''isles'':33B ''it'':34B ''magic'':49B ''of'':10B,28B ''or'':22B ''reflection'':29B ''s'':47B ''shadowrend'':1A,2B ''shadowy'':12B,41B ''shivering'':32B ''summon'':43B ''taking'':7B ''the'':8B,26B,31B,45B ''two'':14B ''two-hand'':13B ''weapon'':16B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Shadowrend is a Daedric artifact, appearing as a shadowy claymore or battleaxe, obtained by defeating a doppelganger in the Grove of Reflection in the Shivering Isles.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('leather_armor', 'Leather Armor is a basic leather chest piece with basic protection quality. Its visual design is simple and flexible, with dark, weathered leather panels stitched together for mobility and basic protection. To craft it: 4 leather and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge.  A Novice smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''3'':40B ''4'':37B ''and'':20B,31B,39B ''armor'':2A,4B ''at'':43B,60B ''basic'':7B,12B,32B ''be'':55B ''blacksmith'':45B ''by'':57B ''can'':50B,54B ''chest'':9B ''craft'':35B,51B ''dark'':23B ''design'':17B ''flexibl'':21B ''for'':29B ''forg'':46B ''is'':5B,18B ''it'':36B,52B,53B ''its'':15B ''leath'':1A,3B,8B,25B,38B,41B,59B ''mobility'':30B ''novic'':48B ''panels'':26B ''piec'':10B ''protection'':13B,33B ''quality'':14B ''simpl'':19B ''smith'':49B ''stitch'':27B ''strips'':42B ''tempered/improved'':56B ''to'':34B ''togeth'':28B ''using'':58B ''visual'':16B ''weather'':24B ''with'':11B,22B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Leather Armor is a basic leather chest piece with basic protection quality. Its visual design is simple and flexible, with dark, weathered leather panels stitched together for mobility and basic protection. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cuirass_of_the_crusader', '
The Cuirass of the Crusader, crafted by either Mara or Akatosh, grants magical protection, enhances the wearer''s health, and damages nearby undead or Daedra. First recovered by the original Knights after defeating the Wyrm of Elynglenn, it remained the only relic safeguarded by the order after its dissolution following Sir Amiel''s death. Protected by the spirits of the Knights in the priory''s undercroft, the cuirass could not be claimed until over 300 years later, when a pilgrim proved their worth in single combat and was granted the relic.', '''300'':79B ''after'':36B,51B ''akatosh'':15B ''amiel'':56B ''and'':24B,91B ''be'':75B ''by'':11B,32B,48B,60B ''claim'':76B ''combat'':90B ''could'':73B ''craft'':10B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''cuirass'':1A,6B,72B ''daedr'':29B ''damag'':25B ''death'':58B ''defeating'':37B ''dissolution'':53B ''eith'':12B ''elynglenn'':41B ''enhanc'':19B ''first'':30B ''following'':54B ''grant'':93B ''grants'':16B ''health'':23B ''in'':66B,88B ''it'':42B ''its'':52B ''knights'':35B,65B ''lat'':81B ''magical'':17B ''mar'':13B ''nearby'':26B ''not'':74B ''of'':2A,7B,40B,63B ''only'':45B ''or'':14B,28B ''order'':50B ''original'':34B ''over'':78B ''pilgrim'':84B ''priory'':68B ''protect'':59B ''protection'':18B ''prov'':85B ''recover'':31B ''relic'':46B,95B ''remain'':43B ''s'':22B,57B,69B ''safeguard'':47B ''singl'':89B ''sir'':55B ''spirits'':62B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,20B,33B,38B,44B,49B,61B,64B,67B,71B,86B,94B ''unde'':27B ''undercroft'':70B ''until'':77B ''was'':92B ''wear'':21B ''when'':82B ''worth'':87B ''wyrm'':39B ''years'':80B', 'imperial, scholar', '
The Cuirass of the Crusader, crafted by Mara or Akatosh, provides magical protection, enhances health, and harms undead or Daedra. Guarded by knightly spirits, it was reclaimed by a worthy pilgrim over 300 years after the order''s dissolution.
', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('giant_toe', 'Giant''s Toes are dropped by giants and are known for their powerful alchemical effects. Alchemy effects: Damage Stamina, Fortify Health, Fortify Carry Weight, and Damage Stamina Regen.', '''alchemical'':16B ''alchemy'':18B ''and'':10B,27B ''are'':6B,11B ''by'':8B ''carry'':25B ''damag'':20B,28B ''dropp'':7B ''effects'':17B,19B ''for'':13B ''fortify'':22B,24B ''giant'':1A,3B ''giants'':9B ''health'':23B ''known'':12B ''powerful'':15B ''reg'':30B ''s'':4B ''stamin'':21B,29B ''the'':14B ''toe'':2A ''toes'':5B ''weight'':26B', 'alchemist', 'Giant''s Toes are dropped by giants and are known for their powerful alchemical effects. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('boots_of_the_crusader', '
The Boots of the Crusader, also known as the Boots of Kynareth, are a sacred artifact created by Kynareth, granting the wearer harmony with nature, preventing attacks from forest creatures. After Sir Juncan''s death while seeking the boots, a pilgrim visited the Shrine of Kynareth and was guided to the Grove of Trials, where they faced the Forest Guardian. By showing reverence for nature and refusing to fight, the pilgrim earned access to the grotto where the boots were hidden. ', '''access'':77B ''after'':35B ''also'':10B ''and'':51B,70B ''are'':17B ''artifact'':20B ''as'':12B ''attacks'':31B ''boots'':1A,6B,14B,43B,83B ''by'':22B,65B ''creat'':21B ''creatur'':34B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''death'':39B ''earn'':76B ''fac'':61B ''fight'':73B ''for'':68B ''forest'':33B,63B ''from'':32B ''granting'':24B ''grott'':80B ''grov'':56B ''guardi'':64B ''guid'':53B ''harmony'':27B ''hidd'':85B ''junc'':37B ''known'':11B ''kynareth'':16B,23B,50B ''natur'':29B,69B ''of'':2A,7B,15B,49B,57B ''pilgrim'':45B,75B ''preventing'':30B ''refusing'':71B ''reverenc'':67B ''s'':38B ''sacr'':19B ''seeking'':41B ''showing'':66B ''shrin'':48B ''sir'':36B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,13B,25B,42B,47B,55B,62B,74B,79B,82B ''they'':60B ''to'':54B,72B,78B ''trials'':58B ''visit'':46B ''was'':52B ''wear'':26B ''wer'':84B ''wher'':59B,81B ''whil'':40B ''with'':28B', 'imperial, scholar', 'The Boots of the Crusader, created by Kynareth, grant harmony with nature and prevent attacks from forest creatures. They were recovered by a pilgrim who earned them by showing reverence for nature in the Grove of Trials.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('gauntlets_of_the_crusader', 'The Gauntlets of the Crusader, created by Stendarr, grant resistance to disease but were cursed after Sir Casimir struck down a beggar in anger, causing them to become immovable and cursing his bloodline with fatigue. Centuries later, a pilgrim redeemed the gauntlets by taking on the curse to free Casimir''s descendant, Kellen, with the curse ultimately lifted by the Blessing of Talos.', '''after'':20B ''and'':34B ''anger'':28B ''becom'':32B ''begg'':26B ''blessing'':65B ''bloodlin'':37B ''but'':17B ''by'':11B,47B,63B ''casim'':22B,54B ''causing'':29B ''centuri'':40B ''creat'':10B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''curs'':19B,51B,60B ''cursing'':35B ''descendant'':56B ''dis'':16B ''down'':24B ''fatig'':39B ''fre'':53B ''gauntlets'':1A,6B,46B ''grant'':13B ''his'':36B ''immov'':33B ''in'':27B ''kell'':57B ''lat'':41B ''lift'':62B ''of'':2A,7B,66B ''on'':49B ''pilgrim'':43B ''redeem'':44B ''resistanc'':14B ''s'':55B ''sir'':21B ''stendarr'':12B ''struck'':23B ''taking'':48B ''tal'':67B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,45B,50B,59B,64B ''them'':30B ''to'':15B,31B,52B ''ultimately'':61B ''wer'':18B ''with'':38B,58B', 'imperial, scholar', 'The Gauntlets of the Crusader, created by Stendarr, grant resistance to disease but were cursed due to a past misdeed. They were redeemed centuries later by a pilgrim who lifted the curse with the Blessing of Talos.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('helm_of_the_crusader', 'The Helm of the Crusader, created by Dibella, grants the wearer serene beauty, enhances bartering abilities, and improves skills in Illusion magic. After Pelinal Whitestrake''s death, his followers enshrined the helm in the halls of Vanua, which later became submerged under Lake Rumare. In 3E 153, Sir Amiel perished in the haunted ruins while seeking the helm to restore his order’s honor. Centuries later, a pilgrim, guided by a vision of Whitestrake, discovered Sir Amiel’s remains and reclaimed the helm.', '''153'':51B ''3e'':50B ''abiliti'':20B ''after'':27B ''amiel'':53B,81B ''and'':21B,84B ''bartering'':19B ''beauty'':17B ''becam'':44B ''by'':11B,74B ''centuri'':69B ''creat'':10B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''death'':31B ''dibell'':12B ''discover'':79B ''enhanc'':18B ''enshrin'':34B ''followers'':33B ''grants'':13B ''guid'':73B ''halls'':39B ''haunt'':57B ''helm'':1A,6B,36B,62B,87B ''his'':32B,65B ''honor'':68B ''illusion'':25B ''improv'':22B ''in'':24B,37B,49B,55B ''lak'':47B ''lat'':43B,70B ''magic'':26B ''of'':2A,7B,40B,77B ''order'':66B ''pelinal'':28B ''perish'':54B ''pilgrim'':72B ''reclaim'':85B ''remains'':83B ''restor'':64B ''ruins'':58B ''rumar'':48B ''s'':30B,67B,82B ''seeking'':60B ''seren'':16B ''sir'':52B,80B ''skills'':23B ''submerg'':45B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,14B,35B,38B,56B,61B,86B ''to'':63B ''under'':46B ''vanu'':41B ''vision'':76B ''wear'':15B ''which'':42B ''whil'':59B ''whitestrak'':29B,78B', 'imperial, scholar', '
The Helm of the Crusader, created by Dibella, enhances beauty, bartering, and Illusion skills. It was enshrined in Vanua after Pelinal Whitestrake''s death and reclaimed centuries later by a pilgrim guided by a vision.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shield_of_the_crusader', '
The Shield of the Crusader, crafted by Julianos, reflects or deflects spells and is shaped like the Chim-el Adabal, symbolizing the Imperial pantheon. Originally retrieved by Sir Henrik, the shield was hidden in Fort Bulwark, where he died before completing its defenses. Centuries later, a pilgrim, guided by Sir Henrik’s ghost, braved the fort’s traps and puzzles, freeing Sir Thedret from captivity and recovering the shield from the ruins'' depths.', '''adabal'':25B ''and'':17B,64B,71B ''befor'':45B ''brav'':59B ''bulwark'':41B ''by'':11B,32B,54B ''captivity'':70B ''centuri'':49B ''chim'':23B ''chim-el'':22B ''completing'':46B ''craft'':10B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''defens'':48B ''deflects'':15B ''depths'':78B ''died'':44B ''fort'':40B,61B ''freeing'':66B ''from'':69B,75B ''ghost'':58B ''guid'':53B ''henrik'':34B,56B ''hidd'':38B ''imperial'':28B ''in'':39B ''is'':18B ''its'':47B ''julian'':12B ''lat'':50B ''lik'':20B ''of'':2A,7B ''or'':14B ''originally'':30B ''pantheon'':29B ''pilgrim'':52B ''puzzl'':65B ''recovering'':72B ''reflects'':13B ''retriev'':31B ''ruins'':77B ''s'':57B,62B ''shap'':19B ''shield'':1A,6B,36B,74B ''sir'':33B,55B,67B ''spells'':16B ''symbolizing'':26B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,21B,27B,35B,60B,73B,76B ''thedret'':68B ''traps'':63B ''was'':37B ''wher'':42B', 'imperial, scholar', '
The Shield of the Crusader, crafted by Julianos, reflects spells and symbolizes the Imperial pantheon. Hidden in Fort Bulwark, it was reclaimed centuries later by a pilgrim who overcame its traps and freed Sir Thedret.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('gray_cowl', 'The Gray Cowl of Nocturnal, also known as the Shadow Queen''s Cowl, is a Daedric artifact tied to Nocturnal, revered by thieves across Tamriel as the Mistress of Shadows. This dark leather cowl obscures the wearer''s identity, originally cursed to erase the owner''s name from history and memory. Legends suggest it was stolen by Emer Dareloth, a Thieves Guild guildmaster, but the curse was later broken using an Elder Scroll. Inscribed with the phrase "Shadow hide you" in Daedric, the cowl symbolizes the connection between thieves and Nocturnal, with the Nightingales believing it represents their journey to the Evergloam after death. It has inspired curiosity among scholars, such as the Cult of the Ancestor Moth, who sought to study the curse.', '''across'':26B ''after'':105B ''also'':8B ''among'':111B ''an'':73B ''ancestor'':119B ''and'':52B,92B ''artifact'':19B ''as'':10B,28B,114B ''believing'':97B ''betw'':90B ''brok'':71B ''but'':66B ''by'':24B,59B ''connection'':89B ''cowl'':2A,5B,15B,36B,86B ''cult'':116B ''curiosity'':110B ''curs'':43B,68B,126B ''daedric'':18B,84B ''dareloth'':61B ''dark'':34B ''death'':106B ''elder'':74B ''emer'':60B ''eras'':45B ''evergloam'':104B ''from'':50B ''gray'':1A,4B ''guild'':64B ''guildmast'':65B ''hid'':81B ''history'':51B ''identity'':41B ''in'':83B ''inscrib'':76B ''inspir'':109B ''is'':16B ''it'':56B,98B,107B ''journey'':101B ''known'':9B ''lat'':70B ''leath'':35B ''legends'':54B ''memory'':53B ''mistress'':30B ''moth'':120B ''nam'':49B ''nightingal'':96B ''nocturnal'':7B,22B,93B ''obscur'':37B ''of'':6B,31B,117B ''originally'':42B ''owner'':47B ''phras'':79B ''que'':13B ''represents'':99B ''rever'':23B ''s'':14B,40B,48B ''scholars'':112B ''scroll'':75B ''shadow'':12B,80B ''shadows'':32B ''sought'':122B ''stol'':58B ''study'':124B ''such'':113B ''suggest'':55B ''symboliz'':87B ''tamriel'':27B ''the'':3B,11B,29B,38B,46B,67B,78B,85B,88B,95B,100B,103B,115B,118B,125B ''thiev'':25B,63B,91B ''this'':33B ''tied'':20B ''to'':21B,44B,102B,123B ''using'':72B ''was'':57B,69B ''wear'':39B ''who'':121B ''with'':77B,94B ''you'':82B', 'thievesguild, scholar', '
The Gray Cowl of Nocturnal, a Daedric artifact tied to Nocturnal, obscures the wearer''s identity and was once cursed to erase their name from history. Revered by thieves, it symbolizes their connection to Nocturnal and the Evergloam.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ectoplasm', 'Ectoplasm is an uncommon greyish goo ingredient obtained from ghosts, known for its magical and destructive alchemical properties. Alchemy effects: Restore Magicka, Fortify Destruction, Fortify Magicka, and Damage Health.', '''alchemical'':18B ''alchemy'':20B ''an'':4B ''and'':16B,28B ''damag'':29B ''destruction'':25B ''destructiv'':17B ''ectoplasm'':1A,2B ''effects'':21B ''for'':13B ''fortify'':24B,26B ''from'':10B ''ghosts'':11B ''goo'':7B ''greyish'':6B ''health'':30B ''ingredient'':8B ''is'':3B ''its'':14B ''known'':12B ''magical'':15B ''magick'':23B,27B ''obtain'':9B ''properti'':19B ''restor'':22B ''uncommon'':5B', 'alchemist', 'Ectoplasm is an uncommon greyish goo ingredient obtained from ghosts, known for its magical and destructive alchemical properties.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('goldbrand', 'Goldbrand is a legendary golden katana created by the dragons of the North and imbued with the power of the Daedric Prince Boethiah, capable of burning those it strikes. First bestowed upon the Nordic warrior Sivdur, an ancestor of the Battle-Born clan, the blade has been revered through history, with its significance documented by Yagrum Bagarn in Tamrielic Lore, spreading its legend across Tamriel.', '''across'':66B ''an'':38B ''ancestor'':39B ''and'':15B ''bagarn'':59B ''battl'':43B ''battle-born'':42B ''been'':49B ''bestow'':32B ''blad'':47B ''boethiah'':24B ''born'':44B ''burning'':27B ''by'':9B,57B ''capabl'':25B ''clan'':45B ''creat'':8B ''daedric'':22B ''document'':56B ''dragons'':11B ''first'':31B ''gold'':6B ''goldbrand'':1A,2B ''history'':52B ''imbu'':16B ''in'':60B ''is'':3B ''it'':29B ''its'':54B,64B ''katan'':7B ''legend'':65B ''legendary'':5B ''lor'':62B ''nordic'':35B ''north'':14B ''of'':12B,20B,26B,40B ''pow'':19B ''princ'':23B ''rever'':50B ''significanc'':55B ''sivdur'':37B ''spreading'':63B ''strik'':30B ''tamriel'':67B ''tamrielic'':61B ''the'':10B,13B,18B,21B,34B,41B,46B ''thos'':28B ''through'':51B ''upon'':33B ''warrior'':36B ''with'':17B,53B ''yagrum'':58B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
Goldbrand is a legendary golden katana created by Northern dragons and imbued with Boethiah''s power, capable of burning enemies. First given to the Nordic warrior Sivdur, its legacy is documented in Tamrielic Lore and revered across Tamriel.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('eltonbrand', 'Eltonbrand is an upgraded version of the legendary sword Goldbrand, offering higher damage, additional enchantments, and increased uses. To obtain Eltonbrand, the wielder must meet specific conditions, including possessing Goldbrand, Shashev''s Key, exactly 11,171 gold, and being a vampire. You have a hunch that the creator of this powerful sword likes to watch people play a sports game involving bouncing a ball.', '''11'':36B ''171'':37B ''additional'':15B ''an'':4B ''and'':17B,39B ''ball'':65B ''being'':40B ''bouncing'':63B ''conditions'':28B ''creator'':49B ''damag'':14B ''eltonbrand'':1A,2B,22B ''enchantments'':16B ''exactly'':35B ''gam'':61B ''gold'':38B ''goldbrand'':11B,31B ''hav'':44B ''high'':13B ''hunch'':46B ''including'':29B ''increas'':18B ''involving'':62B ''is'':3B ''key'':34B ''legendary'':9B ''lik'':54B ''meet'':26B ''must'':25B ''obtain'':21B ''of'':7B,50B ''offering'':12B ''peopl'':57B ''play'':58B ''possessing'':30B ''powerful'':52B ''s'':33B ''shashev'':32B ''specific'':27B ''sports'':60B ''sword'':10B,53B ''that'':47B ''the'':8B,23B,48B ''this'':51B ''to'':20B,55B ''upgrad'':5B ''uses'':19B ''vampir'':42B ''version'':6B ''watch'':56B ''wield'':24B ''you'':43B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
Eltonbrand is an upgraded version of Goldbrand with greater damage and enchantments, obtainable under specific conditions involving Goldbrand, Shashev''s Key, 11,171 gold, and vampirism. Its creation is linked to a sports enthusiast. You have a hunch this weapon was created as a joke.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ayleid_crown_of_nenalata', '
The Ayleid Crown of Nenalata is an ancient artifact associated with the Ayleid city-state of Nenalata, known for its Daedraphile culture and allegiance to the Alessian Empire. Distinguished by its royal glyph, the crown enhances spell reflection and boosts skills in Alteration and Conjuration magic. Traditionally worn by Nenalata''s king, its last known bearer was Laloriaran Dynar, the Last King of the Ayleids, who inherited it before 1E 331. The crown''s immense value and mysterious potential make it a significant piece of Ayleid history.', '''1e'':75B ''331'':76B ''alessi'':32B ''allegianc'':29B ''alteration'':48B ''an'':11B ''ancient'':12B ''and'':28B,44B,49B,82B ''artifact'':13B ''associat'':14B ''ayle'':1A,6B,17B,91B ''ayleids'':70B ''bear'':61B ''befor'':74B ''boosts'':45B ''by'':35B,54B ''city'':19B ''city-stat'':18B ''conjuration'':50B ''crown'':2A,7B,40B,78B ''cultur'':27B ''daedraphil'':26B ''distinguish'':34B ''dynar'':64B ''empir'':33B ''enhanc'':41B ''for'':24B ''glyph'':38B ''history'':92B ''immens'':80B ''in'':47B ''inherit'':72B ''is'':10B ''it'':73B,86B ''its'':25B,36B,58B ''king'':57B,67B ''known'':23B,60B ''lalori'':63B ''last'':59B,66B ''magic'':51B ''mak'':85B ''mysterious'':83B ''nenalat'':4A,9B,22B,55B ''of'':3A,8B,21B,68B,90B ''piec'':89B ''potential'':84B ''reflection'':43B ''royal'':37B ''s'':56B,79B ''significant'':88B ''skills'':46B ''spell'':42B ''stat'':20B ''the'':5B,16B,31B,39B,65B,69B,77B ''to'':30B ''traditionally'':52B ''valu'':81B ''was'':62B ''who'':71B ''with'':15B ''worn'':53B', 'scholar', '
The Ayleid Crown of Nenalata is an ancient artifact linked to the Ayleid city-state of Nenalata, enhancing spell reflection and magic skills. Last worn by Laloriaran Dynar, the Last King of the Ayleids, it is a valuable and significant relic of Ayleid history.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('staff_of_hasedoki', '
The Staff of Hasedoki is a legendary artifact created by the powerful wizard Hasedoki, who bonded his soul to the staff to combat his isolation. This engraved metallic staff, adorned with a horned blue head, offers its wielder resistance to magicka, the ability to knock back enemies with forceful projectiles, and a soul trap effect. Revered by magic users across Tamriel, it is highly sought after for its potent defensive and offensive capabilities.', '''ability'':46B ''across'':63B ''adorn'':33B ''after'':69B ''and'':54B,74B ''artifact'':11B ''back'':49B ''blu'':37B ''bond'':19B ''by'':13B,60B ''capabiliti'':76B ''combat'':26B ''creat'':12B ''defensiv'':73B ''effect'':58B ''enemi'':50B ''engrav'':30B ''for'':70B ''forceful'':52B ''hasedoki'':3A,7B,17B ''head'':38B ''highly'':67B ''his'':20B,27B ''horn'':36B ''is'':8B,66B ''isolation'':28B ''it'':65B ''its'':40B,71B ''knock'':48B ''legendary'':10B ''magic'':61B ''magick'':44B ''metallic'':31B ''of'':2A,6B ''offensiv'':75B ''offers'':39B ''potent'':72B ''powerful'':15B ''projectil'':53B ''resistanc'':42B ''rever'':59B ''sought'':68B ''soul'':21B,56B ''staff'':1A,5B,24B,32B ''tamriel'':64B ''the'':4B,14B,23B,45B ''this'':29B ''to'':22B,25B,43B,47B ''trap'':57B ''users'':62B ''who'':18B ''wield'':41B ''with'':34B,51B ''wizard'':16B', 'scholar, mage', '
The Staff of Hasedoki is a legendary artifact created by the wizard Hasedoki, offering resistance to magicka, the ability to knock back enemies, and a soul trap effect. Highly sought after by magic users, it is revered for its powerful defensive and offensive capabilities.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bow_of_shadows', 'The Bow of Shadows is a Daedric artifact attributed to Nocturnal, granting its wielder invisibility and increased speed. Originally given to the ranger Raerlas Ghile for a failed mission, the bow was lost, though legends say Raerlas used it to vanquish many foes before his demise.', '''and'':19B ''artifact'':11B ''attribut'':12B ''befor'':47B ''bow'':1A,5B,34B ''daedric'':10B ''demis'':49B ''fail'':31B ''foes'':46B ''for'':29B ''ghil'':28B ''giv'':23B ''granting'':15B ''his'':48B ''increas'':20B ''invisibility'':18B ''is'':8B ''it'':42B ''its'':16B ''legends'':38B ''lost'':36B ''many'':45B ''mission'':32B ''nocturnal'':14B ''of'':2A,6B ''originally'':22B ''raerl'':27B,40B ''rang'':26B ''say'':39B ''shadows'':3A,7B ''spe'':21B ''the'':4B,25B,33B ''though'':37B ''to'':13B,24B,43B ''used'':41B ''vanquish'':44B ''was'':35B ''wield'':17B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', 'The Bow of Shadows is a Daedric artifact from Nocturnal, granting invisibility and increased speed. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('daedric_crescent', 'The Daedric Crescent Blade is a rare artifact created by Mehrunes Dagon, capable of paralyzing foes, damaging their armor, and emitting an enigmatic green energy. Once used by Dagon''s forces during the Imperial Simulacrum to seize the Battlespire, most Crescents were destroyed when the Empire reclaimed the academy, though one is rumored to still exist in Tamriel. The crescent shape also appears symbolically in Daedric architecture dedicated to Dagon in Morrowind.', '''academy'':51B ''also'':64B ''an'':24B ''and'':22B ''appears'':65B ''architectur'':69B ''armor'':21B ''artifact'':10B ''battlespir'':41B ''blad'':6B ''by'':12B,30B ''capabl'':15B ''creat'':11B ''crescent'':2A,5B,62B ''crescents'':43B ''daedric'':1A,4B,68B ''dagon'':14B,31B,72B ''damaging'':19B ''dedicat'':70B ''destroy'':45B ''during'':34B ''emitting'':23B ''empir'':48B ''energy'':27B ''enigmatic'':25B ''exist'':58B ''foes'':18B ''forc'':33B ''gre'':26B ''imperial'':36B ''in'':59B,67B,73B ''is'':7B,54B ''mehrun'':13B ''morrowind'':74B ''most'':42B ''of'':16B ''once'':28B ''one'':53B ''paralyzing'':17B ''rar'':9B ''reclaim'':49B ''rumor'':55B ''s'':32B ''seiz'':39B ''shap'':63B ''simulacrum'':37B ''still'':57B ''symbolically'':66B ''tamriel'':60B ''the'':3B,20B,35B,40B,47B,50B,61B ''though'':52B ''to'':38B,56B,71B ''used'':29B ''wer'':44B ''when'':46B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', 'The Daedric Crescent Blade is a rare artifact created by Mehrunes Dagon, capable of paralyzing foes and damaging armor. Used by Dagon''s forces during the Imperial Simulacrum, most were destroyed, but one is rumored to remain in Tamriel.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fork_of_horripilation', 'The Fork of Horripilation is a cursed artifact of Sheogorath, appearing as a simple iron fork with enchantments that excite magicka and curse its wielder with magicka-draining effects. Fondly called "Forky" by Sheogorath, it is often used by the Mad God to torment mortals by forcing them to wield it as a weapon. The Fork has a strange history, including being "lost" during Sheogorath''s visit to the Dragon Priest Korthor in the Merethic Era and later recovered by the Vestige in various Sheogorath-related trials. Notably, it smells faintly of roast beef, adding to its bizarre nature.', '''adding'':100B ''and'':25B,81B ''appearing'':14B ''artifact'':11B ''as'':15B,56B ''beef'':99B ''being'':66B ''bizarr'':103B ''by'':37B,43B,50B,84B ''call'':35B ''curs'':10B,26B ''dragon'':74B ''draining'':32B ''during'':68B ''effects'':33B ''enchantments'':21B ''excit'':23B ''faintly'':96B ''fondly'':34B ''forcing'':51B ''fork'':1A,5B,19B,60B ''forky'':36B ''god'':46B ''history'':64B ''horripilation'':3A,7B ''in'':77B,87B ''including'':65B ''iron'':18B ''is'':8B,40B ''it'':39B,55B,94B ''its'':27B,102B ''korthor'':76B ''lat'':82B ''lost'':67B ''mad'':45B ''magick'':24B,31B ''magicka-draining'':30B ''merethic'':79B ''mortals'':49B ''natur'':104B ''notably'':93B ''of'':2A,6B,12B,97B ''often'':41B ''priest'':75B ''recover'':83B ''relat'':91B ''roast'':98B ''s'':70B ''sheogorath'':13B,38B,69B,90B ''sheogorath-relat'':89B ''simpl'':17B ''smells'':95B ''strang'':63B ''that'':22B ''the'':4B,44B,59B,73B,78B,85B ''them'':52B ''to'':47B,53B,72B,101B ''torment'':48B ''trials'':92B ''used'':42B ''various'':88B ''vestig'':86B ''visit'':71B ''weapon'':58B ''wield'':28B,54B ''with'':20B,29B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
The Fork of Horripilation is a cursed artifact of Sheogorath, appearing as a simple iron fork that drains magicka and torments its wielder. Known as "Forky," it has a bizarre history and is often used by Sheogorath to torment mortals, smelling faintly of roast beef.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('spear_of_bitter_mercy', '
The Spear of Bitter Mercy is a mysterious artifact believed to be of Daedric origin, originally forged by Mehrunes Dagon and later associated with Hircine, earning him the Reachfolk title "Spear with Five Points." Imbued with powerful energies capable of instantly killing all but High Daedra Lords, the Spear is central to Hircine''s Great Hunt and can only be wielded by those sanctified to its rules. Though once in Sheogorath''s possession, its history remains enigmatic, and it is known to reject unworthy wielders outside its intended purpose.', '''all'':47B ''and'':25B,61B,82B ''artifact'':13B ''associat'':27B ''be'':16B,64B ''believ'':14B ''bitt'':3A,8B ''but'':48B ''by'':22B,66B ''can'':62B ''capabl'':43B ''central'':55B ''daedr'':50B ''daedric'':18B ''dagon'':24B ''earning'':30B ''energi'':42B ''enigmatic'':81B ''fiv'':37B ''forg'':21B ''great'':59B ''high'':49B ''him'':31B ''hircin'':29B,57B ''history'':79B ''hunt'':60B ''imbu'':39B ''in'':74B ''instantly'':45B ''intend'':92B ''is'':10B,54B,84B ''it'':83B ''its'':70B,78B,91B ''killing'':46B ''known'':85B ''lat'':26B ''lords'':51B ''mehrun'':23B ''mercy'':4A,9B ''mysterious'':12B ''of'':2A,7B,17B,44B ''once'':73B ''only'':63B ''origin'':19B ''originally'':20B ''outsid'':90B ''points'':38B ''possession'':77B ''powerful'':41B ''purpos'':93B ''reachfolk'':33B ''reject'':87B ''remains'':80B ''rul'':71B ''s'':58B,76B ''sanctifi'':68B ''sheogorath'':75B ''spe'':1A,6B,35B,53B ''the'':5B,32B,52B ''thos'':67B ''though'':72B ''titl'':34B ''to'':15B,56B,69B,86B ''unworthy'':88B ''wield'':65B ''wielders'':89B ''with'':28B,36B,40B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
