INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ancient_nord_helmet', 'Ancient Nord Helmet has good protection quality. Its visual design is iconic and imposing, with a horned metal design etched with Nordic symbols and a worn, battle-hardened finish. Can only be crafted at the Skyforge, 3 steel ingots, 2 iron ingots, 2 leather, 3 leather strips. It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '''2'':44B,47B ''3'':41B,49B ''ancient'':1A,4B ''and'':16B,27B ''at'':38B,59B ''battl'':31B ''battle-harden'':30B ''be'':36B,54B ''by'':56B ''can'':34B,53B ''craft'':37B ''design'':13B,22B ''etched'':23B ''finish'':33B ''good'':8B ''harden'':32B ''helmet'':3A,6B ''horn'':20B ''iconic'':15B ''imposing'':17B ''ingots'':43B,46B ''iron'':45B,58B ''is'':14B ''it'':52B ''its'':11B ''leath'':48B,50B ''metal'':21B ''nord'':2A,5B ''nordic'':25B ''only'':35B ''protection'':9B ''quality'':10B ''skyforg'':40B ''steel'':42B ''strips'':51B ''symbols'':26B ''tempered/improved'':55B ''the'':39B ''using'':57B ''visual'':12B ''with'':18B,24B ''workbench'':61B ''worn'':29B', 'blacksmith', 'Ancient Nord Helmet has good protection quality. Its visual design is iconic and imposing, with a horned metal design etched with Nordic symbols and a worn, battle-hardened finish. Can only be crafted at the Skyforge, 3 steel ingots, 2 iron ingots, 2 leather, 3 leather strips. It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ash_creep_cluster', 'Ash Creep Cluster is a unique red ingredient from Solstheim, distinguished by its yellow-tan color and distinct alchemical properties compared to the mainland creep cluster. Alchemy effects: Damage Stamina, Invisibility, Resist Fire, and Fortify Destruction.', '''alchemical'':23B ''alchemy'':31B ''and'':21B,38B ''ash'':1A,4B ''by'':15B ''clust'':3A,6B,30B ''color'':20B ''compar'':25B ''creep'':2A,5B,29B ''damag'':33B ''destruction'':40B ''distinct'':22B ''distinguish'':14B ''effects'':32B ''fir'':37B ''fortify'':39B ''from'':12B ''ingredient'':11B ''invisibility'':35B ''is'':7B ''its'':16B ''mainland'':28B ''properti'':24B ''red'':10B ''resist'':36B ''solstheim'':13B ''stamin'':34B ''tan'':19B ''the'':27B ''to'':26B ''uniqu'':9B ''yellow'':18B ''yellow-t'':17B', 'alchemist', 'Ash Creep Cluster is a unique red ingredient from Solstheim, distinguished by its yellow-tan color and distinct alchemical properties compared to the mainland creep cluster. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('corrundum', 'Corundum is a valuable metal used primarily for creating stronger alloys in the crafting of weapons and armor. When mixed with iron, it produces steel, a widely utilized material known for its durability. The most common alloy consists of equal parts of iron and corundum, while smaller amounts can enhance the strength of lower-quality alloys, such as those used in banded iron armor. Additionally, by incorporating extra corundum into steel, blacksmiths can forge advanced armors, including scaled and steel plate varieties.', '''additionally'':67B ''advanc'':77B ''alloy'':38B ''alloys'':12B,58B ''amounts'':49B ''and'':18B,45B,81B ''armor'':19B,66B ''armors'':78B ''as'':60B ''band'':64B ''blacksmiths'':74B ''by'':68B ''can'':50B,75B ''common'':37B ''consists'':39B ''corrundum'':1A ''corundum'':2B,46B,71B ''crafting'':15B ''creating'':10B ''durability'':34B ''enhanc'':51B ''equal'':41B ''extra'':70B ''for'':9B,32B ''forg'':76B ''in'':13B,63B ''including'':79B ''incorporating'':69B ''into'':72B ''iron'':23B,44B,65B ''is'':3B ''it'':24B ''its'':33B ''known'':31B ''low'':56B ''lower-quality'':55B ''material'':30B ''metal'':6B ''mix'':21B ''most'':36B ''of'':16B,40B,43B,54B ''parts'':42B ''plat'':83B ''primarily'':8B ''produc'':25B ''quality'':57B ''scal'':80B ''small'':48B ''steel'':26B,73B,82B ''strength'':53B ''strong'':11B ''such'':59B ''the'':14B,35B,52B ''thos'':61B ''used'':7B,62B ''utiliz'':29B ''valuabl'':5B ''varieti'':84B ''weapons'':17B ''when'':20B ''whil'':47B ''widely'':28B ''with'':22B', 'blacksmith', 'Corundum is a valuable metal used primarily for creating stronger alloys in the crafting of weapons and armor. ', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonbone', 'Dragon items are high-quality armor and weapons made from dragon parts, including light Dragonscale Armor and heavy Dragonplate Armor. These can be crafted with the Dragon Armor perk, which requires a master Blacksmith .', '''and'':9B,19B ''are'':4B ''armor'':8B,18B,22B,30B ''be'':25B ''blacksmith'':36B ''can'':24B ''craft'':26B ''dragon'':2B,13B,29B ''dragonbon'':1A ''dragonplat'':21B ''dragonscal'':17B ''from'':12B ''heavy'':20B ''high'':6B ''high-quality'':5B ''including'':15B ''items'':3B ''light'':16B ''mad'':11B ''mast'':35B ''parts'':14B ''perk'':31B ''quality'':7B ''requir'':33B ''the'':28B ''thes'':23B ''weapons'':10B ''which'':32B ''with'':27B', 'blacksmith', 'Dragon Bone is used to craft powerful dragon armor and weapons from only the most masterful blacksmiths.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stalhrim', '
Stalhrim is a rare, enchanted ice found only on the island of Solstheim. It has a rich history, initially used in ancient Nordic burial rituals to encase the deceased as a form of protection, and later as a crafting material for weapons, armor, clothing, and jewelry. Stalhrim armor can be made in light or heavy variants and is known for its impressive protection. It also enhances frost enchantments, making them more powerful.

Described as a rigid, blue-white crystalline metal, stalhrim is as hard as iron and nearly indestructible by conventional means. The only way to mine it is with an ancient Nordic pickaxe, crafted with superior skill. In addition to its use in armor and crafting, raw stalhrim can be used in alchemy to induce paralysis and inflict frost damage. Working with stalhrim is similar to ebony smithing and requires the expertise of a skilled blacksmith.', '''addition'':112B ''alchemy'':126B ''also'':66B ''an'':103B ''ancient'':23B,104B ''and'':36B,46B,58B,89B,118B,130B,142B ''armor'':44B,49B,117B ''as'':31B,38B,75B,85B,87B ''be'':51B,123B ''blacksmith'':149B ''blu'':79B ''blue-whit'':78B ''burial'':25B ''by'':92B ''can'':50B,122B ''clothing'':45B ''conventional'':93B ''craft'':107B ''crafting'':40B,119B ''crystallin'':81B ''damag'':133B ''deceas'':30B ''describ'':74B ''ebony'':140B ''encas'':28B ''enchant'':6B ''enchantments'':69B ''enhanc'':67B ''expertis'':145B ''for'':42B,61B ''form'':33B ''found'':8B ''frost'':68B,132B ''hard'':86B ''heavy'':56B ''history'':19B ''ice'':7B ''impressiv'':63B ''in'':22B,53B,111B,116B,125B ''indestruct'':91B ''induc'':128B ''inflict'':131B ''initially'':20B ''iron'':88B ''is'':3B,59B,84B,101B,137B ''island'':12B ''it'':15B,65B,100B ''its'':62B,114B ''jewelry'':47B ''known'':60B ''lat'':37B ''light'':54B ''mad'':52B ''making'':70B ''material'':41B ''means'':94B ''metal'':82B ''min'':99B ''mor'':72B ''nearly'':90B ''nordic'':24B,105B ''of'':13B,34B,146B ''on'':10B ''only'':9B,96B ''or'':55B ''paralysis'':129B ''pickax'':106B ''powerful'':73B ''protection'':35B,64B ''rar'':5B ''raw'':120B ''requir'':143B ''rich'':18B ''rig'':77B ''rituals'':26B ''simil'':138B ''skill'':110B,148B ''smithing'':141B ''solstheim'':14B ''stalhrim'':1A,2B,48B,83B,121B,136B ''superior'':109B ''the'':11B,29B,95B,144B ''them'':71B ''to'':27B,98B,113B,127B,139B ''use'':115B ''used'':21B,124B ''variants'':57B ''way'':97B ''weapons'':43B ''whit'':80B ''with'':102B,108B,135B ''working'':134B', 'blacksmith, skaal', 'Stalhrim is a rare, enchanted ice found only on the island of Solstheim. It has a rich history, initially used in ancient Nordic burial rituals to encase the deceased as a form of protection, and later as a crafting material for weapons, armor, clothing, and jewelry. Stalhrim armor can be made in light or heavy variants and is known for its impressive protection. It also enhances frost enchantments, making them more powerful.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ebony', 'Ebony is a rare and valuable volcanic glass found primarily in Vvardenfell, particularly in the lava flows from Red Mountain. It is also located in smaller quantities in regions such as Solstheim, Skyrim, Cyrodiil, and High Rock. Known for its durability and strength, ebony is often referred to as "Godsblood," believed to be the crystallized essence of a deity, particularly Lorkhan. The material is highly sought after for crafting weapons and armor, notably forming a significant part of both Daedric and Dunmer designs.', '''after'':68B ''also'':24B ''and'':6B,36B,43B,72B,82B ''armor'':73B ''as'':32B,50B ''be'':54B ''believ'':52B ''both'':80B ''crafting'':70B ''crystalliz'':56B ''cyrodiil'':35B ''daedric'':81B ''deity'':60B ''designs'':84B ''dunm'':83B ''durability'':42B ''ebony'':1A,2B,45B ''essenc'':57B ''flows'':18B ''for'':40B,69B ''forming'':75B ''found'':10B ''from'':19B ''glass'':9B ''godsblood'':51B ''high'':37B ''highly'':66B ''in'':12B,15B,26B,29B ''is'':3B,23B,46B,65B ''it'':22B ''its'':41B ''known'':39B ''lav'':17B ''locat'':25B ''lorkh'':62B ''material'':64B ''mountain'':21B ''notably'':74B ''of'':58B,79B ''often'':47B ''part'':78B ''particularly'':14B,61B ''primarily'':11B ''quantiti'':28B ''rar'':5B ''red'':20B ''referr'':48B ''regions'':30B ''rock'':38B ''significant'':77B ''skyrim'':34B ''small'':27B ''solstheim'':33B ''sought'':67B ''strength'':44B ''such'':31B ''the'':16B,55B,63B ''to'':49B,53B ''valuabl'':7B ''volcanic'':8B ''vvardenfell'':13B ''weapons'':71B', 'blacksmith, darkelf', 'Ebony is a rare and valuable volcanic glass found primarily in Vvardenfell in Morrowind. It is used to create powerful weapons and armor.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('malachite', 'Malachite is a rare volcanic crystal known for its distinctive milky translucent green color and its ability to absorb magicka under certain conditions. It is primarily utilized in crafting lightweight yet strong armor and weapons, making it a favored material among skilled artisans. Though less durable than ebony, malachite boasts a higher melting point and is significantly stronger than common glass, which it is often mistakenly associated with. The most abundant sources of malachite are found on the volcanic island of Vvardenfell in Morrowind, but ore veins are also distributed across Tamriel.', '''ability'':18B ''absorb'':20B ''abundant'':72B ''across'':92B ''also'':90B ''among'':42B ''and'':16B,35B,56B ''are'':76B,89B ''armor'':34B ''artisans'':44B ''associat'':68B ''boasts'':51B ''but'':86B ''certain'':23B ''color'':15B ''common'':61B ''conditions'':24B ''crafting'':30B ''crystal'':7B ''distinctiv'':11B ''distribut'':91B ''durabl'':47B ''ebony'':49B ''favor'':40B ''for'':9B ''found'':77B ''glass'':62B ''gre'':14B ''high'':53B ''in'':29B,84B ''is'':3B,26B,57B,65B ''island'':81B ''it'':25B,38B,64B ''its'':10B,17B ''known'':8B ''less'':46B ''lightweight'':31B ''magick'':21B ''making'':37B ''malachit'':1A,2B,50B,75B ''material'':41B ''melting'':54B ''milky'':12B ''mistakenly'':67B ''morrowind'':85B ''most'':71B ''of'':74B,82B ''often'':66B ''on'':78B ''ore'':87B ''point'':55B ''primarily'':27B ''rar'':5B ''significantly'':58B ''skill'':43B ''sourc'':73B ''strong'':33B,59B ''tamriel'':93B ''than'':48B,60B ''the'':70B,79B ''though'':45B ''to'':19B ''translucent'':13B ''under'':22B ''utiliz'':28B ''veins'':88B ''volcanic'':6B,80B ''vvardenfell'':83B ''weapons'':36B ''which'':63B ''with'':69B ''yet'':32B', 'blacksmith, darkelf', 'Malachite is a rare volcanic crystal known for its distinctive milky translucent green color and its ability to absorb magicka. I.t is primarily utilized in crafting lightweight yet strong armor and weapons.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('holy_water', 'Holy Water is referenced in tales and songs, often as a joke or a mythical substance associated with divine protection.', '''and'':9B ''as'':12B ''associat'':19B ''divin'':21B ''holy'':1A,3B ''in'':7B ''is'':5B ''jok'':14B ''mythical'':17B ''often'':11B ''or'':15B ''protection'':22B ''referenc'':6B ''songs'':10B ''substanc'':18B ''tal'':8B ''wat'':2A,4B ''with'':20B', 'sanguine', 'You know nothing about this and suspect it may be an invention of a bard’s tale.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('moonstone', 'Moonstone is a rare ivory-colored metal found in veins throughout Tamriel, prized for its unique properties and applications in crafting. Primarily, it is used in the creation of elven armor, often combined with quicksilver, a practice that was historically guarded as a secret by the Altmer of Summerset. The crafting process is complex due to moonstone''s higher melting point compared to quicksilver, necessitating careful handling to ensure the materials fuse properly.', '''altmer'':49B ''and'':20B ''applications'':21B ''armor'':33B ''as'':44B ''by'':47B ''careful'':68B ''color'':8B ''combin'':35B ''compar'':64B ''complex'':56B ''crafting'':23B,53B ''creation'':30B ''due'':57B ''elven'':32B ''ensur'':71B ''for'':16B ''found'':10B ''fus'':74B ''guard'':43B ''handling'':69B ''high'':61B ''historically'':42B ''in'':11B,22B,28B ''is'':3B,26B,55B ''it'':25B ''its'':17B ''ivory'':7B ''ivory-color'':6B ''materials'':73B ''melting'':62B ''metal'':9B ''moonston'':1A,2B,59B ''necessitating'':67B ''of'':31B,50B ''often'':34B ''point'':63B ''practic'':39B ''primarily'':24B ''priz'':15B ''process'':54B ''properly'':75B ''properti'':19B ''quicksilv'':37B,66B ''rar'':5B ''s'':60B ''secret'':46B ''summerset'':51B ''tamriel'':14B ''that'':40B ''the'':29B,48B,52B,72B ''throughout'':13B ''to'':58B,65B,70B ''uniqu'':18B ''used'':27B ''veins'':12B ''was'':41B ''with'':36B', 'blacksmith, highelf', 'Moonstone is a rare ivory-colored metal found in veins throughout Tamriel, prized for its unique properties and applications in crafting. Primarily, it is used in the creation of elven armor.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orichalcum', 'Orichalcum, also known as orichalc, is a gray-green metal renowned for its use in crafting weapons and armor, particularly by the Orcs, who are celebrated for their orichalcum equipment. The metal is typically melded with iron at low temperatures to maintain its strength and prevent brittleness. Orcish armor, which is often crafted with superior skill, is characterized as medium to heavy in weight, while orichalcum weapons are less common and can vary in quality.', '''also'':3B ''and'':20B,47B,73B ''are'':27B,70B ''armor'':21B,51B ''as'':5B,61B ''at'':40B ''brittleness'':49B ''by'':23B ''can'':74B ''celebrat'':28B ''characteriz'':60B ''common'':72B ''craft'':55B ''crafting'':18B ''equipment'':32B ''for'':14B,29B ''gray'':10B ''gray-gr'':9B ''gre'':11B ''heavy'':64B ''in'':17B,65B,76B ''iron'':39B ''is'':7B,35B,53B,59B ''its'':15B,45B ''known'':4B ''less'':71B ''low'':41B ''maintain'':44B ''medium'':62B ''meld'':37B ''metal'':12B,34B ''often'':54B ''orcish'':50B ''orcs'':25B ''orichalc'':6B ''orichalcum'':1A,2B,31B,68B ''particularly'':22B ''prevent'':48B ''quality'':77B ''renown'':13B ''skill'':58B ''strength'':46B ''superior'':57B ''temperatur'':42B ''the'':24B,30B,33B ''to'':43B,63B ''typically'':36B ''use'':16B ''vary'':75B ''weapons'':19B,69B ''weight'':66B ''which'':52B ''whil'':67B ''who'':26B ''with'':38B,56B', 'blacksmith, orc', 'Orichalcum, also known as orichalc, is a gray-green metal renowned for its use in crafting weapons and armor, particularly by the Orcs, who are celebrated for their orichalcum equipment.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ustengrav_puzzle', 'Three rounded stones are found in a staggered row in front of a portcullis gate. The stones glow red and making a chiming noise when you stand close to them. When all three stones are active, the portcullis opens for a few seconds.
