INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tiid_klo_ul', 'Slow Time is a Shout that commands time itself to obey, causing the world around you to stand still while you move at normal speed. The three words of power in this Shout are Tiid (Time), which controls the flow of time; Klo (Sand), which symbolizes the slow passage of time, like grains of sand slipping away; and Ul (Eternity), which extends the effect, allowing time to remain frozen for a longer duration.', '''allowing'':68B ''and'':61B ''are'':37B ''around'':18B ''at'':26B ''away'':60B ''causing'':15B ''commands'':10B ''controls'':41B ''duration'':76B ''effect'':67B ''eternity'':63B ''extends'':65B ''flow'':43B ''for'':73B ''froz'':72B ''grains'':56B ''in'':34B ''is'':6B ''itself'':12B ''klo'':2A,46B ''lik'':55B ''long'':75B ''mov'':25B ''normal'':27B ''obey'':14B ''of'':32B,44B,53B,57B ''passag'':52B ''pow'':33B ''remain'':71B ''sand'':47B,58B ''shout'':8B,36B ''slipping'':59B ''slow'':4B,51B ''spe'':28B ''stand'':21B ''still'':22B ''symboliz'':49B ''that'':9B ''the'':16B,29B,42B,50B,66B ''this'':35B ''thre'':30B ''tiid'':1A,38B ''tim'':5B,11B,39B,45B,54B,69B ''to'':13B,20B,70B ''ul'':3A,62B ''which'':40B,48B,64B ''whil'':23B ''words'':31B ''world'':17B ''you'':19B,24B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('transmute', 'Transmute is an Alteration spell that converts one piece of unrefined iron ore into silver ore or silver ore into gold ore. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''alteration'':5B ''an'':4B,26B ''apprentic'':27B ''cast'':31B ''converts'':8B ''gold'':22B ''into'':15B,21B ''iron'':13B ''is'':3B ''it'':24B ''level'':29B ''of'':11B ''one'':9B ''or'':18B ''ore'':14B,17B,20B,23B ''piec'':10B ''requir'':25B ''silv'':16B,19B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':6B ''that'':7B ''to'':30B ''transmut'':1A,2B ''unrefin'':12B', 'mage', 'Transmute is a spell that changes iron ore into silver ore, or silver ore into gold ore, making the metals more valuable. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cod', 'Cod are a large yellow fish found in freezing waters during any weather. They can be eaten with a mild, delicate, and slightly sweet flavor with a flaky texture.', '''and'':23B ''any'':13B ''are'':3B ''be'':17B ''can'':16B ''cod'':1A,2B ''delicat'':22B ''during'':12B ''eat'':18B ''fish'':7B ''flaky'':29B ''flavor'':26B ''found'':8B ''freezing'':10B ''in'':9B ''larg'':5B ''mild'':21B ''slightly'':24B ''sweet'':25B ''textur'':30B ''they'':15B ''waters'':11B ''weath'':14B ''with'':19B,27B ''yellow'':6B', 'fisher', 'Cod are a large yellow fish. They can be eaten with a mild, delicate, and slightly sweet flavor with a flaky texture. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('transmute_mineral_ore', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Alteration spells that transform iron ore into silver ore and silver ore into gold ore. This effect is only available as a spell, offering resourceful adventurers a way to increase the value of raw materials for crafting or trade.', '''adventurers'':36B ''alteration'':11B ''and'':20B ''are'':7B ''as'':31B ''avail'':30B ''crafting'':47B ''effect'':27B ''effects'':6B ''focus'':10B ''for'':46B ''gold'':24B ''incre'':40B ''into'':17B,23B ''iron'':15B ''is'':28B ''magical'':5B ''materials'':45B ''mineral'':2A ''of'':43B ''offering'':34B ''only'':29B ''or'':48B ''ore'':3A,16B,19B,22B,25B ''raw'':44B ''resourceful'':35B ''silv'':18B,21B ''spell'':33B ''spells'':12B ''that'':13B ''the'':41B ''thes'':4B ''this'':26B ''to'':39B ''trad'':49B ''transform'':14B ''transmut'':1A ''utility'':9B ''utility-focus'':8B ''valu'':42B ''way'':38B', 'mage', 'This spell turns iron into silver and silver into gold, useful for making money or fancy things. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('turn_greater_undead', 'Turn Greater Undead is a Restoration spell that causes powerful undead creatures, such as Draugr Deathlords and Liches, to flee in terror, rendering them temporarily neutralized. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''an'':32B ''and'':20B ''as'':17B ''cast'':37B ''caus'':12B ''creatur'':15B ''deathlords'':19B ''draugr'':18B ''expert'':33B ''fle'':23B ''great'':2A,5B ''in'':24B ''is'':7B ''it'':30B ''level'':35B ''lich'':21B ''neutraliz'':29B ''powerful'':13B ''rendering'':26B ''requir'':31B ''restoration'':9B ''skill'':34B ''spell'':10B ''such'':16B ''temporarily'':28B ''terror'':25B ''that'':11B ''them'':27B ''to'':22B,36B ''turn'':1A,4B ''unde'':3A,6B,14B', 'mage', 'Repel Undead is a spell that forces undead creatures to flee in terror, effectively neutralizing them for a short period. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('turn_lesser_undead', 'Turn Lesser Undead is a Restoration spell that forces weaker undead creatures to flee in terror, making them temporarily neutralized. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''an'':26B ''apprentic'':27B ''cast'':31B ''creatur'':15B ''fle'':17B ''forc'':12B ''in'':18B ''is'':7B ''it'':24B ''less'':2A,5B ''level'':29B ''making'':20B ''neutraliz'':23B ''requir'':25B ''restoration'':9B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':10B ''temporarily'':22B ''terror'':19B ''that'':11B ''them'':21B ''to'':16B,30B ''turn'':1A,4B ''unde'':3A,6B,14B ''weak'':13B', 'mage', '
Turn Lesser Undead is a spell that forces weaker undead creatures to flee in terror, temporarily neutralizing them. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('turn_undead', 'These magical effects are offensive Restoration spells that force undead creatures to flee in fear, ensuring they cannot approach or attack the caster. This effect is available as a spell and can also be found on enchanted weapons and gear, making it a sacred tool of Arkay;s faithful.', '''also'':35B ''and'':33B,41B ''approach'':21B ''are'':6B ''arkay'':49B ''as'':30B ''attack'':23B ''avail'':29B ''be'':36B ''can'':34B ''cannot'':20B ''cast'':25B ''creatur'':13B ''effect'':27B ''effects'':5B ''enchant'':39B ''ensuring'':18B ''faithful'':51B ''fear'':17B ''fle'':15B ''forc'':11B ''found'':37B ''gear'':42B ''in'':16B ''is'':28B ''it'':44B ''magical'':4B ''making'':43B ''of'':48B ''offensiv'':7B ''on'':38B ''or'':22B ''restoration'':8B ''s'':50B ''sacr'':46B ''spell'':32B ''spells'':9B ''that'':10B ''the'':24B ''thes'':3B ''they'':19B ''this'':26B ''to'':14B ''tool'':47B ''turn'':1A ''unde'':2A,12B ''weapons'':40B', 'mage', 'This spell scares undead creatures, making them run away instead of attacking. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('unrelenting_force', 'Unrelenting Force is a Shout that uses raw power to push aside anything or anyone in your path. The three words of power in this Shout are Fus (Force), which unleashes the power of your voice; Ro (Balance), which knocks back enemies and objects; and Dah (Push), which sends your target flying, clearing your way.', '''and'':45B,47B ''anyon'':17B ''anything'':15B ''are'':29B ''asid'':14B ''back'':43B ''balanc'':40B ''clearing'':55B ''dah'':48B ''enemi'':44B ''flying'':54B ''forc'':2A,4B,31B ''fus'':30B ''in'':18B,26B ''is'':5B ''knocks'':42B ''objects'':46B ''of'':24B,36B ''or'':16B ''path'':20B ''pow'':11B,25B,35B ''push'':13B,49B ''raw'':10B ''ro'':39B ''sends'':51B ''shout'':7B,28B ''target'':53B ''that'':8B ''the'':21B,34B ''this'':27B ''thre'':22B ''to'':12B ''unleash'':33B ''unrelenting'':1A,3B ''uses'':9B ''voic'':38B ''way'':57B ''which'':32B,41B,50B ''words'':23B ''your'':19B,37B,52B,56B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vampire''s_bane', 'Vampire''s Bane is a Restoration spell that unleashes a burst of light, dealing damage to vampires and healing the caster if the target is a vampire. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':34B ''an'':33B ''and'':21B ''ban'':3A,6B ''burst'':14B ''cast'':24B,38B ''damag'':18B ''dealing'':17B ''healing'':22B ''if'':25B ''is'':7B,28B ''it'':31B ''level'':36B ''light'':16B ''of'':15B ''requir'':32B ''restoration'':9B ''s'':2A,5B ''skill'':35B ''spell'':10B ''target'':27B ''that'':11B ''the'':23B,26B ''to'':19B,37B ''unleash'':12B ''vampir'':1A,4B,20B,30B', 'mage', 'Vampire''s Bane is a spell that releases a burst of light, dealing damage to vampires and healing the caster if the target is a vampire. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vampiric_drain', 'Vampiric Drain is a Destruction spell that drains the life force from a target, restoring health to the caster while dealing damage to the enemy. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''an'':30B ''apprentic'':31B ''cast'':21B,35B ''damag'':24B ''dealing'':23B ''destruction'':7B ''drain'':2A,4B ''drains'':10B ''enemy'':27B ''forc'':13B ''from'':14B ''health'':18B ''is'':5B ''it'':28B ''level'':33B ''lif'':12B ''requir'':29B ''restoring'':17B ''skill'':32B ''spell'':8B ''target'':16B ''that'':9B ''the'':11B,20B,26B ''to'':19B,25B,34B ''vampiric'':1A,3B ''whil'':22B', 'mage', '
Vampiric Drain is a spell that drains the life force from a target, restoring health to the caster while dealing damage to the enemy. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vampirism', 'Vampirism is a disease that transforms individuals into blood-drinking creatures of the night. The disease is contracted through encounters with vampires, typically when they use a draining power, with a chance of infection. Initially, the disease causes a slight reduction in health and can be easily cured. However, if not treated within a few days, the disease progresses into full vampirism, which becomes irreversible. In some cases, individuals can be turned into vampires through specific rituals or encounters, gaining special powers.

Vampirism changes the appearance of the afflicted significantly. Those transformed develop dark, reddish eyes, pale skin, fangs, and gaunt faces. Certain races have additional physical traits, such as slitted pupils or multiple sets of fangs, and their skin or fur becomes paler. In some instances, vampirism causes even more monstrous features, including bat-like characteristics. Vampires are generally feared and despised, with the most advanced stages of vampirism leading to hostility from others. 

Vampirism in Tamriel is a curse originating from Molag Bal, the Daedric Prince of Domination, who created the first vampire, Lamae Beolfag, after violating her. Her transformation into a vampire spread across Tamriel, making a mockery of the Aedra Arkay’s sphere of life and death. While the traditional belief traces vampirism back to Molag Bal, other stories suggest it can be caused by magical artifacts, curses, or necromancy, with variations in regional lore. Some alchemists have even replicated the disease through experimentation, creating new strains of vampirism, such as Chaotica Vampiris, which transforms afflicted individuals into monstrous forms. Vampires'' bloodlines can vary greatly, with some strains possessing unique traits, and many are linked to Daedric energies, regardless of their origin. The result is always the same: an undead creature that shuns sunlight and craves blood.', '''across'':190B ''additional'':108B ''advanc'':150B ''aedr'':197B ''afflict'':91B,253B ''after'':181B ''alchemists'':234B ''always'':283B ''an'':286B ''and'':46B,102B,120B,145B,203B,269B,292B ''appearanc'':88B ''are'':142B,271B ''arkay'':198B ''artifacts'':224B ''as'':112B,248B ''back'':211B ''bal'':168B,214B ''bat'':138B ''bat-lik'':137B ''be'':48B,73B,220B ''becom'':66B,125B ''belief'':208B ''beolfag'':180B ''blood'':11B,294B ''blood-drinking'':10B ''bloodlin'':259B ''by'':222B ''can'':47B,72B,219B,260B ''cas'':70B ''caus'':40B,131B,221B ''certain'':105B ''chanc'':34B ''chang'':86B ''chaotic'':249B ''characteristics'':140B ''contract'':20B ''crav'':293B ''creat'':175B ''creating'':242B ''creatur'':13B,288B ''cur'':50B ''curs'':164B,225B ''daedric'':170B,274B ''dark'':96B ''days'':58B ''death'':204B ''despis'':146B ''develop'':95B ''dis'':5B,18B,39B,60B,239B ''domination'':173B ''draining'':30B ''drinking'':12B ''easily'':49B ''encounters'':22B,81B ''energi'':275B ''even'':132B,236B ''experimentation'':241B ''eyes'':98B ''fac'':104B ''fangs'':101B,119B ''fear'':144B ''featur'':135B ''few'':57B ''first'':177B ''forms'':257B ''from'':157B,166B ''full'':63B ''fur'':124B ''gaining'':82B ''gaunt'':103B ''generally'':143B ''greatly'':262B ''hav'':107B,235B ''health'':45B ''her'':183B,184B ''hostility'':156B ''howev'':51B ''if'':52B ''in'':44B,68B,127B,160B,230B ''including'':136B ''individuals'':8B,71B,254B ''infection'':36B ''initially'':37B ''instanc'':129B ''into'':9B,62B,75B,186B,255B ''irrevers'':67B ''is'':3B,19B,162B,282B ''it'':218B ''lama'':179B ''leading'':154B ''lif'':202B ''lik'':139B ''link'':272B ''lor'':232B ''magical'':223B ''making'':192B ''many'':270B ''mockery'':194B ''molag'':167B,213B ''monstrous'':134B,256B ''mor'':133B ''most'':149B ''multipl'':116B ''necromancy'':227B ''new'':243B ''night'':16B ''not'':53B ''of'':14B,35B,89B,118B,152B,172B,195B,201B,245B,277B ''or'':80B,115B,123B,226B ''origin'':279B ''originating'':165B ''other'':215B ''others'':158B ''pal'':99B,126B ''physical'':109B ''possessing'':266B ''pow'':31B ''powers'':84B ''princ'':171B ''progress'':61B ''pupils'':114B ''rac'':106B ''reddish'':97B ''reduction'':43B ''regardless'':276B ''regional'':231B ''replicat'':237B ''result'':281B ''rituals'':79B ''s'':199B ''sam'':285B ''sets'':117B ''shuns'':290B ''significantly'':92B ''skin'':100B,122B ''slight'':42B ''slitt'':113B ''som'':69B,128B,233B,264B ''special'':83B ''specific'':78B ''spher'':200B ''spre'':189B ''stag'':151B ''stori'':216B ''strains'':244B,265B ''such'':111B,247B ''suggest'':217B ''sunlight'':291B ''tamriel'':161B,191B ''that'':6B,289B ''the'':15B,17B,38B,59B,87B,90B,121B,148B,169B,176B,196B,206B,238B,278B,280B,284B ''they'':27B ''thos'':93B ''through'':21B,77B,240B ''to'':155B,212B,273B ''trac'':209B ''traditional'':207B ''traits'':110B,268B ''transform'':94B ''transformation'':185B ''transforms'':7B,252B ''treat'':54B ''turn'':74B ''typically'':25B ''unde'':287B ''uniqu'':267B ''use'':28B ''vampir'':24B,76B,141B,178B,188B,258B ''vampiris'':250B ''vampirism'':1A,2B,64B,85B,130B,153B,159B,210B,