INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('flame_atronach', 'Flame Atronachs are elemental Daedra originating from the realm of Infernace, a fiery domain composed of lava and flames. These beings appear to be made entirely of fire and can be found either unbound in the wild or summoned by skilled mages to serve various roles, such as guards or laborers. The process of summoning Flame Atronachs typically involves the spell known as Koron''s Peremptory Summons, which allows conjurers to customize the specifics of the summon, including the Daedric form and the plane from which they are called.', '''allows'':71B ''and'':20B,31B,84B ''appe'':24B ''are'':5B,90B ''as'':50B,65B ''atronach'':2A ''atronachs'':4B,59B ''be'':26B,33B ''beings'':23B ''by'':42B ''call'':91B ''can'':32B ''comp'':17B ''conjurers'':72B ''customiz'':74B ''daedr'':7B ''daedric'':82B ''domain'':16B ''eith'':35B ''elemental'':6B ''entirely'':28B ''fiery'':15B ''fir'':30B ''flam'':1A,3B,21B,58B ''form'':83B ''found'':34B ''from'':9B,87B ''guards'':51B ''in'':37B ''including'':80B ''infernac'':13B ''involv'':61B ''known'':64B ''koron'':66B ''laborers'':53B ''lav'':19B ''mad'':27B ''mag'':44B ''of'':12B,18B,29B,56B,77B ''or'':40B,52B ''originating'':8B ''peremptory'':68B ''plan'':86B ''process'':55B ''realm'':11B ''rol'':48B ''s'':67B ''serv'':46B ''skill'':43B ''specifics'':76B ''spell'':63B ''such'':49B ''summon'':41B,79B ''summoning'':57B ''summons'':69B ''the'':10B,38B,54B,62B,75B,78B,81B,85B ''thes'':22B ''they'':89B ''to'':25B,45B,73B ''typically'':60B ''unbound'':36B ''various'':47B ''which'':70B,88B ''wild'':39B', 'mage, daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Flame Atronachs are elemental Daedra. These beings appear to be made entirely of fire and can be found either unbound in the wild.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frost_atronach', 'Frost Atronachs, also known as Ice Atronachs or Water Atronachs, are elemental Daedra that hail from the realm of Oblivion. Composed entirely of ice, these beings can be encountered unbound in the wild or summoned by skilled mages to fulfill various roles, including guards or laborers.', '''also'':5B ''are'':13B ''as'':7B ''atronach'':2A ''atronachs'':4B,9B,12B ''be'':30B ''beings'':28B ''by'':38B ''can'':29B ''comp'':23B ''daedr'':15B ''elemental'':14B ''encounter'':31B ''entirely'':24B ''from'':18B ''frost'':1A,3B ''fulfill'':42B ''guards'':46B ''hail'':17B ''ice'':8B,26B ''in'':33B ''including'':45B ''known'':6B ''laborers'':48B ''mag'':40B ''oblivion'':22B ''of'':21B,25B ''or'':10B,36B,47B ''realm'':20B ''rol'':44B ''skill'':39B ''summon'':37B ''that'':16B ''the'':19B,34B ''thes'':27B ''to'':41B ''unbound'':32B ''various'':43B ''wat'':11B ''wild'':35B', 'mage, daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Frost Atronachs, also known as Ice Atronachs or Water Atronachs. They can be found either unbound in the wild.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('storm_atronach', '
Storm Atronachs, sometimes referred to as Thundernachs, are elemental Daedra originating from the realm of Levinace. These formidable beings are composed of lightning and rocky debris, giving them a striking and chaotic appearance. Storm Atronachs can be found both unbound in the wild and summoned by skilled mages to serve various functions, such as guards or laborers. ', '''and'':26B,33B,46B ''appearanc'':35B ''are'':10B,22B ''as'':8B,56B ''atronach'':2A ''atronachs'':4B,37B ''be'':39B ''beings'':21B ''both'':41B ''by'':48B ''can'':38B ''chaotic'':34B ''comp'':23B ''daedr'':12B ''debris'':28B ''elemental'':11B ''formid'':20B ''found'':40B ''from'':14B ''functions'':54B ''giving'':29B ''guards'':57B ''in'':43B ''laborers'':59B ''levinac'':18B ''lightning'':25B ''mag'':50B ''of'':17B,24B ''or'':58B ''originating'':13B ''realm'':16B ''referr'':6B ''rocky'':27B ''serv'':52B ''skill'':49B ''sometim'':5B ''storm'':1A,3B,36B ''striking'':32B ''such'':55B ''summon'':47B ''the'':15B,44B ''them'':30B ''thes'':19B ''thundernachs'':9B ''to'':7B,51B ''unbound'':42B ''various'':53B ''wild'':45B', 'mage, daedra, daedric, scholar,', '
Storm Atronachs are elemental Daedra from the realm of Levinace, made of lightning and rocky debris.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('angelfish', 'Angelfish are rare orange fish with black stripes found in temperate lakes. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Regenerate Health, Resist Fire, Fortify Marksman, and Waterbreathing. ', '''an'':17B ''and'':33B ''angelfish'':1A,2B ''are'':3B ''as'':16B,26B ''black'':8B ''effects'':24B ''fir'':30B ''fish'':6B ''for'':19B ''fortify'':31B ''found'':10B ''health'':28B ''in'':11B ''ingredient'':18B ''lak'':13B ''making'':21B ''marksm'':32B ''offer'':23B ''orang'':5B ''potion'':20B ''rar'':4B ''regenerat'':27B ''resist'':29B ''strip'':9B ''such'':25B ''temperat'':12B ''they'':22B ''used'':15B ''waterbreathing'':34B ''when'':14B ''with'':7B', 'fisher', 'Angelfish are rare orange fish with black stripes. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_spider', 'Dwarven Spiders, also known as Dwemer Spiders or Centurion Spiders, are small mechanical constructs commonly found in the ruins of the Dwemer civilization. Resembling actual spiders, these versatile automatons serve multiple purposes, including guarding locations and performing repairs. They often scuttle around the ruins, and in certain areas, they can swarm out of hidden compartments to ambush intruders.', '''actual'':27B ''also'':5B ''ambush'':59B ''and'':38B,47B ''are'':13B,50B ''around'':44B ''as'':7B ''automatons'':31B ''can'':52B ''centurion'':11B ''certain'':49B ''civilization'':25B ''commonly'':17B ''compartments'':57B ''constructs'':16B ''dwarv'':1A,3B ''dwem'':8B,24B ''found'':18B ''guarding'':36B ''hidd'':56B ''in'':19B,48B ''including'':35B ''intruders'':60B ''known'':6B ''locations'':37B ''mechanical'':15B ''multipl'':33B ''of'':22B,55B ''often'':42B ''or'':10B ''out'':54B ''performing'':39B ''purp'':34B ''repairs'':40B ''resembling'':26B ''ruins'':21B,46B ''scuttl'':43B ''serv'':32B ''small'':14B ''spid'':2A ''spiders'':4B,9B,12B,28B ''swarm'':53B ''the'':20B,23B,45B ''thes'':29B ''they'':41B,51B ''to'':58B ''versatil'':30B', 'dwemer', '
Dwarven Spiders are mechanical constructs found in Dwemer ruins, resembling actual spiders, that will attack anyone foolish enough to enter a dwemer ruin.', '', '', 'creatures');
