INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_centurion', 'Dwarven Centurions, often referred to as Steam Centurions, are imposing and heavily armored constructs that serve as formidable guardians in Dwemer ruins. Equipped with either an extendable mace or hammer on one arm and a spring-loaded blade on the other, they can deliver devastating melee attacks. Some variants are capable of emitting a scalding blast of steam, enhancing their offensive capabilities. While not as common as smaller Dwarven constructs, their presence signifies heightened security within ancient ruins.', '''an'':28B ''ancient'':80B ''and'':13B,36B ''are'':11B,53B ''arm'':35B ''armor'':15B ''as'':8B,19B,68B,70B ''attacks'':50B ''blad'':41B ''blast'':59B ''can'':46B ''capabiliti'':65B ''capabl'':54B ''centurion'':2A ''centurions'':4B,10B ''common'':69B ''constructs'':16B,73B ''deliv'':47B ''devastating'':48B ''dwarv'':1A,3B,72B ''dwem'':23B ''eith'':27B ''emitting'':56B ''enhancing'':62B ''equipp'':25B ''extend'':29B ''formid'':20B ''guardians'':21B ''hamm'':32B ''heavily'':14B ''heighten'':77B ''imposing'':12B ''in'':22B ''load'':40B ''mac'':30B ''mele'':49B ''not'':67B ''of'':55B,60B ''offensiv'':64B ''often'':5B ''on'':33B,42B ''one'':34B ''or'':31B ''other'':44B ''presenc'':75B ''referr'':6B ''ruins'':24B,81B ''scalding'':58B ''security'':78B ''serv'':18B ''signifi'':76B ''small'':71B ''som'':51B ''spring'':39B ''spring-load'':38B ''steam'':9B,61B ''that'':17B ''the'':43B,63B,74B ''they'':45B ''to'':7B ''variants'':52B ''whil'':66B ''with'':26B ''within'':79B', 'dwemer', '
Dwarven Centurions, or Steam Centurions, are heavily armored constructs found in Dwemer ruins,, that will attack anyone foolish enough to enter a dwemer ruin.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('arctic_char', 'Arctic Char are long blue and green fish uncommonly found in freezing waters. They can be eaten with a mild, delicate, and slightly sweet flavor.', '''and'':8B,24B ''arctic'':1A,3B ''are'':5B ''be'':18B ''blu'':7B ''can'':17B ''char'':2A,4B ''delicat'':23B ''eat'':19B ''fish'':10B ''flavor'':27B ''found'':12B ''freezing'':14B ''gre'':9B ''in'':13B ''long'':6B ''mild'':22B ''slightly'':25B ''sweet'':26B ''they'':16B ''uncommonly'':11B ''waters'':15B ''with'':20B', 'fisher', 'Arctic Char are long blue and green fish. They can be eaten with a mild, delicate, and slightly sweet flavor. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwemer_centurion', 'Dwarven Centurions, often referred to as Steam Centurions, are imposing and heavily armored constructs that serve as formidable guardians in Dwemer ruins. Equipped with either an extendable mace or hammer on one arm and a spring-loaded blade on the other, they can deliver devastating melee attacks. Some variants are capable of emitting a scalding blast of steam, enhancing their offensive capabilities. While not as common as smaller Dwarven constructs, their presence signifies heightened security within ancient ruins.', '''an'':28B ''ancient'':80B ''and'':13B,36B ''are'':11B,53B ''arm'':35B ''armor'':15B ''as'':8B,19B,68B,70B ''attacks'':50B ''blad'':41B ''blast'':59B ''can'':46B ''capabiliti'':65B ''capabl'':54B ''centurion'':2A ''centurions'':4B,10B ''common'':69B ''constructs'':16B,73B ''deliv'':47B ''devastating'':48B ''dwarv'':3B,72B ''dwem'':1A,23B ''eith'':27B ''emitting'':56B ''enhancing'':62B ''equipp'':25B ''extend'':29B ''formid'':20B ''guardians'':21B ''hamm'':32B ''heavily'':14B ''heighten'':77B ''imposing'':12B ''in'':22B ''load'':40B ''mac'':30B ''mele'':49B ''not'':67B ''of'':55B,60B ''offensiv'':64B ''often'':5B ''on'':33B,42B ''one'':34B ''or'':31B ''other'':44B ''presenc'':75B ''referr'':6B ''ruins'':24B,81B ''scalding'':58B ''security'':78B ''serv'':18B ''signifi'':76B ''small'':71B ''som'':51B ''spring'':39B ''spring-load'':38B ''steam'':9B,61B ''that'':17B ''the'':43B,63B,74B ''they'':45B ''to'':7B ''variants'':52B ''whil'':66B ''with'':26B ''within'':79B', 'dwemer', '
Dwarven Centurions, or Steam Centurions, are heavily armored constructs found in Dwemer ruins, that will attack anyone foolish enough to enter a dwemer ruin.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chaurus', 'Chaurus are medium-to-large, hostile creatures resembling earwigs, commonly found in swamps, marshlands, and deep underground caverns throughout Tamriel. Known for their aggressive nature, Chaurus possess a potent acidic poison that they can project with remarkable accuracy, capable of quickly eroding most forms of armor. Their ability to cling to walls adds to their menace, as they can ambush unsuspecting prey from above.', '''ability'':50B ''abov'':66B ''accuracy'':40B ''acidic'':32B ''adds'':55B ''aggressiv'':26B ''ambush'':62B ''and'':17B ''are'':3B ''armor'':48B ''as'':59B ''can'':36B,61B ''capabl'':41B ''caverns'':20B ''chaurus'':1A,2B,28B ''cling'':52B ''commonly'':12B ''creatur'':9B ''deep'':18B ''earwigs'':11B ''eroding'':44B ''for'':24B ''forms'':46B ''found'':13B ''from'':65B ''hostil'':8B ''in'':14B ''known'':23B ''larg'':7B ''marshlands'':16B ''medium'':5B ''medium-to-larg'':4B ''menac'':58B ''most'':45B ''natur'':27B ''of'':42B,47B ''poison'':33B ''possess'':29B ''potent'':31B ''prey'':64B ''project'':37B ''quickly'':43B ''remark'':39B ''resembling'':10B ''swamps'':15B ''tamriel'':22B ''that'':34B ''the'':25B,49B,57B ''they'':35B,60B ''throughout'':21B ''to'':6B,51B,53B,56B ''underground'':19B ''unsuspecting'':63B ''walls'':54B ''with'':38B', 'dwemer', '
Chaurus are hostile, earwig-like creatures found in swamps and underground caverns. They are known for their aggressive behavior, acidic poison, and ability to cling to walls to ambush prey.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragon', 'Dragons are formidable, flying reptilian creatures native to Skyrim, revered and feared for their immense power and intelligence. Historically worshipped by the ancient Nordic people, dragons possess an affinity for magic and can harness the power of the Thu''um, or Dragon Shouts, to unleash devastating attacks. While thought to be extinct, dragons have begun to re-emerge, playing a central role in the events unfolding across the province.', '''across'':69B ''affinity'':30B ''an'':29B ''ancient'':24B ''and'':12B,18B,33B ''are'':3B ''attacks'':48B ''be'':52B ''begun'':56B ''by'':22B ''can'':34B ''central'':63B ''creatur'':7B ''devastating'':47B ''dragon'':1A,43B ''dragons'':2B,27B,54B ''emerg'':60B ''events'':67B ''extinct'':53B ''fear'':13B ''flying'':5B ''for'':14B,31B ''formid'':4B ''harness'':35B ''hav'':55B ''historically'':20B ''immens'':16B ''in'':65B ''intelligenc'':19B ''magic'':32B ''nativ'':8B ''nordic'':25B ''of'':38B ''or'':42B ''peopl'':26B ''playing'':61B ''possess'':28B ''pow'':17B,37B ''provinc'':71B ''re'':59B ''re-emerg'':58B ''reptili'':6B ''rever'':11B ''rol'':64B ''shouts'':44B ''skyrim'':10B ''the'':15B,23B,36B,39B,66B,70B ''thought'':50B ''thu'':40B ''to'':9B,45B,51B,57B ''um'':41B ''unfolding'':68B ''unleash'':46B ''whil'':49B ''worshipp'':21B', 'dragon, scholar', '
Dragons are powerful, intelligent flying creatures native to Skyrim, known for their mastery of magic and the Thu''um. Once thought extinct, they have re-emerged, playing a key role in Skyrim''s events.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frostbite_spider', 'Frostbite Spiders are dangerous arachnids native to Skyrim, commonly found in dark, underground lairs or roaming the wilderness. These spiders are often identifiable by their web-covered nests, which can create obstacles for travelers. Equipped with the ability to spit poisonous venom at their prey from a distance, they also engage in close combat using their pincers.

Frostbite spiders typically exhibit a brown and gray coloration, although blue variants have also been observed. Their venom, known as Frostbite Venom, is frequently harvested for use in various poisons, while spider eggs can be collected from sacs within their webs for alchemical purposes. These creatures pose a significant threat to those who venture too close, using both ranged and melee attacks to defend their territory.', '''ability'':41B ''alchemical'':103B ''also'':53B,74B ''although'':70B ''and'':67B,120B ''arachnids'':7B ''are'':5B,23B ''as'':80B ''at'':46B ''attacks'':122B ''be'':95B ''been'':75B ''blu'':71B ''both'':118B ''brown'':66B ''by'':26B ''can'':33B,94B ''clos'':56B,116B ''collect'':96B ''coloration'':69B ''combat'':57B ''commonly'':11B ''cover'':30B ''creat'':34B ''creatur'':106B ''dangerous'':6B ''dark'':14B ''defend'':124B ''distanc'':51B ''eggs'':93B ''engag'':54B ''equipp'':38B ''exhibit'':64B ''for'':36B,86B,102B ''found'':12B ''frequently'':84B ''from'':49B,97B ''frostbit'':1A,3B,61B,81B ''gray'':68B ''harvest'':85B ''hav'':73B ''identifi'':25B ''in'':13B,55B,88B ''is'':83B ''known'':79B ''lairs'':16B ''mele'':121B ''nativ'':8B ''nests'':31B ''observ'':76B ''obstacl'':35B ''often'':24B ''or'':17B ''pincers'':60B ''poisonous'':44B ''poisons'':90B ''pos'':107B ''prey'':48B ''purp'':104B ''rang'':119B ''roaming'':18B ''sacs'':98B ''significant'':109B ''skyrim'':10B ''spid'':2A,92B ''spiders'':4B,22B,62B ''spit'':43B ''territory'':126B ''the'':19B,27B,40B,47B,59B,77B,100B,125B ''thes'':21B,105B ''they'':52B ''thos'':112B ''threat'':110B ''to'':9B,42B,111B,123B ''too'':115B ''travelers'':37B ''typically'':63B ''underground'':15B ''use'':87B ''using'':58B,117B ''variants'':72B ''various'':89B ''venom'':45B,78B,82B ''ventur'':114B ''web'':29B ''web-cover'':28B ''webs'':101B ''which'':32B ''whil'':91B ''who'':113B ''wilderness'':20B ''with'':39B ''within'':99B', 'nord, hunter', 'Frostbite Spiders are dangerous arachnids found in Skyrim''s dark lairs and wilderness. They can spit poisonous venom and use pincers in close combat.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('giants', 'Giants are enormous humanoid beings known for their immense strength and towering stature, found primarily in the wilderness of Skyrim and other regions such as High Rock, Hammerfell, Cyrodiil, and Valenwood. These colossal figures, often referred to as the "big folk," typically stand between 11 and 12 feet tall, with some individuals reaching even greater heights. They have thick gray skin, long limbs, large hands and feet, and distinctive thick grayish-brown hair, often adorned with braids, beads, and decorative scars carved into their chests. Giants usually wear fur pelts, sometimes embellished with animal bones, although many opt for a simpler loincloth.', '''11'':46B ''12'':48B ''adorn'':77B ''although'':98B ''and'':12B,22B,31B,47B,67B,69B,81B ''animal'':96B ''are'':3B ''as'':26B,39B ''beads'':80B ''beings'':6B ''betw'':45B ''big'':41B ''bon'':97B ''braids'':79B ''brown'':74B ''carv'':84B ''chests'':87B ''colossal'':34B ''cyrodiil'':30B ''decorativ'':82B ''distinctiv'':70B ''embellish'':94B ''enormous'':4B ''even'':55B ''feet'':49B,68B ''figur'':35B ''folk'':42B ''for'':8B,101B ''found'':15B ''fur'':91B ''giants'':1A,2B,88B ''gray'':61B ''grayish'':73B ''grayish-brown'':72B ''great'':56B ''hair'':75B ''hammerfell'':29B ''hands'':66B ''hav'':59B ''heights'':57B ''high'':27B ''human'':5B ''immens'':10B ''in'':17B ''individuals'':53B ''into'':85B ''known'':7B ''larg'':65B ''limbs'':64B ''loincloth'':104B ''long'':63B ''many'':99B ''of'':20B ''often'':36B,76B ''opt'':100B ''other'':23B ''pelts'':92B ''primarily'':16B ''reaching'':54B ''referr'':37B ''regions'':24B ''rock'':28B ''scars'':83B ''simpl'':103B ''skin'':62B ''skyrim'':21B ''som'':52B ''sometim'':93B ''stand'':44B ''statur'':14B ''strength'':11B ''such'':25B ''tall'':50B ''the'':9B,18B,40B,86B ''thes'':33B ''they'':58B ''thick'':60B,71B ''to'':38B ''towering'':13B ''typically'':43B ''usually'':89B ''valenwood'':32B ''wear'':90B ''wilderness'':19B ''with'':51B,78B,95B', 'nord, hunter', '
Giants are massive humanoid beings, known for their great strength and towering height, typically standing between 11 and 12 feet tall. Found in regions like Skyrim, they have gray skin, long limbs, and wear fur pelts, often adorned with animal bones and decorative markings. They should be avoided at all costs.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('angler', 'The elusive Angler is a very small, rare fish found exclusively in freezing waters when using an Argonian Fishing Rod. It has large teeth, a glowing lantern on its head, and dark slimey scales. It can be eaten though it has a rather horrible smell.', '''an'':18B ''and'':32B ''angler'':1A,4B ''argoni'':19B ''be'':38B ''can'':37B ''dark'':33B ''eat'':39B ''elusiv'':3B ''exclusively'':12B ''fish'':10B ''fishing'':20B ''found'':11B ''freezing'':14B ''glowing'':27B ''head'':31B ''horribl'':45B ''in'':13B ''is'':5B ''it'':22B,36B,41B ''its'':30B ''lantern'':28B ''larg'':24B ''on'':29B ''rar'':9B ''rath'':44B ''rod'':21B ''scal'':35B ''slimey'':34B ''small'':8B ''smell'':46B ''teeth'':25B ''the'':2B ''though'':40B ''using'':17B ''very'':7B ''waters'':15B ''when'':16B', 'fisher', 'The elusive Angler is a very small, rare fish. It has large teeth, a glowing lantern on its head, and dark slimey scales. It can be eaten though it has a rather horrible smell. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('goblin', 'Goblins are primitive humanoid creatures commonly found in various regions of Tamriel and Akavir, typically inhabiting sewers, caves, and ancient ruins. They are known for their small, clan-based societies, with heights ranging from three to over eight feet. Goblins usually exhibit green or yellow skin, pronounced canine teeth, yellow eyes with slitted pupils, and pointed ears, and may also possess horns or hunchbacks. Despite their often violent nature towards more civilized races, Goblins display a surprising degree of intelligence and adaptability, capable of coexistence with others when circumstances allow.', '''adaptability'':84B ''akav'':15B ''allow'':92B ''also'':62B ''ancient'':21B ''and'':14B,20B,57B,60B,83B ''are'':3B,24B ''bas'':31B ''canin'':50B ''capabl'':85B ''cav'':19B ''circumstanc'':91B ''civiliz'':74B ''clan'':30B ''clan-bas'':29B ''coexistenc'':87B ''commonly'':7B ''creatur'':6B ''degre'':80B ''despit'':67B ''display'':77B ''ears'':59B ''eight'':40B ''exhibit'':44B ''eyes'':53B ''feet'':41B ''for'':26B ''found'':8B ''from'':36B ''goblin'':1A ''goblins'':2B,42B,76B ''gre'':45B ''heights'':34B ''horns'':64B ''human'':5B ''hunchbacks'':66B ''in'':9B ''inhabiting'':17B ''intelligenc'':82B ''known'':25B ''may'':61B ''mor'':73B ''natur'':71B ''of'':12B,81B,86B ''often'':69B ''or'':46B,65B ''others'':89B ''over'':39B ''point'':58B ''possess'':63B ''primitiv'':4B ''pronounc'':49B ''pupils'':56B ''rac'':75B ''ranging'':35B ''regions'':11B ''ruins'':22B ''sewers'':18B ''skin'':48B ''slitt'':55B ''small'':28B ''societi'':32B ''surprising'':79B ''tamriel'':13B ''teeth'':51B ''the'':27B,68B ''they'':23B ''thre'':37B ''to'':38B ''towards'':72B ''typically'':16B ''usually'':43B ''various'':10B ''violent'':70B ''when'':90B ''with'':33B,54B,88B ''yellow'':47B,52B', 'scholar, hunter', 'Goblins are small, primitive humanoids found in Tamriel and Akavir, often living in sewers, caves, or ruins. They are known to be cunning, sometimes violent creatures with green or yellow skin and pointed ears.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hagraven', 'Hagravens are sinister creatures, grotesque hybrids of old women and birds, resulting from a dark ritual that witches undergo to gain powerful magic at the cost of their humanity. This transformation infuses them with a corrupted essence, leading to a horrific appearance and depraved behavior. Hagravens are notorious for their malevolent appetite, often consuming living victims, particularly savoring fresh eyeballs. Their cunning nature allows them to employ both savage tactics and magical prowess, making them formidable adversaries in combat.', '''adversari'':78B ''allows'':65B ''and'':11B,44B,72B ''appearanc'':43B ''appetit'':53B ''are'':3B,48B ''at'':25B ''behavior'':46B ''birds'':12B ''both'':69B ''combat'':80B ''consuming'':55B ''corrupt'':37B ''cost'':27B ''creatur'':5B ''cunning'':63B ''dark'':16B ''deprav'':45B ''employ'':68B ''essenc'':38B ''eyeballs'':61B ''for'':50B ''formid'':77B ''fresh'':60B ''from'':14B ''gain'':22B ''grotesqu'':6B ''hagrav'':1A ''hagravens'':2B,47B ''horrific'':42B ''humanity'':30B ''hybrids'':7B ''in'':79B ''infus'':33B ''leading'':39B ''living'':56B ''magic'':24B ''magical'':73B ''making'':75B ''malevolent'':52B ''natur'':64B ''notorious'':49B ''of'':8B,28B ''often'':54B ''old'':9B ''particularly'':58B ''powerful'':23B ''prowess'':74B ''resulting'':13B ''ritual'':17B ''savag'':70B ''savoring'':59B ''sinist'':4B ''tactics'':71B ''that'':18B ''the'':26B,29B,51B,62B ''them'':34B,66B,76B ''this'':31B ''to'':21B,40B,67B ''transformation'':32B ''underg'':20B ''victims'':57B ''witch'':19B ''with'':35B ''wom'':10B', 'breton, witch, forsworn', 'Hagravens are sinister, bird-like hybrids of women and witches, created through dark rituals to gain powerful magic. Known for their grotesque appearance, malevolent nature, and cunning, they are formidable foes who often consume living victims.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ice_wraith', 'Ice Wraiths are ethereal, serpentine spirits composed entirely of ice, commonly found in the frigid landscapes and mountain ranges of Skyrim, as well as in regions of High Rock and Cyrodiil. These magical beings possess the ability to blend seamlessly with their snowy surroundings, rendering them nearly invisible to unsuspecting prey. Ice Wraiths are known for their swift and lethal attacks, lunging at victims to inflict fatal bites, and they can transmit Witbane, a disease that impairs mental acuity. Notably, they are immune to paralysis, making them challenging opponents in combat.', '''ability'':39B ''acuity'':81B ''and'':19B,32B,61B,71B ''are'':5B,56B,84B ''as'':24B,26B ''at'':65B ''attacks'':63B ''beings'':36B ''bit'':70B ''blend'':41B ''can'':73B ''challenging'':90B ''combat'':93B ''commonly'':13B ''comp'':9B ''cyrodiil'':33B ''dis'':77B ''entirely'':10B ''ethereal'':6B ''fatal'':69B ''for'':58B ''found'':14B ''frig'':17B ''high'':30B ''ice'':1A,3B,12B,54B ''immun'':85B ''impairs'':79B ''in'':15B,27B,92B ''inflict'':68B ''invis'':50B ''known'':57B ''landscap'':18B ''lethal'':62B ''lunging'':64B ''magical'':35B ''making'':88B ''mental'':80B ''mountain'':20B ''nearly'':49B ''notably'':82B ''of'':11B,22B,29B ''opponents'':91B ''paralysis'':87B ''possess'':37B ''prey'':53B ''rang'':21B ''regions'':28B ''rendering'':47B ''rock'':31B ''seamlessly'':42B ''serpentin'':7B ''skyrim'':23B ''snowy'':45B ''spirits'':8B ''surroundings'':46B ''swift'':60B ''that'':78B ''the'':16B,38B,44B,59B ''them'':48B,89B ''thes'':34B ''they'':72B,83B ''to'':40B,51B,67B,86B ''transmit'':74B ''unsuspecting'':52B ''victims'':66B ''well'':25B ''witban'':75B ''with'':43B ''wraith'':2A ''wraiths'':4B,55B', 'nord, hunter', 'Ice Wraiths are ethereal, ice-based spirits found in Skyrim and surrounding regions, blending with their snowy surroundings to ambush prey. Known for their swift attacks and ability to transmit Witbane.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('spriggan', 'Spriggans, often referred to as Nature''s Guardians, are mystical nature spirits typically taking the form of tree-like humanoids, although they can also assume animal-like shapes. Known for their moderate intelligence, Spriggans are generally hostile toward travelers, protecting secluded groves and glades across Tamriel. They blend seamlessly with the surrounding plant life, ambushing unsuspecting intruders with sharp fingers and teeth, as well as a toxic poison. Their regenerative abilities are formidable, making them difficult to defeat; they can call upon nearby woodland creatures for assistance during combat, and some can even summon powerful black bears.', '''abiliti'':74B ''across'':48B ''also'':26B ''although'':23B ''ambushing'':58B ''and'':46B,64B,93B ''animal'':29B ''animal-lik'':28B ''are'':10B,38B,75B ''as'':6B,66B,68B ''assistanc'':90B ''assum'':27B ''bears'':100B ''black'':99B ''blend'':51B ''call'':84B ''can'':25B,83B,95B ''combat'':92B ''creatur'':88B ''defeat'':81B ''difficult'':79B ''during'':91B ''even'':96B ''fingers'':63B ''for'':33B,89B ''form'':17B ''formid'':76B ''generally'':39B ''glad'':47B ''grov'':45B ''guardians'':9B ''hostil'':40B ''humanoids'':22B ''intelligenc'':36B ''intruders'':60B ''known'':32B ''lif'':57B ''lik'':21B,30B ''making'':77B ''moderat'':35B ''mystical'':11B ''natur'':7B,12B ''nearby'':86B ''of'':18B ''often'':3B ''plant'':56B ''poison'':71B ''powerful'':98B ''protecting'':43B ''referr'':4B ''regenerativ'':73B ''s'':8B ''seamlessly'':52B ''seclud'':44B ''shap'':31B ''sharp'':62B ''som'':94B ''spirits'':13B ''sprigg'':1A ''spriggans'':2B,37B ''summon'':97B ''surrounding'':55B ''taking'':15B ''tamriel'':49B ''teeth'':65B ''the'':16B,34B,54B,72B ''them'':78B ''they'':24B,50B,82B ''to'':5B,80B ''toward'':41B ''toxic'':70B ''travelers'':42B ''tre'':20B ''tree-lik'':19B ''typically'':14B ''unsuspecting'':59B ''upon'':85B ''well'':67B ''with'':53B,61B ''woodland'':87B', 'hunter, priest, scholar', '
Spriggans are mystical nature spirits, often tree-like humanoids, that protect secluded groves in Tamriel. They are hostile to travelers, and can summon woodland creatures, including black bears, for assistance.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('arctic_grayling', 'Arctic Grayling are long grey fish with a big top fin commonly found in freezing waters. They can be eaten and have are a white-fleshed fish with flaky meat that some say is delicious and versatile.', '''and'':23B,39B ''arctic'':1A,3B ''are'':5B,25B ''be'':21B ''big'':11B ''can'':20B ''commonly'':14B ''delicious'':38B ''eat'':22B ''fin'':13B ''fish'':8B,30B ''flaky'':32B ''flesh'':29B ''found'':15B ''freezing'':17B ''grayling'':2A,4B ''grey'':7B ''hav'':24B ''in'':16B ''is'':37B ''long'':6B ''meat'':33B ''say'':36B ''som'':35B ''that'':34B ''they'':19B ''top'':12B ''versatil'':40B ''waters'':18B ''whit'':28B ''white-flesh'':27B ''with'':9B,31B', 'fisher', 'Arctic Grayling are long grey fish with a big top fin commonly found in freezing waters. They can be eaten and have are a white-fleshed fish with flaky meat that some say is delicious and versatile. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('trolls', 'Trolls are large, ape-like creatures found throughout Tamriel, often characterized by their three eyes and formidable stature. Known for their exceptional regenerative abilities, trolls are difficult to kill, often recovering from injuries that would be fatal to other beings. However, they have a significant vulnerability to fire, which can disrupt their healing process. Typically found in caves and forested regions, trolls tend to be reclusive and prefer to dwell away from well-traveled paths.', '''abiliti'':26B ''and'':18B,61B,69B ''ape'':6B ''ape-lik'':5B ''are'':3B,28B ''away'':73B ''be'':38B,67B ''beings'':42B ''by'':14B ''can'':52B ''cav'':60B ''characteriz'':13B ''creatur'':8B ''difficult'':29B ''disrupt'':53B ''dwell'':72B ''exceptional'':24B ''eyes'':17B ''fatal'':39B ''fir'':50B ''for'':22B ''forest'':62B ''formid'':19B ''found'':9B,58B ''from'':34B,74B ''hav'':45B ''healing'':55B ''howev'':43B ''in'':59B ''injuri'':35B ''kill'':31B ''known'':21B ''larg'':4B ''lik'':7B ''often'':12B,32B ''other'':41B ''paths'':78B ''pref'':70B ''process'':56B ''reclusiv'':68B ''recovering'':33B ''regenerativ'':25B ''regions'':63B ''significant'':47B ''statur'':20B ''tamriel'':11B ''tend'':65B ''that'':36B ''the'':15B,23B,54B ''they'':44B ''thre'':16B ''throughout'':10B ''to'':30B,40B,49B,66B,71B ''travel'':77B ''trolls'':1A,2B,27B,64B ''typically'':57B ''vulnerability'':48B ''well'':76B ''well-travel'':75B ''which'':51B ''would'':37B', 'hunter', '
Trolls are dangerous large, ape-like creatures with three eyes,  typically found in caves or forests, avoiding well-traveled paths.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wispmother', 'Wispmothers, sometimes referred to as wispfathers, are mystical entities believed to be ghosts, wraiths, or nature spirits, commonly found in the wilds of Tamriel. These beings can communicate and often refer to the wisps that accompany them as their children. Legends from Black Marsh suggest that while a wispmother can be killed, its essence must be sealed to prevent it from resurrecting. In Valenwood, a rarer variant is known as the Amronal.', '''accompany'':37B ''amronal'':73B ''and'':30B ''are'':8B ''as'':6B,39B,71B ''be'':13B,52B,57B ''beings'':27B ''believ'':11B ''black'':44B ''can'':28B,51B ''childr'':41B ''commonly'':19B ''communicat'':29B ''entiti'':10B ''essenc'':55B ''found'':20B ''from'':43B,62B ''ghosts'':14B ''in'':21B,64B ''is'':69B ''it'':61B ''its'':54B ''kill'':53B ''known'':70B ''legends'':42B ''marsh'':45B ''must'':56B ''mystical'':9B ''natur'':17B ''of'':24B ''often'':31B ''or'':16B ''prevent'':60B ''rar'':67B ''ref'':32B ''referr'':4B ''resurrecting'':63B ''seal'':58B ''sometim'':3B ''spirits'':18B ''suggest'':46B ''tamriel'':25B ''that'':36B,47B ''the'':22B,34B,40B,72B ''them'':38B ''thes'':26B ''to'':5B,12B,33B,59B ''valenwood'':65B ''variant'':68B ''whil'':48B ''wilds'':23B ''wispfathers'':7B ''wispmoth'':1A,50B ''wispmothers'':2B ''wisps'':35B ''wraiths'':15B', 'scholar, mage', '
Wispmothers are mystical entities, often believed to be ghosts or nature spirits, found in the wilds of Tamriel. They are accompanied by wisps, which they refer to as their children.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wisp', '
Wisps, also known as Witchlights, are mysterious floating entities often encountered near Wispmothers, although they can also exist independently. The nature of wisps is a topic of debate among scholars; some believe they are scavengers that attract prey to the Wispmother, sharing in the psychoetherial energy released from her kills. Others theorize that wisps are mere manifestations or conjurations of the Wispmother, lacking independent existence. This latter view is supported by the observation that killing a Wispmother also results in the death of the surrounding wisps, leaving behind only glow dust.

In nature''s cycle, wisps are associated with Y''ffre, who sends them to announce the arrival of storms during Rain''s Hand. Seeing a wisp is often interpreted as a sign of renewal, symbolizing new growth and the beginning of a fresh chapter in the cycle of life.', '''also'':3B,18B,79B ''although'':15B ''among'':30B ''and'':130B ''announc'':107B ''are'':7B,35B,56B,98B ''arrival'':109B ''as'':5B,122B ''associat'':99B ''attract'':38B ''beginning'':132B ''behind'':89B ''believ'':33B ''by'':72B ''can'':17B ''chapt'':136B ''conjurations'':60B ''cycle'':96B,139B ''death'':83B ''debat'':29B ''during'':112B ''dust'':92B ''encounter'':12B ''energy'':47B ''entiti'':10B ''exist'':19B ''existenc'':66B ''ffre'':102B ''floating'':9B ''fresh'':135B ''from'':49B ''glow'':91B ''growth'':129B ''hand'':115B ''her'':50B ''in'':44B,81B,93B,137B ''independent'':65B ''independently'':20B ''interpret'':121B ''is'':25B,70B,119B ''killing'':76B ''kills'':51B ''known'':4B ''lacking'':64B ''latt'':68B ''leaving'':88B ''lif'':141B ''manifestations'':58B ''mer'':57B ''mysterious'':8B ''natur'':22B,94B ''near'':13B ''new'':128B ''observation'':74B ''of'':23B,28B,61B,84B,110B,125B,133B,140B ''often'':11B,120B ''only'':90B ''or'':59B ''others'':52B ''prey'':39B ''psychoetherial'':46B ''rain'':113B ''releas'':48B ''renewal'':126B ''results'':80B ''s'':95B,114B ''scavengers'':36B ''scholars'':31B ''seeing'':116B ''sends'':104B ''sharing'':43B ''sign'':124B ''som'':32B ''storms'':111B ''support'':71B ''surrounding'':86B ''symbolizing'':127B ''that'':37B,54B,75B ''the'':21B,41B,45B,62B,73B,82B,85B,108B,131B,138B ''them'':105B ''theoriz'':53B ''they'':16B,34B ''this'':67B ''to'':40B,106B ''topic'':27B ''view'':69B ''who'':103B ''wisp'':1A,118B ''wispmoth'':42B,63B,78B ''wispmothers'':14B ''wisps'':2B,24B,55B,87B,97B ''witchlights'':6B ''with'':100B', 'scholar, mage', 'Wisps, also known as Witchlights, are mysterious floating entities often found near Wispmothers. Associated with Y''ffre, they are believed to signal storms and symbolize renewal in the cycle of life.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragon_priest', 'Dragon Priests are powerful undead beings that were once the devoted servants of the ancient dragons in Skyrim. Revered for their formidable magical abilities, these priests commanded legions of warriors in the name of their dragon deities. Today, they reside in ornate coffins within prominent dragon worship sites, and if disturbed, they will rise with great force to confront intruders.', '''abiliti'':26B ''ancient'':17B ''and'':51B ''are'':5B ''beings'':8B ''coffins'':45B ''command'':29B ''confront'':61B ''deiti'':39B ''devot'':13B ''disturb'':53B ''dragon'':1A,3B,38B,48B ''dragons'':18B ''for'':22B ''forc'':59B ''formid'':24B ''great'':58B ''if'':52B ''in'':19B,33B,43B ''intruders'':62B ''legions'':30B ''magical'':25B ''nam'':35B ''of'':15B,31B,36B ''once'':11B ''ornat'':44B ''powerful'':6B ''priest'':2A ''priests'':4B,28B ''prominent'':47B ''resid'':42B ''rever'':21B ''ris'':56B ''servants'':14B ''sit'':50B ''skyrim'':20B ''that'':9B ''the'':12B,16B,23B,34B,37B ''thes'':27B ''they'':41B,54B ''to'':60B ''today'':40B ''unde'':7B ''warriors'':32B ''wer'':10B ''will'':55B ''with'':57B ''within'':46B ''worship'':49B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Dragon Priests are powerful undead beings who once served ancient dragons in Skyrim. They are thought to rest in ornate coffins at dragon worship sites, rising to confront intruders if disturbed.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('draugr', 'Draugr are the mummified remains of ancient Nords, found primarily in the cold, tomb-laden landscapes of Skyrim and Solstheim. These undead creatures were preserved before their reanimation, which has helped them retain much of their physical integrity, allowing their muscles and ligaments to resist decay. This preservation has resulted in a diverse range of combat styles among draugr, reflecting the varied skills they possessed in life.', '''allowing'':41B ''among'':60B ''ancient'':8B ''and'':21B,44B ''are'':3B ''befor'':28B ''cold'':14B ''combat'':58B ''creatur'':25B ''decay'':48B ''div'':55B ''draugr'':1A,2B,61B ''found'':10B ''help'':33B ''in'':12B,53B,68B ''integrity'':40B ''lad'':17B ''landscap'':18B ''lif'':69B ''ligaments'':45B ''much'':36B ''mummifi'':5B ''muscl'':43B ''nords'':9B ''of'':7B,19B,37B,57B ''physical'':39B ''possess'':67B ''preserv'':27B ''preservation'':50B ''primarily'':11B ''rang'':56B ''reanimation'':30B ''reflecting'':62B ''remains'':6B ''resist'':47B ''result'':52B ''retain'':35B ''skills'':65B ''skyrim'':20B ''solstheim'':22B ''styles'':59B ''the'':4B,13B,29B,38B,42B,63B ''them'':34B ''thes'':23B ''they'':66B ''this'':49B ''to'':46B ''tomb'':16B ''tomb-lad'':15B ''unde'':24B ''vari'':64B ''wer'':26B ''which'':31B', 'nord, scholar', 'Draugr are the mummified remains of ancient Nords. They are believed to reanimate and attack any intruders to their ancient burial sites.', '', '', 'creatures');
