INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ritual_stone', 'The Ritual Stone is one of Skyrim''s thirteen enigmatic Standing Stones, located east of Whiterun by the roadside, perched on a rocky outcrop overlooking the entrance to Graywinter Watch. This ancient monument is marked by its circle of candles and commands a commanding view of the surrounding landscape.

The stone grants a powerful and unique blessing to those who activate it, enabling them to reanimate nearby corpses to fight as allies for a limited time. The raised bodies remain intact after the power''s effects wear off, and there is no limit to how many corpses can be reanimated.

The path leading to the stone winds upward through squared-off arches, reflecting the artistry and mysticism of the Nords who revered these ancient relics. The Ritual Stone''s eerie aura and potent magic serve as a testament to the mysterious forces that shape Skyrim''s untamed lands.', '''activat'':63B ''after'':84B ''alli'':74B ''ancient'':34B,127B ''and'':43B,57B,91B,119B,135B ''arches'':115B ''artistry'':118B ''as'':73B,139B ''aur'':134B ''be'':101B ''blessing'':59B ''bodi'':81B ''by'':19B,38B ''can'':100B ''candl'':42B ''circl'':40B ''commanding'':46B ''commands'':44B ''corps'':70B,99B ''east'':16B ''eeri'':133B ''effects'':88B ''enabling'':65B ''enigmatic'':12B ''entranc'':29B ''fight'':72B ''for'':75B ''forc'':145B ''grants'':54B ''graywint'':31B ''how'':97B ''intact'':83B ''is'':6B,36B,93B ''it'':64B ''its'':39B ''lands'':151B ''landscap'':51B ''leading'':105B ''limit'':77B,95B ''locat'':15B ''magic'':137B ''many'':98B ''mark'':37B ''monument'':35B ''mysterious'':144B ''mysticism'':120B ''nearby'':69B ''nords'':123B ''of'':8B,17B,41B,48B,121B ''off'':90B,114B ''on'':23B ''one'':7B ''outcrop'':26B ''overlooking'':27B ''path'':104B ''perch'':22B ''potent'':136B ''pow'':86B ''powerful'':56B ''rais'':80B ''reanimat'':68B,102B ''reflecting'':116B ''relics'':128B ''remain'':82B ''rever'':125B ''ritual'':1A,4B,130B ''roadsid'':21B ''rocky'':25B ''s'':10B,87B,132B,149B ''serv'':138B ''shap'':147B ''skyrim'':9B,148B ''squar'':113B ''squared-off'':112B ''standing'':13B ''ston'':2A,5B,14B,53B,108B,131B ''surrounding'':50B ''testament'':141B ''that'':146B ''the'':3B,20B,28B,49B,52B,79B,85B,103B,107B,117B,122B,129B,143B ''them'':66B ''ther'':92B ''thes'':126B ''thirt'':11B ''this'':33B ''thos'':61B ''through'':111B ''tim'':78B ''to'':30B,60B,67B,71B,96B,106B,142B ''uniqu'':58B ''untam'':150B ''upward'':110B ''view'':47B ''watch'':32B ''wear'':89B ''whiterun'':18B ''who'':62B,124B ''winds'':109B', 'whiterun, scholar, traveler', 'The Ritual Stone is one of Skyrim''s thirteen enigmatic Standing Stones, located east of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('guardian_stones ', 'The Guardian Stones are a revered trio of Standing Stones located east of Lake Ilinalta, along the road between Helgen and Riverwood in Falkreath Hold. Set against the tranquil backdrop of the river and forest, these stones are among the most well-known and accessible in Skyrim, offering powerful blessings to those who seek to hone their skills.

The stones represent the three primary paths of mastery: magic, stealth, and combat. The Mage Stone grants those under its sign the ability to learn all magical skills faster, fostering the arcane arts. The Thief Stone accelerates the mastery of stealth-related skills, appealing to those who prefer cunning and subtlety. Lastly, the Warrior Stone enhances the training of all combat skills, empowering those who choose strength and valor.', '''ability'':84B ''accelerat'':98B ''access'':48B ''against'':29B ''all'':87B,122B ''along'':18B ''among'':41B ''and'':23B,36B,47B,73B,112B,130B ''appealing'':106B ''arcan'':93B ''are'':6B,40B ''arts'':94B ''backdrop'':32B ''betw'':21B ''blessings'':53B ''choos'':128B ''combat'':74B,123B ''cunning'':111B ''east'':14B ''empowering'':125B ''enhanc'':118B ''falkreath'':26B ''fast'':90B ''forest'':37B ''fostering'':91B ''grants'':78B ''guardi'':1A,4B ''helg'':22B ''hold'':27B ''hon'':59B ''ilinalt'':17B ''in'':25B,49B ''its'':81B ''known'':46B ''lak'':16B ''lastly'':114B ''learn'':86B ''locat'':13B ''mag'':76B ''magic'':71B ''magical'':88B ''mastery'':70B,100B ''most'':43B ''of'':10B,15B,33B,69B,101B,121B ''offering'':51B ''paths'':68B ''powerful'':52B ''pref'':110B ''primary'':67B ''relat'':104B ''represent'':64B ''rever'':8B ''riv'':35B ''riverwood'':24B ''road'':20B ''seek'':57B ''set'':28B ''sign'':82B ''skills'':61B,89B,105B,124B ''skyrim'':50B ''standing'':11B ''stealth'':72B,103B ''stealth-relat'':102B ''ston'':2A,5B,12B,39B,63B,77B,97B,117B ''strength'':129B ''subtlety'':113B ''the'':3B,19B,30B,34B,42B,60B,62B,65B,75B,83B,92B,95B,99B,115B,119B ''thes'':38B ''thief'':96B ''thos'':55B,79B,108B,126B ''thre'':66B ''to'':54B,58B,85B,107B ''training'':120B ''tranquil'':31B ''tri'':9B ''under'':80B ''valor'':131B ''warrior'':116B ''well'':45B ''well-known'':44B ''who'':56B,109B,127B', 'whiterun, scholar, traveler', 'Guardian Stones are a revered trio of Standing Stones located east of Lake Ilinalta, along the road between Helgen and Riverwood in Falkreath Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('greenspring_hollow', 'Greenspring Hollow is a shallow outdoor cave nestled west-northwest of Whiterun and southwest of Hamvir''s Rest, situated amidst the rolling plains of Whiterun Hold. ', '''amidst'':23B ''and'':16B ''cav'':9B ''greenspring'':1A,3B ''hamv'':19B ''hold'':29B ''hollow'':2A,4B ''is'':5B ''nestl'':10B ''northwest'':13B ''of'':14B,18B,27B ''outdoor'':8B ''plains'':26B ''rest'':21B ''rolling'':25B ''s'':20B ''shallow'':7B ''situat'':22B ''southwest'':17B ''the'':24B ''west'':12B ''west-northwest'':11B ''whiterun'':15B,28B', 'whiterun', 'Greenspring Hollow is a shallow outdoor cave nestled west-northwest of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('throat_of_the_world', 'The Throat of the World, known as Monahven ("Mother Wind") in the language of dragons, is the highest mountain in all of Tamriel, dominating the landscape of Skyrim. Towering above the northern province, it was once rivaled only by Red Mountain before the latter''s catastrophic eruption in the Fourth Era. The mountain is home to the revered settlement of High Hrothgar, perched near its summit, where the Greybeards dwell in silence, dedicating their lives to the mastery of the Thu’um. The ascent to High Hrothgar is marked by the legendary "7,000 steps," a path rich with Nordic lore, including tales of King Wulfharth rebuilding the 418th step.

The Throat of the World holds profound significance for the Nords, often symbolizing their homeland as a whole. Also referred to as Snow Throat or Throat Mountain, it is one of the mystical Towers, ancient anchors of power in Tamriel. Prophecy links it to the destiny of the Dragonborn, foretelling a time when the "Snow Tower" will lie "sundered, kingless, bleeding," reflecting Skyrim’s turbulent history and uncertain future. This sacred peak stands as a testament to the power and mystery that define the land of the Nords.', '''000'':98B ''418th'':113B ''7'':97B ''abov'':34B ''all'':25B ''also'':133B ''anchors'':150B ''ancient'':149B ''and'':181B,194B ''as'':11B,130B,136B,188B ''ascent'':88B ''befor'':46B ''bleeding'':175B ''by'':43B,94B ''catastrophic'':50B ''dedicating'':77B ''defin'':197B ''destiny'':160B ''dominating'':28B ''dragonborn'':163B ''dragons'':19B ''dwell'':74B ''eruption'':51B ''for'':123B ''foretelling'':164B ''fourth'':54B ''futur'':183B ''greybeards'':73B ''high'':65B,90B ''highest'':22B ''history'':180B ''holds'':120B ''hom'':59B ''homeland'':129B ''hrothg'':66B,91B ''in'':15B,24B,52B,75B,153B ''including'':106B ''is'':20B,58B,92B,143B ''it'':38B,142B,157B ''its'':69B ''king'':109B ''kingless'':174B ''known'':10B ''land'':199B ''landscap'':30B ''languag'':17B ''latt'':48B ''legendary'':96B ''lie'':172B ''links'':156B ''liv'':79B ''lor'':105B ''mark'':93B ''mastery'':82B ''monahv'':12B ''moth'':13B ''mountain'':23B,45B,57B,141B ''mystery'':195B ''mystical'':147B ''near'':68B ''nordic'':104B ''nords'':125B,202B ''northern'':36B ''of'':2A,7B,18B,26B,31B,64B,83B,108B,117B,145B,151B,161B,200B ''often'':126B ''once'':40B ''one'':144B ''only'':42B ''or'':139B ''path'':101B ''peak'':186B ''perch'':67B ''pow'':152B,193B ''profound'':121B ''prophecy'':155B ''provinc'':37B ''rebuilding'':111B ''red'':44B ''referr'':134B ''reflecting'':176B ''rever'':62B ''rich'':102B ''rival'':41B ''s'':49B,178B ''sacr'':185B ''settlement'':63B ''significanc'':122B ''silenc'