', '''and'':22B ''belongs'':29B ''betw'':20B ''divin'':48B ''dwelling'':10B ''extolling'':42B ''fervent'':33B ''for'':38B ''gildergr'':17B ''heimskr'':1A,4B,31B ''his'':39B ''hom'':28B ''hous'':3A,6B ''impassion'':40B ''in'':12B ''is'':7B ''jorrvaskr'':21B ''known'':37B ''kynareth'':26B ''locat'':11B ''modest'':9B ''near'':14B ''nestl'':19B ''ninth'':47B ''of'':25B,35B,45B ''priest'':34B ''s'':2A,5B ''sacr'':16B ''sermons'':41B ''tal'':36B ''templ'':24B ''the'':15B,23B,27B,43B,46B ''to'':30B ''tre'':18B ''virtu'':44B ''whiterun'':13B', 'whiterun', 'Heimskr''s House is a modest dwelling located in the Winds District in Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('house_gray-mane', 'House Gray-Mane is the ancestral home of Clan Gray-Mane, one of Whiterun''s most prominent and traditional families. Situated in the Wind District, the house stands directly opposite the sacred Gildergreen tree, at the top of the stairs leading up from the bustling marketplace.

The home reflects the clan''s storied history and deep-rooted Nordic pride, serving as a gathering place for its members amidst the political tensions of Whiterun. As staunch supporters of the Stormcloak rebellion and advocates for Nordic independence, the Gray-Manes are known for their unwavering values and rivalry with the Imperial-aligned Clan Battle-Born. ', '''advocat'':89B ''align'':109B ''amidst'':75B ''ancestral'':11B ''and'':24B,61B,88B,103B ''are'':97B ''as'':68B,81B ''at'':41B ''battl'':112B ''battle-born'':111B ''born'':113B ''bustling'':51B ''clan'':14B,57B,110B ''deep'':63B ''deep-root'':62B ''directly'':35B ''district'':31B ''famili'':26B ''for'':72B,90B,99B ''from'':49B ''gathering'':70B ''gildergr'':39B ''gray'':3A,7B,16B,95B ''gray-man'':2A,6B,15B,94B ''history'':60B ''hom'':12B,54B ''hous'':1A,5B,33B ''imperial'':108B ''imperial-align'':107B ''in'':28B ''independenc'':92B ''is'':9B ''its'':73B ''known'':98B ''leading'':47B ''man'':4A,8B,17B,96B ''marketplac'':52B ''members'':74B ''most'':22B ''nordic'':65B,91B ''of'':13B,19B,44B,79B,84B ''one'':18B ''opposit'':36B ''plac'':71B ''political'':77B ''prid'':66B ''prominent'':23B ''rebellion'':87B ''reflects'':55B ''rivalry'':104B ''root'':64B ''s'':21B,58B ''sacr'':38B ''serving'':67B ''situat'':27B ''stairs'':46B ''stands'':34B ''staunch'':82B ''stori'':59B ''stormcloak'':86B ''supporters'':83B ''tensions'':78B ''the'':10B,29B,32B,37B,42B,45B,50B,53B,56B,76B,85B,93B,100B,106B ''top'':43B ''traditional'':25B ''tre'':40B ''unwavering'':101B ''up'':48B ''valu'':102B ''whiterun'':20B,80B ''wind'':30B ''with'':105B', 'whiterun, noble', 'House Gray-Mane is the ancestral home of Clan Gray-Mane, one of Whiterun''s most prominent and traditional families. Situated in the Wind District.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('house_of_clan_battle-born', 'The House of Clan Battle-Born is the residence of the influential Battle-Born family, situated in the Wind District of Whiterun. Nestled beside the Hall of the Dead, the home is a prominent landmark in the city, standing directly across from the house of their rivals, Clan Gray-Mane.

The Battle-Borns are staunch supporters of the Empire and the Imperial Legion, embodying loyalty to tradition and order. Their home reflects their status and role in Whiterun’s political and social landscape. As one of the city’s leading families, the House of Clan Battle-Born serves as both a symbol of their allegiance to the Empire and a focal point in the ongoing feud with the fiercely independent Gray-Manes.', '''across'':49B ''allegianc'':116B ''and'':70B,78B,85B,91B,120B ''are'':64B ''as'':94B,110B ''battl'':5A,12B,21B,62B,107B ''battle-born'':4A,11B,20B,106B ''battle-borns'':61B ''besid'':32B ''born'':6A,13B,22B,108B ''borns'':63B ''both'':111B ''city'':46B,98B ''clan'':3A,10B,56B,105B ''dead'':37B ''directly'':48B ''district'':28B ''embodying'':74B ''empir'':69B,119B ''famili'':101B ''family'':23B ''feud'':127B ''fiercely'':130B ''focal'':122B ''from'':50B ''gray'':58B,133B ''gray-man'':57B,132B ''hall'':34B ''hom'':39B,81B ''hous'':1A,8B,52B,103B ''imperial'':72B ''in'':25B,44B,87B,124B ''independent'':131B ''influential'':19B ''is'':14B,40B ''landmark'':43B ''landscap'':93B ''leading'':100B ''legion'':73B ''loyalty'':75B ''man'':59B,134B ''nestl'':31B ''of'':2A,9B,17B,29B,35B,53B,67B,96B,104B,114B ''one'':95B ''ongoing'':126B ''order'':79B ''point'':123B ''political'':90B ''prominent'':42B ''reflects'':82B ''residenc'':16B ''rivals'':55B ''rol'':86B ''s'':89B,99B ''serv'':109B ''situat'':24B ''social'':92B ''standing'':47B ''status'':84B ''staunch'':65B ''supporters'':66B ''symbol'':113B ''the'':7B,15B,18B,26B,33B,36B,38B,45B,51B,54B,60B,68B,71B,80B,83B,97B,102B,115B,118B,125B,129B ''to'':76B,117B ''tradition'':77B ''whiterun'':30B,88B ''wind'':27B ''with'':128B', 'whiterun, noble', 'The House of Clan Battle-Born is the residence of the influential Battle-Born family, situated in the Wind District of Whiterun. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('jorrvaskr', 'Jorrvaskr is the legendary mead hall and headquarters of the Companions, situated atop the steps leading from Whiterun''s central plaza. It is the oldest structure in Whiterun, predating the city itself, and was established around the revered Skyforge. Over centuries, Whiterun grew around this sacred site, cementing Jorrvaskr''s role as a cornerstone of Nordic heritage.

The building, crafted from the overturned hull of a longship, reflects its deep ties to Atmoran tradition. Jorrvaskr was originally the ship of Ysgramor’s fleet, carried across the land by its crew and repurposed as a shelter when Jeek of the River founded the Great City. This connection to Ysgramor and the Five Hundred Companions imbues the hall with immense historical and cultural significance.', '''across'':86B ''and'':8B,34B,92B,110B,121B ''around'':37B,45B ''as'':53B,94B ''atmor'':74B ''atop'':14B ''building'':60B ''by'':89B ''carri'':85B ''cementing'':49B ''central'':21B ''centuri'':42B ''city'':32B,105B ''companions'':12B,114B ''connection'':107B ''cornerston'':55B ''craft'':61B ''crew'':91B ''cultural'':122B ''deep'':71B ''establish'':36B ''fiv'':112B ''fleet'':84B ''found'':102B ''from'':18B,62B ''great'':104B ''grew'':44B ''hall'':7B,117B ''headquarters'':9B ''heritag'':58B ''historical'':120B ''hull'':65B ''hundr'':113B ''imbu'':115B ''immens'':119B ''in'':28B ''is'':3B,24B ''it'':23B ''its'':70B,90B ''itself'':33B ''jeek'':98B ''jorrvaskr'':1A,2B,50B,76B ''land'':88B ''leading'':17B ''legendary'':5B ''longship'':68B ''mead'':6B ''nordic'':57B ''of'':10B,56B,66B,81B,99B ''oldest'':26B ''originally'':78B ''over'':41B ''overturn'':64B ''plaz'':22B ''predating'':30B ''reflects'':69B ''repurp'':93B ''rever'':39B ''riv'':101B ''rol'':52B ''s'':20B,51B,83B ''sacr'':47B ''shelt'':96B ''ship'':80B ''significanc'':123B ''sit'':48B ''situat'':13B ''skyforg'':40B ''steps'':16B ''structur'':27B ''the'':4B,11B,15B,25B,31B,38B,59B,63B,79B,87B,100B,103B,111B,116B ''this'':46B,106B ''ties'':72B ''to'':73B,108B ''tradition'':75B ''was'':35B,77B ''when'':97B ''whiterun'':19B,29B,43B ''with'':118B ''ysgramor'':82B,109B', 'whiterun, companions', 'Jorrvaskr is the legendary mead hall and headquarters of the Companions, situated atop the steps leading from Whiterun''s central plaza. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('olava_the_feeble''s_house', 'Olava the Feeble''s House is a quaint, modest home located in the southern part of Whiterun, tucked away directly behind Breezehome. This small residence serves as the dwelling of Olava the Feeble, an elderly seer known for her wisdom and mystical insights.', '''an'':39B ''and'':46B ''as'':32B ''away'':24B ''behind'':26B ''breezehom'':27B ''directly'':25B ''dwelling'':34B ''elderly'':40B ''feebl'':3A,8B,38B ''for'':43B ''her'':44B ''hom'':15B ''hous'':5A,10B ''in'':17B ''insights'':48B ''is'':11B ''known'':42B ''locat'':16B ''modest'':14B ''mystical'':47B ''of'':21B,35B ''olav'':1A,6B,36B ''part'':20B ''quaint'':13B ''residenc'':30B ''s'':4A,9B ''seer'':41B ''serv'':31B ''small'':29B ''southern'':19B ''the'':2A,7B,18B,33B,37B ''this'':28B ''tuck'':23B ''whiterun'':22B ''wisdom'':45B', 'whiterun', 'Olava the Feeble''s House is a quaint, modest home located in the southern part of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('severio_pelagia''s_house', 'Severio Pelagia''s House is a modest residence located in the Plains District of Whiterun, nestled between the Drunken Huntsman and the bustling market stalls. The home serves as the city dwelling of Severio Pelagia, the proprietor of Pelagia Farm, a prominent agricultural holding just outside Whiterun''s walls.', '''agricultural'':47B ''and'':25B ''as'':33B ''betw'':21B ''bustling'':27B ''city'':35B ''district'':17B ''drunk'':23B ''dwelling'':36B ''farm'':44B ''holding'':48B ''hom'':31B ''hous'':4A,8B ''huntsm'':24B ''in'':14B ''is'':9B ''just'':49B ''locat'':13B ''market'':28B ''modest'':11B ''nestl'':20B ''of'':18B,37B,42B ''outsid'':50B ''pelagi'':2A,6B,39B,43B ''plains'':16B ''prominent'':46B ''proprietor'':41B ''residenc'':12B ''s'':3A,7B,52B ''serv'':32B ''severi'':1A,5B,38B ''stalls'':29B ''the'':15B,22B,26B,30B,34B,40B ''walls'':53B ''whiterun'':19B,51B', 'whiterun', 'Severio Pelagia''s House is a modest residence located in the Plains District of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skyforge', 'Skyforge is an ancient and mystical forge located atop a rocky outcrop in Whiterun, near the Companions'' hall, Jorrvaskr. Renowned for its unparalleled craftsmanship, it is tended by Eorlund Gray-Mane, widely regarded as the finest blacksmith in Skyrim. The forge’s searing heat is used to craft powerful weapons and armor, as well as to light the funeral pyres of fallen Companions, intertwining its purpose with the traditions and legacy of the order.

Legend holds that the Skyforge predates human settlement in the area. The ancient elves believed it to be a relic of the gods, an artifact so sacred that they avoided it entirely. When Ysgramor and his Five Hundred Companions arrived, they claimed the forge as their own, building Jorrvaskr nearby to honor its power. This act marked the beginning of human settlement in the region, eventually giving rise to the city of Whiterun.', '''act'':132B ''an'':4B,100B ''ancient'':5B,89B ''and'':6B,53B,72B,111B ''are'':87B ''armor'':54B ''arriv'':116B ''artifact'':101B ''as'':36B,55B,57B,121B ''atop'':10B ''avoid'':106B ''be'':94B ''beginning'':135B ''believ'':91B ''blacksmith'':39B ''building'':124B ''by'':29B ''city'':147B ''claim'':118B ''companions'':18B,65B,115B ''craft'':50B ''craftsmanship'':25B ''elves'':90B ''entirely'':108B ''eorlund'':30B ''eventually'':142B ''fall'':64B ''finest'':38B ''fiv'':113B ''for'':22B ''forg'':8B,43B,120B ''funeral'':61B ''giving'':143B ''gods'':99B ''gray'':32B ''gray-man'':31B ''hall'':19B ''heat'':46B ''his'':112B ''holds'':78B ''honor'':128B ''hum'':83B,137B ''hundr'':114B ''in'':14B,40B,85B,139B ''intertwining'':66B ''is'':3B,27B,47B ''it'':26B,92B,107B ''its'':23B,67B,129B ''jorrvaskr'':20B,125B ''legacy'':73B ''legend'':77B ''light'':59B ''locat'':9B ''man'':33B ''mark'':133B ''mystical'':7B ''near'':16B ''nearby'':126B ''of'':63B,74B,97B,136B,148B ''order'':76B ''outcrop'':13B ''own'':123B ''pow'':130B ''powerful'':51B ''predat'':82B ''purpos'':68B ''pyres'':62B ''regard'':35B ''region'':141B ''relic'':96B ''renown'':21B ''ris'':144B ''rocky'':12B ''s'':44B ''sacr'':103B ''searing'':45B ''settlement'':84B,138B ''skyforg'':1A,2B,81B ''skyrim'':41B ''so'':102B ''tend'':28B ''that'':79B,104B ''the'':17B,37B,42B,60B,70B,75B,80B,86B,88B,98B,119B,122B,134B,140B,146B ''they'':105B,117B ''this'':131B ''to'':49B,58B,93B,127B,145B ''traditions'':71B ''unparallel'':24B ''used'':48B ''weapons'':52B ''well'':56B ''when'':109B ''whiterun'':15B,149B ''widely'':34B ''with'':69B ''ysgramor'':110B', 'whiterun, companions', 'Skyforge is an ancient and mystical forge located atop a rocky outcrop in Whiterun, near the Companions'' hall, Jorrvaskr. Renowned for its unparalleled craftsmanship, it is tended by Eorlund Gray-Mane, widely regarded as the finest blacksmith in Skyrim. The forge’s searing heat is used to craft powerful weapons and armor, as well as to light the funeral pyres of fallen Companions, intertwining its purpose with the traditions and legacy of the order.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('temple_of_kynareth', 'The Temple of Kynareth is a humble yet sacred sanctuary located in Whiterun, dedicated to the worship of Kynareth, the goddess of nature, wind, and the heavens. Within its serene walls, Danica Pure-Spring and Acolyte Jenssen tirelessly tend to the wounded, providing healing and solace to those affected by the ongoing war between the Imperials and Stormcloaks.
', '''acolyt'':40B ''affect'':53B ''and'':28B,39B,49B,61B ''betw'':58B ''by'':54B ''danic'':35B ''dedicat'':17B ''goddess'':24B ''healing'':48B ''heavens'':30B ''humbl'':10B ''imperials'':60B ''in'':15B ''is'':8B ''its'':32B ''jenss'':41B ''kynareth'':3A,7B,22B ''locat'':14B ''natur'':26B ''of'':2A,6B,21B,25B ''ongoing'':56B ''providing'':47B ''pur'':37B ''pure-spring'':36B ''sacr'':12B ''sanctuary'':13B ''seren'':33B ''solac'':50B ''spring'':38B ''stormcloaks'':62B ''templ'':1A,5B ''tend'':43B ''the'':4B,19B,23B,29B,45B,55B,59B ''thos'':52B ''tirelessly'':42B ''to'':18B,44B,51B ''walls'':34B ''war'':57B ''whiterun'':16B ''wind'':27B ''within'':31B ''worship'':20B ''wound'':46B ''yet'':11B', 'whiterun, priest', 'The Temple of Kynareth is a humble yet sacred sanctuary located in Whiterun, dedicated to the worship of Kynareth, the goddess of nature, wind, and the heavens. You do not know the head priest of this temple.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('warmaiden''s', 'Warmaiden''s is a bustling smithy and weapons shop located just inside Whiterun''s main gate. Owned and operated by Ulfberth War-Bear and his wife, Adrianne Avenicci, the store provides a wide selection of weapons, armor, and smithing supplies to adventurers and city residents alike.

The shop features a single trading area where a variety of finely crafted wares are displayed, reflecting the skill and dedication of its proprietors. Adrianne, a talented blacksmith, often works at the forge outside, crafting and refining goods, while Ulfberth manages sales inside.', '''adriann'':30B,74B ''adventurers'':45B ''alik'':49B ''and'':9B,20B,27B,41B,46B,69B,85B ''are'':56B,64B ''armor'':40B ''at'':80B ''avenicci'':31B ''bear'':26B ''blacksmith'':77B ''bustling'':7B ''by'':22B ''city'':47B ''craft'':62B ''crafting'':84B ''dedication'':70B ''display'':65B ''featur'':52B ''finely'':61B ''forg'':82B ''gat'':18B ''goods'':87B ''his'':28B ''insid'':14B,92B ''is'':5B ''its'':72B ''just'':13B ''locat'':12B ''main'':17B ''manag'':90B ''of'':38B,60B,71B ''often'':78B ''operat'':21B ''outsid'':83B ''owned'':19B ''proprietors'':73B ''provid'':34B ''refining'':86B ''reflecting'':66B ''residents'':48B ''s'':2A,4B,16B ''sal'':91B ''selection'':37B ''shop'':11B,51B ''singl'':54B ''skill'':68B ''smithing'':42B ''smithy'':8B ''stor'':33B ''suppli'':43B ''talent'':76B ''the'':32B,50B,67B,81B ''to'':44B ''trading'':55B ''ulfberth'':23B,89B ''variety'':59B ''war'':25B,63B ''war-b'':24B ''warmaid'':1A,3B ''weapons'':10B,39B ''wher'':57B ''whil'':88B ''whiterun'':15B ''wid'':36B ''wif'':29B ''works'':79B', 'whiterun', 'Warmaiden''s is a bustling smithy and weapons shop located just inside Whiterun''s main gate. You do not know who owns it.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ysolda''s_house', 'Ysolda''s House is a modest residence in Whiterun, tucked behind Arcadia''s Cauldron and Belethor''s General Goods. This simple home belongs to Ysolda, an ambitious local aspiring to become a prominent merchant in the city. She lives here alone, reflecting her independent and determined nature.', '''alon'':44B ''ambitious'':30B ''an'':29B ''and'':18B,48B ''arcadi'':15B ''aspiring'':32B ''becom'':34B ''behind'':14B ''belethor'':19B ''belongs'':26B ''cauldron'':17B ''city'':40B ''determin'':49B ''general'':21B ''goods'':22B ''her'':43B,46B ''hom'':25B ''hous'':3A,6B ''in'':11B,38B ''independent'':47B ''is'':7B ''liv'':42B ''local'':31B ''merchant'':37B ''modest'':9B ''natur'':50B ''prominent'':36B ''reflecting'':45B ''residenc'':10B ''s'':2A,5B,16B,20B ''she'':41B ''simpl'':24B ''the'':39B ''this'':23B ''to'':27B,33B ''tuck'':13B ''whiterun'':12B ''ysold'':1A,4B,28B', 'whiterun', 'Ysolda''s House is a modest residence in Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bleakfalls_barrow', 'Bleak Falls Barrow is an ancient and foreboding ruin, steeped in local legend and mystery. located on the hills north of Riverwood. It is  seen as a place of danger, thought to be inhabited by restless spirits and the undead, such as the draugr that are said to roam its dark halls. There are said to be old Nordic treasures hidden within, though few dare to venture inside due to its reputation for being cursed.It is seen as  as a relic of a long-lost past, but only the bravest or most desperate would consider exploring its depths.

It’s also known as the site of a valuable artifact, the Dragonstone, which was once sought by a group of adventurers but is said to be hidden deep within the barrow. There are rumors of the ancient knowledge or power buried within Bleak Falls Barrow, but it’s generally regarded as a dangerous and mysterious place best avoided.', '''adventurers'':123B ''also'':104B ''an'':7B ''ancient'':8B,139B ''and'':9B,16B,40B,156B ''are'':48B,56B,135B ''artifact'':112B ''as'':28B,44B,80B,81B,106B,153B ''avoid'':160B ''barrow'':2A,5B,133B,147B ''be'':35B,59B,128B ''being'':76B ''best'':159B ''bleak'':3B,145B ''bleakfalls'':1A ''bravest'':93B ''buri'':143B ''but'':90B,124B,148B ''by'':37B,119B ''consid'':98B ''cursed.it'':77B ''dang'':32B ''dangerous'':155B ''dar'':67B ''dark'':53B ''deep'':130B ''depths'':101B ''desperat'':96B ''dragonston'':114B ''draugr'':46B ''due'':71B ''exploring'':99B ''falls'':4B,146B ''few'':66B ''for'':75B ''foreboding'':10B ''generally'':151B ''group'':121B ''halls'':54B ''hidd'':63B,129B ''hills'':21B ''in'':13B ''inhabit'':36B ''insid'':70B ''is'':6B,26B,78B,125B ''it'':25B,102B,149B ''its'':52B,73B,100B ''knowledg'':140B ''known'':105B ''legend'':15B ''local'':14B ''locat'':18B ''long'':87B ''long-lost'':86B ''lost'':88B ''most'':95B ''mysterious'':157B ''mystery'':17B ''nordic'':61B ''north'':22B ''of'':23B,31B,84B,109B,122B,137B ''old'':60B ''on'':19B ''once'':117B ''only'':91B ''or'':94B,141B ''past'':89B ''plac'':30B,158B ''pow'':142B ''regard'':152B ''relic'':83B ''reputation'':74B ''restless'':38B ''riverwood'':24B ''roam'':51B ''ruin'':11B ''rumors'':136B ''s'':103B,150B ''said'':49B,57B,126B ''seen'':27B,79B ''sit'':108B ''sought'':118B ''spirits'':39B ''steep'':12B ''such'':43B ''that'':47B ''the'':20B,41B,45B,92B,107B,113B,132B,138B ''ther'':55B,134B ''though'':65B ''thought'':33B ''to'':34B,50B,58B,68B,72B,127B ''treasur'':62B ''unde'':42B ''valuabl'':111B ''ventur'':69B ''was'':116B ''which'':115B ''within'':64B,131B,144B ''would'':97B', '