INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('new_gnisis_cornerclub', 'New Gnisis Cornerclub is a tavern located in Windhelm''s Gray Quarter, situated next to Sadri''s Used Wares. The tavern is owned and operated by Ambarys Rendar, who tends the counter, with the help of his employee Malthyr Elenil, who is responsible for cleaning the taproom.', '''ambarys'':30B ''and'':27B ''by'':29B ''cleaning'':48B ''cornerclub'':3A,6B ''count'':35B ''elenil'':43B ''employe'':41B ''for'':47B ''gnisis'':2A,5B ''gray'':14B ''help'':38B ''his'':40B ''in'':11B ''is'':7B,25B,45B ''locat'':10B ''malthyr'':42B ''new'':1A,4B ''next'':17B ''of'':39B ''operat'':28B ''owned'':26B ''quart'':15B ''rend'':31B ''respons'':46B ''s'':13B,20B ''sadri'':19B ''situat'':16B ''taproom'':50B ''tavern'':9B,24B ''tends'':33B ''the'':23B,34B,37B,49B ''to'':18B ''used'':21B ''war'':22B ''who'':32B,44B ''windhelm'':12B ''with'':36B', 'eastmarch', 'New Gnisis Cornerclub is a tavern located in Windhelm''s Gray Quarter. You do not know who owns it.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('niranye''s_house', 'Niranye''s House is a large, single-story residence located in Windhelm, immediately to the east of the main city gates. The rear of the house is part of the city''s surrounding walls. It features a small yard between the side entrance and Calixto''s House of Curiosities.', '''and'':48B ''betw'':44B ''calixt'':49B ''city'':24B,35B ''curiositi'':53B ''east'':20B ''entranc'':47B ''featur'':40B ''gat'':25B ''hous'':3A,6B,30B,51B ''immediately'':17B ''in'':15B ''is'':7B,31B ''it'':39B ''larg'':9B ''locat'':14B ''main'':23B ''nirany'':1A,4B ''of'':21B,28B,33B,52B ''part'':32B ''rear'':27B ''residenc'':13B ''s'':2A,5B,36B,50B ''sid'':46B ''singl'':11B ''single-story'':10B ''small'':42B ''story'':12B ''surrounding'':37B ''the'':19B,22B,26B,29B,34B,45B ''to'':18B ''walls'':38B ''windhelm'':16B ''yard'':43B', 'eastmarch', 'Niranye''s House is a large, single-story residence located in Windhelm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sadri''s_used_wares', 'Sadri''s Used Wares is a general shop located in the Gray Quarter of Windhelm. Owned by Revyn Sadri, a Dunmer trader, the shop specializes in secondhand goods. Revyn also serves as a common trainer for Speech. ', '''also'':34B ''as'':36B ''by'':21B ''common'':38B ''dunm'':25B ''for'':40B ''general'':11B ''goods'':32B ''gray'':16B ''in'':14B,30B ''is'':9B ''locat'':13B ''of'':18B ''owned'':20B ''quart'':17B ''revyn'':22B,33B ''s'':2A,6B ''sadri'':1A,5B,23B ''secondhand'':31B ''serv'':35B ''shop'':12B,28B ''specializ'':29B ''speech'':41B ''the'':15B,27B ''trad'':26B ''train'':39B ''used'':3A,7B ''war'':4A,8B ''windhelm'':19B', 'eastmarch', 'Sadri''s Used Wares is a general shop located in the Gray Quarter of Windhelm. Owned by Revyn Sadri.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('temple_of_talos', 'The Temple of Talos in Windhelm, located just northwest of Candlehearth Hall, houses a shrine dedicated to Talos in front of a statue of the deity. The temple consists of a main room with a row of five wooden benches facing the statue. After the Empire signed the White-Gold Concordat with the Thalmor, outlawing the worship of Talos, this temple became the only formal one in Skyrim under the protection of Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak.

The temple is tended by two residents, Lortheim and Jora.', '''after'':47B ''and'':88B ''becam'':66B ''bench'':43B ''by'':84B ''candlehearth'':14B ''concordat'':55B ''consists'':32B ''dedicat'':19B ''deity'':29B ''empir'':49B ''facing'':44B ''fiv'':41B ''formal'':69B ''front'':23B ''gold'':54B ''hall'':15B ''hous'':16B ''in'':8B,22B,71B ''is'':82B ''jarl'':77B ''jor'':89B ''just'':11B ''locat'':10B ''lortheim'':87B ''main'':35B ''northwest'':12B ''of'':2A,6B,13B,24B,27B,33B,40B,62B,76B ''one'':70B ''only'':68B ''outlawing'':59B ''protection'':75B ''residents'':86B ''room'':36B ''row'':39B ''shrin'':18B ''sign'':50B ''skyrim'':72B ''statu'':26B,46B ''stormcloak'':79B ''tal'':3A,7B,21B,63B ''templ'':1A,5B,31B,65B,81B ''tend'':83B ''thalmor'':58B ''the'':4B,28B,30B,45B,48B,51B,57B,60B,67B,74B,80B ''this'':64B ''to'':20B ''two'':85B ''ulfric'':78B ''under'':73B ''whit'':53B ''white-gold'':52B ''windhelm'':9B ''with'':37B,56B ''wood'':42B ''worship'':61B', 'eastmarch, priest', 'The Temple of Talos in Windhelm, located just northwest of Candlehearth Hall, houses a shrine dedicated to Talos in front of a statue of the deity.  You do not know who runs the shrine.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_white_phial', 'The White Phial is an alchemical shop located on the north side of Windhelm''s market district. It is owned by Nurelion, who named the shop after the legendary artifact he has spent many years searching for. When Nurelion is unavailable, his assistant, Quintus Navale, handles the shop duties. The White Phial itself is a legendary item, crafted from the magically infused snow that fell on the Throat of the World. It is said to have the ability to replenish any fluid placed inside of it, adding to its mystique and Nurelion''s obsession with finding it.', '''ability'':81B ''adding'':90B ''after'':30B ''alchemical'':9B ''an'':8B ''and'':94B ''any'':84B ''artifact'':33B ''assistant'':46B ''by'':24B ''craft'':61B ''district'':20B ''duti'':52B ''fell'':68B ''finding'':99B ''flu'':85B ''for'':40B ''from'':62B ''handl'':49B ''hav'':79B ''his'':45B ''infus'':65B ''insid'':87B ''is'':7B,22B,43B,57B,76B ''it'':21B,75B,89B,100B ''item'':60B ''its'':92B ''itself'':56B ''legendary'':32B,59B ''locat'':11B ''magically'':64B ''many'':37B ''market'':19B ''mystiqu'':93B ''nam'':27B ''naval'':48B ''north'':14B ''nurelion'':25B,42B,95B ''obsession'':97B ''of'':16B,72B,88B ''on'':12B,69B ''owned'':23B ''phial'':3A,6B,55B ''plac'':86B ''quintus'':47B ''replenish'':83B ''s'':18B,96B ''said'':77B ''searching'':39B ''shop'':10B,29B,51B ''sid'':15B ''snow'':66B ''spent'':36B ''that'':67B ''the'':1A,4B,13B,28B,31B,50B,53B,63B,70B,73B,80B ''throat'':71B ''to'':78B,82B,91B ''unavail'':44B ''when'':41B ''whit'':2A,5B,54B ''who'':26B ''windhelm'':17B ''with'':98B ''world'':74B ''years'':38B', 'eastmarch, alchemist', 'The White Phial is an alchemical shop located on the north side of Windhelm''s market district. The White Phial itself is a legendary item, crafted from the magically infused snow that fell on the Throat of the World. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('viola_giordano''s_house', 'Viola Giordano''s House is a large, two-story Nordic-style residence located in Windhelm''s Valunstrad district. It is positioned in one of the city''s better neighborhoods, directly opposite the house of Clan Shatter-Shield and to the north of the graveyard and Hall of the Dead. Viola Giordano is the sole occupant of the house, though she is rarely seen there, spending little time in her home.', '''and'':45B,52B ''bett'':34B ''city'':32B ''clan'':41B ''dead'':56B ''directly'':36B ''district'':24B ''giordan'':2A,6B,58B ''graveyard'':51B ''hall'':53B ''her'':76B ''hom'':77B ''hous'':4A,8B,39B,65B ''in'':20B,28B,75B ''is'':9B,26B,59B,68B ''it'':25B ''larg'':11B ''littl'':73B ''locat'':19B ''neighborhoods'':35B ''nordic'':16B ''nordic-styl'':15B ''north'':48B ''occupant'':62B ''of'':30B,40B,49B,54B,63B ''one'':29B ''opposit'':37B ''position'':27B ''rarely'':69B ''residenc'':18B ''s'':3A,7B,22B,33B ''seen'':70B ''shatt'':43B ''shatter-shield'':42B ''she'':67B ''shield'':44B ''sol'':61B ''spending'':72B ''story'':14B ''style'':17B ''the'':31B,38B,47B,50B,55B,60B,64B ''ther'':71B ''though'':66B ''tim'':74B ''to'':46B ''two'':13B ''two-story'':12B ''valunstr'':23B ''viol'':1A,5B,57B ''windhelm'':21B', 'eastmarch', 'Viola Giordano''s House is a large, two-story Nordic-style residence located in Windhelm''s Valunstrad district.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('falkreath_hold', 'Falkreath Hold is a location in southern Skyrim, bordered by Cyrodiil to the south across the Jerall Mountains and Hammerfell to the west. It is the second southernmost hold in Skyrim, after the Rift. Its capital, Falkreath, lies nestled amidst dense pine forests, while the hold’s only other notable town, Helgen, is infamous as the site of the first dragon attack in Skyrim.

The hold is renowned for its mist-shrouded landscapes, giving it a timeless and seasonless quality. Towering snow-capped mountains contrast sharply with the verdant forests below, and Lake Ilinalta dominates the central region, serving as the source of the White River. Falkreath also holds Skyrim’s largest cemetery, a reflection of its bloody history of battles, and this heritage influences the names of many local shops and farms.

The region’s flora includes abundant thistles, mora tapinella, and mountain flowers, while nightshade grows more commonly here than in other parts of Skyrim. Lake Ilinalta teems with fish, and snowberry bushes thrive in the snowy eastern areas. Under Jarl Siddgeir’s rule, Falkreath retains its Imperial allegiance, though its control can shift during Skyrim’s civil conflict.', '''abundant'':143B ''across'':17B ''after'':34B ''allegianc'':185B ''also'':112B ''amidst'':42B ''and'':21B,81B,96B,126B,136B,147B,167B ''are'':175B ''as'':57B,104B ''attack'':64B ''battl'':125B ''below'':95B ''bloody'':122B ''border'':11B ''bush'':169B ''by'':12B ''can'':189B ''capital'':38B ''capp'':87B ''cemetery'':117B ''central'':101B ''civil'':194B ''commonly'':154B ''conflict'':195B ''contrast'':89B ''control'':188B ''cyrodiil'':13B ''dens'':43B ''dominat'':99B ''dragon'':63B ''during'':191B ''eastern'':174B ''falkreath'':1A,3B,39B,111B,181B ''farms'':137B ''first'':62B ''fish'':166B ''flor'':141B ''flowers'':149B ''for'':71B ''forests'':45B,94B ''giving'':77B ''grows'':152B ''hammerfell'':22B ''helg'':54B ''her'':155B ''heritag'':128B ''history'':123B ''hold'':2A,4B,31B,48B,68B ''holds'':113B ''ilinalt'':98B,163B ''imperial'':184B ''in'':8B,32B,65B,157B,171B ''includ'':142B ''infamous'':56B ''influenc'':129B ''is'':5B,27B,55B,69B ''it'':26B,78B ''its'':37B,72B,121B,183B,187B ''jarl'':177B ''jerall'':19B ''lak'':97B,162B ''landscap'':76B ''largest'':116B ''lies'':40B ''local'':134B ''location'':7B ''many'':133B ''mist'':74B ''mist-shroud'':73B ''mor'':145B,153B ''mountain'':148B ''mountains'':20B,88B ''nam'':131B ''nestl'':41B ''nightshad'':151B ''notabl'':52B ''of'':60B,107B,120B,124B,132B,160B ''only'':50B ''other'':51B,158B ''parts'':159B ''pin'':44B ''quality'':83B ''reflection'':119B ''region'':102B,139B ''renown'':70B ''retains'':182B ''rift'':36B ''riv'':110B ''rul'':180B ''s'':49B,115B,140B,179B,193B ''seasonless'':82B ''second'':29B ''serving'':103B ''sharply'':90B ''shift'':190B ''shops'':135B ''shroud'':75B ''siddg'':178B ''sit'':59B ''skyrim'':10B,33B,66B,114B,161B,192B ''snow'':86B ''snow-capp'':85B ''snowberry'':168B ''snowy'':173B ''sourc'':106B ''south'':16B ''southern'':9B ''southernmost'':30B ''tapinell'':146B ''teems'':164B ''than'':156B ''the'':15B,18B,24B,28B,35B,47B,58B,61B,67B,92B,100B,105B,108B,130B,138B,172B ''this'':127B ''thistl'':144B ''though'':186B ''thriv'':170B ''timeless'':80B ''to'':14B,23B ''towering'':84B ''town'':53B ''under'':176B ''verdant'':93B ''west'':25B ''whil'':46B,150B ''whit'':109B ''with'':91B,165B', 'falkreath, noble, scholar', 'Falkreath Hold is a location in southern Skyrim, bordered by Cyrodiil to the south across the Jerall Mountains and Hammerfell to the west. It is the second southernmost hold in Skyrim, after the Rift. Its capital, Falkreath, lies nestled amidst dense pine forests, while the hold’s only other notable town, Helgen, is infamous as the site of the first dragon attack in Skyrim.

The hold is renowned for its mist-shrouded landscapes, giving it a timeless and seasonless quality. Towering snow-capped mountains contrast sharply with the verdant forests below, and Lake Ilinalta dominates the central region, serving as the source of the White River. Falkreath also holds Skyrim’s largest cemetery, a reflection of its bloody history of battles, and this heritage influences the names of many local shops and farms.', '', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('falkreath', 'Falkreath is a city in the south of Skyrim and serves as the capital of Falkreath Hold. Situated near the borders of Cyrodiil and Hammerfell, it was historically considered part of Cyrodiil but is now firmly within Skyrim''s boundaries. Governed by Jarl Siddgeir, Falkreath is initially aligned with the Empire, though its allegiance may shift during Skyrim''s civil war.

The city''s economy thrives on lumber harvested from its expansive surrounding forests. Falkreath''s most notable feature is its vast cemetery, the largest in Skyrim, which holds generations of the dead. This burial ground is a cultural cornerstone for its residents, influencing the names of many local businesses and homes. The cemetery symbolizes Falkreath''s deep connection to its history and the legacy of its fallen.

Falkreath Hold is a location in southern Skyrim, bordered by Cyrodiil to the south across the Jerall Mountains and Hammerfell to the west. It is the second southernmost hold in Skyrim, after the Rift. Its capital, Falkreath, lies nestled amidst dense pine forests, while the hold’s only other notable town, Helgen, is infamous as the site of the first dragon attack in Skyrim.', '''across'':144B ''after'':161B ''align'':49B ''allegianc'':55B ''amidst'':169B ''and'':11B,25B,112B,124B,148B ''as'':13B,184B ''attack'':191B ''border'':138B ''borders'':22B ''boundari'':41B ''burial'':96B ''business'':111B ''but'':34B ''by'':43B,139B ''capital'':15B,165B ''cemetery'':84B,115B ''city'':5B,64B ''civil'':61B ''connection'':120B ''consider'':30B ''cornerston'':101B ''cultural'':100B ''cyrodiil'':24B,33B,140B ''dead'':94B ''deep'':119B ''dens'':170B ''dragon'':190B ''during'':58B ''economy'':66B ''empir'':52B ''expansiv'':73B ''falkreath'':1A,2B,17B,46B,76B,117B,130B,166B ''fall'':129B ''featur'':80B ''firmly'':37B ''first'':189B ''for'':102B ''forests'':75B,172B ''from'':71B ''generations'':91B ''govern'':42B ''ground'':97B ''hammerfell'':26B,149B ''harvest'':70B ''helg'':181B ''historically'':29B ''history'':123B ''hold'':18B,131B,158B,175B ''holds'':90B ''hom'':113B ''in'':6B,87B,135B,159B,192B ''infamous'':183B ''influencing'':105B ''initially'':48B ''is'':3B,35B,47B,81B,98B,132B,154B,182B ''it'':27B,153B ''its'':54B,72B,82B,103B,122B,128B,164B ''jarl'':44B ''jerall'':146B ''largest'':86B ''legacy'':126B ''lies'':167B ''local'':110B ''location'':134B ''lumb'':69B ''many'':109B ''may'':56B ''most'':78B ''mountains'':147B ''nam'':107B ''near'':20B ''nestl'':168B ''notabl'':79B,179B ''now'':36B ''of'':9B,16B,23B,32B,92B,108B,127B,187B ''on'':68B ''only'':177B ''other'':178B ''part'':31B ''pin'':171B ''residents'':104B ''rift'':163B ''s'':40B,60B,65B,77B,118B,176B ''second'':156B ''serv'':12B ''shift'':57B ''siddg'':45B ''sit'':186B ''situat'':19B ''skyrim'':10B,39B,59B,88B,137B,1