INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wreck_of_the_icerunner', 'The Wreck of the Icerunner is a location east of Solitude, where an Imperial ship has run aground. The ship was originally transporting passengers and cargo between Skyrim and Cyrodiil, there are rumors that a noteable imperial scholar, who you do not know the name of, was looking for a rare unkown artifact in Skyrim.', '''aground'':22B ''an'':17B ''and'':29B,33B ''are'':36B ''artifact'':57B ''betw'':31B ''carg'':30B ''cyrodiil'':34B ''do'':45B ''east'':13B ''for'':53B ''icerunn'':4A,9B ''imperial'':18B,41B ''in'':58B ''is'':10B ''know'':47B ''location'':12B ''looking'':52B ''nam'':49B ''not'':46B ''noteabl'':40B ''of'':2A,7B,14B,50B ''originally'':26B ''passengers'':28B ''rar'':55B ''rumors'':37B ''run'':21B ''schol'':42B ''ship'':19B,24B ''skyrim'':32B,59B ''solitud'':15B ''that'':38B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,23B,48B ''ther'':35B ''transporting'':27B ''unkown'':56B ''was'':25B,51B ''wher'':16B ''who'':43B ''wreck'':1A,6B ''you'':44B', 'hjaalmarch, sailor', 'The Wreck of the Icerunner is a location east of Solitude, where an Imperial ship has run aground. The ship was originally transporting passengers and cargo between Skyrim and Cyrodiil, there are rumors that a noteable imperial scholar, who you do not know the name of, was looking for a rare unkown artifact in Skyrim.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('eldersblood_peak', 'Eldersblood Peak is a mountaintop dragon lair located south of Morthal and north-northeast of Rannveig''s Fast in Hjaalmarch. To reach Eldersblood Peak from the north, travelers should take the main road south of Morthal, then look for a dirt path on the left that winds past an unmarked hunter''s camp and North Cold Rock Pass.', '''an'':52B ''and'':14B,57B ''camp'':56B ''cold'':59B ''dirt'':44B ''dragon'':8B ''eldersblood'':1A,3B,26B ''fast'':21B ''for'':42B ''from'':28B ''hjaalmarch'':23B ''hunt'':54B ''in'':22B ''is'':5B ''lair'':9B ''left'':48B ''locat'':10B ''look'':41B ''main'':35B ''morthal'':13B,39B ''mountaintop'':7B ''north'':16B,30B,58B ''north-northeast'':15B ''northeast'':17B ''of'':12B,18B,38B ''on'':46B ''pass'':61B ''past'':51B ''path'':45B ''peak'':2A,4B,27B ''rannveig'':19B ''reach'':25B ''road'':36B ''rock'':60B ''s'':20B,55B ''should'':32B ''south'':11B,37B ''tak'':33B ''that'':49B ''the'':29B,34B,47B ''then'':40B ''to'':24B ''travelers'':31B ''unmark'':53B ''winds'':50B', 'hjaalmarch, dragon', 'Eldersblood Peak is a mountaintop dragon lair located south of Morthal in Hjaalmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skyborn_altar', 'Skyborn Altar is a mountaintop dragon lair located east-southeast of Morthal and south of Stonehills in Hjaalmarch. The path to the altar can be accessed from the south by traveling between Silent Moons Camp and Dustman''s Cairn, with a dirt path marked by two stone bird heads flanking the base of stone steps leading up the mountain.', '''access'':29B ''altar'':2A,4B,26B ''and'':16B,39B ''bas'':55B ''be'':28B ''betw'':35B ''bird'':51B ''by'':33B,48B ''cairn'':42B ''camp'':38B ''can'':27B ''dirt'':45B ''dragon'':8B ''dustm'':40B ''east'':12B ''east-southeast'':11B ''flanking'':53B ''from'':30B ''heads'':52B ''hjaalmarch'':21B ''in'':20B ''is'':5B ''lair'':9B ''leading'':59B ''locat'':10B ''mark'':47B ''moons'':37B ''morthal'':15B ''mountain'':62B ''mountaintop'':7B ''of'':14B,18B,56B ''path'':23B,46B ''s'':41B ''silent'':36B ''skyborn'':1A,3B ''south'':17B,32B ''southeast'':13B ''steps'':58B ''ston'':50B,57B ''stonehills'':19B ''the'':22B,25B,31B,54B,61B ''to'':24B ''traveling'':34B ''two'':49B ''up'':60B ''with'':43B', 'hjaalmarch, dragon', 'Skyborn Altar is a mountaintop dragon lair located east-southeast of Morthal and in Hjaalmarch. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('jorgen_and_lami''s_house', 'Jorgen and Lami''s House is a modest, one-room cottage located on the outskirts of Morthal, across from the town''s lumber mill. The house is home to Jorgen, a Nord lumberjack, and his wife Lami, who runs the Thaumaturgist''s Hut in Morthal as the town''s apothecary.', '''across'':24B ''and'':2A,7B,40B ''apothecary'':56B ''as'':52B ''cottag'':17B ''from'':25B ''his'':41B ''hom'':34B ''hous'':5A,10B,32B ''hut'':49B ''in'':50B ''is'':11B,33B ''jorg'':1A,6B,36B ''lami'':3A,8B,43B ''locat'':18B ''lumb'':29B ''lumberjack'':39B ''mill'':30B ''modest'':13B ''morthal'':23B,51B ''nord'':38B ''of'':22B ''on'':19B ''one'':15B ''one-room'':14B ''outskirts'':21B ''room'':16B ''runs'':45B ''s'':4A,9B,28B,48B,55B ''thaumaturgist'':47B ''the'':20B,26B,31B,46B,53B ''to'':35B ''town'':27B,54B ''who'':44B ''wif'':42B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Jorgen and Lami''s House is located in Morthal. You do not know the occupents of the house.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_apprentice_stone', 'The Apprentice Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located on an island in the marsh, just north of Fort Snowhawk and west-northwest of Morthal in Hjaalmarch. When activated, the Apprentice Stone increases magicka regeneration by a large amount but also makes the user more susceptible to magicka damage by an equally large amount, making it a powerful but risky boon for magic users.

The stone is set in a typical Standing Stone arrangement on the northeast end of a small marsh archipelago, surrounded by common marsh plants, including deathbell plants and swamp fungal pods. A nirnroot can also be found on the shoreline southeast of the stone, adding a touch of rare flora to the mystical and dangerous environment of the area.', '''across'':15B ''activat'':38B ''adding'':118B ''also'':50B,108B ''amount'':48B,63B ''an'':19B,60B ''and'':29B,101B,127B ''apprentic'':2A,5B,40B ''archipelag'':92B ''are'':132B ''arrangement'':83B ''be'':109B ''boon'':70B ''but'':49B,68B ''by'':45B,59B,94B ''can'':107B ''common'':95B ''damag'':58B ''dangerous'':128B ''deathbell'':99B ''end'':87B ''environment'':129B ''equally'':61B ''flor'':123B ''for'':71B ''fort'':27B ''found'':110B ''fungal'':103B ''hjaalmarch'':36B ''in'':21B,35B,78B ''including'':98B ''incre'':42B ''is'':7B,76B ''island'':20B ''it'':65B ''just'':24B ''larg'':47B,62B ''locat'':17B ''magic'':72B ''magick'':43B,57B ''mak'':51B ''making'':64B ''marsh'':23B,91B,96B ''mor'':54B ''morthal'':34B ''mystical'':126B ''nirnroot'':106B ''north'':25B ''northeast'':86B ''northwest'':32B ''of'':9B,26B,33B,88B,115B,121B,130B ''on'':18B,84B,111B ''one'':8B ''plants'':97B,100B ''pods'':104B ''powerful'':67B ''rar'':122B ''regeneration'':44B ''risky'':69B ''scatter'':14B ''set'':77B ''shorelin'':113B ''skyrim'':16B ''small'':90B ''snowhawk'':28B ''southeast'':114B ''standing'':12B,81B ''ston'':3A,6B,13B,41B,75B,82B,117B ''surround'':93B ''suscept'':55B ''swamp'':102B ''the'':1A,4B,10B,22B,39B,52B,74B,85B,112B,116B,125B,131B ''thirt'':11B ''to'':56B,124B ''touch'':120B ''typical'':80B ''user'':53B ''users'':73B ''west'':31B ''west-northwest'':30B ''when'':37B', 'hjaalmarch, scholar, traveler', 'The Apprentice Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located on an island in the marsh, just west-northwest of Morthal in Hjaalmarch. When activated, the Apprentice Stone increases magicka regeneration by a large amount but also makes the user more susceptible to magicka damage by an equally large amount, making it a powerful but risky boon for magic users.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_lord_stone', 'The Lord Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located east of Morthal and northeast of the Shrine of Mehrunes Dagon in Hjaalmarch. When activated, the Lord Stone grants a moderate boost to your armor rating and  a decent amount of magic resistance, making it easier to reach the armor and magic resistance caps. While it offers less defense than the Atronach Stone, it has no associated penalty, making it a more balanced defensive option.

The stone itself is perched atop a stone base, flanked by the remains of large arches. To reach the Lord Stone, follow the path that leads past the Shrine of Mehrunes Dagon, which begins to the west of the Hall of the Vigilant. The route is marked by several piles of rocks, some with remnants of banners flapping in the wind. After passing Dimhollow Crypt, ascend a flight of stone steps leading up to the shrine, then turn northeast to find the Lord Stone atop a nearby hill.', '''across'':15B ''activat'':32B ''after'':144B ''amount'':47B ''and'':21B,44B,58B ''arches'':98B ''armor'':42B,57B ''ascend'':148B ''associat'':74B ''atop'':88B,167B ''atronach'':69B ''balanc'':80B ''banners'':139B ''bas'':91B ''begins'':116B ''boost'':39B ''by'':93B,130B ''caps'':61B ''crypt'':147B ''dagon'':28B,114B ''decent'':46B ''defens'':66B ''defensiv'':81B ''dimhollow'':146B ''easi'':53B ''east'':18B ''find'':163B ''flank'':92B ''flapping'':140B ''flight'':150B ''follow'':104B ''grants'':36B ''hall'':122B ''hill'':170B ''hjaalmarch'':30B ''in'':29B,141B ''is'':7B,86B,128B ''it'':52B,63B,71B,77B ''itself'':85B ''larg'':97B ''leading'':154B ''leads'':108B ''less'':65B ''locat'':17B ''lord'':2A,5B,34B,102B,165B ''magic'':49B,59B ''making'':51B,76B ''mark'':129B ''mehrun'':27B,113B ''moderat'':38B ''mor'':79B ''morthal'':20B ''nearby'':169B ''northeast'':22B,161B ''of'':9B,19B,23B,26B,48B,96B,112B,120B,123B,133B,138B,151B ''offers'':64B ''one'':8B ''option'':82B ''passing'':145B ''past'':109B ''path'':106B ''penalty'':75B ''perch'':87B ''pil'':132B ''rating'':43B ''reach'':55B,100B ''remains'':95B ''remnants'':137B ''resistanc'':50B,60B ''rocks'':134B ''rout'':127B ''scatter'':14B ''several'':131B ''shrin'':25B,111B,158B ''skyrim'':16B ''som'':135B ''standing'':12B ''steps'':153B ''ston'':3A,6B,13B,35B,70B,84B,90B,103B,152B,166B ''than'':67B ''that'':107B ''the'':1A,4B,10B,24B,33B,56B,68B,83B,94B,101B,105B,110B,118B,121B,124B,126B,142B,157B,164B ''then'':159B ''thirt'':11B ''to'':40B,54B,99B