Haafingar is defined by a large ridge that stretches across the hold, with pine forests and meadows covering the southern slopes down to the Karth River. Jarl Elisif the Fair governs the region.', '', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('solitude', 'Solitude is a major city located on the northwest coast of Skyrim, serving as the capital of both Haafingar and the entire province. Built atop a natural arch over the Sea of Ghosts, it is the largest city in Skyrim and the seat of the province''s High King. The city is ruled by Jarl Elisif the Fair, widow of the late High King Torygg, and her throne resides in the Blue Palace.

Solitude is home to many important buildings and institutions, including the headquarters of the Imperial Legion in Skyrim, the East Empire Company Warehouse, and the Bards College. The Thalmor Embassy is located nearby, adding to the city’s political significance. Notable locations within Solitude include the Bards College, Bits and Pieces shop, Blue Palace, Castle Dour, the Fletcher, the Temple of the Divines, and the Winking Skeever inn.', '''adding'':108B ''and'':21B,42B,67B,82B,98B,124B,138B ''arch'':29B ''as'':15B ''atop'':26B ''bards'':100B,121B ''bits'':123B ''blu'':73B,127B ''both'':19B ''buildings'':81B ''built'':25B ''by'':55B ''capital'':17B ''castl'':129B ''city'':6B,39B,52B,111B ''coast'':11B ''colleg'':101B,122B ''company'':96B ''divin'':137B ''dour'':130B ''east'':94B ''elisif'':57B ''embassy'':104B ''empir'':95B ''entir'':23B ''fair'':59B ''fletch'':132B ''ghosts'':34B ''haafing'':20B ''headquarters'':86B ''her'':68B ''high'':49B,64B ''hom'':77B ''imperial'':89B ''important'':80B ''in'':40B,71B,91B ''includ'':119B ''including'':84B ''inn'':142B ''institutions'':83B ''is'':3B,36B,53B,76B,105B ''it'':35B ''jarl'':56B ''king'':50B,65B ''largest'':38B ''lat'':63B ''legion'':90B ''locat'':7B,106B ''locations'':116B ''major'':5B ''many'':79B ''natural'':28B ''nearby'':107B ''northwest'':10B ''notabl'':115B ''of'':12B,18B,33B,45B,61B,87B,135B ''on'':8B ''over'':30B ''palac'':74B,128B ''piec'':125B ''political'':113B ''provinc'':24B,47B ''resid'':70B ''rul'':54B ''s'':48B,112B ''seat'':44B ''serving'':14B ''shop'':126B ''significanc'':114B ''skeev'':141B ''skyrim'':13B,41B,92B ''solitud'':1A,2B,75B,118B ''templ'':134B ''thalmor'':103B ''the'':9B,16B,22B,31B,37B,43B,46B,51B,58B,62B,72B,85B,88B,93B,99B,102B,110B,120B,131B,133B,136B,139B ''thron'':69B ''to'':78B,109B ''torygg'':66B ''warehous'':97B ''widow'':60B ''winking'':140B ''within'':117B', 'haafingar, noble, scholar', 'Solitude is a major city located on the northwest coast of Skyrim, serving as the capital of both Haafingar and the entire province. Built atop a natural arch over the Sea of Ghosts, it is the largest city in Skyrim and the seat of the province''s High King. The city is ruled by Jarl Elisif the Fair, widow of the late High King Torygg, and her throne resides in the Blue Palace.', '', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('blue_palace', 'The Blue Palace is the seat of power for Solitude, Haafingar, and all of Skyrim. It serves as the home of Jarl Elisif the Fair, the current High Queen of Skyrim, following the death of her husband, High King Torygg. Perched on the tip of the arch that Solitude is built upon, the palace is an imposing structure that commands attention, especially once you pass Castle Dour. The palace walls are part of Solitude’s city walls, built on the edge of the natural arch overlooking the Sea of Ghosts. The Blue Palace is located on the south side of Solitude, and it is home to several key figures: Bolgeir Bearclaw, the housecarl; Falk Firebeard, the steward; and Sybille Stentor, the court wizard.', '''all'':15B ''an'':58B ''and'':14B,104B,120B ''arch'':49B,87B ''are'':73B ''as'':20B ''attention'':63B ''bearclaw'':113B ''blu'':1A,4B,94B ''bolg'':112B ''built'':53B,80B ''castl'':68B ''city'':78B ''commands'':62B ''court'':124B ''current'':29B ''death'':36B ''dour'':69B ''edge'':83B ''elisif'':25B ''especially'':64B ''fair'':27B ''falk'':116B ''figur'':111B ''firebeard'':117B ''following'':34B ''for'':11B ''ghosts'':92B ''haafing'':13B ''her'':38B ''high'':30B,40B ''hom'':22B,107B ''housecarl'':115B ''husband'':39B ''imposing'':59B ''is'':6B,52B,57B,96B,106B ''it'':18B,105B ''jarl'':24B ''key'':110B ''king'':41B ''locat'':97B ''natural'':86B ''of'':9B,16B,23B,32B,37B,47B,75B,84B,91B,102B ''on'':44B,81B,98B ''once'':65B ''overlooking'':88B ''palac'':2A,5B,56B,71B,95B ''part'':74B ''pass'':67B ''perch'':43B ''pow'':10B ''que'':31B ''s'':77B ''seat'':8B ''serv'':19B ''several'':109B ''sid'':101B ''skyrim'':17B,33B ''solitud'':12B,51B,76B,103B ''south'':100B ''stentor'':122B ''steward'':119B ''structur'':60B ''sybill'':121B ''that'':50B,61B ''the'':3B,7B,21B,26B,28B,35B,45B,48B,55B,70B,82B,85B,89B,93B,99B,114B,118B,123B ''tip'':46B ''to'':108B ''torygg'':42B ''upon'':54B ''walls'':72B,79B ''wizard'':125B ''you'':66B', 'haafingar, noble, scholar', 'The Blue Palace is the seat of power for Solitude, Haafingar, and all of Skyrim. It serves as the home of Jarl Elisif the Fair, the current High Queen of Skyrim, following the death of her husband, High King Torygg. Perched on the tip of the arch that Solitude is built upon, the palace is an imposing structure that commands attention.', '', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ironback_hideout', 'Ironback Hideout is a dilapidated house located to the northwest of Solitude, a short distance east of The Steed Stone in Haafingar. The structure is in ruins, with no roof, windows, or doors, and has been taken over by a group of bandits, including a bandit chief.

The hideout can be accessed by following the road towards the Thalmor Embassy, turning west once you are east of the house.', '''access'':54B ''and'':36B ''are'':67B ''bandit'':48B ''bandits'':45B ''be'':53B ''been'':38B ''by'':41B,55B ''can'':52B ''chief'':49B ''dilapidat'':7B ''distanc'':17B ''doors'':35B ''east'':18B,68B ''embassy'':62B ''following'':56B ''group'':43B ''haafing'':24B ''hideout'':2A,4B,51B ''hous'':8B,71B ''in'':23B,28B ''including'':46B ''ironback'':1A,3B ''is'':5B,27B ''locat'':9B ''northwest'':12B ''of'':13B,19B,44B,69B ''once'':65B ''or'':34B ''over'':40B ''road'':58B ''roof'':32B ''ruins'':29B ''short'':16B ''solitud'':14B ''ste'':21B ''ston'':22B ''structur'':26B ''tak'':39B ''thalmor'':61B ''the'':11B,20B,25B,50B,57B,60B,70B ''to'':10B ''towards'':59B ''turning'':63B ''west'':64B ''windows'':33B ''with'':30B ''you'':66B', 'haafingar', 'Ironback Hideout is a dilapidated house located to the northwest of Solitude in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('east_empire_company_warehouse', 'The East Empire Company Warehouse is located on the Solitude docks, immediately southeast of the city. It serves as the headquarters and main storage facility for the East Empire Company in Skyrim. The entrance to the warehouse is typically locked, and entering without permission will result in trespassing charges. A Solitude guard can often be found patrolling outside, while the warehouse''s interior is staffed by Dockworkers, the Dockmaster, and Snorreid, along with three patrolling Solitude guards.
', '''along'':76B ''and'':26B,45B,74B ''as'':23B ''be'':59B ''by'':70B ''can'':57B ''charg'':53B ''city'':20B ''company'':3A,8B,34B ''dockmast'':73B ''docks'':15B ''dockworkers'':71B ''east'':1A,6B,32B ''empir'':2A,7B,33B ''entering'':46B ''entranc'':38B ''facility'':29B ''for'':30B ''found'':60B ''guard'':56B ''guards'':81B ''headquarters'':25B ''immediately'':16B ''in'':35B,51B ''interior'':67B ''is'':10B,42B,68B ''it'':21B ''locat'':11B ''lock'':44B ''main'':27B ''of'':18B ''often'':58B ''on'':12B ''outsid'':62B ''patrolling'':61B,79B ''permission'':48B ''result'':50B ''s'':66B ''serv'':22B ''skyrim'':36B ''snorr'':75B ''solitud'':14B,55B,80B ''southeast'':17B ''staff'':69B ''storag'':28B ''the'':5B,13B,19B,24B,31B,37B,40B,64B,72B ''thre'':78B ''to'':39B ''trespassing'':52B ''typically'':43B ''warehous'':4A,9B,41B,65B ''whil'':63B ''will'':49B ''with'':77B ''without'':47B', 'haafingar, legion', 'The East Empire Company Warehouse is located on the Solitude docks, immediately southeast of the city. It serves as the headquarters and main storage facility for the East Empire Company in Skyrim.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orphan''s_tear', 'Orphan''s Tear is a shipwreck located west of Ravenscar Hollow on the northern coast of Haafingar. The wreck is inhabited by bandits who have made it their hideout.', '''bandits'':26B ''by'':25B ''coast'':18B ''haafing'':20B ''hav'':28B ''hideout'':32B ''hollow'':14B ''inhabit'':24B ''is'':7B,23B ''it'':30B ''locat'':10B ''mad'':29B ''northern'':17B ''of'':12B,19B ''on'':15B ''orphan'':1A,4B ''ravensc'':13B ''s'':2A,5B ''shipwreck'':9B ''tear'':3A,6B ''the'':16B,21B,31B ''west'':11B ''who'':27B ''wreck'':22B', 'haafingar', 'Orphan''s Tear is a shipwreck located on the northern coast of Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.
', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('thalmor_embassy', 'The Thalmor Embassy is a heavily guarded diplomatic compound located northwest of Solitude, in Haafingar. It serves as the headquarters for the Aldmeri Dominion''s operations in Skyrim and is a focal point for Thalmor activity in the province. 

The embassy is led by Elenwen, the Thalmor ambassador, who is known for hosting extravagant parties attended by Skyrim''s most influential figures. The building is a center for the Thalmor''s political maneuvering in Skyrim, and it is here that you infiltrate the compound using a forged invitation as part of the main quest. The embassy is situated in a remote area, east of Ironback Hideout, making it a secretive and well-protected location.', '''activity'':38B ''aldmeri'':25B ''ambass'':50B ''and'':31B,78B,113B ''are'':104B ''as'':20B,91B ''attend'':58B ''building'':66B ''by'':46B,59B ''cent'':69B ''compound'':11B,86B ''diplomatic'':10B ''dominion'':26B ''east'':105B ''elenw'':47B ''embassy'':2A,5B,43B,98B ''extravagant'':56B ''figur'':64B ''focal'':34B ''for'':23B,36B,54B,70B ''forg'':89B ''guard'':9B ''haafing'':17B ''headquarters'':22B ''heavily'':8B ''her'':81B ''hideout'':108B ''hosting'':55B ''in'':16B,29B,39B,76B,101B ''infiltrat'':84B ''influential'':63B ''invitation'':90B ''ironback'':107B ''is'':6B,32B,44B,52B,67B,80B,99B ''it'':18B,79B,110B ''known'':53B ''led'':45B ''locat'':12B ''location'':117B ''main'':95B ''making'':109B ''maneuvering'':75B ''most'':62B ''northwest'':13B ''of'':14B,93B,106B ''operations'':28B ''part'':92B ''parti'':57B ''point'':35B ''political'':74B ''protect'':116B ''provinc'':41B ''quest'':96B ''remot'':103B ''s'':27B,61B,73B ''secretiv'':112B ''serv'':19B ''situat'':100B ''skyrim'':30B,60B,77B ''solitud'':15B ''thalmor'':1A,4B,37B,49B,72B ''that'':82B ''the'':3B,21B,24B,40B,42B,48B,65B,71B,85B,94B,97B ''using'':87B ''well'':115B ''well-protect'':114B ''who'':51B ''you'':83B', 'haafingar, thalmor, legion', 'The Thalmor Embassy is a heavily guarded diplomatic compound located northwest of Solitude, in Haafingar. It serves as the headquarters for the Aldmeri Dominion''s operations in Skyrim and is a focal point for Thalmor activity in the province. You do not know who runs the embassy.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragon_bridge', 'Dragon Bridge is a small town located in northwestern Skyrim, near the iconic Dragon Bridge, southwest of the Statue to Meridia and east-southeast of Deepwood Redoubt. The town and its famous bridge are of strategic importance in the civil war, as both the Stormcloaks and Imperials view it as a key location.', '''and'':24B,33B,49B ''are'':37B ''as'':45B,53B ''both'':46B ''bridg'':2A,4B,17B,36B ''civil'':43B ''deepwood'':29B ''dragon'':1A,3B,16B ''east'':26B ''east-southeast'':25B ''famous'':35B ''iconic'':15B ''imperials'':50B ''importanc'':40B ''in'':10B,41B ''is'':5B ''it'':52B ''its'':34B ''key'':55B ''locat'':9B ''location'':56B ''meridi'':23B ''near'':13B ''northwestern'':11B ''of'':19B,28B,38B ''redoubt'':30B ''skyrim'':12B ''small'':7B ''southeast'':27B ''southwest'':18B ''statu'':21B ''stormcloaks'':48B ''strategic'':39B ''the'':14B,20B,31B,42B,47B ''to'':22B ''town'':8B,32B ''view'':51B ''war'':44B', 'haafingar, scholar', 'Dragon Bridge is a small town located in northwestern Skyrim, near the iconic Dragon Bridge, south of Solitude. The town and its famous bridge are of strategic importance in the civil war, as both the Stormcloaks and Imperials view it as a key location.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('katla''s_farm', 'Katla''s Farm is a small farm and stable located along the Karth River, just outside of Solitude. The farm is owned by Katla, who lives there with her husband Snilling and their son Knud. The farm is situated southwest of Solitude, west of the East Empire Company Warehouse, offering a peaceful rural setting in the shadow of the bustling city.', '''along'':14B ''and'':11B,35B ''bustling'':63B ''by'':26B ''city'':64B ''company'':51B ''east'':49B ''empir'':50B ''farm'':3A,6B,10B,23B,40B ''her'':32B ''husband'':33B ''in'':58B ''is'':7B,24B,41B ''just'':18B ''karth'':16B ''katl'':1A,4B,27B ''knud'':38B ''liv'':29B ''locat'':13B ''of'':20B,44B,47B,61B ''offering'':53B ''outsid'':19B ''owned'':25B ''peaceful'':55B ''riv'':17B ''rural'':56B ''s'':2A,5B ''setting'':57B ''shadow'':60B ''situat'':42B ''small'':9B ''snilling'':34B ''solitud'':21B,45B ''southwest'':43B ''stabl'':12B ''the'':15B,22B,36B,39B,48B,59B,62B ''ther'':30B ''warehous'':52B ''west'':46B ''who'':28B ''with'':31B', 'haafingar', 'Katla''s Farm is a small farm and stable located along the Karth River, just outside of Solitude. The farm is owned by Katla who you do not know.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('solitude_sawmill', 'Solitude Sawmill is a wood mill located southwest of Solitude in Haafingar. The sawmill consists of a house and the mill itself, and is owned by Hjorunn, a Nord who works alongside his employee, Kharag gro-Shurkul, an Orc. ', '''alongsid'':34B ''an'':41B ''and'':21B,25B ''by'':28B ''consists'':17B ''employe'':36B ''gro'':39B ''gro-shurkul'':38B ''haafing'':14B ''his'':35B ''hjorunn'':29B ''hous'':20B ''in'':13B ''is'':5B,26B ''itself'':24B ''kharag'':37B ''locat'':9B ''mill'':8B,23B ''nord'':31B ''of'':11B,18B ''orc'':42B ''owned'':27B ''sawmill'':2A,4B,16B ''shurkul'':40B ''solitud'':1A,3B,12B ''southwest'':10B ''the'':15B,22B ''who'':32B ''wood'':7B ''works'':33B', 'haafingar', 'Solitude Sawmill is a wood mill located southwest of Solitude in Haafingar. You do not know who runs the mill.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('haafingar_stormcloak_camp', 'Haafingar Stormcloak Camp is a Stormcloak military encampment located northeast of Dragon Bridge and south of the Statue to Meridia in Haafingar. This camp serves as a base for Stormcloak forces operating in the region during the civil war.', '''and'':17B ''as'':29B ''bas'':31B ''bridg'':16B ''camp'':3A,6B,27B ''civil'':41B ''dragon'':15B ''during'':39B ''encampment'':11B ''for'':32B ''forc'':34B ''haafing'':1A,4B,25B ''in'':24B,36B ''is'':7B ''locat'':12B ''meridi'':23B ''military'':10B ''northeast'':13B ''of'':14B,19B ''operating'':35B ''region'':38B ''serv'':28B ''south'':18B ''statu'':21B ''stormcloak'':2A,5B,9B,33B ''the'':20B,37B,40B ''this'':26B ''to'':22B ''war'':42B', 'haafingar, stormcloak', 'Haafingar Stormcloak Camp is a Stormcloak military encampment located northeast of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fort_hraggstad', 'Fort Hraggstad is a medium-sized fort located west of Solitude and east of Steepfall Burrow in Haafingar.  It is occupied by bandits, the fort serves as a stronghold in the region, offering a strategic vantage point.', '''and'':15B ''as'':30B ''bandits'':26B ''burrow'':19B ''by'':25B ''east'':16B ''fort'':1A,3B,10B,28B ''haafing'':21B ''hraggst'':2A,4B ''in'':20B,33B ''is'':5B,23B ''it'':22B ''locat'':11B ''medium'':8B ''medium-siz'':7B ''occupi'':24B ''of'':13B,17B ''offering'':36B ''point'':40B ''region'':35B ''serv'':29B ''siz'':9B ''solitud'':14B ''steepfall'':18B ''strategic'':38B ''stronghold'':32B ''the'':27B,34B ''vantag'':39B ''west'':12B', 'haafingar, legion, stormcloak', 'Fort Hraggstad is a medium-sized fort located west of Solitude in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('northwatch_keep', 'Northwatch Keep is a small fort located northwest of Dragon Bridge and north of Rimerock Burrow in Haafingar. The fort is occupied by the Thalmor and serves as a prison, off-limits to anyone not authorized by the Thalmor.', '''and'':14B,28B ''anyon'':37B ''as'':30B ''authoriz'':39B ''bridg'':13B ''burrow'':18B ''by'':25B,40B ''dragon'':12B ''fort'':8B,22B ''haafing'':20B ''in'':19B ''is'':5B,23B ''keep'':2A,4B ''limits'':35B ''locat'':9B ''north'':15B ''northwatch'':1A,3B ''northwest'':10B ''not'':38B ''occupi'':24B ''of'':11B,16B ''off'':34B ''off-limits'':33B ''prison'':32B ''rimerock'':17B ''serv'':29B ''small'':7B ''thalmor'':27B,42B ''the'':21B,26B,41B ''to'':36B', 'haafingar, thalmor', 'Northwatch Keep is a small fort located northwest of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('castle_volkihar', 'Castle Volkihar is a large, ominous castle located on an island far northwest of Solitude, connected to Volkihar Keep. It serves as the base of operations for the Volkihar Vampire Clan. To reach Castle Volkihar, you can hire a rowboat at Dawnstar or Icewater Jetty.', '''an'':12B ''as'':24B ''at'':43B ''bas'':26B ''can'':39B ''castl'':1A,3B,9B,36B ''clan'':33B ''connect'':18B ''dawnst'':44B ''far'':14B ''for'':29B ''hir'':40B ''icewat'':46B ''is'':5B ''island'':13B ''it'':22B ''jetty'':47B ''keep'':21B ''larg'':7B ''locat'':10B ''northwest'':15B ''of'':16B,27B ''ominous'':8B ''on'':11B ''operations'':28B ''or'':45B ''reach'':35B ''rowboat'':42B ''serv'':23B ''solitud'':17B ''the'':25B,30B ''to'':19B,34B ''vampir'':32B ''volkih'':2A,4B,20B,31B,37B ''you'':38B', 'haafingar, volkihar, dawnguard, vampire', 'Castle Volkihar is a large, ominous castle located on an island far northwest of Solitude, connected to Volkihar Keep. Rumors of a powerful vampire clan lives here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pinefrost_tower', 'Pinefrost Tower is a small, ruined tower located northwest of Dragon Bridge and south of Rimerock Burrow in Haafingar. Perched atop the western mountains of Haafingar, the fallen tower lies a short distance south of Northwatch Keep.', '''and'':15B ''atop'':23B ''bridg'':14B ''burrow'':19B ''distanc'':35B ''dragon'':13B ''fall'':30B ''haafing'':21B,28B ''in'':20B ''is'':5B ''keep'':39B ''lies'':32B ''locat'':10B ''mountains'':26B ''northwatch'':38B ''northwest'':11B ''of'':12B,17B,27B,37B ''perch'':22B ''pinefrost'':1A,3B ''rimerock'':18B ''ruin'':8B ''short'':34B ''small'':7B ''south'':16B,36B ''the'':24B,29B ''tow'':2A,4B,9B,31B ''western'':25B', 'haafingar', 'Pinefrost Tower is a small, ruined tower located northwest of Dragon Bridge  in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
