The site is marked by the remnants of ancient Nordic architecture, and its crumbling halls and towers make it a haunting place to visit.', '''ancient'':35B ''and'':14B,38B,42B ''architectur'':37B ''bandits'':26B ''by'':31B ''crumbling'':40B ''haafing'':20B ''halls'':41B ''haunting'':47B ''hom'':24B ''in'':19B ''is'':3B,23B,29B ''it'':45B ''its'':39B ''locat'':10B ''mak'':44B ''mark'':30B ''medium'':6B ''medium-siz'':5B ''nordic'':8B,36B ''of'':12B,16B,34B ''pinefrost'':17B ''plac'':48B ''remnants'':33B ''ruin'':9B,22B ''sit'':28B ''siz'':7B ''solitud'':13B ''southeast'':15B ''the'':21B,27B,32B ''to'':25B,49B ''tow'':18B ''towers'':43B ''visit'':50B ''volskygg'':1A,2B ''west'':11B', 'haafingar', 'Volskygge is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located west of Solitude in Haafingar..
