INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hag''s_end', 'Hag''s End is a small Nordic ruin located west of Dragon Bridge, within Deepwood Vale in The Reach. The site is home to a hagraven, hags, and witches, making it a dangerous and eerie destination for adventurers.

Hag''s End is only accessible via Deepwood Redoubt, a fort situated in the mountains west of Dragon Bridge, south of the barrow Volskygge.', '''access'':47B ''adventurers'':41B ''and'':31B,37B ''barrow'':64B ''bridg'':16B,60B ''dangerous'':36B ''deepwood'':18B,49B ''destination'':39B ''dragon'':15B,59B ''eeri'':38B ''end'':3A,6B,44B ''for'':40B ''fort'':52B ''hag'':1A,4B,42B ''hagrav'':29B ''hags'':30B ''hom'':26B ''in'':20B,54B ''is'':7B,25B,45B ''it'':34B ''locat'':12B ''making'':33B ''mountains'':56B ''nordic'':10B ''of'':14B,58B,62B ''only'':46B ''reach'':22B ''redoubt'':50B ''ruin'':11B ''s'':2A,5B,43B ''sit'':24B ''situat'':53B ''small'':9B ''south'':61B ''the'':21B,23B,55B,63B ''to'':27B ''val'':19B ''via'':48B ''volskygg'':65B ''west'':13B,57B ''witch'':32B ''within'':17B', 'haafingar, witch', 'Hag''s End is a small Nordic ruin located west of Dragon Bridge in The Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('broken_tusk_mine', '
Broken Tusk Mine is a small heart stone mine located north of Raven Rock and southeast of Bristleback Cave on Solstheim. The mine is inhabited by rieklings, who have taken over the site and claimed it as their own.', '''and'':18B,37B ''as'':40B ''bristleback'':21B ''brok'':1A,4B ''by'':29B ''cav'':22B ''claim'':38B ''hav'':32B ''heart'':10B ''inhabit'':28B ''is'':7B,27B ''it'':39B ''locat'':13B ''min'':3A,6B,12B,26B ''north'':14B ''of'':15B,20B ''on'':23B ''over'':34B ''own'':42B ''rav'':16B ''rieklings'':30B ''rock'':17B ''sit'':36B ''small'':9B ''solstheim'':24B ''southeast'':19B ''ston'':11B ''tak'':33B ''the'':25B,35B,41B ''tusk'':2A,5B ''who'':31B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('kilkreath_ruins', 'Kilkreath Ruins is a large, ancient temple located west of Solitude and southeast of Wolfskull Cave in Haafingar. The ruins are home to corrupted shades, spectral enemies who haunt the temple''s dilapidated halls. There are rumors that a necromancer has taken over the ruins, causing the shades to appear. ', '''ancient'':8B ''and'':14B ''appe'':52B ''are'':23B,38B ''causing'':48B ''cav'':18B ''corrupt'':26B ''dilapidat'':35B ''enemi'':29B ''haafing'':20B ''halls'':36B ''haunt'':31B ''hom'':24B ''in'':19B ''is'':5B ''kilkreath'':1A,3B ''larg'':7B ''locat'':10B ''necromanc'':42B ''of'':12B,16B ''over'':45B ''ruins'':2A,4B,22B,47B ''rumors'':39B ''s'':34B ''shad'':27B,50B ''solitud'':13B ''southeast'':15B ''spectral'':28B ''tak'':44B ''templ'':9B,33B ''that'':40B ''the'':21B,32B,46B,49B ''ther'':37B ''to'':25B,51B ''west'':11B ''who'':30B ''wolfskull'':17B', 'haafingar, daedra, daedric', 'Kilkreath Ruins is a large, ancient temple located west of Solitude in Haafingar.  You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('statue_to_meridia', 'The Statue to Meridia is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince of Life and Light, Meridia. Located west of Solitude and east of Clearpine Pond in Haafingar, the statue stands as a beacon of Meridia''s influence in Skyrim. It is rumored that the Beacon of Meridia is missing from this location, hidden somewhere in Skyrim.', '''and'':18B,25B ''as'':35B ''beacon'':37B,49B ''clearpin'':28B ''daedric'':14B ''dedicat'':11B ''east'':26B ''from'':54B ''haafing'':31B ''hidd'':57B ''in'':30B,42B,59B ''influenc'':41B ''is'':8B,45B,52B ''it'':44B ''lif'':17B ''light'':19B ''locat'':21B ''location'':56B ''meridi'':3A,7B,20B,39B,51B ''missing'':53B ''of'':16B,23B,27B,38B,50B ''pond'':29B ''princ'':15B ''rumor'':46B ''s'':40B ''shrin'':10B ''skyrim'':43B,60B ''solitud'':24B ''somewher'':58B ''stands'':34B ''statu'':1A,5B,33B ''that'':47B ''the'':4B,13B,32B,48B ''this'':55B ''to'':2A,6B,12B ''west'':22B', 'haafingar, daedra, daedric', 'The Statue to Meridia is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince of Life and Light, Meridia. Located west of Solitude in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lost_echo_cave', 'Lost Echo Cave is a small cave located west of Solitude in Falkreath Hold, south of Steepfall Burrow. The cave is situated along the road that runs west of Fort Hraggstad, near the point where it turns south. The entrance is marked by piles of stones leading up to stone steps, and, unusually for a cave, the entrance is a wooden door adorned with lit candles on either side, with a statue positioned to the right. Rumors of Falmer have been seen coming out the cave late at night.', '''adorn'':66B ''along'':26B ''and'':55B ''at'':91B ''been'':84B ''burrow'':21B ''by'':46B ''candl'':69B ''cav'':3A,6B,10B,23B,59B,89B ''coming'':86B ''door'':65B ''echo'':2A,5B ''eith'':71B ''entranc'':43B,61B ''falkreath'':16B ''falm'':82B ''for'':57B ''fort'':33B ''hav'':83B ''hold'':17B ''hraggst'':34B ''in'':15B ''is'':7B,24B,44B,62B ''it'':39B ''lat'':90B ''leading'':50B ''lit'':68B ''locat'':11B ''lost'':1A,4B ''mark'':45B ''near'':35B ''night'':92B ''of'':13B,19B,32B,48B,81B ''on'':70B ''out'':87B ''pil'':47B ''point'':37B ''position'':76B ''right'':79B ''road'':28B ''rumors'':80B ''runs'':30B ''seen'':85B ''sid'':72B ''situat'':25B ''small'':9B ''solitud'':14B ''south'':18B,41B ''statu'':75B ''steepfall'':20B ''steps'':54B ''ston'':49B,53B ''that'':29B ''the'':22B,27B,36B,42B,60B,78B,88B ''to'':52B,77B ''turns'':40B ''unusually'':56B ''up'':51B ''west'':12B,31B ''wher'':38B ''with'':67B,73B ''wood'':64B', 'haafingar', 'Lost Echo Cave is a small cave located west of Solitude in Haafingar Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wolfskull_cave', 'Wolfskull Cave is a medium-sized cave located west of Solitude and southeast of Fort Hraggstad in Haafingar. The cave is rumored to be steeped in dark magic, particularly necromantic forces.', '''and'':15B ''be'':27B ''cav'':2A,4B,10B,23B ''dark'':30B ''forc'':34B ''fort'':18B ''haafing'':21B ''hraggst'':19B ''in'':20B,29B ''is'':5B,24B ''locat'':11B ''magic'':31B ''medium'':8B ''medium-siz'':7B ''necromantic'':33B ''of'':13B,17B ''particularly'':32B ''rumor'':25B ''siz'':9B ''solitud'':14B ''southeast'':16B ''steep'':28B ''the'':22B ''to'':26B ''west'':12B ''wolfskull'':1A,3B', 'haafingar', 'Wolfskull Cave is a medium-sized cave located west of Solitude in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('broken_oar_grotto', 'Broken Oar Grotto is a small cave located north of Solitude, northwest of Brinewater Grotto, along the northern tip of the coastline in Haafingar. The entrance to the cave is marked by a landslide, next to a small cave opening, with a crushed longboat visible among the rubble, rocks, and broken trees.

