INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rimerock_burrow', 'Rimerock Burrow is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge and south of Northwatch Keep in Haafingar. To reach the cave, follow a rough path that leads over a wooden bridge spanning a crevice in the cliff wall just before the entrance. The path branches off from the larger road near Pinefrost Tower, marked by a pile of rocks, though the fork can be easily missed. It is rumored that a powerful Conjuer, who has angered a Daedric God, resides in this location.', '''and'':14B ''anger'':79B ''be'':67B ''befor'':43B ''branch'':48B ''bridg'':13B,34B ''burrow'':2A,4B ''by'':58B ''can'':66B ''cav'':8B,24B ''cliff'':40B ''conju'':76B ''crevic'':37B ''daedric'':81B ''dragon'':12B ''easily'':68B ''entranc'':45B ''follow'':25B ''fork'':65B ''from'':50B ''god'':82B ''haafing'':20B ''in'':19B,38B,84B ''is'':5B,71B ''it'':70B ''just'':42B ''keep'':18B ''larg'':52B ''leads'':30B ''locat'':9B ''location'':86B ''mark'':57B ''miss'':69B ''near'':54B ''northwatch'':17B ''northwest'':10B ''of'':11B,16B,61B ''off'':49B ''over'':31B ''path'':28B,47B ''pil'':60B ''pinefrost'':55B ''powerful'':75B ''reach'':22B ''resid'':83B ''rimerock'':1A,3B ''road'':53B ''rocks'':62B ''rough'':27B ''rumor'':72B ''small'':7B ''south'':15B ''spanning'':35B ''that'':29B,73B ''the'':23B,39B,44B,46B,51B,64B ''this'':85B ''though'':63B ''to'':21B ''tow'':56B ''wall'':41B ''who'':77B ''wood'':33B', 'haafingar', 'Rimerock Burrow is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steepfall_burrow', 'Steepfall Burrow is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge and east of Northwatch Keep in Haafingar. It is inhabited by trolls and wolves.', '''and'':14B,26B ''bridg'':13B ''burrow'':2A,4B ''by'':24B ''cav'':8B ''dragon'':12B ''east'':15B ''haafing'':20B ''in'':19B ''inhabit'':23B ''is'':5B,22B ''it'':21B ''keep'':18B ''locat'':9B ''northwatch'':17B ''northwest'':10B ''of'':11B,16B ''small'':7B ''steepfall'':1A,3B ''trolls'':25B ''wolv'':27B', 'haafingar', 'Steepfall Burrow is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ravenscar_hollow', 'Ravenscar Hollow is a small cave located west of the Thalmor Embassy and due east of the Steed Stone in Haafingar. The cave is inhabited by hagravens, making it a perilous location for those who dare to venture inside.

To find the cave, head east along the road that passes Wolfskull Cave, continuing downhill past a switchback. Along the way, you’ll notice two cairns on the left, marking the beginning of a path that winds downhill, passing several more cairns and leading you to the cave’s entrance along the shore. The eerie atmosphere of the cave and its hagraven occupants make it a notable site for adventurers in the region.', '''adventurers'':111B ''along'':48B,60B,92B ''and'':15B,84B,101B ''atmospher'':97B ''beginning'':73B ''by'':28B ''cairns'':67B,83B ''cav'':8B,25B,45B,54B,89B,100B ''continuing'':55B ''dar'':38B ''downhill'':56B,79B ''due'':16B ''east'':17B,47B ''eeri'':96B ''embassy'':14B ''entranc'':91B ''find'':43B ''for'':35B,110B ''haafing'':23B ''hagrav'':103B ''hagravens'':29B ''head'':46B ''hollow'':2A,4B ''in'':22B,112B ''inhabit'':27B ''insid'':41B ''is'':5B,26B ''it'':31B,106B ''its'':102B ''leading'':85B ''left'':70B ''ll'':64B ''locat'':9B ''location'':34B ''mak'':105B ''making'':30B ''marking'':71B ''mor'':82B ''notabl'':108B ''notic'':65B ''occupants'':104B ''of'':11B,18B,74B,98B ''on'':68B ''pass'':52B ''passing'':80B ''past'':57B ''path'':76B ''perilous'':33B ''ravensc'':1A,3B ''region'':114B ''road'':50B ''s'':90B ''several'':81B ''shor'':94B ''sit'':109B ''small'':7B ''ste'':20B ''ston'':21B ''switchback'':59B ''thalmor'':13B ''that'':51B,77B ''the'':12B,19B,24B,44B,49B,61B,69B,72B,88B,93B,95B,99B,113B ''thos'':36B ''to'':39B,42B,87B ''two'':66B ''ventur'':40B ''way'':62B ''west'':10B ''who'':37B ''winds'':78B ''wolfskull'':53B ''you'':63B,86B', 'haafingar', 'Ravenscar Hollow is a small cave located west of the Thalmor Embassy in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pinemoon_cave', 'Pinemoon Cave is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge and east of Volskygge in Haafingar. The cave is inhabited by vampires, making it a dangerous place for anyone who ventures inside.

Its secluded location, nestled between Dragon Bridge and Volskygge, adds to the mystery and menace of the cave. Adventurers who explore Pinemoon Cave can expect to face off against the vampire inhabitants and uncover the dark secrets hidden within its depths.', '''adds'':45B ''adventurers'':54B ''against'':64B ''and'':14B,43B,49B,68B ''anyon'':32B ''betw'':40B ''bridg'':13B,42B ''by'':24B ''can'':59B ''cav'':2A,4B,8B,21B,53B,58B ''dangerous'':29B ''dark'':71B ''depths'':76B ''dragon'':12B,41B ''east'':15B ''expect'':60B ''explor'':56B ''fac'':62B ''for'':31B ''haafing'':19B ''hidd'':73B ''in'':18B ''inhabit'':23B ''inhabitants'':67B ''insid'':35B ''is'':5B,22B ''it'':27B ''its'':36B,75B ''locat'':9B ''location'':38B ''making'':26B ''menac'':50B ''mystery'':48B ''nestl'':39B ''northwest'':10B ''of'':11B,16B,51B ''off'':63B ''pinemoon'':1A,3B,57B ''plac'':30B ''seclud'':37B ''secrets'':72B ''small'':7B ''the'':20B,47B,52B,65B,70B ''to'':46B,61B ''uncov'':69B ''vampir'':25B,66B ''ventur'':34B ''volskygg'':17B,44B ''who'':33B,55B ''within'':74B', 'haafingar', 'Pinemoon Cave is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_katariah', 'The Katariah is the personal transport vessel of the Emperor, Titus Mede II. It serves as both a luxury ship and a symbol of the Emperor''s power, allowing him to travel across the seas in style and security. The ship is named after Empress Katariah, the wife of the Emperor, reflecting her importance.', '''across'':35B ''after'':46B ''allowing'':31B ''and'':23B,40B ''as'':18B ''both'':19B ''emperor'':12B,28B,53B ''empress'':47B ''her'':55B ''him'':32B ''ii'':15B ''importanc'':56B ''in'':38B ''is'':5B,44B ''it'':16B ''katariah'':2A,4B,48B ''luxury'':21B ''med'':14B ''nam'':45B ''of'':10B,26B,51B ''personal'':7B ''pow'':30B ''reflecting'':54B ''s'':29B ''security'':41B ''serv'':17B ''ship'':22B,43B ''style'':39B ''symbol'':25B ''the'':1A,3B,6B,11B,27B,36B,42B,49B,52B ''titus'':13B ''to'':33B ''transport'':8B ''travel'':34B ''vessel'':9B ''wif'':50B', 'haafingar, sailor, legion', 'The Katariah is the personal transport vessel of the Emperor, Titus Mede II. It serves as both a luxury ship and a symbol of the Emperor''s power, allowing him to travel across the seas in style and security. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dainty_sload', 'The Dainty Sload is a ship docked north of Solitude, located southwest of the Solitude Lighthouse in Haafingar. The ship is currently docked for supplies and is home to corsairs.', '''and'':28B ''corsairs'':32B ''currently'':24B ''dainty'':1A,4B ''dock'':9B,25B ''for'':26B ''haafing'':20B ''hom'':30B ''in'':19B ''is'':6B,23B,29B ''lighthous'':18B ''locat'':13B ''north'':10B ''of'':11B,15B ''ship'':8B,22B ''slo'':2A,5B ''solitud'':12B,17B ''southwest'':14B ''suppli'':27B ''the'':3B,16B,21B ''to'':31B', 'haafingar, sailor', 'The Dainty Sload is a ship docked north of Solitude, located southwest of the Solitude Lighthouse in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_steed_stone', 'The Steed Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located northwest of Solitude and east of Fort Hraggstad in Haafingar. Activating the Steed Stone increases your carry weight by a sigfnicant amount and removes the movement penalty of armor, making it especially beneficial for heavy armor wearers. Additionally, it makes worn armor weigh nothing, allowing even those who favor heavy armor to move with ease.

The stone is situated at the top of several flights of stairs, placed upon a stone structure near the highest point of the mountain. The Steed Stone offers a significant advantage for adventurers looking to improve their carrying capacity and mobility, especially those focusing on strength and endurance.', '''across'':15B ''activating'':28B ''additionally'':55B ''advantag'':103B ''adventurers'':105B ''allowing'':62B ''amount'':39B ''and'':21B,40B,112B,119B ''armor'':46B,53B,59B,68B ''at'':77B ''beneficial'':50B ''by'':36B ''capacity'':111B ''carry'':34B ''carrying'':110B ''eas'':72B ''east'':22B ''enduranc'':120B ''especially'':49B,114B ''even'':63B ''favor'':66B ''flights'':82B ''focusing'':116B ''for'':51B,104B ''fort'':24B ''haafing'':27B ''heavy'':52B,67B ''highest'':92B ''hraggst'':25B ''improv'':108B ''in'':26B ''incre'':32B ''is'':7B,75B ''it'':48B,56B ''locat'':17B ''looking'':106B ''mak'':57B ''making'':47B ''mobility'':113B ''mountain'':96B ''mov'':70B ''movement'':43B ''near'':90B ''northwest'':18B ''nothing'':61B ''of'':9B,19B,23B,45B,80B,83B,94B ''offers'':100B ''on'':117B ''one'':8B ''penalty'':44B ''plac'':85B ''point'':93B ''remov'':41B ''scatter'':14B ''several'':81B ''sigfnicant'':38B ''significant'':102B ''situat'':76B ''skyrim'':16B ''solitud'':20B ''stairs'':84B ''standing'':12B ''ste'':2A,5B,30B,98B ''ston'':3A,6B,13B,31B,74B,88B,99B ''strength'':118B ''structur'':89B ''the'':1A,4B,10B,29B,42B,73B,78B,91B,95B,97B,109B ''thirt'':11B ''thos'':64B,115B ''to'':69B,107B ''top'':79B ''upon'':86B ''wearers'':54B ''weigh'':60B ''weight'':35B ''who'':65B ''with'':71B ''worn'':58B ''your'':33B', 'haafingar, traveler, scholar', 'The Steed Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located northwest of Solitude and east of Fort Hraggstad in Haafingar. Activating the Steed Stone increases your carry weight by a sigfnicant amount and removes the movement penalty of armor, making it especially beneficial for heavy armor wearers. Additionally, it makes worn armor weigh nothing, allowing even those who favor heavy armor to move with ease.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('clearpine_pond', 'Clearpine Pond is a serene pond located west-southwest of Solitude, just northeast of Pinemoon Cave in Haafingar. The pond features a small island that is easily identifiable by a pile of logs and several fallen trees surrounding it, adding a rustic charm to the landscape.', '''adding'':43B ''and'':37B ''by'':32B ''cav'':19B ''charm'':46B ''clearpin'':1A,3B ''easily'':30B ''fall'':39B ''featur'':24B ''haafing'':21B ''identifi'':31B ''in'':20B ''is'':5B,29B ''island'':27B ''it'':42B ''just'':15B ''landscap'':49B ''locat'':9B ''logs'':36B ''northeast'':16B ''of'':13B,17B,35B ''pil'':34B ''pinemoon'':18B ''pond'':2A,4B,8B,23B ''rustic'':45B ''seren'':7B ''several'':38B ''small'':26B ''solitud'':14B ''southwest'':12B ''surrounding'':41B ''that'':28B ''the'':22B,48B ''to'':47B ''tre'':40B ''west'':11B ''west-southwest'':10B', 'haafingar', 'Clearpine Pond is a serene pond located west-southwest of Solitude in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('solitude_lighthouse', 'Solitude Lighthouse is a stone structure located on the northern coast of Skyrim, northeast of Solitude. The lighthouse plays an important role in guiding ships safely into Solitude''s harbor. It is tended to by a solitary Khajiit named Ma''zaka, who lives in the lighthouse. It is rumored that if the lighthouse was to go out, it cause extreme danger for ships coming into port.', '''an'':22B ''by'':37B ''caus'':61B ''coast'':13B ''coming'':66B ''dang'':63B ''extrem'':62B ''for'':64B ''go'':58B ''guiding'':26B ''harbor'':32B ''if'':53B ''important'':23B ''in'':25B,46B ''into'':29B,67B ''is'':5B,34B,50B ''it'':33B,49B,60B ''khajiit'':40B ''lighthous'':2A,4B,20B,48B,55B ''liv'':45B ''locat'':9B ''ma'':42B ''nam'':41B ''northeast'':16B ''northern'':12B ''of'':14B,17B ''on'':10B ''out'':59B ''plays'':21B ''port'':68B ''rol'':24B ''rumor'':51B ''s'':31B ''safely'':28B ''ships'':27B,65B ''skyrim'':15B ''solitary'':39B ''solitud'':1A,3B,18B,30B ''ston'':7B ''structur'':8B ''tend'':35B ''that'':52B ''the'':11B,19B,47B,54B ''to'':36B,57B ''was'':56B ''who'':44B ''zak'':43B', 'haafingar, sailor', 'Solitude Lighthouse is a stone structure located on the northern coast of Skyrim, northeast of Solitude. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('forgotten_vale', 'The Forgotten Vale is an isolated region located in northwestern Skyrim, once inhabited by the Snow Elves, who worshipped the god Auri-El. This secluded area is only accessible after navigating both Darkfall Cave and Darkfall Passage, and it provides access to eight distinct locations: Darkfall Grotto, Darkfall Passage, Forgotten Vale Cave, Forgotten Vale Forest, Forgotten Vale Overlook, the Glacial Crevice, the Inner Sanctum, and Sharpslope Cave.

Now, the Forgotten Vale is home to the corrupted Falmer, once the Snow Elves, along with a variety of dangerous creatures such as frost giants. The Snow Elves once built a temple dedicated to Auri-El, which can be found in the Inner Sanctum', '''access'':32B,44B ''after'':33B ''along'':85B ''an'':7B ''and'':38B,41B,68B ''are'':29B ''as'':93B ''auri'':25B,106B ''auri-el'':24B,105B ''be'':110B ''both'':35B ''built'':100B ''by'':16B ''can'':109B ''cav'':37B,55B,70B ''corrupt'':79B ''creatur'':91B ''crevic'':64B ''dangerous'':90B ''darkfall'':36B,39B,49B,51B ''dedicat'':103B ''distinct'':47B ''eight'':46B ''elves'':19B,84B,98B ''falm'':80B ''forest'':58B ''forgott'':1A,4B,53B,56B,59B,73B ''found'':111B ''frost'':94B ''giants'':95B ''glacial'':63B ''god'':23B ''grott'':50B ''hom'':76B ''in'':11B,112B ''inhabit'':15B ''inner'':66B,114B ''is'':6B,30B,75B ''isolat'':8B ''it'':42B ''locat'':10B ''locations'':48B ''navigating'':34B ''northwestern'':12B ''now'':71B ''of'':89B ''once'':14B,81B,99B ''only'':31B ''overlook'':61B ''passag'':40B,52B ''provid'':43B ''region'':9B ''sanctum'':67B,115B ''seclud'':28B ''sharpslop'':69B ''skyrim'':13B ''snow'':18B,83B,97B ''such'':92B ''templ'':102B ''the'':3B,17B,22B,62B,65B,72B,78B,82B,96B,113B ''this'':27B ''to'':45B,77B,104B ''val'':2A,5B,54B,57B,60B,74B ''variety'':88B ''which'':108B ''who'':20B ''with'':86B ''worshipp'':21B', 'snowelf', 'The Forgotten Vale is an isolated region located in northwestern Skyrim, once inhabited by the Snow Elves, who worshipped the god Auri-El. It is hidden somwhere in Haafingar Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'dawnguard, volkihar', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('addvar''s_house', 'Addvar''s House is a small residence located in the residential district of Solitude, right next to Evette San''s House. It is the home of Addvar, the town''s fishmonger, along with his wife Greta and their daughter Svari. ', '''addvar'':1A,4B,30B ''along'':35B ''and'':40B ''daught'':42B ''district'':15B ''evett'':21B ''fishmong'':34B ''gret'':39B ''his'':37B ''hom'':28B ''hous'':3A,6B,24B ''in'':12B ''is'':7B,26B ''it'':25B ''locat'':11B ''next'':19B ''of'':16B,29B ''residenc'':10B ''residential'':14B ''right'':18B ''s'':2A,5B,23B,33B ''san'':22B ''small'':9B ''solitud'':17B ''svari'':43B ''the'':13B,27B,31B,41B ''to'':20B ''town'':32B ''wif'':38B ''with'':36B', 'haafingar', 'Addvar''s House is a small residence located in the residential district of Solitude. You do not know Addvar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('angeline''s_aromatics', 'Angeline''s Aromatics is the alchemy shop in Solitude, located as the second building on the left after passing through Solitude''s main gate, just past The Winking Skeever. The shop is owned by Angeline Morrard, who specializes in selling potions, food, ingredients, and books.', '''after'':21B ''alchemy'':9B ''and'':47B ''angelin'':1A,4B,38B ''aromatics'':3A,6B ''as'':14B ''books'':48B ''building'':17B ''by'':37B ''food'':45B ''gat'':27B ''in'':11B,42B ''ingredients'':46B ''is'':7B,35B ''just'':28B ''left'':20B ''locat'':13B ''main'':26B ''morrard'':39B ''on'':18B ''owned'':36B ''passing'':22B ''past'':29B ''potions'':44B ''s'':2A,5B,25B ''second'':16B ''selling'':43B ''shop'':10B,34B ''skeev'':32B ''solitud'':12B,24B ''specializ'':41B ''the'':8B,15B,19B,30B,33B ''through'':23B ''who'':40B ''winking'':31B', 'haafingar', 'Angeline''s Aromatics is the alchemy shop in Solitude.  You do not know.who owns it.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bits_and_pieces', 'Bits and Pieces is the general goods store in Solitude, run by Sayma, a Redguard merchant. The store is located next door to Radiant Raiment, on the corner by the market square. It is the second building on the right as you enter Solitude from the main gate.

