INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('solitude_blacksmith', 'Solitude Blacksmith is a smithy located on the western side of Solitude, up the ramp to Castle Dour and to the right. The smithy is operated by Beirand and Heimvar, with a spacious interior filled with various weapons, armor, and crafting materials.', '''and'':21B,31B,42B ''armor'':41B ''beirand'':30B ''blacksmith'':2A,4B ''by'':29B ''castl'':19B ''crafting'':43B ''dour'':20B ''fill'':37B ''heimv'':32B ''interior'':36B ''is'':5B,27B ''locat'':8B ''materials'':44B ''of'':13B ''on'':9B ''operat'':28B ''ramp'':17B ''right'':24B ''sid'':12B ''smithy'':7B,26B ''solitud'':1A,3B,14B ''spacious'':35B ''the'':10B,16B,23B,25B ''to'':18B,22B ''up'':15B ''various'':39B ''weapons'':40B ''western'':11B ''with'':33B,38B', 'haafingar', 'Solitude Blacksmith is a smithy located in Solitude. You do not know who runs the blacksmith.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('temple_of_the_divines', 'The Temple of the Divines is the main temple of Solitude and Skyrim, housing shrines dedicated to the Eight Divines. The temple serves as a place of worship and is an important religious site in the city.

It is located on the eastern side of Castle Dour''s courtyard, northwest of the Blue Palace in Solitude. The temple is a central location for those seeking spiritual guidance or wishing to honor the Divines, and it is a peaceful contrast to the bustling political and military activity surrounding Castle Dour.', '''activity'':90B ''an'':35B ''and'':16B,33B,78B,88B ''as'':28B ''blu'':57B ''bustling'':86B ''castl'':50B,92B ''central'':65B ''city'':41B ''contrast'':83B ''courtyard'':53B ''dedicat'':20B ''divin'':4A,9B,24B,77B ''dour'':51B,93B ''eastern'':47B ''eight'':23B ''for'':67B ''guidanc'':71B ''honor'':75B ''housing'':18B ''important'':36B ''in'':39B,59B ''is'':10B,34B,43B,63B,80B ''it'':42B,79B ''locat'':44B ''location'':66B ''main'':12B ''military'':89B ''northwest'':54B ''of'':2A,7B,14B,31B,49B,55B ''on'':45B ''or'':72B ''palac'':58B ''peaceful'':82B ''plac'':30B ''political'':87B ''religious'':37B ''s'':52B ''seeking'':69B ''serv'':27B ''shrin'':19B ''sid'':48B ''sit'':38B ''skyrim'':17B ''solitud'':15B,60B ''spiritual'':70B ''surrounding'':91B ''templ'':1A,6B,13B,26B,62B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,11B,22B,25B,40B,46B,56B,61B,76B,85B ''thos'':68B ''to'':21B,74B,84B ''wishing'':73B ''worship'':32B', 'haafingar, priest', 'The Temple of the Divines is the main temple of Solitude and Skyrim, housing shrines dedicated to the Eight Divines. The temple serves as a place of worship and is an important religious site in the city. You do not know who runs the temples.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('thalmor_headquarters', 'Thalmor Headquarters is a building located within the walls of Castle Dour in Solitude, Haafingar. The entrance is accessed via a long straight flight of stairs that lead up from the courtyard in Castle Dour.

Despite its name, the building is notably devoid of Thalmor personnel or anyone else, giving it an eerie, abandoned feel. It seems to have been left suddenly, adding an air of mystery surrounding its purpose and the circumstances of its abandonment. The empty headquarters stands in stark contrast to the bustling political and military presence elsewhere in Castle Dour.', '''abandon'':56B ''abandonment'':78B ''access'':21B ''adding'':65B ''air'':67B ''an'':54B,66B ''and'':73B,90B ''anyon'':50B ''been'':62B ''building'':7B,42B ''bustling'':88B ''castl'':13B,36B,95B ''circumstanc'':75B ''contrast'':85B ''courtyard'':34B ''despit'':38B ''dev'':45B ''dour'':14B,37B,96B ''eeri'':55B ''else'':51B ''elsewher'':93B ''empty'':80B ''entranc'':19B ''feel'':57B ''flight'':26B ''from'':32B ''giving'':52B ''haafing'':17B ''hav'':61B ''headquarters'':2A,4B,81B ''in'':15B,35B,83B,94B ''is'':5B,20B,43B ''it'':53B,58B ''its'':39B,71B,77B ''lead'':30B ''left'':63B ''locat'':8B ''long'':24B ''military'':91B ''mystery'':69B ''nam'':40B ''notably'':44B ''of'':12B,27B,46B,68B,76B ''or'':49B ''personnel'':48B ''political'':89B ''presenc'':92B ''purpos'':72B ''seems'':59B ''solitud'':16B ''stairs'':28B ''stands'':82B ''stark'':84B ''straight'':25B ''suddenly'':64B ''surrounding'':70B ''thalmor'':1A,3B,47B ''that'':29B ''the'':10B,18B,33B,41B,74B,79B,87B ''to'':60B,86B ''up'':31B ''via'':22B ''walls'':11B ''within'':9B', 'haafingar, thalmor, legion', 'Thalmor Headquarters is a building located within the walls of Castle Dour in Solitude, Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_winking_skeever', '
The Winking Skeever is a popular inn and bar located in Solitude, situated on the left-hand side as you enter from the southwest. The inn proudly displays its name on a sign adorning its front door, and it is a well-known establishment in the city.

The owner, Corpulus Vinius, shares that the inn is named after a childhood pet skeever that was said to have the remarkable ability to wink. Minette Vinius, Corpulus''s daughter, lives in Solitude and often frequents the inn. Lisette, a Breton bard, performs at the inn, adding to its lively atmosphere.', '''ability'':75B ''adding'':99B ''adorning'':38B ''after'':63B ''and'':11B,42B,86B ''as'':23B ''at'':96B ''atmospher'':103B ''bar'':12B ''bard'':94B ''breton'':93B ''childhood'':65B ''city'':52B ''corpulus'':55B,80B ''daught'':82B ''displays'':32B ''door'':41B ''enter'':25B ''establishment'':49B ''frequents'':88B ''from'':26B ''front'':40B ''hand'':21B ''hav'':72B ''in'':14B,50B,84B ''inn'':10B,30B,60B,90B,98B ''is'':7B,44B,61B ''it'':43B ''its'':33B,39B,101B ''known'':48B ''left'':20B ''left-hand'':19B ''lisett'':91B ''liv'':83B ''lively'':102B ''locat'':13B ''minett'':78B ''nam'':34B,62B ''often'':87B ''on'':17B,35B ''owner'':54B ''performs'':95B ''pet'':66B ''popul'':9B ''proudly'':31B ''remark'':74B ''s'':81B ''said'':70B ''shar'':57B ''sid'':22B ''sign'':37B ''situat'':16B ''skeev'':3A,6B,67B ''solitud'':15B,85B ''southwest'':28B ''that'':58B,68B ''the'':1A,4B,18B,27B,29B,51B,53B,59B,73B,89B,97B ''to'':71B,76B,100B ''vinius'':56B,79B ''was'':69B ''well'':47B ''well-known'':46B ''wink'':77B ''winking'':2A,5B ''you'':24B', 'haafingar, innkeeper, traveler', 'The Winking Skeever is a popular inn and bar located in Solitude,. You do not know who runs the inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_pale', 'The Pale is a hold in northern Skyrim, with its capital in Dawnstar. It is aligned with the Stormcloaks. 

The Pale is a sparsely populated region, known for its harsh, snow-covered terrain and limited safe havens for travelers. The unforgiving landscape is largely unsuitable for farming, though the far southern edges, where the mountains give way to more hospitable terrain, offer better conditions. The hold''s largest lake, Lake Yorgrim, lies to the south, feeding the River Yorgrim. One of three entrances to Blackreach can be found in Raldbthar, a Dwarven ruin located south of the lake.

Despite its challenging climate, the Pale is rich in natural resources. Snowberries thrive in the snowy environment, while sturdy blue and purple mountain flowers can be found in the region. Along the coastline, Nordic barnacles, clams, and spiky grass are abundant. The hold''s wildlife includes giants, sabre cats, wolves, ice wraiths, trolls, and frostbite spiders, making it a rugged and dangerous region. Brina Merilis serves as the Jarl of the Pale, overseeing the hold from Dawnstar.', '''abundant'':142B ''align'':18B ''along'':132B ''and'':37B,122B,138B,155B,162B ''are'':141B ''as'':168B ''barnacl'':136B ''be'':90B,127B ''bett'':66B ''blackreach'':88B ''blu'':121B ''brin'':165B ''can'':89B,126B ''capital'':13B ''cats'':150B ''challenging'':104B ''clams'':137B ''climat'':105B ''coastlin'':134B ''conditions'':67B ''cover'':35B ''dangerous'':163B ''dawnst'':15B,178B ''despit'':102B ''dwarv'':95B ''edges'':55B ''entranc'':86B ''environment'':118B ''far'':53B ''farming'':50B ''feeding'':79B ''flowers'':125B ''for'':30B,41B,49B ''found'':91B,128B ''from'':177B ''frostbit'':156B ''giants'':148B ''giv'':59B ''grass'':140B ''harsh'':32B ''havens'':40B ''hold'':7B,69B,144B,176B ''hospit'':63B ''ice'':152B ''in'':8B,14B,92B,110B,115B,129B ''includ'':147B ''is'':5B,17B,24B,46B,108B ''it'':16B,159B ''its'':12B,31B,103B ''jarl'':170B ''known'':29B ''lak'':72B,73B,101B ''landscap'':45B ''largely'':47B ''largest'':71B ''lies'':75B ''limit'':38B ''locat'':97B ''making'':158B ''merilis'':166B ''mor'':62B ''mountain'':124B ''mountains'':58B ''natural'':111B ''nordic'':135B ''northern'':9B ''of'':84B,99B,171B ''offer'':65B ''one'':83B ''overseeing'':174B ''pal'':2A,4B,23B,107B,173B ''populat'':27B ''purpl'':123B ''raldbth'':93B ''region'':28B,131B,164B ''resourc'':112B ''rich'':109B ''riv'':81B ''rugg'':161B ''ruin'':96B ''s'':70B,145B ''sabr'':149B ''saf'':39B ''serv'':167B ''skyrim'':10B ''snow'':34B ''snow-cover'':33B ''snowberri'':113B ''snowy'':117B ''south'':78B,98B ''southern'':54B ''sparsely'':26B ''spiders'':157B ''spiky'':139B ''stormcloaks'':21B ''sturdy'':120B ''terrain'':36B,64B ''the'':1A,3B,20B,22B,43B,52B,57B,68B,77B,80B,100B,106B,116B,130B,133B,143B,169B,172B,175B ''though'':51B ''thre'':85B ''thriv'':114B ''to'':61B,76B,87B ''travelers'':42B ''trolls'':154B ''unforgiving'':44B ''unsuit'':48B ''way'':60B ''wher'':56B ''whil'':119B ''wildlif'':146B ''with'':11B,19B ''wolv'':151B ''wraiths'':153B ''yorgrim'':74B,82B', 'pale, scholar, noble', 'The Pale is a hold in northern Skyrim, with its capital in Dawnstar. It is aligned with the Stormcloaks. 

The Pale is a sparsely populated region, known for its harsh, snow-covered terrain and limited safe havens for travelers. The unforgiving landscape is largely unsuitable for farming, though the far southern edges, where the mountains give way to more hospitable terrain, offer better conditions. The hold''s largest lake, Lake Yorgrim, lies to the south, feeding the River Yorgrim. One of three entrances to Blackreach can be found in Raldbthar, a Dwarven ruin located south of the lake.', '', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dawnstar', 'Dawnstar (also known as Danstrar) is a settlement on the northern coast of Skyrim and serves as the capital of The Pale. Historically, it was a garrison town used as an exile post due to its cold, harsh climate and notorious gales. Its name is said to come from its reputation for "greeting the sun as it begins its journey." Dawnstar has a turbulent history, often troubled by the Ice Tribes and Gehenoth, and it has been the site of battles that have significantly impacted the fate of the Empire.

The settlement is surrounded by several neighboring locations, including Bardmont to the south, Helarchen Creek to the southeast, Stonehills to the southwest, and Winterhold to the east. Due to the nearby glacial icefields, Dawnstar is the last major port before Windhelm that remains ice-free following the Great Collapse. Its economy is supported by its two productive mines: Iron-Breaker Mine, which supplies iron, and Quicksilver Mine, which produces quicksilver. Additionally, fishing plays a significant role in the town''s livelihood.

Key locations in Dawnstar include The White Hall, the seat of the Jarl of the Pale, Windpeak Inn, The Sea Squall, and The Mortar and Pestle, a local alchemy shop. Despite its small size, Dawnstar remains an essential hub for trade and travel along Skyrim''s northern coast.', '''additionally'':164B ''alchemy'':203B ''along'':218B ''also'':3B ''an'':32B,211B ''and'':16B,41B,73B,75B,114B,158B,196B,199B,216B ''as'':5B,18B,31B,57B ''bardmont'':101B ''battl'':82B ''been'':78B ''befor'':131B ''begins'':59B ''break'':153B ''by'':69B,96B,146B ''capital'':20B ''climat'':40B ''coast'':13B,222B ''cold'':38B ''collaps'':141B ''com'':49B ''creek'':106B ''danstr'':6B ''dawnst'':1A,2B,62B,125B,178B,209B ''despit'':205B ''due'':35B,119B ''east'':118B ''economy'':143B ''empir'':91B ''essential'':212B ''exil'':33B ''fat'':88B ''fishing'':165B ''following'':138B ''for'':53B,214B ''fre'':137B ''from'':50B ''gal'':43B ''garrison'':28B ''gehenoth'':74B ''glacial'':123B ''great'':140B ''greeting'':54B ''hall'':182B ''harsh'':39B ''hav'':84B ''helarch'':105B ''historically'':24B ''history'':66B ''hub'':213B ''ice'':71B,136B ''ice-fre'':135B ''icefields'':124B ''impact'':86B ''in'':170B,177B ''includ'':179B ''including'':100B ''inn'':192B ''iron'':152B,157B ''iron-break'':151B ''is'':7B,46B,94B,126B,144B ''it'':25B,58B,76B ''its'':37B,44B,51B,60B,142B,147B,206B ''jarl'':187B ''journey'':61B ''key'':175B ''known'':4B ''last'':128B ''livelihood'':174B ''local'':202B ''locations'':99B,176B ''major'':129B ''min'':150B,154B,160B ''mort'':198B ''nam'':45B ''nearby'':122B ''neighboring'':98B ''northern'':12B,221B ''notorious'':42B ''of'':14B,21B,81B,89B,185B,188B ''often'':67B ''on'':10B ''pal'':23B,190B ''pestl'':200B ''plays'':166B ''port'':130B ''post'':34B ''produc'':162B ''productiv'':149B ''quicksilv'':159B,163B ''remains'':134B,210B ''reputation'':52B ''rol'':169B ''s'':173B,220B ''said'':47B ''seat'':184B ''serv'':17B ''settlement'':9B,93B ''several'':97B ''shop'':204B ''significant'':168B ''significantly'':85B ''sit'':80B ''siz'':208B ''skyrim'':15B,219B ''small'':207B ''south'':104B ''southeast'':109B ''southwest'':113B ''squall'':195B ''stonehills'':110B ''sun'':56B ''suppli'':156B ''support'':145B ''surround'':95B ''that'':83B,133B ''the'':11B,19B,22B,55B,70B,79B,87B,90B,92B,103B,108B,112B,117B,121B,127B,139B,171B,180B,183B,186B,189B,193B,197B ''to'':36B,48B,102B,107B,111B,116B,120B ''town'':29B,172B ''trad'':215B ''travel'':217B ''trib'':72B ''troubl'':68B ''turbulent'':65B ''two'':148B ''used'':30B ''was'':26B ''which'':155B,161B ''whit'':181B ''windhelm'':132B ''windpeak'':191B ''winterhold'':115B', 'pale, scholar, noble', 'Dawnstar is a settlement on the northern coast of Skyrim and serves as the capital of The Pale. Historically, it was a garrison town used as an exile post due to its cold, harsh climate and notorious gales. Its name is said to come from its reputation for "greeting the sun as it begins its journey." Dawnstar has a turbulent history, often troubled by the Ice Tribes and Gehenoth, and it has been the site of battles that have significantly impacted the fate of the Empire. 

Key locations in Dawnstar include The White Hall, the seat of the Jarl of the Pale, Windpeak Inn, The Sea Squall, and The Mortar and Pestle, a local alchemy shop. Despite its small size, Dawnstar remains an essential hub for trade and travel along Skyrim''s northern coast.', '', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dawnstar_sanctuary', 'Dawnstar Sanctuary is an abandoned Dark Brotherhood sanctuary located on the shore of the Sea of Ghosts, just north of Dawnstar in The Pale. Once one of the first sanctuaries established by the Dark Brotherhood in Skyrim, it has been deserted for nearly a century.', '''abandon'':7B ''an'':6B ''been'':42B ''brotherhood'':9B,37B ''by'':34B ''century'':47B ''dark'':8B,36B ''dawnst'':1A,3B,23B ''desert'':43B ''establish'':33B ''first'':31B ''for'':44B ''ghosts'':19B ''in'':24B,38B ''is'':5B ''it'':40B ''just'':20B ''locat'':11B ''nearly'':45B ''north'':21B ''of'':15B,18B,22B,29B ''on'':12B ''once'':27B ''one'':28B ''pal'':26B ''sanctuari'':32B ''sanctuary'':2A,4B,10B ''shor'':14B ''skyrim'':39B ''the'':13B,16B,25B,30B,35B', 'darkbrotherhood', 'Dawnstar Sanctuary is an abandoned Dark Brotherhood sanctuary located somewhere in Dawnstar.', 'legion', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nightgate_inn', 'Nightgate Inn is a remote inn located west of Windhelm and east of Shrouded Grove in The Pale

The inn is run by Hadring, a Nord warrior who serves as its proprietor. Nightgate Inn is a quiet, secluded location, offering respite to travelers navigating the harsh, snowy terrain of the region. Its isolation adds to its charm, providing a peaceful retreat far from the hustle and bustle of Skyrim''s cities.', '''adds'':56B ''and'':13B,68B ''as'':32B ''bustl'':69B ''by'':25B ''charm'':59B ''citi'':73B ''east'':14B ''far'':64B ''from'':65B ''grov'':17B ''hadring'':26B ''harsh'':48B ''hustl'':67B ''in'':18B ''inn'':2A,4B,8B,22B,36B ''is'':5B,23B,37B ''isolation'':55B ''its'':33B,54B,58B ''locat'':9B ''location'':41B ''navigating'':46B ''nightgat'':1A,3B,35B ''nord'':28B ''of'':11B,15B,51B,70B ''offering'':42B ''pal'':20B ''peaceful'':62B ''proprietor'':34B ''providing'':60B ''quiet'':39B ''region'':53B ''remot'':7B ''respit'':43B ''retreat'':63B ''run'':24B ''s'':72B ''seclud'':40B ''serv'':31B ''shroud'':16B ''skyrim'':71B ''snowy'':49B ''terrain'':50B ''the'':19B,21B,47B,52B,66B ''to'':44B,57B ''travelers'':45B ''warrior'':29B ''west'':10B ''who'':30B ''windhelm'':12B', 'pale, traveler, innkeeper', '"Nightgate Inn is a remote inn located west of Windhelm  in The Pale. You do not know who runs the inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hall_of_the_vigilant', 'The Hall of the Vigilant is a secluded lodge located south-southwest of Dawnstar and northwest of Fort Dunstad in The Pale. It serves as the headquarters for the Vigilants of Stendarr, a group dedicated to hunting Daedra and other malevolent forces in Skyrim.

The lodge is led by Keeper Carcette, who provides expert training in Restoration magic to those seeking to improve their healing abilities. The Hall of the Vigilant is a refuge for the Vigilants, offering a safe haven for their mission to protect Skyrim from supernatural threats.', '''abiliti'':71B ''and'':20B,44B ''as'':30B ''by'':54B ''carcett'':56B ''daedr'':43B ''dawnst'':19B ''dedicat'':40B ''dunst'':24B ''expert'':59B ''for'':33B,80B,87B ''forc'':47B ''fort'':23B ''from'':93B ''group'':39B ''hall'':1A,6B,73B ''hav'':86B ''headquarters'':32B ''healing'':70B ''hunting'':42B ''improv'':68B ''in'':25B,48B,61B ''is'':10B,52B,77B ''it'':28B ''keep'':55B ''led'':53B ''locat'':14B ''lodg'':13B,51B ''magic'':63B ''malevolent'':46B ''mission'':89B ''northwest'':21B ''of'':2A,7B,18B,22B,36B,74B ''offering'':83B ''other'':45B ''pal'':27B ''protect'':91B ''provid'':58B ''refug'':79B ''restoration'':62B ''saf'':85B ''seclud'':12B ''seeking'':66B ''serv'':29B ''skyrim'':49B,92B ''south'':16B ''south-southwest'':15B ''southwest'':17B ''stendarr'':37B ''supernatural'':94B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,26B,31B,34B,50B,69B,72B,75B,81B,88B ''thos'':65B ''threats'':95B ''to'':41B,64B,67B,90B ''training'':60B ''vigilant'':4A,9B,76B ''vigilants'':35B,82B ''who'':57B', 'pale, dawnguard, volkihar', 'The Hall of the Vigilant is a secluded lodge located south-southwest of Dawnstar in The Pale. It serves as the headquarters for the Vigilants of Stendarr, a group dedicated to hunting Daedra and other malevolent forces in Skyrim. You do not know who is in charge of the hall/You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('loreius_farm', 'Loreius Farm is a small farm located in The Pale, north of Whitewatch Tower and south of Blizzard Rest. The farm is home to Vantus Loreius and his wife, Curwe.', '''and'':17B,29B ''blizzard'':20B ''curw'':32B ''farm'':2A,4B,8B,23B ''his'':30B ''hom'':25B ''in'':10B ''is'':5B,24B ''locat'':9B ''loreius'':1A,3B,28B ''north'':13B ''of'':14B,19B ''pal'':12B ''rest'':21B ''small'':7B ''south'':18B ''the'':11B,22B ''to'':26B ''tow'':16B ''vantus'':27B ''whitewatch'':15B ''wif'':31B', 'pale', 'Loreius Farm is a small farm located in The Pale, north of Whitewatch Tower. You do not know who Loreius is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('anga''s_mill', 'Anga''s Mill is a small wood mill located along the north bank of the River Yorgrim, west of the Windhelm Stables and north of Morvunskar, in The Pale. The mill consists of two houses and a sawmill, providing lumber for the surrounding area.

The mill is owned by Aeri, a Nord woman who inherited it from her father, who perished during the Great War.', '''aeri'':53B ''along'':13B ''and'':26B,39B ''anga'':1A,4B ''are'':47B ''bank'':16B ''by'':52B ''consists'':35B ''during'':65B ''fath'':62B ''for'':44B ''from'':60B ''great'':67B ''her'':61B ''hous'':38B ''in'':30B ''inherit'':58B ''is'':7B,50B ''it'':59B ''locat'':12B ''lumb'':43B ''mill'':3A,6B,11B,34B,49B ''morvunsk'':29B ''nord'':55B ''north'':15B,27B ''of'':17B,22B,28B,36B ''owned'':51B ''pal'':32B ''perish'':64B ''providing'':42B ''riv'':19B ''s'':2A,5B ''sawmill'':41B ''small'':9B ''stabl'':25B ''surrounding'':46B ''the'':14B,18B,23B,31B,33B,45B,48B,66B ''two'':37B ''war'':68B ''west'':21B ''who'':57B,63B ''windhelm'':24B ''wom'':56B ''wood'':10B ''yorgrim'':20B', 'pale', 'Anga''s Mill is a small wood mill located along the north bank of the River Yorgrim, west of the Windhelm Stables in The Pale. You do not know much about Anga, apart from the fact she runs the mill. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
