INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('yorgrim_overlook', 'Yorgrim Overlook (also referred to as Yorgrim''s Overlook) is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located on the southern slope of the mountain range directly south of Winterhold. The path to the overlook begins just northeast of Forsaken Cave, leading up a series of steps flanked by ancient Nordic statues.', '''also'':5B ''ancient'':50B ''as'':8B ''begins'':36B ''by'':49B ''cav'':41B ''directly'':27B ''flank'':48B ''forsak'':40B ''is'':12B ''just'':37B ''leading'':42B ''locat'':18B ''mountain'':25B ''nordic'':16B,51B ''northeast'':38B ''of'':23B,29B,39B,46B ''on'':19B ''outdoor'':15B ''overlook'':2A,4B,11B,35B ''path'':32B ''rang'':26B ''referr'':6B ''ruin'':17B ''s'':10B ''seri'':45B ''slop'':22B ''small'':14B ''south'':28B ''southern'':21B ''statu'':52B ''steps'':47B ''the'':20B,24B,31B,34B ''to'':7B,33B ''up'':43B ''winterhold'':30B ''yorgrim'':1A,3B,9B', 'pale', 'Yorgrim Overlook is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located on the southern slope of the mountain range directly south of Winterhold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tower_of_mzark', 'The Tower of Mzark is a small Dwarven tower located in Blackreach, accessible only from within the cavern. It is situated in the southwestern corner of Blackreach, perched on a spire between two waterfalls. A stone bridge crosses the river below, connecting to the northern face of the tower.', '''access'':16B ''below'':44B ''betw'':35B ''blackreach'':15B,30B ''bridg'':40B ''cavern'':21B ''connecting'':45B ''corn'':28B ''cross'':41B ''dwarv'':11B ''fac'':49B ''from'':18B ''in'':14B,25B ''is'':8B,23B ''it'':22B ''locat'':13B ''mzark'':3A,7B ''northern'':48B ''of'':2A,6B,29B,50B ''on'':32B ''only'':17B ''perch'':31B ''riv'':43B ''situat'':24B ''small'':10B ''southwestern'':27B ''spir'':34B ''ston'':39B ''the'':4B,20B,26B,42B,47B,51B ''to'':46B ''tow'':1A,5B,12B,52B ''two'':36B ''waterfalls'':37B ''within'':19B', 'pale, dwemer', 'The Tower of Mzark is a small Dwarven tower located in Blackreach.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('raldbthar', 'Raldbthar is a medium-sized Dwarven ruin located west-southwest of Windhelm in The Pale. The ruin is filled with ancient Dwemer machinery, traps, and automatons, making it a challenging destination for adventurers. Bandits have taken refugee in the area.', '''adventurers'':36B ''ancient'':24B ''and'':28B ''are'':43B ''automatons'':29B ''bandits'':37B ''challenging'':33B ''destination'':34B ''dwarv'':8B ''dwem'':25B ''fill'':22B ''for'':35B ''hav'':38B ''in'':16B,41B ''is'':3B,21B ''it'':31B ''locat'':10B ''machinery'':26B ''making'':30B ''medium'':6B ''medium-siz'':5B ''of'':14B ''pal'':18B ''raldbth'':1A,2B ''refuge'':40B ''ruin'':9B,20B ''siz'':7B ''southwest'':13B ''tak'':39B ''the'':17B,19B,42B ''traps'':27B ''west'':12B ''west-southwest'':11B ''windhelm'':15B ''with'':23B', 'pale, dwemer', 'Raldbthar is a medium-sized Dwarven ruin located west-southwest of Windhelm in The Pale. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('beitild''s_house', '
Beitild''s House is the residence of Beitild, a Nord miner and the owner of Iron-Breaker Mine, located in Dawnstar.  Beitild is known for her strong personality and her position as a key figure in Dawnstar''s economy, with the mine being one of the town''s primary sources of income.', '''and'':15B,33B ''as'':36B ''being'':47B ''beitild'':1A,4B,11B,26B ''break'':21B ''dawnst'':25B,41B ''economy'':43B ''figur'':39B ''for'':29B ''her'':30B,34B ''hous'':3A,6B ''in'':24B,40B ''incom'':56B ''iron'':20B ''iron-break'':19B ''is'':7B,27B ''key'':38B ''known'':28B ''locat'':23B ''min'':14B,22B,46B ''nord'':13B ''of'':10B,18B,49B,55B ''one'':48B ''owner'':17B ''personality'':32B ''position'':35B ''primary'':53B ''residenc'':9B ''s'':2A,5B,42B,52B ''sourc'':54B ''strong'':31B ''the'':8B,16B,45B,50B ''town'':51B ''with'':44B', 'pale', 'Beitild''s House is the residence of Beitild, located in Dawnstar. You do not know who Betilid is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('irkngthand', 'Irkngthand is a large Dwarven ruin located west of Windhelm and northwest of Raldbthar in The Pale. The ruin is initially occupied by bandits.

The entrance to Irkngthand can be reached by following a dirt path south from Nightgate Inn. When the path diverges, take the eastern route, as the southwest branch leads to Tumble Arch Pass. Alternatively, the entrance can be accessed by descending the mountain from the south and navigating a series of wooden bridges leading up to the ruin.', '''access'':64B ''alternatively'':59B ''and'':12B,72B ''arch'':57B ''as'':50B ''bandits'':25B ''be'':31B,63B ''branch'':53B ''bridg'':78B ''by'':24B,33B,65B ''can'':30B,62B ''descending'':66B ''dirt'':36B ''diverg'':45B ''dwarv'':6B ''eastern'':48B ''entranc'':27B,61B ''following'':34B ''from'':39B,69B ''in'':16B ''initially'':22B ''inn'':41B ''irkngthand'':1A,2B,29B ''is'':3B,21B ''larg'':5B ''leading'':79B ''leads'':54B ''locat'':8B ''mountain'':68B ''navigating'':73B ''nightgat'':40B ''northwest'':13B ''occupi'':23B ''of'':10B,14B,76B ''pal'':18B ''pass'':58B ''path'':37B,44B ''raldbth'':15B ''reach'':32B ''rout'':49B ''ruin'':7B,20B,83B ''seri'':75B ''south'':38B,71B ''southwest'':52B ''tak'':46B ''the'':17B,19B,26B,43B,47B,51B,60B,67B,70B,82B ''to'':28B,55B,81B ''tumbl'':56B ''up'':80B ''west'':9B ''when'':42B ''windhelm'':11B ''wood'':77B', 'pale, dwemer', 'Irkngthand is a large Dwarven ruin located west of Windhelm in The Pale.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shrine_of_mehrunes_dagon', 'The Shrine of Mehrunes Dagon is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon, located in The Pale, south-southeast of Stonehills and southwest of The Lord Stone.

The shrine is best reached by traveling southwest from The Lord Stone, following a winding path that leads to its remote location in the mountainous terrain.', '''and'':29B ''best'':38B ''by'':40B ''daedric'':16B ''dagon'':4A,9B,19B ''dedicat'':13B ''following'':47B ''from'':43B ''in'':21B,57B ''is'':10B,37B ''its'':54B ''leads'':52B ''locat'':20B ''location'':56B ''lord'':33B,45B ''mehrun'':3A,8B,18B ''mountainous'':59B ''of'':2A,7B,27B,31B ''pal'':23B ''path'':50B ''princ'':17B ''reach'':39B ''remot'':55B ''shrin'':1A,6B,12B,36B ''south'':25B ''south-southeast'':24B ''southeast'':26B ''southwest'':30B,42B ''ston'':34B,46B ''stonehills'':28B ''terrain'':60B ''that'':51B ''the'':5B,15B,22B,32B,35B,44B,58B ''to'':14B,53B ''traveling'':41B ''winding'':49B', 'pale, daedra, daedric', 'The Shrine of Mehrunes Dagon is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon, located somewhere near the mountains in south of Dawnstar The Pale.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('duskglow_crevice', 'Duskglow Crevice is a small cave located south of Dawnstar and east of Fort Dunstad in The Pale. The cave is inhabited by Falmer. The cave is accessible via a path off the road between Dawnstar and Windhelm, not far north-northeast of the Weynon Stones. It can also be approached from Fort Fellhammer. ', '''access'':30B ''also'':52B ''and'':13B,39B ''approach'':54B ''be'':53B ''betw'':37B ''by'':25B ''can'':51B ''cav'':8B,22B,28B ''crevic'':2A,4B ''dawnst'':12B,38B ''dunst'':17B ''duskglow'':1A,3B ''east'':14B ''falm'':26B ''far'':42B ''fellhamm'':57B ''fort'':16B,56B ''from'':55B ''in'':18B ''inhabit'':24B ''is'':5B,23B,29B ''it'':50B ''locat'':9B ''north'':44B ''north-northeast'':43B ''northeast'':45B ''not'':41B ''of'':11B,15B,46B ''off'':34B ''pal'':20B ''path'':33B ''road'':36B ''small'':7B ''south'':10B ''ston'':49B ''the'':19B,21B,27B,35B,47B ''via'':31B ''weynon'':48B ''windhelm'':40B', 'pale', 'Duskglow Crevice is a small cave located south of Dawnstar in The Pale. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dimhollow_crypt', 'Dimhollow Crypt is a medium-sized cave located east of Stonehills and southwest of Frostmere Crypt in The Pale. Rumors of vampires have been seen around the area.', '''and'':15B ''are'':31B ''around'':29B ''been'':27B ''cav'':10B ''crypt'':2A,4B,19B ''dimhollow'':1A,3B ''east'':12B ''frostmer'':18B ''hav'':26B ''in'':20B ''is'':5B ''locat'':11B ''medium'':8B ''medium-siz'':7B ''of'':13B,17B,24B ''pal'':22B ''rumors'':23B ''seen'':28B ''siz'':9B ''southwest'':16B ''stonehills'':14B ''the'':21B,30B ''vampir'':25B', 'pale', 'Dimhollow Crypt is a medium-sized cave located east of Stonehills in The Pale. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wreck_of_the_brinehammer', 'The Wreck of the Brinehammer is a shipwreck located northwest of Dawnstar and northeast of High Gate Ruins, along the shore of the Sea of Ghosts in The Pale. The remains of the ship are scattered across the coastline.', '''across'':41B ''along'':23B ''and'':17B ''are'':39B ''brinehamm'':4A,9B ''coastlin'':43B ''dawnst'':16B ''gat'':21B ''ghosts'':30B ''high'':20B ''in'':31B ''is'':10B ''locat'':13B ''northeast'':18B ''northwest'':14B ''of'':2A,7B,15B,19B,26B,29B,36B ''pal'':33B ''remains'':35B ''ruins'':22B ''scatter'':40B ''ship'':38B ''shipwreck'':12B ''shor'':25B ''the'':3A,5B,8B,24B,27B,32B,34B,37B,42B ''wreck'':1A,6B', 'pale, sailor', 'The Wreck of the Brinehammer is a shipwreck located  along the shore of the Sea of Ghosts in The Pale.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shearpoint', 'Shearpoint is a mountaintop dragon lair located northeast of Whiterun and southwest of Irkngthand in The Pale. To reach Shearpoint, adventurers can follow a rough path northwest past Fellglow Keep, circling northeast to the summit.', '''adventurers'':22B ''and'':12B ''can'':23B ''circling'':32B ''dragon'':6B ''fellglow'':30B ''follow'':24B ''in'':16B ''irkngthand'':15B ''is'':3B ''keep'':31B ''lair'':7B ''locat'':8B ''mountaintop'':5B ''northeast'':9B,33B ''northwest'':28B ''of'':10B,14B ''pal'':18B ''past'':29B ''path'':27B ''reach'':20B ''rough'':26B ''shearpoint'':1A,2B,21B ''southwest'':13B ''summit'':36B ''the'':17B,35B ''to'':19B,34B ''whiterun'':11B', 'pale, dragon', 'Shearpoint is a mountaintop dragon lair located northeast of Whiterun in The Pale. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shrouded_grove', 'Shrouded Grove is a secluded grove with a small cave located in The Pale, west of Lake Yorgrim, due south of Silverdrift Lair, and west of Nightgate Inn.', '''and'':26B ''cav'':12B ''due'':21B ''grov'':2A,4B,8B ''in'':14B ''inn'':30B ''is'':5B ''lair'':25B ''lak'':19B ''locat'':13B ''nightgat'':29B ''of'':18B,23B,28B ''pal'':16B ''seclud'':7B ''shroud'':1A,3B ''silverdrift'':24B ''small'':11B ''south'':22B ''the'':15B ''west'':17B,27B ''with'':9B ''yorgrim'':20B', 'pale', 'Shrouded Grove is a secluded grove with a small cave located west of Nightigate Inn in The Pale.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('weynon_stones', 'The Weynon Stones are an ancient landmark in The Pale, consisting of a circle of standing stones. The site is located south of Dawnstar, between Korvanjund and Fort Dunstad, just south of the main path connecting these locations.', '''an'':7B ''ancient'':8B ''and'':29B ''are'':6B ''betw'':27B ''circl'':16B ''connecting'':38B ''consisting'':13B ''dawnst'':26B ''dunst'':31B ''fort'':30B ''in'':10B ''is'':22B ''just'':32B ''korvanjund'':28B ''landmark'':9B ''locat'':23B ''locations'':40B ''main'':36B ''of'':14B,17B,25B,34B ''pal'':12B ''path'':37B ''sit'':21B ''south'':24B,33B ''standing'':18B ''ston'':2A,5B,19B ''the'':3B,11B,20B,35B ''thes'':39B ''weynon'':1A,4B', 'pale, traveler, scholar', 'The Weynon Stones are an ancient landmark in The Pale. The site is located south of Dawnstar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('brina''s_house', 'Brina''s House is a small residence in Dawnstar, home to Brina Merilis, a Nord warrior and former commander in the Imperial Legion. She is accompanied by Horik Halfhand, a retired Nord Legionnaire who remains fiercely loyal to Brina, his former commander.', '''accompani'':29B ''and'':20B ''brin'':1A,4B,15B,42B ''by'':30B ''command'':22B,45B ''dawnst'':12B ''fiercely'':39B ''form'':21B,44B ''halfhand'':32B ''his'':43B ''hom'':13B ''horik'':31B ''hous'':3A,6B ''imperial'':25B ''in'':11B,23B ''is'':7B,28B ''legion'':26B ''legionnair'':36B ''loyal'':40B ''merilis'':16B ''nord'':18B,35B ''remains'':38B ''residenc'':10B ''retir'':34B ''s'':2A,5B ''she'':27B ''small'':9B ''the'':24B ''to'':14B,41B ''warrior'':19B ''who'':37B', 'pale', 'Brina''s House is a residence in Dawnstar, home to Brina Merilis. You do not know who she is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fruki''s_house', 'Fruki''s House is a small residence located in Dawnstar, just north of Quicksilver Mine. The house is home to Fruki, a hardworking Nord miner employed at the mine.', '''at'':30B ''dawnst'':13B ''employ'':29B ''fruki'':1A,4B,24B ''hardworking'':26B ''hom'':22B ''hous'':3A,6B,20B ''in'':12B ''is'':7B,21B ''just'':14B ''locat'':11B ''min'':18B,28B,32B ''nord'':27B ''north'':15B ''of'':16B ''quicksilv'':17B ''residenc'':10B ''s'':2A,5B ''small'':9B ''the'':19B,31B ''to'':23B', 'pale', 'Fruki''s House is a small residence located in Dawnstar. You do not know who she is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('irgnir''s_house', 'Irgnir''s House is a modest home located at the eastern end of Dawnstar. It serves as the residence of Irgnir, a Nord miner who works under Beitild at the Iron-Breaker Mine.', '''as'':20B ''at'':12B,32B ''beitild'':31B ''break'':36B ''dawnst'':17B ''eastern'':14B ''end'':15B ''hom'':10B ''hous'':3A,6B ''irgnir'':1A,4B,24B ''iron'':35B ''iron-break'':34B ''is'':7B ''it'':18B ''locat'':11B ''min'':27B,37B ''modest'':9B ''nord'':26B ''of'':16B,23B ''residenc'':22B ''s'':2A,5B ''serv'':19B ''the'':13B,21B,33B ''under'':30B ''who'':28B ''works'':29B', 'pale', 'Irgnir''s House is ahome located in Dawnstar. You do not know who Irgnir is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('iron-breaker_mine', 'Iron-Breaker Mine is a small iron mine located in the eastern part of Dawnstar. The mine is owned by Beitild, a prominent Nord figure in the town''s mining industry, and serves as a critical part of the local economy. Several miners work under Beitild''s supervision, including Gjak, Karl, and Bodil.', '''and'':37B,57B ''as'':39B ''beitild'':26B,51B ''bodil'':58B ''break'':3A,7B ''by'':25B ''critical'':41B ''dawnst'':20B ''eastern'':17B ''economy'':46B ''figur'':30B ''gjak'':55B ''in'':15B,31B ''including'':54B ''industry'':36B ''iron'':2A,6B,12B ''iron-break'':1A,5B ''is'':9B,23B ''karl'':56B ''local'':45B ''locat'':14B ''min'':4A,8B,13B,22B ''miners'':48B ''mining'':35B ''nord'':29B ''of'':19B,43B ''owned'':24B ''part'':18B,42B ''prominent'':28B ''s'':34B,52B ''serv'':38B ''several'':47B ''small'':11B ''supervision'':53B ''the'':16B,21B,32B,44B ''town'':33B ''under'':50B ''work'':49B', 'pale', 'Iron-Breaker Mine is a small iron mine located in the eastern part of Dawnstar. You do not know who runs the mine.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('leigelf''s_house', 'Leigelf''s House is the home of Leigelf, a Nord miner and the owner of Quicksilver Mine in Dawnstar. Located in the center of town, next to the blacksmith, the house reflects Leigelf''s standing as a key figure in Dawnstar''s mining industry.', '''and'':15B ''as'':39B ''blacksmith'':32B ''cent'':26B ''dawnst'':22B,44B ''figur'':42B ''hom'':9B ''hous'':3A,6B,34B ''in'':21B,24B,43B ''industry'':47B ''is'':7B ''key'':41B ''leigelf'':1A,4B,11B,36B ''locat'':23B ''min'':14B,20B ''mining'':46B ''next'':29B ''nord'':13B ''of'':10B,18B,27B ''owner'':17B ''quicksilv'':19B ''reflects'':35B ''s'':2A,5B,37B,45B ''standing'':38B ''the'':8B,16B,25B,31B,33B ''to'':30B ''town'':28B', 'pale', 'Leigelf''s House is the home of Leigelf in Dawnstar. You do not know who Leigelf is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('quicksilver_mine', 'Quicksilver Mine is a small but significant quicksilver mine located in the western part of Dawnstar. Owned by Leigelf, the mine is an essential part of the town''s economy, providing valuable quicksilver ore and employment for its residents.

Among the miners working in Quicksilver Mine are Orgny, Edith, and Lond.', '''among'':42B ''an'':25B ''and'':37B,52B ''are'':49B ''but'':8B ''by'':20B ''dawnst'':18B ''economy'':32B ''edith'':51B ''employment'':38B ''essential'':26B ''for'':39B ''in'':13B,46B ''is'':5B,24B ''its'':40B ''leigelf'':21B ''locat'':12B ''lond'':53B ''min'':2A,4B,11B,23B,48B ''miners'':44B ''of'':17B,28B ''ore'':36B ''orgny'':50B ''owned'':19B ''part'':16B,27B ''providing'':33B ''quicksilv'':1A,3B,10B,35B,47B ''residents'':41B ''s'':31B ''significant'':9B ''small'':7B ''the'':14B,22B,29B,43B ''town'':30B ''valuabl'':34B ''western'':15B ''working'':45B', 'pale', 'Quicksilver Mine is a small but quicksilver mine located in Dawnstar. You do not know who runs the mine.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rustleif''s_house', 'Rustleif''s House is a smithy located near the shoreline of Dawnstar, facing the bay. It serves as both the home and workshop of Rustleif, a renowned weaponsmith known for crafting arms and armor for the jarl''s men. His skill and reputation make him an important figure in the town''s economy and defense.

Rustleif is assisted by his Redguard wife, Seren, who is pregnant and plays an active role in the business. Both Rustleif and Seren offer merchant services, providing weapons, armor, and crafting supplies to adventurers and locals alike. ', '''activ'':73B ''adventurers'':92B ''alik'':95B ''an'':49B,72B ''and'':25B,36B,45B,57B,70B,80B,88B,93B ''armor'':37B,87B ''arms'':35B ''as'':21B ''assist'':61B ''bay'':18B ''both'':22B,78B ''business'':77B ''by'':62B ''crafting'':34B,89B ''dawnst'':15B ''defens'':58B ''economy'':56B ''facing'':16B ''figur'':51B ''for'':33B,38B ''him'':48B ''his'':43B,63B ''hom'':24B ''hous'':3A,6B ''important'':50B ''in'':52B,75B ''is'':7B,60B,68B ''it'':19B ''jarl'':40B ''known'':32B ''locals'':94B ''locat'':10B ''mak'':47B ''men'':42B ''merchant'':83B ''near'':11B ''of'':14B,27B ''offer'':82B ''plays'':71B ''pregnant'':69B ''providing'':85B ''redguard'':64B ''renown'':30B ''reputation'':46B ''rol'':74B ''rustleif'':1A,4B,28B,59B,79B ''s'':2A,5B,41B,55B ''ser'':66B,81B ''serv'':20B ''servic'':84B ''shorelin'':13B ''skill'':44B ''smithy'':9B ''suppli'':90B ''the'':12B,17B,23B,39B,53B,76B ''to'':91B ''town'':54B ''weapons'':86B ''weaponsmith'':31B ''who'':67B ''wif'':65B ''workshop'':26B', 'pale', 'Rustleif''s House is a building located in Dawnstar. You do not know who Rustleif is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vvardenfell', 'Vvardenfell, also known as the Black Isle, is a large island situated within the bay-like Inner Sea of Morrowind, bordered by the mainland except for its northern coast, which meets the Sea of Ghosts. The island is dominated by the towering volcano, Red Mountain, and derives its name from the original Dwemeri term for the mountain, meaning "City of the Strong Shield." The landscape of Vvardenfell is characterized by arid wastelands, rocky highlands, and coastal wetlands that host a variety of unique flora and fauna. The volcanic activity of Red Mountain, including lava flows and ash-falls, contributes to a constant cycle of ecological renewal, enriching the soil and allowing new plants and fungi to flourish in the aftermath of eruptions.

Historically, Vvardenfell was home to House Dagoth, the only Chimer clan with its capital located on the island, alongside a significant Dwemer kingdom. However, the influence of Dagoth Ur and the corruption of the Ash Blight dramatically impacted the island''s environment and its inhabitants, leading to a noticeable decline in its vibrancy by the late Third Era, including the extinction of native species such as Cliff Striders and Nix-Oxen. The island faced catastrophic destruction during the Red Year in 4E 5 when the Ministry of Truth collided with the city of Vivec, triggering a massive eruption of Red Mountain. The resulting ash coverage forced the majority of Vvardenfell''s population to evacuate, marking a significant turning point in the region''s history.', '''4e'':208B ''5'':209B ''activity'':91B ''aftermath'':123B ''allowing'':114B ''alongsid'':144B ''also'':3B ''and'':48B,77B,87B,98B,113B,117B,155B,168B,194B ''arid'':73B ''as'':5B,191B ''ash'':100B,160B,230B ''ash-falls'':99B ''bay'':17B ''bay-lik'':16B ''black'':7B ''blight'':161B ''border'':23B ''by'':24B,42B,72B,179B ''capital'':139B ''catastrophic'':201B ''characteriz'':71B ''chim'':135B ''city'':61B,218B ''clan'':136B ''cliff'':192B ''coast'':31B ''coastal'':78B ''collid'':215B ''constant'':105B ''contribut'':102B ''corruption'':157B ''coverag'':231B ''cycle'':106B ''dagoth'':132B,153B ''declin'':175B ''deriv'':49B ''destruction'':202B ''dominat'':41B ''dramatically'':162B ''during'':203B ''dwem'':147B ''dwemeri'':55B ''ecological'':108B ''enriching'':110B ''environment'':167B ''eruption'':224B ''eruptions'':125B ''evacuat'':240B ''except'':27B ''extinction'':186B ''fac'':200B ''falls'':101B ''faun'':88B ''flor'':86B ''flourish'':120B ''flows'':97B ''for'':28B,57B ''forc'':232B ''from'':52B ''fungi'':118B ''ghosts'':37B ''highlands'':76B ''historically'':126B ''history'':250B ''hom'':129B ''host'':81B ''hous'':131B ''howev'':149B ''impact'':163B ''in'':121B,176B,207B,246B ''including'':95B,184B ''influenc'':151B ''inhabitants'':170B ''inner'':19B ''is'':9B,40B,70B ''island'':12B,39B,143B,165B,199B ''isle'':8B ''its'':29B,50B,138B,169B,177B ''kingdom'':148B ''known'':4B ''landscap'':67B ''larg'':11B ''lat'':181B ''lav'':96B ''leading'':171B ''lik'':18B ''locat'':140B ''mainland'':26B ''majority'':234B ''marking'':241B ''massiv'':223B ''meaning'':60B ''meets'':33B ''ministry'':212B ''morrowind'':22B ''mountain'':47B,59B,94B,227B ''nam'':51B ''nativ'':188B ''new'':115B ''nix'':196B ''nix-ox'':195B ''northern'':30B ''notic'':174B ''of'':21B,36B,62B,68B,84B,92B,107B,124B,152B,158B,187B,213B,219B,225B,235B ''on'':141B ''only'':134B ''original'':54B ''oxen'':197B ''plants'':116B ''point'':245B ''population'':238B ''red'':46B,93B,205B,226B ''region'':248B ''renewal'':109B ''resulting'':229B ''rocky'':75B ''s'':166B,237B,249B ''shield'':65B ''significant'':146B,243B ''situat'':13B ''soil'':112B ''speci'':189B ''striders'':193B ''strong'':64B ''such'':190B ''term'':56B ''that'':80B ''the'':6B,15B,25B,34B,38B,43B,53B,58B,63B,66B,89B,111B,122B,133B,142B,150B,156B,159B,164B,180B,185B,198B,204B,211B,217B,228B,233B,247B ''third'':182B ''to'':103B,119B,130B,172B,239B ''towering'':44B ''triggering'':221B ''truth'':214B ''turning'':244B ''uniqu'':85B ''ur'':154B ''variety'':83B ''vibrancy'':178B ''vivec'':220B ''volcan'':45B ''volcanic'':90B ''vvardenfell'':1A,2B,69B,127B,236B ''was'':128B ''wastelands'':74B ''wetlands'':79B ''when'':210B ''which'':32B ''with'':137B,216B ''within'':14B ''year'':206B', 'scholar, darkelf', '
Vvardenfell, also known as the Black Isle, is an island in Morrowind dominated by the volcano Red Mountain. The landscape features arid wastelands, rocky highlands, and coastal wetlands, with volcanic activity enriching the soil. Historically home to House Dagoth and the Dwemer, the island suffered from the corruption of the Ash Blight and the influence of Dagoth Ur. By the late Third Era, many species became extinct, and the region was devastated during the Red Year in 4E 5 when Red Mountain erupted, causing widespread destruction and forcing the evacuation of most of the population.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sanuarach_mine', 'Sanuarach Mine is a small silver mine located in northern Karthwasten in the Reach. It is occupied by Silver-Blood mercenaries attempting to take control of the mine.

