INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_sea_squall', 'The Sea Squall is a ship permanently docked in Dawnstar''s Northstar Port. Captain Wayfinder, a Nord owns the ship serves. Among the inhabitants of The Sea Squall are Guthrum, an aging Nord ranger who has made the ship his home, and Ravam Verethi, a Dark Elf.', '''aging'':35B ''among'':25B ''an'':34B ''and'':45B ''are'':32B ''captain'':17B ''dark'':49B ''dawnst'':13B ''dock'':11B ''elf'':50B ''guthrum'':33B ''his'':43B ''hom'':44B ''in'':12B ''inhabitants'':27B ''is'':7B ''mad'':40B ''nord'':20B,36B ''northst'':15B ''of'':28B ''owns'':21B ''permanently'':10B ''port'':16B ''rang'':37B ''ravam'':46B ''s'':14B ''serv'':24B ''ship'':9B,23B,42B ''squall'':3A,6B,31B ''the'':1A,4B,22B,26B,29B,41B ''verethi'':47B ''wayfind'':18B ''who'':38B', 'pale, sailor', 'The Sea Squall is a ship permanently docked in Dawnstar''s Northstar Port. You do not know who owns the ship.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_white_hall', 'The White Hall is a prominent two-story structure located on a hillside overlooking Dawnstar. Positioned next to the Dawnstar Barracks, it serves as the seat of power for the Jarl of the Pale and their court. The hall is home to Jarl Skald, the ruler of the Pale, along with key members of his court, including Madena, the court wizard; Jod, the housecarl; Frorkmar Banner-Torn, the military advisor; and Bulfrek, the servant. The White Hall is central to the governance of the Pale, reflecting both its importance and the modest nature of its northern setting.', '''advisor'':75B ''along'':54B ''and'':39B,76B,95B ''as'':28B ''bann'':71B ''banner-torn'':70B ''barracks'':25B ''both'':92B ''bulfrek'':77B ''central'':84B ''court'':41B,60B,64B ''dawnst'':19B,24B ''for'':33B ''frorkm'':69B ''governanc'':87B ''hall'':3A,6B,43B,82B ''hillsid'':17B ''his'':59B ''hom'':45B ''housecarl'':68B ''importanc'':94B ''including'':61B ''is'':7B,44B,83B ''it'':26B ''its'':93B,100B ''jarl'':35B,47B ''jod'':66B ''key'':56B ''locat'':14B ''maden'':62B ''members'':57B ''military'':74B ''modest'':97B ''natur'':98B ''next'':21B ''northern'':101B ''of'':31B,36B,51B,58B,88B,99B ''on'':15B ''overlooking'':18B ''pal'':38B,53B,90B ''position'':20B ''pow'':32B ''prominent'':9B ''reflecting'':91B ''rul'':50B ''seat'':30B ''serv'':27B ''servant'':79B ''setting'':102B ''skald'':48B ''story'':12B ''structur'':13B ''the'':1A,4B,23B,29B,34B,37B,40B,42B,49B,52B,63B,67B,73B,78B,80B,86B,89B,96B ''to'':22B,46B,85B ''torn'':72B ''two'':11B ''two-story'':10B ''whit'':2A,5B,81B ''with'':55B ''wizard'':65B', 'pale, noble', 'The White Hall is a prominent structure in Dawnstar. It serves as the seat of power for the Jarl of the Pale and their court. The hall is home to Jarl Skald, the ruler of the Pale. You do now know anyone else who works here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('windpeak_inn', 'Windpeak Inn is a cozy inn located in Dawnstar, conveniently situated as the first building you''ll encounter when entering the town from the main road. The inn is run by Thoring, who manages the establishment, rents out rooms, and offers food and drinks to travelers and locals alike.

Karita, Thoring''s daughter, serves as the inn''s bard, providing music and entertainment to patrons. ', '''alik'':51B ''and'':42B,45B,49B,64B ''as'':14B,57B ''bard'':61B ''building'':17B ''by'':33B ''conveniently'':12B ''cozy'':7B ''daught'':55B ''dawnst'':11B ''drinks'':46B ''encount'':20B ''entering'':22B ''entertainment'':65B ''establishment'':38B ''first'':16B ''food'':44B ''from'':25B ''in'':10B ''inn'':2A,4B,8B,30B,59B ''is'':5B,31B ''karit'':52B ''ll'':19B ''locals'':50B ''locat'':9B ''main'':27B ''manag'':36B ''music'':63B ''offers'':43B ''out'':40B ''patrons'':67B ''providing'':62B ''rents'':39B ''road'':28B ''rooms'':41B ''run'':32B ''s'':54B,60B ''serv'':56B ''situat'':13B ''the'':15B,23B,26B,29B,37B,58B ''thoring'':34B,53B ''to'':47B,66B ''town'':24B ''travelers'':48B ''when'':21B ''who'':35B ''windpeak'':1A,3B ''you'':18B', 'pale, innkeeper, traveler', 'Windpeak Inn is an inn located in Dawnstar. You do not know who runs the Inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_reach', 'The Reach is a mountainous hold in western Skyrim, with its capital, Markarth, nestled in the southwestern corner of the region. It is aligned with the Imperial Legion. The hold is dominated by the rugged Druadach Mountains, while its eastern edge, stretching from Broken Tower Redoubt to Fort Sungard, is characterized by hilly terrain. The Karth River originates in the southern mountains, carving the dramatic Karth River Canyon as it flows through the hold.

Markarth, a former Dwemer city, rises from the living rock of the Druadach Mountains, reflecting the ancient ingenuity of its creators. The Reach is also home to smaller settlements such as Karthwasten and Old Hroldan, as well as the  Orc stronghold Dushnikh Yal in the southern steppes. The region is populated by the native Reachmen, who form the majority in many settlements, and the Forsworn, a militant faction that fiercely guards their independence, attacking outsiders on sight.

Flora in the Reach includes juniper berry bushes, hanging moss, mora tapinella, and scattered mountain flowers, with greater concentrations in the northeast. Its fauna is equally rugged, with bears, sabre cats, and other predators roaming its hills and valleys.', '''align'':26B ''also'':101B ''ancient'':93B ''and'':109B,139B,166B,185B,191B ''as'':71B,107B,112B,114B ''attacking'':150B ''bears'':182B ''berry'':160B ''brok'':46B ''bush'':161B ''by'':35B,54B,128B ''canyon'':70B ''capital'':14B ''carving'':65B ''cats'':184B ''characteriz'':53B ''city'':81B ''concentrations'':172B ''corn'':20B ''creators'':97B ''dominat'':34B ''dramatic'':67B ''druadach'':38B,89B ''dushnikh'':118B ''dwem'':80B ''eastern'':42B ''edge'':43B ''equally'':179B ''faction'':144B ''faun'':177B ''fiercely'':146B ''flor'':154B ''flowers'':169B ''flows'':73B ''form'':79B,133B ''forsworn'':141B ''fort'':50B ''from'':45B,83B ''great'':171B ''guards'':147B ''hanging'':162B ''hills'':190B ''hilly'':55B ''hold'':8B,32B,76B ''hom'':102B ''hrold'':111B ''imperial'':29B ''in'':9B,17B,61B,120B,136B,155B,173B ''includ'':158B ''independenc'':149B ''ingenuity'':94B ''is'':5B,25B,33B,52B,100B,126B,178B ''it'':24B,72B ''its'':13B,41B,96B,176B,189B ''junip'':159B ''karth'':58B,68B ''karthwast'':108B ''legion'':30B ''living'':85B ''majority'':135B ''many'':137B ''markarth'':15B,77B ''militant'':143B ''mor'':164B ''moss'':163B ''mountain'':168B ''mountainous'':7B ''mountains'':39B,64B,90B ''nativ'':130B ''nestl'':16B ''northeast'':175B ''of'':21B,87B,95B ''old'':110B ''on'':152B ''orc'':116B ''originat'':60B ''other'':186B ''outsiders'':151B ''populat'':127B ''predators'':187B ''reach'':2A,4B,99B,157B ''reachm'':131B ''redoubt'':48B ''reflecting'':91B ''region'':23B,125B ''ris'':82B ''riv'':59B,69B ''roaming'':188B ''rock'':86B ''rugg'':37B,180B ''sabr'':183B ''scatter'':167B ''settlements'':105B,138B ''sight'':153B ''skyrim'':11B ''small'':104B ''southern'':63B,122B ''southwestern'':19B ''stepp'':123B ''stretching'