Markarth, a former Dwemer city, rises from the living rock of the Druadach Mountains, reflecting the ancient ingenuity of its creators. The Reach is also home to smaller settlements such as Karthwasten and Old Hroldan, as well as the  The region is populated by the native Reachmen, who form the majority in many settlements, and the Forsworn, a militant faction that fiercely guards their independence, attacking outsiders on sight.
', '', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('markarth', 'Markarth is a major city located in the southwest of Skyrim, near the border of High Rock, and serves as the capital of the Reach. Built within an ancient Dwemer city, its architecture is strikingly unique, with much of it carved into the surrounding rock. Jarl Igmund, the ruler, struggles with the Forsworn, a militant group that infests the surrounding countryside, attacking travelers and threatening the hold. The people of Markarth are wary of outsiders, with the city guards treating them with suspicion and hostility.

The Silver-Blood family holds significant influence in Markarth, owning half the city, including the Silver-Blood Inn and Cidhna Mine, a notorious prison considered the most secure in Skyrim. The city’s poor live in The Warrens, a cliffside area of extreme poverty, with many working in the mines and smelters. Near the city entrance, an open-air marketplace hosts several shops, while the guards are stationed in a Dwemer dormitory beneath the central Guard Tower.

Markarth is also home to Understone Keep, the ancient Dwemer castle and seat of government located at the western end of the city. Other notable locations include the Temple of Dibella, the Hag''s Cure, Arnleif and Sons Trading Company, and Salvius Farm. ', '''air'':148B ''also'':169B ''an'':29B,145B ''ancient'':30B,175B ''and'':19B,65B,85B,107B,139B,178B,203B,207B ''architectur'':34B ''are'':73B,129B,156B ''arnleif'':202B ''as'':21B ''at'':183B ''attacking'':63B ''beneath'':162B ''blood'':90B,105B ''bord'':15B ''built'':27B ''capital'':23B ''carv'':42B ''castl'':177B ''central'':164B ''cidhn'':108B ''city'':6B,32B,79B,100B,120B,143B,189B ''cliffsid'':128B ''company'':206B ''consider'':113B ''countrysid'':62B ''cur'':201B ''dibell'':197B ''dormitory'':161B ''dwem'':31B,160B,176B ''end'':186B ''entranc'':144B ''extrem'':131B ''family'':91B ''farm'':209B ''forsworn'':54B ''government'':181B ''group'':57B ''guard'':165B ''guards'':80B,155B ''hag'':199B ''half'':98B ''high'':17B ''hold'':68B ''holds'':92B ''hom'':170B ''hostility'':86B ''hosts'':150B ''igmund'':48B ''in'':8B,95B,117B,124B,136B,158B ''includ'':193B ''including'':101B ''infests'':59B ''influenc'':94B ''inn'':106B ''into'':43B ''is'':3B,35B,168B ''it'':41B ''its'':33B ''jarl'':47B ''keep'':173B ''liv'':123B ''locat'':7B,182B ''locations'':192B ''major'':5B ''many'':134B ''markarth'':1A,2B,72B,96B,167B ''marketplac'':149B ''militant'':56B ''min'':109B,138B ''most'':115B ''much'':39B ''near'':13B,141B ''notabl'':191B ''notorious'':111B ''of'':11B,16B,24B,40B,71B,75B,130B,180B,187B,196B ''open'':147B ''open-'':146B ''other'':190B ''outsiders'':76B ''owning'':97B ''peopl'':70B ''poor'':122B ''poverty'':132B ''prison'':112B ''reach'':26B ''rock'':18B,46B ''rul'':50B ''s'':121B,200B ''salvius'':208B ''seat'':179B ''secur'':116B ''serv'':20B ''several'':151B ''shops'':152B ''significant'':93B ''silv'':89B,104B ''silver-blood'':88B,103B ''skyrim'':12B,118B ''smelters'':140B ''sons'':204B ''southwest'':10B ''statio