INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('treasury_house', 'The Treasury House is a location at the northern end of the first terrace in Markarth, overlooking the city and the surrounding Reach. This vital financial institution serves as the lifeblood of the region''s economy, offering support and services to landowners, particularly the influential Silver-Blood family. The Treasury House is where miners, farmers, and day-laborers receive their wages, making it essential to the daily functioning of the Reach.

Rhiada runs the front desk, overseeing the flow of gold and coin, while the treasury itself is secured behind an expert-locked gate. Nana Ildene and Donnel maintain order and cleanliness in the building, with Nana having worked there for over twenty years. ', '''an'':95B ''and'':22B,41B,59B,86B,102B,106B ''as'':31B ''at'':9B ''behind'':94B ''blood'':50B ''building'':110B ''city'':21B ''cleanliness'':107B ''coin'':87B ''daily'':71B ''day'':61B ''day-laborers'':60B ''desk'':80B ''donnel'':103B ''economy'':38B ''end'':12B ''essential'':68B ''expert'':97B ''expert-lock'':96B ''family'':51B ''farmers'':58B ''financial'':28B ''first'':15B ''flow'':83B ''for'':116B ''front'':79B ''functioning'':72B ''gat'':99B ''gold'':85B ''having'':113B ''hous'':2A,5B,54B ''ilden'':101B ''in'':17B,108B ''influential'':47B ''institution'':29B ''is'':6B,55B,92B ''it'':67B ''itself'':91B ''laborers'':62B ''landowners'':44B ''lifeblood'':33B ''location'':8B ''lock'':98B ''maintain'':104B ''making'':66B ''markarth'':18B ''miners'':57B ''nan'':100B,112B ''northern'':11B ''of'':13B,34B,73B,84B ''offering'':39B ''order'':105B ''over'':117B ''overlooking'':19B ''overseeing'':81B ''particularly'':45B ''reach'':25B,75B ''receiv'':63B ''region'':36B ''rhi'':76B ''runs'':77B ''s'':37B ''secur'':93B ''serv'':30B ''servic'':42B ''silv'':49B ''silver-blood'':48B ''support'':40B ''surrounding'':24B ''terrac'':16B ''the'':3B,10B,14B,20B,23B,32B,35B,46B,52B,64B,70B,74B,78B,82B,89B,109B ''ther'':115B ''this'':26B ''to'':43B,69B ''treasury'':1A,4B,53B,90B ''twenty'':118B ''vital'':27B ''wag'':65B ''wher'':56B ''whil'':88B ''with'':111B ''work'':114B ''years'':119B', 'reach', 'The Treasury House is a location at the northern end of the first terrace in Markarth, overlooking the city and the surrounding Reach.  You do not know who works here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vlindrel_hall', 'Vlindrel Hall is a location at the southern edge of Markarth, nestled within the city''s towering stone structures. It sits on the second terrace, offering stunning views of the surrounding Reach and the bustling city below. The house is available for purchase.', '''and'':35B ''at'':8B ''avail'':43B ''below'':39B ''bustling'':37B ''city'':17B,38B ''edge'':11B ''for'':44B ''hall'':2A,4B ''hous'':41B ''is'':5B,42B ''it'':22B ''location'':7B ''markarth'':13B ''nestl'':14B ''of'':12B,31B ''offering'':28B ''on'':24B ''purch'':45B ''reach'':34B ''s'':18B ''second'':26B ''sits'':23B ''southern'':10B ''ston'':20B ''structur'':21B ''stunning'':29B ''surrounding'':33B ''terrac'':27B ''the'':9B,16B,25B,32B,36B,40B ''towering'':19B ''views'':30B ''vlindrel'':1A,3B ''within'':15B', 'reach', 'Vlindrel Hall is a location at the southern edge of Markarth, nestled within the city''s towering stone structures. The house is available for purchase you have heard.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('winterhold', 'Winterhold is a hold in northeast Skyrim, with its capital in the city of Winterhold, located on the Sea of Ghosts’ coast. The city is aligned with the Stormcloaks under Jarl Korir. Winterhold is the northernmost hold in Skyrim, with harsh weather and bleak landscapes, bordered by Eastmarch to the southeast, the Pale to the south and west, and the Sea of Ghosts to the north. The region is primarily composed of barren tundra, snowy mountains, and rocky coastlines.

Once a prosperous and vibrant city, Winterhold was devastated in the Great Collapse of 4E 122, in which most of the city was swallowed by the Sea of Ghosts. Today, only a few buildings remain standing near the College of Winterhold, which miraculously survived. The College, a fortress-like institution for mages, is perched on a rocky outcropping, sparking rumors among locals that its magical experiments caused the city''s destruction. Despite this, the College maintains that the event was a result of the earthquake in Vivec and the eruption of Red Mountain in Morrowind. The remaining residents can be found at The Frozen Hearth, where they often drown their sorrows. The sparse wildlife of Winterhold includes wolves, snow bears, and the occasional ice wraith, with little plant life beyond snowberry bushes and mountain flowers. The hold is traversed by a single main road leading to the city, with another path leading to the ancient ruins of Saarthal.', '''122'':96B ''4e'':95B ''align'':27B ''among'':142B ''ancient'':236B ''and'':44B,58B,60B,78B,84B,169B,202B,214B ''anoth'':231B ''at'':183B ''barr'':74B ''be'':181B ''bears'':201B ''beyond'':211B ''bleak'':45B ''border'':47B ''buildings'':114B ''bush'':213B ''by'':48B,105B,221B ''can'':180B ''capital'':11B ''caus'':148B ''city'':14B,25B,86B,102B,150B,229B ''coast'':23B ''coastlin'':80B ''collaps'':93B ''colleg'':119B,126B,156B ''comp'':72B ''despit'':153B ''destruction'':152B ''devastat'':89B ''drown'':190B ''earthquak'':166B ''eastmarch'':49B ''eruption'':171B ''event'':160B ''experiments'':147B ''few'':113B ''flowers'':216B ''for'':132B ''fortress'':129B ''fortress-lik'':128B ''found'':182B ''froz'':185B ''ghosts'':22B,64B,109B ''great'':92B ''harsh'':42B ''hearth'':186B ''hold'':5B,38B,218B ''ice'':205B ''in'':6B,12B,39B,90B,97B,167B,175B ''includ'':198B ''institution'':131B ''is'':3B,26B,35B,70B,134B,219B ''its'':10B,145B ''jarl'':32B ''kor'':33B ''landscap'':46B ''leading'':226B,233B ''lif'':210B ''lik'':130B ''littl'':208B ''locals'':143B ''locat'':17B ''mag'':133B ''magical'':146B ''main'':224B ''maintains'':157B ''miraculously'':123B ''morrowind'':176B ''most'':99B ''mountain'':174B,215B ''mountains'':77B ''near'':117B ''north'':67B ''northeast'':7B ''northernmost'':37B ''occasional'':204B ''of'':15B,21B,63B,73B,94B,100B,108B,120B,164B,172B,196B,238B ''often'':189B ''on'':18B,136B ''once'':81B ''only'':111B ''outcropping'':139B ''pal'':54B ''path'':232B ''perch'':135B ''plant'':209B ''primarily'':71B ''prosperous'':83B ''red'':173B ''region'':69B ''remain'':115B ''remaining'':178B ''residents'':179B ''result'':163B ''road'':225B ''rocky'':79B,138B ''ruins'':237B ''rumors'':141B ''s'':151B ''saarthal'':239B ''singl'':223B ''skyrim'':8B,40B ''snow'':200B ''snowberry'':212B ''snowy'':76B ''sorrows'':192B ''south'':57B ''southeast'':52B ''sparking'':140B ''spars'':194B ''standing'':116B ''stormcloaks'':30B ''surviv'':124B ''swallow'':104B ''that'':144B,158B ''the'':13B,19B,24B,29B,36B,51B,53B,56B,61B,66B,68B,91B,101B,106B,118B,125B,149B,155B,159B,165B,170B,177B,184B,191B,193B,203B,217B,228B,235B ''they'':188B ''this'':154B ''to'':50B,55B,65B,227B,234B ''today'':110B ''travers'':220B ''tundr'':75B ''under'':31B ''vibrant'':85B ''vivec'':168B ''was'':88B,103B,161B ''weath'':43B ''west'':59B ''wher'':187B ''which'':98B,122B ''wildlif'':195B ''winterhold'':1A,2B,16B,34B,87B,121B,197B ''with'':9B,28B,41B,207B,230B ''wolv'':199B ''wraith'':206B', 'winterhold, noble, scholar', 'Winterhold is a hold in northeast Skyrim, with its capital in the city of Winterhold, located on the Sea of Ghosts’ coast. The city is aligned with the Stormcloaks under Jarl Korir. Winterhold is the northernmost hold in Skyrim, with harsh weather and bleak landscapes, bordered by Eastmarch to the southeast, the Pale to the south and west, and the Sea of Ghosts to the north. The region is primarily composed of barren tundra, snowy mountains, and rocky coastlines.

Once a prosperous and vibrant city, Winterhold was devastated in the Great Collapse of 4E 122, in which most of the city was swallowed by the Sea of Ghosts. Today, only a few buildings remain standing near the College of Winterhold, which miraculously survived. The College, a fortress-like institution for mages, is perched on a rocky outcropping, sparking rumors among locals that its magical experiments caused the city''s destruction.  The hold is traversed by a single main road leading to the city, with another path leading to the ancient ruins of Saarthal.You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('college_of_winterhold', 'The College of Winterhold is a renowned school for magic located in the city of Winterhold, perched on a rocky outcrop, and reachable only by crossing a narrow stone bridge after the Great Collapse. Though it functions similarly to the Mages Guild, the College is an independent institution, separate from the Guild, and has a storied history dating back to the First Era. It is believed to have been founded by the legendary mage Shalidor, though this claim, like many others associated with him, is shrouded in mystery. The College boasts documents from as far back as the late Second Era and houses some of Tamriel''s most valuable arcane knowledge.

A selective institution, the College admits only those who prove their aptitude in the magical arts. Once enrolled, students enjoy greater freedom in their studies, including the practice of controversial magic such as Necromancy. The College''s central building, the Hall of the Elements, serves as the site for all types of magical practice and contains the famous Arcanaeum library. The Arch-Mage’s quarters are located within, while students and faculty are housed in separate accommodations. Beneath the College lies the Midden, a mysterious underground area that holds many of the College''s secrets. The Eye of Shalidor, a symbol of the institution, is displayed prominently across the campus, honoring the College''s ancient roots.

Notable residents of the College include the Arch-Mage Savos Aren, Master-Wizard Mirabelle Ervine, and various experts and trainers in different magical disciplines, including Faralda (Destruction), Tolfdir (Alteration), and Phinis Gestor (Conjuration). The College also hosts a range of followers, such as Brelyna Maryon and J''zargo, alongside other figures like Enthir, a general goods vendor, and the enigmatic Ancano, a Thalmor advisor.', '''accommodations'':192B ''across'':223B ''admits'':120B ''advisor'':297B ''after'':34B ''all'':164B ''alongsid'':282B ''also'':269B ''alteration'':262B ''an'':49B ''ancan'':294B ''ancient'':230B ''and'':25B,56B,105B,169B,186B,249B,252B,263B,279B,291B ''aptitud'':126B ''arcan'':113B ''arcanaeum'':173B ''arch'':177B,240B ''arch-mag'':176B,239B ''are'':181B,188B,202B ''aren'':243B ''arts'':130B ''as'':97B,100B,147B,160B,276B ''associat'':85B ''back'':62B,99B ''been'':72B ''believ'':69B ''beneath'':193B ''boasts'':94B ''brelyn'':277B ''bridg'':33B ''building'':153B ''by'':28B,74B ''campus'':225B ''central'':152B ''city'':17B ''claim'':81B ''collaps'':37B ''colleg'':1A,5B,47B,93B,119B,150B,195B,208B,228B,236B,268B ''conjuration'':266B ''contains'':170B ''controversial'':144B ''crossing'':29B ''dating'':61B ''destruction'':260B ''different'':255B ''disciplin'':257B ''display'':221B ''documents'':95B ''elements'':158B ''enigmatic'':293B ''enjoy'':134B ''enroll'':132B ''enthir'':286B ''ervin'':248B ''experts'':251B ''eye'':212B ''faculty'':187B ''famous'':172B ''far'':98B ''farald'':259B ''figur'':284B ''first'':65B ''followers'':274B ''for'':12B,163B ''found'':73B ''freedom'':136B ''from'':53B,96B ''functions'':40B ''general'':288B ''gestor'':265B ''goods'':289B ''great'':36B,135B ''guild'':45B,55B ''hall'':155B ''hav'':71B ''him'':87B ''history'':60B ''holds'':204B ''honoring'':226B ''hosts'':270B ''hous'':106B,189B ''in'':15B,90B,127B,137B,190B,254B ''includ'':237B ''including'':140B,258B ''independent'':50B ''institution'':51B,117B,2