INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sightless_pit', 'Sightless Pit is a medium-sized cave located south-southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and south-southeast of Saarthal. The cave is inhabited by Falmer, the blind and hostile subterranean elves, who make their homes in dark and forsaken places like this one.', '''and'':21B,35B,45B ''blind'':34B ''by'':31B ''cav'':10B,28B ''dark'':44B ''elves'':38B ''falm'':32B ''forsak'':46B ''hom'':42B ''hostil'':36B ''in'':17B,43B ''inhabit'':30B ''is'':5B,29B ''lik'':48B ''locat'':11B ''mak'':40B ''medium'':8B ''medium-siz'':7B ''of'':15B,25B ''one'':50B ''pit'':2A,4B ''plac'':47B ''region'':20B ''saarthal'':26B ''sightless'':1A,3B ''siz'':9B ''south'':13B,23B ''south-southeast'':22B ''south-southwest'':12B ''southeast'':24B ''southwest'':14B ''subterran'':37B ''the'':18B,27B,33B,41B ''this'':49B ''who'':39B ''winterhold'':16B,19B', 'winterhold', 'Sightless Pit is a medium-sized cave located south-southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ramshackle_trading_post', 'The Ramshackle Trading Post is an old, weathered shack located south of Kagrumez and west-northwest of Ashfallow Citadel on Solstheim. Despite its dilapidated appearance, the trading post serves as an unconventional merchant spot, operated by Falas Selvayn, a Dark Elf trader with an unusual schedule.

Falas can be found at the trading post only between the hours of midnight and 5 a.m., offering goods to adventurers who stumble upon this remote location during the night. ', '''5'':66B ''a.m'':67B ''adventurers'':71B ''an'':9B,35B,48B ''and'':17B,65B ''appearanc'':29B ''as'':34B ''ashfallow'':22B ''at'':55B ''be'':53B ''betw'':60B ''by'':40B ''can'':52B ''citadel'':23B ''dark'':44B ''despit'':26B ''dilapidat'':28B ''during'':78B ''elf'':45B ''fal'':41B,51B ''found'':54B ''goods'':69B ''hours'':62B ''is'':8B ''its'':27B ''kagrumez'':16B ''locat'':13B ''location'':77B ''merchant'':37B ''midnight'':64B ''night'':80B ''northwest'':20B ''of'':15B,21B,63B ''offering'':68B ''old'':10B ''on'':24B ''only'':59B ''operat'':39B ''post'':3A,7B,32B,58B ''ramshackl'':1A,5B ''remot'':76B ''schedul'':50B ''selvayn'':42B ''serv'':33B ''shack'':12B ''solstheim'':25B ''south'':14B ''spot'':38B ''stumbl'':73B ''the'':4B,30B,56B,61B,79B ''this'':75B ''to'':70B ''trad'':46B ''trading'':2A,6B,31B,57B ''unconventional'':36B ''unusual'':49B ''upon'':74B ''weather'':11B ''west'':19B ''west-northwest'':18B ''who'':72B ''with'':47B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('saarthal', 'Saarthal is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southwest of Winterhold. As the first Nord settlement in Skyrim, Saarthal holds significant historical and archaeological value, particularly to the College of Winterhold, who is actively excavating the site in search of ancient artifacts. The ruins are believed to have a deeper significance, potentially tied to a powerful past.

The original settlement of Saarthal was destroyed during the Merethic Era in an event known as the Night of Tears, where elves launched a brutal attack on the city. The incident, as detailed in the book Night of Tears, suggests that the elven assault was driven by a desire to control a powerful item hidden beneath the city. ', '''actively'':36B ''an'':72B ''ancient'':43B ''and'':25B ''archaeological'':26B ''are'':47B ''artifacts'':44B ''as'':14B,75B,91B ''assault'':103B ''attack'':85B ''believ'':48B ''beneath'':115B ''book'':95B ''brutal'':84B ''by'':106B ''city'':88B,117B ''colleg'':31B ''control'':110B ''deep'':52B ''desir'':108B ''destroy'':66B ''detail'':92B ''driv'':105B ''during'':67B ''elven'':102B ''elves'':81B ''event'':73B ''excavating'':37B ''first'':16B ''hav'':50B ''hidd'':114B ''historical'':24B ''holds'':22B ''in'':19B,40B,71B,93B ''incident'':90B ''is'':3B,35B ''item'':113B ''known'':74B ''launch'':82B ''locat'':10B ''medium'':6B ''medium-siz'':5B ''merethic'':69B ''night'':77B,96B ''nord'':17B ''nordic'':8B ''of'':12B,32B,42B,63B,78B,97B ''on'':86B ''original'':61B ''particularly'':28B ''past'':59B ''potentially'':54B ''powerful'':58B,112B ''ruin'':9B ''ruins'':46B ''saarthal'':1A,2B,21B,64B ''search'':41B ''settlement'':18B,62B ''significanc'':53B ''significant'':23B ''sit'':39B ''siz'':7B ''skyrim'':20B ''southwest'':11B ''suggests'':99B ''tears'':79B,98B ''that'':100B ''the'':15B,30B,38B,45B,60B,68B,76B,87B,89B,94B,101B,116B ''tied'':55B ''to'':29B,49B,56B,109B ''valu'':27B ''was'':65B,104B ''wher'':80B ''who'':34B ''winterhold'':13B,33B', 'collegeofwinterhold, scholar', 'Saarthal is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southwest of Winterhold, As the first Nord settlement in Skyrim, Saarthal holds significant historical and archaeological value, particularly to the College of Winterhold, who is actively excavating the site in search of ancient artifacts. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch, winterhold', '',