INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('snow_veil_sanctum', 'Snow Veil Sanctum is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located north-northeast of Windhelm, in the Winterhold region, and south of Bleakcoast Cave. The ruin is home to draugr, the ancient undead guardians that protect Nordic tombs, making it a dangerous and foreboding site for any who dare enter.', '''ancient'':36B ''and'':24B,47B ''any'':51B ''bleakcoast'':27B ''cav'':28B ''dangerous'':46B ''dar'':53B ''draugr'':34B ''enter'':54B ''for'':50B ''foreboding'':48B ''guardians'':38B ''hom'':32B ''in'':20B ''is'':7B,31B ''it'':44B ''locat'':14B ''making'':43B ''medium'':10B ''medium-siz'':9B ''nordic'':12B,41B ''north'':16B ''north-northeast'':15B ''northeast'':17B ''of'':18B,26B ''protect'':40B ''region'':23B ''ruin'':13B,30B ''sanctum'':3A,6B ''sit'':49B ''siz'':11B ''snow'':1A,4B ''south'':25B ''that'':39B ''the'':21B,29B,35B ''to'':33B ''tombs'':42B ''unde'':37B ''veil'':2A,5B ''who'':52B ''windhelm'':19B ''winterhold'':22B', 'winterhold', 'Snow Veil Sanctum is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located north-northeast of Windhelm, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ysgramor''s_tomb', 'Ysgramor''s Tomb is a small Nordic ruin located northwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and east of Pilgrim''s Trench. The tomb is the final resting place of Ysgramor, a legendary figure known as Ysgramor the Invader, or "the harbinger of us all." Ysgramor was an Atmoran who fled civil war in Atmora and arrived in Tamriel long before recorded history. He is often regarded as the first human ruler and king of Skyrim, playing a foundational role in the region''s history.

The tomb is a place of great significance, tied to the origins of Skyrim and the early history of the Nords. As a revered figure, Ysgramor''s legacy lives on, and his tomb is a site of both reverence and mystery.', '''all'':48B ''an'':51B ''and'':20B,59B,76B,103B,119B,128B ''arriv'':60B ''as'':39B,71B,110B ''atmor'':52B,58B ''befor'':64B ''both'':126B ''civil'':55B ''early'':105B ''east'':21B ''figur'':37B,113B ''final'':30B ''first'':73B ''fled'':54B ''foundational'':82B ''great'':95B ''harbing'':45B ''his'':120B ''history'':66B,88B,106B ''hum'':74B ''in'':16B,57B,61B,84B ''invad'':42B ''is'':7B,28B,68B,91B,122B ''king'':77B ''known'':38B ''legacy'':116B ''legendary'':36B ''liv'':117B ''locat'':12B ''long'':63B ''mystery'':129B ''nordic'':10B ''nords'':109B ''northwest'':13B ''of'':14B,22B,33B,46B,78B,94B,101B,107B,125B ''often'':69B ''on'':118B ''or'':43B ''origins'':100B ''pilgrim'':23B ''plac'':32B,93B ''playing'':80B ''record'':65B ''regard'':70B ''region'':19B,86B ''resting'':31B ''rever'':112B ''reverenc'':127B ''rol'':83B ''ruin'':11B ''rul'':75B ''s'':2A,5B,24B,87B,115B ''significanc'':96B ''sit'':124B ''skyrim'':79B,102B ''small'':9B ''tamriel'':62B ''the'':17B,26B,29B,41B,44B,72B,85B,89B,99B,104B,108B ''tied'':97B ''to'':98B ''tomb'':3A,6B,27B,90B,121B ''trench'':25B ''us'':47B ''war'':56B ''was'':50B ''who'':53B ''winterhold'':15B,18B ''ysgramor'':1A,4B,34B,40B,49B,114B', 'companions', 'Ysgramor''s Tomb is a small Nordic ruin located northwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region. The tomb is the final resting place of Ysgramor, a legendary figure known as Ysgramor the Invader, or "the harbinger of us all." Ysgramor was an Atmoran who fled civil war in Atmora and arrived in Tamriel long before recorded history. He is often regarded as the first human ruler and king of Skyrim, playing a foundational role in the region''s history.
You do not know anything else about this area.', 'pale', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('journeyman''s_nook', 'Journeyman''s Nook is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located southeast of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and northwest of Snow Veil Sanctum. Despite its modest size, the ruin is home to a bandit who has taken shelter within its crumbling walls, using it as a hideout.

The site is relatively isolated, set against the harsh northern landscape, making it a perfect place for the bandit to remain hidden from the law.', '''against'':57B ''and'':21B ''as'':48B ''bandit'':37B,69B ''crumbling'':44B ''despit'':27B ''for'':67B ''from'':73B ''harsh'':59B ''hidd'':72B ''hideout'':50B ''hom'':34B ''in'':17B ''is'':7B,33B,53B ''isolat'':55B ''it'':47B,63B ''its'':28B,43B ''journeym'':1A,4B ''landscap'':61B ''law'':75B ''locat'':13B ''making'':62B ''modest'':29B ''nook'':3A,6B ''nordic'':11B ''northern'':60B ''northwest'':22B ''of'':15B,23B ''outdoor'':10B ''perfect'':65B ''plac'':66B ''region'':20B ''relatively'':54B ''remain'':71B ''ruin'':12B,32B ''s'':2A,5B ''sanctum'':26B ''set'':56B ''shelt'':41B ''sit'':52B ''siz'':30B ''small'':9B ''snow'':24B ''southeast'':14B ''tak'':40B ''the'':18B,31B,51B,58B,68B,74B ''to'':35B,70B ''using'':46B ''veil'':25B ''walls'':45B ''who'':38B ''winterhold'':16B,19B ''within'':42B', 'winterhold', 'Journeyman''s Nook is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located southeast of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skytemple_ruins', 'Skytemple Ruins is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located north of the College of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and east of Ysgramor''s Tomb. The ruins are perched atop a large glacial mound on an island off the northern coast of Skyrim, offering a dramatic and isolated setting.

The sparse remains of the temple are home to draugr and skeletons, the undead guardians of the site, making it a dangerous location for those who venture into its depths.', '''an'':38B ''and'':22B,49B,62B ''are'':30B,58B ''atop'':32B ''coast'':43B ''colleg'':15B ''dangerous'':73B ''depths'':81B ''dramatic'':48B ''draugr'':61B ''east'':23B ''for'':75B ''glacial'':35B ''guardians'':66B ''hom'':59B ''in'':18B ''into'':79B ''is'':5B ''island'':39B ''isolat'':50B ''it'':71B ''its'':80B ''larg'':34B ''locat'':11B ''location'':74B ''making'':70B ''mound'':36B ''nordic'':9B ''north'':12B ''northern'':42B ''of'':13B,16B,24B,44B,55B,67B ''off'':40B ''offering'':46B ''on'':37B ''outdoor'':8B ''perch'':31B ''region'':21B ''remains'':54B ''ruin'':10B ''ruins'':2A,4B,29B ''s'':26B ''setting'':51B ''sit'':69B ''skeletons'':63B ''skyrim'':45B ''skytempl'':1A,3B ''small'':7B ''spars'':53B ''templ'':57B ''the'':14B,19B,28B,41B,52B,56B,64B,68B ''thos'':76B ''to'':60B ''tomb'':27B ''unde'':65B ''ventur'':78B ''who'':77B ''winterhold'':17B,20B ''ysgramor'':25B', 'winterhold', 'Skytemple Ruins is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located north of the College of Winterhold.You do not know anything else about this area.
', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shrine_of_azura', 'The Shrine of Azura is a massive sacred site dedicated to Azura, the Daedric Prince of Dawn and Dusk. It is located south of Winterhold, perched atop the summit of a tall mountain. The path leading to the shrine is found not far south of Whistling Mine, where it rises sharply to the west. To reach the shrine, travelers must head southeast along the path from Winterhold, heading in the direction of Windhelm. On clear days one can enjoy sweeping views from the summit, with expansive vistas stretching in all directions.

The shrine itself is situated atop a stone fort-like structure, believed to have been built by the Dunmer, who revere Azura. A massive statue of Azura dominates the site, with an altar positioned in front of it. Aranea Ienith, a devout worshiper of Azura, spends her time at the altar, offering prayers when she is not following you. To the right of the altar, a small camp lies below on a lower level.', '''all'':93B ''along'':66B ''altar'':128B,146B,160B ''an'':127B ''and'':21B ''arane'':134B ''at'':144B ''atop'':30B,100B ''azur'':3A,7B,15B,117B,122B,140B ''been'':110B ''believ'':107B ''below'':165B ''built'':111B ''by'':112B ''camp'':163B ''can'':81B ''cle'':78B ''daedric'':17B ''dawn'':20B ''days'':79B ''dedicat'':13B ''devout'':137B ''direction'':74B ''directions'':94B ''dominat'':123B ''dunm'':114B ''dusk'':22B ''enjoy'':82B ''expansiv'':89B ''far'':46B ''following'':153B ''fort'':104B ''fort-lik'':103B ''found'':44B ''from'':69B,85B ''front'':131B ''hav'':109B ''head'':64B ''heading'':71B ''her'':142B ''ienith'':135B ''in'':72B,92B,130B ''is'':8B,24B,43B,98B,151B ''it'':23B,52B,133B ''itself'':97B ''leading'':39B ''level'':169B ''lies'':164B ''lik'':105B ''locat'':25B ''low'':168B ''massiv'':10B,119B ''min'':50B ''mountain'':36B ''must'':63B ''not'':45B,152B ''of'':2A,6B,19B,27B,33B,48B,75B,121B,132B,139B,158B ''offering'':147B ''on'':77B,166B ''one'':80B ''path'':38B,68B ''perch'':29B ''position'':129B ''prayers'':148B ''princ'':18B ''reach'':59B ''rever'':116B ''right'':157B ''ris'':53B ''sacr'':11B ''sharply'':54B ''she'':150B ''shrin'':1A,5B,42B,61B,96B ''sit'':12B,125B ''situat'':99B ''small'':162B ''south'':26B,47B ''southeast'':65B ''spends'':141B ''statu'':120B ''ston'':102B ''stretching'':91B ''structur'':106B ''summit'':32B,87B ''sweeping'':83B ''tall'':35B ''the'':4B,16B,31B,37B,41B,56B,60B,67B,73B,86B,95B,113B,124B,145B,156B,159B ''tim'':143B ''to'':14B,40B,55B,58B,108B,155B ''travelers'':62B ''views'':84B ''vist'':90B ''west'':57B ''when'':149B ''wher'':51B ''whistling'':49B ''who'':115B ''windhelm'':76B ''winterhold'':28B,70B ''with'':88B,126B ''worship'':138B ''you'':154B', 'winterhold, daedra, daedric', 'The Shrine of Azura is a massive sacred site dedicated to Azura, the Daedric Prince of Dawn and Dusk. It is located south of Winterhold, perched atop the summit of a tall mountain.

A massive statue of Azura dominates the site that can be seen from almost anywhere in Skyrim.You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bleakcoast_cave', 'Bleakcoast Cave is a small cave located southeast of Winterhold, directly east of the Shrine of Azura, in the Winterhold region. The cave is home to a number of frost trolls, making it a dangerous location for adventurers who may venture inside.', '''adventurers'':40B ''azur'':19B ''bleakcoast'':1A,3B ''cav'':2A,4B,8B,25B ''dangerous'':37B ''directly'':13B ''east'':14B ''for'':39B ''frost'':32B ''hom'':27B ''in'':20B ''insid'':44B ''is'':5B,26B ''it'':35B ''locat'':9B ''location'':38B ''making'':34B ''may'':42B ''numb'':30B ''of'':11B,15B,18B,31B ''region'':23B ''shrin'':17B ''small'':7B ''southeast'':10B ''the'':16B,21B,24B ''to'':28B ''trolls'':33B ''ventur'':43B ''who'':41B ''winterhold'':12B,22B', 'winterhold', '
