INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('kraldar''s_house', 'Kraldar''s House is located in Winterhold, situated as the last building on the left before the bridge leading to the College of Winterhold. The house serves as the residence of Kraldar, a local figure, and his manservant, Thonjolf.', '''and'':39B ''as'':12B,31B ''befor'':19B ''bridg'':21B ''building'':15B ''colleg'':25B ''figur'':38B ''his'':40B ''hous'':3A,6B,29B ''in'':9B ''is'':7B ''krald'':1A,4B,35B ''last'':14B ''leading'':22B ''left'':18B ''local'':37B ''locat'':8B ''manservant'':41B ''of'':26B,34B ''on'':16B ''residenc'':33B ''s'':2A,5B ''serv'':30B ''situat'':11B ''the'':13B,17B,20B,24B,28B,32B ''thonjolf'':42B ''to'':23B ''winterhold'':10B,27B', 'winterhold', 'Kraldar''s House is located in Winterhold. You dot know who Kraldar is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_frozen_hearth', 'The Frozen Hearth is a cozy inn located in the heart of Winterhold, one of the few inhabited buildings left in the city. Situated directly across the street from the Jarl''s Longhouse, it serves as a central gathering point for the remaining residents of Winterhold, offering a warm respite from the harsh northern climate.

The inn is run by Dagur, a Nord innkeeper, alongside his wife Haran, who operates a food stall in the town. Together, they manage The Frozen Hearth, providing food, drink, and shelter to the people of Winterhold. Their daughter, Eirid, also resides in the inn, with her parents working together to maintain the establishment and serve the few souls left in the dwindling city.', '''across'':29B ''alongsid'':68B ''also'':99B ''and'':89B,113B ''as'':39B ''buildings'':22B ''by'':63B ''central'':41B ''city'':26B,122B ''climat'':58B ''cozy'':9B ''dagur'':64B ''daught'':97B ''directly'':28B ''drink'':88B ''dwindling'':121B ''eir'':98B ''establishment'':112B ''few'':20B,116B ''food'':75B,87B ''for'':44B ''from'':32B,54B ''froz'':2A,5B,84B ''gathering'':42B ''har'':71B ''harsh'':56B ''heart'':14B ''hearth'':3A,6B,85B ''her'':105B ''his'':69B ''in'':12B,24B,77B,101B,119B ''inhabit'':21B ''inn'':10B,60B,103B ''innkeep'':67B ''is'':7B,61B ''it'':37B ''jarl'':34B ''left'':23B,118B ''locat'':11B ''longhous'':36B ''maintain'':110B ''manag'':82B ''nord'':66B ''northern'':57B ''of'':15B,18B,48B,94B ''offering'':50B ''one'':17B ''operat'':73B ''parents'':106B ''peopl'':93B ''point'':43B ''providing'':86B ''remaining'':46B ''resid'':100B ''residents'':47B ''respit'':53B ''run'':62B ''s'':35B ''serv'':38B,114B ''shelt'':90B ''situat'':27B ''souls'':117B ''stall'':76B ''street'':31B ''the'':1A,4B,13B,19B,25B,30B,33B,45B,55B,59B,78B,83B,92B,96B,102B,111B,115B,120B ''they'':81B ''to'':91B,109B ''togeth'':80B,108B ''town'':79B ''warm'':52B ''who'':72B ''wif'':70B ''winterhold'':16B,49B,95B ''with'':104B ''working'':107B', 'winterhold, innkeeper, traveler', 'The Frozen Hearth is a cozy inn located in the heart of Winterhold, one of the few inhabited buildings left in the city. You do not know who runs the Inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('solstheim', 'Solstheim is a large island located in the Sea of Ghosts, to the north of Tamriel, with a history that stretches back to the ancient Snow Elves, the first inhabitants of the region. They built grand settlements on Solstheim that outlasted their mainland holdings, leaving a lasting mark on the island. Though the island has been home to various races over the centuries, it has traditionally been dominated by Nordic influence. In 4E 16, Solstheim officially became part of Morrowind.

The island’s history took a tragic turn during the Red Year of 4E 5, when the eruption of Red Mountain devastated the southern half of Solstheim. Fort Frostmoth was destroyed, leaving the Imperial garrison in disarray and killing General Carius. Raven Rock, a settlement on the island, quickly took over the remnants of the garrison and was fortified by elite members of the Redoran Guard. In the aftermath of the eruption, the ash from Red Mountain transformed the southern part of the island into vast ashlands. To protect Raven Rock from the encroaching ash, Brara Morvayn designed and oversaw the construction of a great stone wall known as the Bulwark, funded by the East Empire Company.

In 4E 16, as part of a political compromise, Skyrim ceded control of Solstheim to Morrowind. While this act appeared to be a compassionate gesture toward the Dunmer, it was driven by political motives. Skyrim sought to avoid a conflict with Morrowind, which had long claimed the island, and by relinquishing control, it preserved its image as a savior to the Dunmer. As a result, many Dunmer refugees, including members of the minor House Sathil, began flocking to the island. The East Empire Company was forced to hand over control of Raven Rock to House Redoran, and by 4E 48, Solstheim was no longer considered part of the Empire.', '''16'':75B,201B ''48'':298B ''4e'':74B,95B,200B,297B ''5'':96B ''act'':217B ''aftermath'':150B ''ancient'':26B ''and'':119B,138B,180B,247B,295B ''appear'':218B ''as'':190B,202B,255B,261B ''ash'':155B,176B ''ashlands'':168B ''avo'':236B ''back'':23B ''be'':220B ''becam'':78B ''been'':57B,68B ''beg'':274B ''brar'':177B ''built'':36B ''bulwark'':192B ''by'':70B,141B,194B,230B,248B,296B ''carius'':122B ''ced'':209B ''centuri'':64B ''claim'':244B ''company'':198B,282B ''compassionat'':222B ''compromis'':207B ''conflict'':238B ''consider'':303B ''construction'':183B ''control'':210B,250B,288B ''design'':179B ''destroy'':112B ''devastat'':103B ''disarray'':118B ''dominat'':69B ''driv'':229B ''dunm'':226B,260B,265B ''during'':90B ''east'':196B,280B ''elit'':142B ''elves'':28B ''empir'':197B,281B,307B ''encroaching'':175B ''eruption'':99B,153B ''first'':30B ''flocking'':275B ''forc'':284B ''fort'':109B ''fortifi'':140B ''from'':156B,173B ''frostmoth'':110B ''fund'':193B ''garrison'':116B,137B ''general'':121B ''gestur'':223B ''ghosts'':12B ''grand'':37B ''great'':186B ''guard'':147B ''had'':242B ''half'':106B ''hand'':286B ''history'':20B,85B ''holdings'':45B ''hom'':58B ''hous'':272B,293B ''imag'':254B ''imperial'':115B ''in'':8B,73B,117B,148B,199B ''including'':267B ''influenc'':72B ''inhabitants'':31B ''into'':166B ''is'':3B ''island'':6B,52B,55B,