over the centuries, it has traditionally been dominated by Nordic influence. In 4E 16, Solstheim officially became part of Morrowind. The island’s history took a tragic turn during the Red Year of 4E 5, when the eruption of Red Mountain devastated the southern half of Solstheim. You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('raven_rock', 'Raven Rock is a city located on the southwest coast of Solstheim, serving as the first settlement encountered in the Dragonborn expansion. Once a thriving East Empire Company mining outpost, it has since become a House Redoran colony. The depletion of its ebony mine has left Raven Rock a shadow of its former prosperity, now a largely forgotten settlement struggling to endure amidst the ash-laden environment caused by the nearby Red Mountain.

The city features a single thoroughfare running from the entrance through the Bulwark in the east to the Earth Stone in the west, following the curve of a small adjacent bay. The Bulwark, a sturdy defensive wall, houses both the city’s jail and the Redoran guards'' garrison, providing protection against the encroaching ash. A curved wooden boardwalk lines the bay, complete with a short pier and a longer pier to the east, where the Northern Maiden is docked, offering transport between Solstheim and Windhelm in Skyrim.

Raven Rock''s central marketplace, located near the city''s well north of the bay, is home to its shops and services. The Temple of Raven Rock is situated near the Bulwark to the east, providing spiritual guidance to the community. Scattered throughout the city are various crafting stations, including smelters, tanning racks, a forge, an alchemy lab, and more, located near key sites such as Alor House, Glover Mallory''s House, Ienth Farm, and Raven Rock Mine. ', '''adjacent'':106B ''against'':127B ''alchemy'':220B ''alor'':230B ''amidst'':65B ''an'':219B ''and'':120B,143B,160B,184B,222B,238B ''are'':209B ''as'':16B,229B ''ash'':68B,130B ''ash-lad'':67B ''bay'':107B,137B,178B ''becom'':36B ''betw'':158B ''boardwalk'':134B ''both'':115B ''bulwark'':89B,109B,195B ''by'':72B ''caus'':71B ''central'':167B ''city'':7B,78B,117B,172B,208B ''coast'':12B ''colony'':40B ''community'':204B ''company'':30B ''complet'':138B ''crafting'':211B ''curv'':102B,132B ''defensiv'':112B ''depletion'':42B ''dock'':155B ''dragonborn'':23B ''earth'':95B ''east'':28B,92B,149B,198B ''ebony'':45B ''empir'':29B ''encounter'':20B ''encroaching'':129B ''endur'':64B ''entranc'':86B ''environment'':70B ''expansion'':24B ''farm'':237B ''featur'':79B ''first'':18B ''following'':100B ''forg'':218B ''forgott'':60B ''form'':55B ''from'':84B ''garrison'':124B ''glov'':232B ''guards'':123B ''guidanc'':201B ''hom'':180B ''hous'':38B,114B,231B,235B ''ienth'':236B ''in'':21B,90B,97B,162B ''including'':213B ''is'':5B,154B,179B,191B ''it'':33B ''its'':44B,54B,182B ''jail'':119B ''key'':226B ''lab'':221B ''lad'':69B ''largely'':59B ''left'':48B ''lin'':135B ''locat'':8B,169B,224B ''long'':145B ''maid'':153B ''mallory'':233B ''marketplac'':168B ''min'':46B,241B ''mining'':31B ''mor'':223B ''mountain'':76B ''near'':170B,193B,225B ''nearby'':74B ''north'':175B ''northern'':152B ''now'':57B ''of'':13B,43B,53B,103B,176B,188B ''offering'':156B ''on'':9B ''once'':25B ''outpost'':32B ''pier'':142B,146B ''prosperity'':56B ''protection'':126B ''providing'':125B,199B ''racks'':216B ''rav'':1A,3B,49B,164B,189B,239B ''red'':75B ''redor'':39B,122B ''rock'':2A,4B,50B,165B,190B,240B ''running'':83B ''s'':118B,166B,173B,234B ''scatter'':205B ''servic'':185B ''serving'':15B ''settlement'':19B,61B ''shadow'':52B ''shops'':183B ''short'':141B ''sinc'':35B ''singl'':81B ''sit'':227B ''situat'':192B ''skyrim'':163B ''small'':105B ''smelters'':214B ''solstheim'':14B,159B ''southwest'':11B ''spiritual'':200B ''stations'':212B ''ston'':96B ''struggling'':62B ''sturdy'':111B ''such'':228B ''tanning'':215B ''templ'':187B ''the'':10B,17B,22B,41B,66B,73B,77B,85B,88B,91B,94B,98B,101B,108B,116B,121B,128B,136B,148B,151B,171B,177B,186B,194B,197B,203B,207B ''thoroughfar'':82B ''thriving'':27B ''through'':87B ''throughout'':206B ''to'':63B,93B,147B,181B,196B,202B ''transport'':157B ''various'':210B ''wall'':113B ''well'':174B ''west'':99B ''wher'':150B ''windhelm'':161B ''with'':139B ''wood'':133B', 'solstheim, noble, scholar', 'Raven Rock is a city located on the southwest coast of Solstheim, serving as the first settlement encountered in the Dragonborn expansion. Once a thriving East Empire Company mining outpost, it has since become a House Redoran colony. You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skaal_village', 'Skaal Village is a small, secluded settlement located in the northeastern region of Solstheim, along the Felsaad Coast, just north of Lake Fjalding and east of the Isild River. It is home to the Skaal, a unique offshoot tribe of Nords who live in harmony with nature as part of their worship of the All-Maker. The Skaal lead a simple, self-sufficient life in the frozen north, relying on hunting, minor agriculture, and their knowledge of crafting stalhrim, a rare and ancient material.

The village consists of eight buildings arranged in a circle around a central well, reflecting the communal nature of Skaal society. The Skaal believe Solstheim was originally part of Skyrim, transformed into an island during a climactic battle between Dragon Cult loyalists and rebels. The Skaal trace their lineage back to the loyalist faction and have preserved their history through oral tradition. This narrative is supported by archaeological evidence, including multiple Dragon Cult ruins and carvings uncovered in the Fourth Era. ', '''agricultur'':77B ''all'':58B ''all-mak'':57B ''along'':17B ''an'':121B ''ancient'':87B ''and'':26B,78B,86B,131B,143B,163B ''archaeological'':156B ''around'':99B ''arrang'':95B ''as'':50B ''back'':138B ''battl'':126B ''believ'':112B ''betw'':127B ''buildings'':94B ''by'':155B ''carvings'':164B ''central'':101B ''circl'':98B ''climactic'':125B ''coast'':20B ''communal'':105B ''consists'':91B ''crafting'':82B ''cult'':129B,161B ''dragon'':128B,160B ''during'':123B ''east'':27B ''eight'':93B ''evidenc'':157B ''faction'':142B ''fels'':19B ''fjalding'':25B ''fourth'':168B ''froz'':71B ''harmony'':47B ''hav'':144B ''history'':147B ''hom'':34B ''hunting'':75B ''in'':11B,46B,69B,96B,166B ''including'':158B ''into'':120B ''is'':5B,33B,153B ''isild'':30B ''island'':122B ''it'':32B ''just'':21B ''knowledg'':80B ''lak'':24B ''lead'':62B ''lif'':68B ''lineag'':137B ''liv'':45B ''locat'':10B ''loyalist'':141B ''loyalists'':130B ''mak'':59B ''material'':88B ''minor'':76B ''multipl'':159B ''narrativ'':152B ''natur'':49B,106B ''nords'':43B ''north'':22B,72B ''northeastern'':13B ''of'':15B,23B,28B,42B,52B,55B,81B,92B,107B,117B ''offshoot'':40B ''on'':74B ''oral'':149B ''originally'':115B ''part'':51B,116B ''preserv'':145B ''rar'':85B ''rebels'':132B ''reflecting'':103B ''region'':14B ''relying'':73B ''riv'':31B ''ruins'':162B ''seclud'':8B ''self'':66B ''self-sufficient'':65B ''settlement'':9B ''simpl'':64B ''skaal'':1A,3B,37B,61B,108B,111B,134B ''skyrim'':118B ''small'':7B ''society'':109B ''solstheim'':16B,113B ''stalhrim'':83B ''sufficient'':67B ''support'':154B ''the'':12B,18B,29B,36B,53B,56B,60B,70B,79B,89B,104B,110B,133B,136B,140B,146B,167B ''this'':151B ''through'':148B ''to'':35B,139B ''trac'':135B ''tradition'':150B ''transform'':119B ''trib'':41B ''uncover'':165B ''uniqu'':39B ''villag'':2A,4B,90B ''was'':114B ''well'':102B ''who'':44B ''with'':48B ''worship'':54B', 'skaal. scholar, miraakcult', 'Skaal Village is a small, secluded settlement located in the northeastern region of Solstheim. It is home to the Skaal, Nordic people who worship animal gods.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'solstheim', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tel_mithryn', 'Tel Mithryn is a Telvanni tower settlement located east of Fort Frostmoth on the island of Solstheim. This unique settlement is home to Master Wizard Neloth of House Telvanni, a prominent and eccentric figure with a reputation for both brilliance and controversy. Tel Mithryn consists of four large mushroom structures grown from special fungal spores brought from Morrowind at the beginning of the Fourth Era. These structures include the main tower, the apothecary, the kitchen, and the steward''s house.

Access to each building is provided by long, organic ramps that lead to round wooden doors, blending seamlessly with the settlement’s distinctive fungal architecture. Surrounding the structures, various flora, such as bleeding crown, fly amanita fungi, and scathecraw, thrive near the ramps, adding to the natural ambiance of the area. Behind the kitchen lies a heart stone deposit with a conveniently placed pickaxe, and additional deposits can be found on the cliffs near the southeastern coast.', '''access'':83B ''adding'':126B ''additional'':148B ''amanit'':118B ''ambianc'':130B ''and'':34B,43B,78B,120B,147B ''apothecary'':75B ''architectur'':107B ''are'':133B ''as'':114B ''at'':61B ''be'':151B ''beginning'':63B ''behind'':134B ''bleeding'':115B ''blending'':99B ''both'':41B ''brillianc'':42B ''brought'':58B ''building'':86B ''by'':89B ''can'':150B ''cliffs'':155B ''coast'':159B ''consists'':47B ''controversy'':44B ''conveniently'':144B ''crown'':116B ''deposit'':141B ''deposits'':149B ''distinctiv'':105B ''doors'':98B ''each'':85B ''east'':11B ''eccentric'':35B ''figur'':36B ''flor'':112B ''fly'':117B ''for'':40B ''fort'':13B ''found'':152B ''four'':49B ''fourth'':66B ''from'':54B,59B ''frostmoth'':14B ''fungal'':56B,106B ''fungi'':119B ''grown'':53B ''heart'':139B ''hom'':24B ''hous'':30B,82B ''includ'':70B ''is'':5B,23B,87B ''island'':17B ''kitch'':77B,136B ''larg'':50B ''lead'':94B ''lies'':137B ''locat'':10B ''long'':90B ''main'':72B ''mast'':26B ''mithryn'':2A,4B,46B ''morrowind'':60B ''mushroom'':51B ''natural'':129B ''near'':123B,156B ''neloth'':28B ''of'':12B,18B,29B,48B,64B,131B ''on'':15B,153B ''organic'':91B ''pickax'':146B ''plac'':145B ''prominent'':33B ''provid'':88B ''ramps'':92B,125B ''reputation'':39B ''round'':96B ''s'':81B,104B ''scathecraw'':121B ''seamlessly'':100B ''settlement'':9B,22B,103B ''solstheim'':19B ''southeastern'':158B ''special'':55B ''spor'':57B ''steward'':80B ''ston'':140B ''structur'':52B,69B,110B ''such'':113B ''surrounding'':1