INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_retching_netch', 'The Retching Netch is the only inn in Raven Rock, located in the marketplace between Alor House to the northwest and Glover Mallory''s House to the southwest. As the sole inn on Solstheim, it serves as a gathering place for locals and travelers alike, offering food, drinks, and respite from the island’s harsh environment. The cornerclub is a lively hub, known for its warmth and hospitality, but also its colorful history.

Owned and operated by Geldis Sadri, a charismatic proprietor, the inn''s name has a rather unusual origin. Several years ago, Geldis witnessed a memorable scene when a drunken patron, stumbling around the docks with a bottle of sujamma while naked and singing loudly, tossed the bottle at a floating netch. The bottle shattered upon impact, causing the netch to tilt and eventually vomit. ', '''ago'':97B ''alik'':48B ''alor'':19B ''also'':73B ''and'':24B,46B,52B,70B,78B,118B,138B ''around'':108B ''as'':32B,40B ''at'':124B ''betw'':18B ''bottl'':113B,123B,129B ''but'':72B ''by'':80B ''causing'':133B ''charismatic'':84B ''colorful'':75B ''cornerclub'':61B ''docks'':110B ''drinks'':51B ''drunk'':105B ''environment'':59B ''eventually'':139B ''floating'':126B ''food'':50B ''for'':44B,67B ''from'':54B ''gathering'':42B ''geldis'':81B,98B ''glov'':25B ''harsh'':58B ''history'':76B ''hospitality'':71B ''hous'':20B,28B ''hub'':65B ''impact'':132B ''in'':11B,15B ''inn'':10B,35B,87B ''is'':7B,62B ''island'':56B ''it'':38B ''its'':68B,74B ''known'':66B ''lively'':64B ''locals'':45B ''locat'':14B ''loudly'':120B ''mallory'':26B ''marketplac'':17B ''memor'':101B ''nak'':117B ''nam'':89B ''netch'':3A,6B,127B,135B ''northwest'':23B ''of'':114B ''offering'':49B ''on'':36B ''only'':9B ''operat'':79B ''origin'':94B ''owned'':77B ''patron'':106B ''plac'':43B ''proprietor'':85B ''rath'':92B ''rav'':12B ''respit'':53B ''retching'':2A,5B ''rock'':13B ''s'':27B,57B,88B ''sadri'':82B ''scen'':102B ''serv'':39B ''several'':95B ''shatter'':130B ''singing'':119B ''sol'':34B ''solstheim'':37B ''southwest'':31B ''stumbling'':107B ''sujamm'':115B ''the'':1A,4B,8B,16B,22B,30B,33B,55B,60B,86B,109B,122B,128B,134B ''tilt'':137B ''to'':21B,29B,136B ''toss'':121B ''travelers'':47B ''unusual'':93B ''upon'':131B ''vomit'':140B ''warmth'':69B ''when'':103B ''whil'':116B ''with'':111B ''witness'':99B ''years'':96B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('severin_manor', 'Severin Manor is a distinguished home in Raven Rock, originally inhabited by Mirri Severin, Tilisu Severin, and Vendil Severin, all of whom are Dark Elves. The manor stands as a symbol of the Severin family''s prominence within the town, offering a large and well-appointed space amid the rugged surroundings of Solstheim.

Mirri Severin is a key figure in the family, known for her strong presence in Raven Rock. Her brother, Tilisu Severin, also resides in the manor, adding to the family''s legacy within the community. Vendil Severin, another member of the family, is a prominent figure who, like his relatives, plays a significant role in Raven Rock''s life.', '''adding'':83B ''all'':22B ''also'':78B ''amid'':51B ''and'':19B,46B ''anoth'':94B ''appoint'':49B ''are'':25B ''as'':31B ''broth'':75B ''by'':14B ''community'':91B ''dark'':26B ''distinguish'':7B ''elves'':27B ''family'':37B,65B,86B,98B ''figur'':62B,102B ''for'':67B ''her'':68B,74B ''his'':105B ''hom'':8B ''in'':9B,63B,71B,80B,111B ''inhabit'':13B ''is'':5B,59B,99B ''key'':61B ''known'':66B ''larg'':45B ''legacy'':88B ''lif'':115B ''lik'':104B ''manor'':2A,4B,29B,82B ''memb'':95B ''mirri'':15B,57B ''of'':23B,34B,55B,96B ''offering'':43B ''originally'':12B ''plays'':107B ''presenc'':70B ''prominenc'':39B ''prominent'':101B ''rav'':10B,72B,112B ''relativ'':106B ''resid'':79B ''rock'':11B,73B,113B ''rol'':110B ''rugg'':53B ''s'':38B,87B,114B ''severin'':1A,3B,16B,18B,21B,36B,58B,77B,93B ''significant'':109B ''solstheim'':56B ''spac'':50B ''stands'':30B ''strong'':69B ''surroundings'':54B ''symbol'':33B ''the'':28B,35B,41B,52B,64B,81B,85B,90B,97B ''tilisu'':17B,76B ''to'':84B ''town'':42B ''vendil'':20B,92B ''well'':48B ''well-appoint'':47B ''who'':103B ''whom'':24B ''within'':40B,89B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('morvayn_ancestral_tomb', '
The Morvayn Ancestral Tomb is a solemn Dunmer tomb located in Raven Rock, positioned northwest of the flight of stairs that leads up to the Temple of Miraak, directly opposite the entrance to Morvayn Manor. This sacred site serves as the final resting place for members of the Morvayn family, a prominent line within House Redoran, and is where they are interred if they pass away on Solstheim.

The tomb holds the remains of past family members, including Remas and his wife Brara Morvayn, both former House Redoran Councilors from Vvardenfell. They were the parents of Lleril Morvayn, the current Councilor of Raven Rock and formal ruler of Solstheim. The tomb also honors Varel Morvayn, a smith who resided in Anvil. ', '''also'':115B ''ancestral'':2A,6B ''and'':60B,83B,108B ''anvil'':124B ''are'':64B ''as'':43B ''away'':69B ''both'':88B ''brar'':86B ''councilor'':104B ''councilors'':92B ''current'':103B ''directly'':32B ''dunm'':11B ''entranc'':35B ''family'':53B,79B ''final'':45B ''flight'':21B ''for'':48B ''form'':89B ''formal'':109B ''from'':93B ''his'':84B ''holds'':74B ''honors'':116B ''hous'':58B,90B ''if'':66B ''in'':14B,123B ''including'':81B ''interr'':65B ''is'':8B,61B ''leads'':25B ''lin'':56B ''lleril'':100B ''locat'':13B ''manor'':38B ''members'':49B,80B ''miraak'':31B ''morvayn'':1A,5B,37B,52B,87B,101B,118B ''northwest'':18B ''of'':19B,22B,30B,50B,77B,99B,105B,111B ''on'':70B ''opposit'':33B ''parents'':98B ''pass'':68B ''past'':78B ''plac'':47B ''position'':17B ''prominent'':55B ''rav'':15B,106B ''redor'':59B,91B ''rem'':82B ''remains'':76B ''resid'':122B ''resting'':46B ''rock'':16B,107B ''rul'':110B ''sacr'':40B ''serv'':42B ''sit'':41B ''smith'':120B ''solemn'':10B ''solstheim'':71B,112B ''stairs'':23B ''templ'':29B ''that'':24B ''the'':4B,20B,28B,34B,44B,51B,72B,75B,97B,102B,113B ''they'':63B,67B,95B ''this'':39B ''to'':27B,36B ''tomb'':3A,7B,12B,73B,114B ''up'':26B ''varel'':117B ''vvardenfell'':94B ''wer'':96B ''wher'':62B ''who'':121B ''wif'':85B ''within'':57B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('temple_ancestral_tomb', 'The Temple Ancestral Tomb is a sacred Dunmer tomb located within the heart of Raven Rock, uniquely accessible only from within the Raven Rock Temple, the Morvayn Ancestral Tomb, and the Ulen Ancestral Tomb. Unlike other tombs on Solstheim, it does not have a direct external entrance, and its connections to these three distinct areas are unlocked through a special key obtained during the "Clean Sweep" quest. This tomb serves as a place of reverence for the Dunmer people, housing the remains of their ancestors in a private, secluded space.

The tomb’s restricted access and its connections to the other ancestral tombs make it a place of significance, both spiritually and historically. Those who seek to enter the Temple Ancestral Tomb must navigate through the sacred grounds of Raven Rock, guided by the traditions and rituals that connect the past and present. ', '''access'':21B,98B ''ancestors'':88B ''ancestral'':2A,6B,31B,36B,105B,124B ''and'':33B,51B,99B,115B,139B,145B ''are'':58B,59B ''as'':74B ''both'':113B ''by'':136B ''cle'':68B ''connect'':142B ''connections'':53B,101B ''direct'':48B ''distinct'':57B ''does'':44B ''dunm'':11B,81B ''during'':66B ''enter'':121B ''entranc'':50B ''external'':49B ''for'':79B ''from'':23B ''grounds'':131B ''guid'':135B ''hav'':46B ''heart'':16B ''historically'':116B ''housing'':83B ''in'':89B ''is'':8B ''it'':43B,108B ''its'':52B,100B ''key'':64B ''locat'':13B ''mak'':107B ''morvayn'':30B ''must'':126B ''navigat'':127B ''not'':45B ''obtain'':65B ''of'':17B,77B,86B,111B,132B ''on'':41B ''only'':22B ''other'':39B,104B ''past'':144B ''peopl'':82B ''plac'':76B,110B ''present'':146B ''privat'':91B ''quest'':70B ''rav'':18B,26B,133B ''remains'':85B ''restrict'':97B ''reverenc'':78B ''rituals'':140B ''rock'':19B,27B,134B ''s'':96B ''sacr'':10B,130B ''seclud'':92B ''seek'':119B ''serv'':73B ''significanc'':112B ''solstheim'':42B ''spac'':93B ''special'':63B ''spiritually'':114B ''sweep'':69B ''templ'':1A,5B,28B,123B ''that'':141B ''the'':4B,15B,25B,29B,34B,67B,80B,84B,87B,94B,103B,122B,129B,137B,143B ''thes'':55B ''this'':71B ''thos'':117B ''thre'':56B ''through'':61B,128B ''to'':54B,102B,120B ''tomb'':3A,7B,12B,32B,37B,72B,95B,125B ''tombs'':40B,106B ''traditions'':138B ''ulen'':35B ''uniquely'':20B ''unlik'':38B ''unlock'':60B ''who'':118B ''within'':14B,24B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ulen_ancestral_tomb', 'The Ulen Ancestral Tomb is a revered Dunmer tomb located in Raven Rock, southeast of the flight of stairs leading up to the Temple of Miraak, directly opposite the entrance to Caerellius House. This sacred site serves as the final resting place for members of the Ulen family, a respected line within the Dunmer community of Raven Rock.

The tomb, like other ancestral sites on Solstheim, is a place of reflection and reverence, where the spirits of the departed are honored and remembered by their descendants.', '''ancestral'':2A,6B,66B ''and'':75B,85B ''are'':83B ''as'':41B ''by'':87B ''caerellius'':35B ''community'':58B ''depart'':82B ''descendants'':89B ''directly'':30B ''dunm'':11B,57B ''entranc'':33B ''family'':51B ''final'':43B ''flight'':20B ''for'':46B ''honor'':84B ''hous'':36B ''in'':14B ''is'':8B,70B ''leading'':23B ''lik'':64B ''lin'':54B ''locat'':13B ''members'':47B ''miraak'':29B ''of'':18B,21B,28B,48B,59B,73B,80B ''on'':68B ''opposit'':31B ''other'':65B ''plac'':45B,72B ''rav'':15B,60B ''reflection'':74B ''remember'':86B ''respect'':53B ''resting'':44B ''rever'':10B ''reverenc'':76B ''rock'':16B,61B ''sacr'':38B ''serv'':40B ''sit'':39B,67B ''solstheim'':69B ''southeast'':17B ''spirits'':79B ''stairs'':22B ''templ'':27B ''the'':4B,19B,26B,32B,42B,49B,56B,62B,78B,81B,88B ''this'':37B ''to'':25B,34B ''tomb'':3A,7B,12B,63B ''ulen'':1A,5B,50B ''up'':24B ''wher'':77B ''within'':55B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sadrith_mora', 'Sadrith Mora, meaning "Mushroom Forest" in Dark Elvish, was the seat of power for Great House Telvanni on the island of Vvardenfell. Situated on an island in the Zafirbel Bay, it was accessible primarily by boat or teleportation, and entry required a certification of hospitality. Dominated by Tel Naga, the central Telvanni tower and home of the local councilor, Sadrith Mora was characterized by its mushroom-inspired architecture, sprawling markets, and strict governance by House Telvanni. The city also hosted the Telvanni Council House and Wolverine Hall, an Imperial bastion incongruously located in Telvanni territory. Known for its exclusive culture, the city exemplified Telvanni independence and disdain for outside influence.

In its history, Sadrith Mora played a critical role in Telvanni politics and magical innovation. During the Second Era, Archmagister Nelos Otheri advanced the House’s magical capabilities, including the creation of the Spore Steed. By the Third Era, the city was ruled by the eccentric Magister Neloth, who gave his support to the Nerevarine during their quest to fulfill prophecy. Sadrith Mora was devastated during the Red Year in 4E 5, when the eruption of Red Mountain destroyed much of Vvardenfell. Though its fate afterward remains unclear, the city''s legacy endures as a symbol of Telvanni magical prowess and defiance of convention.', '''4e'':184B ''5'':185B ''access'':35B ''advanc'':136B ''afterward'':199B ''also'':82B ''an'':27B,91B ''and'':41B,56B,74B,88B,109B,126B,214B ''architectur'':71B ''archmagist'':133B ''as'':207B ''bastion'':93B ''bay'':32B ''boat'':38B ''by'':37B,49B,66B,77B,149B,157B ''capabiliti'':141B ''central'':53B ''certification'':45B ''characteriz'':65B ''city'':81B,105B,154B,203B ''convention'':217B ''council'':86B ''councilor'':61B ''creation'':144B ''critical'':121B ''cultur'':103B ''dark'':9B ''defianc'':215B ''destroy'':192B ''devastat'':178B ''disdain'':110B ''dominat'':48B ''during'':129B,169B,179B ''eccentric'':159B ''elvish'':10B ''endur'':206B ''entry'':42B ''eruption'':188B ''exclusiv'':102B ''exemplifi'':106B ''fat'':198B ''for'':16B,100B,111B ''forest'':7B ''fulfill'':173B ''gav'':163B ''governanc'':76B ''great'':17B ''hall'':90B ''his'':164B ''history'':116B ''hom'':57B ''hospitality'':47B ''host'':83B ''hous'':18B,78B,87B,138B ''imperial'':92B ''in'':8B,29B,96B,114B,123B,183B ''including'':142B ''incongruously'':94B ''independenc'':108B ''influenc'':113B ''innovation'':128B ''inspir'':70B ''island'':22B,28B ''it'':33B ''its'':67B,101B,115B,197B ''known'':99B ''legacy'':205B ''local'':60B ''locat'':95B ''magical'':127B,140B,212B ''magist'':160B ''markets'':73B ''meaning'':5B ''mor'':2A,4B,63B,118B,176B ''mountain'':191B ''much'':193B ''mushroom'':6B,69B ''mushroom-inspir'':68B ''nag'':51B ''nel'':134B ''neloth'':161B ''nerevarin'':168B ''of'':14B,23B,46B,58B,145B,189B,194B,210B,216B ''on'':20B,26B ''or'':39B ''otheri'':135B ''outsid'':112B ''play'':119B ''politics'':125B ''pow'':15B ''primarily'':36B ''prophecy'':174B ''prowess'':213B ''quest'':171B ''red'':181B,190B ''remains'':200B ''requir'':43B ''rol'':122B ''rul'':156B ''s'':139B,204B ''sadrith'':1A,3B,62B,117B,175B ''seat'':13B ''second'':131B ''situat'':25B ''spor'':147B ''sprawling'':72B ''ste'':148B ''strict'':75B ''support'':165B ''symbol'':209B ''tel'':50B ''teleportation'':40B ''telvanni'':19B,54B,79B,85B,97B,107B,124B,211B ''territory'':98B ''the'':12B,21B,30B,52B,59B,80B,84B,104B,130B,137B,143B,146B,150B,153B,158B,167B,170B,180B,187B,202B ''third'':151B ''though'':196B ''to'':166B,172B ''tow'':55B ''uncle'':201B ''vvardenfell'':24B,195B ''was'':11B,34B,64B,155B,177B ''when'':186B ''who'':162B ''wolverin'':89B ''year'':182B ''zafirbel'':31B', 'scholar, darkelf', '
Sadrith Mora, meaning "Mushroom Forest" in Dark Elvish, was the seat of House Telvanni''s power on Vvardenfell, located on an island in Zafirbel Bay. Known for its mushroom-inspired architecture and strict Telvanni governance, the city was dominated by the central Tel Naga tower and featured notable structures like the Telvanni Council House and Wolverine Hall. Sadrith Mora played a crucial role in Telvanni politics and magical advancements, especially under Archmagister Nelos Otheri and Magister Neloth in later years. Devastated during the Red Year by the eruption of Red Mountain, its fate remains uncertain, but it remains a symbol of Telvanni''s magical prowess and independence.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('baldor_iron-shaper''s_house', 'Baldor Iron-Shaper''s House is a sturdy, well-crafted home located on the south side of Skaal Village, nestled between Deor Woodcutter''s House to the west and the Shaman''s Hut to the east. As the name suggests, it is the residence of Baldor Iron-Shaper, a skilled Nord blacksmith known for his expertise in forging weapons and armor.

Baldor Iron-Shaper is a respected member of Skaal Village, contributing to the community through his craft.', '''and'':37B,69B ''armor'':70B ''as'':45B ''baldor'':1A,7B,54B,71B ''betw'':29B ''blacksmith'':61B ''community'':85B ''contributing'':82B ''craft'':18B,88B ''deor'':30B ''east'':44B ''expertis'':65B ''for'':63B ''forging'':67B ''his'':64B,87B ''hom'':19B ''hous'':6A,12B,33B ''hut'':41B ''in'':66B ''iron'':3A,9B,56B,73B ''iron-shap'':2A,8B,55B,72B ''is'':13B,50B,75B ''it'':49B ''known'':62B ''locat'':20B ''memb'':78B ''nam'':47B ''nestl'':28B ''nord'':60B ''of'':25B,53B,79B ''on'':21B ''residenc'':52B ''respect'':77B ''s'':5A,11B,32B,40B ''sham'':39B ''shap'':4A,10B,57B,74B ''sid'':24B ''skaal'':26B,80B ''skill'':59B ''south'':23B ''sturdy'':15B ''suggests'':48B ''the'':22B,35B,38B,43B,46B,51B,84B ''through'':86B ''to'':34B,42B,83B ''villag'':27B,81B ''weapons'':68B ''well'':17B ''well-craft'':16B ''west'':36B ''woodcutt'':31B', 'skaal', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('deor_woodcutter''s_house', 'Deor Woodcutter''s House is a humble home located on the south side of Skaal Village, positioned between Oslaf''s House to the northwest and Baldor Iron-Shaper''s House to the east. This modest residence is the home of Deor Woodcutter, a hard-working Nord who, as his name suggests, spends his days felling trees and providing firewood for the village. His efforts are essential to the survival of Skaal Village, as wood is needed for warmth, building, and crafting.

