INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cyrodiil', '
Cyrodiil, the heartland of Tamriel and home to the Imperials, serves as the seat of the Empire and the location of its capital, the Imperial City. Dominated by the iconic White-Gold Tower, Cyrodiil is central to Tamriel''s history and culture. Though initially described as a jungle, its climate is temperate, possibly altered by Emperor Tiber Septim. The province''s early history is marked by the rule of the Ayleids, who enslaved the native Nedic people. The rebellion led by Alessia in 1E 242 ended Ayleid dominance, establishing the Alessian Empire and shaping Cyrodiil into a center of human governance and culture. The Alessians expanded westward, influenced by the prophet Marukh''s teachings, which codified much of Tamriel’s religion.

Cyrodiil’s history is defined by cycles of conquest and upheaval, from the Akaviri invasion of 1E 2703, which united Tamriel under Emperor Reman I, to the eventual collapse of the Second Empire. The chaos of the Interregnum ended with Tiber Septim''s rise, uniting Tamriel under the Third Empire. The Fourth Era brought new challenges, including the Great War against the Aldmeri Dominion, marked by the brutal Battle of the Red Ring and the controversial White-Gold Concordat. While Cyrodiil remains the seat of the Empire, these events have left a lasting impact, straining relations with Skyrim and reshaping the political landscape of Tamriel.', '''1e'':86B,140B ''242'':87B ''2703'':141B ''against'':184B ''akaviri'':137B ''aldmeri'':186B ''alessi'':84B,93B ''alessians'':107B ''alter'':56B ''and'':7B,19B,43B,95B,104B,133B,197B,223B ''as'':13B,48B ''ayle'':89B ''ayleids'':73B ''battl'':192B ''brought'':177B ''brutal'':191B ''by'':29B,57B,68B,83B,111B,129B,189B ''capital'':24B ''cent'':100B ''central'':38B ''cha'':158B ''challeng'':179B ''city'':27B ''climat'':52B ''codifi'':118B ''collaps'':152B ''concordat'':203B ''conquest'':132B ''controversial'':199B ''cultur'':44B,105B ''cycles'':130B ''cyrodiil'':1A,2B,36B,97B,124B,205B ''defin'':128B ''describ'':47B ''dominanc'':90B ''dominat'':28B ''dominion'':187B ''early'':64B ''emperor'':58B,146B ''empir'':18B,94B,156B,173B,211B ''ended'':88B,162B ''enslav'':75B ''establishing'':91B ''events'':213B ''eventual'':151B ''expand'':108B ''fourth'':175B ''from'':135B ''gold'':34B,202B ''governanc'':103B ''great'':182B ''hav'':214B ''heartland'':4B ''history'':42B,65B,126B ''hom'':8B ''hum'':102B ''i'':148B ''iconic'':31B ''impact'':218B ''imperial'':26B ''imperials'':11B ''in'':85B ''including'':180B ''influenc'':110B ''initially'':46B ''interregnum'':161B ''into'':98B ''invasion'':138B ''is'':37B,53B,66B,127B ''its'':23B,51B ''jungl'':50B ''landscap'':227B ''lasting'':217B ''led'':82B ''left'':215B ''location'':21B ''mark'':67B,188B