INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('summerset_isles', 'The Summerset Isles, officially renamed Alinor in 4E 22, is a province in southwestern Tamriel consisting of 14 islands, including the prominent Summerset Isle, Auridon, and the elusive Artaeum. Home to the Altmer (High Elves), the region boasts a rich history dating back to the Early Merethic Era when the Aldmer first arrived, claiming the land and founding cities like Firsthold and the Crystal Tower. Over time, the Aldmer evolved into the Altmer, establishing a strict class system with their society centered around the monarchy in Alinor. Despite their idyllic lifestyle, the Altmer faced frequent conflicts, including invasions by the necromantic Sload and the rival Maormer. The Summerset Isles were eventually incorporated into the Second Empire under favorable terms, minimizing contact with outsiders.

During the Oblivion Crisis, the Thalmor rose to power by successfully defending the Isles, later overthrowing the ancient monarchy and renaming the region Alinor. This marked the foundation of the Third Aldmeri Dominion, with Valenwood and Elsweyr joining as client states. The Thalmor''s dominance persisted into the Fourth Era, significantly influencing Tamriel''s political landscape. The Summerset Isles remains a symbol of Altmeri culture, history, and their enduring pursuit of power and isolation.', '''14'':20B ''22'':11B ''4e'':10B ''aldmer'':53B,71B ''aldmeri'':157B ''alinor'':8B,89B,149B ''altmer'':35B,75B,95B ''altmeri'':189B ''ancient'':143B ''and'':28B,59B,64B,105B,145B,161B,192B,198B ''around'':85B ''arriv'':55B ''artaeum'':31B ''as'':164B ''auridon'':27B ''back'':45B ''boasts'':40B ''by'':101B,135B ''center'':84B ''citi'':61B ''claiming'':56B ''class'':79B ''client'':165B ''conflicts'':98B ''consisting'':18B ''contact'':123B ''crisis'':129B ''crystal'':66B ''cultur'':190B ''dating'':44B ''defending'':137B ''despit'':90B ''dominanc'':170B ''dominion'':158B ''during'':126B ''early'':48B ''elsweyr'':162B ''elusiv'':30B ''elves'':37B ''empir'':118B ''enduring'':194B ''establishing'':76B ''eventually'':113B ''evolv'':72B ''fac'':96B ''favor'':120B ''first'':54B ''firsthold'':63B ''foundation'':153B ''founding'':60B ''fourth'':174B ''frequent'':97B ''high'':36B ''history'':43B,191B ''hom'':32B ''idyllic'':92B ''in'':9B,15B,88B ''including'':22B,99B ''incorporat'':114B ''influencing'':177B ''into'':73B,115B,172B ''invasions'':100B ''is'':12B ''islands'':21B ''isle'':26B ''isles'':2A,5B,111B,139B,184B ''isolation'':199B ''joining'':163B ''land'':58B ''landscap'':181B ''lat'':140B ''lifestyl'':93B ''lik'':62B ''maorm'':108B ''mark'':151B ''merethic'':49B ''minimizing'':122B ''monarchy'':87B,144B ''necromantic'':103B ''oblivion'':128B ''of'':19B,154B,188B,196B ''officially'':6B ''outsiders'':125B ''over'':68B ''overthrowing'':141B ''persist'':171B ''political'':180B ''pow'':134B,197B ''prominent'':24B ''provinc'':14B ''pursuit'':195B ''region'':39B,148B ''remains'':185B ''renam'':7B ''renaming'':146B ''rich'':42B ''rival'':107B ''ros'':132B ''s'':169B,179B ''second'':117B ''significantly'':176B ''slo'':104B ''society'':83B ''southwestern'':16B ''stat'':166B ''strict'':78B ''successfully'':136B ''summerset'':1A,4B,25B,110B,183B ''symbol'':187B ''system'':80B ''tamriel'':17B,178B ''terms'':121B ''thalmor'':131B,168B ''the'':3B,23B,29B,34B,38B,47B,52B,57B,65B,70B,74B,82B,86B,91B,94B,102B,106B,109B,116B,127B,130B,138B,142B,147B,152B,155B,167B,173B,182B,193B ''third'':156B ''this'':150B ''tim'':69B ''to'':33B,46B,133B ''tow'':67B ''under'':119B ''valenwood'':160B ''wer'':112B ''when'':51B ''with'':81B,124B,159B', 'scholar,  highelf', '
The Summerset Isles, renamed Alinor in 4E 22, is a province in southwestern Tamriel consisting of 14 islands, including Summerset Isle and Auridon. Home to the Altmer (High Elves), the region has a rich history dating back to the Early Merethic Era, when the Aldmer arrived and founded cities like Firsthold. Over time, the Altmer established a strict class system centered around their monarchy. The Isles faced conflicts with invaders like the necromantic Sload and Maormer. After the Oblivion Crisis, the Thalmor rose to power, founding the Third Aldmeri Dominion, which continued to shape Tamriel’s politics in the Fourth Era. The Summerset Isles remains a symbol of Altmeri culture and power.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('valenwood', '
Valenwood is a lush, densely forested province in southwestern Tamriel, renowned for its sprawling rainforests, rolling hills, and mangrove swamps. Home to the Bosmer (Wood Elves), as well as races like Wood Orcs, Imga, and Centaurs, Valenwood is a natural haven often referred to as "Tamriel''s garden." A unique feature of the region is its massive, migratory trees, some of which serve as cities. Among these is Falinesti, a mile-high tree that acts as the capital of Valenwood. The province is bordered by Elsweyr to the east, Cyrodiil to the north, and lies across the sea from the Summerset Isles.

The region is divided into Grahtwood, Greenshade, Malabal Tor, and western Reaper''s March, with its landscapes ranging from coastal mangroves to temperate inland forests nourished by heavy rainfall. The Bosmer inhabit timber clanhouses scattered across Valenwood, blending seamlessly with the natural environment. Despite its beauty, the province''s dense woodlands and remote settlements make travel difficult, with only a few Imperial roads connecting its widely separated communities.', '''across'':98B,140B ''acts'':77B ''among'':67B ''and'':19B,36B,96B,114B,156B ''as'':28B,30B,46B,65B,78B ''beauty'':150B ''blending'':142B ''border'':86B ''bosm'':25B,135B ''by'':87B,131B ''capital'':80B ''centaurs'':37B ''citi'':66B ''clanhous'':138B ''coastal'':124B ''communiti'':172B ''connecting'':168B ''cyrodiil'':92B ''dens'':154B ''densely'':6B ''despit'':148B ''difficult'':161B ''divid'':108B ''east'':91B ''elsweyr'':88B ''elves'':27B ''environment'':147B ''falinesti'':70B ''featur'':52B ''few'':165B ''for'':13B ''forest'':7B ''forests'':129B ''from'':101B,123B ''gard'':49B ''grahtwood'':110B ''greenshad'':111B ''hav'':42B ''heavy'':132B ''high'':74B ''hills'':18B ''hom'':22B ''imga'':35B ''imperial'':166B ''in'':9B ''inhabit'':136B ''inland'':128B ''into'':109B ''is'':3B,39B,56B,69B,85B,107B ''isles'':104B ''its'':14B,57B,120B,149B,169B ''landscap'':121B ''lies'':97B ''lik'':32B ''lush'':5B ''mak'':159B ''malabal'':112B ''mangrov'':20B,125B ''march'':118B ''massiv'':58B ''migratory'':59B ''mil'':73B ''mile-high'':72B ''natural'':41B,146B ''north'':95B ''nourish'':130B ''of'':53B,62B,81B ''often'':43B ''only'':163B ''orcs'':34B ''provinc'':8B,84B,152B ''rac'':31B ''rainfall'':133B ''rainforests'':16B ''ranging'':122B ''reap'':116B ''referr'':44B ''region'':55B,106B ''remot'':157B ''renown'':12B ''roads'':167B ''rolling'':17B ''s'':48B,117B,153B ''scatter'':139B ''seamlessly'':143B ''separat'':171B ''serv'':64B ''settlements'':158B ''som'':61B ''southwestern'':10B ''sprawling'':15B ''summerset'':103B ''swamps'':21B ''tamriel'':11B,47B ''temperat'':127B ''that'':76B ''the'':24B,54B,79B,83B,90B,94B,99B,102B,105B,134B,145B,151B ''thes'':68B ''timb'':137B ''to'':23B,45B,89B,93B,126B ''tor'':113B ''travel'':160B ''tre'':60B,75B ''uniqu'':51B ''valenwood'':1A,2B,38B,82B,141B ''well'':29B ''western'':115B ''which'':63B ''widely'':170B ''with'':119B,144B,162B ''wood'':26B,33B ''woodlands'':155B', 'scholar, woodelf', 'Valenwood is a lush, densely forested province in southwestern Tamriel, home to the Bosmer (Wood Elves) and other races like Wood Orcs, Imga, and Centaurs. The region is known for its sprawling rainforests, rolling hills, and mangrove swamps, with unique migratory trees that serve as cities, including Falinesti, the capital. Valenwood is bordered by Elsweyr, Cyrodiil, and the Summerset Isles, and is divided into regions like Grahtwood, Greenshade, and Malabal Tor. The Bosmer live in harmony with nature, in timber clanhouses scattered across the province. Despite its beauty, the province''s remote location and difficult terrain make travel challenging.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('anvil', 'Anvil, located on the Gold Coast by the Abecean Sea, is a prominent harbor city and the seat of County Anvil in southwestern Cyrodiil. Known for its Redguard-influenced architecture and bustling maritime trade, Anvil features notable districts such as Castle Anvil, Chapelgate, and Harborside. The city''s landmarks include the Chapel of Dibella, the mysterious Mermaid Statue, and Benirus Manor, which carries a dark history of necromancy. Anvil also hosts the Fighters Guild and a Mages Guild chapter specializing in Restoration. Historically, the city served as a pirate haven before being transformed into a fortified settlement by King Bendu Olo, who led the All Flags Navy against the Sload in the First Era.

Throughout its history, Anvil has endured periods of turmoil and prosperity. In the Second Era, it became a free city under pirate control, and during the Oblivion Crisis in the Third Era, it faced attacks by Daedra, thieves, and the Dark Brotherhood. Despite these challenges, the city thrived under Count Corvus Umbranox and his lineage. Anvil''s strategic location made it a target during the Great War in the Fourth Era, resulting in a siege by the Aldmeri Dominion. Despite this, Anvil remains a vital cultural and economic hub, blending its rich maritime heritage with the resilience of its people.', '''abec'':10B ''against'':110B ''aldmeri'':194B ''all'':107B ''also'':72B ''and'':17B,33B,46B,61B,77B,126B,140B,155B,169B,203B ''anvil'':1A,2B,22B,37B,44B,71B,120B,172B,198B ''architectur'':32B ''as'':42B,89B ''attacks'':151B ''becam'':133B ''befor'':93B ''being'':94B ''bendu'':102B ''benirus'':62B ''blending'':206B ''brotherhood'':158B ''bustling'':34B ''by'':8B,100B,152B,192B ''carri'':65B ''castl'':43B ''challeng'':161B ''chapel'':54B ''chapelgat'':45B ''chapt'':81B ''city'':16B,49B,87B,136B,163B ''coast'':7B ''control'':139B ''corvus'':167B ''count'':166B ''county'':21B ''crisis'':144B ''cultural'':202B ''cyrodiil'':25B ''daedr'':153B ''dark'':67B,157B ''despit'':159B,196B ''dibell'':56B ''districts'':40B ''dominion'':195B ''during'':141B,180B ''economic'':204B ''endur'':122B ''fac'':150B ''featur'':38B ''fighters'':75B ''first'':115B ''flags'':108B ''for'':27B ''fortifi'':98B ''fourth'':186B ''fre'':135B ''gold'':6B ''great'':182B ''guild'':76B,80B ''harbor'':15B ''harborsid'':47B ''hav'':92B ''heritag'':210B ''his'':170B ''historically'':85B ''history'':68B,119B ''hosts'':73B ''hub'':205B ''in'':23B,83B,113B,128B,145B,184B,189B ''includ'':52B ''influenc'':31B ''into'':96B ''is'':12B ''it'':132B,149B,177B ''its'':28B,118B,207B,215B ''king'':101B ''known'':26B ''landmarks'':51B ''led'':105B ''lineag'':171B ''locat'':3B ''location'':175B ''mad'':176B ''mag'':79B ''man