Anvil is a prominent harbor city on the Gold Coast of Cyrodiil, known for its Redguard-influenced architecture and bustling maritime trade. It features landmarks like the Chapel of Dibella, the Mermaid Statue, and Benirus Manor, with a history rooted in piracy and maritime warfare. The city has hosted both the Fighters Guild and a Mages Guild chapter, and has endured periods of turmoil, including pirate control, Daedric attacks during the Oblivion Crisis, and a siege in the Fourth Era. Despite these challenges, Anvil remains a vital cultural and economic hub with a rich history.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sancre_tor', 'Sancre Tor, known as the "Golden Hill," was an ancient city in the Jerall Mountains of Colovia, central to the history and mythology of Cyrodiil. Believed to be the birthplace and resting place of Reman Cyrodiil, it was associated with various legends, including Alessia''s divine inspiration and the mythical union of King Hrol and Saint Alessia, which supposedly birthed the Reman dynasty. Initially a vibrant settlement marked by its sacred crypts and fortifications, it fell into ruin after the collapse of the Reman Dynasty. Over the centuries, Sancre Tor became a haunted site, known for its crypts filled with undead and its ties to pivotal events such as the hiding of the Amulet of Kings during the Second Era.

Throughout history, Sancre Tor played a significant role in the Elder Scrolls lore, serving as a battleground for General Talos (later Tiber Septim) during the Tiber Wars and as the site of his eventual ascension to godhood. In the Third Era, the ruins were corrupted by the Underking and sealed by the Blades, with its guardians cursed to undeath. The Hero of Kvatch later unsealed the ruins, freed the cursed Blades, and retrieved the Armor of Tiber Septim during their quest. Sancre Tor remains a symbol of both glory and decay, reflecting the cyclical nature of power and its legacy in Tamrielic history.', '''after'':81B ''alessi'':46B,59B ''amulet'':116B ''an'':11B ''ancient'':12B ''and'':24B,33B,50B,57B,75B,104B,150B,171B,194B,212B,220B ''armor'':197B ''as'':6B,111B,137B,151B ''ascension'':157B ''associat'':41B ''battleground'':139B ''be'':30B ''becam'':93B ''believ'':28B ''birth'':62B ''birthplac'':32B ''blad'':175B,193B ''both'':210B ''by'':71B,168B,173B ''central'':20B ''centuri'':90B ''city'':13B ''collaps'':83B ''colovi'':19B ''corrupt'':167B ''crypts'':74B,100B ''curs'':179B,192B ''cyclical'':216B ''cyrodiil'':27B,38B ''decay'':213B ''divin'':48B ''during'':119B,146B,201B ''dynasty'':65B,87B ''elder'':133B ''events'':109B ''eventual'':156B ''fell'':78B ''fill'':101B ''for'':98B,140B ''fortifications'':76B ''fre'':190B ''general'':141B ''glory'':211B ''godhood'':159B ''gold'':8B ''guardians'':178B ''haunt'':95B ''her'':183B ''hiding'':113B ''hill'':9B ''his'':155B ''history'':23B,124B,225B ''hrol'':56B ''in'':14B,131B,160B,223B ''including'':45B ''initially'':66B ''inspiration'':49B ''into'':79B ''it'':39B,77B ''its'':72B,99B,105B,177B,221B ''jerall'':16B ''king'':55B ''kings'':118B ''known'':5B,97B ''kvatch'':185B ''lat'':143B,186B ''legacy'':222B ''legends'':44B ''lor'':135B ''mark'':70B ''mountains'':17B ''mythical'':52B ''mythology'':25B ''natur'':217B ''of'':18B,26B,36B,54B,84B,114B,117B,154B,184B,198B,209B,218B ''over'':88B ''pivotal'':108B ''plac'':35B ''