INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bruma', 'Bruma, a Nibenese city nestled in the Jerall Mountains north of the Imperial City, is known for its Nordic population and snow-covered, cold climate. The city''s architecture reflects its Nordic influence, and its residents practice a mix of traditional Nordic beliefs and the worship of the Divines. The Great Chapel of Talos dominates the city center, and Bruma is connected to other regions by the Silver Road to the Imperial City and the Orange Road to Chorrol. Nearby landmarks include the historic Cloud Ruler Temple, and the city''s underground network of sewers and caves has been the site of significant events, including use by the Mythic Dawn during the Oblivion Crisis.

Bruma has a storied history, playing a key role in various conflicts, such as Varen''s Rebellion and the Oblivion Crisis in 3E 433. The city successfully repelled a Daedric siege during the Crisis, thanks to Martin Septim and reinforcements from other Cyrodiilic cities. Later, Bruma endured attacks from Molag Bal''s forces during the Planemeld in 2E 582 and suffered losses like the destruction of its Mages Guild hall by the Order of the Black Worm. In the Fourth Era, Bruma faced continued challenges, including the destruction of the Dark Brotherhood sanctuary and raids by groups like the Crimson Dirks. Despite these adversities, Bruma remains a resilient and culturally rich city in northern Cyrodiil.', '''2e'':174B ''3e'':139B ''433'':140B ''582'':175B ''adversiti'':220B ''and'':22B,36B,46B,61B,76B,90B,98B,134B,155B,176B,210B,225B ''architectur'':31B ''as'':130B ''attacks'':164B ''bal'':167B ''been'':101B ''beliefs'':45B ''black'':192B ''brotherhood'':208B ''brum'':1A,2B,62B,117B,162B,198B,221B ''by'':68B,109B,187B,212B ''cav'':99B ''cent'':60B ''challeng'':201B ''chapel'':54B ''chorrol'':81B ''citi'':160B ''city'':5B,15B,29B,59B,75B,92B,142B,228B ''climat'':27B ''cloud'':87B ''cold'':26B ''conflicts'':128B ''connect'':64B ''continu'':200B ''cover'':25B ''crimson'':216B ''crisis'':116B,137B,150B ''culturally'':226B ''cyrodiil'':231B ''cyrodiilic'':159B ''daedric'':146B ''dark'':207B ''dawn'':112B ''despit'':218B ''destruction'':181B,204B ''dirks'':217B ''divin'':51B ''dominat'':57B ''during'':113B,148B,170B ''endur'':163B ''events'':106B ''fac'':199B ''for'':18B ''forc'':169B ''fourth'':196B ''from'':157B,165B ''great'':53B ''groups'':213B ''guild'':185B ''hall'':186B ''historic'':86B ''history'':121B ''imperial'':14B,74B ''in'':7B,126B,138B,173B,194B,229B ''includ'':84B ''including'':107B,202B ''influenc'':35B ''is'':16B,63B ''its'':19B,33B,37B,183B ''jerall'':9B ''key'':124B ''known'':17B ''landmarks'':83B ''lat'':161B ''lik'':179B,214B ''loss'':178B ''mag'':184B 