INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cheydinhal', 'Cheydinhal is a prosperous city in the eastern Nibenay region of Cyrodiil, near the border with Morrowind. Known for its picturesque beauty, Cheydinhal features lush greenery, flowing waterways, and a blend of Cyrodiilic and Dunmeri architectural styles, reflecting its close ties to Morrowind and its significant Dunmer population. The city is connected to the Imperial City via the Red Ring Road and is surrounded by fertile farmlands and scenic landscapes.

Cheydinhal is home to the Great Chapel of Arkay and notable guild chapters, including the Fighters Guild and the Mages Guild. Beneath its peaceful exterior, the city also hosts the sanctuary of the Dark Brotherhood, a secretive and infamous organization of assassins. Cheydinhal''s history is shaped by its cultural diversity, strategic location, and role as a hub for trade and governance in eastern Cyrodiil.', '''also'':99B ''and'':30B,35B,45B,63B,69B,81B,89B,109B,125B,132B ''architectural'':37B ''arkay'':80B ''as'':127B ''assassins'':113B ''beauty'':23B ''beneath'':93B ''blend'':32B ''bord'':16B ''brotherhood'':106B ''by'':66B,119B ''chapel'':78B ''chapters'':84B ''cheydinhal'':1A,2B,24B,72B,114B ''city'':6B,51B,57B,98B ''clos'':41B ''connect'':53B ''cultural'':121B ''cyrodiil'':13B,136B ''cyrodiilic'':34B ''dark'':105B ''diversity'':122B ''dunm'':48B ''dunmeri'':36B ''eastern'':9B,135B ''exterior'':96B ''farmlands'':68B ''featur'':25B ''fertil'':67B ''fighters'':87B ''flowing'':28B ''for'':20B,130B ''governanc'':133B ''great'':77B ''greenery'':27B ''guild'':83B,88B,92B ''history'':116B ''hom'':74B ''hosts'':100B ''hub'':129B ''imperial'':56B ''in'':7B,134B ''including'':85B ''infamous'':110B ''is'':3B,52B,64B,73B,117B ''its'':21B,40B,46B,94B,120B ''known'':19B ''landscap'':71B ''location'':124B ''lush'':26B ''mag'':91B ''morrowind'':18B,44B ''near'':14B ''nibenay'':10B ''notabl'':82B ''of'':12B,33B,79B,103B,112B ''organization'':111B ''peaceful'':95B ''picturesqu'':22B ''population'':49B ''prosperous'':5B ''red'':60B ''reflecting'':39B ''region'':11B ''ring'':61B ''road'':62B ''rol'':126B ''s'':115B ''sanctuary'':102B ''scenic'':70B ''secretiv'':108B ''shap'':118B ''significant'':47B ''strategic'':123B ''styles'':38B ''surround'':65B ''the'':8B,15B,50B,55B,59B,76B,86B,90B,97B,101B,104B ''ties'':42B ''to'':43B,54B,75B ''trad'':131B ''via'':58B ''waterways'':29B ''with'':17B', 'scholar, imperial', '
Cheydinhal is a prosperous city in eastern Cyrodiil, near the Morrowind border, known for its lush greenery and mix of Cyrodiilic and Dunmeri architecture. The city is home to the Great Chapel of Arkay and several guilds, including the Fighters Guild and the Mages Guild. Despite its peaceful appearance, Cheydinhal also hosts the Dark Brotherhood sanctuary. Its strategic location and cultural diversity make it a key hub for trade and governance in eastern Cyrodiil.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chorrol', 'Chorrol is a picturesque Colovian town located in northwestern Cyrodiil, nestled between the Great Forest and the Colovian Highlands near the Hammerfell border. Known for its serene environment, Chorrol is shaded by large oak canopies, with the iconic Great Oak standing at its center. The town is divided into districts, including Castle Chorrol, Chapel Street, and Great Oak Place, and is surrounded by thick walls and guard towers for protection. It is home to notable landmarks such as the Great Chapel of Stendarr, Weynon Priory, and the historic statue of Saint Osla at Fountain Gate.

Chorrol has a rich history dating back to the Merethic Era and has played a role in many key events, such as the Colovian Revolt led by Varen Aquilarios and the Oblivion Crisis of the Third Era when it came under siege by Daedric forces. Countess Arriana Valga ruled the town at the close of the Third Era, and its legacy as a hub of Colovian culture and trade endures into the Fourth Era. The town''s blend of history, beauty, and community makes it a notable gem in Cyrodiil''s landscape.', '''and'':17B,57B,61B,67B,87B,108B,126B,155B,164B,178B ''aquilari'':125B ''arrian'':143B ''as'':79B,118B,158B ''at'':43B,94B,148B ''back'':103B ''beauty'':177B ''betw'':13B ''blend'':174B ''bord'':24B ''by'':33B,64B,123B,139B ''cam'':136B ''canopi'':36B ''castl'':53B ''cent'':45B ''chapel'':55B,82B ''chorrol'':1A,2B,30B,54B,97B ''clos'':150B ''colovi'':6B,19B,120B,162B ''community'':179B ''countess'':142B ''crisis'':129B ''cultur'':163B ''cyrodiil'':11B,186B ''daedric'':140B ''dating'':102B ''districts'':51B ''divid'':49B ''endur'':166B ''environment'':29B ''events'':116B ''for'':26B,70B ''forc'':141B ''forest'':16B ''fountain'':95B ''fourth'':169B ''gat'':96B ''gem'':184B ''great'':15B,40B,58B,81B ''guard'':68B ''hammerfell'':23B ''highlands'':20B ''historic'':89B ''history'':101B,176B ''hom'':74B ''hub'':160B ''iconic'':39B ''in'':9B,113B,185B ''including'':52B ''into'':50B,167B ''is'':3B,31B,48B,62B,73B ''it'':72B,135B,181B ''its'':27B,44B,156B ''key'':115B ''known'':25B ''landmarks'':77B ''landscap'':188B ''larg'':34B ''led'':122B ''legacy'':157B ''locat'':8B ''mak'':180B ''many'':114B ''merethic'':106B ''near'':21B ''nestl'':12B ''northwestern'':10B ''notabl'':76B,183B ''oak'':35B,41B,59B ''oblivion'':128B ''of'':83B,91B,130B,151B,161B,175B ''osla'':93B ''picturesqu'':5B ''plac'':60B ''play'':110B ''priory'':86B ''protection'':71B ''revolt'':121B ''rich'':100B ''rol'':112B ''rul'':145B ''s'':173B,187B ''saint'':92B ''seren'':28B ''shad'':32B ''sieg'':138B ''standing'':42B ''statu'':90B ''stendarr'':84B ''street'':56B ''such'':78B,117B ''surround'':63B ''the'':14B,18B,22B,38B,46B,80B,88B,105B,119B,127B,131B,146B,149B,152B,168B,171B ''thick'':65B ''third'':132B,153B ''to'':75B,104B ''towers'':69B ''town'':7B,47B,147B,172B ''trad'':165B ''under'':137B ''valg'':144B ''var'':124B ''walls'':66B ''weynon'':85B ''when'':134B ''with'':37B', 'scholar, imperial', 'Chorrol is a picturesque town in northwestern Cyrodiil, known for its serene environment, large oak trees, and the iconic Great Oak. The town features districts like Castle Chorrol and Chapel Street, and is home to landmarks such as the Great Chapel of Stendarr and Weynon Priory. With a rich history dating back to the Merethic Era, Chorrol played a role in events like the Colovian Revolt and the Oblivion Crisis. Its legacy as a cultural and trade hub continues into the Fourth Era, making it a notable part of Cyrodiil’s landscape.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cloud_ruler_temple', 'Cloud Ruler Temple, perched high in the Jerall Mountains near Bruma, was an ancient and iconic stronghold of the Blades, showcasing dramatic Akaviri architecture. Constructed by the Akaviri Dragonguard during the founding of the Second Empire under Reman Cyrodiil, it served as the Blades'' headquarters until the end of the Third Era. The temple was revered for its Great Hall, where swords of those who died protecting the Dragonborn were displayed, and for its archives, which housed invaluable lore on the Blades.

Throughout its history, Cloud Ruler Temple played a crucial role in Tamrielic events. It became a refuge for Martin Septim during the Oblivion Crisis of 3E 433, where the Blades aided his efforts to thwart Mehrunes Dagon. In the Fourth Era, the temple was a key target during the Great War, as the Thalmor besieged it to eliminate the Blades, who had orchestrated resistance missions against the Dominion. The siege led to the destruction of the temple’s archives, and only a few, like Acilius Bolar, survived to continue the Blades’ legacy in exile.', '''3e'':111B ''433'':112B ''acilius'':170B ''against'':151B ''aid'':116B ''akaviri'':26B,31B ''an'':16B ''ancient'':17B ''and'':18B,75B,165B ''architectur'':27B ''archiv'':78B,164B ''as'':45B,137B ''becam'':100B ''besieg'':140B ''blad'':23B,47B,85B,115B,145B,176B ''bol'':171B ''brum'':14B ''by'':29B ''cloud'':1A,4B,89B ''construct'':28B ''continu'':174B ''crisis'':109B ''crucial'':94B ''cyrodiil'':42B ''dagon'':122B ''destruction'':159B ''died'':69B ''display'':74B ''dominion'':153B ''dragonborn'':72B ''dragonguard'':32B ''dramatic'':25B ''during'':33B,106B,133B ''efforts'':118B ''eliminat'':143B ''empir'':39B ''end'':51B ''events'':98B ''exil'':179B ''few'':168B ''for'':60B,76B,103B ''founding'':35B ''fourth'':125B ''great'':62B,135B ''had'':147B ''hall'':63B ''headquarters'':48B ''high'':8B ''his'':117B ''history'':88B ''hous'':80B ''iconic'':19B ''in'':9B,96B,123B,178B ''invalu'':81B ''it'':43B,99B,141B ''its'':61B,77B,87B ''jerall'':11B ''key'':131B ''led'':156B ''legacy'':177B ''lik'':169B ''lor'':82B ''martin'':104B ''mehrun'':121B ''missions'':150B ''mountains'':12B ''near'':13B ''oblivion'':108B ''of'':21B,36B,52B,66B,110B,160B ''on'':83B ''only'':166B ''orchestrat'':148B ''perch'':7B ''play'':92B ''protecting'':70B ''refug'':102B ''rem'':41B ''resistanc'':149B ''rever'':59B ''rol'':95B ''rul'':2A,5B,90B ''s'':163B ''second'':38B ''septim'':105B ''serv'':44B ''showcasing'':24B ''sieg'':155B ''stronghold'':20B ''surviv'':172B ''swords'':65B ''tamrielic'':97B ''target'':132B ''templ'':3A,6B,57B,91B,128B,162B ''thalmor'':139B ''the'':10B,22B,30B,34B,37B,46B,50B,53B,56B,71B,84B,107B,114B,124B,127B,134B,138B,144B,152B,154B,158B,161B,175B ''third'':54B ''thos'':67B ''throughout'':86B ''thwart'':120B ''to'':119B,142B,157B,173B ''under'':40B ''until'':49B ''war'':136B ''was'':15B,58B,129B ''wer'':73B ''wher'':64B,113B ''which'':79B ''who'':68B,146B', 'scholar, imperial', 'Cloud Ruler Temple, located in the Jerall Mountains near Bruma, was a significant stronghold of the Blades, founded by the Akaviri Dragonguard during the Second Empire. Known for its dramatic Akaviri architecture, it served as the Blades'' headquarters until the end of the Third Era. The temple housed the Great Hall, displaying swords of fallen protectors, and valuable archives. It played a crucial role during the Oblivion Crisis as a refuge for Martin Septim, and later became a target during the Great War, resulting in its destruction and the scattering of the Blades'' legacy.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stormhold', 'Stormhold, one of the largest cities in Black Marsh, serves as the capital of the Shadowfen region and is steeped in a history of conflict, resilience, and transformation. Built atop the ancient Ayleid ruins of Silyanorn, Stormhold retains remnants of its past as a hub of Elven slavery during the Dark Elves’ control. The city’s architecture reflects its layered history, combining Argonian mud huts, Ayleid ruins, and Dark Elf stonework. A prominent Hist tree sits at its heart, surrounded by ancient relics, emphasizing its cultural and spiritual significance. During the Second Era, Stormhold became the capital of the Ebonheart Pact’s allied regions, playing a pivotal role in uniting Argonians, Nords, and Dark Elves against external threats, including the Akaviri invasion and the influence of the Aldmeri Dominion.

In the Third Era, Stormhold''s history took a darker turn as it became notorious for its corrupted prison system under Warden Quintus Varus, who exploited prisoners to mine the magical Stormhold Crystals. These events culminated in the heroic efforts of a prisoner who neutralized the corruption caused by Varus’s obsession with the mystical Storm Crystal. By the Fourth Era, the city faced destruction during Umbriel’s undead invasion, highlighting its enduring struggles in the volatile swamps of Black Marsh. Despite its challenges, Stormhold remains a symbol of Argonian resilience and adaptation, blending ancient traditions with the scars of its tumultuous past.', '''adaptation'':223B ''against'':117B ''akaviri'':122B ''aldmeri'':129B ''alli'':104B ''ancient'':33B,83B,225B ''and'':19B,28B,69B,88B,114B,124B,222B ''architectur'':58B ''argoni'':64B,220B ''argonians'':112B ''as'':12B,44B,142B ''at'':78B ''atop'':31B ''ayle'':34B,67B ''becam'':96B,144B ''black'':9B,210B ''blending'':224B ''built'':30B ''by'':82B,179B,188B ''capital'':14B,98B ''caus'':178B ''challeng'':214B ''citi'':7B ''city'':56B,193B ''combining'':63B ''conflict'':26B ''control'':54B ''corrupt'':148B ''corruption'':177B ''crystal'':187B ''crystals'':163B ''culminat'':166B ''cultural'':87B ''dark'':52B,70B,115B,140B ''despit'':212B ''destruction'':195B ''dominion'':130B ''during'':50B,91B,196B ''ebonheart'':101B ''efforts'':170B ''elf'':71B ''elven'':48B ''elves'':53B,116B ''emphasizing'':85B ''enduring'':203B ''events'':165B ''exploit'':156B ''external'':118B ''fac'':194B ''for'':146B ''fourth'':190B ''heart'':80B ''heroic'':169B ''highlighting'':201B ''hist'':75B ''history'':24B,62B,137B ''hub'':46B ''huts'':66B ''in'':8B,22B,110B,131B,167B,205B ''including'':120B ''influenc'':126B ''invasion'':123B,200B ''is'':20B ''it'':143B ''its'':42B,60B,79B,86B,147B,202B,213B,231B ''largest'':6B ''layer'':61B ''magical'':161B ''marsh'':10B,211B ''min'':159B ''mud'':65B ''mystical'':185B ''neutraliz'':175B ''nords'