INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sentinel', '
Sentinel, the capital of its eponymous kingdom in Hammerfell, is a significant cultural and political hub in the northwestern hills overlooking the Iliac Bay. Despite the arid Alik''r Desert surrounding it, the city thrives as a major population center, with fertile fields along the coast supporting its vibrant economy. Founded by the warrior-sailors of Grandee Yaghoub during the Ra Gada migration, Sentinel''s history is deeply intertwined with Redguard heritage and resilience. The city is renowned for its architectural marvels, particularly the grand Sentinel Palace (Samaruik), and its bustling market streets that attract both locals and visiting nobility from across Tamriel. Its strategic location has made it a crucial player in trade, controlling a significant portion of Iliac Bay commerce during the Second Era.

Throughout history, Sentinel has endured numerous challenges, including pirate raids, invasions, and the tensions between the Crown and Forebear factions. In the Second Era, the city faced threats such as necromantic armies and internal conflict during the political shifts following High King Thassad II''s death. Sentinel remained pivotal during the Third Empire, flourishing as a beacon of opportunity and adventure despite setbacks like the War of Betony. In the Fourth Era, the city demonstrated unity when Forebears came to the aid of Crowns during the Great War, leading to a reconciliation of the two factions. Today, Sentinel stands as a testament to Redguard tenacity, blending cultural richness with a history of overcoming adversity.', '''across'':104B ''adventur'':189B ''adversity'':242B ''aid'':210B ''alik'':29B ''along'':45B ''and'':15B,75B,91B,100B,140B,146B,161B,188B ''architectural'':83B ''arid'':28B ''armi'':160B ''as'':37B,158B,183B,228B ''attract'':97B ''bay'':25B,123B ''beacon'':185B ''betony'':196B ''betw'':143B ''blending'':234B ''both'':98B ''bustling'':93B ''by'':53B ''cam'':207B ''capital'':4B ''cent'':41B ''challeng'':135B ''city'':35B,78B,154B,202B ''coast'':47B ''commerc'':124B ''conflict'':163B ''controlling'':117B ''crown'':145B ''crowns'':212B ''crucial'':113B ''cultural'':14B,235B ''death'':174B ''deeply'':70B ''demonstrat'':203B ''desert'':31B ''despit'':26B,190B ''during'':61B,125B,164B,178B,213B ''economy'':51B ''empir'':181B ''endur'':133B ''eponymous'':7B ''fac'':155B ''factions'':148B,224B ''fertil'':43B ''fields'':44B ''flourishing'':182B ''following'':168B ''for'':81B ''foreb'':147B ''forebears'':206B ''found'':52B ''fourth'':199B ''from'':103B ''gad'':64B ''grand'':87B ''grande'':59B ''great'':215B ''hammerfell'':10B ''heritag'':74B ''high'':169B ''hills'':21B ''history'':68B,130B,239B ''hub'':17B ''ii'':172B ''iliac'':24B,122B ''in'':9B,18B,115B,149B,197B ''including'':136B ''internal'':162B ''intertwin'':71B ''invasions'':139B ''is