Necrom, also known as the "City of the Dead," is a major cultural and religious center in Morrowind, focused on ancestor worship and remembrance. Situated on a steep island, the city features interconnected districts, with the Necropolis housing ancestral remains. Governed by the Keepers of the Dead under House Indoril, it serves as a hub for pilgrims and traders. Necrom''s origins date back to the Merethic Era, with ties to Chimer traditions and Tribunal mythology. Despite political and cultural shifts, it remains a vital metropolis, celebrating its deep connection to death through rituals, festivals, and historical artifacts.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('alinor', 'Alinor, the ancient capital of the Summerset Isles, is a shining symbol of High Elven civilization, renowned for its towering, light-catching architecture and its position as the seat of the High Kingship for millennia. Nestled on the Oleander Coast between verdant mountains and idyllic beaches, Alinor boasts a sophisticated layout, from bustling lower streets and marketplaces to the majestic Royal Palace that overlooks the city. Known as the "forest city of Summerset," it is surrounded by vineyards and features the Alinor Docks, a hub for trade despite its landlocked location. Alinor''s sister city, Sunhold, lies just beyond the mountains, and together they form the cultural heart of the Altmer. The city has long been a focal point for diplomacy, art, and governance, maintaining its grandeur through eras of isolation and global engagement.

Throughout its history, Alinor has been central to major events shaping Tamriel. It has weathered conflicts with Maormer and Sload, contributed to the All Flags Navy, and led the formation of the Aldmeri Dominions under leaders like Queen Ayrenn. The city played a pivotal role in resisting Tiber Septim''s conquests, though it ultimately fell to the Numidium, leading to the integration of Summerset into the Third Empire. By the Fourth Era, Alinor was transformed under Thalmor rule, as the monarchy was abolished and the province was renamed "Alinor" to evoke its ancient past. Despite periods of turmoil, the city''s enduring legacy as a beacon of Altmeri culture and innovation remains unchallenged.', '''abolish'':219B ''aldmeri'':169B ''alinor'':1A,2B,49B,84B,94B,140B,209B,225B ''all'':160B ''altmer'':113B ''altmeri'':244B ''ancient'':4B,229B ''and'':26B,46B,58B,81B,104B,125B,134B,155B,163B,220B,246B ''architectur'':25B ''art'':124B ''as'':29B,70B,215B,240B ''ayrenn'':175B ''beach'':48B ''beacon'':242B ''been'':118B,142B ''betw'':43B ''beyond'':101B ''boasts'':50B ''bustling'':55B ''by'':79B,205B ''capital'':5B ''catching'':24B ''central'':143B ''city'':68B,73B,97B,115B,177B,236B ''civilization'':17B ''coast'':42B ''conflicts'':152B ''conquests'':187B ''contribut'':157B ''cultur'':245B ''cultural'':109B ''despit'':90B,231B ''diplomacy'':123B ''docks'':85B ''dominions'':170B ''elven'':16B ''empir'':204B ''enduring'':238B ''engagement'':136B ''events'':146B ''evok'':227B ''featur'':82B ''fell'':191B ''flags'':161B ''focal'':120B ''for'':19B,36B,88B,122B ''forest'':72B ''form'':107B ''formation'':166B ''fourth'':207B ''from'':54B ''global'':135B ''governanc'':126B ''grandeur'':129B ''heart'':110B ''high'':15B,34B ''history'':139B ''hub'':87B ''idyllic'':47B ''in'':182B ''innovation'':247B ''integration'':198B ''into'':201B ''is'':10B,77B ''isles'':9B ''isolation'':133B ''it'':76B,149B,189B ''its'':20B,27B,91B,128B,138B,228B ''just'':100B ''kingship'':35B ''known'':69B ''landlock'':92B ''layout'':53B ''leaders'':172B ''leading'':195B ''led'':164B ''legacy'':239B ''lies'':99B ''light'':23B ''light-catching'':22B ''lik'':173B ''location'':93B ''long'':117B ''low'':56B ''maintaining'':127B ''majestic'':62B ''major'':145B ''maorm'':154B ''marketplac'':59B ''millenni'':37B ''monarchy'':217B ''mountains'':45B,103B ''navy'':162B ''nestl'':38B ''numidium'':194B ''of'':6B,14B,32B,74B,111B,132B,167B,199B,233B,243B ''oleand'':41B ''on'':39B ''overlooks'':66B ''palac'':64B ''past'':230B ''periods'':232B ''pivotal'':180B ''play'':178B ''point'':121B ''position'':28B ''provinc'':222B ''que'':174B ''remains'':248B ''renam'':224B ''renown'':18B ''resisting'':183B ''rol'':181B ''royal'':63B ''rul'':214B ''s'':95B,186B,237B ''seat'':31B ''septim'':185B ''shaping'':147B ''shining'':12B ''sist'':96B ''slo'':156B ''sophisticat'':52B ''streets'':57B ''summerset'':8B,75B,200B ''sunhold'':98B ''surround'':78B ''symbol'':13B ''tamriel'':148B ''thalmor'':213B ''that'':65B ''the'':3B,7B,30B,33B,40B,61B,67B,71B,83B,102B,108B,112B,114B,159B,165B,168B,176B,193B,197B,202B,206B,216B,221B,235B ''they'':106B ''third'':203B ''though'':188B ''through'':130B ''throughout'':137B ''tib'':184B ''to'':60B,144B,158B,192B,196B,226B ''togeth'':105B ''towering'':21B ''trad'':89B ''transform'':211B ''turmoil'':234B ''ultimately'':190B ''unchalleng'':249B ''under'':171B,212B ''verdant'':44B ''vineyards'':80B ''was'':210B,218B,223B ''weather'':151B ''with'':153B', 'scholar,  highelf', '
Alinor, the ancient capital of the Summerset Isles, is a symbol of High Elven civilization known for its striking architecture and central role in the Altmer culture. Situated between mountains and beaches, the city boasts a sophisticated layout with bustling streets and the majestic Royal Palace. Historically, Alinor has been a hub for diplomacy, art, and governance, playing a significant role in events such as conflicts with the Maormer, the formation of the Aldmeri Dominion, and resistance to Tiber Septim''s conquest. By the Fourth Era, it was transformed under Thalmor rule, though it remains a key center of Altmeri culture and innovation.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('marbruk', 'Marbruk, located in the forested region of Greenshade in Valenwood, serves as a significant historical and cultural site. Originally settled by an Ayleid clan following the Alessian Slave Rebellion, the city evolved into a Bosmer settlement before being transformed into a fortified bastion by the Aldmeri Dominion in 2E 580. Built to defend Greenshade from external threats, its construction showcased modern Altmeri architecture, blending imported materials to respect the Green Pact while constructing atop ancient Ayleid ruins. The city became a symbol of Dominion unity but also sparked cultural tensions, as the Altmer enforced restrictions on traditional Bosmer practices. Marbruk''s Mages Guild vault housed priceless artifacts, including the Staff of Magnus, which played a central role in a Veiled Heritance attack led by the lich Prince Naemon. The Dominion, with the Vestige''s aid, repelled the undead assault and secured the city.

Throughout its history, Marbruk changed hands multiple times, reflecting the shifting political landscape of Valenwood. It was annexed by the Second Aldmeri Dominion during a Camoran civil war in 2E 830 but fell to Tiber Septim''s forces following his use of the Numidium in 2E 896, becoming part of the Third Empire. By the Third Era, the city had diminished to a small settlement known as Marbruk Field, ruled by Lord Palinis and enduring periods of rebellion and strife, including the Camoran Usurper Rebellion and the Oblivion Crisis. In 4E 29, a Thalmor-backed coup reclaimed Valenwood for the Aldmeri Dominion, marking Marbruk''s third incorporation into the Dominion. Despite its turbulent past, Marbruk remains a testament to the layered history and cultural dynamics of Valenwood.', '''29'':236B ''2e'':50B,174B,190B ''4e'':235B ''580'':51B ''830'':175B ''896'':191B ''aid'':136B ''aldmeri'':47B,166B,246B ''alessi'':28B ''also'':88B ''altmer'':94B ''altmeri'':63B ''an'':23B ''ancient'':76B ''and'':17B,141B,218B,223B,230B,268B ''annex'':162B ''architectur'':64B ''artifacts'':108B ''as'':13B,92B,211B ''assault'':140B ''atop'':75B ''attack'':123B ''ayle'':24B,77B ''back'':240B ''bastion'':44B ''becam'':81B ''becoming'':192B ''befor'':38B ''being'':39B ''blending'':65B ''bosm'':36B,99B ''built'':52B ''but'':87B,176B ''by'':22B,45B,125B,163B,198B,215B ''camor'':170B,227B ''central'':117B ''chang'':149B ''city'':32B,80B,144B,203B ''civil'':171B ''clan'':25B ''constructing'':74B ''construction'':60B ''coup'':241B ''crisis'':233B ''cultural'':18B,90B,269B ''defend'':54B ''despit'':256B ''diminish'':205B ''dominion'':48B,85B,131B,167B,247B,255B ''during'':168B ''dynamics'':270B ''empir'':197B ''enduring'':219B ''enforc'':95B ''evolv'':33B ''external'':57B ''fell'':177B ''field'':213B ''following'':26B,183B ''for'':244B ''forc'':182B ''forest'':6B ''fortifi'':43B ''from'':56B ''gre'':71B ''greenshad'':9B,55B ''guild'':104B ''had'':204B ''hands'':150B ''heritanc'':122B ''his'':184B ''historical'':16B ''history'':147B,267B ''hous'':106B ''import'':66B ''in'':4B,10B,49B,119B,173B,189B,234B ''including'':109B,225B ''incorporation'':252B ''into'':34B,41B,253B ''it'':160B ''its'':59B,146B,257B ''known'':210B ''landscap'':157B ''layer'':266B ''led'':124B ''lich'':127B ''locat'':3B ''lord'':216B ''mag'':103B ''magnus'':113B ''marbruk'':1A,2B,101B,148B,212B,249B,260B ''marking'':248B ''materials'':67B ''modern'':62B ''multipl'':151B ''naemon'':129B ''numidium'':188B ''oblivion'':232B ''of'':8B,84B,112B,158B,186B,194B,221B,271B ''on'':97B ''originally'':20B ''pact'':72B ''palinis'':217B ''part'':193B ''past'':259B ''periods'':220B ''play'':115B ''political'':156B ''practic'':100B ''priceless'':107B ''princ'':128B ''rebellion'':30B,222B,229B ''reclaim'':242B ''reflecting'':153B ''region'':7B ''remains'':261B ''repell'':137B ''respect'':69B ''restrictions'':96B ''rol'':118B ''ruins'':78B ''rul'':214B ''s'':102B,135B,181B,250B ''second'':165B ''secur'':142B ''septim'':180B ''serv'':12B ''settl'':21B ''settlement'':37B,209B ''shifting'':155B ''showcas'':61B ''significant'':15B ''sit'':19B ''slav'':29B ''small'':208B ''spark'':89B ''staff'':111B ''strif'':224B ''symbol'':83B ''tensions'':91B ''testament'':263B ''thalmor'':239B ''thalmor-back'':238B ''the'':5B,27B,31B,46B,70B,79B,93B,110B,126B,130B,133B,138B,143B,154B,164B,187B,195B,199B,202B,226B,231B,245B,254B,265B ''third'':196B,200B,251B ''threats'':58B ''throughout'':145B ''tib'':179B ''tim'':152B ''to'':53B,68B,178B,206B,264B ''traditional'':98B ''transform'':40B ''turbulent'':258B ''unde'':139B ''unity'':86B ''use'':185B ''usurp'':228B ''valenwood'':11B,159B,243B,272B ''vault'':105B ''veil'':121B ''vestig'':134B ''war'':172B ''was'':161B ''which'':114B ''whil'':73B ''with'':132B', 'scholar, woodelf', 'Marbruk, located in Greenshade, Valenwood, is a city with a rich history, originally settled by Ayleids and later transformed into a Bosmer settlement before being fortified by the Aldmeri Dominion in 2E 580. The city blends Altmeri architecture with respect for the Green Pact, standing atop ancient Ayleid ruins. Marbruk has been a focal point of conflict, from the Veiled Heritance attack to its shifting political control, including annexation by the Dominion and later conquest by Tiber Septim. Despite turmoil, Marbruk remains a symbol of Valenwood''s complex history, culture, and resilience.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('apocrypha', 'Apocrypha, the realm of Hermaeus Mora, Daedric Prince of Knowledge and Fate, is a vast and surreal domain designed to house all forbidden knowledge. Its geography alternates between eerie open fields, an endless library of black-covered books, and a dark, inky sea populated by writhing tentacles. This plane, haunted by the ghosts of mortals seeking knowledge, features towering book stacks, labyrinthine mazes, and ominous ruins under an unnatural green sky. Entry is primarily granted through Black Books, powerful artifacts scattered across Tamriel. Mortals who venture into Apocrypha risk insanity from unending revelations, as the realm operates outside the laws of the mortal world. Among its inhabitants are grotesque Daedric servants like Seekers, Lurkers, and the Watchers, who catalog and guard its secrets.

The realm is dotted with significant locations, including the Infinite Panopticon, a pocket dimension holding Mora''s most precious and dangerous knowledge, and Cipher’s Midden, a mortal settlement governed by the Prince’s will. Mortals entering Apocrypha are often drawn into Mora''s web of intrigue, with many succumbing to the overwhelming truths contained within. Historical events, such as the saga of Miraak, the First Dragonborn, highlight the realm''s power. Apocrypha also serves as the setting for Mora''s omnipresent influence, where secrets shape destiny, and knowledge becomes both a blessing and a curse.', '''across'':84B ''all'':23B ''also'':199B ''alternat'':28B ''among'':107B ''an'':33B,70B ''and'':12B,17B,41B,66B,117B,122B,145B,148B,213B,219B ''apocryph'':1A,2B,90B,163B,198B ''are'':110B,164B ''artifacts'':82B ''as'':96B,185B,201B ''becom'':215B ''betw'':29B ''black'':38B,79B ''black-cover'':37B ''blessing'':218B ''book'':62B ''books'':40B,80B ''both'':216B ''by'':47B,53B,156B ''catalog'':121B ''ciph'':149B ''contain'':180B ''cover'':39B ''curs'':221B ''daedric'':8B,112B ''dangerous'':146B ''dark'':43B ''design'':20B ''destiny'':212B ''dimension'':139B ''domain'':19B ''dott'':129B ''dragonborn'':192B ''drawn'':166B ''eeri'':30B ''endless'':34B ''entering'':162B ''entry'':74B ''events'':183B ''fat'':13B ''featur'':60B ''fields'':32B ''first'':191B ''for'':204B ''forbidd'':24B ''from'':93B ''geography'':27B ''ghosts'':55B ''govern'':155B ''grant'':77B ''gre'':72B ''grotesqu'':111B ''guard'':123B ''haunt'':52B ''hermaeus'':6B ''highlight'':193B ''historical'':182B ''holding'':140B ''hous'':22B ''including'':133B ''infinit'':135B ''influenc'':208B ''inhabitants'':109B ''inky'':44B ''insanity'':92B ''into'':89B,167B ''intrig'':172B ''is'':14B,75B,128B ''its'':26B,108B,124B ''knowledg'':11B,25B,59B,147B,214B ''labyrinthin'':64B ''laws'':102B ''library'':35B ''lik'':114B ''locations'':132B ''lurkers'':116B ''many'':174B ''maz'':65B ''midd'':151B ''miraak'':189B ''mor'':7B,141B,168B,205B ''mortal'':105B,153B ''mortals'':57B,86B,161B ''most'':143B ''of'':5B,10B,36B,56B,103B,171B,188B ''often'':165B ''ominous'':67B ''omnipresent'':207B ''open'':31B ''operat'':99B ''outsid'':100B ''overwhelming'':178B ''panopticon'':136B ''plan'':51B ''pocket'':138B ''populat'':46B ''pow'':197B ''powerful'':81B ''precious'':144B ''primarily'':76B ''princ'':9B,158B ''realm'':4B,98B,127B,195B ''revelations'':95B ''risk'':91B ''ruins'':68B ''s'':142B,150B,159B,169B,196B,206B ''sag'':187B ''scatter'':83B ''secrets'':125B,210B ''seekers'':115B ''seeking'':58B ''serv'':200B ''servants'':113B ''setting'':203B ''settlement'':154B ''shap'':211B ''significant'':131B ''sky'':73B ''stacks'':63B ''succumbing'':175B ''such'':184B ''surreal'':18B ''tamriel'':85B ''tentacl'':49B ''the'':3B,54B,97B,101B,104B,118B,126B,134B,157B,177B,186B,190B,194B,202B ''this'':50B ''through'':78B ''to'':21B,176B ''towering'':61B ''truths'':179B ''under'':69B ''unending'':94B ''unnatural'':71B ''vast'':16B ''ventur'':88B ''watchers'':119B ''web'':170B ''wher'':209B ''who'':87B,120B ''will'':160B ''with'':130B,173B ''within'':181B ''world'':106B ''writhing'':48B', 'scholar, daedra, daedric', 'Apocrypha, the realm of Hermaeus Mora, is a surreal and vast domain filled with forbidden knowledge. Its landscape includes endless libraries, dark seas, and eerie fields, all under a green sky. Accessible through Black Books, this plane is dangerous, often driving mortals insane with its overwhelming revelations. Its inhabitants include grotesque Daedric servants, such as Seekers and Lurkers, who protect Mora''s secrets. Key locations in Apocrypha include the Infinite Panopticon and Cipher’s Midden, with the realm serving as the setting for events like Miraak''s saga, where knowledge becomes both a power and a curse.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stros_m''kai', 'Stros M''Kai, a tropical island off Hammerfell''s southern coast, is notable for its rich history, Dwemer ruins, and strategic importance. Its main settlements, Port Hunding and Saintsport, are surrounded by unique geography, including the Ogres Tooth Mountains and the Goblin Caverns. The island''s history is intertwined with the Redguard colonization following the Dwemer disappearance and the arrival of the Ra Gada. The city of Port Hunding became a hub of activity during the Second Era, playing a central role in the Tiber War and the subsequent conflict between the Crowns and the Empire, culminating in the rise of the Restless League and the rebellion led by Cyrus.

During the Tiber War, Stros M''Kai became a final stronghold for the Crowns after the death of Prince A''tor. The island was the site of a pivotal battle where the Empire''s dragon, Nafaalilargus, and Admiral Richton secured victory. The rebellion led by Cyrus restored Redguard autonomy after the signing of the First Treaty of Stros M''Kai, legitimizing their rule under Tiber Septim. In the Fourth Era, the island played a key role in the Second Treaty of Stros M''Kai, marking Hammerfell''s independence from both the Empire and the Aldmeri Dominion after resisting Dominion conquest during the Great War. This independence cemented the island''s legacy as a symbol of Redguard resilience and self-determination.', '''activity'':77B ''admiral'':151B ''after'':128B,163B,210B ''aldmeri'':208B ''and'':23B,31B,43B,61B,90B,97B,108B,150B,206B,231B ''are'':33B ''arrival'':63B ''as'':225B ''autonomy'':162B ''battl'':143B ''becam'':73B,121B ''betw'':94B ''both'':203B ''by'':35B,112B,158B ''caverns'':46B ''cement'':220B ''central'':84B ''city'':69B ''coast'':14B ''colonization'':56B ''conflict'':93B ''conquest'':213B ''crowns'':96B,127B ''culminating'':100B ''cyrus'':113B,159B ''death'':130B ''determination'':234B ''disappearanc'':60B ''dominion'':209B,212B ''dragon'':148B ''during'':78B,114B,214B ''dwem'':21B,59B ''empir'':99B,146B,205B ''final'':123B ''first'':168B ''following'':57B ''for'':17B,125B ''fourth'':182B ''from'':202B ''gad'':67B ''geography'':37B ''goblin'':45B ''great'':216B ''hammerfell'':11B,199B ''history'':20B,50B ''hub'':75B ''hunding'':30B,72B ''importanc'':25B ''in'':86B,101B,180B,190B ''including'':38B ''independenc'':201B,219B ''intertwin'':52B ''is'':15B,51B ''island'':9B,48B,136B,185B,222B ''its'':18B,26B ''kai'':3A,6B,120B,173B,197B ''key'':188B ''leag'':107B ''led'':111B,157B ''legacy'':224B ''legitimizing'':174B ''m'':2A,5B,119B,172B,196B ''main'':27B ''marking'':198B ''mountains'':42B ''nafaalilargus'':149B ''notabl'':16B ''of'':64B,70B,76B,104B,131B,140B,166B,170B,194B,228B ''off'':10B ''ogres'':40B ''pivotal'':142B ''play'':186B ''playing'':82B ''port'':29B,71B ''princ'':132B ''ra'':66B ''rebellion'':110B,156B ''redguard'':55B,161B,229B ''resilienc'':230B ''resisting'':211B ''restless'':106B ''restor'':160B ''rich'':19B ''richton'':152B ''ris'':103B ''rol'':85B,189B ''ruins'':22B ''rul'':176B ''s'':12B,49B,147B,200B,223B ''saintsport'':32B ''second'':80B,192B ''secur'':153B ''self'':233B ''self-determination'':232B ''septim'':179B ''settlements'':28B ''signing'':165B ''sit'':139B ''southern'':13B ''strategic'':24B ''stronghold'':124B ''stros'':1A,4B,118B,171B,195B ''subsequent'':92B ''surround'':34B ''symbol'':227B ''the'':39B,44B,47B,54B,58B,62B,65B,68B,79B,87B,91B,95B,98B,102B,105B,109B,115B,126B,129B,135B,138B,145B,155B,164B,167B,175B,181B,184B,191B,204B,207B,215B,221B ''this'':218B ''tib'':88B,116B,178B ''tooth'':41B ''tor'':134B ''treaty'':169B,193B ''tropical'':8B ''under'':177B ''uniqu'':36B ''victory'':154B ''war'':89B,117B,217B ''was'':137B ''wher'':144B ''with'':53B', 'scholar, redguard, sailor', '
Stros M''Kai, an island off Hammerfell''s southern coast, is known for its rich history, Dwemer ruins, and strategic location. Key settlements like Port Hunding played important roles in the Tiber War and the conflict between the Crowns and the Empire. The island was a last stronghold for the Crowns during the war and became a symbol of Redguard resilience after Cyrus led a rebellion that secured their autonomy. In the Fourth Era, the island''s role in the Second Treaty of Stros M''Kai solidified Hammerfell''s independence from both the Empire and the Aldmeri Dominion.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orsinium', 'Orsinium, known as the "City of Orcs," has been the cultural and political center of the Orsimer for centuries, enduring a tumultuous history of destruction and rebuilding. First established in the First Era by Chieftain Torug gro-Igron in the Wrothgarian Mountains, Orsinium became a symbol of Orc unity. It attracted refugees from Hammerfell and other regions, forming a stronghold that rivaled its neighbors. However, its ambition led to conflict, most notably the 30-year Siege of Orsinium (1E 950-980) by allied Breton, Redguard, and Yokudan forces, which resulted in its destruction. Despite this, Orsinium was rebuilt multiple times, each iteration representing the Orcs'' resilience and desire for recognition.

In the Second Era, King Kurog relocated Orsinium to eastern Wrothgar and allied it with the Daggerfall Covenant, seeking to unite the Orcs while navigating tensions with Bretons and Redguards. Following Kurog’s death, his successor, Bazrag, continued efforts toward unity while fostering peace. In the Third Era, Gortwog gro-Nagorm established Nova Orsinium near Wayrest, achieving political stability and prosperity through diplomacy. However, Orsinium faced destruction again in the Fourth Era after the Oblivion Crisis, forcing the Orcs to relocate to a site between Skyrim and Hammerfell. Despite constant adversities, Orsinium remains a testament to the Orcs'' indomitable spirit and their enduring quest for a homeland.', '''-980'':83B ''1e'':81B ''30'':76B ''950'':82B ''achieving'':170B ''adversiti'':204B ''after'':186B ''again'':181B ''alli'':85B,125B ''ambition'':69B ''and'':13B,27B,57B,88B,109B,124B,141B,173B,200B,214B ''as'':4B ''attract'':53B ''bazrag'':149B ''becam'':46B ''been'':10B ''betw'':198B ''breton'':86B ''bretons'':140B ''by'':35B,84B ''cent'':15B ''centuri'':20B ''chieftain'':36B ''city'':6B ''conflict'':72B ''constant'':203B ''continu'':150B ''covenant'':130B ''crisis'':189B ''cultural'':12B ''daggerfall'':129B ''death'':146B ''desir'':110B ''despit'':96B,202B ''destruction'':26B,95B,180B ''diplomacy'':176B ''each'':103B ''eastern'':122B ''efforts'':151B ''enduring'':21B,216B ''establish'':30B,165B ''fac'':179B ''first'':29B,33B ''following'':143B ''for'':19B,111B,218B ''forc'':90B ''forcing'':190B ''forming'':60B ''fostering'':155B ''fourth'':184B ''from'':55B ''gortwog'':161B ''gro'':39B,163B ''gro-igron'':38B ''gro-nagorm'':162B ''hammerfell'':56B,201B ''his'':147B ''history'':24B ''homeland'':220B ''howev'':67B,177B ''igron'':40B ''in'':31B,41B,93B,113B,157B,182B ''indomit'':212B ''it'':52B,126B ''iteration'':104B ''its'':65B,68B,94B ''king'':117B ''known'':3B ''kurog'':118B,144B ''led'':70B ''most'':73B ''mountains'':44B ''multipl'':101B ''nagorm'':164B ''navigating'':137B ''near'':168B ''neighbors'':66B ''notably'':74B ''nov'':166B ''oblivion'':188B ''of'':7B,16B,25B,49B,79B ''orc'':50B ''orcs'':8B,107B,135B,192B,211B ''orsim'':18B ''orsinium'':1A,2B,45B,80B,98B,120B,167B,178B,205B ''other'':58B ''peac'':156B ''political'':14B,171B ''prosperity'':174B ''quest'':217B ''rebuilding'':28B ''rebuilt'':100B ''recognition'':112B ''redguard'':87B ''redguards'':142B ''refug'':54B ''regions'':59B ''relocat'':119B,194B ''remains'':206B ''representing'':105B ''resilienc'':108B ''result'':92B ''rival'':64B ''s'':145B ''second'':115B ''seeking'':131B ''sieg'':78B ''sit'':197B ''skyrim'':199B ''spirit'':213B ''stability'':172B ''stronghold'':62B ''successor'':148B ''symbol'':48B ''tensions'':138B ''testament'':208B ''that'':63B ''the'':5B,11B,17B,32B,42B,75B,106B,114B,128B,134B,158B,183B,187B,191B,210B,215B ''third'':159B ''this'':97B ''through'':175B ''tim'':102B ''to'':71B,121B,132B,193B,195B,209B ''torug'':37B ''toward'':152B ''tumultuous'':23B ''unit'':133B ''unity'':51B,153B ''was'':99B ''wayrest'':169B ''which'':91B ''whil'':136B,154B ''with'':127B,139B ''wrothg'':123B ''wrothgari'':43B ''year'':77B ''yokud'':89B', 'scholar, orc', '
Orsinium, the City of Orcs, has long been the heart of Orc culture and politics, enduring a history marked by destruction and resilience. Founded in the First Era, it faced the 30-year Siege of Orsinium, which led to its initial fall. The city was rebuilt several times, including a relocation in the Second Era by King Kurog. In the Third Era, Gortwog gro-Nagorm established Nova Orsinium, achieving political success. Despite facing destruction again in the Fourth Era during the Oblivion Crisis, Orsinium''s history remains a symbol of the Orcs'' perseverance and their continued struggle for recognition and a homeland.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orc_stronghold', '
Orc strongholds are fortified settlements primarily inhabited by Orcs, also known as Orsimer. These strongholds are typically located in remote, harsh regions such as Skyrim, Hammerfell, and Orsinium (the Orc homeland). They are often isolated from the rest of Tamrielic society, with the Orcs living a clan-based, warrior culture. The strongholds are often led by a chief, and Orcs are known for their crafting, particularly their skill in blacksmithing and the forging of weapons and armor. Though Orcs were once ostracized by other races, especially after the sacking of Orsinium, many Orcs now live in these strongholds, maintaining a fierce independence. Some strongholds have formed alliances with other factions, while others remain neutral or wary of outsiders. The Orcs’ traditional way of life is rooted in honor, strength, and self-reliance, making their strongholds key centers of Orcish identity.






', '''after'':90B ''allianc'':110B ''also'':12B ''and'':29B,62B,74B,79B,133B ''are'':5B,18B,35B,56B,64B ''armor'':80B ''as'':14B,26B ''bas'':51B ''blacksmithing'':73B ''by'':10B,59B,86B ''centers'':141B ''chief'':61B ''clan'':50B ''clan-bas'':49B ''crafting'':68B ''cultur'':53B ''especially'':89B ''factions'':113B ''fierc'':104B ''for'':66B ''forging'':76B ''form'':109B ''fortifi'':6B ''from'':38B ''hammerfell'':28B ''harsh'':23B ''hav'':108B ''homeland'':33B ''honor'':131B ''identity'':144B ''in'':21B,72B,99B,130B ''independenc'':105B ''inhabit'':9B ''is'':128B ''isolat'':37B ''key'':140B ''known'':13B,65B ''led'':58B ''lif'':127B ''liv'':98B ''living'':47B ''locat'':20B ''maintaining'':102B ''making'':137B ''many'':95B ''neutral'':117B ''now'':97B ''of'':41B,77B,93B,120B,126B,142B ''often'':36B,57B ''once'':84B ''or'':118B ''orc'':1A,3B,32B ''orcish'':143B ''orcs'':11B,46B,63B,82B,96B,123B ''orsim'':15B ''orsinium'':30B,94B ''ostraciz'':85B ''other'':87B,112B ''others'':115B ''outsiders'':121B ''particularly'':69B ''primarily'':8B ''rac'':88B ''regions'':24B ''relianc'':136B ''remain'':116B ''remot'':22B ''rest'':40B ''root'':129B ''sacking'':92B ''self'':135B ''self-relianc'':134B ''settlements'':7B ''skill'':71B ''skyrim'':27B ''society'':43B ''som'':106B ''strength'':132B ''stronghold'':2A ''strongholds'':4B,17B,55B,101B,107B,139B ''such'':25B ''tamrielic'':42B ''the'':31B,39B,45B,54B,67B,70B,75B,91B,122B,138B ''thes'':16B,100B ''they'':34B ''though'':81B ''traditional'':124B ''typically'':19B ''warrior'':52B ''wary'':119B ''way'':125B ''weapons'':78B ''wer'':83B ''whil'':114B ''with'':44B,111B', 'orc, scholar', 'Orc strongholds are fortified settlements primarily inhabited by Orcs, also known as Orsimer. These strongholds are typically located in remote, harsh regions such as Skyrim, Hammerfell, and Orsinium (the Orc homeland). They are often isolated from the rest of Tamrielic society, with the Orcs living a clan-based, warrior culture. The strongholds are often led by a chief, and Orcs are known for their crafting, particularly their skill in blacksmithing and the forging of weapons and arm', '', '', 'locationother');


